": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\nTesting Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"total_lines\":151}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"f09d8cf8-a699-4b5a-bb06-6361b753f106"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a massive game implementation task.\n\nSTAGE.md instructs building the game described in PLAN.md. TASK.md provides file names and hand-in requirements. PROGRESS.md tracks progress for resumption after context compaction.\n\nThe plan must specify outcomes rather than architecture. It must not dictate module layout, class names, or exact signatures. PLAN.md serves as the implementer's specification.\n\nThe plan must preserve the OBJECTIVE's must-have terms verbatim. Named games like Wii Fit require research with the web_search tool. PLAN.md already specifies the defining mechanics for this original game inspired by Wii Fit.\n\nThe brief governs design, title method, file names, dates, and deliverables. PLAN.md explicitly frames the output as an original game inspired by the source rather than a recreation. A quick web search on Wii Fit mechanics will confirm PLAN.md captures them accurately before folding those findings into the acceptance criteria.\n\nThe implementer must follow PLAN.md exactly. PLAN.md is the contract, not a memory of Wii Fit. The web search is only to verify PLAN.md did not miss core mechanics.\n\nThe acceptance criteria should be capped at three to five items. The plan is extensive, so related mechanics must be grouped into a compact set. The done condition requires all PLAN.md tasks to be completed on this computer and all TASK.md deliverables to reside in the folder.\n\nTASK.md lists eight deliverables: a dated subfolder with dev files, a single HTML file in the root, PROGRESS.md, an exit-interview.json, feedback sections in chat and in-game credits, a title chosen by RNG after fifty brainstormed titles, the game built on the shardfall engine, and all PLAN.md features. The next step is to identify which of these can be completed on this computer.\n\nPhysical hardware and human players are excluded from this computer. Stand-ins are specified in the brief.\n\nThe acceptance criteria will be outcome-based and gating. The plan is being grouped into roughly three to five criteria that cover defining mechanics without one giant end-to-end gate.\n\nThe criteria are being split into two groups. One covers all TASK.md deliverables: the correctly named HTML file, dated dev subfolder, exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, and an About screen with source info blocks. The other captures a playable vertical slice of the game loop, including New Stay through five wellness days, Balance Core mechanics, morning wobble checks, Balance Age, minute banking, calendar stamps, checkout endings, free play, and bot credits.\n\nThe third criterion covers all events with scoring, stars, and bot ratings. Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, and Plank Standoff are optional cuts for time constraints. They are not computer-based limitations, so the full event set is required unless the implementer chooses to cut.\n\nThe full event set is required by the acceptance criteria. PLAN.md explicitly permits cutting Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, and Plank Standoff as time-based contingencies, provided no stubs remain.\n\nThe event criterion will require the full roster unless Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, and Plank Standoff were legitimately cut in that order. The verifier must accept those documented exceptions and not fail for missing events.\n\nThe phrase \"can be done on this computer\" refers to hardware and environment constraints, not time. The full event roster must be required by the acceptance criteria. PLAN.md's optional cuts are implementer contingencies for time pressure, not computer-based limitations.\n\nControls, UI, 10-foot view, attract mode, dev mode, audio, and multiplayer are all required by TASK.md and PLAN.md.\n\nThe acceptance criteria are being compressed into three to five items. The first criterion covers deliverables and identity: the title chosen by RNG, the correctly named folder and HTML file, a valid exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, an About screen with source information and feedback blocks, and no TODOs or placeholders in shipped text.\n\nThe third criterion specifies the Balance Core play loop. It requires a third-person sports mini-game anthology framed as a life simulation. The guest stay at Tippy Cay includes morning wobble checks that produce Balance Age without weight or BMI. Island free time and four discipline pavilions must each contain the specified events played through one lean-driven Balance Core. Minute banking and calendar stamps are required. Day five Big Stand includes thirty-second Long Stillness. Two endings are required: checkout at age forty or below versus extended stay. A headless bot must play New Stay through credits.\n\nThe fourth criterion covers feel, presentation, and audio. The game uses a high-key pastel aesthetic with new beach and wellness props, hand-keyed exercise clips, and synthesized music, sound effects, and animal voices. Music defaults to ten percent. The writing stays deadpan and original. The UI is controller-first with PS glyphs and an Xbox option, plus native keyboard and mouse support. Prompts follow the last input.\n\nThe fifth criterion covers shell systems. These include attract mode after ten seconds of idle time, dev mode from pause with live sliders and reset, touch-only prompts requiring a controller or keyboard, saves, settings, absence comments, wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, Play Together for two to four players, and AI Hub ghost medley one through four.\n\nA fifth criterion covers the verification bar. It requires tests/run.sh to print only failures and a count. Core tests must cover bot playthrough, per-event stars, balance core feel, attract mode, pause, settings music at ten percent, and browser and hub checks with honest fallbacks for hardware this computer cannot provide.\n\nThe five criteria are now complete. Criterion two is too holistic as a single atomic check. It will be decomposed into smaller independently verifiable items.\n\nThe bot playthrough is a unit-level simulation test inside cargo tests, not a browser end-to-end gate. This satisfies the instruction against holistic checks because it is automated and atomic.\n\nThe hand-in package criterion now specifies exact schema requirements for exit-interview.json, including the usage field set to \"added on import\". The title constant must be a single value drawn from fifty brainstormed titles and match the file names. The Balance play criterion is being narrowed to require one lean-driven Balance Core as the verb for every event.\n\nThe bot must complete the full vertical slice from New Stay through five wellness days, Big Stand, and one of the two endings without reading the wall clock. Morning checks produce a clamped Balance Age from the skill formula; better input yields a lower age. The game must contain no weight, BMI, body-shape, or diet content, and no Nintendo names except in the About source line and title riff.\n\nEvery specified event must be playable from its scene, scoring 0–1000 with star thresholds, banking minutes, and showing a result card. A bot must earn at least two stars on each event and idle under one star.\n\nThe optional Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, and Plank Standoff cuts are being recorded in Risks as a documented exception. The objective requires everything that can be done on this computer, so those events remain in scope.\n\nThe presentation and input criterion now specifies exact UI requirements. The 10-foot egui interface uses minimum sizes. Controllers are primary with keyboard and mouse on the same screens. Prompts show last-input glyphs including an Xbox option. Music defaults to ten percent linear with synthesized sound effects and animalese voices; no audio files are used. A touch-only card appears when no touch controls exist while attract mode continues running. Title and menu screens exit after ten seconds of idle time or on any input. Pause freezes the world.\n\nThe fifth criterion is being expanded to cover multiplayer and save systems. It requires AI Hub ghost sessions running the Inter-Resort Medley with a reported score, a solo page that works when AIHub.active is false, Play Together hot-seat for two to four players, Yesterday You ghosts, and versioned localStorage saves. The hub client must be pasted byte-for-byte. Stand-ins are used for pad, touch, sound, second player, WebKit iPhone, and 1080p capture. The verification plan must include real in-repo tests.\n\nThe verification plan now includes a browser launch check. Playwright will serve the page and assert zero errors, valid render dimensions, visible input-driven changes, and a screenshot. The engine is Rust/WASM, so WebGPU runs on Chromium with flags and file:// works. Tests will run at 320x180 because software rendering is slow. Launches must be repeated to confirm consistent success.\n\nThe deliverable is a single HTML file. Playwright will launch it via a local server with WebGPU flags enabled. The verification plan must follow PLAN section 16 because that defines the objective. Engine structure may be described in the implementation approach, but specific file names and layout cannot become acceptance criteria.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The brief is a full Wii Fit-inspired game on a named engine. I’ll confirm the source’s defining mechanics, then freeze outcomes rather than a build recipe."},{"type":"server_tool_use","id":"ws_d59011f6-65d3-9c6b-a360-b7cde8e55ec4_call-14dfa678-b8ff-47aa-ad24-a05b80c8320b-4","name":"web_search","input":{"query":"Wii Fit defining gameplay mechanics balance board body test fitness age yoga strength aerobics balance games daily calendar"}},{"type":"web_search_tool_result","tool_use_id":"ws_d59011f6-65d3-9c6b-a360-b7cde8e55ec4_call-14dfa678-b8ff-47aa-ad24-a05b80c8320b-4","content":[{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://www.gamespot.com/articles/wii-fit-users-guide/1100-6191333/","title":"https://www.gamespot.com/articles/wii-fit-users-guide/1100-6191333/"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://w.atwiki.jp/gcmatome/pages/7748.html","title":"https://w.atwiki.jp/gcmatome/pages/7748.html"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/wii/942009-wii-fit/faqs/52634","title":"https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/wii/942009-wii-fit/faqs/52634"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://www.gamesdatabase.org/game/nintendo-wii/wii-fit","title":"https://www.gamesdatabase.org/game/nintendo-wii/wii-fit"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wii_Fit","title":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wii_Fit"}]},{"type":"server_tool_use","id":"ws_d59011f6-65d3-9c6b-a360-b7cde8e55ec4_call-14dfa678-b8ff-47aa-ad24-a05b80c8320b-5","name":"web_search","input":{"query":"Wii Fit game modes body test balance games yoga strength training aerobic exercises Wii Fit Plus island plaza"}},{"type":"web_search_tool_result","tool_use_id":"ws_d59011f6-65d3-9c6b-a360-b7cde8e55ec4_call-14dfa678-b8ff-47aa-ad24-a05b80c8320b-5","content":[{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://miiwiki.org/wiki/Yoga","title":"https://miiwiki.org/wiki/Yoga"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://miiwiki.org/wiki/Wii_Fit","title":"https://miiwiki.org/wiki/Wii_Fit"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://miiwiki.org/wiki/Wii_Fit_(series)","title":"https://miiwiki.org/wiki/Wii_Fit_(series)"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/wii/960488-wii-fit-plus/faqs/61704","title":"https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/wii/960488-wii-fit-plus/faqs/61704"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MHZXDnllW1Y","title":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MHZXDnllW1Y"}]},{"type":"text","text":"PLAN.md already turns Wii Fit’s balance-board loop into an original resort game, and this machine can run that build. I’ll freeze the observable contract, not the file layout."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-14dfa678-b8ff-47aa-ad24-a05b80c8320b-6","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d%2Fwork/01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce/goal/plan-01a1aa27-bbea-7912-86a4-6a7240dd1889.md","content":"# Plan: Ship a playable Tippy Cay balance-and-wellness demo inspired by Wii Fit, plus the hand-in files TASK.md names\n\n## Goal kind\ncode-change\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. **Hand-in package.** The work-folder root contains `PROGRESS.md`, a parseable `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape TASK.md specifies (every value filled, `\"usage\"` exactly `added on import`, `aiHub.genre` one of the allowed catalogue genres, `aiHub.players` `1–4`), and one self-contained HTML file named `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html`. A sibling folder with that same basename (no `.html`) holds the dev tree. `{Title}` is a playful riff on “Wii Fit”, chosen by listing 50 titles and selecting one with a real RNG; the same string is the title-screen name, the page `<title>`, and `aiHub.name`. The 50 titles and the RNG draw are recorded in the dev folder. Opening the HTML from disk boots this game (a WebGPU-missing message only when WebGPU is absent).\n2. **Wii Fit loop, original world.** It is a third-person sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame: a five-day stay at Tippy Cay staffed by talking gym gear. The only play verb is a centre-of-pressure lean (left stick, keyboard ramp, or mouse offset from screen centre — last device wins) driving one shared balance model: shaped lean, stiffness/damping, sim-time wobble, tip only after the dot stays outside the unit disc for the tip time. Tips cost time or score and never end the stay. Each morning a wobble check (still, lean targets, eyes-closed tone, step timing) yields a Balance Age from PLAN.md’s skill formula, clamped 18–99; better input gives a lower age. There is no weight, BMI, body-shape, or diet content, and no Nintendo product names inside play (About source line and the title riff only). Days open in order — stillness, strength, cardio, lagoon — with minute goals 3, 5, 7, 9, then a Day-5 Big Stand whose last phase is 30 seconds of doing nothing (fake “press to skip”; any press forfeits the bonus). First clear of an event banks 1 + stars; repeats bank 1. Age 40 or better may check out by rowboat; otherwise the Extended Stay ending. Both roll credits and unlock free play. A headless bot, from a fresh New Stay, reaches credits on 3 seeds: won, 5 stamps, every event played, under 60 sim-minutes, without reading the wall clock.\n3. **Every event is a finished mini-game.** Shipped and directly startable: Morning Wobble Check, Breath Bloom, Pose Parade, Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff, Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap, Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup, and the five-phase Big Stand, with the twists named in PLAN.md §5 (breath guide, drifting pose ring and gull, squat tempo, plank flop, 96 BPM two-lane chart, hula-style spin and ring catches, lap with step-rate zone, shell-tilt boards, paddle gates, tray of smoothies, cannonball judges, Long Stillness). Each event has a card, countdown, result (score, stars, deadpan title, minutes, personal best, Retry or Back), a bot that earns at least 2 stars on 5 seeds, and an idle-input result under 1 star. Score events use 0–1000 with stars at 400, 650, and 850; Plank uses the time gates in PLAN.md (25 / 40 / 55 s). Time-cut permission in PLAN.md §17 does not apply: this computer can run the full roster.\n4. **10-foot play shell, audio, and dev tools.** Same screens for pad, keyboard, and mouse. Prompts follow the last input: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs via Settings, keycaps, or mouse buttons. Bindings match PLAN.md §3, including pause and schedule. After 10 seconds (600 sim ticks) with no input on the title or pre-game menus, attract mode loops the PLAN.md §12 sequence with a DEMO ribbon; any input returns to the title; nothing is saved; it stays silent until a real input. Pause freezes the world and opens Dev Mode (not in a hub session) with jump, cheats, time scale, live sliders for the tunables named in PLAN.md §11, and reset to defaults. Settings include music default 0.10 linear, SFX, voices, glyphs, lean sensitivity, wobble assist, rhythm offset, text speed, fullscreen, and reset-save confirm. Touch-only devices get a “Controller or keyboard required” card plus Settings, no touch controls, and attract keeps running. All music, at least 30 sound effects, and Animalese/Simlish voices are synthesized in code (no audio files); speakers are audibly distinct; dialogue types out with syllable blips. UI is large enough for 10 feet (body ≥34 px and titles ≥64 px at 1080p, scaled down with the frame), at most two lines of dialogue, no dense stat tables. Look is high-key pastel on the engine’s cel style, with new beach and wellness props and new exercise poses; library props only for generic dressing.\n5. **Saves, local multiplayer, and AI Hub.** Versioned `localStorage` saves cover up to four guest slots (name from a preset list, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings, written on day change and on each result. Real dates passed in at boot drive absence comments; the sim does not read the clock. Play Together is hot-seat for 2–4 guests through the same three-event medley, with a pass-the-pad card and a podium. Yesterday You replays a best run beside you from day 3 and does not affect scoring. An AI Hub session in mode `ghost`, 1–4 players, skips title, menu, attract, quit, restart, and dev mode, and opens into the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup, same seed, same course). Other seats are tinted ghosts in a matching area only. Final score is the sum (0–3000) reported to the hub. Solo play leaves `AIHub.active` false. The About/Credits screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback, plus font and motion-library credits. No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features remain.\n\n## Verification plan\n1. **gating:** Add in-repo tests that construct the shipped game from a fresh start (no browser, no GPU) and drive its real update loop. Assert criterion 2’s bot run (3 seeds), criterion 3’s per-event bot and idle results (5 seeds), balance-model settle and tip timing, age direction and 18–99 bounds, attract start at 600 idle ticks plus exit without saving, pause freezing world time, music default 0.10, a dev slider changing a live value and resetting, save round-trip, medley determinism for the same seed and inputs, and Play Together reaching a podium. Lint shipped text for `TODO`, placeholder copy, weight/BMI/diet talk, and Nintendo names outside the About source line. Put them behind one command that prints only failures and a final `N passed, 0 failed` line. Run that command twice; both runs must print the same pass line. Save the log to `{SCRATCH}/tests-core.log`.\n2. **gating:** Launch the shipped HTML on its real entry path more than once. Prefer `file://`. If a server is required, bind `127.0.0.1` with `python3 -u -m http.server 0` and stop only that PID. Use Playwright Chromium (already installed) with the WebGPU flags in TASK.md. At 320×180, twice: zero page errors, `__gameStatus` appears and its tick advances across samples, a standard-mapping gamepad stub moves menu focus and confirms, keyboard does the same, mouse hover moves focus and click activates using rects the page publishes, prompts change with the device, Settings exposes Xbox glyphs, and after about 10 real seconds attract starts and an input exits it. Phone and tablet Chromium profiles show “Controller or keyboard required”, keep attract running, and a Settings tap opens Settings. WebKit with an iPhone profile (no WebGPU here) shows the fallback that both a controller or keyboard and WebGPU are required. The drawing surface’s dimensions equal the requested viewport. A blank WebGPU canvas while ticks advance is the known software-readback limit, not a pass: also capture a 1920×1080 frame with the engine’s headless capture of the title (menu and title text readable) and of one event (figure plus balance puck substantially filling the frame). A blank engine capture is a failure. Two browser boots and two engine captures must agree. Logs and images go to `{SCRATCH}/`. If Playwright or the engine capture cannot start, save that launcher error to `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.log`; criteria 2–4 then rest on step 1 plus the static checks in step 4. A capture that runs and returns a blank frame is not this fallback.\n3. **gating:** Hub check on the shipped page. Serve the page with the hub harness files and open the harness for 2 players; for 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and for `scenario=host-leave`. Each run must finish with the harness complete flag and its own pass flag set. Then open the page outside a session, press Enter and Space, and require no errors, `AIHub.active` false, and `Math.random` left unseeded. The session client embedded in the page must byte-match the downloaded `session.js`. Save logs to `{SCRATCH}/tests-hub.log`. If the hub files cannot be fetched, keep this step gating and record the blocker in `{SCRATCH}/hub-unverifiable.log` instead of inventing a pass.\n4. **gating:** Static hand-in check. `exit-interview.json` parses as one object with the TASK.md keys; `usage` is `added on import`; `aiHub.name` equals the title screen. The HTML filename and dev-folder name match criterion 1. The page’s about-data block includes Source Information and the three feedback lists. `PROGRESS.md` exists. Dev-folder notes contain the 50 titles and the RNG output. Confirm no audio files are referenced by the game.\n5. **evidence:** One 1920×1080 engine capture per set, plus a short filmstrip of at least one hand-keyed pose. Sound: either the unit render at music 0.10 is about a tenth of full scale, or a browser patch of the audio buffer shows non-silent music after a gesture. Absence of these images does not fail the goal when steps 1–4 pass.\n\n## Non-goals\n- Not a Wii Fit recreation: no BMI or weight goals, no Miis or face editors, no Wuhu Island, no source music, layouts, or quoted lines, and not the full 40-activity list (soccer heading, ski jump, hula hoop as named in the source, and the rest).\n- No real Balance Board, DualSense, iPhone, TV, listener, or second human. Use the stand-ins in TASK.md.\n- No touch-play controls, no shared-world netcode, no FPS optimization, and no review subagents.\n- No audio files and no spoken real words.\n\n## Assumed scope\n- Work root: `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`, and `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html`.\n- Dev folder of that basename: clone of `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall` (PLAN.md was checked against commit `49ef2ba`), game content and tests, notes, and a small README for adding an event, a set, or a song.\n- AI Hub client files from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` (`session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`).\n- Fredoka and Nunito (SIL OFL) embedded for UI text; engine puppet, egui, and synthesized audio extended as PLAN.md §§8–14 describe. Behavior is the contract; file names in PLAN.md are guidance.\n- Playwright 1.63 (system Python, not `python3 -I`), Cargo, and `wasm-bindgen` 0.2.129. Chromium only for WebGPU play; Firefox and WebKit are fallback-message checks.\n\n## Implementation approach\nFollow PLAN.md for design numbers, writing, and the hub snippet; do not invent a second balance model or a second synth. Keep the whole flow (menus, dialogue, pause, settings, dev toggles, events) in the simulation so tests drive it with no GPU. Keep UI a pure view of that state. Keep tunable numbers and all dialogue in data files the tests load. Build a single HTML only after the sim tests pass. Disable the engine’s demo keys and on-screen chrome while this game is active so captures show the game, not the engine shell. Record any spec gap in one line in the dev notes and continue.\n\n## Task checklist\n- [ ] Pick the title with a real RNG from 50 riffs, record the draw, create the dev folder, clone the engine, and keep `PROGRESS.md` current.\n- [ ] Register the game, hide engine chrome, add lean input and the title/pause shell, save, and the hub page tags so a boot smoke test passes.\n- [ ] Implement the shared balance model, the morning check, the island day loop, and one full event; lock them with sim tests.\n- [ ] Implement the remaining events, day unlocks, Big Stand, both endings, free play, and the bot playthrough.\n- [ ] Add synthesized music, effects, and gibberish voices (music default 0.10), attract mode, settings, dev sliders with reset, and the touch-only card.\n- [ ] Add wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, Play Together, and the hub ghost medley; run the hub harness.\n- [ ] Write the full script and About text, fill `exit-interview.json`, build the single HTML into the work root, run the one test command twice, capture title and one event, then delete build caches only.\n\n## Risks / Contradictions\n- PLAN.md §17 allows cutting Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, and Plank Standoff if time runs short. The objective requires everything this computer can run, so a cut roster fails criterion 3.\n- TASK.md warns that a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank even when the frame is live. A blank browser bitmap is not success and not an automatic environment waiver: the engine’s own capture must show a filled frame (step 2). Only a launcher that will not start is the fallback.\n- Browser timing at 1920×1080 is too slow here (software WebGPU). The 10-second attract check is valid only around 320×180; a slow 1080p browser clock is not a game bug. Judge the 10-foot layout from the 1080p engine capture.\n- Firefox and WebKit have no WebGPU here, so they cannot play the game. There is no physical pad, touch screen, listener, second human, or TV.\n- A fresh clone may not be commit `49ef2ba`. If a “verified” engine note is wrong on the cloned revision, adapt and record the commit and the change; do not pretend the old note still held.\n- Other agents share this machine. Use one browser, bind an OS-picked localhost port, and stop only PIDs this run started. `earlyoom` killing the browser is memory pressure, not a game bug.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30540,"output_tokens":12897,"cache_read_input_tokens":51712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"82888a57-0b6d-4aec-82cd-b3961ee5dcd9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-14dfa678-b8ff-47aa-ad24-a05b80c8320b-6","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Plan: Ship a playable Tippy Cay balance-and-wellness demo inspired by Wii Fit, plus the hand-in files TASK.md names\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in package.** The work-folder root contains `PROGRESS.md`, a parseable `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape TASK.md specifies (every value filled, `\\\"usage\\\"` exactly `added on import`, `aiHub.genre` one of the allowed catalogue genres, `aiHub.players` `1–4`), and one self-contained HTML file named `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html`. A sibling folder with that same basename (no `.html`) holds the dev tree. `{Title}` is a playful riff on “Wii Fit”, chosen by listing 50 titles and selecting one with a real RNG; the same string is the title-screen name, the page `<title>`, and `aiHub.name`. The 50 titles and the RNG draw are recorded in the dev folder. Opening the HTML from disk boots this game (a WebGPU-missing message only when WebGPU is absent).\\n2. **Wii Fit loop, original world.** It is a third-person sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame: a five-day stay at Tippy Cay staffed by talking gym gear. The only play verb is a centre-of-pressure lean (left stick, keyboard ramp, or mouse offset from screen centre — last device wins) driving one shared balance model: shaped lean, stiffness/damping, sim-time wobble, tip only after the dot stays outside the unit disc for the tip time. Tips cost time or score and never end the stay. Each morning a wobble check (still, lean targets, eyes-closed tone, step timing) yields a Balance Age from PLAN.md’s skill formula, clamped 18–99; better input gives a lower age. There is no weight, BMI, body-shape, or diet content, and no Nintendo product names inside play (About source line and the title riff only). Days open in order — stillness, strength, cardio, lagoon — with minute goals 3, 5, 7, 9, then a Day-5 Big Stand whose last phase is 30 seconds of doing nothing (fake “press to skip”; any press forfeits the bonus). First clear of an event banks 1 + stars; repeats bank 1. Age 40 or better may check out by rowboat; otherwise the Extended Stay ending. Both roll credits and unlock free play. A headless bot, from a fresh New Stay, reaches credits on 3 seeds: won, 5 stamps, every event played, under 60 sim-minutes, without reading the wall clock.\\n3. **Every event is a finished mini-game.** Shipped and directly startable: Morning Wobble Check, Breath Bloom, Pose Parade, Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff, Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap, Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup, and the five-phase Big Stand, with the twists named in PLAN.md §5 (breath guide, drifting pose ring and gull, squat tempo, plank flop, 96 BPM two-lane chart, hula-style spin and ring catches, lap with step-rate zone, shell-tilt boards, paddle gates, tray of smoothies, cannonball judges, Long Stillness). Each event has a card, countdown, result (score, stars, deadpan title, minutes, personal best, Retry or Back), a bot that earns at least 2 stars on 5 seeds, and an idle-input result under 1 star. Score events use 0–1000 with stars at 400, 650, and 850; Plank uses the time gates in PLAN.md (25 / 40 / 55 s). Time-cut permission in PLAN.md §17 does not apply: this computer can run the full roster.\\n4. **10-foot play shell, audio, and dev tools.** Same screens for pad, keyboard, and mouse. Prompts follow the last input: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs via Settings, keycaps, or mouse buttons. Bindings match PLAN.md §3, including pause and schedule. After 10 seconds (600 sim ticks) with no input on the title or pre-game menus, attract mode loops the PLAN.md §12 sequence with a DEMO ribbon; any input returns to the title; nothing is saved; it stays silent until a real input. Pause freezes the world and opens Dev Mode (not in a hub session) with jump, cheats, time scale, live sliders for the tunables named in PLAN.md §11, and reset to defaults. Settings include music default 0.10 linear, SFX, voices, glyphs, lean sensitivity, wobble assist, rhythm offset, text speed, fullscreen, and reset-save confirm. Touch-only devices get a “Controller or keyboard required” card plus Settings, no touch controls, and attract keeps running. All music, at least 30 sound effects, and Animalese/Simlish voices are synthesized in code (no audio files); speakers are audibly distinct; dialogue types out with syllable blips. UI is large enough for 10 feet (body ≥34 px and titles ≥64 px at 1080p, scaled down with the frame), at most two lines of dialogue, no dense stat tables. Look is high-key pastel on the engine’s cel style, with new beach and wellness props and new exercise poses; library props only for generic dressing.\\n5. **Saves, local multiplayer, and AI Hub.** Versioned `localStorage` saves cover up to four guest slots (name from a preset list, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings, written on day change and on each result. Real dates passed in at boot drive absence comments; the sim does not read the clock. Play Together is hot-seat for 2–4 guests through the same three-event medley, with a pass-the-pad card and a podium. Yesterday You replays a best run beside you from day 3 and does not affect scoring. An AI Hub session in mode `ghost`, 1–4 players, skips title, menu, attract, quit, restart, and dev mode, and opens into the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup, same seed, same course). Other seats are tinted ghosts in a matching area only. Final score is the sum (0–3000) reported to the hub. Solo play leaves `AIHub.active` false. The About/Credits screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback, plus font and motion-library credits. No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features remain.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** Add in-repo tests that construct the shipped game from a fresh start (no browser, no GPU) and drive its real update loop. Assert criterion 2’s bot run (3 seeds), criterion 3’s per-event bot and idle results (5 seeds), balance-model settle and tip timing, age direction and 18–99 bounds, attract start at 600 idle ticks plus exit without saving, pause freezing world time, music default 0.10, a dev slider changing a live value and resetting, save round-trip, medley determinism for the same seed and inputs, and Play Together reaching a podium. Lint shipped text for `TODO`, placeholder copy, weight/BMI/diet talk, and Nintendo names outside the About source line. Put them behind one command that prints only failures and a final `N passed, 0 failed` line. Run that command twice; both runs must print the same pass line. Save the log to `{SCRATCH}/tests-core.log`.\\n2. **gating:** Launch the shipped HTML on its real entry path more than once. Prefer `file://`. If a server is required, bind `127.0.0.1` with `python3 -u -m http.server 0` and stop only that PID. Use Playwright Chromium (already installed) with the WebGPU flags in TASK.md. At 320×180, twice: zero page errors, `__gameStatus` appears and its tick advances across samples, a standard-mapping gamepad stub moves menu focus and confirms, keyboard does the same, mouse hover moves focus and click activates using rects the page publishes, prompts change with the device, Settings exposes Xbox glyphs, and after about 10 real seconds attract starts and an input exits it. Phone and tablet Chromium profiles show “Controller or keyboard required”, keep attract running, and a Settings tap opens Settings. WebKit with an iPhone profile (no WebGPU here) shows the fallback that both a controller or keyboard and WebGPU are required. The drawing surface’s dimensions equal the requested viewport. A blank WebGPU canvas while ticks advance is the known software-readback limit, not a pass: also capture a 1920×1080 frame with the engine’s headless capture of the title (menu and title text readable) and of one event (figure plus balance puck substantially filling the frame). A blank engine capture is a failure. Two browser boots and two engine captures must agree. Logs and images go to `{SCRATCH}/`. If Playwright or the engine capture cannot start, save that launcher error to `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.log`; criteria 2–4 then rest on step 1 plus the static checks in step 4. A capture that runs and returns a blank frame is not this fallback.\\n3. **gating:** Hub check on the shipped page. Serve the page with the hub harness files and open the harness for 2 players; for 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and for `scenario=host-leave`. Each run must finish with the harness complete flag and its own pass flag set. Then open the page outside a session, press Enter and Space, and require no errors, `AIHub.active` false, and `Math.random` left unseeded. The session client embedded in the page must byte-match the downloaded `session.js`. Save logs to `{SCRATCH}/tests-hub.log`. If the hub files cannot be fetched, keep this step gating and record the blocker in `{SCRATCH}/hub-unverifiable.log` instead of inventing a pass.\\n4. **gating:** Static hand-in check. `exit-interview.json` parses as one object with the TASK.md keys; `usage` is `added on import`; `aiHub.name` equals the title screen. The HTML filename and dev-folder name match criterion 1. The page’s about-data block includes Source Information and the three feedback lists. `PROGRESS.md` exists. Dev-folder notes contain the 50 titles and the RNG output. Confirm no audio files are referenced by the game.\\n5. **evidence:** One 1920×1080 engine capture per set, plus a short filmstrip of at least one hand-keyed pose. Sound: either the unit render at music 0.10 is about a tenth of full scale, or a browser patch of the audio buffer shows non-silent music after a gesture. Absence of these images does not fail the goal when steps 1–4 pass.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- Not a Wii Fit recreation: no BMI or weight goals, no Miis or face editors, no Wuhu Island, no source music, layouts, or quoted lines, and not the full 40-activity list (soccer heading, ski jump, hula hoop as named in the source, and the rest).\\n- No real Balance Board, DualSense, iPhone, TV, listener, or second human. Use the stand-ins in TASK.md.\\n- No touch-play controls, no shared-world netcode, no FPS optimization, and no review subagents.\\n- No audio files and no spoken real words.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- Work root: `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`, and `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html`.\\n- Dev folder of that basename: clone of `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall` (PLAN.md was checked against commit `49ef2ba`), game content and tests, notes, and a small README for adding an event, a set, or a song.\\n- AI Hub client files from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` (`session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`).\\n- Fredoka and Nunito (SIL OFL) embedded for UI text; engine puppet, egui, and synthesized audio extended as PLAN.md §§8–14 describe. Behavior is the contract; file names in PLAN.md are guidance.\\n- Playwright 1.63 (system Python, not `python3 -I`), Cargo, and `wasm-bindgen` 0.2.129. Chromium only for WebGPU play; Firefox and WebKit are fallback-message checks.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md for design numbers, writing, and the hub snippet; do not invent a second balance model or a second synth. Keep the whole flow (menus, dialogue, pause, settings, dev toggles, events) in the simulation so tests drive it with no GPU. Keep UI a pure view of that state. Keep tunable numbers and all dialogue in data files the tests load. Build a single HTML only after the sim tests pass. Disable the engine’s demo keys and on-screen chrome while this game is active so captures show the game, not the engine shell. Record any spec gap in one line in the dev notes and continue.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Pick the title with a real RNG from 50 riffs, record the draw, create the dev folder, clone the engine, and keep `PROGRESS.md` current.\\n- [ ] Register the game, hide engine chrome, add lean input and the title/pause shell, save, and the hub page tags so a boot smoke test passes.\\n- [ ] Implement the shared balance model, the morning check, the island day loop, and one full event; lock them with sim tests.\\n- [ ] Implement the remaining events, day unlocks, Big Stand, both endings, free play, and the bot playthrough.\\n- [ ] Add synthesized music, effects, and gibberish voices (music default 0.10), attract mode, settings, dev sliders with reset, and the touch-only card.\\n- [ ] Add wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, Play Together, and the hub ghost medley; run the hub harness.\\n- [ ] Write the full script and About text, fill `exit-interview.json`, build the single HTML into the work root, run the one test command twice, capture title and one event, then delete build caches only.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §17 allows cutting Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, and Plank Standoff if time runs short. The objective requires everything this computer can run, so a cut roster fails criterion 3.\\n- TASK.md warns that a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank even when the frame is live. A blank browser bitmap is not success and not an automatic environment waiver: the engine’s own capture must show a filled frame (step 2). Only a launcher that will not start is the fallback.\\n- Browser timing at 1920×1080 is too slow here (software WebGPU). The 10-second attract check is valid only around 320×180; a slow 1080p browser clock is not a game bug. Judge the 10-foot layout from the 1080p engine capture.\\n- Firefox and WebKit have no WebGPU here, so they cannot play the game. There is no physical pad, touch screen, listener, second human, or TV.\\n- A fresh clone may not be commit `49ef2ba`. If a “verified” engine note is wrong on the cloned revision, adapt and record the commit and the change; do not pretend the old note still held.\\n- Other agents share this machine. Use one browser, bind an OS-picked localhost port, and stop only PIDs this run started. `earlyoom` killing the browser is memory pressure, not a game bug.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d%2Fwork/01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce/goal/plan-01a1aa27-bbea-7912-86a4-6a7240dd1889.md has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d%2Fwork/01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce/goal/plan-01a1aa27-bbea-7912-86a4-6a7240dd1889.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d%2Fwork/01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce/goal/plan-01a1aa27-bbea-7912-86a4-6a7240dd1889.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Plan: Ship a playable Tippy Cay balance-and-wellness demo inspired by Wii Fit, plus the hand-in files TASK.md names\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in package.** The work-folder root contains `PROGRESS.md`, a parseable `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape TASK.md specifies (every value filled, `\\\"usage\\\"` exactly `added on import`, `aiHub.genre` one of the allowed catalogue genres, `aiHub.players` `1–4`), and one self-contained HTML file named `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html`. A sibling folder with that same basename (no `.html`) holds the dev tree. `{Title}` is a playful riff on “Wii Fit”, chosen by listing 50 titles and selecting one with a real RN