{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_14","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to find where `play_post` is called and examine the rest of `step_inner`.\n\nThe scope is massive, covering puppet motion, audio, and engine integration. I will design a complete but implementable game. The plan is to boot from HTML, add sim tests, browser tests, hub integration, and captures. Engine seams will be modified minimally and targetedly.\n\nFitGame will be a state machine for core logic like balance and scoring, using the 3D world only for island walking and characters. The bot must play through entire room sets including menus. Tests will drive the game via Sim::step with InputFrame in simple rooms. The 60-sim-minute limit equals 216,000 ticks.\n\n\"Under 60 sim-minutes\" means resort minutes, not wall-clock time. The bot must reach credits on three seeds: won, five stamps, and every event played. It must do this from a fresh New Stay without reading the wall clock.\n\nThe bot must finish every event in real time. Morning checks, Pose Parade, Tempo Squats, Plank, Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap, Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball, and Big Stand all add up to roughly fifteen to twenty minutes of simulation time. That equals about seventy-two thousand ticks.\n\nThe starter bot finishes in under one second. The full playthrough must also be fast. Morning checks alone consume roughly twenty-one thousand ticks. Physics runs every tick, so seventy-two thousand ticks of simple logic may still be too slow.\n\nRapier physics at sixty hertz across fifty to eighty thousand ticks could take several seconds to thirty seconds. That is acceptable if the simulation is kept efficient.\n\nThe bot must play the real flow rather than using a dev time scale cheat. It will skip dialogue and walk directly, but it cannot skip events because stars must be earned.\n\nI am now estimating the total runtime.\n\nI will read starter.rs, the end of step_inner for play_post, puppet body_motion and tilt fields, audio sounds_for and Mixer, parts.rs AttachKind, parameter lists, Sim::frame puppet assembly, and web/index.html structure. I am also estimating simulation speed at ten thousand ticks per second, which would make three seeds finish in about twenty-four seconds.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-42809613-bc1a-46be-bea5-ef8ffa71446b-23","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs","offset":670,"limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-42809613-bc1a-46be-bea5-ef8ffa71446b-24","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/puppet.rs","offset":450,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-42809613-bc1a-46be-bea5-ef8ffa71446b-25","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/puppet.rs","offset":760,"limit":220}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-42809613-bc1a-46be-bea5-ef8ffa71446b-26","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs","offset":1,"limit":280}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4834,"output_tokens":1505,"cache_read_input_tokens":66944,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"cd8a0a10-79f6-410f-a84f-86544b3ed0b9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-42809613-bc1a-46be-bea5-ef8ffa71446b-23","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"670→\\n        // Projectiles.\\n        if !self.state.projectiles.list.is_empty() {\\n            let hitbox = self.config.movement.hitbox;\\n            let player = self.state.player;\\n            let targets: Vec<Target> = self\\n                .state\\n                .entities\\n                .iter()\\n                .filter_map(|e| {\\n680→                    let c = e.character.as_ref()?;\\n                    let radius = if Some(e.id) == player { hitbox } else { RADIUS };\\n                    Some(Target { id: e.id, feet: e.pos - Vec3::Y * c.height() * 0.5, height: c.height(), radius })\\n                })\\n                .collect();\\n            let enemies: Vec<crate::projectile::Enemy> = self\\n                .state\\n                .entities\\n                .iter()\\n                .filter(|e| e.health.is_some())\\n690→                .map(|e| crate::projectile::Enemy {\\n                    id: e.id,\\n                    center: e.pos,\\n                    radius: e.visual.as_ref().map(|v| v.shape.half_extents().max_element()).unwrap_or(0.5),\\n                })\\n                .collect();\\n            let physics = &self.state.physics;\\n            let entities = &self.state.entities;\\n            let out = self.state.projectiles.step(dt, &targets, &enemies, |from, dir, len, owner| {\\n                let ignore = owner.and_then(|id| entities.get(id)).and_then(|e| e.body);\\n700→                crate::projectile::static_blocked(physics, from, dir, len, ignore)\\n            });\\n            for (id, at, dir, kb) in out.hits {\\n                self.hit_character(id, at, dir, kb, false, &mut events);\\n            }\\n            for (id, at, dmg) in out.damage {\\n                self.damage(id, at, dmg, &mut events);\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n710→        self.game_post(dt, raw_dt, &mut events);\\n        self.play_post(dt, &mut events);\\n        self.game_travel(&mut events);\\n\\n        if let Some(p) = self.player() {\\n            self.state.focus = p.pos;\\n        }\\n        self.update_zones(&mut events);\\n        self.measure_feel(input);\\n        self.update_room_tracking(&mut events);\\n720→        if self.state.tick.is_multiple_of(15) {\\n            self.update_streaming(2);\\n        }\\n        self.state.tick += 1;\\n        if !self.replaying {\\n            self.events.extend(events);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn measure_feel(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n730→        let Some(e) = self.player() else { return };\\n        let Some(ch) = e.character.as_ref() else { return };\\n        let (vel, grounded, feet) =\\n            (ch.vel, ch.grounded || ch.climbing.is_some() || ch.hang.is_some(), e.pos - Vec3::Y * ch.height() * 0.5);\\n        let dt = self.dt();\\n        let tick = self.state.tick;\\n        self.state.feel.update(tick, dt, input.move_dir, vel, feet, grounded);\\n    }\\n\\n    fn throw_bomb(&mut self, from: Vec3, vel: Vec3, owner: EntityId) {\\n740→        let mut v = Visual::new(Shape::Sphere { radius: 0.2 }, Color::hex(\\\"#2b2d35\\\"));\\n        v.look = Look::Lit;\\n        let id = self.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"bomb\\\", from).visual(v).body(BodyKind::Dynamic).restitution(0.15));\\n        if let Some(e) = self.state.entities.get_mut(id) {\\n            e.bomb = Some(Bomb { fuse: self.config.bombs.fuse, radius: self.config.bombs.radius, owner: Some(owner) });\\n            if let Some(b) = e.body.and_then(|h| self.state.physics.bodies.get_mut(h)) {\\n                b.set_linvel(vel, true);\\n                b.enable_ccd(true);\\n            }\\n        }\\n750→    }\\n\\n    /// Removes destructible blocks in the radius, throws debris and pushes things away.\\n    pub fn explode(&mut self, pos: Vec3, radius: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n        let hit = self.state.statics.blocks_in_sphere(pos, radius);\\n        let mut debris = Vec::new();\\n        for r in hit {\\n            if !self.state.statics.get(r).is_some_and(|b| b.has(block_flags::DESTRUCTIBLE)) {\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n760→            let st = &mut self.state;\\n            if let Some(b) = st.statics.destroy(&mut st.physics, r) {\\n                debris.push((b.center(), b.half(), b.color));\\n            }\\n        }\\n        for (c, half, color) in debris {\\n            let n = 3 + self.state.rng.below(3);\\n            for _ in 0..n {\\n                let rng = &mut self.state.rng;\\n                let off = Vec3::new(rng.range(-half.x, half.x), rng.range(-half.y, half.y), rng.range(-half.z, half.z));\\n770→                let size = Vec3::new(rng.range(0.08, 0.2), rng.range(0.06, 0.14), rng.range(0.08, 0.2));\\n                let out = (c + off - pos).normalize_or(Vec3::Y);\\n                let vel = out * rng.range(2.0, 6.0) + Vec3::Y * rng.range(1.0, 4.0);\\n                let life = (rng.range(2.5, 4.0) * self.config.tick_rate.hz() as f32) as u32;\\n                let rot = Quat::from_euler(glam::EulerRot::XYZ, rng.range(0.0, 3.0), rng.range(0.0, 3.0), 0.0);\\n                let id = self.spawn(\\n                    Spawn::new(\\\"~debris\\\", c + off)\\n                        .visual(Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: size }, color))\\n                        .body(BodyKind::Dynamic)\\n                        .rot(rot),\\n780→                );\\n                if let Some(e) = self.state.entities.get_mut(id) {\\n                    e.lifetime = Some(life);\\n                    if let Some(b) = e.body.and_then(|h| self.state.physics.bodies.get_mut(h)) {\\n                        b.set_linvel(vel, true);\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        // Push props and characters.\\n790→        let push = self.config.bombs.push;\\n        let reach = radius * 2.5;\\n        for e in self.state.entities.map.values_mut() {\\n            let d = e.pos - pos;\\n            let dist = d.length();\\n            if dist > reach || e.bomb.is_some() {\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            let fall = 1.0 - dist / reach;\\n            let dir = (d + Vec3::Y * 0.5).normalize_or(Vec3::Y);\\n800→            if let Some(h) = e.soft.as_ref().and_then(|s| s.handle) {\\n                // Soft bodies: every particle in reach gets kicked away from the blast.\\n                if let Some(sb) = self.state.physics.soft_bodies.get_mut(h) {\\n                    let pv: Vec<(Vec3, Vec3)> = sb.particle_positions().zip(sb.particle_velocities()).collect();\\n                    for (i, (p, v)) in pv.into_iter().enumerate() {\\n                        let d = p - pos;\\n                        let f = 1.0 - d.length() / reach;\\n                        if f > 0.0 {\\n                            sb.set_particle_velocity(i, v + (d + Vec3::Y * 0.5).normalize_or(Vec3::Y) * push * f);\\n                        }\\n810→                    }\\n                }\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            if let Some(ch) = &mut e.character {\\n                ch.impulse += dir * push * fall;\\n                ch.stun = ch.stun.max(0.25 * fall);\\n                ch.hang = None;\\n                ch.anim.hit(dir, 0.5 + 1.5 * fall);\\n            } else if let Some(b) = e.body.and_then(|h| self.state.physics.bodies.get_mut(h)) {\\n820→                if b.is_dynamic() {\\n                    let m = b.mass();\\n                    b.apply_impulse(dir * push * fall * m, true);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.state.physics.wake_near(pos, reach + 4.0);\\n        events.push(SimEvent::Explosion { pos, radius });\\n    }\\n\\n830→    /// Runs `n` ticks with the same input.\\n    pub fn run(&mut self, n: u64, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        for _ in 0..n {\\n            self.step(input);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Takes the events produced since the last call.\\n    pub fn drain_events(&mut self) -> Vec<SimEvent> {\\n        std::mem::take(&mut self.events)\\n840→    }\\n\\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------ time travel\\n\\n    /// Shows the world as it was at `target` (restore + re-simulate). The recorded future is\\n    /// kept until `commit_rewind`, so scrubbing forward again works.\\n    pub fn rewind_to(&mut self, target: u64) -> bool {\\n        let Some(snap) = self.history.snapshots.iter().rev().find(|s| s.tick <= target).cloned() else { return false };\\n        self.restore(snap);\\n        self.replaying = true;\",\"content_concise\":\"670→\\n        // Projectiles.\\n        if !self.state.projectiles.list.is_empty() {\\n            let hitbox = self.config.movement.hitbox;\\n            let player = self.state.player;\\n            let targets: Vec<Target> = self\\n                .state\\n                .entities\\n                .iter()\\n                .filter_map(|e| {\\n680→                    let c = e.character.as_ref()?;\\n                    let radius = if Some(e.id) == player { hitbox } else { RADIUS };\\n                    Some(Target { id: e.id, feet: e.pos - Vec3::Y * c.height() * 0.5, height: c.height(), radius })\\n                })\\n                .collect();\\n            let enemies: Vec<crate::projectile::Enemy> = self\\n                .state\\n                .entities\\n                .iter()\\n                .filter(|e| e.health.is_some())\\n690→                .map(|e| crate::projectile::Enemy {\\n                    id: e.id,\\n                    center: e.pos,\\n                    radius: e.visual.as_ref().map(|v| v.shape.half_extents().max_element()).unwrap_or(0.5),\\n                })\\n                .collect();\\n            let physics = &self.state.physics;\\n            let entities = &self.state.entities;\\n            let out = self.state.projectiles.step(dt, &targets, &enemies, |from, dir, len, owner| {\\n                let ignore = owner.and_then(|id| entities.get(id)).and_then(|e| e.body);\\n700→                crate::projectile::static_blocked(physics, from, dir, len, ignore)\\n            });\\n            for (id, at, dir, kb) in out.hits {\\n                self.hit_character(id, at, dir, kb, false, &mut events);\\n            }\\n            for (id, at, dmg) in out.damage {\\n                self.damage(id, at, dmg, &mut events);\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n710→        self.game_post(dt, raw_dt, &mut events);\\n        self.play_post(dt, &mut events);\\n        self.game_travel(&mut events);\\n\\n        if let Some(p) = self.player() {\\n            self.state.focus = p.pos;\\n        }\\n        self.update_zones(&mut events);\\n        self.measure_feel(input);\\n        self.update_room_tracking(&mut events);\\n720→        if self.state.tick.is_multiple_of(15) {\\n            self.update_streaming(2);\\n        }\\n        self.state.tick += 1;\\n        if !self.replaying {\\n            self.events.extend(events);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn measure_feel(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n730→        let Some(e) = self.player() else { return };\\n        let Some(ch) = e.character.as_ref() else { return };\\n        let (vel, grounded, feet) =\\n            (ch.vel, ch.grounded || ch.climbing.is_some() || ch.hang.is_some(), e.pos - Vec3::Y * ch.height() * 0.5);\\n        let dt = self.dt();\\n        let tick = self.state.tick;\\n        self.state.feel.update(tick, dt, input.move_dir, vel, feet, grounded);\\n    }\\n\\n    fn throw_bomb(&mut self, from: Vec3, vel: Vec3, owner: EntityId) {\\n740→        let mut v = Visual::new(Shape::Sphere { radius: 0.2 }, Color::hex(\\\"#2b2d35\\\"));\\n        v.look = Look::Lit;\\n        let id = self.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"bomb\\\", from).visual(v).body(BodyKind::Dynamic).restitution(0.15));\\n        if let Some(e) = self.state.entities.get_mut(id) {\\n            e.bomb = Some(Bomb { fuse: self.config.bombs.fuse, radius: self.config.bombs.radius, owner: Some(owner) });\\n            if let Some(b) = e.body.and_then(|h| self.state.physics.bodies.get_mut(h)) {\\n                b.set_linvel(vel, true);\\n                b.enable_ccd(true);\\n            }\\n        }\\n750→    }\\n\\n    /// Removes destructible blocks in the radius, throws debris and pushes things away.\\n    pub fn explode(&mut self, pos: Vec3, radius: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n        let hit = self.state.statics.blocks_in_sphere(pos, radius);\\n        let mut debris = Vec::new();\\n        for r in hit {\\n            if !self.state.statics.get(r).is_some_and(|b| b.has(block_flags::DESTRUCTIBLE)) {\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n760→            let st = &mut self.state;\\n            if let Some(b) = st.statics.destroy(&mut st.physics, r) {\\n                debris.push((b.center(), b.half(), b.color));\\n            }\\n        }\\n        for (c, half, color) in debris {\\n            let n = 3 + self.state.rng.below(3);\\n            for _ in 0..n {\\n                let rng = &mut self.state.rng;\\n                let off = Vec3::new(rng.range(-half.x, half.x), rng.range(-half.y, half.y), rng.range(-half.z, half.z));\\n770→                let size = Vec3::new(rng.range(0.08, 0.2), rng.range(0.06, 0.14), rng.range(0.08, 0.2));\\n                let out = (c + off - pos).normalize_or(Vec3::Y);\\n                let vel = out * rng.range(2.0, 6.0) + Vec3::Y * rng.range(1.0, 4.0);\\n                let life = (rng.range(2.5, 4.0) * self.config.tick_rate.hz() as f32) as u32;\\n                let rot = Quat::from_euler(glam::EulerRot::XYZ, rng.range(0.0, 3.0), rng.range(0.0, 3.0), 0.0);\\n                let id = self.spawn(\\n                    Spawn::new(\\\"~debris\\\", c + off)\\n                        .visual(Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: size }, color))\\n                        .body(BodyKind::Dynamic)\\n                        .rot(rot),\\n780→                );\\n                if let Some(e) = self.state.entities.get_mut(id) {\\n                    e.lifetime = Some(life);\\n                    if let Some(b) = e.body.and_then(|h| self.state.physics.bodies.get_mut(h)) {\\n                        b.set_linvel(vel, true);\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        // Push props and characters.\\n790→        let push = self.config.bombs.push;\\n        let reach = radius * 2.5;\\n        for e in self.state.entities.map.values_mut() {\\n            let d = e.pos - pos;\\n            let dist = d.length();\\n            if dist > reach || e.bomb.is_some() {\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            let fall = 1.0 - dist / reach;\\n            let dir = (d + Vec3::Y * 0.5).normalize_or(Vec3::Y);\\n800→            if let Some(h) = e.soft.as_ref().and_then(|s| s.handle) {\\n                // Soft bodies: every particle in reach gets kicked away from the blast.\\n                if let Some(sb) = self.state.physics.soft_bodies.get_mut(h) {\\n                    let pv: Vec<(Vec3, Vec3)> = sb.particle_positions().zip(sb.particle_velocities()).collect();\\n                    for (i, (p, v)) in pv.into_iter().enumerate() {\\n                        let d = p - pos;\\n                        let f = 1.0 - d.length() / reach;\\n                        if f > 0.0 {\\n                            sb.set_particle_velocity(i, v + (d + Vec3::Y * 0.5).normalize_or(Vec3::Y) * push * f);\\n                        }\\n810→                    }\\n                }\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            if let Some(ch) = &mut e.character {\\n                ch.impulse += dir * push * fall;\\n                ch.stun = ch.stun.max(0.25 * fall);\\n                ch.hang = None;\\n                ch.anim.hit(dir, 0.5 + 1.5 * fall);\\n            } else if let Some(b) = e.body.and_then(|h| self.state.physics.bodies.get_mut(h)) {\\n820→                if b.is_dynamic() {\\n                    let m = b.mass();\\n                    b.apply_impulse(dir * push * fall * m, true);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.state.physics.wake_near(pos, reach + 4.0);\\n        events.push(SimEvent::Explosion { pos, radius });\\n    }\\n\\n830→    /// Runs `n` ticks with the same input.\\n    pub fn run(&mut self, n: u64, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        for _ in 0..n {\\n            self.step(input);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Takes the events produced since the last call.\\n    pub fn drain_events(&mut self) -> Vec<SimEvent> {\\n        std::mem::take(&mut self.events)\\n840→    }\\n\\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------ time travel\\n\\n    /// Shows the world as it was at `target` (restore + re-simulate). The recorded future is\\n    /// kept until `commit_rewind`, so scrubbing forward again works.\\n    pub fn rewind_to(&mut self, target: u64) -> bool {\\n        let Some(snap) = self.history.snapshots.iter().rev().find(|s| s.tick <= target).cloned() else { return false };\\n        self.restore(snap);\\n        self.replaying = true;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs\",\"offset\":670,\"limit\":180,\"raw_output\":\"\\n        // Projectiles.\\n        if !self.state.projectiles.list.is_empty() {\\n            let hitbox = self.config.movement.hitbox;\\n            let player = self.state.player;\\n            let targets: Vec<Target> = self\\n                .state\\n                .entities\\n                .iter()\\n                .filter_map(|e| {\\n                    let c = e.character.as_ref()?;\\n                    let radius = if Some(e.id) == player { hitbox } else { RADIUS };\\n                    Some(Target { id: e.id, feet: e.pos - Vec3::Y 