9,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":3,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_view/src/fx.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":439,\"content\":\"        E::Splash { pos } => out.push(with(\\\"fountain\\\", *pos + Vec3::Y * 0.2, 40, &|b| {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":728,\"content\":\"            if let SimEvent::Splash { pos } = e {\"},{\"line_number\":751,\"content\":\"                SimEvent::Splash { pos } => self.effects.push(Effect {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"3f344038-3054-4064-8432-819b2d60f19e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_18","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"t_input constructs InputFrame without `..`.\n\nI'll use `..Default::default()` when updating structs and add lean parsing. I'm writing Rust directly instead of Python. The plan has four phases: engine seams, game simulation, UI/audio/app/web, and art/assets/animations.\n\nPhase E covers HTML, browser, hub, and captures. The game state machine must let the bot complete quickly while still playing every event. A full playthrough needs roughly 70,000 ticks. Physics on a small island should finish in about one to two minutes per seed.\n\nI will not time-scale the official bot path. Events must run at normal speed to satisfy the playthrough requirement.\n\nEvent scoring will reward active play with two or more stars and idle behavior with zero. I will implement real mechanics and guide bots accordingly.\n\nCore balance is the foundation. I will test feel targets numerically before building anything else. At 60 Hz, stiffness 40, damping 8.5, reach 0.92, and tip_time 0.35 should give full stick about 90% reach in 0.4 seconds with roughly 5% overshoot. Release settles in about 0.45 seconds.\n\nIdle radius stays near 0.05 and at most 0.08. Full lean with no wind does not tip; a gust does. I will verify the physics in Python before porting to Rust.\n\nWobble can push the target lean to 1.04, which risks tipping on its own. The plan requires that a held full lean never tips by itself; only a gust should do so. I need to verify whether brief excursions past 1.0 are short enough to avoid triggering tip_time.\n\nRules will be a serde-loaded struct with defaults so missing fields do not break the game. The full flow state enum covers every screen from Title through Credits, including GuestSlot, Name, Look, Intro, Day, Check, EventCard, Countdown, Playing, Result, Sleep, BigStand, and several extras.\n\nThe flow state enum now includes PlayTogether, PassPad, Podium, Medley, and TouchCard. Touch-only mode will be set at boot from the host as a boolean flag so tests can trigger it. The Attract sequence starts after 600 idle ticks on the title screen. Pre-game menus such as Settings and About also count toward that idle timeout.\n\nA demo flag will let the bot play without tips or saving. The save file stores version, settings, four guest slots, and the last played day. Balance age is computed from skill across stillness, targets, blind spots, and steps, then clamped between 18 and 99. Star thresholds are 400, 650, and 850 for general events, and 25, 40, and 55 seconds for the Plank. Minutes are one for a first clear and one for repeats.\n\nDay goals are 3, 5, 7, and 9 minutes. Two stars per event clears the first three days. A middling skill of 0.5 yields an age of about 34 by day five, so the checkout ending triggers.\n\nThe bot should play well enough to keep skill at 0.2 above the 40 age floor. Final Balance Age is morning age minus final score divided by 100, capped at a 10-point reduction. Checkout will use this final age so a close call can still allow departure.\n\nBoth endings will set the outcome to \"Won\". A status field will distinguish a checkout from an extended stay.\n\nA set will track every event played at least once. Five stamps are earned one per day. The under-sixty-minute target applies to resort minutes, not simulation time. A bot that plays each event once with two or three stars should stay well under sixty resort minutes. Both metrics will be recorded and asserted.\n\nIdle playthroughs will fail events by design. Breathing misses the guide, squats lack reps, planks flop immediately, and paddling misses gates. Competent bots will score two stars.\n\nA test will seed the RNG and compare random input against bot performance to ensure the bot scores higher. Medley runs will be deterministic by reseeding from the boot seed, so identical inputs produce identical scores. Play Together tests will drive the flow with bot input for each guest and assert the podium is reached. Ghosts are only drawn or considered when their area matches, and a test will verify this filter. The attract sequence starts after 600 idle ticks; any input exits it without saving.\n\nA test will step empty input 600 times on the title screen to trigger the attract sequence, then press a key to exit and verify the save file remains unchanged. Pause freezes the world by returning early after the pre-tick phase but before physics, so the player position stays fixed from that tick onward.\n\nResuming from pause clears the paused flag and resumes physics normally. A dev slider will adjust stiffness, assert balance uses the new value, and reset to restore the original. Music gain is tested by rendering a buffer at 0.10 and comparing RMS to full scale; the tanh nonlinearity means the result is only approximately one-tenth of the full-range output.\n\nBus gain will be applied as multipliers so quiet audio stays linear and the 0.10 music test can verify a ratio near one-tenth. UI text sizing will use a draw helper that enforces body at least 34 times the viewport scale and titles at least 64 times the scale, with tests calling that helper directly. A content lint script will scan script.toml for TODOs, placeholders, weight, BMI, diet, and Nintendo names. Snapshot, rewind, and replay features will follow the games.rs test pattern.\n\nI need to read the games.rs tests and study CameraCue, build_standalone_room, the clips API, GearLook, and player puppet setup. I will create simple room TOML files so the character stands on a deck, add art props as JSON, and design captures that look like a beach game with a figure and puck. I also need to check an example prop JSON, the clips format, and the app.rs key handler region to know how to gate the new features. Because app.rs is large, I will make minimal hooks.\n\nI will add a `fit_active` helper to detect when the HUD is in fit mode and route keys differently. I am reading the app frame loop, input poll, egui version, font setup, and build flags before writing code. Props will use ASSET_STUDIO format-2 JSON.\n\nAnimations will be defined in fit.json with the planned poses plus extras. Rooms will be written as TOML using the plan's view recipe.\n\nThe bot will use Schedule fast-travel to start events rather than pathfinding, which is more reliable for tests. The player can still walk normally.\n\nThe bot's opening flow is: Title → New Stay → Slot 0 → Name → Look → Intro (mashing confirm to skip dialogue) → Morning check.\n\nThe bot will confirm through the morning check dialogue and play the event. Afterward it opens the schedule, selects the first available event, confirms the card, and plays until the day goal is met. Days repeat until day five. On day five the Big Stand auto-offers after the morning check and the bot confirms. If the balance age is forty or below the bot chooses checkout.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-90c40be9-f6f4-42d8-bf61-6fc288859c72-42","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"scene|__gameBoot|webgpu","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src","glob":"*.rs","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-90c40be9-f6f4-42d8-bf61-6fc288859c72-43","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"--scene|--single-file|--title","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/scripts/build-web.sh"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-90c40be9-f6f4-42d8-bf61-6fc288859c72-44","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-90c40be9-f6f4-42d8-bf61-6fc288859c72-45","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_view/src/fx.rs","offset":400,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-90c40be9-f6f4-42d8-bf61-6fc288859c72-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs","offset":700,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3859,"output_tokens":3887,"cache_read_input_tokens":99328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"24055859-5f22-48de-aa27-5b064d06b04f"}
