{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_28","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The architecture is solid. I am ready to write code.\n\nI am planning the file changes in batches. The engine needs updates to input, game registration, simulation, frame rendering, puppet physics, and audio.\n\nUI, app, tools, and web hub files are also on the list. Game events will be grouped into modules for clarity while still matching the required per-event structure.\n\nDialogue will be brief to keep the bot from getting stuck. The full Pip and coach scripts live in script.toml and are selected by context. The bot only needs to advance whatever text is currently visible. Text speed will default to fast so the bot can hold confirm and skip through lines quickly.\n\nBot timing is now concrete. One press completes a line mid-typing; the next advances it. The bot will press every two ticks. A full playthrough of roughly twenty lines takes about twenty seconds. The countdown sequence adds thirty-nine seconds across thirteen events.\n\nThe morning check will last about 40 to 50 seconds. Active tests total roughly 34 seconds, with the bot finishing each target well under the five-second limit.\n\nThe age formula will use the bot's metrics. Lower mean distance from center yields a higher stillness score. Faster target completion improves the targets score. Eyes-closed and step-timing errors map to their own metrics.\n\nThe step metric will use a 0.15 error clamp. Bot skill should land near 0.85 or higher.\n\nTotal test runtime is roughly 1,100 seconds, or about 66,000 ticks. The full suite spans around 780,000 ticks across all seeds and events. That is lengthy but acceptable for a complete test run.\n\nThe suite is heavier than the one-second target for starter games, but it should still finish in about thirty to ninety seconds. Each event can run directly without full island physics if its scene is small. A million ticks across all seeds and events is acceptable for a single test command. Idle tests will be shorter if events fail early.\n\nIdle events run their full duration even when the bot does nothing, because they lack fail states. The idle pose parade lasts sixty seconds, and thirteen events across five seeds total roughly seven hundred fifteen seconds of idle time.\n\nThe combined test suite should finish in about forty-five seconds at ten thousand ticks per second. I will keep physics scenes small rather than adding a test mode. Direct event starts can use one small room, while the full playthrough still builds all nine rooms.\n\nCargo test spawns one thread per CPU by default, which risks exhausting RAM when many physics simulations run in parallel. I will document a `tests/run.sh` script that limits threads to two or three so the suite stays safe on a 20GB machine.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40233cf9-412f-4b58-9657-82f6e6b2e4af-73","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub fn range|pub fn f32|pub fn below|pub struct Rng","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src","glob":"*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40233cf9-412f-4b58-9657-82f6e6b2e4af-74","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/Cargo.toml","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40233cf9-412f-4b58-9657-82f6e6b2e4af-75","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_ui/Cargo.toml"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40233cf9-412f-4b58-9657-82f6e6b2e4af-76","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112