t;\\n        self.crown = q * self.crown;\\n        self.weapon = q * self.weapon;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// `st` held on its animation frame when the look animates in steps (`anim_fps`).\\nfn stepped(def: &PuppetDef, st: &PuppetState) -> PuppetState {\\n    let mut st = *st;\\n    if def.anim_fps > 0.5 {\\n        // Stepped animation: hold poses between discrete animation frames.\\n        let step = 1.0 / def.anim_fps;\\n        let q = (st.time / step).floor() * step;\\n        let dt = st.time - q;\\n        st.phase = (st.phase - dt * st.speed / (def.stride * def.scale).max(0.1)).rem_euclid(1.0);\\n        st.clip_t -= dt * if st.clip_speed > 0.0 { st.clip_speed } else { 1.0 };\\n    }\\n    st\\n}\\n\\n/// A biped's skeleton for this frame, in character space (feet at the origin, facing +z): the\\n/// procedural pose with the clips it plays laid over it, as `pose` dresses it. An imported\\n/// figure (`crate::figure`) is posed from it.\\npub fn biped_skel(def: &PuppetDef, st: &PuppetState) -> Skel {\\n    let st = stepped(def, st);\\n\",\"total_lines\":1632}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"61d76cc8-1a31-4fec-bfb5-e878b11914ab"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_32","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I understand the goal and am ready to begin.\n\nStarting implementation of the game core and engine seam edits. Designing the FitGame struct with Clone, Serialize, and Deserialize derives to support serde. Considering whether script text should be included in save state or reloaded from disk.\n\nScript text will be loaded lazily from a parsed OnceLock to avoid storing it in snapshots. The game struct will hold flow, active guest, and four slots. Save state is kept separate from simulation state.\n\nThe FitGame struct now includes settings, balance core, event state, check state, finale, medley, together, attract, dialog, UI model, dev state, and runtime flags such as paused, world time, idle ticks, and device configuration.\n\nThe FitGame struct now includes save_serial, outcome, played events, and minutes_banked_today.\n\nUiFrame will live in pav_core so HudFrame can hold it without depending on pav_ui. It stores screen, title, dialogue lines, and UI items.\n\nUiFrame now includes focus, prompts, puck state, score, timer, stars, device flags, toast messages, and time metadata. UiItem defines selectable UI elements with id, label, kind, value, and bounds.\n\nThe drawer will assign rectangles and return hover or click feedback. Prompts will render as both shapes and text labels so headless tests can read glyphs like \"Cross\", \"Circle\", \"A\", \"B\", \"Space\", \"Esc\", and \"LMB\" at 10-foot size.\n\nThe draw helper will enforce font sizes by clamping body text to 34 times scale and titles to 64 times scale. Tests will call `fit_ui::sizes(1920, 1080)` and assert the draw function uses these constants.\n\nAbout page data is read from an `about_json` string set at boot. Tests may verify this content through the game's embedded copy or the static HTML file.\n\nThe exit interview is written at the end of a session and copied into the about-data block by tools/build.sh. During development, a placeholder about-data will be used and replaced at finish. The About screen renders pages from that JSON.\n\nThe simulation will embed a default About page that matches the HTML placeholder. The app can overwrite it from `__gameBoot.about` at boot.\n\nA JSON status object will expose tick, flow, outcome, day, stamps, minutes, played events, age, paused state, attract mode, music volume, world time, and hub data. The JavaScript side expects to parse `window.__gameStatus` and read its `hub` field.\n\nThe application writes the status JSON each frame from `hud.status`. A `SaveFile` struct will hold version, settings, guest slots, and last day. The game will expose `export_save()` and `import_save()` methods. The application will persist saves to localStorage whenever `save_serial` changes. Tests will verify round-trip export and import. The `Guest` struct stores name, skin, outfit, and clothing items.\n\nGuest state now tracks day, minutes, stars, best scores, ghost runs, age history, flipflop bitmask, unlocks, and completion flags. GhostRun records lean, position, and clip samples over time for replay beside the player.\n\nGhost replay will use a filter function to match runs by area. Recording every tick for ninety seconds yields five thousand four hundred samples, which is acceptable.\n\nThe Together state tracks guest count, player turns, scores, and a phase enum covering Setup, Pass, Playing, and Podium. Medley events include paddle, tide, and cannonball.\n\nHub mode starts the flow at medley with no title screen. The hub flag is set from build arguments when rest is medley and a boot flag is present. Tests can launch this directly via `Sim::new(\"fit/medley\", seed)`.\n\nThe browser sets `boot.scene` to `fit/medley` before the WASM module loads, because the session script sits in the HTML head ahead of the game script. The build function receives this scene string and skips the title screen when it is medley. Solo medley can also start this way.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8bfc188c-a844-4526-9be0-e93e0f7f2dcc-84","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn load|scene:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/settings.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8bfc188c-a844-4526-9be0-e93e0f7f2dcc-85","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/settings.rs","limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1710,"output_tokens":2296,"cache_read_input_tokens":139904,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"672af8bd-315f-4bfc-aaea-f7fc6b99ba68"}
