{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_46","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a clear plan and am starting to write code.\n\nI'll write the Rust game directly with the Write tool. The engine will be a single compilation unit. I'm designing a Flow enum for serialization and an EventKind enum to hold structs with update, bot, and score methods. This avoids large match statements.\n\nI'm refining the architecture. An Activity enum will hold each pose and breathing exercise, each with a tick method that updates state through a lean TickCtx. The game phase will cycle from Card to Count to Play to Result. Starting at Card would leave the bot idle forever, so I'll begin at Count instead.\n\nI'll auto-start the game after a brief card phase so idle input still reaches play and result. The bot confirms immediately to avoid blocking. I'm also checking how the full game bot timing will work.\n\nI estimated the full game duration at roughly 52 seconds. I'm now working out the freeze and menu logic: gameplay updates will happen in post(), while menu input is handled in pre(). When frozen, post() skips entirely, so event timers freeze correctly without running during pause.\n\nI realized the post() method cannot receive player input directly, so I will stash it in self.last_input during pre(). Menu and pause logic will run in pre(), while gameplay updates in post() will skip when paused or frozen.\n\nI confirmed that attract mode must not freeze the world, since it updates events in post(). The title screen freezes the simulation to keep the island sweep still, but the camera sweep uses real time so it animates correctly in the window.\n\nI'm now mapping each game state to whether the world should freeze. Island free time and event play remain unfrozen so the player can move and events update in post(). Morning check also stays unfrozen because it needs post() to run. Dialogue, countdown, and result screens can freeze; text advances in pre() while the pose holds in post().","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2c858850-246e-46db-b35d-807951b6873a-107","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn game_time_scale|time_scale","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":850,"output_tokens":1187,"cache_read_input_tokens":170496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"0e52c824-dade-414a-8871-d7e59526e815"}
