{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b2069e18-d4b7-4c81-8c9c-20c18cd299ed-111","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Runs the simulation at a fixed tick rate: on its own thread natively, and stepped from the\\n//! frame loop in the browser (no threads there). The renderer never waits for it: it reads the\\n//! two most recent frames and interpolates between them.\\n\\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\\nuse std::time::Duration;\\n\\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, RenderFrame, Sim, SimEvent};\\nuse web_time::Instant;\\n10→\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\ntype Job = Box<dyn FnOnce(&mut Sim) + Send>;\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nenum Cmd {\\n    Run(Job),\\n    Quit,\\n}\\n\\n20→#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct TimeControl {\\n    pub paused: bool,\\n    /// Simulation speed multiplier (0.05 .. 8).\\n    pub speed: f32,\\n    /// Ticks to advance while paused.\\n    pub step_requests: u32,\\n    /// Holding the rewind button.\\n    pub rewinding: bool,\\n    /// Ticks travelled back per tick while rewinding.\\n30→    pub rewind_speed: u32,\\n    /// Jump to this tick (timeline scrubbing), keeping the future until play resumes.\\n    pub scrub: Option<u64>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for TimeControl {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self { paused: false, speed: 1.0, step_requests: 0, rewinding: false, rewind_speed: 1, scrub: None }\\n    }\\n}\\n40→\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct SimStats {\\n    /// Measured ticks per second of wall time.\\n    pub tps: f32,\\n    /// Average CPU time per tick (ms).\\n    pub tick_ms: f32,\\n    pub tick: u64,\\n    pub entities: usize,\\n    /// Rewind range available (ticks).\\n50→    pub oldest: u64,\\n    pub newest: u64,\\n    pub history_mb: f32,\\n    pub rewound: bool,\\n}\\n\\npub struct FramePair {\\n    pub prev: Arc<RenderFrame>,\\n    pub curr: Arc<RenderFrame>,\\n    /// When `curr` became current (wall clock).\\n60→    pub curr_at: Instant,\\n    /// Wall-clock length of one tick at the current speed.\\n    pub tick_wall: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub struct Shared {\\n    pub frames: Mutex<FramePair>,\\n    pub input: Mutex<InputFrame>,\\n    pub control: Mutex<TimeControl>,\\n    pub stats: Mutex<SimStats>,\\n70→    pub crashed: Mutex<Option<String>>,\\n    /// Events for sound and effects, drained by the render thread.\\n    pub events: Mutex<Vec<SimEvent>>,\\n    /// When the input that is waiting for the next tick was pressed (latency measurement).\\n    pub input_stamp: Mutex<Option<Instant>>,\\n    /// (pressed, consumed by a tick, that tick's number) for the latest measured press.\\n    pub latency_probe: Mutex<Option<(Instant, Instant, u64)>>,\\n    /// Menu commands waiting for a tick (one rides along with each tick's input).\\n    pub cmds: Mutex<std::collections::VecDeque<pav_core::arpg::GameCmd>>,\\n}\\n80→\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Runs the simulation at a fixed tick rate: on its own thread natively, and stepped from the\\n//! frame loop in the browser (no threads there). The renderer never waits for it: it reads the\\n//! two most recent frames and interpolates between them.\\n\\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\\nuse std::time::Duration;\\n\\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, RenderFrame, Sim, SimEvent};\\nuse web_time::Instant;\\n10→\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\ntype Job = Box<dyn FnOnce(&mut Sim) + Send>;\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nenum Cmd {\\n    Run(Job),\\n    Quit,\\n}\\n\\n20→#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct TimeControl {\\n    pub paused: bool,\\n    /// Simulation speed multiplier (0.05 .. 8).\\n    pub speed: f32,\\n    /// Ticks to advance while paused.\\n    pub step_requests: u32,\\n    /// Holding the rewind button.\\n    pub rewinding: bool,\\n    /// Ticks travelled back per tick while rewinding.\\n30→    pub rewind_speed: u32,\\n    /// Jump to this tick (timeline scrubbing), keeping the future until play resumes.\\n    pub scrub: Option<u64>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for TimeControl {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self { paused: false, speed: 1.0, step_requests: 0, rewinding: false, rewind_speed: 1, scrub: None }\\n    }\\n}\\n40→\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct SimStats {\\n    /// Measured ticks per second of wall time.\\n    pub tps: f32,\\n    /// Average CPU time per tick (ms).\\n    pub tick_ms: f32,\\n    pub tick: u64,\\n    pub entities: usize,\\n    /// Rewind range available (ticks).\\n50→    pub oldest: u64,\\n    pub newest: u64,\\n    pub history_mb: f32,\\n    pub rewound: bool,\\n}\\n\\npub struct FramePair {\\n    pub prev: Arc<RenderFrame>,\\n    pub curr: Arc<RenderFrame>,\\n    /// When `curr` became current (wall clock).\\n60→    pub curr_at: Instant,\\n    /// Wall-clock length of one tick at the current speed.\\n    pub tick_wall: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub struct Shared {\\n    pub frames: Mutex<FramePair>,\\n    pub input: Mutex<InputFrame>,\\n    pub control: Mutex<TimeControl>,\\n    pub stats: Mutex<SimStats>,\\n70→    pub crashed: Mutex<Option<String>>,\\n    /// Events for sound and effects, drained by the render thread.\\n    pub events: Mutex<Vec<SimEvent>>,\\n    /// When the input that is waiting for the next tick was pressed (latency measurement).\\n    pub input_stamp: Mutex<Option<Instant>>,\\n    /// (pressed, consumed by a tick, that tick's number) for the latest measured press.\\n    pub latency_probe: Mutex<Option<(Instant, Instant, u64)>>,\\n    /// Menu commands waiting for a tick (one rides along with each tick's input).\\n    pub cmds: Mutex<std::collections::VecDeque<pav_core::arpg::GameCmd>>,\\n}\\n80→\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"//! Runs the simulation at a fixed tick rate: on its own thread natively, and stepped from the\\n//! frame loop in the browser (no threads there). The renderer never waits for it: it reads the\\n//! two most recent frames and interpolates between them.\\n\\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\\nuse std::time::Duration;\\n\\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, RenderFrame, Sim, SimEvent};\\nuse web_time::Instant;\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\ntype Job = Box<dyn FnOnce(&mut Sim) + Send>;\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nenum Cmd {\\n    Run(Job),\\n    Quit,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct TimeControl {\\n    pub paused: bool,\\n    /// Simulation speed multiplier (0.05 .. 8).\\n    pub speed: f32,\\n    /// Ticks to advance while paused.\\n    pub step_requests: u32,\\n    /// Holding the rewind button.\\n    pub rewinding: bool,\\n    /// Ticks travelled back per tick while rewinding.\\n    pub rewind_speed: u32,\\n    /// Jump to this tick (timeline scrubbing), keeping the future until play resumes.\\n    pub scrub: Option<u64>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for TimeControl {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self { paused: false, speed: 1.0, step_requests: 0, rewinding: false, rewind_speed: 1, scrub: None }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct SimStats {\\n    /// Measured ticks per second of wall time.\\n    pub tps: f32,\\n    /// Average CPU time per tick (ms).\\n    pub tick_ms: f32,\\n    pub tick: u64,\\n    pub entities: usize,\\n    /// Rewind range available (ticks).\\n    pub oldest: u64,\\n    pub newest: u64,\\n    pub history_mb: f32,\\n    pub rewound: bool,\\n}\\n\\npub struct FramePair {\\n    pub prev: Arc<RenderFrame>,\\n    pub curr: Arc<RenderFrame>,\\n    /// When `curr` became current (wall clock).\\n    pub curr_at: Instant,\\n    /// Wall-clock length of one tick at the current speed.\\n    pub tick_wall: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub struct Shared {\\n    pub frames: Mutex<FramePair>,\\n    pub input: Mutex<InputFrame>,\\n    pub control: Mutex<TimeControl>,\\n    pub stats: Mutex<SimStats>,\\n    pub crashed: Mutex<Option<String>>,\\n    /// Events for sound and effects, drained by the render thread.\\n    pub events: Mutex<Vec<SimEvent>>,\\n    /// When the input that is waiting for the next tick was pressed (latency measurement).\\n    pub input_stamp: Mutex<Option<Instant>>,\\n    /// (pressed, consumed by a tick, that tick's number) for the latest measured press.\\n    pub latency_probe: Mutex<Option<(Instant, Instant, u64)>>,\\n    /// Menu commands waiting for a tick (one rides along with each tick's input).\\n    pub cmds: Mutex<std::collections::VecDeque<pav_core::arpg::GameCmd>>,\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":427}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"50bdf255-3704-4714-aa50-dd7598bdc304"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_51","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The app already has TimeControl with speed.\n\nDev mode will store time_scale on the game and multiply game dt. The app can read this value each frame to set TimeControl.speed, slowing the world too. Sim tests will verify Rules.stiffness changes via the dev slider.\n\nThe pause menu will use frozen() instead of TimeControl.paused. A dev.pause flag will freeze the simulation. Single-step mode will decrement a dev.step_request counter in pre() to unfreeze one tick, then restore frozen() for the next frame.\n\nThe stepping flag is cleared at the end of post. Title screens remain frozen while attract mode runs. The idle counter still increments during frozen pre ticks. A save_serial counter will trigger app-side localStorage writes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1191c4a5-4901-4eb3-8cb9-87b07cf2a956-112","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/params.rs","offset":100,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":883,"output_tokens":703,"cache_read_input_tokens":173952,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"67f41892-cd3a-4696-be38-158e7e82bb3b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1191c4a5-4901-4eb3-8cb9-87b07cf2a956-112","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"100→\\n/// Declares a C-like enum as a `ChoiceParam` with snake_case display names.\\n#[macro_export]\\nmacro_rules! choice_enum {\\n    ($(#[$m:meta])* $vis:vis enum $name:ident { $($(#[$vm:meta])* $var:ident => $label:literal),+ $(,)? }) => {\\n        $(#[$m])*\\n        #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize)]\\n        #[serde(rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\n        $vis enum $name { $($(#[$vm])* $var),+ }\\n        impl $crate::params::ChoiceParam for $name {\\n110→            const NAMES: &'static [&'static str] = &[$($label),+];\\n            fn to_index(self) -> usize { self as usize }\\n            fn from_index(i: usize) -> Self {\\n                const ALL: &[$name] = &[$($name::$var),+];\\n                ALL[i.min(ALL.len() - 1)]\\n            }\\n        }\\n    };\\n}\\n\\n120→struct PathTracker {\\n    stack: Vec<String>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl PathTracker {\\n    fn path(&self, name: &str) -> String {\\n        if self.stack.is_empty() { name.to_string() } else { format!(\\\"{}.{}\\\", self.stack.join(\\\".\\\"), name) }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n130→/// Lists every parameter with its current value.\\npub fn list(t: &mut dyn Tunable) -> Vec<ParamInfo> {\\n    struct L {\\n        p: PathTracker,\\n        out: Vec<ParamInfo>,\\n    }\\n    impl ParamVisitor for L {\\n        fn float(&mut self, name: &str, v: &mut f32, min: f32, max: f32, help: &str) {\\n            self.out.push(ParamInfo {\\n                path: self.p.path(name),\\n140→                kind: ParamKind::Float { min, max },\\n                value: ParamValue::Float(*v as f64),\\n                help: help.into(),\\n            });\\n        }\\n        fn int(&mut self, name: &str, v: &mut i32, min: i32, max: i32, help: &str) {\\n            self.out.push(ParamInfo {\\n                path: self.p.path(name),\\n                kind: ParamKind::Int { min, max },\\n                value: ParamValue::Int(*v as i64),\\n150→                help: help.into(),\\n            });\\n        }\\n        fn bool(&mut self, name: &str, v: &mut bool, help: &str) {\\n            self.out.push(ParamInfo {\\n                path: self.p.path(name),\\n                kind: ParamKind::Bool,\\n                value: ParamValue::Bool(*v),\\n                help: help.into(),\\n            });\\n160→        }\\n        fn choice(&mut self, name: &str, v: &mut usize, options: &[&str], help: &str) {\\n            self.out.push(ParamInfo {\\n                path: self.p.path(name),\\n                kind: ParamKind::Choice { options: options.iter().map(|s| s.to_string()).collect() },\\n                value: ParamValue::Text(options.get(*v).copied().unwrap_or(\\\"?\\\").to_string()),\\n                help: help.into(),\\n            });\\n        }\\n        fn enter(&mut self, name: &str) -> bool {\\n170→            self.p.stack.push(name.into());\\n            true\\n        }\\n        fn exit(&mut self) {\\n            self.p.stack.pop();\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let mut l = L { p: PathTracker { stack: vec![] }, out: vec![] };\\n    t.visit(&mut l);\\n    l.out\",\"content_concise\":\"100→\\n/// Declares a C-like enum as a `ChoiceParam` with snake_case display names.\\n#[macro_export]\\nmacro_rules! choice_enum {\\n    ($(#[$m:meta])* $vis:vis enum $name:ident { $($(#[$vm:meta])* $var:ident => $label:literal),+ $(,)? }) => {\\n        $(#[$m])*\\n        #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize)]\\n        #[serde(rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\n        $vis enum $name { $($(#[$vm])* $var),+ }\\n        impl $crate::params::ChoiceParam for $name {\\n110→            const NAMES: &'static [&'static str] = &[$($label),+];\\n            fn to_index(self) -> usize { self as usize }\\n            fn from_index(i: usize) -> Self {\\n                const ALL: &[$name] = &[$($name::$var),+];\\n                ALL[i.min(ALL.len() - 1)]\\n            }\\n        }\\n    };\\n}\\n\\n120→struct PathTracker {\\n    stack: Vec<String>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl PathTracker {\\n    fn path(&self, name: &str) -> String {\\n        if self.stack.is_empty() { name.to_string() } else { format!(\\\"{}.{}\\\", self.stack.join(\\\".\\\"), name) }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n130→/// Lists every parameter with its current value.\\npub fn list(t: &mut dyn Tunable) -> Vec<ParamInfo> {\\n    struct L {\\n        p: PathTracker,\\n        out: Vec<ParamInfo>,\\n    }\\n    impl ParamVisitor for L {\\n        fn float(&mut self, name: &str, v: &mut f32, min: f32, max: f32, help: &str) {\\n            self.out.push(ParamInfo {\\n                path: self.p.path(name),\\n140→                kind: ParamKind::Float { min, max },\\n                value: ParamValue::Float(*v as f64),\\n                help: help.into(),\\n            });\\n        }\\n        fn int(&mut self, name: &str, v: &mut i32, min: i32, max: i32, help: &str) {\\n            self.out.push(ParamInfo {\\n                path: self.p.path(name),\\n                kind: ParamKind::Int { min, max },\\n                value: ParamValue::Int(*v as i64),\\n150→                help: help.into(),\\n            });\\n        }\\n        fn bool(&mut self, name: &str, v: &mut bool, help: &str) {\\n            self.out.push(ParamInfo {\\n                path: self.p.path(name),\\n                kind: ParamKind::Bool,\\n                value: ParamValue::Bool(*v),\\n                help: help.into(),\\n            });\\n160→        }\\n        fn choice(&mut self, name: &str, v: &mut usize, options: &[&str], help: &str) {\\n            self.out.push(ParamInfo {\\n                path: self.p.path(name),\\n                kind: ParamKind::Choice { options: options.iter().map(|s| s.to_string()).collect() },\\n                value: ParamValue::Text(options.get(*v).copied().unwrap_or(\\\"?\\\").to_string()),\\n                help: help.into(),\\n            });\\n        }\\n        fn enter(&mut self, name: &str) -> bool {\\n170→            self.p.stack.push(name.into());\\n            true\\n        }\\n        fn exit(&mut self) {\\n            self.p.stack.pop();\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let mut l = L { p: PathTracker { stack: vec![] }, out: vec![] };\\n    t.visit(&mut l);\\n    l.out\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/params.rs\",\"offset\":100,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"\\n/// Declares a C-like enum as a `ChoiceParam` with snake_case display names.\\n#[macro_export]\\nmacro_rules! choice_enum {\\n    ($(#[$m:meta])* $vis:vis enum $name:ident { $($(#[$vm:meta])* $var:ident => $label:literal),+ $(,)? }) => {\\n        $(#[$m])*\\n        #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize)]\\n        #[serde(rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\n        $vis enum $name { $($(#[$vm])* $var),+ }\\n        impl $crate::params::ChoiceParam for $name {\\n            const NAMES: &'static [&'static str] = &[$($label),+];\\n            fn to_index(self) -> usize { self as usize }\\n            fn from_index(i: usize) -> Self {\\n                const ALL: &[$name] = &[$($name::$var),+];\\n                ALL[i.min(ALL.len() - 1)]\\n            }\\n        }\\n    };\\n}\\n\\nstruct PathTracker {\\n    stack: Vec<String>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl PathTracker {\\n    fn path(&self, name: &str) -> String {\\n        if self.stack.is_empty() { name.to_string() } else { format!(\\\"{}.{}\\\", self.stack.join(\\\".\\\"), name) }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Lists every parameter with its current value.\\npub fn list(t: &mut dyn Tunable) -> Vec<ParamInfo> {\\n    struct L {\\n        p: PathTracker,\\n        out: Vec<ParamInfo>,\\n    }\\n    impl ParamVisitor for L {\\n        fn float(&mut self, name: &str, v: &mut f32, min: f32, max: f32, help: &str) {\\n            self.out.push(ParamInfo {\\n                path: self.p.path(name),\\n                kind: ParamKind::Float { min, max },\\n                value: ParamValue::Float(*v as f64),\\n                help: help.into(),\\n            });\\n        }\\n        fn int(&mut self, name: &str, v: &mut i32, min: i32, max: i32, help: &str) {\\n            self.out.push(ParamInfo {\\n                path: self.p.path(name),\\n                kind: ParamKind::Int { min, max },\\n                value: ParamValue::Int(*v as i64),\\n                help: help.into(),\\n            });\\n        }\\n        fn bool(&mut self, name: &str, v: &mut bool, help: &str) {\\n            self.out.push(ParamInfo {\\n                path: self.p.path(name),\\n                kind: ParamKind::Bool,\\n                value: ParamValue::Bool(*v),\\n                help: help.into(),\\n            });\\n        }\\n        fn choice(&mut self, name: &str, v: &mut usize, options: &[&str], help: &str) {\\n            self.out.push(ParamInfo {\\n                path: self.p.path(name),\\n                kind: ParamKind::Choice { options: options.iter().map(|s| s.to_string()).collect() },\\n                value: ParamValue::Text(options.get(*v).copied().unwrap_or(\\\"?\\\").to_string()),\\n                help: help.into(),\\n            });\\n        }\\n        fn enter(&mut self, name: &str) -> bool {\\n            self.p.stack.push(name.into());\\n            true\\n        }\\n        fn exit(&mut self) {\\n            self.p.stack.pop();\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let mut l = L { p: PathTracker { stack: vec![] }, out: vec![] };\\n    t.visit(&mut l);\\n    l.out\\n\",\"total_lines\":302}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"2a96d9fa-0e97-4f17-afb0-cef6f5cb1cde"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_52","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will implement Tunable for Rules using params::list and params::set.\n\nThe `visit` method will group parameters into \"core\" and \"breath\" sections using `enter()` and `exit()`. `Tunable`, `params::set`, and `params::list` are all public.\n\nRules will be mutable in the game state. Dev sliders will update them via `params::set`. Reset will restore the original `base_rules` cloned at build time, preserving TOML overrides over Rust defaults. I will patch the engine first, then the game files.\n\nI will update PROGRESS.md as I complete each checklist item. I am using 6 parallel build jobs to stay within memory limits. I also plan to mutate the player's puppet after spawn to set its look.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b2f62526-30fa-45c3-ae75-83a5eefc4086-113","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub puppet:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/character.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b2f62526-30fa-45c3-ae75-83a5eefc4086-114","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/puppet.rs","offset":1,"limit":70}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1680,"output_tokens":728,"cache_read_input_tokens":174720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"c05ded27-b2a1-4c2c-b1e6-c6f6394d5c11"}
