"},{\"line_number\":1000,\"content\":\"        let rewinding = game_input && self.studio_mode == StudioMode::World && self.input.rewind_held();\"},{\"line_number\":1010,\"content\":\"        let game_input = game_input && !studio_active;\"},{\"line_number\":1156,\"content\":\"        let touch_game = curr.game.as_deref().filter(|_| game_input).map(|g| (g, feet, facing));\"},{\"line_number\":1159,\"content\":\"        if game_input {\"},{\"line_number\":1176,\"content\":\"        if left_tap && !self.editor.on && game_input {\"},{\"line_number\":1198,\"content\":\"            if game_input {\"},{\"line_number\":1257,\"content\":\"        if let Some(a) = intent.aiming.filter(|_| game_input) {\"},{\"line_number\":1277,\"content\":\"        if self.app_settings.aim_marker && game_input && curr.player.is_some() && !self.editor.on && curr.game.is_none() {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"fca1cee1-8329-4a49-a433-b882bc56a2b2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_60","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Game input is active and the InputFrame is filled when the menu is closed outside of studio mode.\n\nThe fit game's pre() strips action bits from player input, so Space cannot jump. The character tick uses sanitized input when provided; otherwise it falls back to the original input and Space would work. A lean action is also required.\n\nThe app always sets both move_dir and lean. The game uses move_dir for walking on the island and for balance, but switches to lean during events. A stateful key ramp for lean should live in the app.\n\nThe lean integrator belongs in the app's input state. The game exposes a pure function for tests to call. Mouse lean derives from cursor offset normalized by 0.38 times screen height. The last active device wins: mouse, pad stick, or keyboard key ramp.\n\nThe pad stick deadzone will change from 0.18 to 0.12 with a x^1.5 curve. The fit lean path will apply this curve to the raw stick axis before it is deadzoned, rather than on the already deadzoned value.\n\nThe app will set input.any for key taps, mouse clicks, mouse movement over six pixels, stick input above 0.3, and any button press. Mouse cursor deltas will be tracked against the previous position. The implementation is large, so a Python script will write files iteratively to avoid tool-call failures.\n\nThe Write tool handles large files directly, so a Python script is unnecessary. Engine changes and the core game will be implemented first, followed by compilation. Fonts will be unpacked in parallel. A complete script.toml will be written. The test command lives in the DEV folder and runs cargo test from the engine directory. The -q flag suppresses passing tests and shows only failures.\n\nThe test script will filter cargo output to show only failures, then print a final line formatted as `212 passed, 0 failed` to match the plan.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-37831475-6540-4bc1-b79f-649bde33f67b-124","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/headless.rs","limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":568,"output_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":188928,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"5f187fdb-f405-47ff-a2b2-c6aa0a1c01a7"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-37831475-6540-4bc1-b79f-649bde33f67b-124","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! The game UI without a window (doctrine 2, 3): the tools draw the HUD, the open windows and\\n//! the touch controls with the same code the window runs, on a headless egui context. A frame\\n//! gives a reading of what is on screen (every text with where it is, grouped by window, and the\\n//! touch controls) and egui's output, which `Overlay` paints over a capture.\\n\\nuse egui::{Pos2, Rect, Shape};\\nuse glam::Mat4;\\nuse pav_core::arpg::{GameCmd, GameFrame};\\nuse pav_core::frame::HudFrame;\\n10→use serde::Serialize;\\n\\nuse crate::Device;\\nuse crate::arpg_items::GameUi;\\nuse crate::arpg_ui::{Projector, hud};\\nuse crate::touch::{Touch, View};\\n\\n/// Passes per frame: windows size themselves from the pass before.\\nconst PASSES: usize = 3;\\n\\n20→/// The UI's state between frames: which windows are open, the device, the touch controls.\\n#[derive(Default)]\\npub struct Headless {\\n    pub game: GameUi,\\n    pub touch: Touch,\\n    pub device: Device,\\n}\\n\\n/// What a frame drew.\\npub struct Drawn {\\n30→    /// What `Overlay::paint` draws.\\n    pub paint: Paint,\\n    pub reading: Reading,\\n    /// What the player gave by clicking (`Input::click`).\\n    pub commands: Vec<GameCmd>,\\n}\\n\\n/// What is on screen, as text.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, Serialize)]\\npub struct Reading {\\n40→    pub screen: [f32; 2],\\n    pub device: &'static str,\\n    /// The windows the UI has open (`inventory`, `tree`, ...).\\n    pub open: Vec<&'static str>,\\n    /// Text outside any window: the HUD, loot labels, banners.\\n    pub hud: Vec<Text>,\\n    /// Each window or panel on screen: its title (its first line) and its text.\\n    pub windows: Vec<Window>,\\n    /// Touch: the controls a finger can press.\\n    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \\\"Vec::is_empty\\\")]\\n50→    pub controls: Vec<Control>,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize)]\\npub struct Text {\\n    pub text: String,\\n    /// Top-left corner, in points (pixels: the tools draw at one point per pixel).\\n    pub at: [f32; 2],\\n}\\n\\n60→#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize)]\\npub struct Window {\\n    pub title: String,\\n    /// `[x0, y0, x1, y1]`.\\n    pub rect: [f32; 4],\\n    pub text: Vec<Text>,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize)]\\npub struct Control {\\n70→    pub control: String,\\n    pub rect: [f32; 4],\\n}\\n\\n/// A frame's triangles and the textures they need.\\npub struct Paint {\\n    pub primitives: Vec<egui::ClippedPrimitive>,\\n    pub textures: egui::TexturesDelta,\\n    pub pixels_per_point: f32,\\n}\\n80→\\nimpl Drop for Paint {\\n    /// A reading that is never painted drops its textures unapplied (egui checks).\\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\\n        self.textures.clear();\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Pointer input for a frame: hover (tooltips) or a click at a point.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\n90→pub struct Input {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! The game UI without a window (doctrine 2, 3): the tools draw the HUD, the open windows and\\n//! the touch controls with the same code the window runs, on a headless egui context. A frame\\n//! gives a reading of what is on screen (every text with where it is, grouped by window, and the\\n//! touch controls) and egui's output, which `Overlay` paints over a capture.\\n\\nuse egui::{Pos2, Rect, Shape};\\nuse glam::Mat4;\\nuse pav_core::arpg::{GameCmd, GameFrame};\\nuse pav_core::frame::HudFrame;\\n10→use serde::Serialize;\\n\\nuse crate::Device;\\nuse crate::arpg_items::GameUi;\\nuse crate::arpg_ui::{Projector, hud};\\nuse crate::touch::{Touch, View};\\n\\n/// Passes per frame: windows size themselves from the pass before.\\nconst PASSES: usize = 3;\\n\\n20→/// The UI's state between frames: which windows are open, the device, the touch controls.\\n#[derive(Default)]\\npub struct Headless {\\n    pub game: GameUi,\\n    pub touch: Touch,\\n    pub device: Device,\\n}\\n\\n/// What a frame drew.\\npub struct Drawn {\\n30→    /// What `Overlay::paint` draws.\\n    pub paint: Paint,\\n    pub reading: Reading,\\n    /// What the player gave by clicking (`Input::click`).\\n    pub commands: Vec<GameCmd>,\\n}\\n\\n/// What is on screen, as text.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, Serialize)]\\npub struct Reading {\\n40→    pub screen: [f32; 2],\\n    pub device: &'static str,\\n    /// The windows the UI has open (`inventory`, `tree`, ...).\\n    pub open: Vec<&'static str>,\\n    /// Text outside any window: the HUD, loot labels, banners.\\n    pub hud: Vec<Text>,\\n    /// Each window or panel on screen: its title (its first line) and its text.\\n    pub windows: Vec<Window>,\\n    /// Touch: the controls a finger can press.\\n    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \\\"Vec::is_empty\\\")]\\n50→    pub controls: Vec<Control>,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize)]\\npub struct Text {\\n    pub text: String,\\n    /// Top-left corner, in points (pixels: the tools draw at one point per pixel).\\n    pub at: [f32; 2],\\n}\\n\\n60→#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize)]\\npub struct Window {\\n    pub title: String,\\n    /// `[x0, y0, x1, y1]`.\\n    pub rect: [f32; 4],\\n    pub text: Vec<Text>,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize)]\\npub struct Control {\\n70→    pub control: String,\\n    pub rect: [f32; 4],\\n}\\n\\n/// A frame's triangles and the textures they need.\\npub struct Paint {\\n    pub primitives: Vec<egui::ClippedPrimitive>,\\n    pub textures: egui::TexturesDelta,\\n    pub pixels_per_point: f32,\\n}\\n80→\\nimpl Drop for Paint {\\n    /// A reading that is never painted drops its textures unapplied (egui checks).\\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\\n        self.textures.clear();\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Pointer input for a frame: hover (tooltips) or a click at a point.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\n90→pub struct Input {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/headless.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":90,\"raw_output\":\"//! The game UI without a window (doctrine 2, 3): the tools draw the HUD, the open windows and\\n//! the touch controls with the same code the window runs, on a headless egui context. A frame\\n//! gives a reading of what is on screen (every text with where it is, grouped by window, and the\\n//! touch controls) and egui's output, which `Overlay` paints over a capture.\\n\\nuse egui::{Pos2, Rect, Shape};\\nuse glam::Mat4;\\nuse pav_core::arpg::{GameCmd, GameFrame};\\nuse pav_core::frame::HudFrame;\\nuse serde::Serialize;\\n\\nuse crate::Device;\\nuse crate::arpg_items::GameUi;\\nuse crate::arpg_ui::{Projector, hud};\\nuse crate::touch::{Touch, View};\\n\\n/// Passes per frame: windows size themselves from the pass before.\\nconst PASSES: usize = 3;\\n\\n/// The UI's state between frames: which windows are open, the device, the touch controls.\\n#[derive(Default)]\\npub struct Headless {\\n    pub game: GameUi,\\n    pub touch: Touch,\\n    pub device: Device,\\n}\\n\\n/// What a frame drew.\\npub struct Drawn {\\n    /// What `Overlay::paint` draws.\\n    pub paint: Paint,\\n    pub reading: Reading,\\n    /// What the player gave by clicking (`Input::click`).\\n    pub commands: Vec<GameCmd>,\\n}\\n\\n/// What is on screen, as text.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, Serialize)]\\npub struct Reading {\\n    pub screen: [f32; 2],\\n    pub device: &'static str,\\n    /// The windows the UI has open (`inventory`, `tree`, ...).\\n    pub open: Vec<&'static str>,\\n    /// Text outside any window: the HUD, loot labels, banners.\\n    pub hud: Vec<Text>,\\n    /// Each window or panel on screen: its title (its first line) and its text.\\n    pub windows: Vec<Window>,\\n    /// Touch: the controls a finger can press.\\n    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \\\"Vec::is_empty\\\")]\\n    pub controls: Vec<Control>,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize)]\\npub struct Text {\\n    pub text: String,\\n    /// Top-left corner, in points (pixels: the tools draw at one point per pixel).\\n    pub at: [f32; 2],\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize)]\\npub struct Window {\\n    pub title: String,\\n    /// `[x0, y0, x1, y1]`.\\n    pub rect: [f32; 4],\\n    pub text: Vec<Text>,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize)]\\npub struct Control {\\n    pub control: String,\\n    pub rect: [f32; 4],\\n}\\n\\n/// A frame's triangles and the textures they need.\\npub struct Paint {\\n    pub primitives: Vec<egui::ClippedPrimitive>,\\n    pub textures: egui::TexturesDelta,\\n    pub pixels_per_point: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Drop for Paint {\\n    /// A reading that is never painted drops its textures unapplied (egui checks).\\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\\n        self.textures.clear();\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Pointer input for a frame: hover (tooltips) or a click at a point.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct Input {\\n\",\"total_lines\":369}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"dcaf969f-7e5c-4fab-bd0e-3d130287ad10"}
