,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":21,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/settings.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"    /// --scene NAME or --room NAME.\"},{\"line_number\":16,\"content\":\"    pub scene: String,\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"            scene: String::new(),\"},{\"line_number\":63,\"content\":\"    pub fn load(_args: &[String]) -> (Self, String) {\"},{\"line_number\":68,\"content\":\"                s.scene = format!(\\\"world/{r}\\\");\"},{\"line_number\":70,\"content\":\"            if let Some(r) = p.get(\\\"scene\\\").filter(|r| !r.is_empty()) {\"},{\"line_number\":71,\"content\":\"                s.scene = r;\"},{\"line_number\":83,\"content\":\"        if (s.animation_studio || s.asset_studio || s.creature_studio) && s.scene.is_empty() {\"},{\"line_number\":84,\"content\":\"            s.scene = \\\"empty\\\".into();\"},{\"line_number\":86,\"content\":\"        if s.scene.is_empty() {\"},{\"line_number\":87,\"content\":\"            // Shardfall's town; the engine's pavilion is the `world` scene (pause menu).\"},{\"line_number\":88,\"content\":\"            s.scene = \\\"town\\\".into();\"},{\"line_number\":95,\"content\":\"    pub fn load(args: &[String]) -> (Self, String) {\"},{\"line_number\":150,\"content\":\"                \\\"--scene\\\" => s.scene = it.next().cloned().unwrap_or(s.scene),\"},{\"line_number\":151,\"content\":\"                \\\"--room\\\" => s.scene = it.next().map(|r| format!(\\\"world/{r}\\\")).unwrap_or(s.scene),\"},{\"line_number\":165,\"content\":\"            if s.scene.is_empty() {\"},{\"line_number\":166,\"content\":\"                s.scene = \\\"empty\\\".into();\"},{\"line_number\":172,\"content\":\"        if s.scene.is_empty() {\"},{\"line_number\":173,\"content\":\"            // Shardfall's town; the engine's pavilion is the `world` scene (pause menu).\"},{\"line_number\":174,\"content\":\"            s.scene = \\\"town\\\".into();\"},{\"line_number\":194,\"content\":\"            \\\"start_room\\\" if !v.is_empty() => s.scene = format!(\\\"world/{v}\\\"),\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"3facfe06-836d-474e-bde7-e67397bef5be"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_80","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a large task. I need to implement a complete game efficiently.\n\nI'm reviewing PLAN.md carefully to ensure I don't miss any requirements. The implementation will be compact but complete. Physics will stay lightweight: frozen menus skip physics entirely, and the player stands in place during events. For island free-time, bots will use fast-travel teleportation instead of walking.\n\nA simple visual world will include colored ground, water, props, and a character to keep captures non-blank. The FitGame state machine defines eleven frozen or playing phases: Title, Slots, Name, Look, Intro, DayTalk, Check, Free, Card, Countdown, Play, and Result.\n\nThe state machine now includes Sleep, BigStand, Ending, Credits, and FreePlay. Bot behavior will press CONFIRM in menus and lean during events. An attract demo triggers after 600 ticks of idle input in frozen phases. Pause freezes the world and stores the phase.\n\nThe balance physics uses a semi-implicit Euler integrator. It applies stiffness 40 and damping 8.5 to pull the center of pressure toward the lean target, then caps the distance at one unit to trigger tipping after 0.35 seconds.\n\nThe balance constants were verified against a Python reference check. The semi-implicit Euler integrator will run at 60Hz to match the reference simulation.\n\nA skill age formula was defined: 30% stillness, 25% targets, 25% blind, and 20% steps.\n\nThe age formula is now fully defined: 24 plus 56 times (1 minus skill) raised to the 1.1 power, minus two times days completed, minus the minimum of total stars divided by three and eight, clamped between 18 and 99.\n\nMorning check events will test stillness, targets, blind, and steps. The bot will hold center; idle input causes a wobble that pushes off.\n\nEvents will score from 0 to 1000 with star thresholds at 400, 650, and 850. The design targets an idle score below 400 and a guide-following score above 650 so bots can earn two stars quickly. Event durations will be optimized for fast testing.\n\nEvent durations are now estimated. Most events will last 8 to 12 seconds for a good bot, capped at roughly 20 seconds. The plank event needs 40 seconds for two stars. Morning checks should finish in about 15 seconds. Big stand lasts 30 seconds. Song step party runs about 62.5 seconds per seed, totaling over five minutes across five seeds. A full playthrough is estimated at around 420 seconds.\n\nIdle tests must run the full event duration to score below one star. Each event needs five bot seeds plus one idle seed. The worst-case idle test for step party and plank alone would take about 690 seconds.\n\nSimulation speed is now estimated at roughly one minute total. A 60-second event at 0.2 ms per tick yields about 36 seconds of actual simulation time. Balance events will skip heavy physics to keep the engine lightweight. The history buffer will store 24 snapshots over eight seconds, with FitGame kept small.\n\nInput recording is safe at 75,000 ticks. The maximum history buffer holds 216,000 ticks.\n\nPlay Together mode will support two to four local players with a podium at the end. I will write a test in tests/fit.rs that drives the real game: select Play Together, add players, play a short event, and show the sorted podium.\n\nPlay Together will be a real mode inside FitGame, not a fake simulation. The medley scene runs without the hub and uses a fixed seed for deterministic scores; the ghost medley combines Paddle, Tide, and Cannonball into a 0–3000 total. Save round-trip testing will serialize FitGame through GameBox CBOR to verify snapshot and restore. Music gain is set to 0.10 in the audio bus, exposed via a game status field so tests can read it directly.\n\nA dev slider will be reachable through the pause-to-dev-mode path. Tests can change a tunable such as stiffness and reset it to restore defaults.\n\nDev sliders will be part of the game state. Input during dev mode adjusts the focused slider with MENU_LEFT and MENU_RIGHT, and a reset button restores defaults. Tests will pause, navigate, change a value, verify it, then reset.\n\nTouch-only input sets a `touch_only` flag from the input device code. The test can set the device to touch and check that status.\n\nContent linting will count lines in scripts, coaches, and SFX IDs, and will reject any files containing Nintendo names or weight and BMI references.\n\nYesterday You will save the best score per event and show a comparison. The test round-trip will include yesterday scores.\n\nLook selection changes puppet colors and gear. Flip-flops are a cosmetic that shifts balance slightly; they are optional but included in the look menu.\n\nThe hub needs session.js, meta tags, an IIFE wrapper, ghost mode, and medley score display. This web work will be done after the simulation compiles.\n\nThe UI frame is built inside the game's frame method.\n\nThe Game trait will gain a `ui` method returning `Option<UiModel>`, defaulting to None. UiModel will live in pav_core as a plain struct so the simulation and UI can share it without coupling to egui. The camera yaw will be stored in HudFrame and applied by the application.\n\nA `tint` method on the Game trait will return an optional color and alpha for ghost entities. FitGame will supply this during events.\n\nThe dev time scale will be stored in FitGame.dev.time_scale. Tests can multiply game timers by this value in post-processing, since the engine tick duration is fixed.\n\nThe dev time scale will be applied by scaling the game logic delta time and event timers. During pause, the simulation still increments ticks but leaves player positions unchanged, so tests can verify frozen world time by checking that the character stays in place.\n\nThe pause behavior is being reconsidered. If the engine increments tick during pause, sim.time() advances and violates the requirement to freeze world time. The design may need to skip tick advancement during pause instead of just freezing physics.\n\nThe engine tick will still increment during pause. The frozen state applies only to physics and the game clock, not the engine tick itself.\n\nThe attract mode will trigger after 600 idle engine ticks on the title screen. Any input exits back to the title, and save serial only increments during real saves, not during attract. A helper `any(input)` will detect button or movement input. Tests will snapshot save_serial before and after attract to verify it stays unchanged.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1f16d7c4-4ce9-4669-9b3d-0ac18a96327c-30","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn build\\(|fn build_standalone_room|play\\.is_none|GAMES","glob":"**/pav_core/src/scenes.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1f16d7c4-4ce9-4669-9b3d-0ac18a96327c-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/rooms/_template.toml","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1f16d7c4-4ce9-4669-9b3d-0ac18a96327c-32","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/starter.toml","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1f16d7c4-4ce9-4669-9b3d-0ac18a96327c-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn play_clip|clip_id|pub fn say\\(","glob":"**/pav_core/src/**/*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1f16d7c4-4ce9-4669-9b3d-0ac18a96327c-34","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_tools/src/tools.rs","offset":1355,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5704,"output_tokens":3630,"c