 bool) {\"},{\"line_number\":778,\"content\":\"    fn handle_key(&mut self, code: KeyCode) {\"},{\"line_number\":877,\"content\":\"            KeyCode::F1 => self.panel.open = !self.panel.open,\"},{\"line_number\":908,\"content\":\"            KeyCode::F10 if self.studio_mode == StudioMode::World => {\"},{\"line_number\":914,\"content\":\"            KeyCode::F11 => {\"},{\"line_number\":920,\"content\":\"            KeyCode::F12 => self.screenshot_requested = true,\"},{\"line_number\":1416,\"content\":\"            ui::boot_panel(&ctx, &mut show_boot);\"},{\"line_number\":1543,\"content\":\"                        _ => \\\"Esc menu · F1 tuning · F2 rooms · F12 screenshot\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":2168,\"content\":\"                            | KeyCode::F1\"},{\"line_number\":2177,\"content\":\"                            | KeyCode::F10\"},{\"line_number\":2178,\"content\":\"                            | KeyCode::F11\"},{\"line_number\":2179,\"content\":\"                            | KeyCode::F12\"},{\"line_number\":2182,\"content\":\"                        self.handle_key(code);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"314931ae-6cfc-4121-af5d-267371142cce"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_88","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"InputFrame literals in tools.rs are full structs without trailing dots.\n\nThree InputFrame literals in tools.rs need updating. Most other files already use `..Default::default()`. I will write the game code now and plan file sizes for core.rs and intent.rs.\n\nui_model.rs will be about 200 lines. mod.rs is the largest file at roughly 2000–3000 lines; events may move to a separate events.rs. rules.toml and charts.toml hold numbers and notes. script.toml will be generated by a script to ensure correct counts. fit.toml or sets will define the hub room and other smaller rooms.\n\nRooms will be built as compact hand-written toml maps rather than many separate files. A few simple JSON props will be added, possibly using engine primitives for beach objects.\n\nAnimation fit.json will add clips like Breath and Tree with simple key poses. Extending the audio mixer with buses and a sequencer is the riskiest compile area, so I will inspect Mixer::render first. I will patch app.rs in targeted sections around lines 750–930, 1100–1250, 1400–1560, and 2140–2200. To speed up implementation, I will spawn subagents for audio extension, UI fit_ui, and web/app chrome while writing the game simulation.\n\nI will write the files myself rather than spawning subagents to avoid coordination bugs. Engine patches come first, then the main game file. I have started designing the FitGame struct with fields for rules, flow, save data, active slot, and day.\n\nThe FitGame struct now includes fields for time tracking, star totals, event history, best scores, stamps, world time, idle state, attract mode, save serial, and UI state.\n\nThe FitGame struct now includes balance, settings, hub state, medley tracking, guest runs, device flags, ending state, flipflops, look data, name index, event clock, card timer, result card, menu, input tick, version, and slider index.\n\nThe FitGame struct now includes cheat notes, yesterday and free play flags, a phase clock, check state, finale, song index, and UI click data. The Flow enum covers every game state from title through credits, including check, island, schedule, card, event, result, sleep, finale, and attract mode.\n\nThe frozen() state covers most UI screens but excludes Island, Countdown, Event, Check, Finale, and Attract. Pause is frozen. Card mode still ticks and updates its timer while physics are paused.\n\nHub mode will use rest \"medley\" sets with hub=true and flow set to Card or Event of the first medley event. The game will freeze until HUB_GO arrives before starting the medley. Regular fit/medley tests start immediately. Hub sessions are detected via boot.scene, which the page only sets when AIHub.active.\n\nA conflict emerged between deterministic tests and the hub flow. Tests load `fit/medley` immediately, but the hub page sends `HUB_GO` only after the game reports ready. If the medley finishes before the hub connects, JavaScript may report a score prematurely. The timing between Rust status reporting and the hub signal needs resolution.\n\nA Waiting state for `fit/medley` is being considered. It would run for 0.5 seconds without HUB_GO to detect a test session, but this approach is deemed racy.\n\nThe medley will start immediately for deterministic tests, but wait for HUB_GO when the scene is `medley-hub` or a boot flag is present. This satisfies both test determinism and hub timing.\n\nThe web weblink will set the `HUB_GO` input bit when `window.__hub.go` is true. Tests lack this signal, so they start the medley immediately. A `hub_wait` flag will default to false in the simulation.\n\nA new `InputFrame.hub` field will carry three states: 0 for non-hub frames, 1 for waiting, and 2 for go. Tests leave it at zero so the medley starts immediately; the browser weblink sets it to 1 then 2 to trigger the wait.\n\nAn `Activity` struct is being designed with a `kind` enum and shared fields for all event types. It stores timer, score, stars, and per-event data like lungs and pose.\n\nThe Activity struct now includes per-event fields for streak, in-time, squat depth and reps, plank survival time, step notes hit, floatie angle and spin, lap progress and zone time, tide shells and board state, paddle position and gates, tray glass positions, and a placeholder for the cannon event.\n\nThe Activity struct now includes shared fields for tips and a tipped lock, plus per-event data for dive bounces, power, air, tuck, and dives.\n\nBalanceCore is being defined with center-of-balance, velocity, tip timer, tipping state, phase vectors, kick-in, and wobble amplitude. Its step function blends lean target with a wobble offset, applies stiffness and damping, adds gust and nudge forces, integrates velocity and position, and advances time.\n\nBalance tipping will use a one-tick pulse when the timer crosses tip_time, resetting the timer and adding a recovery lock so events do not retrigger every frame. The bot will compute desired lean in screen space and write it to both input.lean and move_dir.\n\nBot menu navigation will use one button press per tick. The bot computes the exact required action for the current focus index and executes it immediately. Title screen confirms New Stay. Slot selection confirms slot 0. Name entry confirms name 0.\n\nThe bot will press Confirm every tick to complete and advance dialogue lines. On the Island screen it opens the schedule and fast-travels to the next event. When minutes are met the bot ends the day. After Day 5 the finale triggers automatically. First clears earn one minute plus stars; repeats earn one minute.\n\nDay goals are 3, 5, 7, and 9 minutes. The bot will play every unlocked event each day even after the goal is reached. Day 1 has breath and pose. Day 2 has squats and plank. Day 5 has the big stand. Five stamps total. A `stars_score` function is being drafted.\n\nStar thresholds are now fixed: 850 for three stars, 650 for two, 400 for one. Plank survival scores three stars at 55 seconds, two at 40, and one at 25.\n\nAge is computed as 24 plus 56 times (1 minus skill) raised to the 1.1 power. A skill of 0.9 on day one yields an age near 28.4. By day five the age drops to about 12 and clamps to 18, triggering checkout. Idle mode will use low skill and high age.\n\nCheck duration is being estimated at roughly 37 seconds. Still, targets, blind, and steps will not be skipped early. The full five-day playthrough should total about 175 seconds.\n\nEvents end at their duration or a flop. Plank runs until 60 seconds or the bot flops. The bot will not force a flop after 45 seconds. Tests will accept the full runtime. The dev.time_scale flag is ignored by the bot. The test harness steps at 1/60 second intervals.\n\nTo speed up balance events, physics will be frozen during pure balance checks. The freeze logic is being adjusted so that play_post still runs after play_pre, ensuring scoring and state updates continue even when the world is paused.\n\nAll game simulation logic will move into `pre` so it still runs while the world is frozen. `post` can remain empty. This keeps tests fast during balance events without needing the character to animate.\n\nCapture runs with physics enabled so the figure stands and tilts visibly. Freezing would freeze the character tick and hide the tilt. Balance events will not be frozen during capture. A tiny benchmark will measure simulation cost after the first compile. Eight seconds of snapshot history should be acceptable.\n\nSnapshot history costs about ten seconds extra, which is acceptable. The UiFrame struct is being drafted to expose screen state, menu items, focus index, prompt, device flags, puck data, demo mode, touch card state, age, day, minutes, goal, stars, and score.\n\nThe UiFrame struct now includes timer, about_page, and big fields. UiItem stores id, label, and a four-element rect array for normalized screen coordinates. The simulation will precompute logical layout slots, and the UI layer will scale them to pixels for browser tests and headless rendering.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8d496797-ec86-44ef-93ec-516c3407e806-57","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"struct Mixer|fn render|struct Voice|struct Patch|fn play\\(","glob":"**/pav_audio/src/lib.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8d496797-ec86-44ef-93ec-516c3407e806-58","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_tools/src/tools.rs","offset":1660,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8d496797-ec86-44ef-93ec-516c3407e806-59","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/lib.rs","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8d496797-ec86-44ef-93ec-516c3407e806-60","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/headless.rs","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8971,"output_tokens":5304,"cache_read_input_tokens":105984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"43234dd6-302e-4023-a67b-8d8c1f194c54"}
