gs\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":40,\"content\":\"        AttachKind::Wings,\"},{\"line_number\":202,\"content\":\"            AttachKind::Wings => {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"05743553-0607-49c9-9fb5-74534531582a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_95","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Only parts.rs needs changes. I'll add Handle.\n\nI'll read app.rs around lines 760-930, 1050-1250, 1400-1560, and 2140-2200 to prepare accurate patches. Engine patches and game files will be written next.\n\nCore tests will be compiled before wiring the app and web. I'll add `pub mod fit_ui` to pav_core and `pub mod fit` to games/mod.rs. The fit game will use a `UiFrame` struct in `fit_ui.rs`. Core logic will split into `core.rs` and `intent.rs`.\n\nThe fit game will be organized into `events.rs` for activity simulation, `flow.rs` for menus and bot logic, and `mod.rs` for module glue. I'm defining exact duration constants in seconds for each exercise. Big stand step is 40 seconds at 96 BPM. The full step chart spans 102.4 beats.\n\nBot notes will be placed on beats from charts.toml as [time, lane] tuples. Lane 0 is left. Lane 1 is right. Lane 2 is both. The bot presses on the exact tick when a note falls. That lands within the 55ms window. Idle misses all notes. Score equals perfect times 1000 divided by total notes. A perfect bot gets 1000 points. Two stars require 650. The paddle score formula is `clamp((1.6 * par - t) / (0.8 * par)) * 1000`.\n\nIdle paddle completion scores 125 points, which is below the 400 threshold. Missed gates add two seconds each. The bot must finish in under 1.08 times the par to earn two stars and under 0.92 times the par for three stars. The target finish time is about 0.7 times the par.\n\nPaddle par is 30 seconds. At forward lean 0.5 the bot moves at 4 m/s and covers an 80-meter channel in about 20 seconds, scoring 1000 points. Idle wobble leaves the bot stuck, so its score stays low.\n\nTide scores shells potted divided by total times 800 plus a time bonus. The bot pots all 15 shells for 1000 points. Idle pots none.\n\nTray gives 200 points per glass. Five glasses equal 1000 points. Idle spills all before the end.\n\nJolts are scripted impulses at known times. Each adds tilt times speed times delta time to glass position. If absolute position exceeds one the glass plops.\n\nCannon score averages height, tuck, and timing across three dives. The bot scores about 900 points; idle gets zero.\n\nFloatie score equals rings multiplied by band time, clamped and scaled to 1000. Seven rings with full band time yields 1000 points. The bot catches all seven rings with high band time; idle catches none.\n\nFloatie guests will toss rings every 7 seconds. The bot presses within 0.25 seconds to catch them; idle misses yield zero rings and zero score.\n\nLap scoring uses zone time, ribbons, and bumps. The bot stays in the 1.6–2.4 step zone and alternates direction every 0.5 seconds. Idle stays out of the zone with zero steps.\n\nSquats require 10 reps. Each rep scores 0–100 points. Total score is that sum multiplied by ten, giving a maximum of 1000.\n\nSquats last 50 seconds. The guide is 2 seconds down and 1 second up per rep. The bot scores 100 points per rep for a perfect total of 1000. Idle scores zero because depth never changes.\n\nPose score equals weighted time divided by total duration, capped at 1000. A streak multiplier can push the raw value above 1000, but it clamps to the ceiling. Idle scores about 300.\n\nBreath score is the average tick score multiplied by 1000.\n\nThe check game will compare bot age against idle age, keeping both in the 18–99 range. The slot machine will simply set age; its visual is UI-only. Roughly forty names will be hardcoded into a script. Six skins and eight outfits are planned. Five flip-flop pickups will be placed on the island for optional collection by the bot.\n\nThe absence feature will track `today` from boot and `last_played` in save data. A comment appears if the day difference is at least one. The app writes to localStorage whenever `save_serial` changes. The serial increments on day changes and results. Tests verify this incrementing behavior. The save JSON includes a version field set to 1. Unknown versions are rejected. Credits always end with a win outcome. After credits, confirming proceeds to free play on the island with all events open.\n\nFree play unlocks when credits begin. Five stamps appear after the day-five finale. The test checks that all thirteen events are marked played, including Big Stand and Morning Check.\n\nThe test will assert the total simulation time stays under 3600 seconds, or sixty minutes. It will also mark the daily check as played.\n\nWake dialogue takes about eight ticks. The check event needs roughly twenty-eight seconds. Day one totals about one hundred forty-eight seconds. Day two totals about one hundred sixty-one seconds.\n\nDay three totals about 263 seconds. Day four totals about 262 seconds. Day five totals about 187 seconds. The full playthrough spans roughly 1021 seconds, or about 17 minutes. The event tests alone require roughly 284,760 simulation steps across six runs. Combined with the playthrough, the total is approximately 469,000 steps.\n\nTotal simulation steps are estimated at roughly 500,000. Physics will not be frozen during events to keep figure captures visible; skipping physics would make tests faster but break the tilt capture.\n\nThe rewind test needs `history_seconds` set to 4 on the build config. Recording every step is acceptable at roughly 60,000 inputs. A small physics world with one kinematic character should step in about 0.15 milliseconds, so all core tests finish in roughly 75 seconds. Running with `--test-threads=1` prevents memory exhaustion from parallel simulations.\n\nI'll use two test threads to keep memory usage around 400 MB. All heavy tests will be grouped into a single `suite()` function so they run sequentially and avoid parallelizing with each other. The long playthrough and event tests will share this one function, while smaller unit tests can still run in parallel. I'll also disable history recording during that lengthy simulation by setting `history_seconds` to zero after building the config.\n\nHistory will be set to 8 in the build config for the rewind test, then disabled mid-run for the long suite. Recording stays small at roughly 4 MB. Next I'll generate script.toml with a Python script and start coding core compilation.\n\nA single hub room will be built in code with a readable title and visible island. Each event set will have its own small toml file for data. The 3D scene needs ground, water, the character, and a few objects so captures are not blank. All events will teleport to markers on this one room. Camera cues will change per event. The figure stands on the mat. This satisfies the figure-plus-puck requirement.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1797ca30-5ab2-47a1-a2e8-813aed18fdae-77","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/assets/props/lib/core/rowboat.json","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1797ca30-5ab2-47a1-a2e8-813aed18fdae-78","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn spawn_prop|prop:","glob":"**/entity.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":371,"output_tokens":3603,"cache_read_input_tokens":135424,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"1b183cd7-8070-4e14-8137-dbce79a9084f"}
