{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_99","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can create and place simple props.\n\nI'll spawn island visuals in Rust and use TOML for the room layout. I'm drafting a hub.toml with a beach scene using legend colors and objects like a rowboat and umbrella. I've also started writing a palm JSON prop.\n\nI'll use centimeters to match the rowboat prop's scale. I'm now writing files in batches, starting with small engine patches before the larger Rust modules. I've also begun drafting the `fit_ui.rs` structure.\n\nThe `FitUi` struct now includes fields for body text, menu items, focus state, device flags, prompts, demo mode, touch cards, a puck, HUD strings, about pages, and a big label. A `FitItem` struct with an ID and label is also defined.\n\nFitItem now includes normalized x, y, width, and height fields. A Puck struct with position, radius, and target angle is also defined.\n\nGame trait methods frozen() and fit_ui() are being added. Sim::frame will call fit_ui on the active game state and wrap the result in an Arc.\n\nstatus() will return JSON via to_string. camera_yaw will be added to FitUi and copied into HudFrame.\n\nstep_inner freeze logic will run after play_pre. When frozen, play_post is skipped. All game logic will move into pre so post stays empty.\n\nWhen frozen, the step function skips physics and returns early. It still updates the tick counter and extends events unless replaying.\n\nA tint method is being added to the Game trait for ghost effects. Puppet tilt fields will use serde defaults.\n\nPuppet tilt will be computed from forward and side lean angles. Body motion will apply this rotation about the feet. The input button structure will gain an optional lean field, and its constructor will use `..Default::default()` to support future additions.\n\nThe InputFrame constructor will use `..Default::default()` with explicit fields for move_dir, aim, held, and pressed. The lean field will be set conditionally from the argument vector. Audio support is also being added to Patch.\n\nPatch fields `formant` and `lfo` will be added to the end of the struct and inside `new()`. Struct update syntax with `..Patch::new()` still works because the constructor now supplies the new values.\n\nVoice synthesis will gain formant state. When `formant[0]` is active, `next()` will apply two bandpass approximations as a simple resonator.\n\nMixer gains are being split into separate music, sfx, and voice buses. The existing `play()` method will stay on the sfx bus, while a new `play_bus()` will handle other buses. Voice will carry a `bus: u8` tag so the renderer can route it correctly. Music sequencing will run during render when a song is active, with notes triggered every N samples. A default music gain constant of 0.10 is defined. New sound events will be added to the SFX branch in `sounds_for` before the catch-all arm.\n\nplay_event will handle Music, Syllable, and Sfx events. The audio callback will set the mixer song for Music events. Offline render_events will also handle Music events by setting the mixer song.\n\nBigSplash and Wake views will be added to build.rs near Splash. The splash burst effect in fx.rs will also be patched.\n\nApp changes and web index updates are deferred until the core engine is working.\n\nI'm checking how egui handles font installation so fit_ui can use custom fonts. The plan says to install Fredoka and Nunito before the first run_ui, but Headless::frame creates a fresh context each frame with three passes. I need to place set_fonts carefully so it takes effect on the first pass without panicking.\n\nA dummy `run_ui` pass will be inserted after `install_fonts` to warm the font atlas. This prevents the first real pass from panicking on custom fonts. The TTF files will be unpacked next.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9aa44a6f-1d84-4ebc-a3bc-bb5039bcfdbb-83","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"tar -tzf \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/notes/fonts-pack/expo-google-fonts-fredoka-0.4.1.tgz\" | head -40; echo '---'; tar -tzf \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/notes/fonts-pack/expo-google-fonts-nunito-0.4.2.tgz\" | rg -i \"700Bold|600Semi\" | head","description":"List font files inside the tarballs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":428,"output_tokens":2414,"cache_read_input_tokens":142208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"7e13060f-2030-473f-b9f8-77e7e0f904cb"}
