{\\n                b.area = Vec3::splat(s * 0.5);\\n                b.spread = 2.0 * s;\\n                b.size = (0.3 * s.max(0.6), 0.05);\\n                b.life = (0.25, 0.6);\\n            }));\\n        }\\n        E::Land { pos, speed } if *speed > 8.0 => out.push(with(\\\"dust\\\", *pos, 12, &|b| b.spread = 2.0)),\\n        _ => {}\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":480}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"834bef94-8a6a-424f-a3de-a0c550d47e32"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_107","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"BigSplash will be added before the wildcard.\n\nWake is silent. Water dent in build.rs. Engine patches come first. Then game files. script.toml will be generated with Python. App integration waits for core tests. A comprehensive mod.rs and EventId enum are being written.\n\nEventId now lists Check, Breath, Pose, Squat, Plank, Step, Floatie, Lap, Tide, Paddle, Tray, Cannon, and BigStand. Day unlocks map each day to specific events, with BigStand as the wildcard for later days. Free play unlocks all events. Minute goals scale from 3 to 9 minutes by day.\n\nEvents will be handled in a single `tick_event` match function. The bot state machine will press SCHEDULE on the island, then focus and confirm the next unplayed event each tick. It will end the day once all events are done and the goal is met. If the goal is not met, it replays an event. First clearing Breath with three stars banks four minutes.\n\nPose is still played because the bot finishes all events before ending the day. Sleep advances the day and stamp, then returns to Check and Island for days one through four. On day five it goes straight to Finale and Ending instead of the island. Five sleep stamps total.\n\nThe intro will show Pip dialogue after the look screen, then proceed to day one wake. Character names will be stored in a constant array of forty entries. The look screen lets the player pick a skin and outfit from two rows; the bot will confirm the default selection. On continue, the bot will select New Stay to reset slot zero instead of resuming a saved guest. Settings from the title screen are unnecessary for the bot. During gameplay, pressing Esc opens a pause menu with Resume, Schedule, Calendar, Wardrobe, Settings, How to Play, About, Dev Mode, and Quit.\n\nDev mode will include jump and slider controls. The hub medley combines Paddle, Tide, and Cannon; it finishes once all three are done and shows no title. `fit/medley` starts immediately with a countdown card for Paddle. Because the RNG is seeded, the bot produces a deterministic score. In Play Together, each player's score is stored and displayed on a Podium after all turns; the test drives the bot manually to begin, then calls a function to advance. The medley alone takes about 290 seconds, or roughly 17,400 steps, which fits within the test budget.\n\nAn attract playlist maps each event to a duration. Island runs for eight seconds. Title runs for five. All other events run for fifteen. During attract mode the engine runs bot inputs internally and exits if any external input arrives. The test supplies empty inputs for six hundred ticks. The title idle counter only increments when no input is present and the menu is open.\n\nThe attract mode switch will happen at the start of the pre-tick step. After 600 idle ticks, the counter reaches 600 and the flow enters attract mode.\n\nExit during attract mode returns to the title screen with the same save serial. Save serial only increments on day changes and non-demo results, so attract mode never saves.\n\nMusic defaults to 0.10 in settings and audio constants.\n\nDev tuning uses pause menu focus indices mapped to parameters. MENU_RIGHT adds one unit or five percent of the range to the focused float. Reset item restores default rules.\n\nThe test will load the pose event scene, pause, then exercise the dev slider controls.\n\nTests will drive the dev menu through `UiEvent::Click` and `UiEvent::Slider` on item IDs. This reuses the same code path as player input. The test will pause, click the dev button, set stiffness to 55, verify the value, then reset and confirm it returns to 40.\n\nItem IDs will be constants. The game handles keyboard lean by reading input.lean, while tests can set it directly; intent.rs unit tests cover the shaping functions that the app invokes.\n\nA `mouse_lean` helper is being added to intent.rs. The keyboard ramp state will live in the app between frames so tests can exercise it directly. Balance tests will set lean directly.\n\nA `lean_of` helper is being drafted to select between `input.lean` and `input.move_dir`. Zero lean is valid, so a length check cannot distinguish an unset value from a centered stick. The logic must rely on device flags or test conventions to tell whether the player is walking or using a verb.\n\nThe `lean_of` helper is simplified to always return `input.lean`. The app will compute both `lean` and `move_dir` from the same stick or keys, so island walking and event balance can coexist cleanly. The game will ignore `move_dir` during events and rely on `lean` for balance. The last device to set a value wins.\n\nThe app will track the last input device and only update lean from that source. The game stores `self.device` whenever `input.device` is non-zero.\n\nThe game module will be kept compact under two thousand lines. A clip JSON and a simple room are also needed: a 24 by 18 island map with sand, water border, player marker, colored decks, camera tilt 35 distance 16, pastel view, and a water zone legend.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5cda10b5-0347-4549-83a1-82c0c6f9b4c4-92","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/puppet.rs","offset":150,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1200,"output_tokens":2632,"cache_read_input_tokens":150400,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"faff2b7b-1d5c-42ce-a561-679d4e1b12ec"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5cda10b5-0347-4549-83a1-82c0c6f9b4c4-92","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"150→\\n/// Proportions, colours and animation settings. Everything is a slider.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(default)]\\npub struct PuppetDef {\\n    pub scale: f32,\\n    pub head_radius: f32,\\n    pub torso_length: f32,\\n    pub torso_radius: f32,\\n    pub hip_width: f32,\\n160→    pub shoulder_width: f32,\\n    pub leg_length: f32,\\n    pub arm_length: f32,\\n    pub limb_radius: f32,\\n    pub skin: String,\\n    pub shirt: String,\\n    pub pants: String,\\n    pub shoes: String,\\n    pub eyes: String,\\n    pub look: Look,\\n170→    /// Metres travelled per full walk cycle (two steps).\\n    pub stride: f32,\\n    pub step_height: f32,\\n    pub arm_swing: f32,\\n    pub bob: f32,\\n    pub lean: f32,\\n    pub squash: f32,\\n    /// Stepped animation: 0 = smooth, 12 = \\\"on twos\\\" at 24 fps, etc.\\n    pub anim_fps: f32,\\n    /// Tilt the eyes toward the camera so they stay visible from above (0..1).\\n180→    pub eyes_to_camera: f32,\\n    /// Lean the whole body toward the camera (0..1): a 2D \\\"cheat\\\" for high camera angles.\\n    pub face_camera: f32,\\n    /// Skeleton: biped, or a creature with planted feet (spider, lizard, beetle) or a blob.\\n    pub body: BodyPlan,\\n    /// Leg pairs of creatures (0 = the body plan's usual number).\\n    pub legs: i32,\\n    /// Creature body length (m).\\n    pub body_length: f32,\\n    /// Tail length (m, 0 = none); swings with secondary motion.\\n190→    pub tail_length: f32,\\n    /// Antenna length (m, 0 = none).\\n    pub antenna_length: f32,\\n    /// Seconds a creature foot takes for one step.\\n    pub step_time: f32,\\n    /// Floppiness of tails, antennae and abdomens (0 = stiff, 2 = very floppy).\\n    pub wobble: f32,\\n    /// Second colour (shells, stripes, tail tips).\\n    pub accent: String,\\n    /// Held weapon and off hand.\\n200→    pub weapon: WeaponLook,\\n    /// Worn armour.\\n    pub gear: GearLook,\\n    /// Horns, spikes, wings... (any body plan).\\n    pub parts: Vec<crate::parts::Attach>,\\n    /// A motion clip (`SET/Clip`, see the `clips` tool) the character plays while it stands\\n    /// still with nothing to do, in place of the procedural idle (bipeds). Empty = none.\\n    pub idle_clip: String,\\n    /// A walk loop (`STYLE100/Old_Walk`...) the character walks with in place of the\\n    /// procedural walk while it heads forward on the ground, played as fast as it moves\\n210→    /// (bipeds). Empty = none.\\n    pub walk_clip: String,\\n    /// A run loop for speeds the walk loop would have to hurry through (a monster giving\\n    /// chase): it plays instead of the walk above the pace between the two (bipeds). Empty =\\n    /// none.\\n    pub run_clip: String,\\n    /// A captured fall the character dies with, in place of the procedural topple (bipeds;\\n    /// the hero has falls of its own). Empty = none.\\n    pub death_clip: String,\\n    /// Captured attacks by skill (`claw = \\\"QUATERNIUS/Zombie_Scratch\\\"`), played in place of the\\n220→    /// skill's move and timed so the clip's strike lands on the hit: the moment a hand reaches\\n    /// furthest ahead of the hips (a foot, for a clip tagged `kick`), or `@seconds` written\\n    /// after the name (bipeds). A list plays one per swing of a combo (`slash = [\\\"A\\\", \\\"B\\\",\\n    /// \\\"C\\\"]`: jab, cross, kick).\\n    pub attack_clips: std::collections::BTreeMap<String, PerSwing>,\\n    /// Moves by skill (anim/moves.toml names: `cleave = \\\"sweep\\\"`), played in place of the\\n    /// skill's own move; a list plays one per swing of a combo (`slash = [\\\"jab\\\", \\\"cross\\\",\\n    /// \\\"roundhouse\\\"]`). A captured attack for the skill wins over its move.\\n    pub attack_moves: std::collections::BTreeMap<String, PerSwing>,\\n    /// A captured dodge (`QUATERNIUS/Roll`, a dive, a cartwheel) the character plays through a\",\"content_concise\":\"150→\\n/// Proportions, colours and animation settings. Everything is a slider.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(default)]\\npub struct PuppetDef {\\n    pub scale: f32,\\n    pub head_radius: f32,\\n    pub torso_length: f32,\\n    pub torso_radius: f32,\\n    pub hip_width: f32,\\n160→    pub shoulder_width: f32,\\n    pub leg_length: f32,\\n    pub arm_length: f32,\\n    pub limb_radius: f32,\\n    pub skin: String,\\n    pub shirt: String,\\n    pub pants: String,\\n    pub shoes: String,\\n    pub eyes: String,\\n    pub look: Look,\\n170→    /// Metres travelled per full walk cycle (two steps).\\n    pub stride: f32,\\n    pub step_height: f32,\\n    pub arm_swing: f32,\\n    pub bob: f32,\\n    pub lean: f32,\\n    pub squash: f32,\\n    /// Stepped animation: 0 = smooth, 12 = \\\"on twos\\\" at 24 fps, etc.\\n    pub anim_fps: f32,\\n    /// Tilt the eyes toward the camera so they stay visible from above (0..1).\\n180→    pub eyes_to_camera: f32,\\n    /// Lean the whole body toward the camera (0..1): a 2D \\\"cheat\\\" for high camera angles.\\n    pub face_camera: f32,\\n    /// Skeleton: biped, or a creature with planted feet (spider, lizard, beetle) or a blob.\\n    pub body: BodyPlan,\\n    /// Leg pairs of creatures (0 = the body plan's usual number).\\n    pub legs: i32,\\n    /// Creature body length (m).\\n    pub body_length: f32,\\n    /// Tail length (m, 0 = none); swings with secondary motion.\\n190→    pub tail_length: f32,\\n    /// Antenna length (m, 0 = none).\\n    pub antenna_length: f32,\\n    /// Seconds a creature foot takes for one step.\\n    pub step_time: f32,\\n    /// Floppiness of tails, antennae and abdomens (0 = stiff, 2 = very floppy).\\n    pub wobble: f32,\\n    /// Second colour (shells, stripes, tail tips).\\n    pub accent: String,\\n    /// Held weapon and off hand.\\n200→    pub weapon: WeaponLook,\\n    /// Worn armour.\\n    pub gear: GearLook,\\n    /// Horns, spikes, wings... (any body plan).\\n    pub parts: Vec<crate::parts::Attach>,\\n    /// A motion clip (`SET/Clip`, see the `clips` tool) the character plays while it stands\\n    /// still with nothing to do, in place of the procedural idle (bipeds). Empty = none.\\n    pub idle_clip: String,\\n    /// A walk loop (`STYLE100/Old_Walk`...) the character walks with in place of the\\n    /// procedural walk while it heads forward on the ground, played as fast as it moves\\n210→    /// (bipeds). Empty = none.\\n    pub walk_clip: String,\\n    /// A run loop for speeds the walk loop would have to hurry through (a monster giving\\n    /// chase): it plays instead of the walk above the pace between the two (bipeds). Empty =\\n    /// none.\\n    pub run_clip: String,\\n    /// A captured fall the character dies with, in place of the procedural topple (bipeds;\\n    /// the hero has falls of its own). Empty = none.\\n    pub death_clip: String,\\n    /// Captured attacks by skill (`claw = \\\"QUATERNIUS/Zombie_Scratch\\\"`), played in place of the\\n220→    /// skill's move and timed so the clip's strike lands on the hit: the moment a hand reaches\\n    /// furthest ahead of the hips (a foot, for a clip tagged `kick`), or `@seconds` written\\n    /// after the name (bipeds). A list plays one per swing of a combo (`slash = [\\\"A\\\", \\\"B\\\",\\n    /// \\\"C\\\"]`: jab, cross, kick).\\n    pub attack_clips: std::collections::BTreeMap<String, PerSwing>,\\n    /// Moves by skill (anim/moves.toml names: `cleave = \\\"sweep\\\"`), played in place of the\\n    /// skill's own move; a list plays one per swing of a combo (`slash = [\\\"jab\\\", \\\"cross\\\",\\n    /// \\\"roundhouse\\\"]`). A captured attack for the skill wins over its move.\\n    pub attack_moves: std::collections::BTreeMap<String, PerSwing>,\\n    /// A captured dodge (`QUATERNIUS/Roll`, a dive, a cartwheel) the character plays through a\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/puppet.rs\",\"offset\":150,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"\\n/// Proportions, colours and animation settings. Everything is a slider.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(default)]\\npub struct PuppetDef {\\n    pub scale: f32,\\n    pub head_radius: f32,\\n    pub torso_length: f32,\\n    pub torso_radius: f32,\\n    pub hip_width: f32,\\n    pub shoulder_width: f32,\\n    pub leg_length: f32,\\n    pub arm_length: f32,\\n    pub limb_radius: f32,\\n    pub skin: String,\\n    pub shirt: String,\\n    pub pants: String,\\n    pub shoes: String,\\n    pub eyes: String,\\n    pub look: Look,\\n    /// Metres travelled per full walk cycle (two steps).\\n    pub stride: f32,\\n    pub step_height: f32,\\n    pub arm_swing: f32,\\n    pub bob: f32,\\n    pub lean: f32,\\n    pub squash: f32,\\n    /// Stepped animation: 0 = smooth, 12 = \\\"on twos\\\" at 24 fps, etc.\\n    pub anim_fps: f32,\\n    /// Tilt the eyes toward the camera so they stay visible from above (0..1).\\n    pub eyes_to_camera: f32,\\n    /// Lean the whole body toward the camera (0..1): a 2D \\\"cheat\\\" for high camera angles.\\n    pub face_camera: f32,\\n    /// Skeleton: biped, or a creature with planted feet (spider, lizard, beetle) or a blob.\\n    pub body: BodyPlan,\\n    /// Leg pairs of creatures (0 = the body plan's usual number).\\n    pub legs: i32,\\n    /// Creature body length (m).\\n    pub body_length: f32,\\n    /// Tail length (m, 0 = none); swings with secondary motion.\\n    pub tail_length: f32,\\n    /// Antenna length (m, 0 = none).\\n    pub antenna_length: f32,\\n    /// Seconds a creature foot takes for one step.\\n    pub step_time: f32,\\n    /// Floppiness of tails, antennae and abdomens (0 = stiff, 2 = very floppy).\\n    pub wobble: f32,\\n    /// Second colour (shells, stripes, tail tips).\\n    pub accent: String,\\n    /// Held weapon and off hand.\\n    pub weapon: WeaponLook,\\n    /// Worn armour.\\n    pub gear: GearLook,\\n    /// Horns, spikes, wings... (any body plan).\\n    pub parts: Vec<crate::parts::Attach>,\\n    /// A motion clip (`SET/Clip`, see the `clips` tool) the character plays while it stands\\n    /// still with nothing to do, in place of the procedural idle (bipeds). Empty = none.\\n    pub idle_clip: String,\\n    /// A walk loop (`STYLE100/Old_Walk`...) the character walks with in place of the\\n    /// procedural walk while it heads forward on the ground, played as fast as it moves\\n    /// (bipeds). Empty = none.\\n    pub walk_clip: String,\\n    /// A run loop for speeds the walk loop would have to hurry through (a monster giving\\n    /// chase): it plays instead of the walk above the pace between the two (bipeds). Empty =\\n    /// none.\\n    pub run_clip: String,\\n    /// A captured fall the character dies with, in place of the procedural topple (bipeds;\\n    /// the hero has falls of its own). Empty = none.\\n    pub death_clip: String,\\n    /// Captured attacks by skill (`claw = \\\"QUATERNIUS/Zombie_Scratch\\\"`), played in place of the\\n    /// skill's move and timed so the clip's strike lands on the hit: the moment a hand reaches\\n    /// furthest ahead of the hips (a foot, for a clip tagged `kick`), or `@seconds` written\\n    /// after the name (bipeds). A list plays one per swing of a combo (`slash = [\\\"A\\\", \\\"B\\\",\\n    /// \\\"C\\\"]`: jab, cross, kick).\\n    pub attack_clips: std::collections::BTreeMap<String, PerSwing>,\\n    /// Moves by skill (anim/moves.toml names: `cleave = \\\"sweep\\\"`), played in place of the\\n    /// skill's own move; a list plays one per swing of a combo (`slash = [\\\"jab\\\", \\\"cross\\\",\\n    /// \\\"roundhouse\\\"]`). A captured attack for the skill wins over its move.\\n   