{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b9e13595-0340-496d-af7f-68f4098b35d3-93","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,112,117,112,112,101,116,46,114,115,10,50,56,52,58,105,109,112,108,32,68,101,102,97,117,108,116,32,102,111,114,32,80,117,112,112,101,116,68,101,102,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/puppet.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":284,\"content\":\"impl Default for PuppetDef {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"909eedde-27a6-43f9-9f35-c4a0ccd5bc0b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_109","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"PuppetDef syntax for the shirt parameter is confirmed.\n\nEngine patches will be applied in a batch. Game files will be written in parts: core.rs, intent.rs, fit_ui.rs, events.rs, and mod.rs. A directory module is preferred for flow. Rules will use serde default without deny_unknown_fields to allow iteration.\n\nRules will be a Tunable struct with many floats. Default trait methods will keep the starter crate compiling without changes. GameBox needs frozen(), fit_ui(), and tint(). PROGRESS.md and notes/decisions.md will be added at the work root. New files will be written directly; engine patches will use StrReplace. FitGame always has dt.\n\nFrozen play_pre returns before character tick, discarding inputs. Attract counts ticks via its idle counter in pre rather than the simulation tick. World time increments only during live flows and not paused states. Physics is skipped during pause, keeping player position stable. History records paused states correctly.\n\nDirect events auto-advance through a Card phase with a one-second timer before the event begins. The idle player does not press confirm during this card, and bots remain idle while the card plays. After the event, the flow becomes Result, frozen, and stars are recorded; tests check the status JSON for stars and wait until phase is result or done.\n\nThe status JSON will include world_time, music, save_serial, demo, hub, podium, day, balance_age, stiffness, and version. Playthrough tests will read these fields. Ghost samples will be capped at thirty per event to keep cloning lightweight. The script will be parsed statically from include_str into a OnceLock instead of living inside the game struct.\n\nTests will read the script and charts from disk for linting. The game will export a public `fit::SCRIPT` constant so tests can include it directly. The event list will also be exported for tests. Files will be split into chunks of roughly 400 to 700 lines if needed. The `events.rs` module will define an `Activity` struct with fields for event kind, timing, duration, score, stars, and completion state.\n\nThe Activity struct now includes generic fields for floats, integers, flags, shells, notes, hits, glasses, alive status, phase, sub-time, tips, lock, and ghost samples. Three functions are defined: start to initialize an activity, tick to advance it with player inputs, and bot to generate AI lean and button states.\n\nBalance is kept outside Activity so all events share it. tick_event receives a mutable reference to BalanceCore. Wobble amplitude will be set per event from rules. Rules will hold stiffness, damping, reach, tip_time, wobble, stick_curve, key_rate, key_return, and breath_secs.\n\nRules now includes pose, squat, plank, step, spin, lap, tide, paddle, tray, cannon, and physics fields like gust, bounce_gain, and rhythm thresholds. All are Tunable. Writing files and engine patches is starting.\n\nScoring correctness is the top priority for the long game file. The breath event uses a 40-second triangle-wave guide and a lung meter that fills while confirm is held and drains otherwise, clamped between zero and one. The bot holds confirm when the guide exceeds lungs plus a small offset and leans toward zero with PD control. The pose event lasts three poses of twenty seconds each; its ring center oscillates on two sine waves at different frequencies, and its radius interpolates from 0.30 to 0.18 over the pose duration.\n\nPose wobble peaks at 1.6x during the 12–17 second window of pose 1. Streak scoring adds a multiplier up to 3× based on time spent inside the ring, resetting when the player leaves. A tip breaks the streak for 1.5 seconds without scoring. The bot steers toward the ring center with PD control.\n\nCheck splits into four phases: 8 seconds still, target aiming, 6-second blindfold, and stepping. Still metric is `(1 - (sum/n)/0.08).clamp(0,1)`, with a velocity nudge at 5 seconds. Targets are placed at `[-0.7, 0.7, 0.0]` and must be held within 0.06 for 1.5 seconds each, capped at five seconds per target. The check score is a blend of fraction of targets hit and time efficiency.\n\nCheck blindfold repeats the still metric while hiding the puck. Step scoring uses eight alternating presses at 100 BPM; error is the absolute deviation from the beat, capped at a 0.15-second window, with idle yielding zero score.\n\nSkill and age formulas are defined. Game state supplies days_completed and total_stars.\n\nThe big stand event has five phases: 32 seconds of reused breath scoring, 20 seconds of pose with a rising gust, 40 seconds of step, 20 seconds of brace, and 30 seconds of stillness. A skip prompt appears at 15 seconds; any press forfeits the bonus. The bonus adds 200 points if the player avoids skipping and keeps the center-of-balance mean low.\n\nFinal score averages the five big stand phases, and stars derive from that average. Tipping costs score but does not end the event. The long stillness bot returns empty input. Age finale subtracts the final score divided by one hundred, clamped to ten years. A test will press during the skip window to verify forfeit. The script will be a Rust const array to avoid TOML parsing complexity.\n\nThe script will be written as TOML and parsed with the toml crate. A Python helper script will generate script.toml, charts.toml, and the room layout before Rust code is written. The Rust game will embed key lines directly while loading the full script for dialogue indexing. Tests will lint the raw file text.\n\nThe dialogue system will use a `Dialog` struct to track speaker, current line, characters revealed, and completion state. Text advances at 40 characters per second scaled by settings. Confirm reveals the full line immediately or advances to the next one. Syllables fire every two to three letters. Once all lines are exhausted, the flow advances automatically. A small `press(bit)` helper will be added for test inputs.\n\nThe integration test file will live at `pav_core/tests/fit.rs` so `cargo test -p pav_core --test fit` works. The `fit` module is public in `games/mod.rs`. Tests will rely on the public status JSON and helpers rather than private fields.\n\n`balance::step_balance` will be exported as a public function so balance unit tests can run without the world. Dev slider tests will read stiffness from status and send UiEvent inputs, relying on the public `InputFrame.ui`. A save round-trip test will snapshot the simulation, restore it, and verify that status matches; the existing pattern is reused. The serialized game will include a version field for GameBox restoration. The first batch of files to write is engine patches.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-02351f91-a72c-4212-86f6-7847704307b3-94","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_tools/src/agent_tools.rs","offset":240,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":231,"output_tokens":3089,"cache_read_input_tokens":155264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"520bfd68-685a-4af0-a157-1211440bd626"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-02351f91-a72c-4212-86f6-7847704307b3-94","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"240→    }\\n    if a.contains_key(\\\"hero_level\\\") {\\n        let mut g = s.sim.state.game.take().unwrap();\\n        pav_core::arpg::refresh_hero(&mut s.sim, &mut g, true);\\n        s.sim.state.game = Some(g);\\n    }\\n    if from > 0 && s.sim.state.game.as_ref().map(|g| g.place) != Some(Place::Level(from)) {\\n        s.sim.step(&pav_core::InputFrame {\\n            cmd: Some(pav_core::arpg::GameCmd::Travel(Place::Level(from).code())),\\n            ..Default::default()\\n250→        });\\n    }\\n    let mut bot = pav_core::arpg::bot::Bot::default();\\n    let snapshot = |s: &Session| {\\n        let g = s.sim.state.game.as_ref().unwrap();\\n        (g.place, s.sim.state.tick, g.hero.kills, g.hero.deaths, g.hero.level, g.hero.gold)\\n    };\\n    let mut start = snapshot(s);\\n    let mut dmg0 = 0.0f32;\\n    let mut rows = Vec::new();\",\"content_concise\":\"240→    }\\n    if a.contains_key(\\\"hero_level\\\") {\\n        let mut g = s.sim.state.game.take().unwrap();\\n        pav_core::arpg::refresh_hero(&mut s.sim, &mut g, true);\\n        s.sim.state.game = Some(g);\\n    }\\n    if from > 0 && s.sim.state.game.as_ref().map(|g| g.place) != Some(Place::Level(from)) {\\n        s.sim.step(&pav_core::InputFrame {\\n            cmd: Some(pav_core::arpg::GameCmd::Travel(Place::Level(from).code())),\\n            ..Default::default()\\n250→        });\\n    }\\n    let mut bot = pav_core::arpg::bot::Bot::default();\\n    let snapshot = |s: &Session| {\\n        let g = s.sim.state.game.as_ref().unwrap();\\n        (g.place, s.sim.state.tick, g.hero.kills, g.hero.deaths, g.hero.level, g.hero.gold)\\n    };\\n    let mut start = snapshot(s);\\n    let mut dmg0 = 0.0f32;\\n    let mut rows = Vec::new();\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_tools/src/agent_tools.rs\",\"offset\":240,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"    }\\n    if a.contains_key(\\\"hero_level\\\") {\\n        let mut g = s.sim.state.game.take().unwrap();\\n        pav_core::arpg::refresh_hero(&mut s.sim, &mut g, true);\\n        s.sim.state.game = Some(g);\\n    }\\n    if from > 0 && s.sim.state.game.as_ref().map(|g| g.place) != Some(Place::Level(from)) {\\n        s.sim.step(&pav_core::InputFrame {\\n            cmd: Some(pav_core::arpg::GameCmd::Travel(Place::Level(from).code())),\\n            ..Default::default()\\n        });\\n    }\\n    let mut bot = pav_core::arpg::bot::Bot::default();\\n    let snapshot = |s: &Session| {\\n        let g = s.sim.state.game.as_ref().unwrap();\\n        (g.place, s.sim.state.tick, g.hero.kills, g.hero.deaths, g.hero.level, g.hero.gold)\\n    };\\n    let mut start = snapshot(s);\\n    let mut dmg0 = 0.0f32;\\n    let mut rows = Vec::new();\\n\",\"total_lines\":531}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"1d3600d6-5f25-4afb-81e4-56cd35a47461"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_110","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Only t_input is a full literal. The rest uses Default.\n\nThe tools InputFrame literal is the only full one without Default. I'll fix it. Next I'll compose the game code. I'll patch Splash and BigSplash effects. Headless frame end needs fit drawing and UI events. UI work waits until core compiles. I'm applying all engine structural patches.\n\nI'm drafting the core modules: core.rs, intent.rs, fit_ui.rs, fit/mod.rs, and events.rs. I'll include events as a submodule in mod.rs. The scoring logic needs careful attention. I've sketched the shell physics for the game: gravity 8, friction 2, pools at fixed positions, and walls with half-bounce. Board 1 has three shells and one pool; board 2 has five shells with a moving pool. Each board gets twenty seconds.\n\nBoard 3 will have seven shells and bumpers. The bot will use a PD controller to aim at the nearest unpotted shell. Idle mode will keep tilt near zero so shells drift slowly; friction must be tuned so oscillating wobble does not pot shells.\n\nIdle wobble will be deadzoned at 0.2 so shells cannot drift into pools by accident. The paddle game uses vertical speed and horizontal lean to navigate gates at z = 10, 20, 30, 40, and 50. Gates sit within ±1.5 of center with width 1.2. A miss adds two seconds to the score. The race ends at z = 60 or the time limit.\n\nThe bot will lean toward the current gate using a clamped horizontal offset. In the tray game, glasses drift with board tilt and scripted jolts; the bot counters each jolt to keep them from spilling. The cannon platform oscillates vertically every 1.2 seconds, reaching its lowest point when the sine phase is 3π/2.\n\nThe cannon game uses a four-press sequence. The first three presses add power; the fourth leap launches the ball. While in the air, holding confirm tucks the body and rotates the lean. Entering the water scores based on tuck angle, height fallen, and timing. The bot will press near the platform bottom.\n\nThe floatie game spins the board to match a required direction that flips every fifteen seconds. The player must align the spin with that direction inside a six-to-nine band scaled by keyboard input. Catch windows appear at six, thirteen, twenty, twenty-seven, thirty-four, forty-one, and forty-eight seconds from either side. Pressing within 0.25 seconds of the correct side earns a ring.\n\nOut-of-band rings sink after three seconds. The floatie score is capped at 1000 and scaled by ring ratio, band time, and a 1.4 multiplier. The bot will spin the board with a cosine-sine vector at angular velocity 7.5 times the direction.\n\nThe lap game uses a step timer. Steps count only when the side changes. Rate is measured in the last second. Progress advances only if the rate stays between 1.6 and 2.4. Lean x steers laterally. Obstacles and ribbons appear at known z positions.\n\nThe lap game score is zone fraction times 700 plus ribbon count times 60 minus bump count times 80. The bot will press left and right alternately every half second to maintain the required two-step rate. Idle mode yields zero score because the rate falls outside the zone.\n\nThe step party game will use a deterministic chart generator producing one hundred notes across sixty-four seconds. Notes will be stored in charts.toml for the game to load. Each tick the judge checks whether a note sits within fifty-five milliseconds of the current time while the correct button is held, scoring it if the press lands within half a tick of the note.\n\nThe step-party chart generator will place forty quarter notes at 96 BPM followed by sixty eighth notes, keeping the full set within sixty-four seconds. Notes alternate lanes and double every eighth note.\n\nThe plank game requires holding both STEP_L and STEP_R to brace. Releasing the brace causes an immediate flop. The survival ring shrinks from forty to twenty over sixty seconds while board wobble increases with time.\n\nThe plank bot braces and centers the board to survive sixty seconds. It earns three stars for a full sixty-second survival, two for forty-five or more, and zero otherwise. Idle mode flops immediately.\n\nThe squats game uses a depth gauge from zero to one. Confirming lowers it; releasing raises it. A three-second guide cycles two seconds down and one up. A rep completes when the guide returns to top while the player stays within fifteen percent of the bottom. The band requires horizontal tilt under twenty-five percent during the rep. Rep score blends timing and band at seventy-thirty. Ten reps total into a score scaled by ten over one thousand. After the tenth rep the game sets an \"eleven\" gag flag.\n\nThe squats bot will hold confirm while the guide descends. A Python script was considered for writing the large Rust file but rejected in favor of the Write tool. Patches and smaller files will be handled first, followed by the larger modules. Adding an `any` field to InputFrame is safe because serde is field-based.\n\nThe attract-mode exit check now includes `input.any` and `input.pressed != 0`, so a button press alone can wake the game. Stick input is gated at 0.3 length for both `move_dir` and `lean`. A touch-only flag will be set when the device is touch and no keyboard or pad input has been seen.\n\nAttract mode will keep running behind the card. Touch input alone will not trigger an exit; the game only wakes when a keyboard, pad, or mouse button is pressed. The settings button on the attract card will be tappable and open the settings screen via UiEvent::Click. UI rectangle publishing is deferred for now.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1ae4543b-3d46-4113-9402-4b5faae8f157-95","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"sticky_cue|pub struct Courses|cue_serial","glob":"**/course.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3479,"output_tokens":2506,"cache_read_input_tokens":155392,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"2fa35c2e-df0f-47c0-b019-2e59093a5366"}
