{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0ea15987-5e4a-4f66-ab67-d033870a02f5-102","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"9803d2ea-4cf0-4d99-86d9-7c42cfc5a581"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_118","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Beginning to write everything.\n\nPlanning parallel writes for engine patches and core files. The large game module will be split into two or three files. Drafting mod.rs tightly to cover the bot playthrough. Writing events.rs for simulation logic and mod.rs for flow control. Day time duration checks out at roughly 17 minutes. The bot presses SCHEDULE once when in Island flow, then advances to Schedule.\n\nBot will set focus to the next event index and press CONFIRM to start fast travel. End Day is confirmed once all daily events are played and minutes reach the goal. Menu items will be rebuilt from state each frame with a stored focus index; MENU_DOWN increments it, and CONFIRM triggers the active item's action ID.\n\nAssigned unique u16 action IDs to every menu item, from 1 through 100. IDs 1–5 cover the main menu, 10–20 handle slots and names, 30–47 cover game actions like Schedule and Quit, and 100 plus an event index identifies individual events.\n\nAssigned action IDs 60 through 92 for dev tools, end day, retry, checkout, stay, together, and pass. Sliders will use IDs starting at 300. Started drafting the bot input function; it returns empty inputs during attract mode and pauses, then branches by flow.\n\nFleshed out the bot input function for each flow state. Title presses CONFIRM. Event, Check, and Finale delegate to the events module's bot helper. Schedule focuses the next event index and presses MENU_DOWN or CONFIRM accordingly. Island presses SCHEDULE. Result presses CONFIRM to return. Credits does nothing. All other flows press CONFIRM. Also noted that dialogue will confirm every tick.\n\nThe bot will skip the intro after a few frames. After the finale, Result confirms return to Island rather than retry. On day five, the check reveal advances into Finale instead of returning to Island. After the ending dialogue, the bot auto-confirms checkout if age is forty or under, otherwise extended stay, then proceeds to Credits with a win.\n\nThe checkout and extended stay lines are now defined: \"The rowboat is ready.\" for ages forty or under, and \"Stay a little longer.\" for older ages. A dev slider is not available for age, so testing both endings will require a different approach.\n\nThe plan's dev tools will be used to test both endings. A \"set age\" cheat will force ages thirty and seventy into the same day-five ending jump, bypassing the normal checkout dialogue.\n\nReal dev menu buttons will be added to jump directly to the checkout and extended endings. The test will click these buttons, confirm through the dialogue, and assert the correct win state and ending name. Both ending scripts will run through this path. The checkout bot will still trigger the checkout flow naturally. A shared `begin_ending` function will handle both paths.\n\nPlay-together and hub medley tests will run deterministically across two full cycles. Long tests will reset history_seconds to zero. The build parser will return an error on room parse failure.\n\nDesigning a compact beach room map for the test environment. The layout uses water, sand, and player markers in a small grid. A 40 by 30 block grid was considered too heavy for physics, so a smaller 20 by 16 grid with 320 static blocks is preferred to keep tests fast.\n\nThe test room is finalized at 32 by 24 blocks. Water will be #7ec8e3, sand #f0d7a8, and the deck #fff6ea. A pavilion box and a few trees will be added as extra objects.\n\n`lib.rs` and `games/mod.rs` will expose `fit_ui` and `fit` modules. The event bot and tick logic in `events.rs` need careful writing. A `stars_of` helper will compute star ratings from activity kind, score, and time. Plank stars will come from the activity status rather than the raw score.\n\nIdle plank will end instantly on the first tick if the player does not brace, since the event is scored immediately. Other idle events will still run their full duration. The test room may be shrunk to 16 by 12 blocks to reduce physics overhead. SimConfig physics settings will remain untouched.\n\nThe physics cost is acceptable with one kinematic character and a small room. I will generate script.toml lines via Python in the shell. The fit_ui module will draw the title, body text, menu buttons, puck circle, prompts, touch card, and demo ribbon.\n\nEgui clicks will feed back into `InputFrame.ui`, while headless tests can read the fit state directly from `Headless::frame`. Browser tests will use window rects published by weblink. UI scaling derives a factor from the smaller of width and height over 1920 by 1080, so small frames shrink proportionally. Cards will use white backgrounds with radius 36 times that scale. The implementation will live in `pav_ui/fit_ui.rs`.\n\nHeadless mode will call fit_ui::draw and append the resulting text labels into reading.hud. The has_ui check will include hud.fit to suppress touch controls when a fit screen is active. Browser rendering will be handled in app.rs, which publishes UI rectangles. I am starting with engine patches and core files, then compiling pav_core before writing UI and app code. Estimated line counts are roughly 800 for events.rs, 900 for mod.rs, 120 for core.rs, 80 for intent.rs, 80 for the fit_ui model, and 400 for tests.\n\nThe script struct will hold dialog lines for nine characters plus titles and names. A OnceLock static will load it from script.toml once, shared across WASM and tests.\n\nThe script is excluded from save data. A `title_for` helper will pick a title by score, clamping to the 30 deadpan titles in the plan. The save struct will gain `today` and `last_day` fields, set at boot from input, since the simulation ignores the clock.\n\nTests will set the absence fields by downcasting to `FitGame` and mutating `today` and `last_day`, since those fields are public. The real comment logic remains in the play path.\n\nThe absence comment will be written into the status line whenever the day gap is nonzero, so tests can read it without rendering the UI. The save struct will derive Clone and avoid holding a OnceLock inside it. Activity notes are cloned on every snapshot, but one hundred notes per event is small enough to keep history updates fast.\n\nA const SFX list of at least thirty sound effect names will be added to the game module. Each entry is a u16 audio id that the game fires at the correct moments. An audio test will verify every id is non-silent by calling sounds_for.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fd3f033d-13ef-4d17-b806-36e71b5374b0-103","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"master|volume|render","glob":"**/pav_audio/**/*test*"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fd3f033d-13ef-4d17-b806-36e71b5374b0-104","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pav_audio::","glob":"**/*test*.rs","head_limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":194,"output_tokens":3622,"cache_read_input_tokens":166016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"5d153d7f-af89-45e9-8f3e-c0d4330ff31b"}
