{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_119","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No audio tests exist. The mixer can be changed.\n\nApplying the 0.8 sfx bus to all existing sounds would make shardfall too quiet. The fit game should set that gain when it starts, but the mixer lives in the app rather than the simulation.\n\nThe default mixer sfx bus will be 1.0 so other games remain unaffected. The fit game will request 0.8 and the app will apply it. Music defaults to 0.10 during playback. A unit test will verify this by comparing renders with music at 0.10 versus 1.0. I am now writing the engine patches and game files.\n\nThe big stand animation will reuse existing tick functions through a shared `tick_kind` dispatcher. Stillness phase tracks elapsed time to score quality.\n\nStillness forfeits only on button presses, not lean. The bot can lean to cancel wobble without losing. Idle wobble may tip and cost score, but it does not forfeit. A bonus applies for staying upright. The bot will show the skip prompt without pressing.\n\nWorld time will only advance during active simulation flows such as Check, Event, Finale, Countdown, Card, Island, Attract, and Wake. Title menus are excluded because they are frozen. The total playthrough duration is estimated at roughly seventeen minutes.\n\nIsland time is short because the bot fast-travels there. The schedule menu pauses world time, so that interval does not count. Physics runs only during events, which is the bulk of the playthrough. I am now starting to write the implementation files.\n\nThe balance age formula is now implemented. It clamps skill between 0 and 1, then computes age from a power curve, subtracts days completed and stars, and rounds to an integer between 18 and 99. A test will compare bot lean against idle during the check event to verify that better input lowers age. Age also depends on total days completed.\n\nThe check event lasts about 37 seconds for idle and 28 seconds for the bot. Idle targets time out at five seconds each, so their metric stays zero. I confirmed that `powf(1.1)` is available on f32. I am now writing all the implementation files.\n\nThe goal plan checklist will be updated as each item is verified. Code style will match surrounding conventions and rustfmt will run afterward. NPCs will be spawned with PuppetDef after room build to populate the island, and the player puppet will be set after spawn.\n\nThe player puppet is assigned to the character field after spawn. The v1 implementation is complete and ready for writing. A run.sh script will execute fit tests in the core package with two threads.\n\nThe run.sh script will filter cargo test output to show only failures and a final pass count. I am checking whether cargo -q suppresses all passing test names or still prints them.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-005a2ba3-e27a-461e-85c7-8302fd500031-105","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\\[workspace.lints|clippy","glob":"**/Cargo.toml"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3810,"output_tokens":1930,"cache_read_input_tokens":166144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"7dbe035d-14a9-44db-b6d6-e6f9e660495b"}
