{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_121","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Warnings might still fail if denied at the crate level.\n\npav_core does not deny warnings by default. The build profile uses opt-level 1 for game code and 3 for dependencies, with incremental compilation disabled. I will now write the patches and game files, including events.rs and mod.rs. I am also considering how the frozen state should behave during Card overlays.\n\nCard, result, and menus will freeze the game. Countdown, event, check, island, attract, and finale will not. Countdown runs in pre without freezing world_time. During events, player input is replaced with zero movement and no jump to prevent jumps. Brace buttons are engine-free so stripping them avoids crouch issues.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d2f4109c-42ee-47f2-bc41-9f65caa602a2-107","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub enabled|pub struct History","glob":"**/history.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":455,"output_tokens":447,"cache_read_input_tokens":172032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"2c2acdf0-a59a-4d8f-98d8-ac399ed5cc8f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d2f4109c-42ee-47f2-bc41-9f65caa602a2-107","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,104,105,115,116,111,114,121,46,114,115,10,49,49,58,112,117,98,32,115,116,114,117,99,116,32,72,105,115,116,111,114,121,32,123,10,49,57,58,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,32,101,110,97,98,108,101,100,58,32,98,111,111,108,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/history.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":11,\"content\":\"pub struct History {\"},{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"    pub enabled: bool,\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"a659628c-5eb0-4938-8cdc-8a98518ae22e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_122","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"history.enabled is public and can be set to false.\n\nhistory_seconds will also be set to 0. Recording storage is acceptable at roughly 5MB for 60k ticks, so it will remain enabled. The bot's confirm input needs edge detection to prevent repeated presses on menus.\n\nEach step advances exactly one screen. The bot will press SCHEDULE on frame 1 to open the schedule.\n\nFrame 2 will press MENU_DOWN if the schedule focus is wrong. Confirm on frame 3 starts the event. The bot returns empty during countdowns and card auto to avoid triggering events prematurely. The credits screen is handled by returning empty since the outcome is already won.\n\nThe outcome is set to Won before the credits screen appears. The bot loop stops immediately on the next iteration.\n\nStamps increment when leaving a day. After the finale, stamps reach 5 and the credits screen follows.\n\nAll events are marked as played upon completion. The daily check event is recorded once.\n\nThe test will cover all 12 event IDs including the daily check. Day 1 plays breath and pose. Day 2 plays squat and plank. Day 3 plays step, floatie, and lap. Day 4 plays tide, paddle, tray, and cannon. Day 5 plays bigstand. Each day's check is recorded too.\n\nMinutes are calculated as one plus stars per event. A zero-star event still banks one minute. The bot replays events if minutes remain short.\n\nThe bot will select Back on the result screen. The island flip-flop collection uses five positions and triggers within 1.2 units.\n\nUnit tests will teleport the bot to flip-flop positions and confirm to verify collection. Ghost replay will record samples every six ticks during events starting on day three or later, saving a new best ghost if the score improves. The test will play an event twice to confirm the ghost area matches.\n\nThe ghost matching logic will be unit-tested as a pure function. A status list will track ghosts with area and visibility flags. The test will record one medley playthrough, then verify the filter matches areas correctly.\n\nA pure unit test will cover the ghost matching logic. A simulation test will inject a ghost directly into the public `FitGame` state to avoid replaying an event. The `sim.state.play` path is accessible for this.\n\nGhost recording will happen naturally inside the event tick rather than being injected manually. The existing bot event tests already run each activity, so the ghost area can be verified at the end of those runs by checking that the recorded ghost area matches the event index. A separate long test will cover play-together.\n\nThe play-together test will run two bots through paddle, tide, and cannon for roughly 300 seconds. Podium scores will be sorted descending with names present to reduce flakiness.\n\nDeterminism is host-independent because only sim.state.rng is used. Wobble phases are seeded once at activity start from the simulation random number generator and stored in BalanceCore. Snapshots restore this state automatically.\n\nTilt will be applied every tick during the pre-phase.\n\nTilt values are written to the character animation during the pre-phase. If the simulation freezes after that phase, the tilt persists until the next unfrozen tick. During active events, the character tick might overwrite these fields when it rebuilds the animation, so I need to verify whether the tick preserves or resets them.\n\nTilt will be applied in the post-phase so it survives the character tick. However, the freeze path returns before post, which would skip menu updates.\n\nMenu logic will run in the pre-phase so it survives freezes. Event simulation stays in the post-phase because events are not frozen. Pause handling also belongs in pre since the card is frozen and the countdown is not. The card timer can live in pre too.\n\nFlow timers will live exclusively in the pre-phase so they keep advancing during freezes. Event score and physics will stay in the post-phase. Countdown timers will advance only in pre to avoid double-counting. The attract demo will run in post while pre handles input to exit.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The engine is still stock. I’m adding the balance game and the small engine hooks it needs, then I’ll compile the sim tests."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6b6cebda-0eb9-4ed6-8616-bab3df701649-108","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs","old_string":"    pub const DODGE: u32 = 1 << 13;\n    pub const POTION: u32 = 1 << 14;\n\n    pub const NAMES: &[(&str, u32)] = &[","new_string":"    pub const DODGE: u32 = 1 << 13;\n    pub const POTION: u32 = 1 << 14;\n    /// Wobble Minutes: menu and balance actions (bits 15–28).\n    pub const CONFIRM: u32 = 1 << 15;\n    pub const BACK: u32 = 1 << 16;\n    pub const MENU_UP: u32 = 1 << 17;\n    pub const MENU_DOWN: u32 = 1 << 18;\n    pub const MENU_LEFT: u32 = 1 << 19;\n    pub const MENU_RIGHT: u32 = 1 << 20;\n    pub const TAB_L: u32 = 1 << 21;\n    pub const TAB_R: u32 = 1 << 22;\n    pub const PAUSE: u32 = 1 << 23;\n    pub const SCHEDULE: u32 = 1 << 24;\n    pub const WAVE: u32 = 1 << 25;\n    pub const STEP_L: u32 = 1 << 26;\n    pub const STEP_R: u32 = 1 << 27;\n    pub const HUB_GO: u32 = 1 << 28;\n\n    pub const NAMES: &[(&str, u32)] = &["}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6b6cebda-0eb9-4ed6-8616-bab3df701649-109","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs","old_string":"        (\"dodge\", DODGE),\n        (\"potion\", POTION),\n    ];","new_string":"        (\"dodge\", DODGE),\n        (\"potion\", POTION),\n        (\"confirm\", CONFIRM),\n        (\"back\", BACK),\n        (\"menu_up\", MENU_UP),\n        (\"menu_down\", MENU_DOWN),\n        (\"menu_left\", MENU_LEFT),\n        (\"menu_right\", MENU_RIGHT),\n        (\"tab_l\", TAB_L),\n        (\"tab_r\", TAB_R),\n        (\"pause\", PAUSE),\n        (\"schedule\", SCHEDULE),\n        (\"wave\", WAVE),\n        (\"step_l\", STEP_L),\n        (\"step_r\", STEP_R),\n        (\"hub_go\", HUB_GO),\n    ];"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6b6cebda-0eb9-4ed6-8616-bab3df701649-110","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs","old_string":"    /// A menu action this tick (Shardfall: equip, sell, travel...), queued one per tick.\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n    pub cmd: Option<crate::arpg::GameCmd>,\n}","new_string":"    /// A menu action this tick (Shardfall: equip, sell, travel...), queued one per tick.\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n    pub cmd: Option<crate::arpg::GameCmd>,\n    /// Screen-space lean for balance games (−1..1, x right, y up). Shaped by the host.\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub lean: Vec2,\n    /// The host saw a real wake-up (key, button, stick past the deadzone, click, or a mouse move).\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub any: bool,\n    /// Pointer hit on the game's own UI. Copy, so replays keep it.\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub ui: Option<UiEvent>,\n    /// Audio-clock position in the current song, when the host has one. Tests leave this empty.\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub song_pos: Option<f32>,\n    /// Last physical device: 0 unset, 1 pad, 2 keyboard, 3 mouse, 4 touch.\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub device: u8,\n    /// Hub frame: 0 none, 1 waiting for the session clock, 2 go.\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub hub: u8,\n}\n\n/// A pointer event on a sim-owned control. `u16` ids are assigned by the game.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub enum UiEvent {\n    Hover(u16),\n    Click(u16),\n    Slider(u16, f32),\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6b6cebda-0eb9-4ed6-8616-bab3df701649-111","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs","old_string":"    pub fn just(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\n        self.pressed & b != 0\n    }\n}","new_string":"    pub fn just(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\n        self.pressed & b != 0\n    }\n\n    /// True when this tick should leave attract mode or count as \"a press\".\n    pub fn woke(&self) -> bool {\n        self.any || self.pressed != 0 || self.lean.length() > 0.3 || self.move_dir.length() > 0.3\n    }\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":674,"output_tokens":3788,"cache_read_input_tokens":172416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"d2823378-50c5-4611-828d-00266cf10b8d"}
