{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a1b47a62-b63d-4c76-8909-5beed86b3af7-133","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"        let hud = crate::frame::HudFrame {\",\"new_string\":\"        let mut hud = crate::frame::HudFrame {\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"        let hud = crate::frame::HudFrame {\",\"old_line\":983,\"new_string\":\"        let mut hud = crate::frame::HudFrame {\",\"new_line\":983,\"context_before\":\"            .map(|r| crate::frame::RoomInfo { id: r.id, key: r.key.clone(), def: r.def.clone(), quarters: r.place.quarters });\\n        let c = &self.state.courses;\\n        let invuln = self.player().and_then(|p| p.character.as_ref()).map(|c| c.invuln).unwrap_or(0.0);\\n\",\"context_after\":\"            course: c.hud(self.state.tick, self.dt()),\\n            last_result: c.last.clone(),\\n            message: c.message.clone(),\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"a71b4e72-236d-474a-aa6c-79e6ee190a8d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_127","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing the core Rust modules: fit_ui.rs, core.rs, intent.rs, events.rs, and mod.rs. Also creating data files and tests.\n\nAdding a `camera_yaw` field to `FitUi`. Fixing `t_input` and audio events so `pav_audio` compiles. Writing the full game code next, then generating `script.toml` via Python with a schema for names, titles, and pip lines.\n\nDefined the `Script` struct with a `Speaker` sub-struct for dialogue lines. Set the exact scene names and event IDs in the game module.\n\nDesigning the `Activity` struct for events.rs. The step-party bot will read upcoming notes within one tick. Song position will use `input.song_pos` when available, otherwise fall back to `act.t` for deterministic behavior. Step notes will be generated from a fixed pattern in `start()`, with optional chart data loaded from `charts.toml` as `[time, lane]` pairs.\n\nThe step-party chart will be generated in Rust as the source of truth. A matching `charts.toml` will be written via Python so the game can load it. The same formula will produce both outputs.\n\nThe step-party chart formula is now concrete: 100 notes at 96 BPM, with quarter-note intervals for the first 32 beats and eighth-note intervals for the rest. This yields roughly 42 seconds total. Floatie catches will also be fixed so the bot can press them.\n\nDrafting the full events.rs module now. Adding menu item activation in mod.rs and button constants. Rules will derive Default and load from rules.toml, falling back to defaults if parsing fails.\n\nThe simulation history is set to 8.0 seconds. Player input will be stripped in the pre phase. The double-fit_ui fix is complete.\n\nFitItem now carries a normalized rect in the 0..1 range with top-left origin and y-down. The view scales these rects to pixels. A shared Ctx struct will bundle lean, pressed, held, and dt to avoid bloated function signatures across events.\n\nThe tick function signature is now concrete: it takes `&mut Activity`, `&mut BalanceCore`, `&mut ScoreBits`, `&mut Sim`, and the input state. ScoreBits will likely become fields on `Activity`. Balance logic runs at the start of each tick. Events are pushed into `SimEvent`. No entity IDs are needed since nothing is spawned.\n\nA Python generator script will produce the remaining data files—script, charts, room, animation, and props—while Rust is written. The Activity struct is being drafted with fields for event kind, elapsed time, duration, score, stars, completion flag, and a score accumulator.\n\nThe Activity struct is being expanded with fields for phase, lungs, depth, reps, streak, spin, rings, and step timing. It also stores the step-party note list and hit counters.\n\nThe Activity struct is being expanded with fields for zone timing, progress, lateral movement, ribbons, bumps, shells, pools, gates, missed attempts, glass targets, jolts, dive scores, and dive physics.\n\nThe Activity struct is being expanded with fields for leaping, forfeit, stillness tracking, target timing, step hit and error counters, nudging, tips, lock, ghost samples, phase scores, and gag state. A Shell struct is also defined to represent shell physics.\n\nGhostSample stores lean, position, and timestamp for ghost replay. Activity will be built in a start() function rather than deriving Default. EventId is now an enum with key, from_key, and name methods.\n\nEventId now has `blurb` and `all` methods. The `start()` function will seed notes, shells, and gates from the simulation RNG so replay is deterministic. Paddle gates are spaced 8 units apart along the Z axis with random X offsets between -1.4 and 1.4. Tide shells are placed at startup. The tick function will be a large match on event kind.\n\nDefined the star rating logic. Plank events award 3 stars for 55 seconds or more, 2 for 40 seconds or more, 1 for 25 seconds or more, and 0 otherwise. Other events use score thresholds: 850 points or more for 3 stars, 650 for 2, 400 for 1, and below for 0. Big stand uses score directly, while Check converts skill to a score by multiplying by 1000.\n\nStarted drafting the bot input helper `bot_lean` and a PD balance controller `pd`.\n\nThe bot's PD balance controller now subtracts wobble and velocity from the target lean, clamped to unit length. BalanceCore stores cob, vel, tip state, time, amplitude, phase, kick_in, and gust. A wobble_axis helper blends two sine waves at 1.3 and 2.9 Hz for the step-party wobble.\n\nKick mechanics now trigger randomly every 1–2 seconds, adding a small random velocity and resetting the timer. A `step_raw` helper will disable wobble and kicks for settle testing. Tip pulses last one tick, reset the timer, and shove the center of balance back inside 0.7 radius to prevent chaining; events read the `tipped` flag to set lock.\n\nGust is added to the balance accumulator. A quick Python script will validate feel numbers in parallel with writing. The full-lean test uses zero amplitude and no kicks, expecting a lean of 1 for two seconds without tipping. The release test checks that the center of balance settles within 0.8 seconds when leaning back. The wander test uses amplitude 0.12 over eight seconds, targeting mean below 0.08 and peak below 0.12.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1b504cbe-0cc6-480b-9f1b-e2372a419c45-134","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - << 'PY'\nimport math\nk,d,reach,dt=40,8.5,0.92,1/60\ndef run(secs, lean, amp=0, gust=0, kicks=False):\n    cob=vel=0\n    tip_t=0\n    tipped=False\n    peak=0\n    t=0\n    kick_in=1.2\n    samples=[]\n    while t<secs:\n        w=amp*(0.7*math.sin(2*math.pi*1.3*t)+0.3*math.sin(2*math.pi*2.9*t+1.7))\n        acc=(lean*reach+w-cob)*k - vel*d + gust\n        if kicks:\n            kick_in-=dt\n            if kick_in<=0:\n                vel+=0.1\n                kick_in=1.5\n        vel+=acc*dt\n        cob+=vel*dt\n        if abs(cob)>1:\n            tip_t+=dt\n            if tip_t>=0.35:\n                tipped=True\n        else:\n            tip_t=0\n        peak=max(peak,abs(cob))\n        samples.append(abs(cob))\n        t+=dt\n    return cob, peak, tipped, sum(samples)/len(samples), max(samples)\n\n# reach 90%\ncob=vel=0\nt=0\nhit=None\npeak=0\nwhile t<2:\n    acc=(1*reach-cob)*k - vel*d\n    vel+=acc*dt; cob+=vel*dt\n    if hit is None and cob>=0.90: hit=t\n    peak=max(peak,cob)\n    t+=dt\nprint('hit90', hit, 'peak', peak, 'overshoot', (peak-reach)/reach)\n\ncob=vel=0\nfor i in range(int(0.8*60)):\n    acc=(reach-cob)*k-vel*d\n    vel+=acc*dt; cob+=vel*dt\nprint('at 0.8 held', cob)\n# release from steady-ish\nfor i in range(int(0.8*60)):\n    acc=(0-cob)*k-vel*d\n    vel+=acc*dt; cob+=vel*dt\nprint('after release 0.8', cob)\n\nprint('full 3s', run(3,1))\nprint('wander', run(10,0,0.12,0,True))\nprint('wander nokick', run(10,0,0.12,0,False))\nprint('gust', run(1.2,1,0,30,False))\nPY","description":"Numerically check the balance model"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":342,"output_tokens":4210,"cache_read_input_tokens":184448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"2ef11f67-d353-4617-a490-1085b8ee607b"}
