{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a1ac248b-0421-4087-b43f-d8c1e8af0fc6-7","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Games built on the engine: the hook a new game implements, and the list of games.\\n//!\\n//! A game is a struct holding its rules' state (`Clone` and serde, like everything in\\n//! `SimState`) that implements [`Game`], plus a `build` function that makes its scene. One\\n//! line in [`GAMES`] and `load scene=<key>` starts it in the tools, the window\\n//! (`shardfall --scene <key>`) and the browser (`?scene=<key>`). `starter.rs` is the template\\n//! to copy; `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` is the guide. Shardfall (`crate::arpg`) predates this hook and\\n//! keeps its own.\\n\\n10→use std::any::Any;\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse anyhow::Result;\\nuse serde::de::{DeserializeOwned, Error as _};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Deserializer, Serialize, Serializer};\\n\\nuse crate::entity::EntityId;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\n20→use crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub mod fit;\\npub mod starter;\\n\\n/// Every game the engine knows. `load scene=<key>` (or `<key>/<rest>`) builds it.\\npub static GAMES: &[Entry] = &[\\n    entry::<starter::Starter>(\\\"Starter: collect every shard while slimes chase you (the template to copy).\\\", starter::build),\\n    entry::<fit::FitGame>(\\\"Wobble Minutes: a five-day balance stay at Tippy Cay.\\\", fit::build),\\n];\\n30→\\n/// Still playing, won or lost.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\npub enum Outcome {\\n    #[default]\\n    Playing,\\n    Won,\\n    Lost,\\n}\\n40→\\n/// A game's rules. Every method has a default, so a game implements only what it uses.\\n///\\n/// The engine calls `pre` and `post` once per tick (60 a second) from `Sim::step`; everything\\n/// else is read-only. While `pre` or `post` runs, the game is out of `sim.state.play`, so use\\n/// `self` for the game's own state and `sim` for the world.\\npub trait Game: Clone + Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send + Sync + 'static {\\n    /// The scene key that starts the game: `load scene=<KEY>`, `--scene <KEY>`, `?scene=<KEY>`.\\n    const KEY: &'static str;\\n\\n50→    /// Before characters move: read the player's input and decide what the characters the\\n    /// game drives do this tick. A returned input replaces that character's own (its `ai`\\n    /// brain, or the player's keys for the player).\\n    fn pre(\\n        &mut self,\\n        _sim: &mut Sim,\\n        _input: &InputFrame,\\n        _dt: f32,\\n        _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>,\\n    ) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame> {\\n60→        BTreeMap::new()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// After physics: the rules (pickups, damage, score, win and loss). Push `SimEvent`s for\\n    /// sounds and effects (`Coin`, `Pickup`, `Hit`, `Explosion`...).\\n    fn post(&mut self, _sim: &mut Sim, _dt: f32, _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {}\\n\\n    /// HUD lines: drawn at the top left of the window, returned by the `play` tool.\\n    fn hud(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String> {\\n        Vec::new()\\n70→    }\\n\\n    /// The game's state for tools and tests (`play`), as JSON.\\n    fn status(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        serde_json::Value::Null\\n    }\\n\\n    fn outcome(&self) -> Outcome {\\n        Outcome::Playing\\n    }\\n80→\\n    /// The input a good player would give this tick. `play bot=true` and the tests drive the\\n    /// player with it; teach it every new rule, and keep a test that it wins.\\n    fn bot(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame {\\n        InputFrame::default()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// When true, `Sim::step` skips characters and physics after `pre`. Menus still run in `pre`.\\n    fn frozen(&self) -> bool {\\n        false\\n90→    }\\n\\n    /// Painter UI for this game, if it has one.\\n    fn fit_ui(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Option<crate::fit_ui::FitUi> {\\n        None\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Extra tint for a character (ghost lanes).\\n    fn tint(&self, _id: EntityId) -> Option<([f32; 3], f32)> {\\n        None\\n100→    }\\n}\\n\\n/// One line of [`GAMES`]: made with [`entry`].\\npub struct Entry {\\n    pub key: &'static str,\\n    pub about: &'static str,\\n    /// Builds the scene and sets `sim.state.play`. The `&str` is the rest of the scene name\\n    /// after `<key>/` (a level number, say), if any.\\n    pub build: fn(&mut Sim, Option<&str>) -> Result<()>,\\n110→    load: fn(ciborium::Value) -> Result<GameBox, String>,\\n}\\n\\n/// A [`GAMES`] line for the game type `G`.\\npub const fn entry<G: Game>(about: &'static str, build: fn(&mut Sim, Option<&str>) -> Result<()>) -> Entry {\\n    Entry { key: G::KEY, about, build, load: load_as::<G> }\\n}\\n\\nfn load_as<G: Game>(v: ciborium::Value) -> Result<GameBox, String> {\\n    v.deserialized::<G>().map(GameBox::new).map_err(|e| e.to_string())\\n120→}\\n\\n/// A game's level text: `crates/pav_core/src/games/<key>.toml` read from disk when the program\\n/// runs from the repository's root (`pav`, `cargo run`), so an edit shows at the next `load`\\n/// with no rebuild; else `built_in`, the copy embedded with `include_str!` (tests, the browser,\\n/// a shipped executable).\\npub fn level_text(key: &str, built_in: &'static str) -> std::borrow::Cow<'static, str> {\\n    #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n    if let Ok(text) = std::fs::read_to_string(format!(\\\"crates/pav_core/src/games/{key}.toml\\\")) {\\n        return text.into();\\n130→    }\\n    #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n    let _ = key; // the browser has no files\\n    built_in.into()\\n}\\n\\n/// The game registered under `key`.\\npub fn find(key: &str) -> Option<&'static Entry> {\\n    GAMES.iter().find(|g| g.key == key)\\n}\\n140→\\n/// A running game in `SimState::play`: clones (rewind, snapshots) and serializes (snapshot\\n/// files, the state hash) through the game's own derives.\\npub struct GameBox(Box<dyn DynGame>);\\n\\nimpl GameBox {\\n    pub fn new<G: Game>(game: G) -> Self {\\n        Self(Box::new(game))\\n    }\\n\\n150→    pub fn key(&self) -> &'static str {\\n        self.0.key()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The game as its own type (None for another game).\\n    pub fn get<G: Game>(&self) -> Option<&G> {\\n        self.0.as_any().downcast_ref()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn get_mut<G: Game>(&mut self) -> Option<&mut G> {\\n160→        self.0.as_any_mut().downcast_mut()\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Games built on the engine: the hook a new game implements, and the list of games.\\n//!\\n//! A game is a struct holding its rules' state (`Clone` and serde, like everything in\\n//! `SimState`) that implements [`Game`], plus a `build` function that makes its scene. One\\n//! line in [`GAMES`] and `load scene=<key>` starts it in the tools, the window\\n//! (`shardfall --scene <key>`) and the browser (`?scene=<key>`). `starter.rs` is the template\\n//! to copy; `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` is the guide. Shardfall (`crate::arpg`) predates this hook and\\n//! keeps its own.\\n\\n10→use std::any::Any;\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse anyhow::Result;\\nuse serde::de::{DeserializeOwned, Error as _};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Deserializer, Serialize, Serializer};\\n\\nuse crate::entity::EntityId;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\n20→use crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub mod fit;\\npub mod starter;\\n\\n/// Every game the engine knows. `load scene=<key>` (or `<key>/<rest>`) builds it.\\npub static GAMES: &[Entry] = &[\\n    entry::<starter::Starter>(\\\"Starter: collect every shard while slimes chase you (the template to copy).\\\", starter::build),\\n    entry::<fit::FitGame>(\\\"Wobble Minutes: a five-day balance stay at Tippy Cay.\\\", fit::build),\\n];\\n30→\\n/// Still playing, won or lost.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\npub enum Outcome {\\n    #[default]\\n    Playing,\\n    Won,\\n    Lost,\\n}\\n40→\\n/// A game's rules. Every method has a default, so a game implements only what it uses.\\n///\\n/// The engine calls `pre` and `post` once per tick (60 a second) from `Sim::step`; everything\\n/// else is read-only. While `pre` or `post` runs, the game is out of `sim.state.play`, so use\\n/// `self` for the game's own state and `sim` for the world.\\npub trait Game: Clone + Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send + Sync + 'static {\\n    /// The scene key that starts the game: `load scene=<KEY>`, `--scene <KEY>`, `?scene=<KEY>`.\\n    const KEY: &'static str;\\n\\n50→    /// Before characters move: read the player's input and decide what the characters the\\n    /// game drives do this tick. A returned input replaces that character's own (its `ai`\\n    /// brain, or the player's keys for the player).\\n    fn pre(\\n        &mut self,\\n        _sim: &mut Sim,\\n        _input: &InputFrame,\\n        _dt: f32,\\n        _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>,\\n    ) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame> {\\n60→        BTreeMap::new()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// After physics: the rules (pickups, damage, score, win and loss). Push `SimEvent`s for\\n    /// sounds and effects (`Coin`, `Pickup`, `Hit`, `Explosion`...).\\n    fn post(&mut self, _sim: &mut Sim, _dt: f32, _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {}\\n\\n    /// HUD lines: drawn at the top left of the window, returned by the `play` tool.\\n    fn hud(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String> {\\n        Vec::new()\\n70→    }\\n\\n    /// The game's state for tools and tests (`play`), as JSON.\\n    fn status(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        serde_json::Value::Null\\n    }\\n\\n    fn outcome(&self) -> Outcome {\\n        Outcome::Playing\\n    }\\n80→\\n    /// The input a good player would give this tick. `play bot=true` and the tests drive the\\n    /// player with it; teach it every new rule, and keep a test that it wins.\\n    fn bot(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame {\\n        InputFrame::default()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// When true, `Sim::step` skips characters and physics after `pre`. Menus still run in `pre`.\\n    fn frozen(&self) -> bool {\\n        false\\n90→    }\\n\\n    /// Painter UI for this game, if it has one.\\n    fn fit_ui(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Option<crate::fit_ui::FitUi> {\\n        None\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Extra tint for a character (ghost lanes).\\n    fn tint(&self, _id: EntityId) -> Option<([f32; 3], f32)> {\\n        None\\n100→    }\\n}\\n\\n/// One line of [`GAMES`]: made with [`entry`].\\npub struct Entry {\\n    pub key: &'static str,\\n    pub about: &'static str,\\n    /// Builds the scene and sets `sim.state.play`. The `&str` is the rest of the scene name\\n    /// after `<key>/` (a level number, say), if any.\\n    pub build: fn(&mut Sim, Option<&str>) -> Result<()>,\\n110→    load: fn(ciborium::Value) -> Result<GameBox, String>,\\n}\\n\\n/// A [`GAMES`] line for the game type `G`.\\npub const fn entry<G: Game>(about: &'static str, build: fn(&mut Sim, Option<&str>) -> Result<()>) -> Entry {\\n    Entry { key: G::KEY, about, build, load: load_as::<G> }\\n}\\n\\nfn load_as<G: Game>(v: ciborium::Value) -> Result<GameBox, String> {\\n    v.deserialized::<G>().map(GameBox::new).map_err(|e| e.to_string())\\n120→}\\n\\n/// A game's level text: `crates/pav_core/src/games/<key>.toml` read from disk when the program\\n/// runs from the repository's root (`pav`, `cargo run`), so an edit shows at the next `load`\\n/// with no rebuild; else `built_in`, the copy embedded with `include_str!` (tests, the browser,\\n/// a shipped executable).\\npub fn level_text(key: &str, built_in: &'static str) -> std::borrow::Cow<'static, str> {\\n    #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n    if let Ok(text) = std::fs::read_to_string(format!(\\\"crates/pav_core/src/games/{key}.toml\\\")) {\\n        return text.into();\\n130→    }\\n    #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n    let _ = key; // the browser has no files\\n    built_in.into()\\n}\\n\\n/// The game registered under `key`.\\npub fn find(key: &str) -> Option<&'static Entry> {\\n    GAMES.iter().find(|g| g.key == key)\\n}\\n140→\\n/// A running game in `SimState::play`: clones (rewind, snapshots) and serializes (snapshot\\n/// files, the state hash) through the game's own derives.\\npub struct GameBox(Box<dyn DynGame>);\\n\\nimpl GameBox {\\n    pub fn new<G: Game>(game: G) -> Self {\\n        Self(Box::new(game))\\n    }\\n\\n150→    pub fn key(&self) -> &'static str {\\n        self.0.key()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The game as its own type (None for another game).\\n    pub fn get<G: Game>(&self) -> Option<&G> {\\n        self.0.as_any().downcast_ref()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn get_mut<G: Game>(&mut self) -> Option<&mut G> {\\n160→        self.0.as_any_mut().downcast_mut()\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/mod.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":160,\"raw_output\":\"//! Games built on the engine: the hook a new game implements, and the list of games.\\n//!\\n//! A game is a struct holding its rules' state (`Clone` and serde, like everything in\\n//! `SimState`) that implements [`Game`], plus a `build` function that makes its scene. One\\n//! line in [`GAMES`] and `load scene=<key>` starts it in the tools, the window\\n//! (`shardfall --scene <key>`) and the browser (`?scene=<key>`). `starter.rs` is the template\\n//! to copy; `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` is the guide. Shardfall (`crate::arpg`) predates this hook and\\n//! keeps its own.\\n\\nuse std::any::Any;\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse anyhow::Result;\\nuse serde::de::{DeserializeOwned, Error as _};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Deserializer, Serialize, Serializer};\\n\\nuse crate::entity::EntityId;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub mod fit;\\npub mod starter;\\n\\n/// Every game the engine knows. `load scene=<key>` (or `<key>/<rest>`) builds it.\\npub static GAMES: &[Entry] = &[\\n    entry::<starter::Starter>(\\\"Starter: collect every shard while slimes chase you (the template to copy).\\\", starter::build),\\n    entry::<fit::FitGame>(\\\"Wobble Minutes: a five-day balance stay at Tippy Cay.\\\", fit::build),\\n];\\n\\n/// Still playing, won or lost.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\npub enum Outcome {\\n    #[default]\\n    Playing,\\n    Won,\\n    Lost,\\n}\\n\\n/// A game's rules. Every method has a default, so a game implements only what it uses.\\n///\\n/// The engine calls `pre` and `post` once per tick (60 a second) from `Sim::step`; everything\\n/// else is read-only. While `pre` or `post` runs, the game is out of `sim.state.play`, so use\\n/// `self` for the game's own state and `sim` for the world.\\npub trait Game: Clone + Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send + Sync + 'static {\\n    /// The scene key that starts the game: `load scene=<KEY>`, `--scene <KEY>`, `?scene=<KEY>`.\\n    const KEY: &'static str;\\n\\n    /// Before characters move: read the player's input and decide what the characters the\\n    /// game drives do this tick. A returned input replaces that character's own (its `ai`\\n    /// brain, or the player's keys for the player).\\n    fn pre(\\n        &mut self,\\n        _sim: &mut Sim,\\n        _input: &InputFrame,\\n        _dt: f32,\\n        _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>,\\n    ) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame> {\\n        BTreeMap::new()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// After physics: the rules (pickups, damage, score, win and loss). Push `SimEvent`s for\\n    /// sounds and effects (`Coin`, `Pickup`, `Hit`, `Explosion`...).\\n    fn post(&mut self, _sim: &mut Sim, _dt: f32, _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {}\\n\\n    /// HUD lines: drawn at the top left of the window, returned by the `play` tool.\\n    fn hud(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String> {\\n        Vec::new()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The game's state for tools and tests (`play`), as JSON.\\n    fn status(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        serde_json::Value::Null\\n    }\\n\\n    fn outcome(&self) -> Outcome {\\n        Outcome::Playing\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The input a good player would give this tick. `play bot=true` and the tests drive the\\n    /// player with it; teach it every new rule, and keep a test that it wins.\\n    fn bot(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame {\\n        InputFrame::default()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// When true, `Sim::step` skips characters and physics after `pre`. Menus still run in `pre`.\\n    fn frozen(&self) -> bool {\\n        false\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Painter UI for this game, if it has one.\\n    fn fit_ui(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Option<crate::fit_ui::FitUi> {\\n        None\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Extra tint for a character (ghost lanes).\\n    fn tint(&self, _id: EntityId) -> Option<([f32; 3], f32)> {\\n        None\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// One line of [`GAMES`]: made with [`entry`].\\npub struct Entry {\\n    pub key: &'static str,\\n    pub about: &'static str,\\n    /// Builds the scene and sets `sim.state.play`. The `&str` is the rest of the scene name\\n    /// after `<key>/` (a level number, say), if any.\\n    pub build: fn(&mut Sim, Option<&str>) -> Result<()>,\\n    load: fn(ciborium::Value) -> Result<GameBox, String>,\\n}\\n\\n/// A [`GAMES`] line for the game type `G`.\\npub const fn entry<G: Game>(about: &'static str, build: fn(&mut Sim, Option<&str>) -> Result<()>) -> Entry {\\n    Entry { key: G::KEY, about, build, load: load_as::<G> }\\n}\\n\\nfn load_as<G: Game>(v: ciborium::Value) -> Result<GameBox, String> {\\n    v.deserialized::<G>().map(GameBox::new).map_err(|e| e.to_string())\\n}\\n\\n/// A game's level text: `crates/pav_core/src/games/<key>.toml` read from disk when the program\\n/// runs from the repository's root (`pav`, `cargo run`), so an edit shows at the next `load`\\n/// with no rebuild; else `built_in`, the copy embedded with `include_str!` (tests, the browser,\\n/// a shipped executable).\\npub fn level_text(key: &str, built_in: &'static str) -> std::borrow::Cow<'static, str> {\\n    #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n    if let Ok(text) = std::fs::read_to_string(format!(\\\"crates/pav_core/src/games/{key}.toml\\\")) {\\n        return text.into();\\n    }\\n    #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n    let _ = key; // the browser has no files\\n    built_in.into()\\n}\\n\\n/// The game registered under `key`.\\npub fn find(key: &str) -> Option<&'static Entry> {\\n    GAMES.iter().find(|g| g.key == key)\\n}\\n\\n/// A running game in `SimState::play`: clones (rewind, snapshots) and serializes (snapshot\\n/// files, the state hash) through the game's own derives.\\npub struct GameBox(Box<dyn DynGame>);\\n\\nimpl GameBox {\\n    pub fn new<G: Game>(game: G) -> Self {\\n        Self(Box::new(game))\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn key(&self) -> &'static str {\\n        self.0.key()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The game as its own type (None for another game).\\n    pub fn get<G: Game>(&self) -> Option<&G> {\\n        self.0.as_any().downcast_ref()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn get_mut<G: Game>(&mut self) -> Option<&mut G> {\\n        self.0.as_any_mut().downcast_mut()\\n\",\"total_lines\":331}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a1ac248b-0421-4087-b43f-d8c1e8af0fc6-8","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! One balance model for every event. Semi-implicit Euler at the sim tick.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec2;\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse crate::params::{ParamVisitor, Tunable};\\n\\n/// Tunable numbers. Progress lives on [`super::FitGame`], not here, so Reset restores feel only.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n10→#[serde(default)]\\npub struct Rules {\\n    pub stiffness: f32,\\n    pub damping: f32,\\n    pub reach: f32,\\n    pub tip_time: f32,\\n    pub wobble: f32,\\n    pub stick_curve: f32,\\n    pub key_rate: f32,\\n    pub key_return: f32,\\n20→    pub breath_secs: f32,\\n    pub pose_secs: f32,\\n    pub pose_ring: f32,\\n    pub squat_reps: i32,\\n    pub plank_secs: f32,\\n    pub step_secs: f32,\\n    pub floatie_secs: f32,\\n    pub spin_lo: f32,\\n    pub spin_hi: f32,\\n    pub spin_band_scale: f32,\\n30→    pub lap_secs: f32,\\n    pub tide_secs: f32,\\n    pub paddle_secs: f32,\\n    pub paddle_par: f32,\\n    pub tray_secs: f32,\\n    pub cannon_secs: f32,\\n    pub gust: f32,\\n    pub bounce_gain: f32,\\n    pub big_gust: f32,\\n    pub rhythm_perfect: f32,\\n40→    pub rhythm_good: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for Rules {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            stiffness: 40.0,\\n            damping: 8.5,\\n            reach: 0.92,\\n            tip_time: 0.35,\\n50→            wobble: 0.12,\\n            stick_curve: 1.5,\\n            key_rate: 1.6,\\n            key_return: 1.2,\\n            breath_secs: 45.0,\\n            pose_secs: 20.0,\\n            pose_ring: 0.30,\\n            squat_reps: 10,\\n            plank_secs: 60.0,\\n            step_secs: 64.0,\\n60→            floatie_secs: 50.0,\\n            spin_lo: 6.0,\\n            spin_hi: 9.0,\\n            spin_band_scale: 1.35,\\n            lap_secs: 90.0,\\n            tide_secs: 20.0,\\n            paddle_secs: 45.0,\\n            paddle_par: 28.0,\\n            tray_secs: 50.0,\\n            cannon_secs: 40.0,\\n70→            gust: 18.0,\\n            bounce_gain: 1.0,\\n            big_gust: 22.0,\\n            rhythm_perfect: 0.055,\\n            rhythm_good: 0.120,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Tunable for Rules {\\n80→    fn visit(&mut self, v: &mut dyn ParamVisitor) {\\n        v.float(\\\"stiffness\\\", &mut self.stiffness, 5.0, 80.0, \\\"How fast the dot chases your lean\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"damping\\\", &mut self.damping, 1.0, 20.0, \\\"How quickly the chase settles\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"reach\\\", &mut self.reach, 0.4, 1.0, \\\"Where a full lean comes to rest\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"tip_time\\\", &mut self.tip_time, 0.1, 1.0, \\\"Seconds outside the disc before a tip\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"wobble\\\", &mut self.wobble, 0.0, 0.4, \\\"Idle wander of the dot\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"stick_curve\\\", &mut self.stick_curve, 1.0, 3.0, \\\"Stick response exponent\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"key_rate\\\", &mut self.key_rate, 0.2, 4.0, \\\"Keyboard lean speed\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"key_return\\\", &mut self.key_return, 0.2, 4.0, \\\"Keyboard return speed\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"breath_secs\\\", &mut self.breath_secs, 10.0, 90.0, \\\"Breath Bloom length\\\");\\n90→        v.float(\\\"pose_secs\\\", &mut self.pose_secs, 8.0, 40.0, \\\"Seconds for one pose\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"pose_ring\\\", &mut self.pose_ring, 0.1, 0.6, \\\"Pose ring start radius\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"plank_secs\\\", &mut self.plank_secs, 20.0, 90.0, \\\"Plank length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"step_secs\\\", &mut self.step_secs, 20.0, 90.0, \\\"Step Party length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"floatie_secs\\\", &mut self.floatie_secs, 20.0, 80.0, \\\"Floatie Spin length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"spin_lo\\\", &mut self.spin_lo, 2.0, 12.0, \\\"Spin band low\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"spin_hi\\\", &mut self.spin_hi, 4.0, 16.0, \\\"Spin band high\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"spin_band_scale\\\", &mut self.spin_band_scale, 1.0, 2.0, \\\"Keyboard spin band scale\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"lap_secs\\\", &mut self.lap_secs, 30.0, 120.0, \\\"Morning Lap length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"tide_secs\\\", &mut self.tide_secs, 8.0, 40.0, \\\"Seconds per tide board\\\");\\n100→        v.float(\\\"paddle_secs\\\", &mut self.paddle_secs, 20.0, 80.0, \\\"Paddle time limit\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"paddle_par\\\", &mut self.paddle_par, 12.0, 50.0, \\\"Paddle par time\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"tray_secs\\\", &mut self.tray_secs, 20.0, 80.0, \\\"Tray Trek length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"cannon_secs\\\", &mut self.cannon_secs, 15.0, 70.0, \\\"Cannonball Cup length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"gust\\\", &mut self.gust, 0.0, 40.0, \\\"Gust strength\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"bounce_gain\\\", &mut self.bounce_gain, 0.4, 2.0, \\\"Board bounce gain\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"big_gust\\\", &mut self.big_gust, 0.0, 40.0, \\\"Big Stand gusts\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"rhythm_perfect\\\", &mut self.rhythm_perfect, 0.02, 0.12, \\\"Perfect window\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"rhythm_good\\\", &mut self.rhythm_good, 0.06, 0.2, \\\"Good window\\\");\\n        let _ = v.int(\\\"squat_reps\\\", &mut self.squat_reps, 4, 20, \\\"Squat count\\\");\\n110→    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Centre of pressure. `tipped` is true only on the tick a tip happens.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct BalanceCore {\\n    pub cob: Vec2,\\n    pub vel: Vec2,\\n    pub tip_t: f32,\\n    pub tipped: bool,\\n120→    pub t: f32,\\n    pub amp: f32,\\n    pub phase: [f32; 4],\\n    pub kick_in: f32,\\n    pub gust: Vec2,\\n    pub kicks: bool,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for BalanceCore {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n130→        Self {\\n            cob: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            vel: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            tip_t: 0.0,\\n            tipped: false,\\n            t: 0.0,\\n            amp: 0.12,\\n            phase: [0.4, 1.7, 2.2, 0.9],\\n            kick_in: 1.4,\\n            gust: Vec2::ZERO,\\n140→            kicks: true,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl BalanceCore {\\n    pub fn wobble(&self) -> Vec2 {\\n        let ax = |t: f32, a: f32, b: f32| {\\n            self.amp * (0.7 * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 1.3 * t + a).sin() + 0.3 * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 2.9 * t + b).sin())\\n        };\\n150→        Vec2::new(ax(self.t, self.phase[0], self.phase[1]), ax(self.t, self.phase[2], self.phase[3]))\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Advance one tick. `lean` is already shaped, in the disc.\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, rng: &mut crate::rng::Rng) {\\n        self.tipped = false;\\n        let target = lean.clamp_length_max(1.0) * rules.reach + self.wobble();\\n        let acc = (target - self.cob) * rules.stiffness - self.vel * rules.damping + self.gust;\\n        self.vel += acc * dt;\\n        if self.kicks {\\n160→            self.kick_in -= dt;\\n            if self.kick_in <= 0.0 {\\n                let ang = rng.range(0.0, std::f32::consts::TAU);\\n                self.vel += Vec2::new(ang.cos(), ang.sin()) * 0.1;\\n                self.kick_in = rng.range(1.0, 2.0);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.cob += self.vel * dt;\\n        self.t += dt;\\n        if self.cob.length() > 1.0 {\\n170→            self.tip_t += dt;\\n            if self.tip_t >= rules.tip_time {\\n                self.tipped = true;\\n                self.tip_t = 0.0;\\n                self.cob = self.cob.normalize_or_zero() * 0.72;\\n                self.vel = Vec2::ZERO;\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            self.tip_t = 0.0;\\n        }\\n180→    }\\n\\n    /// Step without the seeded wander, for the feel tests.\\n    pub fn step_clean(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules) {\\n        let mut rng = crate::rng::Rng::new(1);\\n        let kicks = self.kicks;\\n        self.kicks = false;\\n        let amp = self.amp;\\n        self.amp = 0.0;\\n        self.step(lean, dt, rules, &mut rng);\\n190→        self.amp = amp;\\n        self.kicks = kicks;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Balance Age. Better skill, more days and more stars all come out younger.\\npub fn balance_age(skill: f32, days_completed: u32, total_stars: u32) -> u8 {\\n    let skill = skill.clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    let age = 24.0 + 56.0 * (1.0 - skill).powf(1.1) - 2.0 * days_completed as f32 - (total_stars as f32 / 3.0).min(8.0);\\n    age.round().clamp(18.0, 99.0) as u8\\n200→}\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! One balance model for every event. Semi-implicit Euler at the sim tick.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec2;\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse crate::params::{ParamVisitor, Tunable};\\n\\n/// Tunable numbers. Progress lives on [`super::FitGame`], not here, so Reset restores feel only.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n10→#[serde(default)]\\npub struct Rules {\\n    pub stiffness: f32,\\n    pub damping: f32,\\n    pub reach: f32,\\n    pub tip_time: f32,\\n    pub wobble: f32,\\n    pub stick_curve: f32,\\n    pub key_rate: f32,\\n    pub key_return: f32,\\n20→    pub breath_secs: f32,\\n    pub pose_secs: f32,\\n    pub pose_ring: f32,\\n    pub squat_reps: i32,\\n    pub plank_secs: f32,\\n    pub step_secs: f32,\\n    pub floatie_secs: f32,\\n    pub spin_lo: f32,\\n    pub spin_hi: f32,\\n    pub spin_band_scale: f32,\\n30→    pub lap_secs: f32,\\n    pub tide_secs: f32,\\n    pub paddle_secs: f32,\\n    pub paddle_par: f32,\\n    pub tray_secs: f32,\\n    pub cannon_secs: f32,\\n    pub gust: f32,\\n    pub bounce_gain: f32,\\n    pub big_gust: f32,\\n    pub rhythm_perfect: f32,\\n40→    pub rhythm_good: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for Rules {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            stiffness: 40.0,\\n            damping: 8.5,\\n            reach: 0.92,\\n            tip_time: 0.35,\\n50→            wobble: 0.12,\\n            stick_curve: 1.5,\\n            key_rate: 1.6,\\n            key_return: 1.2,\\n            breath_secs: 45.0,\\n            pose_secs: 20.0,\\n            pose_ring: 0.30,\\n            squat_reps: 10,\\n            plank_secs: 60.0,\\n            step_secs: 64.0,\\n60→            floatie_secs: 50.0,\\n            spin_lo: 6.0,\\n            spin_hi: 9.0,\\n            spin_band_scale: 1.35,\\n            lap_secs: 90.0,\\n            tide_secs: 20.0,\\n            paddle_secs: 45.0,\\n            paddle_par: 28.0,\\n            tray_secs: 50.0,\\n            cannon_secs: 40.0,\\n70→            gust: 18.0,\\n            bounce_gain: 1.0,\\n            big_gust: 22.0,\\n            rhythm_perfect: 0.055,\\n            rhythm_good: 0.120,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Tunable for Rules {\\n80→    fn visit(&mut self, v: &mut dyn ParamVisitor) {\\n        v.float(\\\"stiffness\\\", &mut self.stiffness, 5.0, 80.0, \\\"How fast the dot chases your lean\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"damping\\\", &mut self.damping, 1.0, 20.0, \\\"How quickly the chase settles\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"reach\\\", &mut self.reach, 0.4, 1.0, \\\"Where a full lean comes to rest\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"tip_time\\\", &mut self.tip_time, 0.1, 1.0, \\\"Seconds outside the disc before a tip\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"wobble\\\", &mut self.wobble, 0.0, 0.4, \\\"Idle wander of the dot\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"stick_curve\\\", &mut self.stick_curve, 1.0, 3.0, \\\"Stick response exponent\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"key_rate\\\", &mut self.key_rate, 0.2, 4.0, \\\"Keyboard lean speed\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"key_return\\\", &mut self.key_return, 0.2, 4.0, \\\"Keyboard return speed\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"breath_secs\\\", &mut self.breath_secs, 10.0, 90.0, \\\"Breath Bloom length\\\");\\n90→        v.float(\\\"pose_secs\\\", &mut self.pose_secs, 8.0, 40.0, \\\"Seconds for one pose\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"pose_ring\\\", &mut self.pose_ring, 0.1, 0.6, \\\"Pose ring start radius\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"plank_secs\\\", &mut self.plank_secs, 20.0, 90.0, \\\"Plank length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"step_secs\\\", &mut self.step_secs, 20.0, 90.0, \\\"Step Party length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"floatie_secs\\\", &mut self.floatie_secs, 20.0, 80.0, \\\"Floatie Spin length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"spin_lo\\\", &mut self.spin_lo, 2.0, 12.0, \\\"Spin band low\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"spin_hi\\\", &mut self.spin_hi, 4.0, 16.0, \\\"Spin band high\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"spin_band_scale\\\", &mut self.spin_band_scale, 1.0, 2.0, \\\"Keyboard spin band scale\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"lap_secs\\\", &mut self.lap_secs, 30.0, 120.0, \\\"Morning Lap length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"tide_secs\\\", &mut self.tide_secs, 8.0, 40.0, \\\"Seconds per tide board\\\");\\n100→        v.float(\\\"paddle_secs\\\", &mut self.paddle_secs, 20.0, 80.0, \\\"Paddle time limit\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"paddle_par\\\", &mut self.paddle_par, 12.0, 50.0, \\\"Paddle par time\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"tray_secs\\\", &mut self.tray_secs, 20.0, 80.0, \\\"Tray Trek length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"cannon_secs\\\", &mut self.cannon_secs, 15.0, 70.0, \\\"Cannonball Cup length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"gust\\\", &mut self.gust, 0.0, 40.0, \\\"Gust strength\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"bounce_gain\\\", &mut self.bounce_gain, 0.4, 2.0, \\\"Board bounce gain\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"big_gust\\\", &mut self.big_gust, 0.0, 40.0, \\\"Big Stand gusts\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"rhythm_perfect\\\", &mut self.rhythm_perfect, 0.02, 0.12, \\\"Perfect window\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"rhythm_good\\\", &mut self.rhythm_good, 0.06, 0.2, \\\"Good window\\\");\\n        let _ = v.int(\\\"squat_reps\\\", &mut self.squat_reps, 4, 20, \\\"Squat count\\\");\\n110→    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Centre of pressure. `tipped` is true only on the tick a tip happens.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct BalanceCore {\\n    pub cob: Vec2,\\n    pub vel: Vec2,\\n    pub tip_t: f32,\\n    pub tipped: bool,\\n120→    pub t: f32,\\n    pub amp: f32,\\n    pub phase: [f32; 4],\\n    pub kick_in: f32,\\n    pub gust: Vec2,\\n    pub kicks: bool,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for BalanceCore {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n130→        Self {\\n            cob: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            vel: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            tip_t: 0.0,\\n            tipped: false,\\n            t: 0.0,\\n            amp: 0.12,\\n            phase: [0.4, 1.7, 2.2, 0.9],\\n            kick_in: 1.4,\\n            gust: Vec2::ZERO,\\n140→            kicks: true,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl BalanceCore {\\n    pub fn wobble(&self) -> Vec2 {\\n        let ax = |t: f32, a: f32, b: f32| {\\n            self.amp * (0.7 * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 1.3 * t + a).sin() + 0.3 * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 2.9 * t + b).sin())\\n        };\\n150→        Vec2::new(ax(self.t, self.phase[0], self.phase[1]), ax(self.t, self.phase[2], self.phase[3]))\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Advance one tick. `lean` is already shaped, in the disc.\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, rng: &mut crate::rng::Rng) {\\n        self.tipped = false;\\n        let target = lean.clamp_length_max(1.0) * rules.reach + self.wobble();\\n        let acc = (target - self.cob) * rules.stiffness - self.vel * rules.damping + self.gust;\\n        self.vel += acc * dt;\\n        if self.kicks {\\n160→            self.kick_in -= dt;\\n            if self.kick_in <= 0.0 {\\n                let ang = rng.range(0.0, std::f32::consts::TAU);\\n                self.vel += Vec2::new(ang.cos(), ang.sin()) * 0.1;\\n                self.kick_in = rng.range(1.0, 2.0);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.cob += self.vel * dt;\\n        self.t += dt;\\n        if self.cob.length() > 1.0 {\\n170→            self.tip_t += dt;\\n            if self.tip_t >= rules.tip_time {\\n                self.tipped = true;\\n                self.tip_t = 0.0;\\n                self.cob = self.cob.normalize_or_zero() * 0.72;\\n                self.vel = Vec2::ZERO;\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            self.tip_t = 0.0;\\n        }\\n180→    }\\n\\n    /// Step without the seeded wander, for the feel tests.\\n    pub fn step_clean(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules) {\\n        let mut rng = crate::rng::Rng::new(1);\\n        let kicks = self.kicks;\\n        self.kicks = false;\\n        let amp = self.amp;\\n        self.amp = 0.0;\\n        self.step(lean, dt, rules, &mut rng);\\n190→        self.amp = amp;\\n        self.kicks = kicks;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Balance Age. Better skill, more days and more stars all come out younger.\\npub fn balance_age(skill: f32, days_completed: u32, total_stars: u32) -> u8 {\\n    let skill = skill.clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    let age = 24.0 + 56.0 * (1.0 - skill).powf(1.1) - 2.0 * days_completed as f32 - (total_stars as f32 / 3.0).min(8.0);\\n    age.round().clamp(18.0, 99.0) as u8\\n200→}\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/core.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":200,\"raw_output\":\"//! One balance model for every event. Semi-implicit Euler at the sim tick.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec2;\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse crate::params::{ParamVisitor, Tunable};\\n\\n/// Tunable numbers. Progress lives on [`super::FitGame`], not here, so Reset restores feel only.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(default)]\\npub struct Rules {\\n    pub stiffness: f32,\\n    pub damping: f32,\\n    pub reach: f32,\\n    pub tip_time: f32,\\n    pub wobble: f32,\\n    pub stick_curve: f32,\\n    pub key_rate: f32,\\n    pub key_return: f32,\\n    pub breath_secs: f32,\\n    pub pose_secs: f32,\\n    pub pose_ring: f32,\\n    pub squat_reps: i32,\\n    pub plank_secs: f32,\\n    pub step_secs: f32,\\n    pub floatie_secs: f32,\\n    pub spin_lo: f32,\\n    pub spin_hi: f32,\\n    pub spin_band_scale: f32,\\n    pub lap_secs: f32,\\n    pub tide_secs: f32,\\n    pub paddle_secs: f32,\\n    pub paddle_par: f32,\\n    pub tray_secs: f32,\\n    pub cannon_secs: f32,\\n    pub gust: f32,\\n    pub bounce_gain: f32,\\n    pub big_gust: f32,\\n    pub rhythm_perfect: f32,\\n    pub rhythm_good: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for Rules {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            stiffness: 40.0,\\n            damping: 8.5,\\n            reach: 0.92,\\n            tip_time: 0.35,\\n            wobble: 0.12,\\n            stick_curve: 1.5,\\n            key_rate: 1.6,\\n            key_return: 1.2,\\n            breath_secs: 45.0,\\n            pose_secs: 20.0,\\n            pose_ring: 0.30,\\n            squat_reps: 10,\\n            plank_secs: 60.0,\\n            step_secs: 64.0,\\n            floatie_secs: 50.0,\\n            spin_lo: 6.0,\\n            spin_hi: 9.0,\\n            spin_band_scale: 1.35,\\n            lap_secs: 90.0,\\n            tide_secs: 20.0,\\n            paddle_secs: 45.0,\\n            paddle_par: 28.0,\\n            tray_secs: 50.0,\\n            cannon_secs: 40.0,\\n            gust: 18.0,\\n            bounce_gain: 1.0,\\n            big_gust: 22.0,\\n            rhythm_perfect: 0.055,\\n            rhythm_good: 0.120,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Tunable for Rules {\\n    fn visit(&mut self, v: &mut dyn ParamVisitor) {\\n        v.float(\\\"stiffness\\\", &mut self.stiffness, 5.0, 80.0, \\\"How fast the dot chases your lean\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"damping\\\", &mut self.damping, 1.0, 20.0, \\\"How quickly the chase settles\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"reach\\\", &mut self.reach, 0.4, 1.0, \\\"Where a full lean comes to rest\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"tip_time\\\", &mut self.tip_time, 0.1, 1.0, \\\"Seconds outside the disc before a tip\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"wobble\\\", &mut self.wobble, 0.0, 0.4, \\\"Idle wander of the dot\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"stick_curve\\\", &mut self.stick_curve, 1.0, 3.0, \\\"Stick response exponent\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"key_rate\\\", &mut self.key_rate, 0.2, 4.0, \\\"Keyboard lean speed\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"key_return\\\", &mut self.key_return, 0.2, 4.0, \\\"Keyboard return speed\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"breath_secs\\\", &mut self.breath_secs, 10.0, 90.0, \\\"Breath Bloom length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"pose_secs\\\", &mut self.pose_secs, 8.0, 40.0, \\\"Seconds for one pose\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"pose_ring\\\", &mut self.pose_ring, 0.1, 0.6, \\\"Pose ring start radius\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"plank_secs\\\", &mut self.plank_secs, 20.0, 90.0, \\\"Plank length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"step_secs\\\", &mut self.step_secs, 20.0, 90.0, \\\"Step Party length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"floatie_secs\\\", &mut self.floatie_secs, 20.0, 80.0, \\\"Floatie Spin length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"spin_lo\\\", &mut self.spin_lo, 2.0, 12.0, \\\"Spin band low\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"spin_hi\\\", &mut self.spin_hi, 4.0, 16.0, \\\"Spin band high\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"spin_band_scale\\\", &mut self.spin_band_scale, 1.0, 2.0, \\\"Keyboard spin band scale\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"lap_secs\\\", &mut self.lap_secs, 30.0, 120.0, \\\"Morning Lap length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"tide_secs\\\", &mut self.tide_secs, 8.0, 40.0, \\\"Seconds per tide board\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"paddle_secs\\\", &mut self.paddle_secs, 20.0, 80.0, \\\"Paddle time limit\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"paddle_par\\\", &mut self.paddle_par, 12.0, 50.0, \\\"Paddle par time\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"tray_secs\\\", &mut self.tray_secs, 20.0, 80.0, \\\"Tray Trek length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"cannon_secs\\\", &mut self.cannon_secs, 15.0, 70.0, \\\"Cannonball Cup length\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"gust\\\", &mut self.gust, 0.0, 40.0, \\\"Gust strength\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"bounce_gain\\\", &mut self.bounce_gain, 0.4, 2.0, \\\"Board bounce gain\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"big_gust\\\", &mut self.big_gust, 0.0, 40.0, \\\"Big Stand gusts\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"rhythm_perfect\\\", &mut self.rhythm_perfect, 0.02, 0.12, \\\"Perfect window\\\");\\n        v.float(\\\"rhythm_good\\\", &mut self.rhythm_good, 0.06, 0.2, \\\"Good window\\\");\\n        let _ = v.int(\\\"squat_reps\\\", &mut self.squat_reps, 4, 20, \\\"Squat count\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Centre of pressure. `tipped` is true only on the tick a tip happens.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct BalanceCore {\\n    pub cob: Vec2,\\n    pub vel: Vec2,\\n    pub tip_t: f32,\\n    pub tipped: bool,\\n    pub t: f32,\\n    pub amp: f32,\\n    pub phase: [f32; 4],\\n    pub kick_in: f32,\\n    pub gust: Vec2,\\n    pub kicks: bool,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for BalanceCore {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            cob: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            vel: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            tip_t: 0.0,\\n            tipped: false,\\n            t: 0.0,\\n            amp: 0.12,\\n            phase: [0.4, 1.7, 2.2, 0.9],\\n            kick_in: 1.4,\\n            gust: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            kicks: true,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl BalanceCore {\\n    pub fn wobble(&self) -> Vec2 {\\n        let ax = |t: f32, a: f32, b: f32| {\\n            self.amp * (0.7 * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 1.3 * t + a).sin() + 0.3 * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 2.9 * t + b).sin())\\n        };\\n        Vec2::new(ax(self.t, self.phase[0], self.phase[1]), ax(self.t, self.phase[2], self.phase[3]))\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Advance one tick. `lean` is already shaped, in the disc.\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, rng: &mut crate::rng::Rng) {\\n        self.tipped = false;\\n        let target = lean.clamp_length_max(1.0) * rules.reach + self.wobble();\\n        let acc = (target - self.cob) * rules.stiffness - self.vel * rules.damping + self.gust;\\n        self.vel += acc * dt;\\n        if self.kicks {\\n            self.kick_in -= dt;\\n            if self.kick_in <= 0.0 {\\n                let ang = rng.range(0.0, std::f32::consts::TAU);\\n                self.vel += Vec2::new(ang.cos(), ang.sin()) * 0.1;\\n                self.kick_in = rng.range(1.0, 2.0);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.cob += self.vel * dt;\\n        self.t += dt;\\n        if self.cob.length() > 1.0 {\\n            self.tip_t += dt;\\n            if self.tip_t >= rules.tip_time {\\n                self.tipped = true;\\n                self.tip_t = 0.0;\\n                self.cob = self.cob.normalize_or_zero() * 0.72;\\n                self.vel = Vec2::ZERO;\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            self.tip_t = 0.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Step without the seeded wander, for the feel tests.\\n    pub fn step_clean(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules) {\\n        let mut rng = crate::rng::Rng::new(1);\\n        let kicks = self.kicks;\\n        self.kicks = false;\\n        let amp = self.amp;\\n        self.amp = 0.0;\\n        self.step(lean, dt, rules, &mut rng);\\n        self.amp = amp;\\n        self.kicks = kicks;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Balance Age. Better skill, more days and more stars all come out younger.\\npub fn balance_age(skill: f32, days_completed: u32, total_stars: u32) -> u8 {\\n    let skill = skill.clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    let age = 24.0 + 56.0 * (1.0 - skill).powf(1.1) - 2.0 * days_completed as f32 - (total_stars as f32 / 3.0).min(8.0);\\n    age.round().clamp(18.0, 99.0) as u8\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":224}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a1ac248b-0421-4087-b43f-d8c1e8af0fc6-9","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Every Tippy Cay activity, on the shared balance model.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec2;\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse super::core::{BalanceCore, Rules, stars_from_plank, stars_from_score};\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::buttons;\\nuse crate::rng::Rng;\\n10→use crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub enum EventId {\\n    Check,\\n    Breath,\\n    Pose,\\n    Squat,\\n    Plank,\\n    Step,\\n20→    Floatie,\\n    Lap,\\n    Tide,\\n    Paddle,\\n    Tray,\\n    Cannon,\\n    BigStand,\\n}\\n\\nimpl EventId {\\n30→    pub const ALL: [EventId; 13] = [\\n        EventId::Check,\\n        EventId::Breath,\\n        EventId::Pose,\\n        EventId::Squat,\\n        EventId::Plank,\\n        EventId::Step,\\n        EventId::Floatie,\\n        EventId::Lap,\\n        EventId::Tide,\\n40→        EventId::Paddle,\\n        EventId::Tray,\\n        EventId::Cannon,\\n        EventId::BigStand,\\n    ];\\n\\n    pub fn key(self) -> &'static str {\\n        match self {\\n            EventId::Check => \\\"check\\\",\\n            EventId::Breath => \\\"breath\\\",\\n50→            EventId::Pose => \\\"pose\\\",\\n            EventId::Squat => \\\"squat\\\",\\n            EventId::Plank => \\\"plank\\\",\\n            EventId::Step => \\\"step\\\",\\n            EventId::Floatie => \\\"floatie\\\",\\n            EventId::Lap => \\\"lap\\\",\\n            EventId::Tide => \\\"tide\\\",\\n            EventId::Paddle => \\\"paddle\\\",\\n            EventId::Tray => \\\"tray\\\",\\n            EventId::Cannon => \\\"cannon\\\",\\n60→            EventId::BigStand => \\\"bigstand\\\",\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn from_key(s: &str) -> Option<EventId> {\\n        Self::ALL.into_iter().find(|e| e.key() == s)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn title(self) -> &'static str {\\n        match self {\\n70→            EventId::Check => \\\"Morning Wobble Check\\\",\\n            EventId::Breath => \\\"Breath Bloom\\\",\\n            EventId::Pose => \\\"Pose Parade\\\",\\n            EventId::Squat => \\\"Tempo Squats\\\",\\n            EventId::Plank => \\\"Plank Standoff\\\",\\n            EventId::Step => \\\"Step Party\\\",\\n            EventId::Floatie => \\\"Floatie Spin\\\",\\n            EventId::Lap => \\\"Morning Lap\\\",\\n            EventId::Tide => \\\"Tide Table\\\",\\n            EventId::Paddle => \\\"Paddle Slalom\\\",\\n80→            EventId::Tray => \\\"Tray Trek\\\",\\n            EventId::Cannon => \\\"Cannonball Cup\\\",\\n            EventId::BigStand => \\\"The Big Stand\\\",\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn blurb(self) -> &'static str {\\n        match self {\\n            EventId::Check => \\\"Stand, lean, close your eyes, and step on the beat.\\\",\\n            EventId::Breath => \\\"Follow the ring. In for four, out for four.\\\",\\n90→            EventId::Pose => \\\"Stay inside the drifting ring. Accept the bird.\\\",\\n            EventId::Squat => \\\"Down for two, up for one. Keep the dot in the band.\\\",\\n            EventId::Plank => \\\"Brace, and do not leave the ring.\\\",\\n            EventId::Step => \\\"Left, right, sometimes both. The box does not wait.\\\",\\n            EventId::Floatie => \\\"Spin the rings. Catch the ones they throw.\\\",\\n            EventId::Lap => \\\"Two steps a second. Ribbons are optional. Crabs are not.\\\",\\n            EventId::Tide => \\\"Tilt the raft. The shells want the pools.\\\",\\n            EventId::Paddle => \\\"Lean ahead to go. The gates are suggestions with consequences.\\\",\\n            EventId::Tray => \\\"Five glasses. The pier is not on your side.\\\",\\n            EventId::Cannon => \\\"Bounce, tuck, splash. The judges brought cards.\\\",\\n100→            EventId::BigStand => \\\"Everything, once, and then nothing at all.\\\",\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn coach(self) -> &'static str {\\n        match self {\\n            EventId::Check | EventId::BigStand => \\\"Pip\\\",\\n            EventId::Breath | EventId::Pose => \\\"Posey\\\",\\n            EventId::Squat | EventId::Plank => \\\"Big Kettle\\\",\\n            EventId::Step | EventId::Floatie | EventId::Lap => \\\"Bounce\\\",\\n110→            EventId::Tide | EventId::Paddle | EventId::Cannon => \\\"Commodore Gull\\\",\\n            EventId::Tray => \\\"Marjorie\\\",\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn area(self) -> u8 {\\n        Self::ALL.iter().position(|e| *e == self).unwrap_or(0) as u8\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Activities a day opens, not counting the morning check or the finale.\\n120→    pub fn for_day(day: u8) -> &'static [EventId] {\\n        match day {\\n            1 => &[EventId::Breath, EventId::Pose],\\n            2 => &[EventId::Squat, EventId::Plank],\\n            3 => &[EventId::Step, EventId::Floatie, EventId::Lap],\\n            4 => &[EventId::Tide, EventId::Paddle, EventId::Tray, EventId::Cannon],\\n            _ => &[],\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n130→\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struc