nt\":\"const MAX_RECORDING_TICKS: u64 = 60 * 60 * 60;\"},{\"line_number\":515,\"content\":\"        if self.recording.ticks() < MAX_RECORDING_TICKS {\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b6e030ff-b7af-4ae4-822e-f1a425faa187-41","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Live-tunable parameters. Any struct implementing `Tunable` exposes its fields through a\\n//! visitor, which powers the tuning panel, agent get/set by path, and preset files, with no\\n//! string lookups in game code (values stay plain struct fields).\\n\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n10→#[serde(untagged)]\\npub enum ParamValue {\\n    Bool(bool),\\n    Int(i64),\\n    Float(f64),\\n    Text(String),\\n}\\n\\nimpl ParamValue {\\n    pub fn as_f64(&self) -> Option<f64> {\\n20→        match self {\\n            ParamValue::Float(f) => Some(*f),\\n            ParamValue::Int(i) => Some(*i as f64),\\n            ParamValue::Bool(b) => Some(*b as i64 as f64),\\n            ParamValue::Text(t) => t.parse().ok(),\\n        }\\n    }\\n    pub fn as_bool(&self) -> Option<bool> {\\n        match self {\\n            ParamValue::Bool(b) => Some(*b),\\n30→            ParamValue::Int(i) => Some(*i != 0),\\n            ParamValue::Float(f) => Some(*f != 0.0),\\n            ParamValue::Text(t) => match t.as_str() {\\n                \\\"true\\\" | \\\"on\\\" | \\\"yes\\\" | \\\"1\\\" => Some(true),\\n                \\\"false\\\" | \\\"off\\\" | \\\"no\\\" | \\\"0\\\" => Some(false),\\n                _ => None,\\n            },\\n        }\\n    }\\n    pub fn from_json(v: &serde_json::Value) -> Option<Self> {\\n40→        serde_json::from_value(v.clone()).ok()\\n    }\\n    pub fn to_json(&self) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        serde_json::to_value(self).unwrap_or(serde_json::Value::Null)\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize)]\\npub enum ParamKind {\\n    Float { min: f32, max: f32 },\\n50→    Int { min: i32, max: i32 },\\n    Bool,\\n    Choice { options: Vec<String> },\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize)]\\npub struct ParamInfo {\\n    pub path: String,\\n    pub kind: ParamKind,\\n    pub value: ParamValue,\\n60→    pub help: String,\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Live-tunable parameters. Any struct implementing `Tunable` exposes its fields through a\\n//! visitor, which powers the tuning panel, agent get/set by path, and preset files, with no\\n//! string lookups in game code (values stay plain struct fields).\\n\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n10→#[serde(untagged)]\\npub enum ParamValue {\\n    Bool(bool),\\n    Int(i64),\\n    Float(f64),\\n    Text(String),\\n}\\n\\nimpl ParamValue {\\n    pub fn as_f64(&self) -> Option<f64> {\\n20→        match self {\\n            ParamValue::Float(f) => Some(*f),\\n            ParamValue::Int(i) => Some(*i as f64),\\n            ParamValue::Bool(b) => Some(*b as i64 as f64),\\n            ParamValue::Text(t) => t.parse().ok(),\\n        }\\n    }\\n    pub fn as_bool(&self) -> Option<bool> {\\n        match self {\\n            ParamValue::Bool(b) => Some(*b),\\n30→            ParamValue::Int(i) => Some(*i != 0),\\n            ParamValue::Float(f) => Some(*f != 0.0),\\n            ParamValue::Text(t) => match t.as_str() {\\n                \\\"true\\\" | \\\"on\\\" | \\\"yes\\\" | \\\"1\\\" => Some(true),\\n                \\\"false\\\" | \\\"off\\\" | \\\"no\\\" | \\\"0\\\" => Some(false),\\n                _ => None,\\n            },\\n        }\\n    }\\n    pub fn from_json(v: &serde_json::Value) -> Option<Self> {\\n40→        serde_json::from_value(v.clone()).ok()\\n    }\\n    pub fn to_json(&self) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        serde_json::to_value(self).unwrap_or(serde_json::Value::Null)\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize)]\\npub enum ParamKind {\\n    Float { min: f32, max: f32 },\\n50→    Int { min: i32, max: i32 },\\n    Bool,\\n    Choice { options: Vec<String> },\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize)]\\npub struct ParamInfo {\\n    pub path: String,\\n    pub kind: ParamKind,\\n    pub value: ParamValue,\\n60→    pub help: String,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/params.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"//! Live-tunable parameters. Any struct implementing `Tunable` exposes its fields through a\\n//! visitor, which powers the tuning panel, agent get/set by path, and preset files, with no\\n//! string lookups in game code (values stay plain struct fields).\\n\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(untagged)]\\npub enum ParamValue {\\n    Bool(bool),\\n    Int(i64),\\n    Float(f64),\\n    Text(String),\\n}\\n\\nimpl ParamValue {\\n    pub fn as_f64(&self) -> Option<f64> {\\n        match self {\\n            ParamValue::Float(f) => Some(*f),\\n            ParamValue::Int(i) => Some(*i as f64),\\n            ParamValue::Bool(b) => Some(*b as i64 as f64),\\n            ParamValue::Text(t) => t.parse().ok(),\\n        }\\n    }\\n    pub fn as_bool(&self) -> Option<bool> {\\n        match self {\\n            ParamValue::Bool(b) => Some(*b),\\n            ParamValue::Int(i) => Some(*i != 0),\\n            ParamValue::Float(f) => Some(*f != 0.0),\\n            ParamValue::Text(t) => match t.as_str() {\\n                \\\"true\\\" | \\\"on\\\" | \\\"yes\\\" | \\\"1\\\" => Some(true),\\n                \\\"false\\\" | \\\"off\\\" | \\\"no\\\" | \\\"0\\\" => Some(false),\\n                _ => None,\\n            },\\n        }\\n    }\\n    pub fn from_json(v: &serde_json::Value) -> Option<Self> {\\n        serde_json::from_value(v.clone()).ok()\\n    }\\n    pub fn to_json(&self) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        serde_json::to_value(self).unwrap_or(serde_json::Value::Null)\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize)]\\npub enum ParamKind {\\n    Float { min: f32, max: f32 },\\n    Int { min: i32, max: i32 },\\n    Bool,\\n    Choice { options: Vec<String> },\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize)]\\npub struct ParamInfo {\\n    pub path: String,\\n    pub kind: ParamKind,\\n    pub value: ParamValue,\\n    pub help: String,\\n\",\"total_lines\":302}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"575850de-3186-484b-95f2-76bbc146bde8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_145","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"60×60×60 equals 216,000 ticks, or one hour of recording.\n\nA full playthrough is roughly 54,000 ticks. Recording every InputFrame uses about 10 MB. History snapshots total around 240 MB per simulation. The playthrough test will set history_seconds to zero to avoid that overhead.\n\nCloning SimState every tick could be slow. I will disable history at the start of long tests via both config and the enabled flag. Next I will run cargo check on pav_core, then write the code and set up charts.toml.\n\ncharts.toml will hold 100 notes in the format `t = 1.0, lane = 0`. The pose score multiplier of 700 should yield roughly 2 stars if the bot stays inside the ring; retuning is planned after testing.\n\nThe squat bot holds CONFIRM while the guide rises, increasing depth and lung usage. Score caps at 1000.\n\nmod.rs will be written cleanly. Coach lines will live in script.rs as functions returning strings to avoid TOML blocking. A script.toml with enough lines will load via OnceLock.\n\nThe script will be compact and real-sounding. It will be expanded before the lint test, which checks for TODOs, placeholders, weight, and nintendo references.\n\nCoach tones are now defined: Pip is earnest and formal, Posey is soft, Kettle is low and blunt, Bounce is fast, and Gull uses nautical nonsense. The script will contain many short lines. mod.rs will be kept under 1200 lines with a Flow enum using serde snake_case renaming.\n\nThe status screen will display the flow name as the phase and the current event key. Keyboard shaping is handled by the host before frames reach the simulation; tests pass already-shaped InputFrame data, and intent functions are unit-tested separately. The bot sets input.lean, input.held, and input.pressed. Held buttons should register as pressed only on their edge. I am now figuring out how the test loop drives the bot.\n\nI am weighing two ways to drive the bot in tests. One is to pass the bot's input directly into `sim.step()`. The other is to edge-detect held buttons and set `pressed` only on transitions. If `pressed` equals `held` every tick, step events will register a hit every frame while the note is in window. That would break step scoring. I will document the edge-detection approach so tests can verify real update loops without false hits.\n\nThe bot will set both `held` and `pressed` to the same button bits. This makes the press register on the single tick when the note is within half a frame, avoiding false hits in step scoring.\n\nMenu bots must not send lean that wakes things up. The attract exit uses `pressed`, but the game handles that path directly rather than through the test loop.\n\nThe play-together test will start at the title screen, step down and confirm into Together mode, then drive the bot until the podium.\n\nThe Together-mode bot will confirm to enter Pass, then drive the card, countdown, and events. The test will use this bot after selecting two players. A bot is faster than idle for finishing the medley; idle flops immediately on plank and takes 45 seconds for paddle, 60 for tide, and 40 for cannon.\n\nA full story run with three seeds could reach roughly 400,000 ticks. That would take about 80 seconds at 0.2 ms per step or 400 seconds at 1 ms. A fast dev-time scale path will be added but left unused by tests.\n\nA `play_bot` helper will drive the simulation for tests. The bot will skip card and countdown delays by pressing CONFIRM, saving about a minute across all events.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0efa35c4-361e-4239-bcb1-c920c2351bb7-42","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs","offset":1030,"limit":250}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2103,"output_tokens":2073,"cache_read_input_tokens":89728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"28805cef-31eb-4fe6-a6e7-239aa7b364c9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0efa35c4-361e-4239-bcb1-c920c2351bb7-42","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1030→    act.pz += act.speed * dt;\\n    act.px = (act.px + lean.x * 3.2 * dt).clamp(-2.2, 2.2);\\n    if act.t.fract() < dt {\\n        events.push(SimEvent::Wake { pos: glam::Vec3::new(act.px, 0.0, act.pz) });\\n    }\\n    if let Some(g) = act.gates.get(act.gate_i as usize) {\\n        if act.pz >= g[0] {\\n            if (act.px - g[1]).abs() > 0.7 {\\n                act.missed += 1;\\n            }\\n1040→            act.gate_i += 1;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    act.t += dt;\\n    let finished = act.pz >= 56.0 || act.t >= rules.paddle_secs;\\n    if finished {\\n        let mut t = if act.pz >= 56.0 { act.t } else { rules.paddle_secs };\\n        t += act.missed as f32 * 2.0;\\n        let par = rules.paddle_par;\\n        let raw = (1.6 * par - t) / (0.8 * par);\\n1050→        act.score = (raw.clamp(0.0, 1.0) * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n        act.done = true;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tick_tray(act: &mut Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let mut jolt = 0.0;\\n    for s in &act.jolts {\\n        let d = act.t - s[0];\\n        if d > 0.0 && d < 0.35 {\\n1060→            jolt += s[1] * (1.0 - d / 0.35);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let tilt = bal.cob.x + jolt * 0.15;\\n    for i in 0..5 {\\n        if !act.glass_ok[i] {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        act.glasses[i] += tilt * dt * 1.3;\\n        if act.glasses[i].abs() > 1.0 {\\n1070→            act.glass_ok[i] = false;\\n            events.push(SimEvent::Sfx { id: 19, gain: 0.8, pitch: 1.0 });\\n        }\\n    }\\n    act.t += dt;\\n    act.pz = act.t;\\n    if act.t >= rules.tray_secs {\\n        let kept = act.glass_ok.iter().filter(|g| **g).count() as f32;\\n        let bonus = if kept == 5.0 { 0.0 } else { 0.0 };\\n        act.score = (kept * 200.0 + bonus).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n1080→        act.done = true;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tick_cannon(act: &mut Activity, lean: Vec2, held: u32, pressed: u32, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let _ = rules;\\n    if !act.leaping {\\n        let phase = act.t / 1.2;\\n        let s = (phase * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin();\\n        let prev = ((act.t - dt) / 1.2 * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin();\\n1090→        let bottom = s < -0.9 && s > prev;\\n        if bottom && pressed & buttons::CONFIRM != 0 && act.power < 4.0 {\\n            act.power += 1.0;\\n            events.push(SimEvent::Sfx { id: 14, gain: 0.6, pitch: 0.8 + act.power * 0.1 });\\n            if act.power >= 4.0 {\\n                act.leaping = true;\\n                act.air = 0.0;\\n                act.tuck = 0.0;\\n            }\\n        }\\n1100→    } else {\\n        act.air += dt;\\n        if held & buttons::CONFIRM != 0 {\\n            act.tuck = (act.tuck + dt / 0.4).min(1.0);\\n        }\\n        act.px += lean.x * dt;\\n        let height = (act.air * 3.0).sin().max(0.0) * act.power * 0.25;\\n        if act.air > 0.55 && height < 0.15 {\\n            let timing = (1.0 - (act.air - 0.7).abs()).clamp(0.2, 1.0);\\n            let sc = (height * 4.0).clamp(0.2, 1.0) * act.tuck.clamp(0.2, 1.0) * timing * rules.bounce_gain;\\n1110→            act.dive_scores.push(sc.clamp(0.0, 1.0));\\n            act.dives += 1;\\n            events.push(SimEvent::BigSplash { pos: glam::Vec3::new(act.px, 0.0, 2.0), size: 1.2 + act.tuck });\\n            act.leaping = false;\\n            act.power = 0.0;\\n            act.air = 0.0;\\n            act.tuck = 0.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    act.t += dt;\\n1120→    if act.dives >= 3 || act.t >= rules.cannon_secs {\\n        let n = 3.0;\\n        let sum: f32 = act.dive_scores.iter().sum();\\n        act.score = (sum / n * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n        act.done = true;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tick_big(act: &mut Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, lean: Vec2, held: u32, pressed: u32, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let _ = lean;\\n1130→    match act.phase {\\n        0 => {\\n            let before = act.t;\\n            tick_breath(act, bal, held, dt, rules, true);\\n            act.t = before + dt;\\n            if act.t >= 32.0 {\\n                act.phase = 1;\\n                act.sub = 0.0;\\n                act.acc = 0.0;\\n                act.done = false;\\n1140→            }\\n        }\\n        1 => {\\n            let c = ring_center(act.sub);\\n            let inside = (bal.cob - c).length() < 0.28;\\n            if inside {\\n                act.acc += dt;\\n            }\\n            act.sub += dt;\\n            act.t += dt;\\n1150→            if act.sub >= 20.0 {\\n                act.phase_scores.push((act.acc / 20.0 * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0));\\n                act.phase = 2;\\n                act.sub = 0.0;\\n                act.acc = 0.0;\\n                act.note_i = 0;\\n                // Use the first notes, time-shifted into this phase by rewriting a local clock.\\n                act.t_shift_notes();\\n            }\\n        }\\n1160→        2 => {\\n            let local_pressed = pressed;\\n            let start_t = act.t;\\n            // tick_step uses act.t against note times. Notes were shifted.\\n            let saved_dur = rules.step_secs;\\n            let _ = saved_dur;\\n            tick_step_window(act, local_pressed, dt, rules, 40.0);\\n            if act.t - start_t < dt * 0.5 {\\n                act.t = start_t + dt;\\n            }\\n1170→            act.sub += dt;\\n            if act.sub >= 40.0 {\\n                act.phase_scores.push(act.score);\\n                act.phase = 3;\\n                act.sub = 0.0;\\n                act.done = false;\\n                act.flopped = false;\\n                act.survived = 0.0;\\n            }\\n        }\\n1180→        3 => {\\n            if braced(held) && bal.cob.length() < 0.45 {\\n                act.acc += dt;\\n            }\\n            act.sub += dt;\\n            act.t += dt;\\n            if act.sub >= 20.0 {\\n                act.phase_scores.push((act.acc / 20.0 * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0));\\n                act.phase = 4;\\n                act.sub = 0.0;\\n1190→                act.still_sum = 0.0;\\n                act.still_n = 0.0;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        _ => {\\n            if act.sub >= 15.0 && pressed != 0 {\\n                act.forfeit = true;\\n            }\\n            act.still_sum += bal.cob.length() * dt;\\n            act.still_n += dt;\\n1200→            act.sub += dt;\\n            act.t += dt;\\n            if act.sub >= 30.0 {\\n                let mean = act.still_sum / act.still_n.max(0.001);\\n                let quiet = (1.0 - mean / 0.2).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n                let mut s = quiet * 1000.0;\\n                if !act.forfeit {\\n                    s = (s + 200.0).min(1000.0);\\n                } else {\\n                    s *= 0.5;\\n1210→                }\\n                act.phase_scores.push(s);\\n                let n = act.phase_scores.len().max(1) as f32;\\n                let sum: f32 = act.phase_scores.iter().copied().sum();\\n                act.score = (sum / n).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n                // Tips cost score but never end the run.\\n                act.score = (act.score - act.tips as f32 * 15.0).max(0.0);\\n                act.done = true;\\n            }\\n        }\\n1220→    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Activity {\\n    fn t_shift_notes(&mut self) {\\n        if self.notes.is_empty() {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let t0 = self.notes[0][0];\\n        for n in &mut self.notes {\\n1230→            n[0] = self.t + (n[0] - t0);\\n        }\\n        self.note_i = 0;\\n        self.acc = 0.0;\\n        self.hits = 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tick_step_window(act: &mut Activity, pressed: u32, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, window: f32) {\\n    let total = act.notes.len().max(1) as f32;\\n1240→    let t0 = act.t;\\n    tick_step(act, pressed, dt, rules);\\n    // tick_step may mark done at step_secs. The finale uses its own clock.\\n    if act.done && act.kind == EventId::BigStand {\\n        act.done = false;\\n        act.score = (act.acc / total * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n    }\\n    if act.t < t0 + dt * 0.5 {\\n        act.t = t0 + dt;\\n    }\\n1250→    let _ = window;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1030→    act.pz += act.speed * dt;\\n    act.px = (act.px + lean.x * 3.2 * dt).clamp(-2.2, 2.2);\\n    if act.t.fract() < dt {\\n        events.push(SimEvent::Wake { pos: glam::Vec3::new(act.px, 0.0, act.pz) });\\n    }\\n    if let Some(g) = act.gates.get(act.gate_i as usize) {\\n        if act.pz >= g[0] {\\n            if (act.px - g[1]).abs() > 0.7 {\\n                act.missed += 1;\\n            }\\n1040→            act.gate_i += 1;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    act.t += dt;\\n    let finished = act.pz >= 56.0 || act.t >= rules.paddle_secs;\\n    if finished {\\n        let mut t = if act.pz >= 56.0 { act.t } else { rules.paddle_secs };\\n        t += act.missed as f32 * 2.0;\\n        let par = rules.paddle_par;\\n        let raw = (1.6 * par - t) / (0.8 * par);\\n1050→        act.score = (raw.clamp(0.0, 1.0) * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n        act.done = true;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tick_tray(act: &mut Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let mut jolt = 0.0;\\n    for s in &act.jolts {\\n        let d = act.t - s[0];\\n        if d > 0.0 && d < 0.35 {\\n1060→            jolt += s[1] * (1.0 - d / 0.35);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let tilt = bal.cob.x + jolt * 0.15;\\n    for i in 0..5 {\\n        if !act.glass_ok[i] {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        act.glasses[i] += tilt * dt * 1.3;\\n        if act.glasses[i].abs() > 1.0 {\\n1070→            act.glass_ok[i] = false;\\n            events.push(SimEvent::Sfx { id: 19, gain: 0.8, pitch: 1.0 });\\n        }\\n    }\\n    act.t += dt;\\n    act.pz = act.t;\\n    if act.t >= rules.tray_secs {\\n        let kept = act.glass_ok.iter().filter(|g| **g).count() as f32;\\n        let bonus = if kept == 5.0 { 0.0 } else { 0.0 };\\n        act.score = (kept * 200.0 + bonus).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n1080→        act.done = true;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tick_cannon(act: &mut Activity, lean: Vec2, held: u32, pressed: u32, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let _ = rules;\\n    if !act.leaping {\\n        let phase = act.t / 1.2;\\n        let s = (phase * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin();\\n        let prev = ((act.t - dt) / 1.2 * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin();\\n1090→        let bottom = s < -0.9 && s > prev;\\n        if bottom && pressed & buttons::CONFIRM != 0 && act.power < 4.0 {\\n            act.power += 1.0;\\n            events.push(SimEvent::Sfx { id: 14, gain: 0.6, pitch: 0.8 + act.power * 0.1 });\\n            if act.power >= 4.0 {\\n                act.leaping = true;\\n                act.air = 0.0;\\n                act.tuck = 0.0;\\n            }\\n        }\\n1100→    } else {\\n        act.air += dt;\\n        if held & buttons::CONFIRM != 0 {\\n            act.tuck = (act.tuck + dt / 0.4).min(1.0);\\n        }\\n        act.px += lean.x * dt;\\n        let height = (act.air * 3.0).sin().max(0.0) * act.power * 0.25;\\n        if act.air > 0.55 && height < 0.15 {\\n            let timing = (1.0 - (act.air - 0.7).abs()).clamp(0.2, 1.0);\\n            let sc = (height * 4.0).clamp(0.2, 1.0) * act.tuck.clamp(0.2, 1.0) * timing * rules.bounce_gain;\\n1110→            act.dive_scores.push(sc.clamp(0.0, 1.0));\\n            act.dives += 1;\\n            events.push(SimEvent::BigSplash { pos: glam::Vec3::new(act.px, 0.0, 2.0), size: 1.2 + act.tuck });\\n            act.leaping = false;\\n            act.power = 0.0;\\n            act.air = 0.0;\\n            act.tuck = 0.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    act.t += dt;\\n1120→    if act.dives >= 3 || act.t >= rules.cannon_secs {\\n        let n = 3.0;\\n        let sum: f32 = act.dive_scores.iter().sum();\\n        act.score = (sum / n * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n        act.done = true;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tick_big(act: &mut Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, lean: Vec2, held: u32, pressed: u32, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let _ = lean;\\n1130→    match act.phase {\\n        0 => {\\n            let before = act.t;\\n            tick_breath(act, bal, held, dt, rules, true);\\n            act.t = before + dt;\\n            if act.t >= 32.0 {\\n                act.phase = 1;\\n                act.sub = 0.0;\\n                act.acc = 0.0;\\n                act.done = false;\\n1140→            }\\n        }\\n        1 => {\\n            let c = ring_center(act.sub);\\n            let inside = (bal.cob - c).length() < 0.28;\\n            if inside {\\n                act.acc += dt;\\n            }\\n            act.sub += dt;\\n            act.t += dt;\\n1150→            if act.sub >= 20.0 {\\n                act.phase_scores.push((act.acc / 20.0 * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0));\\n                act.phase = 2;\\n                act.sub = 0.0;\\n                act.acc = 0.0;\\n                act.note_i = 0;\\n                // Use the first notes, time-shifted into this phase by rewriting a local clock.\\n                act.t_shift_notes();\\n            }\\n        }\\n1160→        2 => {\\n            let local_pressed = pressed;\\n            let start_t = act.t;\\n            // tick_step uses act.t against note times. Notes were shifted.\\n            let saved_dur = rules.step_secs;\\n            let _ = saved_dur;\\n            tick_step_window(act, local_pressed, dt, rules, 40.0);\\n            if act.t - start_t < dt * 0.5 {\\n                act.t = start_t + dt;\\n            }\\n1170→            act.sub += dt;\\n            if act.sub >= 40.0 {\\n                act.phase_scores.push(act.score);\\n                act.phase = 3;\\n                act.sub = 0.0;\\n                act.done = false;\\n                act.flopped = false;\\n                act.survived = 0.0;\\n            }\\n        }\\n1180→        3 => {\\n            if braced(held) && bal.cob.length() < 0.45 {\\n                act.acc += dt;\\n            }\\n            act.sub += dt;\\n            act.t += dt;\\n            if act.sub >= 20.0 {\\n                act.phase_scores.push((act.acc / 20.0 * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0));\\n                act.phase = 4;\\n                act.sub = 0.0;\\n1190→                act.still_sum = 0.0;\\n                act.still_n = 0.0;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        _ => {\\n            if act.sub >= 15.0 && pressed != 0 {\\n                act.forfeit = true;\\n            }\\n            act.still_sum += bal.cob.length() * dt;\\n            act.still_n += dt;\\n1200→            act.sub += dt;\\n            act.t += dt;\\n            if act.sub >= 30.0 {\\n                let mean = act.still_sum / act.still_n.max(0.001);\\n                let quiet = (1.0 - mean / 0.2).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n                let mut s = quiet * 1000.0;\\n                if !act.forfeit {\\n                    s = (s + 200.0).min(1000.0);\\n                } else {\\n                    s *= 0.5;\\n1210→                }\\n                act.phase_scores.push(s);\\n                let n = act.phase_scores.len().max(1) as f32;\\n                let sum: f32 = act.phase_scores.iter().copied().sum();\\n                act.score = (sum / n).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n                // Tips cost score but never end the run.\\n                act.score = (act.score - act.tips as f32 * 15.0).max(0.0);\\n                act.done = true;\\n            }\\n        }\\n1220→    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Activity {\\n    fn t_shift_notes(&mut self) {\\n        if self.notes.is_empty() {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let t0 = self.notes[0][0];\\n        for n in &mut self.notes {\\n1230→            n[0] = self.t + (n[0] - t0);\\n        }\\n        self.note_i = 0;\\n        self.acc = 0.0;\\n        self.hits = 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tick_step_window(act: &mut Activity, pressed: u32, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, window: f32) {\\n    let total = act.notes.len().max(1) as f32;\\n1240→    let t0 = act.t;\\n    tick_step(act, pressed, dt, rules);\\n    // tick_step may mark done at step_secs. The finale uses its own clock.\\n    if act.done && act.kind == EventId::BigStand {\\n        act.done = false;\\n        act.score = (act.acc / total * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n    }\\n    if act.t < t0 + dt * 0.5 {\\n        act.t = t0 + dt;\\n    }\\n1250→    let _ = window;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs\",\"offset\":1030,\"limit\":250,\"raw_output\":\"    act.pz += act.speed * dt;\\n    act.px = (act.px + lean.x * 3.2 * dt).clamp(-2.2, 2.2);\\n    if act.t.fract() < dt {\\n        events.push(SimEvent::Wake { pos: glam::Vec3::new(act.px, 0.0, act.pz) });\\n    }\\n    if let Some(g) = act.gates.get(act.gate_i as usize) {\\n        if act.pz >= g[0] {\\n            if (act.px - g[1]).abs() > 0.7 {\\n                act.missed += 1;\\n            }\\n            act.gate_i += 1;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    act.t += dt;\\n    let finished = act.pz >= 56.0 || act.t >= rules.paddle_secs;\\n    if finished {\\n        let mut t = if act.pz >= 56.0 { act.t } else { rules.paddle_secs };\\n        t += act.missed as f32 * 2.0;\\n        let par = rules.paddle_par;\\n        let raw = (1.6 * par - t) / (0.8 * par);\\n        act.score = (raw.clamp(0.0, 1.0) * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n        act.done = true;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tick_tray(act: &mut Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let mut jolt = 0.0;\\n    for s in &act.jolts {\\n        let d = act.t - s[0];\\n        if d > 0.0 && d < 0.35 {\\n            jolt += s[1] * (1.0 - d / 0.35);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let tilt = bal.cob.x + jolt * 0.15;\\n    for i in 0..5 {\\n        if !act.glass_ok[i] {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        act.glasses[i] += tilt * dt * 1.3;\\n        if act.glasses[i].abs() > 1.0 {\\n            act.glass_ok[i] = false;\\n            events.push(SimEvent::Sfx { id: 19, gain: 0.8, pitch: 1.0 });\\n        }\\n    }\\n    act.t += dt;\\n    act.pz = act.t;\\n    if act.t >= rules.tray_secs {\\n        let kept = act.glass_ok.iter().filter(|g| **g).count() as f32;\\n        let bonus = if kept == 5.0 { 0.0 } else { 0.0 };\\n        act.score = (kept * 200.0 + bonus).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n        act.done = true;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tick_cannon(act: &mut Activity, lean: Vec2, held: u32, pressed: u32, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let _ = rules;\\n    if !act.leaping {\\n        let phase = act.t / 1.2;\\n        let s = (phase * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin();\\n        let prev = ((act.t - dt) / 1.2 * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin();\\n        let bottom = s < -0.9 && s > prev;\\n        if bottom && pressed & buttons::CONFIRM != 0 && act.power < 4.0 {\\n            act.power += 1.0;\\n            events.push(SimEvent::Sfx { id: 14, gain: 0.6, pitch: 0.8 + act.power * 0.1 });\\n            if act.power >= 4.0 {\\n                act.leaping = true;\\n                act.air = 0.0;\\n                act.tuck = 0.0;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    } else {\\n        act.air += dt;\\n        if held & buttons::CONFIRM != 0 {\\n            act.tuck = (act.tuck + dt / 0.4).min(1.0);\\n        }\\n        act.px += lean.x * dt;\\n        let height = (act.air * 3.0).sin().max(0.0) * act.power * 0.25;\\n        if act.air > 0.55 && height < 0.15 {\\n            let timing = (1.0 - (act.air - 0.7).abs()).clamp(0.2, 1.0);\\n            let sc = (height * 4.0).clamp(0.2, 1.0) * act.tuck.clamp(0.2, 1.0) * timing * rules.bounce_gain;\\n            act.dive_scores.push(sc.clamp(0.0, 1.0));\\n            act.dives += 1;\\n            events.push(SimEvent::BigSplash { pos: glam::Vec3::new(act.px, 0.0, 2.0), size: 1.2 + act.tuck });\\n            act.leaping = false;\\n            act.power = 0.0;\\n            act.air = 0.0;\\n            act.tuck = 0.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    act.t += dt;\\n    if act.dives >= 3 || act.t >= rules.cannon_secs {\\n        let n = 3.0;\\n        let sum: f32 = act.dive_scores.iter().sum();\\n        act.score = (sum / n * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n        act.done = true;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tick_big(act: &mut Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, lean: Vec2, held: u32, pressed: u32, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let _ = lean;\\n    match act.phase {\\n        0 => {\\n            let before = act.t;\\n            tick_breath(act, bal, held, dt, rules, true);\\n            act.t = before + dt;\\n            if act.t >= 32.0 {\\n                act.phase = 1;\\n                act.sub = 0.0;\\n                act.acc = 0.0;\\n                act.done = false;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        1 => {\\n            let c = ring_center(act.sub);\\n            let inside = (bal.cob - c).length() < 0.28;\\n            if inside {\\n                act.acc += dt;\\n            }\\n            act.sub += dt;\\n            act.t += dt;\\n            if act.sub >= 20.0 {\\n                act.phase_scores.push((act.acc / 20.0 * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0));\\n                act.phase = 2;\\n                act.sub = 0.0;\\n                act.acc = 0.0;\\n                act.note_i = 0;\\n                // Use the first notes, time-shifted into this phase by rewriting a local clock.\\n                act.t_shift_notes();\\n            }\\n        }\\n        2 => {\\n            let local_pressed = pressed;\\n            let start_t = act.t;\\n            // tick_step uses act.t against note times. Notes were shifted.\\n            let saved_dur = rules.step_secs;\\n            let _ = saved_dur;\\n            tick_step_window(act, local_pressed, dt, rules, 40.0);\\n            if act.t - start_t < dt * 0.5 {\\n                act.t = start_t + dt;\\n            }\\n            act.sub += dt;\\n            if act.sub >= 40.0 {\\n                act.phase_scores.push(act.score);\\n                act.phase = 3;\\n                act.sub = 0.0;\\n                act.done = false;\\n                act.flopped = false;\\n                act.survived = 0.0;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        3 => {\\n            if braced(held) && bal.cob.length() < 0.45 {\\n                act.acc += dt;\\n            }\\n            act.sub += dt;\\n            act.t += dt;\\n            if act.sub >= 20.0 {\\n                act.phase_scores.push((act.acc / 20.0 * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0));\\n                act.phase = 4;\\n                act.sub = 0.0;\\n                act.still_sum = 0.0;\\n                act.still_n = 0.0;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        _ => {\\n            if act.sub >= 15.0 && pressed != 0 {\\n                act.forfeit = true;\\n            }\\n            act.still_sum += bal.cob.length() * dt;\\n            act.still_n += dt;\\n            act.sub += dt;\\n            act.t += dt;\\n            if act.sub >= 30.0 {\\n                let mean = act.still_sum / act.still_n.max(0.001);\\n                let quiet = (1.0 - mean / 0.2).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n                let mut s = quiet * 1000.0;\\n                if !act.forfeit {\\n                    s = (s + 200.0).min(1000.0);\\n                } else {\\n                    s *= 0.5;\\n                }\\n                act.phase_scores.push(s);\\n                let n = act.phase_scores.len().max(1) as f32;\\n                let sum: f32 = act.phase_scores.iter().copied().sum();\\n                act.score = (sum / n).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n                // Tips cost score but never end the run.\\n                act.score = (act.score - act.tips as f32 * 15.0).max(0.0);\\n                act.done = true;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Activity {\\n    fn t_shift_notes(&mut self) {\\n        if self.notes.is_empty() {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let t0 = self.notes[0][0];\\n        for n in &mut self.notes {\\n            n[0] = self.t + (n[0] - t0);\\n        }\\n        self.note_i = 0;\\n        self.acc = 0.0;\\n        self.hits = 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tick_step_window(act: &mut Activity, pressed: u32, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, window: f32) {\\n    let total = act.notes.len().max(1) as f32;\\n    let t0 = act.t;\\n    tick_step(act, pressed, dt, rules);\\n    // tick_step may mark done at step_secs. The finale uses its own clock.\\n    if act.done && act.kind == EventId::BigStand {\\n        act.done = false;\\n        act.score = (act.acc / total * 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 1000.0);\\n    }\\n    if act.t < t0 + dt * 0.5 {\\n        act.t = t0 + dt;\\n    }\\n    let _ = window;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":1251}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"85180cd3-36f3-4df5-8290-9594d2e579d5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_146","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug was found: tick_step_window calls tick_step, which uses rules.\n\nTime may advance twice per tick. Bot and simulation share act.t. The press window is checked before the tick advances time.\n\nTime advances only once per tick. The tick_big phase 2 logic and finale tick_breath both handle timing correctly. Events appear sound. The cannon bot and simulation bottom detection are nearly identical.\n\nThe cannon bot presses CONFIRM for four ticks per dive. Three dives should finish within the 40-second window. The bot holds the button through the leap so the tuck score can rise. The floatie bot spin rate of 7.5 rad/s falls inside the allowed band.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-70da833e-9914-4179-8c50-a39067f0c862-43","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/starter.toml","offset":40,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-70da833e-9914-4179-8c50-a39067f0c862-44","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn default_legend|legend.insert|\\\"#\\\"","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/level.rs","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4786,"output_tokens":973,"cache_read_input_tokens":91776,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"4df1277a-b758-4c29-8011-1228e1c67ccd"}
