{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_147","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Coaches could be placed as NPCs in the room for visual flavor.\n\nNPCs will be skipped to save CPU. The room will use a small 16x12 sand floor with colored blocks and a water area. The player figure and balance puck provide the visual elements.\n\nHeadless UI rendering is deferred to the pav_ui phase. The simulation comes first. Files will be written directly rather than via a Python script. A Rust script.rs with static arrays will generate the data files the tests load.\n\nScript.toml will hold the dialogue content. The fit module structure is being defined with core, events, intent, and script submodules. Preset names, skins, and outfits are being planned.\n\nNames, skins, and outfits will be defined in script.rs. Titles will be mapped to score ranges via a title_for function. A StaySave struct with version, slots, settings, and last_day is being designed for round-trip serialization tests.\n\nSave and load methods will use serde_json. The save version increments on day changes. Snapshot round-trip tests will cover both the running simulation and FitGame directly. Fields needing defaults or caches will be handled in deserialization. A dev_open flag and time_scale are being added to the game state. Pause flow logic is being drafted.\n\nHub pause resumes the game flow without freezing it. The frozen() method returns false during Pause in hub mode, allowing post-tick events to continue while the menu is open.\n\nCountdown and Attract flows are not frozen. Player input is cleared during these states so the figure does not move. World time only advances during Island, Event, Check, and Attract. Physics still steps while the player remains on the ground.\n\nAttract mode will not advance world_time to avoid confusing pause tests. It also skips saving. Touch input on device 4 is ignored to keep the attract demo running.\n\nTouch input is detected by device number. Device 4 keeps touch_only active. Devices 1 through 3 disable touch_only and mark the pad as seen. Keyboard input without a device field leaves touch_only false.\n\nThe settings button remains reachable from a touch card overlay even when touch_only is true. The attract demo continues running underneath this overlay.\n\nA phone test will use device 4 to verify the attract demo and settings overlay. Touch input on device 4 will not reset the idle timer, since touch is ignored for wake but still counts as idle input.\n\nOpening settings from the touch card during attract mode will exit the demo and open the settings menu without saving. Item identifiers are being defined, starting with ACT_NEW set to 1.\n\nThe remaining UI item identifiers are being assigned. Actions include Continue, Together, Settings, About, Howto, Back, Resume, End Day, Retry, Result Back, Dev Reset, Rowboat, and Extend. A namespace scheme is planned to prevent collisions between names, skins, outfits, schedule events, dev jumps, and sliders.\n\nFocus will index into the current item list rather than using raw IDs. Menu navigation will use MENU_UP and MENU_DOWN. Keyboard repeat is limited to pressed events only, allowing one move per press. The dialogue system will advance through indexed text lines, with confirmation advancing the flow; bots confirm automatically while humans see a typewriter effect in the UI view.\n\nText speed will advance the visible character count per tick. New characters will trigger syllable events for audio later. Music events will fire on flow changes. The wildcard arms in sounds_for already cover new variants. Pav_core will be checked first to avoid cross-crate compilation issues.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-86d9efdd-a958-43ed-9646-f5734497c674-45","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/puppet.rs","offset":540,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1426,"output_tokens":2339,"cache_read_input_tokens":96512,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"47daeee3-f9f5-4e78-9e65-a29e75941579"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-86d9efdd-a958-43ed-9646-f5734497c674-45","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"540→    pub travel: f32,\\n    /// This character's own beat (0..1), so idle breathing and blinks don't march in step.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub seed: f32,\\n    /// Motion clip (`crate::clips`): id (0 = none), time (seconds, not wrapped), how much of the\\n    /// body it holds (fades in and out), play flags (`clips::UPPER`...) and speed (0 = 1).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip: u32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip_t: f32,\\n550→    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip_w: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip_flags: u8,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip_speed: f32,\\n    /// The clip before, held under the new one while it fades in.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip2: u32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n560→    pub clip2_t: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip2_w: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip2_flags: u8,\\n    /// A dodge was under way last tick (a captured dodge starts once per dodge).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub dodged: bool,\\n    /// Whole-body tilt about the feet, degrees (balance games). Side is right-positive.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n570→    pub tilt_side: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub tilt_fwd: f32,\\n}\\n\\n/// What the character is doing this tick (input to the animator).\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct AnimInput {\\n    pub vel: Vec3,\\n    pub accel: Vec3,\\n580→    pub grounded: bool,\\n    pub crouch: bool,\\n    pub crawl: bool,\\n    pub climbing: bool,\\n    pub facing: f32,\\n    /// Landing impact speed this tick (m/s), 0 if none.\\n    pub landed: f32,\\n    pub jumped: bool,\\n    pub swimming: bool,\\n    pub rolling: bool,\",\"content_concise\":\"540→    pub travel: f32,\\n    /// This character's own beat (0..1), so idle breathing and blinks don't march in step.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub seed: f32,\\n    /// Motion clip (`crate::clips`): id (0 = none), time (seconds, not wrapped), how much of the\\n    /// body it holds (fades in and out), play flags (`clips::UPPER`...) and speed (0 = 1).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip: u32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip_t: f32,\\n550→    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip_w: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip_flags: u8,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip_speed: f32,\\n    /// The clip before, held under the new one while it fades in.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip2: u32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n560→    pub clip2_t: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip2_w: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip2_flags: u8,\\n    /// A dodge was under way last tick (a captured dodge starts once per dodge).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub dodged: bool,\\n    /// Whole-body tilt about the feet, degrees (balance games). Side is right-positive.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n570→    pub tilt_side: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub tilt_fwd: f32,\\n}\\n\\n/// What the character is doing this tick (input to the animator).\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct AnimInput {\\n    pub vel: Vec3,\\n    pub accel: Vec3,\\n580→    pub grounded: bool,\\n    pub crouch: bool,\\n    pub crawl: bool,\\n    pub climbing: bool,\\n    pub facing: f32,\\n    /// Landing impact speed this tick (m/s), 0 if none.\\n    pub landed: f32,\\n    pub jumped: bool,\\n    pub swimming: bool,\\n    pub rolling: bool,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/puppet.rs\",\"offset\":540,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"    pub travel: f32,\\n    /// This character's own beat (0..1), so idle breathing and blinks don't march in step.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub seed: f32,\\n    /// Motion clip (`crate::clips`): id (0 = none), time (seconds, not wrapped), how much of the\\n    /// body it holds (fades in and out), play flags (`clips::UPPER`...) and speed (0 = 1).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip: u32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip_t: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip_w: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip_flags: u8,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip_speed: f32,\\n    /// The clip before, held under the new one while it fades in.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip2: u32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip2_t: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip2_w: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub clip2_flags: u8,\\n    /// A dodge was under way last tick (a captured dodge starts once per dodge).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub dodged: bool,\\n    /// Whole-body tilt about the feet, degrees (balance games). Side is right-positive.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub tilt_side: f32,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub tilt_fwd: f32,\\n}\\n\\n/// What the character is doing this tick (input to the animator).\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct AnimInput {\\n    pub vel: Vec3,\\n    pub accel: Vec3,\\n    pub grounded: bool,\\n    pub crouch: bool,\\n    pub crawl: bool,\\n    pub climbing: bool,\\n    pub facing: f32,\\n    /// Landing impact speed this tick (m/s), 0 if none.\\n    pub landed: f32,\\n    pub jumped: bool,\\n    pub swimming: bool,\\n    pub rolling: bool,\\n\",\"total_lines\":1641}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"08f3b409-8afd-45f8-b556-2cee5494bb68"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_148","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now writing the large files.\n\nRoomDef parsing doesn't need wing fields. NPCs are skipped for now. Pastel high-key view settings will be set for captures. mod.rs will be written in parts. decisions.md and PROGRESS.md come later. A bug was spotted: held CONFIRM during events might be misread as menu confirm.\n\nMenu confirm is now gated to non-event flows only. Island pickup flip-flops will be placed at fixed offsets from spawn and checked by distance in post. The bot uses SCHEDULE on island, so it won't accidentally collect them during story.\n\nPickup will require CONFIRM within 1.2m, not auto-collect. Yesterday's ghost logic will match events by area on day 3 or later and tint spawned characters. Spawning ghosts every event risks physics nondeterminism if they collide.\n\nThe ghost will be a kinematic capsule placed 3m to the side so it cannot block the player. It is purely visual for replay events, and spawning it adds one extra character to steps. Fixed coordinates mean no randomness, so determinism is preserved.\n\nMedley runs on day 0, so no yesterday ghost appears there. BalanceCore phase is seeded from the activity RNG at start, keeping same-seed runs identical while differing seeds produce different events. Paddle wobble kicks use simulation RNG, so matching seeds yield matching kicks.\n\nBalanceCore will be reset at activity start with a seeded phase and wobble amplitude. RNG will not be consumed in menus or pre unless strictly necessary, keeping the simulation deterministic.\n\nWobble assist defaults to zero and scales the amplitude. Phase seeding at activity start ensures different seeds diverge correctly.\n\n`start_activity` will be implemented in `FitGame`. The idle flow begins at the Card state, then counts down before the event starts. The plank idle flops immediately once the event begins with zero score. The status shows live score updates during events. Once finished, the flow becomes Result, the final score is set, stars are assigned, and stars are copied to `game.stars_last`. A `played` array will store event keys.\n\nStatus will include a version field. After the together event, the status will hold a sorted podium array of names and scores. The hub status will contain score, label, done flag, per-game stats, and a ghost flag. Non-hub events will report zero score with done set to false. AIHub active state is browser-side only; the simulation will not touch Math.random or set flags the page reads. Ready to write code.\n\nA `pav_core/tests/fit.rs` integration test will be added. A `dev/tests/run.sh` script will run the fit tests and print only failures with a final pass count.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ebdab967-c829-455d-bbb6-6d01ec6a48ae-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/Cargo.toml","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ebdab967-c829-455d-bbb6-6d01ec6a48ae-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2842,"output_tokens":1596,"cache_read_input_tokens":97920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"9fe4a96d-6196-4470-b4b8-9b0f201b6766"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ebdab967-c829-455d-bbb6-6d01ec6a48ae-46","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→[package]\\nname = \\\"pav_core\\\"\\nversion.workspace = true\\nedition.workspace = true\\npublish.workspace = true\\n\\n[dependencies]\\nglam.workspace = true\\n# One-line physics precision switch: change package to \\\"rapier3d-f64\\\".\\n10→rapier = { package = \\\"rapier3d\\\", version = \\\"0.36\\\", features = [\\\"serde-serialize\\\"] }\\nserde.workspace = true\\nserde_json.workspace = true\\ntoml.workspace = true\\nanyhow.workspace = true\\nciborium.workspace = true\\nlog.workspace = true\\n\\n[lints]\\nworkspace = true\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→[package]\\nname = \\\"pav_core\\\"\\nversion.workspace = true\\nedition.workspace = true\\npublish.workspace = true\\n\\n[dependencies]\\nglam.workspace = true\\n# One-line physics precision switch: change package to \\\"rapier3d-f64\\\".\\n10→rapier = { package = \\\"rapier3d\\\", version = \\\"0.36\\\", features = [\\\"serde-serialize\\\"] }\\nserde.workspace = true\\nserde_json.workspace = true\\ntoml.workspace = true\\nanyhow.workspace = true\\nciborium.workspace = true\\nlog.workspace = true\\n\\n[lints]\\nworkspace = true\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/Cargo.toml\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"[package]\\nname = \\\"pav_core\\\"\\nversion.workspace = true\\nedition.workspace = true\\npublish.workspace = true\\n\\n[dependencies]\\nglam.workspace = true\\n# One-line physics precision switch: change package to \\\"rapier3d-f64\\\".\\nrapier = { package = \\\"rapier3d\\\", version = \\\"0.36\\\", features = [\\\"serde-serialize\\\"] }\\nserde.workspace = true\\nserde_json.workspace = true\\ntoml.workspace = true\\nanyhow.workspace = true\\nciborium.workspace = true\\nlog.workspace = true\\n\\n[lints]\\nworkspace = true\\n\",\"total_lines\":19}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ebdab967-c829-455d-bbb6-6d01ec6a48ae-47","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Games built on the engine (`pav_core::games`): the starter's bot wins on many seeds, the\\n//! starter can be lost, and a game's state survives snapshot files, rewind and replays like\\n//! the rest of the simulation. Copy these tests for a new game.\\n\\nuse pav_core::games::{GAMES, Outcome};\\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim, SimState};\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn the_starter_bot_wins_on_ten_seeds() {\\n10→    for seed in 1..=10 {\\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"starter\\\", seed).unwrap();\\n        let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 60);\\n        let status = sim.play().unwrap().status(&sim);\\n        assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \\\"seed {seed}, {ticks} ticks: {status}\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn standing_still_gets_caught() {\\n20→    let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"starter\\\", 1).unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(sim.frame().hud.lines, [\\\"Shards 0/5\\\", \\\"Lives 3\\\"]);\\n    for _ in 0..60 * 60 {\\n        sim.step(&InputFrame::default());\\n    }\\n    assert_eq!(sim.outcome(), Outcome::Lost);\\n    assert_eq!(sim.frame().hud.lines, [\\\"Shards 0/5\\\", \\\"Lives 0\\\", \\\"Game over\\\"]);\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\n30→fn snapshots_rewind_and_replays_are_exact() {\\n    let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"starter\\\", 3).unwrap();\\n    for _ in 0..240 {\\n        let f = sim.bot_input();\\n        sim.step(&f);\\n    }\\n    // A snapshot file (CBOR) restores the game, and both copies then play on the same.\\n    let mut bytes = Vec::new();\\n    ciborium::into_writer(&sim.snapshot(), &mut bytes).unwrap();\\n    let state: SimState = ciborium::from_reader(bytes.as_slice()).unwrap();\\n40→    let mut copy = Sim::new(\\\"starter\\\", 3).unwrap();\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Games built on the engine (`pav_core::games`): the starter's bot wins on many seeds, the\\n//! starter can be lost, and a game's state survives snapshot files, rewind and replays like\\n//! the rest of the simulation. Copy these tests for a new game.\\n\\nuse pav_core::games::{GAMES, Outcome};\\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim, SimState};\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn the_starter_bot_wins_on_ten_seeds() {\\n10→    for seed in 1..=10 {\\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"starter\\\", seed).unwrap();\\n        let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 60);\\n        let status = sim.play().unwrap().status(&sim);\\n        assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \\\"seed {seed}, {ticks} ticks: {status}\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn standing_still_gets_caught() {\\n20→    let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"starter\\\", 1).unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(sim.frame().hud.lines, [\\\"Shards 0/5\\\", \\\"Lives 3\\\"]);\\n    for _ in 0..60 * 60 {\\n        sim.step(&InputFrame::default());\\n    }\\n    assert_eq!(sim.outcome(), Outcome::Lost);\\n    assert_eq!(sim.frame().hud.lines, [\\\"Shards 0/5\\\", \\\"Lives 0\\\", \\\"Game over\\\"]);\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\n30→fn snapshots_rewind_and_replays_are_exact() {\\n    let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"starter\\\", 3).unwrap();\\n    for _ in 0..240 {\\n        let f = sim.bot_input();\\n        sim.step(&f);\\n    }\\n    // A snapshot file (CBOR) restores the game, and both copies then play on the same.\\n    let mut bytes = Vec::new();\\n    ciborium::into_writer(&sim.snapshot(), &mut bytes).unwrap();\\n    let state: SimState = ciborium::from_reader(bytes.as_slice()).unwrap();\\n40→    let mut copy = Sim::new(\\\"starter\\\", 3).unwrap();\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"//! Games built on the engine (`pav_core::games`): the starter's bot wins on many seeds, the\\n//! starter can be lost, and a game's state survives snapshot files, rewind and replays like\\n//! the rest of the simulation. Copy these tests for a new game.\\n\\nuse pav_core::games::{GAMES, Outcome};\\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim, SimState};\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn the_starter_bot_wins_on_ten_seeds() {\\n    for seed in 1..=10 {\\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"starter\\\", seed).unwrap();\\n        let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 60);\\n        let status = sim.play().unwrap().status(&sim);\\n        assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \\\"seed {seed}, {ticks} ticks: {status}\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn standing_still_gets_caught() {\\n    let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"starter\\\", 1).unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(sim.frame().hud.lines, [\\\"Shards 0/5\\\", \\\"Lives 3\\\"]);\\n    for _ in 0..60 * 60 {\\n        sim.step(&InputFrame::default());\\n    }\\n    assert_eq!(sim.outcome(), Outcome::Lost);\\n    assert_eq!(sim.frame().hud.lines, [\\\"Shards 0/5\\\", \\\"Lives 0\\\", \\\"Game over\\\"]);\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn snapshots_rewind_and_replays_are_exact() {\\n    let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"starter\\\", 3).unwrap();\\n    for _ in 0..240 {\\n        let f = sim.bot_input();\\n        sim.step(&f);\\n    }\\n    // A snapshot file (CBOR) restores the game, and both copies then play on the same.\\n    let mut bytes = Vec::new();\\n    ciborium::into_writer(&sim.snapshot(), &mut bytes).unwrap();\\n    let state: SimState = ciborium::from_reader(bytes.as_slice()).unwrap();\\n    let mut copy = Sim::new(\\\"starter\\\", 3).unwrap();\\n\",\"total_lines\":70}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"12d40d0f-0c80-492f-b948-6311ea618fac"}
