1,101,77,97,112,60,83,116,114,105,110,103,44,32,80,97,114,97,109,86,97,108,117,101,62,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":3,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/room.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":2,\"content\":\"//! plus metadata (info card, primary device, movement model, camera defaults, parameter\"},{\"line_number\":313,\"content\":\"    /// Camera defaults while inside (camera.* parameter names without the prefix).\"},{\"line_number\":315,\"content\":\"    pub camera: BTreeMap<String, ParamValue>,\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"360acf80-beba-439e-bf32-c0ab62620d85"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_157","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Camera is a free map. Unknown keys might be ignored at apply time.\n\nSky and sun settings may be added to the view pastel for a bright room. A sand floor, water blocks, and a deck will be defined. The room will be 14 by 10 cells with one static block per cell. History will be set in build. Sim::new calls build. The key constant is \"fit\". Build routes None to title. It routes \"medley\" to hub medley. It routes direct event paths. Scene splitting uses only the first slash.\n\n\"fit/event/breath\" routes to base fit with the remaining path as the event. \"fit/medley\" is handled too. The begin method initializes activity, balance amplitude, phase, flow, card timer, and live score.\n\nDirect events use a card so idle works. Medley starts immediately to skip the card and countdown. Determinism tests feed inputs from tick zero into the paddle sim.\n\nA card would consume sixty ticks of RNG and alter the paddle state, so medley will start directly without one. Direct events keep their card to let idle reach a result. The hub browser may also need a card.\n\nA zero-length card is cleaner than immediate start. Play together and story events keep their cards. Idle per-event must not skip the card without input; it auto-leaves after one second, then counts down three seconds, then runs the event with zero input until done. The test loops until the phase is result or stars appear and the event ends. Countdown auto-decrements so idle never stalls on a confirm prompt. Plank idle flops on the first tick and finishes in about four seconds. Paddle idle takes forty-five seconds plus four seconds and scores zero.\n\nA `run_until` test helper will advance the simulation until a predicate is satisfied or a maximum tick count is reached. Idle input uses default values with an unset device. The bot loop for per-event tests will skip history, feed bot inputs, and stop once the phase reaches result and stars appear.\n\nThe bot loop breaks once the phase becomes result, reading the score before the next step so it does not leave too early. Idle tests step with default input and assert no stars appear when the phase reaches result. Five seeds are planned, though some events are long: lap ninety seconds, pose sixty, step sixty-four, plank sixty, tide sixty, and bigstand one hundred forty-two.\n\nTotal per-event bot and idle tests may reach two hundred thousand to four hundred thousand ticks. Big stand requires two stars from averaged phase scores. The countdown stays at three seconds with no time scale cheat. Squat duration is about thirty-six seconds. Pose and tide score issues will be fixed after testing.\n\nBalance unit tests will be added to core.rs under cfg(test). They will run with cargo test -p pav_core --lib. Intent tests are also planned. Script text will be stored as static data in script.rs to avoid a TOML dependency. A separate script.toml will provide dialogue for the game.\n\nScript.toml will be parsed once via include_str and cached in a static OnceLock. The format uses a names list and line entries with speaker and text fields. The check nudge must be fixed to actually kick velocity so bot age behaves correctly.\n\nThe idle check nudge adds 0.25 to the still metric for 0.4 seconds, which hurts the score by raising the mean and lowering skill. For the bot, PD keeps cob near zero except during that brief penalty. The resulting mean is roughly 0.04, yielding a metric of about 0.6 and a skill of approximately 0.81.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-54335e6a-4305-4c47-9d21-73a7fc041198-56","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"InputFrame \\{","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine","glob":"*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":698,"output_