es-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/loot.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"    sim.step(&InputFrame { cmd: Some(c), ..Default::default() });\"},{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\"fn fight(sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame {\"},{\"line_number\":40,\"content\":\"    let mut f = InputFrame { aim: Some(t), ..Default::default() };\"},{\"line_number\":179,\"content\":\"        sim.step(&InputFrame { move_dir: Vec2::new(0.3, -1.0), ..Default::default() });\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/animation.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":82,\"content\":\"    sim.run(60, &InputFrame { move_dir: Vec2::new(1.0, 0.0), ..Default::default() });\"},{\"line_number\":98,\"content\":\"    sim.run(90, &InputFrame { move_dir: Vec2::new(0.4, -1.0), ..Default::default() });\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"b0dcc6b0-a1bc-4a2c-947d-98b24521a10c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_158","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Only t_input is a closed literal.\n\nFixing t_input with Default::default(). Checking agent_tools.rs for similar issues. Will write mod.rs next, splitting it into FitGame, flow, pre/post, and ui_build sections.\n\nDrafting the pre-order game logic. It covers time scaling, attract mode exits, hub wait flags, pause toggling, UI events, menu and card timers, and input storage with demo overrides.\n\nDuring events, CONFIRM counts as gameplay rather than menu input. In attract mode, event segments pull the last lean from the demo bot so the player character does not walk. The idle attract timer applies to pre-game menus including Title, Slots, Name, Look, Settings, and About.\n\nIdle attract timer resets when entering or exiting attract mode. This prevents immediate re-entry after a title screen exit.\n\nTouch on the title screen starts attract mode without resetting the idle timer. Clicking settings during attract opens it without saving state. The bot returns CONFIRM on the title screen when focus is zero and the item is New Stay, but this does not set `any` to true. The bot must never set device 4.\n\nThe bot navigates menus by moving focus toward the target item. It selects the next unplayed schedule entry, or the first name on the name screen. In the look screen, it confirms to pick a skin, then confirms again to proceed to the outfit screen.\n\nIntro dialogue advances with confirm, then the bot wakes and begins the check. The title-to-check sequence requires roughly six confirm ticks across intro and wake lines. Sleep uses one line or auto-advances after two seconds.\n\nThe day loop runs wake, check card, check, reveal, island, schedule, events, sleep, and then advances to the next day. Day five follows the same path but ends with a big stand card, big stand, ending, and credits.\n\nReveal is a menu state that the bot confirms through.\n\nAt the end of a check event, skill is computed from the score, age is balanced using days completed and total stars, the age is stored, and the flow switches to Reveal.\n\nFinishing a big stand increments stamps, records the activity as ever played, and sets the flow to Ending.\n\nThe Ending screen shows a rowboat or extended view based on age. Confirming there advances to Credits with outcome Won.\n\nCredits confirm returns the player to the free play island. The bot stops before the credits appear because the loop checks outcome at its start.\n\nWorld time increments in post only during Event, Check, and Island flows.\n\nThe bot skips cards and countdowns with confirm, so menus and events total roughly 920 seconds. That is about 15 minutes of simulation time, which satisfies the under-60-minute requirement.\n\nThe bot function branches by flow. Event, Check, and Attract use the event bot for lean and held input. Island uses SCHEDULE. Countdown, Card, Reveal, Sleep, Intro, Wake, Ending, Credits, and Pass all press CONFIRM.\n\nThe bot now branches by specific flow states. Result moves focus up until it reaches Back, then confirms. Title confirms when focus is zero, otherwise moves up. Together, Podium, Slots, Name, Look, and Outfit all confirm. The schedule bot implementation is next.\n\nThe schedule bot moves focus toward the next unplayed event index, pressing confirm when aligned or menu buttons to adjust otherwise. The title screen places Play Together at index 1, so a single menu down and confirm activates it. The play-together test will send that same sequence before the bot takes over.\n\nContinue is only available for saved slots. After Play Together, the bot selects two guests and confirms. The Pass screen displays \"Pass the pad to Avery\" before the medley event card. Guest names are preset from the list by index. Each guest plays three events and their scores sum for podium sorting. A RunKind enum tracks Story, Medley, Together, Direct, and Demo modes. Between events, result confirm advances to the next event instead of returning to the island.\n\nfinish_event now branches by run mode. Direct stays in Result. Medley records the score and advances to the next event or marks the hub done. Together records the score, then moves to the next card, passes to another player, or shows the podium. Story banks minutes and opens the result screen. Demo remains in attract mode.\n\nFor medley determinism, the test can run until hub.done is set. Continuous inputs apply without waiting for confirm.\n\nThe medley test will use a deterministic `drive(seed)` function that runs the simulation for 180 minutes with history disabled. This ensures both runs receive identical input streams rather than relying on bot behavior.\n\nThe medley test asserts that identical seeds produce identical scores. It also verifies that two different fixed input scripts yield the same result, while different seeds may diverge due to paddle gates. The score should fall between zero and three thousand.\n\nHub wait behavior is noted: if the hub flag is set during a medley, the event freezes until that flag clears.\n\nThe hub_wait freeze works correctly when set before any post-processing. A test will verify the dev slider during pause by pressing pause from the title screen, then sending a slider input.\n\nA dev slider test will verify stiffness changes from 80 to 40 after a click. Music volume is checked immediately after new game creation. A save round-trip test mutates game state, serializes it, reloads it, and asserts the values match.\n\n`get_mut` is available on `GameBox` for test mutations. `save_json` and `load` must preserve the day field. A snapshot test will serialize state, restore it into a fresh simulation, and assert that status matches. `FitGame` serializes through ciborium with all fields covered by serde; `OnceLock` is excluded from the struct. `Vec2`, activity vectors, and the `Flow` enum all support serialization. No `#[serde(default)]` attributes are needed on `FitGame` because every field is always written.\n\nA content lint test will scan scripts and Rust sources for banned words. The list includes TODO, FIXME, placeholder, BMI, body mass, diet, calories, Wii, Nintendo, Balance Board, and Mii. The About page source line may mention the inspiration, so the lint should allow that specific reference.\n\nThe HTML filename may contain \"Wii Fit\" as required by the task, but the lint only scans game text files and ignores filenames. The About page source line is the sole allowed reference to the inspiration. The lint will scan Rust sources and TOML files for banned words while permitting that specific source line.\n\nTests for intent and balance will be added to the fit integration test and unit tests in the modules so `--lib` runs them. The combined test command will target `pav_core`, `games::fit`, and `games`. The games starter test is slower because it runs ten seeds for sixty seconds, so the plan specifies a separate command for our tests.\n\nThe starter tests will be included to guard against engine regressions. They are fast enough to run alongside the fit tests. The fit tests themselves are the longer ones and will use two test threads. Tests will not be marked ignore. The build profile will use opt-level 1 and eight parallel jobs. A Python script will generate charts and the script before writing mod.rs.\n\nCharts.toml will use 100 notes to match the fallback pattern. The step party tempo is 96 BPM, so quarter notes last 0.625 seconds and eighth notes last 0.3125 seconds. Rhythm windows are 0.055 and 0.120 seconds, while the bot hits within 0.008 seconds, which is well inside the acceptable range. If tests do not set song position, act.t serves as the clock. A potential bug was noted: tick_step may skip notes when pressed is zero if the note has passed its good window, because at 60 Hz act.t increments by one sixty-second interval per tick.\n\nNote times are 37.5 ticks apart, so they fall halfway between frames. The bot’s hit window is 0.0093 seconds, which is slightly larger than the 0.00833 second gap to the nearest tick. This means notes are barely caught at their exact timing.\n\nThe bot hit window will be widened to 1.0/60 seconds to avoid missing notes that fall between ticks. The lap press interval is exactly 30 ticks.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2c9d0713-94e6-4459-9f0d-f61140554d96-57","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"SimEvent::","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates","glob":"*.rs","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2c9d0713-94e6-4459-9f0d-f61140554d96-58","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"match .*event|SimEvent \\{","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core","glob":"*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6330,"output_tokens":4653,"cache_read_input_tokens":109568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"12a188a8-0146-4593-985f-3839195d0eb0"}
