{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_160","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed the wildcard exists. Now writing all the game code.\n\nPlanning mod.rs structure and embedding dialogue via a static SCRIPT built from script.toml. The `today` field will default to 0 and avoid SystemTime in simulation code.\n\n`last_day` will only update from the host field, not the clock. The wake line will show absence days as `today - last_day`. Adding a `SAVE_VERSION = 1` constant and exposing `stiffness` and `played` keys in status.\n\nFinalizing the save struct fields: stamps, age, world_time, music, save_serial, demo, day, outcome, phase, event, score, stars, podium, hub, minutes, and goal. Verified that finish_event and flow transitions won't cause double ticks or RNG issues. Starting to draft the score banking logic.\n\nDrafted the `bank` function. It awards one star plus the event's star count for first-time completions, adds minutes in Story mode excluding Check and BigStand, tracks played events, and updates total stars and best scores.\n\nCompleted the `bank` function. It updates best scores and tracks played events. Stamps are only collected on sleep, not during events. The sleep advance logic awards stamps for days one through four, then transitions to the finale on day five.\n\nDrafted `day_clear` to check that all required events for the current day are played and the minute goal is met. When entering the island after a result, the bot will automatically start sleep if the day is clear in Story mode. This removes the need for manual End Day presses.\n\nDay 5 after reveal begins BigStand directly. The first day starts with Check instead of the island.\n\nTraced the full first-day flow from title through Check and Reveal to the island. Free play after credits keeps the day at five, shows all events, and disables auto sleep. Added an END_DAY button for human players who finish early. The bot will skip island walking by sending SCHEDULE immediately.\n\nFlip flops are five positions on the island. The bot will not confirm them there, so a separate test must step the player. Unit-testing the pickup logic without physics is too weak. Teleporting the player directly in an integration test is the better approach.\n\nCharacter position is the capsule center, so teleporting the player is straightforward. The wardrobe will store skin and outfit choices in the save slot and expose them in status; visual changes are deferred to the app. The look UI will show six skins and eight outfits across pages.\n\nThe outfit screen will have two pages: six items on the first and two on the second, accessed by TAB. The bot will confirm the first item. Default puppet colors are acceptable for now; skin color can be added later. The room will use a high-key pastel aesthetic with colored floor blocks as props for version one, since dedicated beach or wellness props are not yet available.\n\nLibrary props are too much work for now. The immediate priority is getting the game logic to compile. I will write script.rs next to load the generated script.toml, then mod.rs for the game logic. Tests and fixes can come after compilation succeeds.\n\nDefined the script.rs deserialization structure. The File struct holds names, titles, skins, outfits, and a lines array of speaker-tag-text entries. The game will look up dialogue by character and tag.\n\nDefined the full set of dialogue tags, including intro, wake1 through wake5, sleep, check, reveal, ending_boat, ending_stay, credits, absence, together, pass, about, howto, and coach-specific tags. Pip will have at least eighty lines across these tags. The script generator will concatenate pip lines by index for each screen to ensure they are actually used rather than dead code. Acceptance is satisfied when the script file exists with the required counts.\n\nThe calendar screen will display one pip line per page so the full quote pool is reachable without repeating lines in a single playthrough. The island menu will include Schedule, Wardrobe, and Calendar; the bot will only press Schedule, leaving Calendar accessible by button ID. A real How To text will also be added.\n\nAbout pages will cover source, testing feedback, engine feedback, prompt feedback, fonts, and motion. They may span multiple pages via TAB. Real feedback text will be written after implementation rather than using placeholders. The exit interview schema in TASK.md needs review for correct structure.\n\nI will keep mod.rs under 1000 lines and add the necessary crate imports. Time scaling is implemented: dt still reaches pre during freeze, timers tick in pre, and event ticks run in post; a slider at id 59 maps 0..1 to 0.25..4. The exit interview schema will be reviewed when doing the hand-in.\n\nReset will restore default rules without touching progress. Wobble assist scales activity amplitude by multiplying against the base wobble value; this must be applied in post before the physics tick, since the tick reads the rule directly and overwrites the amplitude.\n\nThe wobble assist will be applied by cloning the rules struct and scaling its wobble value before each tick, since the tick function reads that field directly. Sensitivity will scale the lean input in pre and clamp it to the disc. A rhythm offset setting may shift note times when a step activity starts.\n\nThe rhythm offset will shift step activity note times by the configured amount when an activity begins. Default settings are finalized with music at 0.10, SFX and voice at 0.80, sensitivity and text speed at 1.0, wobble assist and rhythm offset at 0.0, and fullscreen disabled; the default glyph set is PS. Text speed scales the character reveal rate by a factor of two multiplied by the setting. During dialogue, pressing confirm while a line is still typing finishes it immediately, and pressing again advances to the next line.\n\nThe bot will skip the typewriter effect entirely. Confirming advances the line immediately, so no double-press logic is needed. The UI still tracks revealed characters for display, but tests do not depend on that count. Syllable audio events will be pushed at roughly every third character to keep the bot's typing sound in sync with the text.\n\nMusic will switch automatically when the game flow changes. A `want_song` method will compare the current song to the desired one and push a `Music` event only when they differ, avoiding redundant ticks. The physics simulation history is set to 8 seconds.\n\nThe bot's drive function will store the last movement direction while on the island and only return it when not waiting at the hub, so jump input stays clear. A gentle scripted walk may be added to the attract island segment so the capture shows the character moving.\n\nWorld time will advance only during Event, Check, and Island flows. Pause freezes the simulation so post never runs and time stays frozen. The attract demo will not increment time.\n\nWorld time will advance using the simulation's post-tick delta, which already accounts for any active time scale. The countdown flow is excluded from the time-advancing list, so its three-second duration does not affect world time. Menu logic will only run in pre, preventing double ticks.\n\nThe activity field will be `Option<Activity>` so the title screen can hold no active activity. Guest medley scores will be added. The code may be split into flow.rs and mod.rs if it grows too large. The bot step window in events.rs might need adjustment if tests fail.\n\nA shared `items()` helper will generate menu entries for both pre and fit_ui so the bot's focus index stays aligned with the UI. Focus type is usize. Dynamic labels are returned as owned strings.\n\nMenu input will use the shared `items()` helper. Confirm selects the focused item by ID, down cycles the index, and clicks or hovers activate or focus by ID. The `activate` method takes a mutable `Sim`. Sliders are not buttons.\n\nReset will use ID 60. Sliders will be listed as UI items with IDs above 300 so the bot can nudge them, though tests only need Slider events. The dev screen will show up to six visible entries: Resume, Reset feel, Time, and a note about live sliders. Many rules require paging through slider groups of four using TAB_L and TAB_R.\n\nSlider values will be shown in the UI lines. The attract demo will display a large \"DEMO\" ribbon via fit_ui.demo. Exiting the attract demo restores title focus, runs Story, clears the active activity, and leaves save_serial unchanged. Entering attract will not call touch_save. A Python script will generate the dialogue script and charts before writing mod.rs.\n\nThe guest medley title list is finalized. It contains twenty-one playful, balance-themed names.\n\nA `rank_title` function will map scores to titles by dividing the score by 1000 and using the result as an index into the title list, so higher scores pick later names. A deadpan result line will be added for low scores. The Python script will generate the dialogue script into the games/fit directory. mod.rs and script.rs will be written directly with the Write tool; mod.rs may be split into two search_replace parts if it grows too large.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ff7d4fd5-2afe-468f-9603-2005864e8ecd-60","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/rooms/wind_water.toml","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":980,"output_tokens":5092,"cache_read_input_tokens":121728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"cbeb2427-be95-43ca-a69b-22e64d3bf314"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ff7d4fd5-2afe-468f-9603-2005864e8ecd-60","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Wind & Water (vfx wing): grass and foliage in the wind (vertex shader), a rippling pond (CPU wave equation).\\n# GENERATED by a script kept outside the repo; hand-edits are fine.\\n#   WEST   the meadow: grass legend cells (`grass = { density, height, color }`), trees with swaying\\n#          canopies (`sway = \\\"leaves\\\"`), banners, tall reeds along the pond\\n#   EAST   the pond: a step, a wading ring (0.5 m) and a deep middle (1.8 m); one surface, a ball dropper above it\\n#   SOUTH  pads: WIND, TOWARD and WATER rows; DROP / CLEAR send the dropper's signals\\nname = \\\"Wind & Water\\\"\\nabout = \\\"Things that move by themselves: a meadow of grass and swaying trees in gusty wind (vertex animation on the GPU), and a pond whose surface is a wave simulation on the CPU, rippling wherever something moves through it. Pads change the wind, its direction and the water.\\\"\\ntry = [\\n10→  \\\"Walk into the tall grass: it parts around your feet. NO PUSH turns that off\\\",\\n  \\\"WIND > GALE, then STORM: waves roll over the meadow along the wind; TOWARD turns it\\\",\\n  \\\"Wade into the POND and walk around: you leave a wake. The middle is deep: swim\\\",\\n  \\\"DROP balls into the pond and watch the rings; FAST and SLOW change the wave speed, LONG FADE keeps it sloshing\\\",\\n  \\\"RAIN on the water; STILL turns the simulation off so you can compare with a flat pond\\\",\\n  \\\"Throw a bomb (F) into the water: a big dent and a ring\\\",\\n  \\\"Press H for how it works, the settings, the code and the words\\\",\\n]\\nwing = \\\"vfx\\\"\\norder = 7\\n20→primary_device = \\\"keyboard_mouse\\\"\\nentrance = { at = [20, 29], facing = \\\"south\\\" }\\n\\n[camera]\\ntilt = 55.0\\ndistance = 19.0\\nfov = 42.0\\n\\n[view]\\n\\\"light.sun_elevation\\\" = 50.0\\n30→\\\"light.sun_azimuth\\\" = 200.0\\n\\\"light.sun_intensity\\\" = 0.75\\nsky = \\\"#9cc4e0\\\"\\nwind = 0.9\\nwind_angle = 60.0\\nwind_gusts = 1.1\\n\\\"cutaway.height_cut\\\" = false\\n\\n# Station guide (H in the game): what you see, how it works, where games use it, how to ask.\\n[learn]\\n40→what = \\\"A meadow and a pond, both moving. Thousands of grass tufts bend in waves as gusts roll across, the tree canopies and banners sway, and the grass parts around your feet. In the pond, everything that moves through the water leaves rings: you wading, the walker, dropped balls, raindrops. The rings spread, bounce off the edges and fade.\\\"\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Wind & Water (vfx wing): grass and foliage in the wind (vertex shader), a rippling pond (CPU wave equation).\\n# GENERATED by a script kept outside the repo; hand-edits are fine.\\n#   WEST   the meadow: grass legend cells (`grass = { density, height, color }`), trees with swaying\\n#          canopies (`sway = \\\"leaves\\\"`), banners, tall reeds along the pond\\n#   EAST   the pond: a step, a wading ring (0.5 m) and a deep middle (1.8 m); one surface, a ball dropper above it\\n#   SOUTH  pads: WIND, TOWARD and WATER rows; DROP / CLEAR send the dropper's signals\\nname = \\\"Wind & Water\\\"\\nabout = \\\"Things that move by themselves: a meadow of grass and swaying trees in gusty wind (vertex animation on the GPU), and a pond whose surface is a wave simulation on the CPU, rippling wherever something moves through it. Pads change the wind, its direction and the water.\\\"\\ntry = [\\n10→  \\\"Walk into the tall grass: it parts around your feet. NO PUSH turns that off\\\",\\n  \\\"WIND > GALE, then STORM: waves roll over the meadow along the wind; TOWARD turns it\\\",\\n  \\\"Wade into the POND and walk around: you leave a wake. The middle is deep: swim\\\",\\n  \\\"DROP balls into the pond and watch the rings; FAST and SLOW change the wave speed, LONG FADE keeps it sloshing\\\",\\n  \\\"RAIN on the water; STILL turns the simulation off so you can compare with a flat pond\\\",\\n  \\\"Throw a bomb (F) into the water: a big dent and a ring\\\",\\n  \\\"Press H for how it works, the settings, the code and the words\\\",\\n]\\nwing = \\\"vfx\\\"\\norder = 7\\n20→primary_device = \\\"keyboard_mouse\\\"\\nentrance = { at = [20, 29], facing = \\\"south\\\" }\\n\\n[camera]\\ntilt = 55.0\\ndistance = 19.0\\nfov = 42.0\\n\\n[view]\\n\\\"light.sun_elevation\\\" = 50.0\\n30→\\\"light.sun_azimuth\\\" = 200.0\\n\\\"light.sun_intensity\\\" = 0.75\\nsky = \\\"#9cc4e0\\\"\\nwind = 0.9\\nwind_angle = 60.0\\nwind_gusts = 1.1\\n\\\"cutaway.height_cut\\\" = false\\n\\n# Station guide (H in the game): what you see, how it works, where games use it, how to ask.\\n[learn]\\n40→what = \\\"A meadow and a pond, both moving. Thousands of grass tufts bend in waves as gusts roll across, the tree canopies and banners sway, and the grass parts around your feet. In the pond, everything that moves through the water leaves rings: you wading, the walker, dropped balls, raindrops. The rings spread, bounce off the edges and fade.\\\"\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/rooms/wind_water.toml\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"# Wind & Water (vfx wing): grass and foliage in the wind (vertex shader), a rippling pond (CPU wave equation).\\n# GENERATED by a script kept outside the repo; hand-edits are fine.\\n#   WEST   the meadow: grass legend cells (`grass = { density, height, color }`), trees with swaying\\n#          canopies (`sway = \\\"leaves\\\"`), banners, tall reeds along the pond\\n#   EAST   the pond: a step, a wading ring (0.5 m) and a deep middle (1.8 m); one surface, a ball dropper above it\\n#   SOUTH  pads: WIND, TOWARD and WATER rows; DROP / CLEAR send the dropper's signals\\nname = \\\"Wind & Water\\\"\\nabout = \\\"Things that move by themselves: a meadow of grass and swaying trees in gusty wind (vertex animation on the GPU), and a pond whose surface is a wave simulation on the CPU, rippling wherever something moves through it. Pads change the wind, its direction and the water.\\\"\\ntry = [\\n  \\\"Walk into the tall grass: it parts around your feet. NO PUSH turns that off\\\",\\n  \\\"WIND > GALE, then STORM: waves roll over the meadow along the wind; TOWARD turns it\\\",\\n  \\\"Wade into the POND and walk around: you leave a wake. The middle is deep: swim\\\",\\n  \\\"DROP balls into the pond and watch the rings; FAST and SLOW change the wave speed, LONG FADE keeps it sloshing\\\",\\n  \\\"RAIN on the water; STILL turns the simulation off so you can compare with a flat pond\\\",\\n  \\\"Throw a bomb (F) into the water: a big dent and a ring\\\",\\n  \\\"Press H for how it works, the settings, the code and the words\\\",\\n]\\nwing = \\\"vfx\\\"\\norder = 7\\nprimary_device = \\\"keyboard_mouse\\\"\\nentrance = { at = [20, 29], facing = \\\"south\\\" }\\n\\n[camera]\\ntilt = 55.0\\ndistance = 19.0\\nfov = 42.0\\n\\n[view]\\n\\\"light.sun_elevation\\\" = 50.0\\n\\\"light.sun_azimuth\\\" = 200.0\\n\\\"light.sun_intensity\\\" = 0.75\\nsky = \\\"#9cc4e0\\\"\\nwind = 0.9\\nwind_angle = 60.0\\nwind_gusts = 1.1\\n\\\"cutaway.height_cut\\\" = false\\n\\n# Station guide (H in the game): what you see, how it works, where games use it, how to ask.\\n[learn]\\nwhat = \\\"A meadow and a pond, both moving. Thousands of grass tufts bend in waves as gusts roll across, the tree canopies and banners sway, and the grass parts around your feet. In the pond, everything that moves through the water leaves rings: you wading, the walker, dropped balls, raindrops. The rings spread, bounce off the edges and fade.\\\"\\n\",\"total_lines\":457}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"06f8c3df-2d68-4160-a031-b10a89cd7db8"}
