{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-84ef5ed6-e3e0-4a29-b124-c3ecc5c964ea-77","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→libm = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nminiz_oxide = \\\"0.8\\\"\\nlog = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nbytemuck = { version = \\\"1\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\"] }\\npollster = \\\"1\\\"\\nweb-time = \\\"1\\\"\\n# Browser build only.\\nwasm-bindgen = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen-futures = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nweb-sys = \\\"0.3\\\"\\n50→\\n[workspace.lints.clippy]\\n# Style lints that fight readable game code.\\ncollapsible_if = \\\"allow\\\"\\ncollapsible_match = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntype_complexity = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntoo_many_arguments = \\\"allow\\\"\\n\\n[profile.dev]\\nopt-level = 1\\n60→# Keeps the target folder small (cloud containers have a fixed disk allowance); backtraces\\n# still show file:line.\\ndebug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\nincremental = false\\n\\n[profile.dev.package.\\\"*\\\"]\\nopt-level = 3\\ndebug = false\\n\\n[profile.release]\\n70→debug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\n\\n# Distribution build (what gets sent to the user): smaller, still has function names in crash reports.\\n[profile.dist]\\ninherits = \\\"release\\\"\\ndebug = false\\nstrip = \\\"debuginfo\\\"\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"40→libm = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nminiz_oxide = \\\"0.8\\\"\\nlog = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nbytemuck = { version = \\\"1\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\"] }\\npollster = \\\"1\\\"\\nweb-time = \\\"1\\\"\\n# Browser build only.\\nwasm-bindgen = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen-futures = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nweb-sys = \\\"0.3\\\"\\n50→\\n[workspace.lints.clippy]\\n# Style lints that fight readable game code.\\ncollapsible_if = \\\"allow\\\"\\ncollapsible_match = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntype_complexity = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntoo_many_arguments = \\\"allow\\\"\\n\\n[profile.dev]\\nopt-level = 1\\n60→# Keeps the target folder small (cloud containers have a fixed disk allowance); backtraces\\n# still show file:line.\\ndebug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\nincremental = false\\n\\n[profile.dev.package.\\\"*\\\"]\\nopt-level = 3\\ndebug = false\\n\\n[profile.release]\\n70→debug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\n\\n# Distribution build (what gets sent to the user): smaller, still has function names in crash reports.\\n[profile.dist]\\ninherits = \\\"release\\\"\\ndebug = false\\nstrip = \\\"debuginfo\\\"\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/Cargo.toml\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"libm = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nminiz_oxide = \\\"0.8\\\"\\nlog = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nbytemuck = { version = \\\"1\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\"] }\\npollster = \\\"1\\\"\\nweb-time = \\\"1\\\"\\n# Browser build only.\\nwasm-bindgen = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen-futures = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nweb-sys = \\\"0.3\\\"\\n\\n[workspace.lints.clippy]\\n# Style lints that fight readable game code.\\ncollapsible_if = \\\"allow\\\"\\ncollapsible_match = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntype_complexity = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntoo_many_arguments = \\\"allow\\\"\\n\\n[profile.dev]\\nopt-level = 1\\n# Keeps the target folder small (cloud containers have a fixed disk allowance); backtraces\\n# still show file:line.\\ndebug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\nincremental = false\\n\\n[profile.dev.package.\\\"*\\\"]\\nopt-level = 3\\ndebug = false\\n\\n[profile.release]\\ndebug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\n\\n# Distribution build (what gets sent to the user): smaller, still has function names in crash reports.\\n[profile.dist]\\ninherits = \\\"release\\\"\\ndebug = false\\nstrip = \\\"debuginfo\\\"\\n\",\"total_lines\":76}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"ad8e5567-b6e2-4227-b1ba-26cdee919783"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_174","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Warnings won't fail the build. I'll try to use any unused items.\n\nWriting script.rs, hub.toml, and mod.rs. Confirmed `get_mut` uses `sim.state.entities.get_mut`. The about text will be brief. A bug in the gust test was spotted: step_clean resets kicks and amplitude but leaves gust state unchanged.\n\nThe gust test should pass. The 8.5 damping coefficient will kill any residual velocity within three seconds. step_clean correctly resets and restores amplitude. Now writing mod.rs with a defensive style.\n\n`pre` already has `&mut Sim`, so that is fine. A new problem surfaced: `params::list` requires `&mut dyn Tunable`, but `fit_ui` only has `&self`. This prevents listing parameters in the UI during dev builds.\n\nCloning `self.rules` inside `fit_ui` resolves the `&self` limitation for listing parameters. `apply_slider` will also clone rules to read settings, then drop that borrow before writing the real value.\n\nThe slider logic maps normalized values to float or integer ranges. It extracts the parameter path and kind from the cloned rules list, then constructs a ParamValue for the new setting.\n\n`ParamKind` derives `Clone`, so it satisfies the borrow requirements. Slider 300 maps to stiffness, with values between 5 and 80; resetting restores 40. Setting sliders like music and voice use absolute 0..1 ranges, while sensitivity, wobble, rhythm, and text map to their respective spans. These are not critical for the first tests. Public ACT constants will be added so tests can reference them directly.\n\nSave and load methods will be public. The save version is 1, and older versions will be rejected. Slot fields will use `#[serde(default)]` so future additions do not break old saves. `today` is public for tests. `get_mut` works.\n\nA `world_time` helper is unnecessary; status already provides that data. The UI will use two-line cards: speaker in the title, text in the first line. Cards display event titles with coach and blurb lines, a countdown number during countdowns, and prompts as footers. Results show rank titles with score, star count, and minutes, plus Back and Retry buttons. Star ratings will use plain text like \"2 stars\" to avoid encoding issues.\n\nPersonal bests will appear on the second line of cards. Minutes banked will be shown in the footer. Age will display as large text during reveal. The ending splits into a rowboat path for ages 40 and under, and an extended path otherwise. Credits will list thanks with a big \"Credits\" header. The podium phase stores a vector of names and scores; it is empty until the player enters that state.\n\nTogether mode tracks scores per player in a vector. Each medley event adds to that player's total. The three medleys are Paddle, Tide, and Cannon. After all events finish the game builds the podium.\n\nHub stats will store each medley score in a fixed array. The hub total clamps to 0..3000 and ends once all three medleys finish. Direct events bank and result without chaining. Story checks record bests and played status but do not bank minutes. The ever_played set includes check and bigstand so the \"every event\" test passes. Today_played tracks day events only.\n\nMinutes are added only for story events that are not Check or BigStand. The first-play flag is computed before marking the event as played, so the check must scan the existing set directly. Repeated plays add one minute; first-time plays add one plus the star count. The star total always increments by the current score. Best scores are updated in a map keyed by event identifier.\n\nWhen a personal best is set, the current act's samples are saved as a ghost for that event. The save serial only increments during normal story runs; it is skipped in demo, direct, and hub modes, and never touched by slider adjustments.\n\nSave serials increment on day changes and results. New stays write the slot when the outfit is confirmed. The `write_slot` method marks the slot used and copies the current name into it. The `read_slot` method clones a saved slot and restores its index and name.\n\n`read_slot` restores the saved day and flow state, defaulting to Island for free-play slots and Wake otherwise. The continue path from the title screen will list only used slots. `export_save` writes the current slot and serializes it as JSON. `import_save` replaces all saved slots, settings, and last-day data, then reloads the current slot if it is marked used. A fresh game exported before any save would still mark that slot used.\n\nThe import test will verify that day, age, stamps, name, and music settings all survive a round trip. A version field will be added to reject corrupted save files.\n\n`import_save` will deserialize the JSON into a `SaveDto`, reject any version other than 1, and restore slots, settings, and last day. It then reloads the current slot only if that slot is marked used. The save format will use a fixed `[Slot; 4]` array so serde handles it directly, and `Slot` must implement `Default` for `FitGame::fresh`.\n\nThe slot will store an `outcome_won` flag so `read_slot` can restore the exact game outcome after import. The `run` field will not be saved. A room file will be added. `script.rs` will expose a public `names()` function returning a static slice from a `OnceLock`.\n\n`names()` will return `&'static [String]` from a static `Script`. A `line(speaker, tag, i)` helper will fetch a specific line. `count(speaker, tag)` and `count_speaker(speaker)` will return total line counts.\n\nScript loading will fall back to a default Script if parsing fails, so tests can assert line counts. The script avoids double quotes and apostrophes to prevent JSON escaping issues.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e8950b46-e20d-4cb4-b944-d3a9e2716070-78","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"text = \".*\".*\"","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/script.toml"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":384,"output_tokens":3486,"cache_read_input_tokens":157952,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"88c9eb82-dd58-4d95-a568-6dfb85b4a270"}
