{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-da5882ef-1370-4935-b9aa-b760d8ff7bdf-79","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,108,105,98,46,114,115,10,52,52,58,112,117,98,32,109,111,100,32,112,117,112,112,101,116,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/lib.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":44,\"content\":\"pub mod puppet;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"1e1d110e-506a-4030-a4aa-4e9d3905ff93"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_176","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing files now. The mod.rs file will be comprehensive.\n\nNo NPCs will be added to the room file to avoid AI overhead. The mod.rs write will be split if it becomes too long. I'll add the necessary `use super::core::Rules` imports. Confirmed that `0_f32.powf(1.1)` evaluates to 0 in Rust.\n\nWriting script.rs, hub, and mod.rs together. Verified that finish_play story checks don't overwrite the result. Confirmed big stand stamps bank once without double stamping. Checked that days_completed increments on sleep before the finale check.\n\nDay 4 sleep correctly advances to day 5 and triggers free play. Day 5 is the final day. Auto-sleep after clearing a goal skips the island between events. This is acceptable for the bot.\n\nAuto-sleep is being removed. The bot will press SCHEDULE on the island and select End Day when all events are played, or the next event otherwise. This preserves free time for humans.\n\nThe bot will always return to the island after a result. The schedule ID for End Day is 90. On the schedule screen, unplayed events are focused first and confirmed; otherwise End Day is selected if available.\n\nIf all events are played but minutes are short, the bot will replay the first event until the time limit is met. Once minutes are sufficient, it will select End Day. On day one, the schedule screen opens with focus at zero.\n\nThe schedule screen resets focus to zero on every open. The bot presses SCHEDULE only while the flow is Island, and it never opens the schedule during an event. Selecting End Day triggers Sleep as a talk screen once the day is clear.\n\nThe bot confirms through the sleep screen lines before advancing. Day 5 begins with the big stand reveal instead of the island, so the schedule is not needed there. After confirming the big stand card and playing through the ending and credits, the bot sets the status to Won. The next loop iteration sees this status and returns without stepping, leaving the game in Credits with all five stamps collected.\n\nConfirmed the event list contains exactly 13 items. The test will assert that every EventId is present in played, all five stamps are collected, the outcome is won, and world_time remains under 3600.\n\nMenu overhead is minimal, so total simulation time stays under sixty minutes. The bot will run for up to 216000 ticks. A stuck state was considered: confirming the result screen sends Back, which returns the bot to the island. Focus is reset to zero on entry, preventing any misfire.\n\nThe bot will skip card and countdown screens by pressing CONFIRM. Gameplay events and checks receive actual gameplay inputs instead of menu commands.\n\nConfirmed that the card skip logic only applies to the Card flow, so gameplay events and checks are not accidentally skipped. The bot sends no buttons during long stillness, which leaves pressed at zero and avoids setting forfeit. Step inputs are correctly handled by storing last_pressed in pre and using it in post. One timing issue was noted: the test calls bot() before step(), so the bot sees state at the start of the tick, and a menu confirmation may change the flow between pre and post within the same tick.\n\nConfirmed the pre-post timing is sound. The bot computes its lean from the state at the start of the tick, and menu confirmations change the flow in pre so the next tick sees the new state. During attract mode, the internal demo bot overrides player input for the activity unless a wake button is pressed.\n\nThe attract wake handler exits to the title screen immediately. It returns the player drive without incrementing idle time, and the confirm input is consumed in that single tick so the title screen does not misread it.\n\nThe attract wake handler now uses an early return so the same CONFIRM input cannot activate the title menu in the same tick. Touch clicks and settings are still handled during attract mode.\n\nSettings now stores the previous flow in a return_flow field. Returning from settings restores that flow, and if it is attract mode, the demo bot resumes. Opening settings from anywhere will not nest the menu.\n\nDev resume returns to the paused flow. Pausing during an event freezes the event clock and world time until resumed. The stiffness slider updates rules live, so the next tick uses the new value. Credits can still be paused. Ready to write the code.\n\nA `menu_flow` helper will identify which flows need menu key handling. Event, Check, Island, Attract, and Countdown are excluded because they use their own confirm logic or lack menus entirely.\n\nIsland SCHEDULE is handled as a special case outside the menu flow. Island confirm passes through to post without being consumed by pre, since Island is not a menu. A generic BACK button handler will be added for menu flows.\n\nWardrobe will be added to the pause and dev menus, plus a How To entry. The island already uses SCHEDULE for the schedule screen, so wardrobe needs a separate button.\n\nWardrobe will open as a Flow::Wardrobe screen with skins and outfits paged, and confirm selects the current choice. It is reachable from the Dev pause menu item. Calendar will also appear on the pause screen to show stamps and ages. The Dev menu page zero will list Resume, Reset feel, Wardrobe, Calendar, Settings, and About before the slider pages.\n\nSlider events will be applied globally in pre, but only honored while the flow is Dev or Settings. This prevents random slider inputs during gameplay from affecting rules. Reset clicks are restricted to the Dev flow.\n\nSlider events are now gated by flow and ID range: Dev mode accepts IDs 300–399, while Settings accepts IDs 610–619. Clicks on published items remain functional in any flow, including the attract screen where the settings button is published.\n\nHover moves focus to the item if it is on screen. The settings button will be published during attract mode whenever touch input is active, since the test taps it directly.\n\nDevice detection runs before UI click handling so touch input is visible in the same frame. A top comment will be added to mod.rs. Rules will load from a TOML file with defaults if parsing fails. Squat reps are stored as i32.\n\nExtra TOML keys will be ignored rather than rejected. A brief notes/decisions.md will be added. The integration test will be written after compilation to avoid a broken API, though the author could write it now since the interface is known. The entity map's `get_mut` method is being verified against sim.rs.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The script and the balance tests are in place. Next I’ll wire the stay itself so a fresh game can reach credits."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d3c2a67d-a4cf-406b-b693-f4d7c5692460-80","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/hub.toml","new_string":"# Tippy Cay, loaded on its own for Wobble Minutes. Small on purpose: the sim steps this\n# thousands of times in tests.\nname = \"Tippy Cay\"\nabout = \"A bright deck, a mat, and a lagoon that thinks it is a sports field.\"\nentrance = { at = [2, 10], facing = \"south\" }\n\n[camera]\ntilt = 16.0\ndistance = 8.5\nfov = 36.0\nyaw = 0.0\n\n[view]\nsky = \"#c9e7ff\"\n\"light.sun_elevation\" = 62.0\n\"light.sun_intensity\" = 1.15\n\"light.ambient\" = 0.55\n\"cutaway.height_cut\" = false\n\n[layout]\norigin = [-8.0, 0.0, -6.0]\n\n[[layout.layer]]\ny = 0\nmap = '''\n################\n#..............#\n#..............#\n#....wwwwww....#\n#....wwwwww....#\n#..............#\n#......P.......#\n#..............#\n#..............#\n#..............#\n#..............#\n################\n'''\n\n[layout.legend.'.']\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0.0, color = \"#f0d7a8\" }]\ngrass = { color = \"#b7e0a4\", height = 0.16, density = 2.0 }\n\n[layout.legend.'#']\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0.0, color = \"#f0d7a8\" }, { y0 = 0.0, y1 = 0.35, color = \"#f7b7c8\", rounded = true }]\n\n[layout.legend.'w']\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.7, y1 = -0.02, color = \"#7fd0ea\" }]\n\n[layout.legend.'P']\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0.0, color = \"#ffe8b0\" }]\nmarker = \"player\"\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d3c2a67d-a4cf-406b-b693-f4d7c5692460-81","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/script.rs","new_string":"//! Dialogue, names, titles, and looks. Loaded once from `script.toml`.\n\nuse std::sync::OnceLock;\n\nuse serde::Deserialize;\n\nconst SCRIPT: &str = include_str!(\"script.toml\");\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Deserialize)]\nstruct RawLine {\n    speaker: String,\n    tag: String,\n    text: String,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Deserialize)]\nstruct Raw {\n    #[serde(default)]\n    names: Vec<String>,\n    #[serde(default)]\n    titles: Vec<String>,\n    #[serde(default)]\n    skins: Vec<String>,\n    #[serde(default)]\n    outfits: Vec<String>,\n    #[serde(default)]\n    lines: Vec<RawLine>,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\npub struct Script {\n    pub names: Vec<String>,\n    pub titles: Vec<String>,\n    pub skins: Vec<String>,\n    pub outfits: Vec<String>,\n    lines: Vec<RawLine>,\n}\n\nimpl Script {\n    pub fn line(&self, speaker: &str, tag: &str, i: usize) -> Option<&str> {\n        self.lines.iter().filter(|l| l.speaker == speaker && l.tag == tag).nth(i).map(|l| l.text.as_str())\n    }\n\n    pub fn count(&self, speaker: &str, tag: &str) -> usize {\n        self.lines.iter().filter(|l| l.speaker == speaker && l.tag == tag).count()\n    }\n\n    pub fn speaker_count(&self, speaker: &str) -> usize {\n        self.lines.iter().filter(|l| l.speaker == speaker).count()\n    }\n}\n\npub fn script() -> &'static Script {\n    static CELL: OnceLock<Script> = OnceLock::new();\n    CELL.get_or_init(|| {\n        let text = crate::games::level_text(\"fit/script\", SCRIPT);\n        let raw: Raw = toml::from_str(&text).unwrap_or(Raw {\n            names: vec![\"Avery\".into()],\n            titles: vec![\"Acceptable Human\".into()],\n            skins: vec![\"Sand\".into()],\n            outfits: vec![\"Linen\".into()],\n            lines: vec![RawLine { speaker: \"Pip\".into(), tag: \"intro\".into(), text: \"Welcome ashore.\".into() }],\n        });\n        Script { names: raw.names, titles: raw.titles, skins: raw.skins, outfits: raw.outfits, lines: raw.lines }\n    })\n}\n\npub fn rank_title(score: f32) -> String {\n    let s = script();\n    if s.titles.is_empty() {\n        return \"Acceptable Human\".into();\n    }\n    let t = (score / 1000.0).clamp(0.0, 0.999);\n    let i = (t * s.titles.len() as f32) as usize;\n    s.titles[i.min(s.titles.len() - 1)].clone()\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":409,"output_tokens":5651,"cache_read_input_tokens":161792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"9b5e2573-04a8-4a9e-b231-26c1f76d61f3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d3c2a67d-a4cf-406b-b693-f4d7c5692460-80","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Tippy Cay, loaded on its own for Wobble Minutes. Small on purpose: the sim steps this\\n# thousands of times in tests.\\nname = \\\"Tippy Cay\\\"\\nabout = \\\"A bright deck, a mat, and a lagoon that thinks it is a sports field.\\\"\\nentrance = { at = [2, 10], facing = \\\"south\\\" }\\n\\n[camera]\\ntilt = 16.0\\ndistance = 8.5\\nfov = 36.0\\nyaw = 0.0\\n\\n[view]\\nsky = \\\"#c9e7ff\\\"\\n\\\"light.sun_elevation\\\" = 62.0\\n\\\"light.sun_intensity\\\" = 1.15\\n\\\"light.ambient\\\" = 0.55\\n\\\"cutaway.height_cut\\\" = false\\n\\n[layout]\\norigin = [-8.0, 0.0, -6.0]\\n\\n[[layout.layer]]\\ny = 0\\nmap = '''\\n################\\n#..............#\\n#..............#\\n#....wwwwww....#\\n#....wwwwww....#\\n#..............#\\n#......P.......#\\n#..............#\\n#..............#\\n#..............#\\n#..............#\\n################\\n'''\\n\\n[layout.legend.'.']\\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0.0, color = \\\"#f0d7a8\\\" }]\\ngrass = { color = \\\"#b7e0a4\\\", height = 0.16, density = 2.0 }\\n\\n[layout.legend.'#']\\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0.0, color = \\\"#f0d7a8\\\" }, { y0 = 0.0, y1 = 0.35, color = \\\"#f7b7c8\\\", rounded = true }]\\n\\n[layout.legend.'w']\\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.7, y1 = -0.02, color = \\\"#7fd0ea\\\" }]\\n\\n[layout.legend.'P']\\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0.0, color = \\\"#ffe8b0\\\" }]\\nmarker = \\\"player\\\"\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/hub.toml has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii F