{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7da95720-4c90-4921-bc90-37b81c8677f9-84","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"101→pub struct SimState {\\n    /// The prop definitions placed copies use, each once. Declared first: a restore reads it\\n    /// before the entities that name its keys.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"crate::props::PropDefTable::is_empty\\\")]\\n    pub prop_defs: crate::props::PropDefTable,\\n    pub tick: u64,\\n    pub seed: u64,\\n    pub rng: Rng,\\n    pub physics: PhysicsState,\\n110→    pub entities: Entities,\\n    pub statics: StaticWorld,\\n    pub scene: String,\\n    pub focus: Vec3,\\n    pub player: Option<EntityId>,\\n    pub spawn: Vec3,\\n    pub world: World,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub courses: Courses,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n120→    pub projectiles: Projectiles,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub feel: FeelMeter,\\n    /// Signals sent by pads this tick (read by spawners next tick).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub signals: Vec<String>,\\n    /// Tiles that are crumbling or waiting to regrow.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub crumbles: Vec<crate::destruct::Crumble>,\\n    /// Shardfall, when this scene is part of the game.\\n130→    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub game: Option<Box<crate::arpg::Game>>,\\n    /// A game from `crate::games` (the starter, or one an agent added), when this scene is one.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub play: Option<crate::games::GameBox>,\\n    /// The animation stage freezes this world and publishes its own render frame.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub animation_preview: Option<crate::animation_preview::PreviewState>,\\n    /// None is only for legacy snapshots whose active animation stage predates this field.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n140→    pub studio_mode: Option<crate::prop_preview::StudioMode>,\",\"content_concise\":\"101→pub struct SimState {\\n    /// The prop definitions placed copies use, each once. Declared first: a restore reads it\\n    /// before the entities that name its keys.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"crate::props::PropDefTable::is_empty\\\")]\\n    pub prop_defs: crate::props::PropDefTable,\\n    pub tick: u64,\\n    pub seed: u64,\\n    pub rng: Rng,\\n    pub physics: PhysicsState,\\n110→    pub entities: Entities,\\n    pub statics: StaticWorld,\\n    pub scene: String,\\n    pub focus: Vec3,\\n    pub player: Option<EntityId>,\\n    pub spawn: Vec3,\\n    pub world: World,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub courses: Courses,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n120→    pub projectiles: Projectiles,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub feel: FeelMeter,\\n    /// Signals sent by pads this tick (read by spawners next tick).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub signals: Vec<String>,\\n    /// Tiles that are crumbling or waiting to regrow.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub crumbles: Vec<crate::destruct::Crumble>,\\n    /// Shardfall, when this scene is part of the game.\\n130→    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub game: Option<Box<crate::arpg::Game>>,\\n    /// A game from `crate::games` (the starter, or one an agent added), when this scene is one.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub play: Option<crate::games::GameBox>,\\n    /// The animation stage freezes this world and publishes its own render frame.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub animation_preview: Option<crate::animation_preview::PreviewState>,\\n    /// None is only for legacy snapshots whose active animation stage predates this field.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n140→    pub studio_mode: Option<crate::prop_preview::StudioMode>,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs\",\"offset\":101,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"pub struct SimState {\\n    /// The prop definitions placed copies use, each once. Declared first: a restore reads it\\n    /// before the entities that name its keys.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"crate::props::PropDefTable::is_empty\\\")]\\n    pub prop_defs: crate::props::PropDefTable,\\n    pub tick: u64,\\n    pub seed: u64,\\n    pub rng: Rng,\\n    pub physics: PhysicsState,\\n    pub entities: Entities,\\n    pub statics: StaticWorld,\\n    pub scene: String,\\n    pub focus: Vec3,\\n    pub player: Option<EntityId>,\\n    pub spawn: Vec3,\\n    pub world: World,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub courses: Courses,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub projectiles: Projectiles,\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub feel: FeelMeter,\\n    /// Signals sent by pads this tick (read by spawners next tick).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub signals: Vec<String>,\\n    /// Tiles that are crumbling or waiting to regrow.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub crumbles: Vec<crate::destruct::Crumble>,\\n    /// Shardfall, when this scene is part of the game.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub game: Option<Box<crate::arpg::Game>>,\\n    /// A game from `crate::games` (the starter, or one an agent added), when this scene is one.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub play: Option<crate::games::GameBox>,\\n    /// The animation stage freezes this world and publishes its own render frame.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub animation_preview: Option<crate::animation_preview::PreviewState>,\\n    /// None is only for legacy snapshots whose active animation stage predates this field.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub studio_mode: Option<crate::prop_preview::StudioMode>,\\n\",\"total_lines\":1210}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"c5b4ce62-f4b5-4a62-bb73-0c1890da37ce"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_180","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing mod.rs now. I'll be thorough but skip unnecessary comments.\n\nPlanning the full mod.rs structure. It will include imports, constants, and fields for settings like fullscreen, text_speed, sensitivity, and xbox. The despawn function will be public.\n\nAdding `ending_name` for unit tests. Save round-trip and ending logic will be tested in `mod.rs` without the full simulation. Room construction stays as the integration test.\n\nA save round-trip unit test is being added to mod.rs. It constructs a FitGame, exports its state, then imports it back and asserts all fields match exactly. `fresh()` will serve as the constructor, with `build()` calling it and then applying modifications.\n\nConfirmed the save round-trip logic: export writes the slot, and import reads it back. If the day is zero, it defaults to one. Settings music will default to 0.10 f32 instead of 0.1 to avoid floating-point precision issues; tests will compare with a small epsilon. Now writing mod.rs while ensuring match exhaustiveness.\n\nDefined the Flow and Run enums. Flow covers every game state from Title through Credits and Attract. Run has five modes: Story, Medley, Together, Direct, and Demo.\n\nAttract mode stores the previous run in saved_run and switches to Demo. Exiting attract restores the saved run. Entering attract from Title saves Story and enters Demo. It is blocked when the current run is Medley or a hub.\n\nPregame menus are Title, Slots, Name, Look, and Outfit. Settings and About pause the idle timer without resetting it. Only Title increments the idle count toward attract mode.\n\nAbout and HowTo are also pregame screens that can trigger attract mode. Settings is excluded to avoid interrupting slider sessions. Idle time resets only on these specific screens. Entering attract is blocked if the run is already Demo. Now writing the code in compact style.\n\nThe slots screen uses ACT ids 10 through 14. Slot indices are derived by subtracting 10. The continuing flag is set when Continue is chosen and cleared when New Stay is selected. Choosing Continue from Title opens the slots screen with continuing enabled. Choosing New Stay resets progress, sets the slot index, and advances to Name.\n\nACT_NEW opens the slots screen with continuing disabled. The bot will confirm the first slot when starting a new game. reset_progress preserves settings, today, slot, save_serial, and last_day while clearing everything else. Settings are not wiped during reset. Name is set on the name screen before reset occurs. Entering Together from Title does not reset the story slot.\n\nStarting Together does not reset the current slot or call reset. The mode uses its own scores and does not bank story minutes, so existing save data remains untouched.\n\nDirect and Medley runs start from fresh() with a default name of \"Guest\". The demo flag is set to false in fresh(). Music sync pushes the first song on the first pregame screen. Attract mode stays silent until a real input triggers music.\n\nTouch input will not exit attract mode. It will still resume audio, tracked by an `audio_unlocked` flag set on any real input including touch. This is optional for the first tests.\n\ndesired_song returns 0 during attract and before audio is unlocked. Title stays silent until the first real input. The bot's first CONFIRM unlocks audio. Exiting attract counts as a real input and resumes music. Touch unlocks the audio context without leaving attract mode.\n\nThe internal attract bot will not trigger audio unlocking. Only external input frames can set the `audio_unlocked` flag. The file will be written in a single pass.\n\nFlips will be stored as a u8 bitmask, with golden achieved when all five bits are set. The five flop positions are placed around the spawn point using hardcoded offsets relative to the player's feet coordinates. Ready to write mod.rs.\n\nThe `Game` trait will expose `hud`, `status`, `fit_ui`, `tint`, `frozen`, `bot`, `pre`, `post`, and a `build` function. Public items from the private modules will be re-exported so integration tests can access constants like `balance_age` and `shape_stick`. Unit tests will remain inside the modules, while integration tests will exercise `Sim` and status JSON.\n\nConfirmed medley chaining uses a consistent RNG stream across chained events. The next event starts at tick zero on the following frame without an extra tick in the same post. The hub test completes when the last event sets hub_done.\n\nScore totals are three per stored event. The bot is deterministic because the RNG is seeded, so identical seeds produce matching runs; different seeds shift paddle gates and can change scores. Tests will set history to zero before stepping to avoid recording the default eight seconds. The game_keys integration test builds the room via Sim::new without taking many steps.\n\nVerifying the Piece struct fields and confirming the map dimensions are 16 by 12. The entrance at [2, 10] sits on row 10, which is the bottom wall.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-af81082b-075e-4438-9df9-a46bb8840f7d-85","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"entrance","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/room.rs","head_limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":597,"output_tokens":3461,"cache_read_input_tokens":170112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"55554a1f-7a79-409b-85ea-0567e70c04b2"}
