{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6364b474-6eba-4592-841c-2ffca835f0fd-12","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Plan: Ship a playable Tippy Cay balance-and-wellness demo inspired by Wii Fit, plus the hand-in files TASK.md names\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in package.** The work-folder root contains `PROGRESS.md`, a parseable `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape TASK.md specifies (every value filled, `\\\"usage\\\"` exactly `added on import`, `aiHub.genre` one of the allowed catalogue genres, `aiHub.players` `1–4`), and one self-contained HTML file named `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html`. A sibling folder with that same basename (no `.html`) holds the dev tree. `{Title}` is a playful riff on “Wii Fit”, chosen by listing 50 titles and selecting one with a real RNG; the same string is the title-screen name, the page `<title>`, and `aiHub.name`. The 50 titles and the RNG draw are recorded in the dev folder. Opening the HTML from disk boots this game (a WebGPU-missing message only when WebGPU is absent).\\n2. **Wii Fit loop, original world.** It is a third-person sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame: a five-day stay at Tippy Cay staffed by talking gym gear. The only play verb is a centre-of-pressure lean (left stick, keyboard ramp, or mouse offset from screen centre — last device wins) driving one shared balance model: shaped lean, stiffness/damping, sim-time wobble, tip only after the dot stays outside the unit disc for the tip time. Tips cost time or score and never end the stay. Each morning a wobble check (still, lean targets, eyes-closed tone, step timing) yields a Balance Age from PLAN.md’s skill formula, clamped 18–99; better input gives a lower age. There is no weight, BMI, body-shape, or diet content, and no Nintendo product names inside play (About source line and the title riff only). Days open in order — stillness, strength, cardio, lagoon — with minute goals 3, 5, 7, 9, then a Day-5 Big Stand whose last phase is 30 seconds of doing nothing (fake “press to skip”; any press forfeits the bonus). First clear of an event banks 1 + stars; repeats bank 1. Age 40 or better may check out by rowboat; otherwise the Extended Stay ending. Both roll credits and unlock free play. A headless bot, from a fresh New Stay, reaches credits on 3 seeds: won, 5 stamps, every event played, under 60 sim-minutes, without reading the wall clock.\\n3. **Every event is a finished mini-game.** Shipped and directly startable: Morning Wobble Check, Breath Bloom, Pose Parade, Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff, Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap, Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup, and the five-phase Big Stand, with the twists named in PLAN.md §5 (breath guide, drifting pose ring and gull, squat tempo, plank flop, 96 BPM two-lane chart, hula-style spin and ring catches, lap with step-rate zone, shell-tilt boards, paddle gates, tray of smoothies, cannonball judges, Long Stillness). Each event has a card, countdown, result (score, stars, deadpan title, minutes, personal best, Retry or Back), a bot that earns at least 2 stars on 5 seeds, and an idle-input result under 1 star. Score events use 0–1000 with stars at 400, 650, and 850; Plank uses the time gates in PLAN.md (25 / 40 / 55 s). Time-cut permission in PLAN.md §17 does not apply: this computer can run the full roster.\\n10→4. **10-foot play shell, audio, and dev tools.** Same screens for pad, keyboard, and mouse. Prompts follow the last input: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs via Settings, keycaps, or mouse buttons. Bindings match PLAN.md §3, including pause and schedule. After 10 seconds (600 sim ticks) with no input on the title or pre-game menus, attract mode loops the PLAN.md §12 sequence with a DEMO ribbon; any input returns to the title; nothing is saved; it stays silent until a real input. Pause freezes the world and opens Dev Mode (not in a hub session) with jump, cheats, time scale, live sliders for the tunables named in PLAN.md §11, and reset to defaults. Settings include music default 0.10 linear, SFX, voices, glyphs, lean sensitivity, wobble assist, rhythm offset, text speed, fullscreen, and reset-save confirm. Touch-only devices get a “Controller or keyboard required” card plus Settings, no touch controls, and attract keeps running. All music, at least 30 sound effects, and Animalese/Simlish voices are synthesized in code (no audio files); speakers are audibly distinct; dialogue types out with syllable blips. UI is large enough for 10 feet (body ≥34 px and titles ≥64 px at 1080p, scaled down with the frame), at most two lines of dialogue, no dense stat tables. Look is high-key pastel on the engine’s cel style, with new beach and wellness props and new exercise poses; library props only for generic dressing.\\n5. **Saves, local multiplayer, and AI Hub.** Versioned `localStorage` saves cover up to four guest slots (name from a preset list, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings, written on day change and on each result. Real dates passed in at boot drive absence comments; the sim does not read the clock. Play Together is hot-seat for 2–4 guests through the same three-event medley, with a pass-the-pad card and a podium. Yesterday You replays a best run beside you from day 3 and does not affect scoring. An AI Hub session in mode `ghost`, 1–4 players, skips title, menu, attract, quit, restart, and dev mode, and opens into the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup, same seed, same course). Other seats are tinted ghosts in a matching area only. Final score is the sum (0–3000) reported to the hub. Solo play leaves `AIHub.active` false. The About/Credits screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback, plus font and motion-library credits. No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features remain.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** Add in-repo tests that construct the shipped game from a fresh start (no browser, no GPU) and drive its real update loop. Assert criterion 2’s bot run (3 seeds), criterion 3’s per-event bot and idle results (5 seeds), balance-model settle and tip timing, age direction and 18–99 bounds, attract start at 600 idle ticks plus exit without saving, pause freezing world time, music default 0.10, a dev slider changing a live value and resetting, save round-trip, medley determinism for the same seed and inputs, and Play Together reaching a podium. Lint shipped text for `TODO`, placeholder copy, weight/BMI/diet talk, and Nintendo names outside the About source line. Put them behind one command that prints only failures and a final `N passed, 0 failed` line. Run that command twice; both runs must print the same pass line. Save the log to `{SCRATCH}/tests-core.log`.\\n2. **gating:** Launch the shipped HTML on its real entry path more than once. Prefer `file://`. If a server is required, bind `127.0.0.1` with `python3 -u -m http.server 0` and stop only that PID. Use Playwright Chromium (already installed) with the WebGPU flags in TASK.md. At 320×180, twice: zero page errors, `__gameStatus` appears and its tick advances across samples, a standard-mapping gamepad stub moves menu focus and confirms, keyboard does the same, mouse hover moves focus and click activates using rects the page publishes, prompts change with the device, Settings exposes Xbox glyphs, and after about 10 real seconds attract starts and an input exits it. Phone and tablet Chromium profiles show “Controller or keyboard required”, keep attract running, and a Settings tap opens Settings. WebKit with an iPhone profile (no WebGPU here) shows the fallback that both a controller or keyboard and WebGPU are required. The drawing surface’s dimensions equal the requested viewport. A blank WebGPU canvas while ticks advance is the known software-readback limit, not a pass: also capture a 1920×1080 frame with the engine’s headless capture of the title (menu and title text readable) and of one event (figure plus balance puck substantially filling the frame). A blank engine capture is a failure. Two browser boots and two engine captures must agree. Logs and images go to `{SCRATCH}/`. If Playwright or the engine capture cannot start, save that launcher error to `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.log`; criteria 2–4 then rest on step 1 plus the static checks in step 4. A capture that runs and returns a blank frame is not this fallback.\\n3. **gating:** Hub check on the shipped page. Serve the page with the hub harness files and open the harness for 2 players; for 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and for `scenario=host-leave`. Each run must finish with the harness complete flag and its own pass flag set. Then open the page outside a session, press Enter and Space, and require no errors, `AIHub.active` false, and `Math.random` left unseeded. The session client embedded in the page must byte-match the downloaded `session.js`. Save logs to `{SCRATCH}/tests-hub.log`. If the hub files cannot be fetched, keep this step gating and record the blocker in `{SCRATCH}/hub-unverifiable.log` instead of inventing a pass.\\n4. **gating:** Static hand-in check. `exit-interview.json` parses as one object with the TASK.md keys; `usage` is `added on import`; `aiHub.name` equals the title screen. The HTML filename and dev-folder name match criterion 1. The page’s about-data block includes Source Information and the three feedback lists. `PROGRESS.md` exists. Dev-folder notes contain the 50 titles and the RNG output. Confirm no audio files are referenced by the game.\\n5. **evidence:** One 1920×1080 engine capture per set, plus a short filmstrip of at least one hand-keyed pose. Sound: either the unit render at music 0.10 is about a tenth of full scale, or a browser patch of the audio buffer shows non-silent music after a gesture. Absence of these images does not fail the goal when steps 1–4 pass.\\n\\n20→## Non-goals\\n- Not a Wii Fit recreation: no BMI or weight goals, no Miis or face editors, no Wuhu Island, no source music, layouts, or quoted lines, and not the full 40-activity list (soccer heading, ski jump, hula hoop as named in the source, and the rest).\\n- No real Balance Board, DualSense, iPhone, TV, listener, or second human. Use the stand-ins in TASK.md.\\n- No touch-play controls, no shared-world netcode, no FPS optimization, and no review subagents.\\n- No audio files and no spoken real words.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- Work root: `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`, and `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html`.\\n- Dev folder of that basename: clone of `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall` (PLAN.md was checked against commit `49ef2ba`), game content and tests, notes, and a small README for adding an event, a set, or a song.\\n- AI Hub client files from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` (`session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`).\\n30→- Fredoka and Nunito (SIL OFL) embedded for UI text; engine puppet, egui, and synthesized audio extended as PLAN.md §§8–14 describe. Behavior is the contract; file names in PLAN.md are guidance.\\n- Playwright 1.63 (system Python, not `python3 -I`), Cargo, and `wasm-bindgen` 0.2.129. Chromium only for WebGPU play; Firefox and WebKit are fallback-message checks.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md for design numbers, writing, and the hub snippet; do not invent a second balance model or a second synth. Keep the whole flow (menus, dialogue, pause, settings, dev toggles, events) in the simulation so tests drive it with no GPU. Keep UI a pure view of that state. Keep tunable numbers and all dialogue in data files the tests load. Build a single HTML only after the sim tests pass. Disable the engine’s demo keys and on-screen chrome while this game is active so captures show the game, not the engine shell. Record any spec gap in one line in the dev notes and continue.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Pick the title with a real RNG from 50 riffs, record the draw, create the dev folder, clone the engine, and keep `PROGRESS.md` current.\\n- [ ] Register the game, hide engine chrome, add lean input and the title/pause shell, save, and the hub page tags so a boot smoke test passes.\\n- [ ] Implement the shared balance model, the morning check, the island day loop, and one full event; lock them with sim tests.\\n40→- [ ] Implement the remaining events, day unlocks, Big Stand, both endings, free play, and the bot playthrough.\\n- [ ] Add synthesized music, effects, and gibberish voices (music default 0.10), attract mode, settings, dev sliders with reset, and the touch-only card.\\n- [ ] Add wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, Play Together, and the hub ghost medley; run the hub harness.\\n- [ ] Write the full script and About text, fill `exit-interview.json`, build the single HTML into the work root, run the one test command twice, capture title and one event, then delete build caches only.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §17 allows cutting Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, and Plank Standoff if time runs short. The objective requires everything this computer can run, so a cut roster fails criterion 3.\\n- TASK.md warns that a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank even when the frame is live. A blank browser bitmap is not success and not an automatic environment waiver: the engine’s own capture must show a filled frame (step 2). Only a launcher that will not start is the fallback.\\n- Browser timing at 1920×1080 is too slow here (software WebGPU). The 10-second attract check is valid only around 320×180; a slow 1080p browser clock is not a game bug. Judge the 10-foot layout from the 1080p engine capture.\\n- Firefox and WebKit have no WebGPU here, so they cannot play the game. There is no physical pad, touch screen, listener, second human, or TV.\\n50→- A fresh clone may not be commit `49ef2ba`. If a “verified” engine note is wrong on the cloned revision, adapt and record the commit and the change; do not pretend the old note still held.\\n- Other agents share this machine. Use one browser, bind an OS-picked localhost port, and stop only PIDs this run started. `earlyoom` killing the browser is memory pressure, not a game bug.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Plan: Ship a playable Tippy Cay balance-and-wellness demo inspired by Wii Fit, plus the hand-in files TASK.md names\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in package.** The work-folder root contains `PROGRESS.md`, a parseable `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape TASK.md specifies (every value filled, `\\\"usage\\\"` exactly `added on import`, `aiHub.genre` one of the allowed catalogue genres, `aiHub.players` `1–4`), and one self-contained HTML file named `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html`. A sibling folder with that same basename (no `.html`) holds the dev tree. `{Title}` is a playful riff on “Wii Fit”, chosen by listing 50 titles and selecting one with a real RNG; the same string is the title-screen name, the page `<title>`, and `aiHub.name`. The 50 titles and the RNG draw are recorded in the dev folder. Opening the HTML from disk boots this game (a WebGPU-missing message only when WebGPU is absent).\\n2. **Wii Fit loop, original world.** It is a third-person sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame: a five-day stay at Tippy Cay staffed by talking gym gear. The only play verb is a centre-of-pressure lean (left stick, keyboard ramp, or mouse offset from screen centre — last device wins) driving one shared balance model: shaped lean, stiffness/damping, sim-time wobble, tip only after the dot stays outside the unit disc for the tip time. Tips cost time or score and never end the stay. Each morning a wobble check (still, lean targets, eyes-closed tone, step timing) yields a Balance Age from PLAN.md’s skill formula, clamped 18–99; better input gives a lower age. There is no weight, BMI, body-shape, or diet content, and no Nintendo product names inside play (About source line and the title riff only). Days open in order — stillness, strength, cardio, lagoon — with minute goals 3, 5, 7, 9, then a Day-5 Big Stand whose last phase is 30 seconds of doing nothing (fake “press to skip”; any press forfeits the bonus). First clear of an event banks 1 + stars; repeats bank 1. Age 40 or better may check out by rowboat; otherwise the Extended Stay ending. Both roll credits and unlock free play. A headless bot, from a fresh New Stay, reaches credits on 3 seeds: won, 5 stamps, every event played, under 60 sim-minutes, without reading the wall clock.\\n3. **Every event is a finished mini-game.** Shipped and directly startable: Morning Wobble Check, Breath Bloom, Pose Parade, Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff, Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap, Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup, and the five-phase Big Stand, with the twists named in PLAN.md §5 (breath guide, drifting pose ring and gull, squat tempo, plank flop, 96 BPM two-lane chart, hula-style spin and ring catches, lap with step-rate zone, shell-tilt boards, paddle gates, tray of smoothies, cannonball judges, Long Stillness). Each event has a card, countdown, result (score, stars, deadpan title, minutes, personal best, Retry or Back), a bot that earns at least 2 stars on 5 seeds, and an idle-input result under 1 star. Score events use 0–1000 with stars at 400, 650, and 850; Plank uses the time gates in PLAN.md (25 / 40 / 55 s). Time-cut permission in PLAN.md §17 does not apply: this computer can run the full roster.\\n10→4. **10-foot play shell, audio, and dev tools.** Same screens for pad, keyboard, and mouse. Prompts follow the last input: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs via Settings, keycaps, or mouse buttons. Bindings match PLAN.md §3, including pause and schedule. After 10 seconds (600 sim ticks) with no input on the title or pre-game menus, attract mode loops the PLAN.md §12 sequence with a DEMO ribbon; any input returns to the title; nothing is saved; it stays silent until a real input. Pause freezes the world and opens Dev Mode (not in a hub session) with jump, cheats, time scale, live sliders for the tunables named in PLAN.md §11, and reset to defaults. Settings include music default 0.10 linear, SFX, voices, glyphs, lean sensitivity, wobble assist, rhythm offset, text speed, fullscreen, and reset-save confirm. Touch-only devices get a “Controller or keyboard required” card plus Settings, no touch controls, and attract keeps running. All music, at least 30 sound effects, and Animalese/Simlish voices are synthesized in code (no audio files); speakers are audibly distinct; dialogue types out with syllable blips. UI is large enough for 10 feet (body ≥34 px and titles ≥64 px at 1080p, scaled down with the frame), at most two lines of dialogue, no dense stat tables. Look is high-key pastel on the engine’s cel style, with new beach and wellness props and new exercise poses; library props only for generic dressing.\\n5. **Saves, local multiplayer, and AI Hub.** Versioned `localStorage` saves cover up to four guest slots (name from a preset list, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings, written on day change and on each result. Real dates passed in at boot drive absence comments; the sim does not read the clock. Play Together is hot-seat for 2–4 guests through the same three-event medley, with a pass-the-pad card and a podium. Yesterday You replays a best run beside you from day 3 and does not affect scoring. An AI Hub session in mode `ghost`, 1–4 players, skips title, menu, attract, quit, restart, and dev mode, and opens into the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup, same seed, same course). Other seats are tinted ghosts in a matching area only. Final score is the sum (0–3000) reported to the hub. Solo play leaves `AIHub.active` false. The About/Credits screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback, plus font and motion-library credits. No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features remain.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** Add in-repo tests that construct the shipped game from a fresh start (no browser, no GPU) and drive its real update loop. Assert criterion 2’s bot run (3 seeds), criterion 3’s per-event bot and idle results (5 seeds), balance-model settle and tip timing, age direction and 18–99 bounds, attract start at 600 idle ticks plus exit without saving, pause freezing world time, music default 0.10, a dev slider changing a live value and resetting, save round-trip, medley determinism for the same seed and inputs, and Play Together reaching a podium. Lint shipped text for `TODO`, placeholder copy, weight/BMI/diet talk, and Nintendo names outside the About source line. Put them behind one command that prints only failures and a final `N passed, 0 failed` line. Run that command twice; both runs must print the same pass line. Save the log to `{SCRATCH}/tests-core.log`.\\n2. **gating:** Launch the shipped HTML on its real entry path more than once. Prefer `file://`. If a server is required, bind `127.0.0.1` with `python3 -u -m http.server 0` and stop only that PID. Use Playwright Chromium (already installed) with the WebGPU flags in TASK.md. At 320×180, twice: zero page errors, `__gameStatus` appears and its tick advances across samples, a standard-mapping gamepad stub moves menu focus and confirms, keyboard does the same, mouse hover moves focus and click activates using rects the page publishes, prompts change with the device, Settings exposes Xbox glyphs, and after about 10 real seconds attract starts and an input exits it. Phone and tablet Chromium profiles show “Controller or keyboard required”, keep attract running, and a Settings tap opens Settings. WebKit with an iPhone profile (no WebGPU here) shows the fallback that both a controller or keyboard and WebGPU are required. The drawing surface’s dimensions equal the requested viewport. A blank WebGPU canvas while ticks advance is the known software-readback limit, not a pass: also capture a 1920×1080 frame with the engine’s headless capture of the title (menu and title text readable) and of one event (figure plus balance puck substantially filling the frame). A blank engine capture is a failure. Two browser boots and two engine captures must agree. Logs and images go to `{SCRATCH}/`. If Playwright or the engine capture cannot start, save that launcher error to `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.log`; criteria 2–4 then rest on step 1 plus the static checks in step 4. A capture that runs and returns a blank frame is not this fallback.\\n3. **gating:** Hub check on the shipped page. Serve the page with the hub harness files and open the harness for 2 players; for 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and for `scenario=host-leave`. Each run must finish with the harness complete flag and its own pass flag set. Then open the page outside a session, press Enter and Space, and require no errors, `AIHub.active` false, and `Math.random` left unseeded. The session client embedded in the page must byte-match the downloaded `session.js`. Save logs to `{SCRATCH}/tests-hub.log`. If the hub files cannot be fetched, keep this step gating and record the blocker in `{SCRATCH}/hub-unverifiable.log` instead of inventing a pass.\\n4. **gating:** Static hand-in check. `exit-interview.json` parses as one object with the TASK.md keys; `usage` is `added on import`; `aiHub.name` equals the title screen. The HTML filename and dev-folder name match criterion 1. The page’s about-data block includes Source Information and the three feedback lists. `PROGRESS.md` exists. Dev-folder notes contain the 50 titles and the RNG output. Confirm no audio files are referenced by the game.\\n5. **evidence:** One 1920×1080 engine capture per set, plus a short filmstrip of at least one hand-keyed pose. Sound: either the unit render at music 0.10 is about a tenth of full scale, or a browser patch of the audio buffer shows non-silent music after a gesture. Absence of these images does not fail the goal when steps 1–4 pass.\\n\\n20→## Non-goals\\n- Not a Wii Fit recreation: no BMI or weight goals, no Miis or face editors, no Wuhu Island, no source music, layouts, or quoted lines, and not the full 40-activity list (soccer heading, ski jump, hula hoop as named in the source, and the rest).\\n- No real Balance Board, DualSense, iPhone, TV, listener, or second human. Use the stand-ins in TASK.md.\\n- No touch-play controls, no shared-world netcode, no FPS optimization, and no review subagents.\\n- No audio files and no spoken real words.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- Work root: `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`, and `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html`.\\n- Dev folder of that basename: clone of `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall` (PLAN.md was checked against commit `49ef2ba`), game content and tests, notes, and a small README for adding an event, a set, or a song.\\n- AI Hub client files from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` (`session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`).\\n30→- Fredoka and Nunito (SIL OFL) embedded for UI text; engine puppet, egui, and synthesized audio extended as PLAN.md §§8–14 describe. Behavior is the contract; file names in PLAN.md are guidance.\\n- Playwright 1.63 (system Python, not `python3 -I`), Cargo, and `wasm-bindgen` 0.2.129. Chromium only for WebGPU play; Firefox and WebKit are fallback-message checks.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md for design numbers, writing, and the hub snippet; do not invent a second balance model or a second synth. Keep the whole flow (menus, dialogue, pause, settings, dev toggles, events) in the simulation so tests drive it with no GPU. Keep UI a pure view of that state. Keep tunable numbers and all dialogue in data files the tests load. Build a single HTML only after the sim tests pass. Disable the engine’s demo keys and on-screen chrome while this game is active so captures show the game, not the engine shell. Record any spec gap in one line in the dev notes and continue.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Pick the title with a real RNG from 50 riffs, record the draw, create the dev folder, clone the engine, and keep `PROGRESS.md` current.\\n- [ ] Register the game, hide engine chrome, add lean input and the title/pause shell, save, and the hub page tags so a boot smoke test passes.\\n- [ ] Implement the shared balance model, the morning check, the island day loop, and one full event; lock them with sim tests.\\n40→- [ ] Implement the remaining events, day unlocks, Big Stand, both endings, free play, and the bot playthrough.\\n- [ ] Add synthesized music, effects, and gibberish voices (music default 0.10), attract mode, settings, dev sliders with reset, and the touch-only card.\\n- [ ] Add wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, Play Together, and the hub ghost medley; run the hub harness.\\n- [ ] Write the full script and About text, fill `exit-interview.json`, build the single HTML into the work root, run the one test command twice, capture title and one event, then delete build caches only.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §17 allows cutting Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, and Plank Standoff if time runs short. The objective requires everything this computer can run, so a cut roster fails criterion 3.\\n- TASK.md warns that a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank even when the frame is live. A blank browser bitmap is not success and not an automatic environment waiver: the engine’s own capture must show a filled frame (step 2). Only a launcher that will not start is the fallback.\\n- Browser timing at 1920×1080 is too slow here (software WebGPU). The 10-second attract check is valid only around 320×180; a slow 1080p browser clock is not a game bug. Judge the 10-foot layout from the 1080p engine capture.\\n- Firefox and WebKit have no WebGPU here, so they cannot play the game. There is no physical pad, touch screen, listener, second human, or TV.\\n50→- A fresh clone may not be commit `49ef2ba`. If a “verified” engine note is wrong on the cloned revision, adapt and record the commit and the change; do not pretend the old note still held.\\n- Other agents share this machine. Use one browser, bind an OS-picked localhost port, and stop only PIDs this run started. `earlyoom` killing the browser is memory pressure, not a game bug.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d%2Fwork/01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":250,\"raw_output\":\"# Plan: Ship a playable Tippy Cay balance-and-wellness demo inspired by Wii Fit, plus the hand-in files TASK.md names\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in package.** The work-folder root contains `PROGRESS.md`, a parseable `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape TASK.md specifies (every value filled, `\\\"usage\\\"` exactly `added on import`, `aiHub.genre` one of the allowed catalogue genres, `aiHub.players` `1–4`), and one self-contained HTML file named `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html`. A sibling folder with that same basename (no `.html`) holds the dev tree. `{Title}` is a playful riff on “Wii Fit”, chosen by listing 50 titles and selecting one with a real RNG; the same string is the title-screen name, the page `<title>`, and `aiHub.name`. The 50 titles and the RNG draw are recorded in the dev folder. Opening the HTML from disk boots this game (a WebGPU-missing message only when WebGPU is absent).\\n2. **Wii Fit loop, original world.** It is a third-person sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame: a five-day stay at Tippy Cay staffed by talking gym gear. The only play verb is a centre-of-pressure lean (left stick, keyboard ramp, or mouse offset from screen centre — last device wins) driving one shared balance model: shaped lean, stiffness/damping, sim-time wobble, tip only after the dot stays outside the unit disc for the tip time. Tips cost time or score and never end the stay. Each morning a wobble check (still, lean targets, eyes-closed tone, step timing) yields a Balance Age from PLAN.md’s skill formula, clamped 18–99; better input gives a lower age. There is no weight, BMI, body-shape, or diet content, and no Nintendo product names inside play (About source line and the title riff only). Days open in order — stillness, strength, cardio, lagoon — with minute goals 3, 5, 7, 9, then a Day-5 Big Stand whose last phase is 30 seconds of doing nothing (fake “press to skip”; any press forfeits the bonus). First clear of an event banks 1 + stars; repeats bank 1. Age 40 or better may check out by rowboat; otherwise the Extended Stay ending. Both roll credits and unlock free play. A headless bot, from a fresh New Stay, reaches credits on 3 seeds: won, 5 stamps, every event played, under 60 sim-minutes, without reading the wall clock.\\n3. **Every event is a finished mini-game.** Shipped and directly startable: Morning Wobble Check, Breath Bloom, Pose Parade, Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff, Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap, Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup, and the five-phase Big Stand, with the twists named in PLAN.md §5 (breath guide, drifting pose ring and gull, squat tempo, plank flop, 96 BPM two-lane chart, hula-style spin and ring catches, lap with step-rate zone, shell-tilt boards, paddle gates, tray of smoothies, cannonball judges, Long Stillness). Each event has a card, countdown, result (score, stars, deadpan title, minutes, personal best, Retry or Back), a bot that earns at least 2 stars on 5 seeds, and an idle-input result under 1 star. Score events use 0–1000 with stars at 400, 650, and 850; Plank uses the time gates in PLAN.md (25 / 40 / 55 s). Time-cut permission in PLAN.md §17 does not apply: this computer can run the full roster.\\n4. **10-foot play shell, audio, and dev tools.** Same screens for pad, keyboard, and mouse. Prompts follow the last input: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs via Settings, keycaps, or mouse buttons. Bindings match PLAN.md §3, including pause and schedule. After 10 seconds (600 sim ticks) with no input on the title or pre-game menus, attract mode loops the PLAN.md §12 sequence with a DEMO ribbon; any input returns to the title; nothing is saved; it stays silent until a real input. Pause freezes the world and opens Dev Mode (not in a hub session) with jump, cheats, time scale, live sliders for the tunables named in PLAN.md §11, and reset to defaults. Settings include music default 0.10 linear, SFX, voices, glyphs, lean sensitivity, wobble assist, rhythm offset, text speed, fullscreen, and reset-save confirm. Touch-only devices get a “Controller or keyboard required” card plus Settings, no touch controls, and attract keeps running. All music, at least 30 sound effects, and Animalese/Simlish voices are synthesized in code (no audio files); speakers are audibly distinct; dialogue types out with syllable blips. UI is large enough for 10 feet (body ≥34 px and titles ≥64 px at 1080p, scaled down with the frame), at most two lines of dialogue, no dense stat tables. Look is high-key pastel on the engine’s cel style, with new beach and wellness props and new exercise poses; library props only for generic dressing.\\n5. **Saves, local multiplayer, and AI Hub.** Versioned `localStorage` saves cover up to four guest slots (name from a preset list, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings, written on day change and on each result. Real dates passed in at boot drive absence comments; the sim does not read the clock. Play Together is hot-seat for 2–4 guests through the same three-event medley, with a pass-the-pad card and a podium. Yesterday You replays a best run beside you from day 3 and does not affect scoring. An AI Hub session in mode `ghost`, 1–4 players, skips title, menu, attract, quit, restart, and dev mode, and opens into the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup, same seed, same course). Other seats are tinted ghosts in a matching area only. Final score is the sum (0–3000) reported to the hub. Solo play leaves `AIHub.active` false. The About/Credits screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback, plus font and motion-library credits. No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features remain.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** Add in-repo tests that construct the shipped game from a fresh start (no browser, no GPU) and drive its real update loop. Assert criterion 2’s bot run (3 seeds), criterion 3’s per-event bot and idle results (5 seeds), balance-model settle and tip timing, age direction and 18–99 bounds, attract start at 600 idle ticks plus exit without saving, pause freezing world time, music default 0.10, a dev slider changing a live value and resetting, save round-trip, medley determinism for the same seed and inputs, and Play Together reaching a podium. Lint shipped text for `TODO`, placeholder copy, weight/BMI/diet talk, and Nintendo names outside the About source line. Put them behind one command that prints only failures and a final `N passed, 0 failed` line. Run that command twice; both runs must print the same pass line. Save the log to `{SCRATCH}/tests-core.log`.\\n2. **gating:** Launch the shipped HTML on its real entry path more than once. Prefer `file://`. If a server is required, bind `127.0.0.1` with `python3 -u -m http.server 0` and stop only that PID. Use Playwright Chromium (already installed) with the WebGPU flags in TASK.md. At 320×180, twice: zero page errors, `__gameStatus` appears and its tick advances across samples, a standard-mapping gamepad stub moves menu focus and confirms, keyboard does the same, mouse hover moves focus and click activates using rects the page publishes, prompts change with the device, Settings exposes Xbox glyphs, and after about 10 real seconds attract starts and an input exits it. Phone and tablet Chromium profiles show “Controller or keyboard required”, keep attract running, and a Settings tap opens Settings. WebKit with an iPhone profile (no WebGPU here) shows the fallback that both a controller or keyboard and WebGPU are required. The drawing surface’s dimensions equal the requested viewport. A blank WebGPU canvas while ticks advance is the known software-readback limit, not a pass: also capture a 1920×1080 frame with the engine’s headless capture of the title (menu and title text readable) and of one event (figure plus balance puck substantially filling the frame). A blank engine capture is a failure. Two browser boots and two engine captures must agree. Logs and images go to `{SCRATCH}/`. If Playwright or the engine capture cannot start, save that launcher error to `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.log`; criteria 2–4 then rest on step 1 plus the static checks in step 4. A capture that runs and returns a blank frame is not this fallback.\\n3. **gating:** Hub check on the shipped page. Serve the page with the hub harness files and open the harness for 2 players; for 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and for `scenario=host-leave`. Each run must finish with the harness complete flag and its own pass flag set. Then open the page outside a session, press Enter and Space, and require no errors, `AIHub.active` false, and `Math.random` left unseeded. The session client embedded in the page must byte-match the downloaded `session.js`. Save logs to `{SCRATCH}/tests-hub.log`. If the hub files cannot be fetched, keep this step gating and record the blocker in `{SCRATCH}/hub-unverifiable.log` instead of inventing a pass.\\n4. **gating:** Static hand-in check. `exit-interview.json` parses as one object with the TASK.md keys; `usage` is `added on import`; `aiHub.name` equals the title screen. The HTML filename and dev-folder name match criterion 1. The page’s about-data block includes Source Information and the three feedback lists. `PROGRESS.md` exists. Dev-folder notes contain the 50 titles and the RNG output. Confirm no audio files are referenced by the game.\\n5. **evidence:** One 1920×1080 engine capture per set, plus a short filmstrip of at least one hand-keyed pose. Sound: either the unit render at music 0.10 is about a tenth of full scale, or a browser patch of the audio buffer shows non-silent music after a gesture. Absence of these images does not fail the goal when steps 1–4 pass.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- Not a Wii Fit recreation: no BMI or weight goals, no Miis or face editors, no Wuhu Island, no source music, layouts, or quoted lines, and not the full 40-activity list (soccer heading, ski jump, hula hoop as named in the source, and the rest).\\n- No real Balance Board, DualSense, iPhone, TV, listener, or second human. Use the stand-ins in TASK.md.\\n- No touch-play controls, no shared-world netcode, no FPS optimization, and no review subagents.\\n- No audio files and no spoken real words.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- Work root: `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`, and `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html`.\\n- Dev folder of that basename: clone of `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall` (PLAN.md was checked against commit `49ef2ba`), game content and tests, notes, and a small README for adding an event, a set, or a song.\\n- AI Hub client files from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` (`session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`).\\n- Fredoka and Nunito (SIL OFL) embedded for UI text; engine puppet, egui, and synthesized audio extended as PLAN.md §§8–14 describe. Behavior is the contract; file names in PLAN.md are guidance.\\n- Playwright 1.63 (system Python, not `python3 -I`), Cargo, and `wasm-bindgen` 0.2.129. Chromium only for WebGPU play; Firefox and WebKit are fallback-message checks.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md for design numbers, writing, and the hub snippet; do not invent a second balance model or a second synth. Keep the whole flow (menus, dialogue, pause, settings, dev toggles, events) in the simulation so tests drive it with no GPU. Keep UI a pure view of that state. Keep tunable numbers and all dialogue in data files the tests load. Build a single HTML only after the sim tests pass. Disable the engine’s demo keys and on-screen chrome while this game is active so captures show the game, not the engine shell. Record any spec gap in one line in the dev notes and continue.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Pick the title with a real RNG from 50 riffs, record the draw, create the dev folder, clone the engine, and keep `PROGRESS.md` current.\\n- [ ] Register the game, hide engine chrome, add lean input and the title/pause shell, save, and the hub page tags so a boot smoke test passes.\\n- [ ] Implement the shared balance model, the morning check, the island day loop, and one full event; lock them with sim tests.\\n- [ ] Implement the remaining events, day unlocks, Big Stand, both endings, free play, and the bot playthrough.\\n- [ ] Add synthesized music, effects, and gibberish voices (music default 0.10), attract mode, settings, dev sliders with reset, and the touch-only card.\\n- [ ] Add wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, Play Together, and the hub ghost medley; run the hub harness.\\n- [ ] Write the full script and About text, fill `exit-interview.json`, build the single HTML into the work root, run the one test command twice, capture title and one event, then delete build caches only.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §17 allows cutting Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, and Plank Standoff if time runs short. The objective requires everything this computer can run, so a cut roster fails criterion 3.\\n- TASK.md warns that a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank even when the frame is live. A blank browser bitmap is not success and not an automatic environment waiver: the engine’s own capture must show a filled frame (step 2). Only a launcher that will not start is the fallback.\\n- Browser timing at 1920×1080 is too slow here (software WebGPU). The 10-second attract check is valid only around 320×180; a slow 1080p browser clock is not a game bug. Judge the 10-foot layout from the 1080p engine capture.\\n- Firefox and WebKit have no WebGPU here, so they cannot play the game. There is no physical pad, touch screen, listener, second human, or TV.\\n- A fresh clone may not be commit `49ef2ba`. If a “verified” engine note is wrong on the cloned revision, adapt and record the commit and the change; do not pretend the old note still held.\\n- Other agents share this machine. Use one browser, bind an OS-picked localhost port, and stop only PIDs this run started. `earlyoom` killing the browser is memory pressure, not a game bug.\\n\",\"total_lines\":51}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6364b474-6eba-4592-841c-2ffca835f0fd-13","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Synthesized sound: every sound is built from oscillators, noise, envelopes, pitch sweeps\\n//! and a filter. The mixer runs in the audio callback (cpal) or offline (to .wav). The game\\n//! runs fine without a sound device.\\n\\nuse std::sync::mpsc::{Receiver, Sender, channel};\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\nuse pav_core::SimEvent;\\n\\n10→#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]\\npub enum Wave {\\n    Sine,\\n    Square,\\n    Saw,\\n    Triangle,\\n    Noise,\\n}\\n\\n/// One synthesized sound.\\n20→#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Patch {\\n    pub wave: Wave,\\n    /// Start / end frequency (Hz) and the glide time between them (s, exponential).\\n    pub freq: f32,\\n    pub freq_end: f32,\\n    pub glide: f32,\\n    pub attack: f32,\\n    pub decay: f32,\\n    pub sustain: f32,\\n30→    pub hold: f32,\\n    pub release: f32,\\n    pub volume: f32,\\n    /// One-pole low-pass cutoff (Hz) at start and end of the sound.\\n    pub cutoff: f32,\\n    pub cutoff_end: f32,\\n    /// Square-wave duty cycle.\\n    pub duty: f32,\\n}\\n\\n40→impl Patch {\\n    pub const fn new(wave: Wave, freq: f32) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            wave,\\n            freq,\\n            freq_end: freq,\\n            glide: 0.1,\\n            attack: 0.002,\\n            decay: 0.1,\\n            sustain: 0.0,\\n50→            hold: 0.0,\\n            release: 0.05,\\n            volume: 0.3,\\n            cutoff: 12000.0,\\n            cutoff_end: 12000.0,\\n            duty: 0.5,\\n        }\\n    }\\n    pub fn length(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.attack + self.decay + self.hold + self.release\\n60→    }\\n}\\n\\nstruct Voice {\\n    p: Patch,\\n    t: f32,\\n    delay: f32,\\n    phase: f32,\\n    lp: f32,\\n    noise: u32,\\n70→    gain_l: f32,\\n    gain_r: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Voice {\\n    fn env(&self) -> f32 {\\n        let p = &self.p;\\n        let t = self.t;\\n        if t < p.attack {\\n            return t / p.attack.max(1e-5);\\n80→        }\\n        let t = t - p.attack;\\n        if t < p.decay {\\n            return 1.0 + (p.sustain - 1.0) * (t / p.decay.max(1e-5));\\n        }\\n        let t = t - p.decay;\\n        if t < p.hold {\\n            return p.sustain;\\n        }\\n        let t = t - p.hold;\\n90→        let start = if p.decay > 0.0 || p.hold > 0.0 { p.sustain } else { 1.0 };\\n        (start * (1.0 - t / p.release.max(1e-5))).max(0.0)\\n    }\\n\\n    fn done(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.t > self.p.length() + 0.01\\n    }\\n\\n    fn next(&mut self, dt: f32) -> f32 {\\n        if self.delay > 0.0 {\\n100→            self.delay -= dt;\\n            return 0.0;\\n        }\\n        let p = self.p;\\n        let k = (self.t / p.glide.max(1e-4)).min(1.0);\\n        let freq = p.freq * (p.freq_end / p.freq.max(1.0)).powf(k);\\n        self.phase = (self.phase + freq * dt).fract();\\n        let ph = self.phase;\\n        let raw = match p.wave {\\n            Wave::Sine => (ph * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin(),\\n110→            Wave::Square => {\\n                if ph < p.duty {\\n                    1.0\\n                } else {\\n                    -1.0\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Wave::Saw => ph * 2.0 - 1.0,\\n            Wave::Triangle => 1.0 - 4.0 * (ph - 0.5).abs(),\\n            Wave::Noise => {\\n120→                self.noise ^= self.noise << 13;\\n                self.noise ^= self.noise >> 17;\\n                self.noise ^= self.noise << 5;\\n                (self.noise as f32 / u32::MAX as f32) * 2.0 - 1.0\\n            }\\n        };\\n        let cutoff = p.cutoff * (p.cutoff_end / p.cutoff.max(1.0)).powf((self.t / p.length().max(1e-3)).min(1.0));\\n        let a = 1.0 - (-std::f32::consts::TAU * cutoff * dt).exp();\\n        self.lp += (raw - self.lp) * a;\\n        let s = self.lp * self.env() * p.volume;\\n130→        self.t += dt;\\n        s\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Mixes voices into interleaved stereo.\\npub struct Mixer {\\n    voices: Vec<Voice>,\\n    pub sample_rate: f32,\\n    pub master: f32,\\n140→    seed: u32,\\n}\\n\\nconst MAX_VOICES: usize = 64;\\n\\nimpl Mixer {\\n    pub fn new(sample_rate: f32) -> Self {\\n        Self { voices: Vec::new(), sample_rate, master: 0.8, seed: 0x9e37_79b9 }\\n    }\\n\\n150→    /// pan -1 (left) .. 1 (right); delay in seconds.\\n    pub fn play(&mut self, p: Patch, pan: f32, gain: f32, delay: f32) {\\n        if self.voices.len() >= MAX_VOICES {\\n            // Drop the oldest.\\n            self.voices.remove(0);\\n        }\\n        self.seed = self.seed.wrapping_mul(1_664_525).wrapping_add(1_013_904_223);\\n        let pan = pan.clamp(-1.0, 1.0);\\n        let a = (pan + 1.0) * std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_4;\\n        self.voices.push(Voice {\\n160→            p,\\n            t: 0.0,\\n            delay,\\n            phase: 0.0,\\n            lp: 0.0,\\n            noise: self.seed | 1,\\n            gain_l: a.cos() * gain,\\n            gain_r: a.sin() * gain,\\n        });\\n    }\\n170→\\n    /// Renders into an interleaved stereo buffer (overwrites).\\n    pub fn render(&mut self, out: &mut [f32]) {\\n        let dt = 1.0 / self.sample_rate;\\n        for frame in out.chunks_mut(2) {\\n            let (mut l, mut r) = (0.0, 0.0);\\n            for v in &mut self.voices {\\n                let s = v.next(dt);\\n                l += s * v.gain_l;\\n                r += s * v.gain_r;\\n180→            }\\n            // Soft clip.\\n            let m = self.master;\\n            frame[0] = (l * m).tanh();\\n            if frame.len() > 1 {\\n                frame[1] = (r * m).tanh();\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.voices.retain(|v| !v.done());\\n    }\\n190→\\n    pub fn active(&self) -> usize {\\n        self.voices.len()\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Where the ears are: position and the camera's right vector (for panning).\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Listener {\\n    pub pos: Vec3,\\n200→    pub right: Vec3,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for Listener {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self { pos: Vec3::ZERO, right: Vec3::X }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// The sound bank: which patches play for a simulation event.\\n210→pub fn sounds_for(ev: &SimEvent) -> Vec<(Patch, f32)> {\\n    use Wave::*;\\n    match ev {\\n        SimEvent::Jump { .. } => vec![(\\n            Patch {\\n                freq_end: 640.0,\\n                glide: 0.11,\\n                decay: 0.12,\\n                volume: 0.18,\\n                cutoff: 3500.0,\\n220→                cutoff_end: 2500.0,\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Synthesized sound: every sound is built from oscillators, noise, envelopes, pitch sweeps\\n//! and a filter. The mixer runs in the audio callback (cpal) or offline (to .wav). The game\\n//! runs fine without a sound device.\\n\\nuse std::sync::mpsc::{Receiver, Sender, channel};\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\nuse pav_core::SimEvent;\\n\\n10→#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]\\npub enum Wave {\\n    Sine,\\n    Square,\\n    Saw,\\n    Triangle,\\n    Noise,\\n}\\n\\n/// One synthesized sound.\\n20→#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Patch {\\n    pub wave: Wave,\\n    /// Start / end frequency (Hz) and the glide time between them (s, exponential).\\n    pub freq: f32,\\n    pub freq_end: f32,\\n    pub glide: f32,\\n    pub attack: f32,\\n    pub decay: f32,\\n    pub sustain: f32,\\n30→    pub hold: f32,\\n    pub release: f32,\\n    pub volume: f32,\\n    /// One-pole low-pass cutoff (Hz) at start and end of the sound.\\n    pub cutoff: f32,\\n    pub cutoff_end: f32,\\n    /// Square-wave duty cycle.\\n    pub duty: f32,\\n}\\n\\n40→impl Patch {\\n    pub const fn new(wave: Wave, freq: f32) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            wave,\\n            freq,\\n            freq_end: freq,\\n            glide: 0.1,\\n            attack: 0.002,\\n            decay: 0.1,\\n            sustain: 0.0,\\n50→            hold: 0.0,\\n            release: 0.05,\\n            volume: 0.3,\\n            cutoff: 12000.0,\\n            cutoff_end: 12000.0,\\n            duty: 0.5,\\n        }\\n    }\\n    pub fn length(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.attack + self.decay + self.hold + self.release\\n60→    }\\n}\\n\\nstruct Voice {\\n    p: Patch,\\n    t: f32,\\n    delay: f32,\\n    phase: f32,\\n    lp: f32,\\n    noise: u32,\\n70→    gain_l: f32,\\n    gain_r: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Voice {\\n    fn env(&self) -> f32 {\\n        let p = &self.p;\\n        let t = self.t;\\n        if t < p.attack {\\n            return t / p.attack.max(1e-5);\\n80→        }\\n        let t = t - p.attack;\\n        if t < p.decay {\\n            return 1.0 + (p.sustain - 1.0) * (t / p.decay.max(1e-5));\\n        }\\n        let t = t - p.decay;\\n        if t < p.hold {\\n            return p.sustain;\\n        }\\n        let t = t - p.hold;\\n90→        let start = if p.decay > 0.0 || p.hold > 0.0 { p.sustain } else { 1.0 };\\n        (start * (1.0 - t / p.release.max(1e-5))).max(0.0)\\n    }\\n\\n    fn done(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.t > self.p.length() + 0.01\\n    }\\n\\n    fn next(&mut self, dt: f32) -> f32 {\\n        if self.delay > 0.0 {\\n100→            self.delay -= dt;\\n            return 0.0;\\n        }\\n        let p = self.p;\\n        let k = (self.t / p.glide.max(1e-4)).min(1.0);\\n        let freq = p.freq * (p.freq_end / p.freq.max(1.0)).powf(k);\\n        self.phase = (self.phase + freq * dt).fract();\\n        let ph = self.phase;\\n        let raw = match p.wave {\\n            Wave::Sine => (ph * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin(),\\n110→            Wave::Square => {\\n                if ph < p.duty {\\n                    1.0\\n                } else {\\n                    -1.0\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Wave::Saw => ph * 2.0 - 1.0,\\n            Wave::Triangle => 1.0 - 4.0 * (ph - 0.5).abs(),\\n            Wave::Noise => {\\n120→                self.noise ^= self.noise << 13;\\n                self.noise ^= self.noise >> 17;\\n                self.noise ^= self.noise << 5;\\n                (self.noise as f32 / u32::MAX as f32) * 2.0 - 1.0\\n            }\\n        };\\n        let cutoff = p.cutoff * (p.cutoff_end / p.cutoff.max(1.0)).powf((self.t / p.length().max(1e-3)).min(1.0));\\n        let a = 1.0 - (-std::f32::consts::TAU * cutoff * dt).exp();\\n        self.lp += (raw - self.lp) * a;\\n        let s = self.lp * self.env() * p.volume;\\n130→        self.t += dt;\\n        s\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Mixes voices into interleaved stereo.\\npub struct Mixer {\\n    voices: Vec<Voice>,\\n    pub sample_rate: f32,\\n    pub master: f32,\\n140→    seed: u32,\\n}\\n\\nconst MAX_VOICES: usize = 64;\\n\\nimpl Mixer {\\n    pub fn new(sample_rate: f32) -> Self {\\n        Self { voices: Vec::new(), sample_rate, master: 0.8, seed: 0x9e37_79b9 }\\n    }\\n\\n150→    /// pan -1 (left) .. 1 (right); delay in seconds.\\n    pub fn play(&mut self, p: Patch, pan: f32, gain: f32, delay: f32) {\\n        if self.voices.len() >= MAX_VOICES {\\n            // Drop the oldest.\\n            self.voices.remove(0);\\n        }\\n        self.seed = self.seed.wrapping_mul(1_664_525).wrapping_add(1_013_904_223);\\n        let pan = pan.clamp(-1.0, 1.0);\\n        let a = (pan + 1.0) * std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_4;\\n        self.voices.push(Voice {\\n160→            p,\\n            t: 0.0,\\n            delay,\\n            phase: 0.0,\\n            lp: 0.0,\\n            noise: self.seed | 1,\\n            gain_l: a.cos() * gain,\\n            gain_r: a.sin() * gain,\\n        });\\n    }\\n170→\\n    /// Renders into an interleaved stereo buffer (overwrites).\\n    pub fn render(&mut self, out: &mut [f32]) {\\n        let dt = 1.0 / self.sample_rate;\\n        for frame in out.chunks_mut(2) {\\n            let (mut l, mut r) = (0.0, 0.0);\\n            for v in &mut self.voices {\\n                let s = v.next(dt);\\n                l += s * v.gain_l;\\n                r += s * v.gain_r;\\n180→            }\\n            // Soft clip.\\n            let m = self.master;\\n            frame[0] = (l * m).tanh();\\n            if frame.len() > 1 {\\n                frame[1] = (r * m).tanh();\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.voices.retain(|v| !v.done());\\n    }\\n190→\\n    pub fn active(&self) -> usize {\\n        self.voices.len()\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Where the ears are: position and the camera's right vector (for panning).\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Listener {\\n    pub pos: Vec3,\\n200→    pub right: Vec3,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for Listener {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self { pos: Vec3::ZERO, right: Vec3::X }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// The sound bank: which patches play for a simulation event.\\n210→pub fn sounds_for(ev: &SimEvent) -> Vec<(Patch, f32)> {\\n    use Wave::*;\\n    match ev {\\n        SimEvent::Jump { .. } => vec![(\\n            Patch {\\n                freq_end: 640.0,\\n                glide: 0.11,\\n                decay: 0.12,\\n                volume: 0.18,\\n                cutoff: 3500.0,\\n220→                cutoff_end: 2500.0,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":220,\"raw_output\":\"//! Synthesized sound: every sound is built from oscillators, noise, envelopes, pitch sweeps\\n//! and a filter. The mixer runs in the audio callback (cpal) or offline (to .wav). The game\\n//! runs fine without a sound device.\\n\\nuse std::sync::mpsc::{Receiver, Sender, channel};\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\nuse pav_core::SimEvent;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]\\npub enum Wave {\\n    Sine,\\n    Square,\\n    Saw,\\n    Triangle,\\n    Noise,\\n}\\n\\n/// One synthesized sound.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Patch {\\n    pub wave: Wave,\\n    /// Start / end frequency (Hz) and the glide time between them (s, exponential).\\n    pub freq: f32,\\n    pub freq_end: f32,\\n    pub glide: f32,\\n    pub attack: f32,\\n    pub decay: f32,\\n    pub sustain: f32,\\n    pub hold: f32,\\n    pub release: f32,\\n    pub volume: f32,\\n    /// One-pole low-pass cutoff (Hz) at start and end of the sound.\\n    pub cutoff: f32,\\n    pub cutoff_end: f32,\\n    /// Square-wave duty cycle.\\n    pub duty: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Patch {\\n    pub const fn new(wave: Wave, freq: f32) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            wave,\\n            freq,\\n            freq_end: freq,\\n            glide: 0.1,\\n            attack: 0.002,\\n            decay: 0.1,\\n            sustain: 0.0,\\n            hold: 0.0,\\n            release: 0.05,\\n            volume: 0.3,\\n            cutoff: 12000.0,\\n            cutoff_end: 12000.0,\\n            duty: 0.5,\\n        }\\n    }\\n    pub fn length(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.attack + self.decay + self.hold + self.release\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nstruct Voice {\\n    p: Patch,\\n    t: f32,\\n    delay: f32,\\n    phase: f32,\\n    lp: f32,\\n    noise: u32,\\n    gain_l: f32,\\n    gain_r: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Voice {\\n    fn env(&self) -> f32 {\\n        let p = &self.p;\\n        let t = self.t;\\n        if t < p.attack {\\n            return t / p.attack.max(1e-5);\\n        }\\n        let t = t - p.attack;\\n        if t < p.decay {\\n            return 1.0 + (p.sustain - 1.0) * (t / p.decay.max(1e-5));\\n        }\\n        let t = t - p.decay;\\n        if t < p.hold {\\n            return p.sustain;\\n        }\\n        let t = t - p.hold;\\n        let start = if p.decay > 0.0 || p.hold > 0.0 { p.sustain } else { 1.0 };\\n        (start * (1.0 - t / p.release.max(1e-5))).max(0.0)\\n    }\\n\\n    fn done(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.t > self.p.length() + 0.01\\n    }\\n\\n    fn next(&mut self, dt: f32) -> f32 {\\n        if self.delay > 0.0 {\\n            self.delay -= dt;\\n            return 0.0;\\n        }\\n        let p = self.p;\\n        let k = (self.t / p.glide.max(1e-4)).min(1.0);\\n        let freq = p.freq * (p.freq_end / p.freq.max(1.0)).powf(k);\\n        self.phase = (self.phase + freq * dt).fract();\\n        let ph = self.phase;\\n        let raw = match p.wave {\\n            Wave::Sine => (ph * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin(),\\n            Wave::Square => {\\n                if ph < p.duty {\\n                    1.0\\n                } else {\\n                    -1.0\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Wave::Saw => ph * 2.0 - 1.0,\\n            Wave::Triangle => 1.0 - 4.0 * (ph - 0.5).abs(),\\n            Wave::Noise => {\\n                self.noise ^= self.noise << 13;\\n                self.noise ^= self.noise >> 17;\\n                self.noise ^= self.noise << 5;\\n                (self.noise as f32 / u32::MAX as f32) * 2.0 - 1.0\\n            }\\n        };\\n        let cutoff = p.cutoff * (p.cutoff_end / p.cutoff.max(1.0)).powf((self.t / p.length().max(1e-3)).min(1.0));\\n        let a = 1.0 - (-std::f32::consts::TAU * cutoff * dt).exp();\\n        self.lp += (raw - self.lp) * a;\\n        let s = self.lp * self.env() * p.volume;\\n        self.t += dt;\\n        s\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Mixes voices into interleaved stereo.\\npub struct Mixer {\\n    voices: Vec<Voice>,\\n    pub sample_rate: f32,\\n    pub master: f32,\\n    seed: u32,\\n}\\n\\nconst MAX_VOICES: usize = 64;\\n\\nimpl Mixer {\\n    pub fn new(sample_rate: f32) -> Self {\\n        Self { voices: Vec::new(), sample_rate, master: 0.8, seed: 0x9e37_79b9 }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// pan -1 (left) .. 1 (right); delay in seconds.\\n    pub fn play(&mut self, p: Patch, pan: f32, gain: f32, delay: f32) {\\n        if self.voices.len() >= MAX_VOICES {\\n            // Drop the oldest.\\n            self.voices.remove(0);\\n        }\\n        self.seed = self.seed.wrapping_mul(1_664_525).wrapping_add(1_013_904_223);\\n        let pan = pan.clamp(-1.0, 1.0);\\n        let a = (pan + 1.0) * std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_4;\\n        self.voices.push(Voice {\\n            p,\\n            t: 0.0,\\n            delay,\\n            phase: 0.0,\\n            lp: 0.0,\\n            noise: self.seed | 1,\\n            gain_l: a.cos() * gain,\\n            gain_r: a.sin() * gain,\\n        });\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Renders into an interleaved stereo buffer (overwrites).\\n    pub fn render(&mut self, out: &mut [f32]) {\\n        let dt = 1.0 / self.sample_rate;\\n        for frame in out.chunks_mut(2) {\\n            let (mut l, mut r) = (0.0, 0.0);\\n            for v in &mut self.voices {\\n                let s = v.next(dt);\\n                l += s * v.gain_l;\\n                r += s * v.gain_r;\\n            }\\n            // Soft clip.\\n            let m = self.master;\\n        