{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug was found in tick_big phase 0.\n\ntick_breath increments act.t before checking the 32-second cap. The caller resets t to before+dt after the call, so the phase advances immediately after the score is pushed.\n\nThe score push happens only once. The bot may miss its window after note shifting in phase 2. A low step score could still be offset by high phase scores. Phase 0 likely scores around 800. Phase 1 uses a gust formula.\n\nThe gust adds acceleration rather than a position offset. With stiffness at 40 and gust up to 22, the center of balance will fly off. The bot's PD controller only counters wobble and velocity, not gust, so the pose phase likely scores near zero.\n\nPhase 3 step could score near zero if the bot misses notes. Phase 4 plank brace might reach about 1000 if the center of balance stays in. Phase 5 stillness scores roughly 1000 from sending no buttons plus quiet bonus.\n\nThe average score would be 560, failing the 650 target. The bot will counteract the gust in phase 1 by leaning so the target offset equals the gust divided by stiffness. The step window will also be widened to one frame.\n\nChecking that step notes load correctly. The tide board allows enough acceleration to cross the full distance. Paddle timing is feasible if gates are hit; missed gates add two seconds each. Gate layout is still needed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b64ea1c9-d206-423a-abc7-8e31d62c56e6-32","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs","offset":250,"limit":140}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b64ea1c9-d206-423a-abc7-8e31d62c56e6-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn about_page|Source:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/ru