{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_207","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The path `fit/event/breath` splits on the first slash only. The base becomes `fit`. The remainder becomes `event/breath`.\n\nBuild handles the `fit/medley` path correctly. I will write and run a diagnostic test first, then the real tests. I also need to check player position for pause tests using `sim.feet`. Content linting will scan script.toml, hub.toml, rules, about pages, and fit_ui strings. Integration tests can read files relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`. Lint checks will flag TODO, placeholder, BMI, diet, weight, Wii, and Nintendo.\n\nLines containing `Source:` will be allowed. The lint search is case-insensitive, and \"placeholder\" is matched as a substring. The test runner script will live in the dev folder's empty `tests/` directory. It will run engine tests and rewrite cargo's summary into a clean pass count.\n\nThe test command will run both fit integration tests and fit module unit tests in a single cargo invocation. It will use `--test fit` for integration tests and `--lib games::fit` for unit tests.\n\nA single cargo invocation with a `games::fit` filter would match both integration and unit tests. The shell script will run one cargo command that combines both test types.\n\nThe exact cargo command is `cargo test -p pav_core --lib --test fit fit -- --test-threads=2`. The filter `fit` matches integration test names because they are just function names without a `fit::` prefix. The `--test fit` flag selects the binary, and the filter after `--` narrows down the test functions.\n\nThe combined cargo command would run the entire pav_core test suite, which is too slow. The script will instead run two separate cargo commands: one for fit unit tests and one for fit integration tests. It will capture both outputs, sum the pass and failure counts, and rewrite the summary to show only failures plus a final `N passed, 0 failed` line.\n\nThe test runner will exit with a non-zero code when any test fails. History is set to zero seconds for speed. The default tick rate is 60. A full story run would need about 61,200 steps in a small room with one character. I will time a single event first.\n\nThe diagnostic test will cover breath, check, and plank. Step window math shows 0.3125 notes hit reliably, but 0.625 notes risk half-frame misses from float error. The window will be widened to one frame.\n\nThe check step at beat 0.6 lands exactly on a tick boundary, so it should hit reliably. The cannon press timing is riskier: the bot samples its sine value at t minus 0.02 seconds, while the tick logic uses the previous frame's value. Because dt is about 0.0167 and the bot's phase offset is 0.02, the sample can miss the bottom window when the sine crosses upward through its trough.\n\nThe bot and simulation use slightly different previous-frame references for the cannon press: the bot samples phase minus 0.02, while the sim uses t minus dt. This one-frame gap can cause a tick mismatch. I will align the bot to use dt so both sides check the same frame.\n\nThe bot now samples the sine value at `t - dt` to match the simulation's previous-frame reference. A single tick of the bottom window should register power correctly. The dive cycle lasts about 4.8 seconds per cycle, so three dives in 40 seconds is feasible if presses land. During the leap, the bot holds CONFIRM and the tuck score increases while the button is pressed.\n\nThe dive physics show the splash condition triggers when air time exceeds about 1.0 seconds, while tuck reaches its maximum at 0.4 seconds. The scoring formula multiplies height by tuck and timing, but height is near zero when the splash fires, so the final score will be very low.\n\nThe dive score clamps to 0.2 when height is near zero, so three dives yield only 200 points and zero stars. The scoring should instead trigger at the peak or landing threshold while tuck is held, not after splash.\n\nThe dive landing condition is being rewritten to trigger when the sine of air time descends through a mid-height threshold. Timing will be scored against an ideal landing window near 0.85 seconds, rather than the collapsed height at splash.\n\nThe revised dive scoring formula is now concrete. It weights tuck and timing together: `sc = (0.55 + 0.45 * act.tuck) * (0.45 + 0.55 * timing)`. At the ideal landing window near 0.85 seconds with full tuck, a score of roughly 960 points yields three stars. A missed tuck still scores about 500 points for one star. An idle cannon state correctly produces zero score.\n\nPose, Tide, and Tray will be run to verify the judge fix. The floatie spin math checks out: the bot lean rotates at 7.5 rad/s, which sits inside the band threshold of roughly 4.4 to 12.2, so the spin state should register correctly.\n\nThe floatie spin recovers after the direction flip by reversing the lean and chasing the new sign, so the band stays active for about half a second. Catching all seven rings scores roughly 1260 points, which clamps to 1000. The lap judge counts steps in the last second; at two steps per second the rate lands near two, placing it in zone 1.6 to 2.4.\n\nThe lap step press window is 0.02 seconds, so presses land every 30 ticks at a half-second interval. The rate stays near two steps per second, keeping the zone score high.\n\nThe zone score equals zone times 800 plus ribbon points minus bump penalties. The bot steers laterally toward each ribbon by integrating lean_x, which should let it catch them reliably.\n\nCrab bumps fire when lateral position matches the crab spot, but the bot’s ribbon chase may cause it to cross crabs.\n\nThe lap judge’s ribbon check requires the current tick to fall within a 0.02-second window near integer seconds. The ribbon spots are at 8, 22, 40, 58, and 75 seconds, so the bot must press precisely on those whole-second ticks to catch them.\n\nThe pose ring shrinks to 0.18 radius, and the gull wobble can stretch it to 0.19. That risks breaking the streak, so the pose score scale is being raised from 700 to 1000.\n\nThe plank pose is now a failure. The wobble amplitude reaches 0.36 by the sixty-second mark, which exceeds the ring radius of 0.20. The bot will flop out of the ring before it can stay inside for one second.\n\nThe plank pose is now a survival challenge. The wobble amplitude reaches 0.30 by the forty-fifth second, exceeding the ring radius of 0.25, so the bot will likely fall out around the forty-to-forty-five second mark. That yields roughly two stars, but flopping earlier means only one. The PD controller cancels wobble in theory when the target equals the desired position, yet lag and imperfect cancellation make staying inside difficult.\n\nThe plank wobble amplitude of 0.36 is below the lean reach of 0.92, so the PD controller can cancel it and equilibrium stays at zero. Kicks add velocity that may push the bot outside the ring for over one second, causing a flop after about forty seconds. The probe will confirm this.\n\nThe plank pose is actually achievable. The PD controller cancels wobble, so the bot stays near zero center of balance and the stillness metric stays low. Skill should reach roughly 0.9 with age near zero, yielding two or three stars. The check step is reachable, and the blind phase should score about 950 points. I will still widen the step window and fix the cannon landing. For the tide event, the bot steers lean directly toward the shell rather than using PD.\n\nThe big stand gust is too strong for the PD controller to cancel, so the bot will be pushed out of the ring. I am adding a `pd_gust` helper that subtracts the wind force divided by stiffness from the target to counteract it.\n\nThe `pd_gust` helper subtracts the wind force divided by stiffness from the target, so the big stand phase 1 lean can cancel the 22-unit gust. The pose gull wobble is purely amplitude-driven and does not depend on position, meaning the PD controller cancels it cleanly; staying fully inside the ring scores two stars.\n\nThe pose streak multiplier grows by two every two seconds, so a long inside streak can push the score to three stars. I will probe the pose event before continuing theory.\n\nI will write a probe test and run it. The cannon landing fix, step window widening, and big stand gust cancellation are all necessary corrections. In the big stand phase 0, tick_breath sets done=false and pushes a score when t reaches 32, then the caller overwrites t for phase 1. In phase 2, the step window is too tight because bot_step uses shifted note times, so I will widen it.\n\nThe step phase window is only 40 seconds, but the note chart spans roughly 64 seconds. Notes that fall outside the window are missed, and because the score divides hits by the total number of notes, this drags the step score down to about one star. Combined with the other phases, the overall average still lands near two stars.\n\nEven a zero step score keeps the average near two stars, so big stand can still pass. The step press logic is correct: the bot only triggers when inside the window, and double-hits advance the note index properly. I will now implement the fixes and write tests. The plank minute banking also needs review.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8dd9289-4eb1-4518-b88c-7cf7276395e7-45","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"TODO|placeholder|BMI|diet|weight|Wii|Nintendo","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit","-i":true}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8dd9289-4eb1-4518-b88c-7cf7276395e7-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/core.rs","offset":220,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":933,"output_tokens":5600,"cache_read_input_tokens":111104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"1dc24495-740c-4262-98f7-f4bb2302224e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f8dd9289-4eb1-4518-b88c-7cf7276395e7-45","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,103,97,109,101,115,47,102,105,116,47,109,111,100,46,114,115,10,49,56,49,48,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,34,83,111,117,114,99,101,58,32,97,32,98,97,108,97,110,99,101,45,97,110,100,45,119,101,108,108,110,101,115,115,32,114,101,115,111,114,116,44,32,105,110,32,116,104,101,32,115,112,105,114,105,116,32,111,102,32,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,32,98,121,32,78,105,110,116,101,110,100,111,46,34,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1810,\"content\":\"        \\\"Source: a balance-and-wellness resort, in the spirit of Wii Fit by Nintendo.\\\",\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f8dd9289-4eb1-4518-b88c-7cf7276395e7-46","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"220→        1\\n    } else {\\n        0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n230→    #[test]\\n    fn full_lean_settles_inside_the_disc() {\\n        let rules = Rules::default();\\n        let mut b = BalanceCore::default();\\n        b.kicks = false;\\n        b.amp = 0.0;\\n        let lean = Vec2::new(1.0, 0.0);\\n        let mut peak = 0.0_f32;\\n        for _ in 0..180 {\\n            b.step_clean(lean, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n240→            peak = peak.max(b.cob.length());\\n        }\\n        assert!(peak < 1.0, \\\"peak {peak}\\\");\\n        assert!(b.cob.x > 0.85, \\\"settled at {}\\\", b.cob.x);\\n        assert!(!b.tipped);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn a_hard_gust_tips_and_a_release_returns() {\\n        let rules = Rules::default();\\n250→        let mut b = BalanceCore::default();\\n        b.kicks = false;\\n        b.amp = 0.0;\\n        b.gust = Vec2::new(30.0, 0.0);\\n        let mut tipped = false;\\n        for _ in 0..120 {\\n            b.step_clean(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n            tipped |= b.tipped;\\n        }\\n        assert!(tipped, \\\"gust should tip within 2s\\\");\\n260→        b.gust = Vec2::ZERO;\\n        for _ in 0..180 {\\n            b.step_clean(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n        }\\n        assert!(b.cob.length() < 0.2, \\\"returned to {}\\\", b.cob);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn age_moves_the_right_way_and_stays_in_range() {\\n        let young = balance_age(1.0, 4, 30);\\n270→        let older = balance_age(0.0, 0, 0);\\n        assert!(young < older);\\n        assert!((18..=99).contains(&young));\\n        assert!((18..=99).contains(&older));\\n        assert_eq!(balance_age(1.0, 0, 0), 24);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(399.0), 0);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(400.0), 1);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(650.0), 2);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(850.0), 3);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(24.0), 0);\\n280→        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(25.0), 1);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(40.0), 2);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(55.0), 3);\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"220→        1\\n    } else {\\n        0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n230→    #[test]\\n    fn full_lean_settles_inside_the_disc() {\\n        let rules = Rules::default();\\n        let mut b = BalanceCore::default();\\n        b.kicks = false;\\n        b.amp = 0.0;\\n        let lean = Vec2::new(1.0, 0.0);\\n        let mut peak = 0.0_f32;\\n        for _ in 0..180 {\\n            b.step_clean(lean, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n240→            peak = peak.max(b.cob.length());\\n        }\\n        assert!(peak < 1.0, \\\"peak {peak}\\\");\\n        assert!(b.cob.x > 0.85, \\\"settled at {}\\\", b.cob.x);\\n        assert!(!b.tipped);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn a_hard_gust_tips_and_a_release_returns() {\\n        let rules = Rules::default();\\n250→        let mut b = BalanceCore::default();\\n        b.kicks = false;\\n        b.amp = 0.0;\\n        b.gust = Vec2::new(30.0, 0.0);\\n        let mut tipped = false;\\n        for _ in 0..120 {\\n            b.step_clean(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n            tipped |= b.tipped;\\n        }\\n        assert!(tipped, \\\"gust should tip within 2s\\\");\\n260→        b.gust = Vec2::ZERO;\\n        for _ in 0..180 {\\n            b.step_clean(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n        }\\n        assert!(b.cob.length() < 0.2, \\\"returned to {}\\\", b.cob);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn age_moves_the_right_way_and_stays_in_range() {\\n        let young = balance_age(1.0, 4, 30);\\n270→        let older = balance_age(0.0, 0, 0);\\n        assert!(young < older);\\n        assert!((18..=99).contains(&young));\\n        assert!((18..=99).contains(&older));\\n        assert_eq!(balance_age(1.0, 0, 0), 24);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(399.0), 0);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(400.0), 1);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(650.0), 2);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(850.0), 3);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(24.0), 0);\\n280→        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(25.0), 1);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(40.0), 2);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(55.0), 3);\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/core.rs\",\"offset\":220,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"        1\\n    } else {\\n        0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn full_lean_settles_inside_the_disc() {\\n        let rules = Rules::default();\\n        let mut b = BalanceCore::default();\\n        b.kicks = false;\\n        b.amp = 0.0;\\n        let lean = Vec2::new(1.0, 0.0);\\n        let mut peak = 0.0_f32;\\n        for _ in 0..180 {\\n            b.step_clean(lean, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n            peak = peak.max(b.cob.length());\\n        }\\n        assert!(peak < 1.0, \\\"peak {peak}\\\");\\n        assert!(b.cob.x > 0.85, \\\"settled at {}\\\", b.cob.x);\\n        assert!(!b.tipped);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn a_hard_gust_tips_and_a_release_returns() {\\n        let rules = Rules::default();\\n        let mut b = BalanceCore::default();\\n        b.kicks = false;\\n        b.amp = 0.0;\\n        b.gust = Vec2::new(30.0, 0.0);\\n        let mut tipped = false;\\n        for _ in 0..120 {\\n            b.step_clean(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n            tipped |= b.tipped;\\n        }\\n        assert!(tipped, \\\"gust should tip within 2s\\\");\\n        b.gust = Vec2::ZERO;\\n        for _ in 0..180 {\\n            b.step_clean(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n        }\\n        assert!(b.cob.length() < 0.2, \\\"returned to {}\\\", b.cob);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn age_moves_the_right_way_and_stays_in_range() {\\n        let young = balance_age(1.0, 4, 30);\\n        let older = balance_age(0.0, 0, 0);\\n        assert!(young < older);\\n        assert!((18..=99).contains(&young));\\n        assert!((18..=99).contains(&older));\\n        assert_eq!(balance_age(1.0, 0, 0), 24);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(399.0), 0);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(400.0), 1);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(650.0), 2);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(850.0), 3);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(24.0), 0);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(25.0), 1);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(40.0), 2);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(55.0), 3);\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":284}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"44184aba-9372-4a9b-ad5e-798fe04a7ccb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_208","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking whether step_clean exists.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-06533201-9992-4607-b506-1b8ec5c71cbc-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs","offset":480,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-06533201-9992-4607-b506-1b8ec5c71cbc-48","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn step_clean|fn feet\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src","glob":"*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6527,"output_tokens":348,"cache_read_input_tokens":112000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"d319f740-a476-431b-aeac-61dc61feaecf"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-06533201-9992-4607-b506-1b8ec5c71cbc-47","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"480→        }\\n        if e.prop.is_some() {\\n            self.invalidate_prop_navigation();\\n        }\\n        true\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Advances one fixed tick, recording the input for rewind and replays.\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        let dt = self.dt();\\n490→        match self.studio_mode() {\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Animation => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.animation_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Prop => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.prop_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n500→                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Creature => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.creature_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::World => {}\\n510→        }\\n        if self.history.enabled && self.config.history_seconds > 0.0 {\\n            self.history.window = (self.config.history_seconds * self.config.tick_rate.hz() as f32) as u64;\\n            self.history.record(&self.state, input);\\n        }\\n        if self.recording.ticks() < MAX_RECORDING_TICKS {\\n            self.recording.push(input);\\n        }\\n        self.step_inner(input);\\n    }\\n520→\\n    fn step_inner(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        // Hit-stop slows the whole world for a moment.\\n        let raw_dt = self.dt();\\n        let dt = raw_dt * self.game_time_scale();\\n        self.state.physics.params.dt = dt as Real;\\n        self.state.physics.gravity = Vector::new(0.0, -self.config.gravity as Real, 0.0);\\n\\n        // Behaviours set this tick's velocities of moving objects; characters then move\\n        // (rapier's controller carries them with kinematic platforms) and the physics step\\n530→        // advances everything together.\\n        self.run_behaviors(dt);\\n\\n        // Getting in and out of vehicles.\\n        self.vehicle_interact(input);\\n\\n        // The game decides what the hero and its monsters do this tick.\\n        let mut events = Vec::new();\\n        let mut game_inputs = self.game_pre(input, dt, &mut events);\\n        game_inputs.extend(self.play_pre(input, dt, &mut events));\\n540→        // A frozen game (pause, menus) still ran `pre`. Skip the world so time and bodies stay put.\\n        if self.state.play.as_ref().is_some_and(|g| g.frozen()) {\\n            if let Some(p) = self.player() {\\n                self.state.focus = p.pos;\\n            }\\n            self.state.tick += 1;\\n            if !self.replaying {\\n                self.events.extend(events);\\n            }\\n            return;\\n550→        }\\n\\n        // Characters.\\n        let ids: Vec<EntityId> = self.state.entities.iter().filter(|e| e.character.is_some()).map(|e| e.id).collect();\\n        let mut actions = Vec::new();\\n        let idle = InputFrame::default();\\n        let player_feet = self.player().and_then(|p| Some(p.pos - Vec3::Y * p.character.as_ref()?.height() * 0.5));\\n        let all_feet: Vec<Vec3> =\\n            self.state.entities.iter().filter_map(|e| Some(e.pos - Vec3::Y * e.character.as_ref()?.height() * 0.5)).collect();\\n        let mut fallen = Vec::new();\\n560→        for id in ids {\\n            let npc_input: InputFrame;\\n            let inp = if let Some(gi) = game_inputs.get(&id) {\\n                gi\\n            } else if Some(id) == self.state.player {\\n                input\\n            } else {\\n                // Non-player characters: their brain drives them like a player would.\\n                let st = &mut self.state;\\n                match st.entities.map.get_mut(&id) {\",\"content_concise\":\"480→        }\\n        if e.prop.is_some() {\\n            self.invalidate_prop_navigation();\\n        }\\n        true\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Advances one fixed tick, recording the input for rewind and replays.\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        let dt = self.dt();\\n490→        match self.studio_mode() {\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Animation => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.animation_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Prop => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.prop_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n500→                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Creature => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.creature_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::World => {}\\n510→        }\\n        if self.history.enabled && self.config.history_seconds > 0.0 {\\n            self.history.window = (self.config.history_seconds * self.config.tick_rate.hz() as f32) as u64;\\n            self.history.record(&self.state, input);\\n        }\\n        if self.recording.ticks() < MAX_RECORDING_TICKS {\\n            self.recording.push(input);\\n        }\\n        self.step_inner(input);\\n    }\\n520→\\n    fn step_inner(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        // Hit-stop slows the whole world for a moment.\\n        let raw_dt = self.dt();\\n        let dt = raw_dt * self.game_time_scale();\\n        self.state.physics.params.dt = dt as Real;\\n        self.state.ph