7,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,115,105,109,46,114,115,10,52,50,48,58,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,32,102,110,32,102,101,101,116,40,38,115,101,108,102,44,32,105,100,58,32,69,110,116,105,116,121,73,100,41,32,45,62,32,79,112,116,105,111,110,60,86,101,99,51,62,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/core.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":183,\"content\":\"    pub fn step_clean(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules) {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":420,\"content\":\"    pub fn feet(&self, id: EntityId) -> Option<Vec3> {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"2490d7af-5bc4-4d58-8681-03d6a5921803"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_209","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"play_pre receives a dt value that may be scaled by game_time_scale().\n\nFitGame applies its own time_scale on top of the default game_time_scale. During pause, frozen returns early after play_pre, so world_time stays fixed and player physics is skipped. Tests should verify world_time and feet rather than sim.time(). Recording still pushes every input while frozen, which risks unbounded growth and OOM; disabling history snapshots does not prevent this.\n\nRecording overhead is manageable: roughly 500k steps across two simulations consume only about 32MB of memory. The real bottleneck is rapier physics, which may take several minutes. History snapshots must be disabled before stepping begins; build() sets history_seconds to 8 by default, so the test must override it to 0 after Sim::new.\n\nHistory snapshots are confirmed safe because they are disabled before any physics steps. Recording cannot be turned off, so that is not a concern. The next step is to apply fixes and write tests. A temporary probe test will be used to verify scores before deleting it.\n\nThe real test will print scores in its assertion message. Event tests will run first, then the full stay test. The cannon fix code adds air time, tuck mechanics, lean physics, and landing detection with timing scoring.\n\nThe landing score formula weights tuck and timing equally. At the target air time the sine value is about 0.43, satisfying the 0.45 threshold and yielding a perfect score of 1.0 once tuck saturates. The bot holds confirm for the full leap to maximize tuck. The landing window is narrow because sin(2.7) sits just below the 0.45 limit.\n\nThe landing window opens at air time 0.8916, one tick after the sine drops below 0.45. The bot_cannon function is being drafted to hold CONFIRM during the leap and use a sine-based idle pattern.\n\nThe bot's idle pattern now triggers CONFIRM at the bottom of its sine cycle when fewer than three dives remain. The bot and simulation share the same pre-tick activity state, so their timing stays synchronized. The step function is being drafted next.\n\nThe step bot now checks that the current note is within one frame plus a small margin before acting. Phase 3 will use the same timing guard.\n\nA gust-cancel term is added to the general PD controller. It subtracts stiffness-normalized gust from the target position before computing lean, which helps big stand and does not hurt when no gust is present.\n\nThe bot's paddle and tide bots do not use the PD controller, so they are unaffected by the new gust-cancel term.\n\nThe tray counter's direct jolt term is the real problem. The bot sets lean to -j*0.55, but cob.x lags behind because it follows lean slowly. The direct jolt term is tiny: an 8-jolt burst adds only about 0.055 total to the glass position, so it barely cancels the lagging cob.\n\nThe uncountered jolt sum is only about 0.44, which is below the 1.0 spill threshold, so glasses would not tip over even without a counter. The bot's lean correctly cancels the jolt by moving in the opposite direction. During each jolt, cob.x drifts toward about -0.81, adding to the glass tilt in the same direction as the jolt itself.\n\nA sustained -0.5 cob drift for half a second adds only about -0.325 to the glass tilt, so that is manageable.\n\nIdle tray drift from random wobble and kicks could accumulate over fifty seconds. The mean should stay near zero, but a biased random walk might still tip glasses.\n\nThe idle score must stay under 400 points to qualify for one star. That means keeping fewer than two glasses. Two glasses equal 400 points, which is exactly one star. An idle score of 1000 would fail the threshold.\n\nThe idle score must stay below 400, so at most one glass may remain. Keeping all five glasses scores 1000 and fails. The current jolt effect is too weak to spill glasses on its own; each burst adds only about ±0.24 to tilt, and the integral per jolt is roughly 0.055. Alternating positive and negative jolts might cancel out when integrated over time, so the effect on glasses needs to be stronger.\n\nAlternating jolt pulses cancel out when integrated over time, so the glass never tips on idle. The current jolt is a position offset that returns to zero once the pulse ends; it does not add persistent velocity. To make idle glasses spill, the jolt must be large enough to exceed the 1.0 tilt threshold in a single burst, or the pulses should be grouped with the same sign.\n\nAlternating jolts cancel out when integrated, so they never tip glasses on idle. The fix is to make each jolt add a lasting offset or impulse to the glass tilt instead of returning to zero. If all eight jolts share the same sign, the total exceeds 3.6 and spills every glass; the bot must counter each one with its lean. A sway velocity is being considered as a simpler implementation.\n\nThe simplest fix is to add a direct impulse of 0.55 to every glass on the jolt frame. The bot will counter with a hard opposite lean during that window so cob.x integrates back toward zero before the next jolt arrives. This should tip glasses on idle without requiring slow decay or complex sway tracking.\n\nThe jolt impulse is being tuned to 0.35 so eight uncountered bursts total 2.8 and spill every glass. A single missed counter leaves only 0.35 of residual tilt, which is small enough that the bot should catch all of them. Because every glass shares the same tilt, a single failure spills the entire tray. This makes the idle score exactly zero and the bot score exactly 1000, which cleanly satisfies the test requirements.\n\nThe jolt impulse is fixed at 0.42 per burst, and the glass tilt term is raised to 2.2. The bot counter is being drafted to sum active jolts and apply the opposing lean.\n\nAlternating jolt impulses cancel out when integrated, so idle glasses never tip. The fix is to make every jolt positive with magnitude 1.0 and apply a 0.38 impulse per burst. Eight uncountered bursts total about 3.04, which spills all glasses on idle and yields a score of zero.\n\nThe bot will read the first glass tilt from `act.glasses[0]` to gauge how much jolt debt remains. It also anticipates the next upcoming jolt within 0.15 seconds. The counter lean is set to the negative of twice the glass tilt plus half the anticipated jolt, clamped between -1.0 and 1.0.\n\nThe counter lean of -0.84 against a +0.38 glass tilt drives the cob toward -0.77, clearing the debt in about 0.22 seconds before the glass turns negative and the lean reverses. This keeps the glass under the 1.0 spill threshold while idle glasses still accumulate enough tilt to tip. The jolts will all use a magnitude of 1.0 with an impulse of 0.42 per burst. The tide bot will be left unchanged for now. A potential day-minute bug that could assign zero stars to some events also needs checking.\n\nI am drafting a test harness with helper functions to boot simulations, query status, and run until a condition is met. I will probe floatie direction and lap timing next. Then I will write the test file and apply fixes before running the full event probe.\n\nThe test harness helper steps the simulation using bot input and returns true when a predicate is satisfied. Direct events run until the phase reaches \"result\", while idle mode steps with default input until then.\n\nTick caps are being set for each event type: 20000 for big stand, 40000 for medley, and 216000 for story. Story duration is capped at 60 minutes, though it typically finishes in about 20 minutes.\n\nDeterminism will be verified by running two simulations and comparing their hub statistics. The attract sequence requires 599 default steps, then a demo step with device 2 and confirm pressed while demo is false; the save_serial must remain unchanged and the phase should reach title. The pause test boots an event, skips the card, records world_time and feet, sends PAUSE, holds it for 120 ticks while keeping world_time and feet constant, then resumes and steps for 30 more ticks so time advances.\n\nThe slider test requires the Dev menu to open from the title, a 300-step pause to freeze the flow, a stiffness of 80, and a click on step 60 to reset stiffness to 40. Music status must equal 0.1. Save round-trip is covered by the existing unit test. Age range checks are also handled by the unit test.\n\nThe story integration test will also assert that the age stays between 18 and 99. The play-together sequence will be tested by booting a fit scene, pressing down and confirm to reach the together phase, then running until the podium is non-empty. The bot will confirm both guests during that phase before passing through cards and events. For the story event, the bot will run until it reaches a win outcome or the tick cap.\n\nStory test assertions will verify a win, five stamps, all thirteen event keys in played, and world_time under one hour. The story scene includes Check, two islands, Big Stand, and four events. Island time is negligible because the bot schedules immediately. The test seeds are 1, 2, 3, 7, 11, and 21. Story tests run serially while event tests run in parallel with two threads to stay under the 20 GB memory limit.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0afe1364-4476-49f9-b8f9-d435291b53bc-49","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs","offset":155,"limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0afe1364-4476-49f9-b8f9-d435291b53bc-50","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^pub (mod|use)","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/lib.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1706,"output_tokens":5096,"cache_read_input_tokens":118400,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"f5e53f3b-c304-47fb-b0a5-fdca3b1a5718"}
