Hammock {} · empty\\\", i + 1) };\\n                    v.push((10 + i as u16, label));\\n                }\\n                v.push((ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into()));\\n                v\\n            }\\n            Flow::Name => s.names.iter().enumerate().map(|(i, n)| (400 + i as u16, n.clone())).take(6).collect(),\\n            Flow::Look => s.skins.iter().enumerate().map(|(i, n)| (500 + i as u16, n.clone())).take(6).collect(),\\n            Flow::Outfit => s.outfits.iter().enumerate().map(|(i, n)| (520 + i as u16, n.clone())).take(6).collect(),\\n            Flow::Schedule => {\\n                let evs = self.schedule_events();\\n                let mut v = Vec::new();\\n                for (i, e) in evs.iter().enumerate().take(4) {\\n                    let done = if self.today_played.iter().any(|p| p == e.key()) { \\\" · done\\\" } else { \\\"\\\" };\\n                    v.push((100 + i as u16, format!(\\\"{}{done}\\\", e.title())));\\n                }\\n                if self.day_clear() {\\n                    v.push((ACT_END_DAY, \\\"End the day\\\".into()));\\n                }\\n                v.push((ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into()));\\n                v\\n            }\\n            Flow::Result => vec![\\n                (ACT_RESULT_BACK, \\\"Back to the island\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_RETRY, \\\"Retry\\\".into()),\\n            ],\\n            Flow::Together => vec![\\n                (ACT_G2, \\\"2 guests\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_G3, \\\"3 guests\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_G4, \\\"4 guests\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into()),\\n            ],\\n            Flow::Settings => self.settings_items(),\\n            Flow::Dev => self.dev_items(),\\n            Flow::Pause => vec![(ACT_RESUME, \\\"Resume\\\".into()), (ACT_SETTINGS, \\\"Settings\\\".into())],\\n            Flow::About | Flow::HowTo | Flow::Wardrobe | Flow::Calendar => vec![(ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into())],\\n            Flow::Attract if self.touch_only => vec![(ACT_SETTINGS, \\\"Settings\\\".into())],\\n            Flow::Podium => vec![(ACT_BACK, \\\"Back to the title\\\".into())],\\n            _ => Vec::new(),\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn settings_items(&self) -> Vec<(u16, String)> {\\n        let m = self.settings.music;\\n        match self.page {\\n            0 => vec![\\n                (610, format!(\\\"Music {:.0}%\\\", m * 100.0)),\\n                (611, format!(\\\"Effects {:.0}%\\\", self.settings.sfx * 100.0)),\\n                (612, format!(\\\"Voices {:.0}%\\\", self.settings.voice * 100.0)),\\n                (ACT_XBOX, if self.settings.xbox { \\\"Glyphs: Xbox\\\" } else { \\\"Glyphs: PlayStation\\\" }.into()),\\n                (613, format!(\\\"Lean {:.0}%\\\", self.settings.sensitivity * 100.0)),\\n                (ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into()),\\n            ],\\n            _ => vec![\\n                (614, format!(\\\"Wobble assist {:.0}%\\\", self.settings.wobble_assist * 100.0)),\\n                (615, \\\"Rhythm offset\\\".into()),\\n                (616, format!(\\\"Text {:.1}\\\", self.settings.text_speed)),\\n                (ACT_FULLSCREEN, if self.settings.fullscreen { \\\"Fullscreen on\\\" } else { \\\"Fullscreen off\\\" }.into()),\\n                (ACT_RESET_SAVE, if self.reset_arm { \\\"Confirm erase\\\" } else { \\\"Erase save\\\" }.into()),\\n                (ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into()),\\n            ],\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn dev_items(&self) -> Vec<(u16, String)> {\\n        match self.page {\\n            0 => vec![\\n                (ACT_RESUME, \\\"Resume\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_DEV_RESET, \\\"Reset feel\\\".into()),\\n                (43, \\\"Wardrobe\\\".into()),\\n                (44, \\\"Calendar\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_SETTINGS, \\\"Settings\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_ABOUT, \\\"About\\\".into()),\\n            ],\\n            _ => {\\n                let mut rules = self.rules.clone();\\n                let infos = params::list(&mut rules);\\n                let start = (self.page - 1) * 4;\\n                let mut v: Vec<(u16, String)> = infos\\n                    .iter()\\n                    .enumerate()\\n                    .skip(start)\\n                    .take(4)\\n                    .map(|(i, info)| {\\n                        let label = match &info.value {\\n                            ParamValue::Float(f) => format!(\\\"{} {f:.2}\\\", info.path),\\n                            ParamValue::Int(n) => format!(\\\"{} {n}\\\", info.path),\\n                            _ => info.path.clone(),\\n                        };\\n                        (300 + i as u16, label)\\n                    })\\n                    .collect();\\n                v.push((ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into()));\\n                v\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn start_activity(&mut self, kind: EventId, sim: &mut Sim) {\\n        if let Some(id) = self.ghost_id.take() {\\n            sim.despawn(id);\\n        }\\n        let rules = self.rules.clone();\\n        let mut act = Activity::start(kind, &rules, &mut sim.state.rng);\\n\",\"total_lines\":1852}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"95583a0a-c5f3-4f3a-a287-42eebe2e7f55"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_212","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The schedule contains exactly four events. Day 4 includes Tide, Paddle, Tray, and Cannon.\n\nThe name screen and schedule both respect their item limits. The stiffness slider is on page 1, so the test must navigate there or the apply logic may run regardless of visibility.\n\nSlider events apply regardless of page when the flow is Dev or Settings. The reset button and Xbox toggle are reachable from the Dev page. Music status is 0.10.\n\nIf a day is not cleared, the bot retries the first event. Each retry banks one minute, so even zero-star events eventually clear the day.\n\nEven with zero-star events, the worst-case retry loop still finishes under sixty minutes. Stamps and victory are guaranteed.\n\nStory tests can pass with low stars as long as they avoid infinite loops. The Age check uses Rowboat and Credits, awards five stamps, and marks every event played. Big Stand is banked correctly. Event tests will run first for faster feedback. The unused-events warning is harmless and will be left alone unless that line is modified.\n\nThe unused `events` warning is in `tick_big`, not `tick_cannon`. That function takes the parameter but never uses it.\n\nThe unused `events` parameter in `tick_big` is harmless and will be left as-is. The test will verify that slider 300 changes the stiffness value.\n\nThe slider list places stiffness at index zero, followed by all other floats and squat_reps at the end. The floatie spin direction bug will be probed carefully before implementation. The single test command will live at `{dev}/tests/run.sh` and change into the engine directory.\n\nThe test script will run both the library and integration tests for `pav_core::games::fit`, capturing all output in a temporary log file. Cargo's quiet mode still prints progress dots and summary lines, so the command will filter that output to show only failures and the final result.\n\nThe test script will filter the cargo log to drop progress dots, \"running N tests\", and \"test result:\" lines. It will keep only failure and panic messages, then print a final summary line.\n\nThe two cargo invocations must run sequentially because they share a target directory. The balance tests are in the library and cannot be moved into the integration file, so both test suites will still be executed. I will not suppress the unused-events warning. Next I will edit the Cannon and Tray events and verify that tick_cannon uses rules.bounce_gain.\n\nThe score formula for the new event is `((0.35 + 0.65 * act.tuck) * (0.4 + 0.6 * timing) * rules.bounce_gain).clamp(0.0, 1.0)`.\n\nTray changes will touch its start function, tick_tray, and tray_counter.\n\nAll eight jolt magnitudes are set to 1.0, giving a 50-second duration with the last jolt at 42.5 seconds.\n\nImpulse accumulation uses the sign of each jolt value, but every jolt is positive so the total is simply 8 times 0.48.\n\nThe bot reads the glasses.\n\nThe bot will score zero stars and spill at the third jolt. Controlling glass[0] is enough because all glasses move together. The cobblestone should oscillate within ±0.6 rather than overshoot, since the lean is clamped to -g × 3.0.\n\nA cancel term will be added to the gust PD controller. The step window will be widened. The unused `events` parameter in `tick_big` is not needed for sound effects. A content linting function will scan the play text sources for prohibited terms.\n\nThe content linting function skips lines containing \"Source:\" and panics if any prohibited word appears. Grep confirmed that \"weight\" does not appear in \"lightweight\", and \"diet\" is absent from event comments. Fit UI strings are embedded directly in the code.\n\nThe content lint will also scan fit_ui.rs, events.rs, and mod.rs. A medley determinism test is being drafted: it boots the medley simulation with a fixed seed and runs up to thirty thousand ticks until the hub reports done.\n\nThe medley determinism test will compare stats vectors with epsilon because JSON numbers may be floats. Bot inputs are deterministic, so the same seed should yield identical results. An attract save test will record the save_serial before and after stepping for six hundred frames.\n\nThe attract save test will step 599 frames, verify the phase is still title, then step one more to confirm the demo flag and attract phase appear. Idle increments correctly on default input because no buttons are pressed and lean is zero. The exit logic captures the save_serial.\n\nThe exit test will press the confirm button on device 2 to return to title, then assert that demo is false and the save_serial matches the original value. A pause test for the breath event will boot the simulation, run the bot until the phase reaches \"event\", and advance thirty more ticks so world_time becomes positive.\n\nThe pause test will freeze world time and player position by pressing pause, then verify that both remain unchanged after ninety idle ticks. Pressing pause again resumes the event phase. The bot input must be fetched before the next step to avoid a borrow conflict.\n\nThe slider test will boot the fit game, enter the dev phase, adjust slider 300 to 1.0, and verify that stiffness changes by more than one unit. It will then click button 60 to confirm the value settles near 40.0. The music status must be exactly 0.1. After winning the Age story event, the player age should be between 18 and 99 inclusive.\n\nA direct age comparison test is unnecessary because balance_age is already tested. The touch-device attract test is optional and will be skipped to save time. PROGRESS.md will be written after the tests pass.\n\nThe bot outcome is checked before each step, so a post-confirm tick can set the outcome and halt the loop. The played list must contain all thirteen event keys, so the test will verify membership with a set. Day four sleep logic awards four stamps before Big Stand adds the fifth.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The stay loop typechecks. I’m tightening the event bots that would miss the star line, then I’ll lock them with sim tests."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6ab91d1-5abf-4ba0-8358-958f69b8f304-54","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs","old_string":"fn pd(bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules, target: Vec2) -> Vec2 {\n    let lean = (target - bal.wobble() - bal.vel * 0.15) / rules.reach.max(0.2);\n    lean.clamp_length_max(1.0)\n}","new_string":"fn pd(bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules, target: Vec2) -> Vec2 {\n    // Gust is an acceleration. Cancel it or a strong shove walks the dot off the ring.\n    let cancel = bal.gust / rules.stiffness.max(1.0);\n    let lean = (target - bal.wobble() - cancel - bal.vel * 0.15) / rules.reach.max(0.2);\n    lean.clamp_length_max(1.0)\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6ab91d1-5abf-4ba0-8358-958f69b8f304-55","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs","old_string":"            let press = (act.sub - at).abs() < 0.5 / 60.0 + 0.001 && i < 8.0 && i >= 0.0;","new_string":"            let press = (act.sub - at).abs() <= 1.0 / 60.0 + 0.002 && i < 8.0 && i >= 0.0;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6ab91d1-5abf-4ba0-8358-958f69b8f304-56","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs","old_string":"    if (act.t - n[0]).abs() > 0.5 / 60.0 + 0.001 {\n        return (Vec2::ZERO, 0);\n    }","new_string":"    // A note can fall halfway between ticks. One frame is still inside the perfect window.\n    if (act.t - n[0]).abs() > 1.0 / 60.0 + 0.002 {\n        return (Vec2::ZERO, 0);\n    }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6ab91d1-5abf-4ba0-8358-958f69b8f304-57","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs","old_string":"            for i in 0..8 {\n                let t = 4.0 + i as f32 * 5.0;\n                let mag = if i % 2 == 0 { 1.6 } else { -1.6 };\n                a.jolts.push([t, mag]);\n            }","new_string":"            // Same-direction shoves. An idle tray walks off; a lean the other way keeps the glasses.\n            for i in 0..8 {\n                let t = 4.0 + i as f32 * 5.5;\n                a.jolts.push([t, 1.0]);\n            }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6ab91d1-5abf-4ba0-8358-958f69b8f304-58","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs","old_string":"fn tray_counter(act: &Activity) -> f32 {\n    let mut j = 0.0;\n    for s in &act.jolts {\n        let dt = act.t - s[0];\n        if dt > 0.0 && dt < 0.45 {\n            j += s[1] * (1.0 - dt / 0.45);\n        }\n    }\n    (-j * 0.55).clamp(-1.0, 1.0)\n}","new_string":"fn tray_counter(act: &Activity) -> f32 {\n    // Glasses share one tilt. Lean against whatever the first glass is already doing,\n    // and preload a shove that is about to land.\n    let g = act.glasses[0];\n    let mut soon = 0.0;\n    for s in &act.jolts {\n        let until = s[0] - act.t;\n        if until > 0.0 && until < 0.2 {\n            soon += s[1];\n        }\n    }\n    (-(g * 3.4 + soon * 0.55)).clamp(-1.0, 1.0)\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6ab91d1-5abf-4ba0-8358-958f69b8f304-59","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs","old_string":"fn bot_cannon(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\n    if act.leaping {\n        let lean = Vec2::new(0.0, 0.2);\n        return (lean, buttons::CONFIRM);\n    }\n    let period = 1.2 * (1.0 / act_bounce(1.0));\n    let _ = period;\n    let phase = act.t / 1.2;\n    let s = (phase * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin();\n    let prev = ((phase - 0.02) * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin();\n    // Bottom of the bounce: sine crosses -0.95 going down then up. Press near the minimum.\n    let at_bottom = s < -0.92 && prev < s;\n    let b = if at_bottom && act.dives < 3 { buttons::CONFIRM } else { 0 };\n    (Vec2::ZERO, b)\n}","new_string":"fn bot_cannon(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\n    if act.leaping {\n        return (Vec2::new(0.0, 0.15), buttons::CONFIRM);\n    }\n    let dt = 1.0 / 60.0;\n    let s = (act.t / 1.2 * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin();\n    let prev = ((act.t - dt) / 1.2 * std::f32::consts::TAU).sin();\n    let at_bottom = s < -0.9 && s > prev;\n    let b = if at_bottom && act.dives < 3 { buttons::CONFIRM } else { 0 };\n    (Vec2::ZERO, b)\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6ab91d1-5abf-4ba0-8358-958f69b8f304-60","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs","old_string":"        act.air += dt;\n        if held & buttons::CONFIRM != 0 {\n            act.tuck = (act.tuck + dt / 0.4).min(1.0);\n        }\n        act.px += lean.x * dt;\n        let height = (act.air * 3.0).sin().max(0.0) * act.power * 0.25;\n        if act.air > 0.55 && height < 0.15 {\n            let timing = (1.0 - (act.air - 0.7).abs()).clamp(0.2, 1.0);\n            let sc = (height * 4.0).clamp(0.2, 1.0) * act.tuck.clamp(0.2, 1.0) * timing * rules.bounce_gain;\n            act.dive_scores.push(sc.clamp(0.0, 1.0));\n            act.dives += 1;\n            events.push(SimEvent::BigSplash { pos: glam::Vec3::new(act.px, 0.0, 2.0), size: 1.2 + act.tuck });\n            act.leaping = false;\n            act.power = 0.0;\n            act.air = 0.0;\n            act.tuck = 0.0;\n        }","new_string":"        act.air += dt;\n        if held & buttons::CONFIRM != 0 {\n            act.tuck = (act.tuck + dt / 0.35).min(1.0);\n        }\n        act.px += lean.x * dt;\n        let s = (act.air * 3.0).sin();\n        let prev = ((act.air - dt) * 3.0).sin();\n        // Landing is the way down, while the tuck still counts. Waiting for the splash to flatten scored nothing.\n        let landing = act.air > 0.55 && s > 0.0 && s < prev && s < 0.5;\n        if landing {\n            let timing = (1.0 - (act.air - 0.9).abs() / 0.35).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\n            let sc = ((0.35 + 0.65 * act.tuck) * (0.4 + 0.6 * timing) * rules.bounce_gain).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\n            act.dive_scores.push(sc);\n            act.dives += 1;\n            events.push(SimEvent::BigSplash { pos: glam::Vec3::new(act.px, 0.0, 2.0), size: 1.2 + act.tuck });\n            act.leaping = false;\n            act.power = 0.0;\n            act.air = 0.0;\n            act.tuck = 0.0;\n        }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6ab91d1-5abf-4ba0-8358-958f69b8f304-61","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs","old_string":"    let mut jolt = 0.0;\n    for s in &act.jolts {\n        let d = act.t - s[0];\n        if d > 0.0 && d < 0.35 {\n            jolt += s[1] * (1.0 - d / 0.35);\n        }\n    }\n    let tilt = bal.cob.x + jolt * 0.15;\n    for i in 0..5 {\n        if !act