9,50,57,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,116,119,101,97,107,58,32,68,101,102,97,117,108,116,58,58,100,101,102,97,117,108,116,40,41,44,10,49,51,48,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,125,10,49,51,49,45,32,32,32,32,125,10,49,51,50,45,10,49,51,51,45,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,32,102,110,32,102,114,111,109,95,111,119,110,101,100,40,102,111,110,116,58,32,86,101,99,60,117,56,62,41,32,45,62,32,83,101,108,102,32,123,10,49,51,52,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,83,101,108,102,32,123,10,49,51,53,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,102,111,110,116,58,32,67,111,119,58,58,79,119,110,101,100,40,102,111,110,116,41,44,10,49,51,54,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,105,110,100,101,120,58,32,48,44,10,49,51,55,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,116,119,101,97,107,58,32,68,101,102,97,117,108,116,58,58,100,101,102,97,117,108,116,40,41,44,10,49,51,56,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,125,10,49,51,57,45,32,32,32,32,125,10,49,52,48,45,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/epaint-0.36.2/src/text/fonts.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":125,\"content\":\"    pub fn from_static(font: &'static [u8]) -> Self {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"d5bfb391-7114-4d01-96a5-ba44e7f517b6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_257","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"set_fonts only takes effect on the next pass.\n\nI will call set_fonts before the first run_ui. An empty dummy pass immediately after will let the fonts take effect before the real passes begin.\n\nFredoka will be installed as the first proportional font so FontId::proportional uses it immediately. Titles and body can both use proportional fonts without waiting for a dummy pass.\n\nNunito will be added as the fallback proportional font. A warm-up pass will precede the actual drawing.\n\nFont sizes must be enforced in the draw helper. Titles need at least 64 pixels and body at least 34 pixels at 1080p, scaling down for smaller screens. I will add `scale_for`, `title_px`, and `body_px` helpers to compute these sizes, and unit tests will verify the minimums.\n\nA test in pav_ui will verify that Headless::frame renders the correct prompts. It will build a FitUi, attach it to a HudFrame, call frame, and assert that the resulting HUD text contains the expected glyph prompt.\n\nThe painter draws footer, glyph, title, lines, and items. A test will verify that different FitUi.glyph values appear in the rendered HUD.\n\nMixer::render will handle music mixing. The struct gains song, song_sample, music_gain, and voice_gain fields. Music stays silent by default. When a song is active, notes are mixed at music_gain times master. A test will confirm that 10% music gain produces exactly 0.10 of full scale.\n\nThe test compares a full-gain and a 10% music-gain mixer output. It asserts the quiet mix is within 2% of exactly 10% of the full mix. Tanh soft clipping could distort this ratio if the full mix is too loud.\n\nThe sequencer output will be kept near 0.3 peak at full gain so tanh stays nearly linear. The ratio of tanh(0.24) to tanh(0.024) is about 0.101, which satisfies the 2% tolerance.\n\nEvery SFX id 1..=32 and every song 1..=7 will be non-silent. Each speaker will use a different base frequency so the sounds differ. Syllables will be two sine waves. The mixer will handle SFX, syllables, music, big splashes, and wake events separately.\n\nplay_event and AudioOut::play_event will detect Music events and send Cmd::Song. The Mixer needs a Cmd::MusicGain command for bus gain. The App reads the music field from the status JSON each frame while the fit is active and calls set_music_gain with that value.\n\nAudioOut will gain set_music and set_voice methods. The audio unit test will exercise Mixer directly rather than through the app. Songs will be simple loops of notes at a BPM. Each render pass advances the song clock and triggers notes either by short voices or a dedicated oscillator state to avoid voice explosion.\n\nA sample-accurate oscillator inside the mixer will generate the current song. This avoids spawning voices and keeps the render cheap and deterministic.\n\nSong 6 is the credits track and song 7 is a stinger. Song 0 stays silent. Each song uses a distinct frequency so they are distinguishable.\n\nSFX 32 patches will each use a distinct frequency. Voice formants are two sine waves at fixed frequencies, and speaker waveforms differ because base pitch multipliers vary by speaker. BigSplash and Wake visuals will be added to fx.rs, and water dents will be generated in build.rs. The Input struct is gaining new fields: fit mode, a ramped lean vector, the last device that wrote lean, and raw pad input.\n\nInput gains a `mouse_px` field for the any gesture. The fit layout maps South to Confirm, East to Back, West to Wave, North to Schedule, L1 and R1 to Step Left and Right, D-pad directions to Menu navigation, Start to Pause, and L2/R2 to Step Left and Right. In fit mode, raw pad stick values are stored before deadzone filtering.\n\nIn fit mode, pad rotation and zoom are disabled. Start no longer opens the engine menu; it only pauses. The Mode button is mapped to Create/Guide, and holding it prevents Start from pausing. The App frame will set input.fit to true and apply Bindings::fit() every frame after room rebinds, suppress Escape and Start from opening menus, hide UI chrome during drawing, build lean and device data into InputFrame, and publish the weblink.\n\nThe fit override will run after the room rebind block, forcing fit mode on and hiding the boot screen and panel while it is active. It resets to default bindings when fit ends. The Escape handler will skip opening the menu during fit mode.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-610cb1f4-8006-43b0-b3fb-d579c9541ee8-65","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn handle_key|input\\.key\\(","glob":"**/pav_app/src/app.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-610cb1f4-8006-43b0-b3fb-d579c9541ee8-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/lib.rs","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-610cb1f4-8006-43b0-b3fb-d579c9541ee8-67","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":740,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":786,"output_tokens":3166,"cache_read_input_tokens":119168,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"f48e7882-806e-4f6d-adf0-bdf9f45ba842"}
