{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_262","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The packer reads web/index.html.\n\nI'll modify web/index.html for the game shell. tools/build.sh will insert session.js into a placeholder script tag before packing, then run build-web.sh.\n\nsession.js is 16707 bytes. I'll use a `<!--SESSION-->` marker in index.html and have tools/build.sh inject the exact IIFE before packing. The packed page must contain session.js byte-for-byte.\n\nA Python script will generate the head section of index.html from hub/session.js. The generated file will be committed so packing works immediately. I also need to check session.js for any `</script` tags that could break the HTML.\n\nThe About screen must display the `__gameBoot.about` text. The current sim's about_page is a hardcoded const, so I need to wire the boot data into the About flow.\n\nThe sim cannot read JavaScript directly. The importer edits the HTML about-data block, so the running game must display that HTML text rather than a hardcoded copy baked into the WASM. I am weighing three approaches: duplicating the text in both the HTML and the wasm const, having the UI painter read __gameBoot.about during the About screen, or using an app-level field to pass the string.\n\nI'll add an `about_extra` field to FitGame. The app will set it once from the boot JSON, and the About banner will display that text split into pages. Calling host.exec once at startup is acceptable; doing it per frame is discouraged.\n\nDuplicating the feedback text in both the hardcoded const and the HTML about-data block would break the importer's later edit, so that approach is rejected. Instead, the app will read `about_text` from the boot JSON once via weblink, and the UI painter will draw it as FitUi lines during the About screen.\n\nI'll duplicate the feedback text in both the hardcoded `about_page` strings and the HTML `about-data` JSON. This satisfies the requirement that the About screen, exit-interview, and chat all display the same source information.\n\nThe game will read `__gameBoot.about` from the window at runtime. The sim's hardcoded About text stays for build-time visibility, while the HTML `about-data` block is reserved for the importer to edit.\n\nThe painter cannot access the boot text directly. I will add a `pub about_note: String` field to `FitGame`, defaulting to empty. The app will set it once via `host.exec` from the boot JSON. During the About screen, if the note is non-empty, the banner will display it as an extra line; otherwise it falls back to the hardcoded const.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8f9c943e-3a4d-4c0d-abe6-87f55b386a3d-78","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ACT_XBOX|xbox|fn screen_items|Settings","glob":"**/games/fit/mod.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4383,"output_tokens":1510,"cache_read_input_tokens":128640,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"f81f74f4-5e17-4f6f-b8df-a1636e30d1ef"}
