2,99,111,110,115,116,32,116,121,112,105,99,97,108,32,61,32,78,117,109,98,101,114,40,109,105,110,117,116,101,115,41,59,10,51,52,50,58,32,32,32,32,116,111,80,114,101,115,101,110,116,40,123,32,116,121,112,101,58,32,39,116,105,109,101,45,117,112,39,44,32,103,114,97,99,101,77,115,58,32,116,46,103,114,97,99,101,77,115,32,125,41,59,10,51,52,51,58,32,32,32,32,108,97,116,101,114,40,116,46,103,114,97,99,101,77,115,44,32,40,41,32,61,62,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":6,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/hub/round.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":21,\"content\":\"  graceMs: 5_000,\"},{\"line_number\":60,\"content\":\"/** A round's hard cap: half again its declared length, never past 15 minutes; the longest when it declares none. */\"},{\"line_number\":61,\"content\":\"export function limitFor(minutes, { maxRoundMs = TIMINGS.maxRoundMs } = {}) {\"},{\"line_number\":62,\"content\":\"  const typical = Number(minutes);\"},{\"line_number\":342,\"content\":\"    toPresent({ type: 'time-up', graceMs: t.graceMs });\"},{\"line_number\":343,\"content\":\"    later(t.graceMs, () => {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"8dfdc1a9-1e97-4687-be2d-051401aa68f8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_267","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The limit is half again the declared length.\n\nThe harness only pokes for six seconds. It cannot finish the round. Memory is tight. The hub should auto-complete with the bot so the round ends quickly.\n\nThe harness iframe may be slow at 320x180. The prior run finished in 14–19 seconds, so the game likely reported results quickly or the hub time was short.\n\nThe prior 14–19 second run used the exact same JavaScript block. The game must have reported results quickly because the code checks `s.done` to trigger `report()`. A full medley run would take roughly 2.5 minutes at 60 fps. The harness only pokes for six seconds before waiting for the state record.\n\nThe harness waits for the full round limit unless a result arrives. Auto-botting the hub would steal player control, and the paddle event alone lasts 45 seconds. A fast time scale or generous scoring may be needed to finish in about fifteen seconds.\n\nA high time scale would let the round finish in fifteen seconds, but it would freeze player input. The prior fast run may have used a stub that sets done immediately rather than a full game. I will keep the JavaScript unchanged.\n\nRandom arrow keys cannot finish the paddle event in six seconds. The test will time out and report a zero score. A zero score is likely valid, so the harness may pass without auto-botting.\n\nThe plan requires the meta tag to read exactly 3 minutes. I will not change it to 0.2 minutes. The exact JavaScript block must remain unchanged, so I cannot alter the report timing.\n\nA hub time scale of twenty would compress the full medley to roughly ten seconds. Events end when their duration expires even if the player fails them.\n\nA time_scale of twenty would make the round finish in about twenty seconds, but that would freeze player input and break real sessions. The harness uses bot_input() with press_bits, while live play relies on player input.\n\nI will run the four harnesses sequentially rather than in parallel to avoid exhausting memory. Four WebGPU contexts may still trigger an out-of-memory kill. I will proceed and note any failure. Random keys during events still trigger lean, but events finish by timeout even if the player cannot complete them.\n\nThe hub clock runs on wall time, not simulation time. A slow iframe at 20 fps could stretch the full medley to several minutes. The harness will still wait for the four-and-a-half-minute limit unless the game reports done earlier. The cleanest fix is to keep the hub time scale at one and make the events short enough to finish within that window.\n\nChanging event durations would break core tests. The plan is to set `time_scale` to 8.0 in `pre()` when the hub starts, which compresses events by eight times without freezing player input. A fast-motion session is acceptable for the demo.\n\nThe plan expects a two-minute round, so a twelve-fold speedup is too extreme for human play. I will keep the time scale at one and run the full four-and-a-half minute tests. If that is too slow, I can lower the meta tag to one minute while still satisfying the numeric requirement. Another option is to trigger hub.done after a few seconds of hub play, which would end the round early and let the harness finish in about fifteen seconds, though the score might be partial.\n\nI will not artificially end the round early. The plan requires the full medley to complete for a valid score. I will keep the session length at three minutes as specified.\n\nA thirty-fold time scale would finish the medley in seconds, but it would freeze player input and make hub sessions unplayable. The natural tick_activity path keeps events at roughly two and a half minutes.\n\nI will drive the hub with the bot instead of the player. The harness sends random keys that would override the bot's lean, so ignoring player input in hub mode is necessary for a reliable score. The 4.5-minute wall-time cap remains as a fallback.\n\nI will not replace player input with bot controls. The harness will score zero at the time-up and pass. I may lower the session minutes to 0.15 so the round finishes in about thirteen seconds, while keeping the medley itself unchanged.\n\nI will keep the session length at three minutes. I am starting to write files in batches now, beginning with audio music gain and sound effects.\n\nI will add a `music` module to `pav_audio/src/lib.rs` and create `music.rs`. I also need to write tests for audio and UI. The test runner script must suppress cargo's default summary output. I will run `cargo test -q` on `pav_core`, `pav_audio`, and `pav_ui`.\n\nThe test runner script will strip cargo's default summary lines so only failures remain. The status tick signature is being updated to accept the simulation state. Camera yaw from the HUD will be synced into session data and applied after rig updates in the app.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7b78aa6b-a140-4416-91b3-a0f0d8d8c3e5-84","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_tools/src/session.rs","offset":230,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7b78aa6b-a140-4416-91b3-a0f0d8d8c3e5-85","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs","offset":520,"limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":657,"output_tokens":3213,"cache_read_input_tokens":141312,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"c06a6c31-f929-4279-8089-47e627460664"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7b78aa6b-a140-4416-91b3-a0f0d8d8c3e5-84","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"230→                    for sw in &cue.sweep {\\n                        set.insert(sw.param.clone(), ParamValue::Float(sw.from as f64));\\n                    }\\n                    if let Some(y) = set.get(\\\"yaw\\\").and_then(|v| v.as_f64()) {\\n                        set.insert(\\\"yaw\\\".into(), rot(y, q));\\n                    }\\n                    self.camera.params = base;\\n                    apply_map(&mut self.camera.params, &set);\\n                }\\n                None => {\\n240→                    if let Some(b) = self.cue_base.take() {\\n                        self.camera.params = b;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        // Room changes after cues (leaving a room clears its cue first, then restores the camera).\\n        if now != self.room_cam.as_ref().map(|r| r.0) {\\n            if let Some((_, saved)) = self.room_cam.take() {\\n                self.camera.params = saved;\\n250→            }\\n            if let Some(r) = now.and_then(|i| w.rooms.get(i as usize)).filter(|r| !r.def.camera.is_empty()) {\\n                let saved = self.camera.params.clone();\\n                let mut cam = r.def.camera.clone();\\n                let yaw = cam.get(\\\"yaw\\\").and_then(|v| v.as_f64()).unwrap_or(0.0);\\n                cam.insert(\\\"yaw\\\".into(), rot(yaw, r.place.quarters));\\n                apply_map(&mut self.camera.params, &cam);\\n                self.room_cam = Some((r.id, saved));\\n            }\\n        }\\n260→        self.sync_view();\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Takes `params` as the base camera and applies the current room's `[camera]` on top.\\n    pub fn reset_camera(&mut self, params: CameraParams) {\\n        self.camera.params = params;\\n        self.room_cam = None;\\n        self.cue_base = None;\\n        self.sync_camera();\\n    }\\n270→\\n    /// The camera without the current room's defaults.\\n    pub fn camera_base_or_current(&self) -> CameraParams {\\n        self.room_cam.as_ref().map(|(_, c)| c.clone()).unwrap_or_else(|| self.camera.params.clone())\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The view settings without the current room's / pads' overrides.\\n    pub fn view_base_or_current(&self) -> ViewSettings {\\n        self.view_base.clone().unwrap_or_else(|| self.view.clone())\\n    }\\n280→\\n    /// Takes `view` as the base settings and applies the current room's `[view]` table on top.\\n    pub fn reset_view(&mut self, view: ViewSettings) {\\n        self.view = view;\\n        self.view_base = None;\\n        self.view_room = None;\\n        self.view_serial = u64::MAX;\\n        self.sync_view();\\n    }\\n\\n290→    /// Room `[view]` tables and pad `view.*` overrides, like the game applies them.\\n    fn sync_view(&mut self) {\\n        let w = &self.sim.state.world;\\n        let now = w.current_room;\\n        let serial = self.sim.state.courses.view_serial;\\n        if now == self.view_room && serial == self.view_serial {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        if let Some(base) = self.view_base.take() {\\n            self.view = base;\\n300→        }\\n        self.view_room = now;\\n        self.view_serial = serial;\\n        let q = now.and_then(|i| w.rooms.get(i as usize)).map(|r| r.place.quarters).unwrap_or(0);\\n        let room =\\n            now.and_then(|i| w.rooms.get(i as usize)).map(|r| pav_view::build::room_view_map(&r.def.view, q)).unwrap_or_default();\\n        let pads = pav_view::build::room_view_map(&self.sim.state.courses.view, q);\\n        if room.is_empty() && pads.is_empty() {\\n            return;\\n        }\",\"content_concise\":\"230→                    for sw in &cue.sweep {\\n                        set.insert(sw.param.clone(), ParamValue::Float(sw.from as f64));\\n                    }\\n                    if let Some(y) = set.get(\\\"yaw\\\").and_then(|v| v.as_f64()) {\\n                        set.insert(\\\"yaw\\\".into(), rot(y, q));\\n                    }\\n                    self.camera.params = base;\\n                    apply_map(&mut self.camera.params, &set);\\n                }\\n                None => {\\n240→                    if let Some(b) = self.cue_base.take() {\\n                        self.camera.params = b;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        // Room changes after cues (leaving a room clears its cue first, then restores the camera).\\n        if now != self.room_cam.as_ref().map(|r| r.0) {\\n            if let Some((_, saved)) = self.room_cam.take() {\\n                self.camera.params = saved;\\n250→            }\\n            if let Some(r) = now.and_then(|i| w.rooms.get(i as usize)).filter(|r| !r.def.camera.is_empty()) {\\n                let saved = self.camera.params.clone();\\n                let mut cam = r.def.camera.clone();\\n                let yaw = cam.get(\\\"yaw\\\").and_then(|v| v.as_f64()).unwrap_or(0.0);\\n                cam.insert(\\\"yaw\\\".into(), rot(yaw, r.place.quarters));\\n                apply_map(&mut self.camera.params, &cam);\\n                self.room_cam = Some((r.id, saved));\\n            }\\n        }\\n260→        self.sync_view();\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Takes `params` as the base camera and applies the current room's `[camera]` on top.\\n    pub fn reset_camera(&mut self, params: CameraParams) {\\n        self.camera.params = params;\\n        self.room_cam = None;\\n        self.cue_base = None;\\n        self.sync_camera();\\n    }\\n270→\\n    /// The camera without the current room's defaults.\\n    pub fn camera_base_or_current(&self) -> CameraParams {\\n        self.room_cam.as_ref().map(|(_, c)| c.clone()).unwrap_or_else(|| self.camera.params.clone())\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The view settings without the current room's / pads' overrides.\\n    pub fn view_base_or_current(&self) -> ViewSettings {\\n        self.view_base.clone().unwrap_or_else(|| self.view.clone())\\n    }\\n280→\\n    /// Takes `view` as the base settings and applies the current room's `[view]` table on top.\\n    pub fn reset_view(&mut self, view: ViewSettings) {\\n        self.view = view;\\n        self.view_base = None;\\n        self.view_room = None;\\n        self.view_serial = u64::MAX;\\n        self.sync_view();\\n    }\\n\\n290→    /// Room `[view]` tables and pad `view.*` overrides, like the game applies them.\\n    fn sync_view(&mut self) {\\n        let w = &self.sim.state.world;\\n        let now = w.current_room;\\n        let serial = self.sim.state.courses.view_serial;\\n        if now == self.view_room && serial == self.view_serial {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        if let Some(base) = self.view_base.take() {\\n            self.view = base;\\n300→        }\\n        self.view_room = now;\\n        self.view_serial = serial;\\n        let q = now.and_then(|i| w.rooms.get(i as usize)).map(|r| r.place.quarters).unwrap_or(0);\\n        let room =\\n            now.and_then(|i| w.rooms.get(i as usize)).map(|r| pav_view::build::room_view_map(&r.def.view, q)).unwrap_or_default();\\n        let pads = pav_view::build::room_view_map(&self.sim.state.courses.view, q);\\n        if room.is_empty() && pads.is_empty() {\\n            return;\\n        }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_tools/src/session.rs\",\"offset\":230,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"                    for sw in &cue.sweep {\\n                        set.insert(sw.param.clone(), ParamValue::Float(sw.from as f64));\\n                    }\\n                    if let Some(y) = set.get(\\\"yaw\\\").and_then(|v| v.as_f64()) {\\n                        set.insert(\\\"yaw\\\".into(), rot(y, q));\\n                    }\\n                    self.camera.params = base;\\n                    apply_map(&mut self.camera.params, &set);\\n                }\\n                None => {\\n                    if let Some(b) = self.cue_base.take() {\\n                        self.camera.params = b;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        // Room changes after cues (leaving a room clears its cue first, then restores the camera).\\n        if now != self.room_cam.as_ref().map(|r| r.0) {\\n            if let Some((_, saved)) = self.room_cam.take() {\\n                self.camera.params = saved;\\n            }\\n            if let Some(r) = now.and_then(|i| w.rooms.get(i as usize)).filter(|r| !r.def.camera.is_empty()) {\\n                let saved = self.camera.params.clone();\\n                let mut cam = r.def.camera.clone();\\n                let yaw = cam.get(\\\"yaw\\\").and_then(|v| v.as_f64()).unwrap_or(0.0);\\n                cam.insert(\\\"yaw\\\".into(), rot(yaw, r.place.quarters));\\n                apply_map(&mut self.camera.params, &cam);\\n                self.room_cam = Some((r.id, saved));\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.sync_view();\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Takes `params` as the base camera and applies the current room's `[camera]` on top.\\n    pub fn reset_camera(&mut self, params: CameraParams) {\\n        self.camera.params = params;\\n        self.room_cam = None;\\n        self.cue_base = None;\\n        self.sync_camera();\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The camera without the current room's defaults.\\n    pub fn camera_base_or_current(&self) -> CameraParams {\\n        self.room_cam.as_ref().map(|(_, c)| c.clone()).unwrap_or_else(|| self.camera.params.clone())\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The view settings without the current room's / pads' overrides.\\n    pub fn view_base_or_current(&self) -> ViewSettings {\\n        self.view_base.clone().unwrap_or_else(|| self.view.clone())\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Takes `view` as the base settings and applies the current room's `[view]` table on top.\\n    pub fn reset_view(&mut self, view: ViewSettings) {\\n        self.view = view;\\n        self.view_base = None;\\n        self.view_room = None;\\n        self.view_serial = u64::MAX;\\n        self.sync_view();\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Room `[view]` tables and pad `view.*` overrides, like the game applies them.\\n    fn sync_view(&mut self) {\\n        let w = &self.sim.state.world;\\n        let now = w.current_room;\\n        let serial = self.sim.state.courses.view_serial;\\n        if now == self.view_room && serial == self.view_serial {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        if let Some(base) = self.view_base.take() {\\n            self.view = base;\\n        }\\n        self.view_room = now;\\n        self.view_serial = serial;\\n        let q = now.and_then(|i| w.rooms.get(i as usize)).map(|r| r.place.quarters).unwrap_or(0);\\n        let room =\\n            now.and_then(|i| w.rooms.get(i as usize)).map(|r| pav_view::build::room_view_map(&r.def.view, q)).unwrap_or_default();\\n        let pads = pav_view::build::room_view_map(&self.sim.state.courses.view, q);\\n        if room.is_empty() && pads.is_empty() {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n\",\"total_lines\":436}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7b78aa6b-a140-4416-91b3-a0f0d8d8c3e5-85","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"520→    fn schedule_events(&self) -> Vec<EventId> {\\n        if self.free_play {\\n            EventId::ALL.into_iter().filter(|e| !matches!(e, EventId::Check | EventId::BigStand)).collect()\\n        } else if self.day >= 5 {\\n            vec![EventId::BigStand]\\n        } else {\\n            EventId::for_day(self.day).to_vec()\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n530→    fn screen_items(&self) -> Vec<(u16, String)> {\\n        let s = self.script();\\n        match self.flow {\\n            Flow::Title => {\\n                let mut v = vec![(ACT_NEW, \\\"New Stay\\\".into())];\\n                if self.slots.iter().any(|sl| sl.used) {\\n                    v.push((ACT_CONTINUE, \\\"Continue\\\".into()));\\n                }\\n                v.push((ACT_TOGETHER, \\\"Play Together\\\".into()));\\n                v.push((ACT_SETTINGS, \\\"Settings\\\".into()));\\n540→                v.push((ACT_ABOUT, \\\"About\\\".into()));\\n                v.push((ACT_HOWTO, \\\"How to Stand\\\".into()));\\n                v\\n            }\\n            Flow::Slots => {\\n                let mut v = Vec::new();\\n                for (i, sl) in self.slots.iter().enumerate().take(4) {\\n                    if self.continuing && !sl.used {\\n                        continue;\\n                    }\\n550→                    let label = if sl.used { format!(\\\"{} · day {}\\\", sl.name, sl.day) } else { format!(\\\"Hammock {} · empty\\\", i + 1) };\\n                    v.push((10 + i as u16, label));\\n                }\\n                v.push((ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into()));\\n                v\\n            }\\n            Flow::Name => s.names.iter().enumerate().map(|(i, n)| (400 + i as u16, n.clone())).take(6).collect(),\\n            Flow::Look => s.skins.iter().enumerate().map(|(i, n)| (500 + i as u16, n.clone())).take(6).collect(),\\n            Flow::Outfit => s.outfits.iter().enumerate().map(|(i, n)| (520 + i as u16, n.clone())).take(6).collect(),\\n            Flow::Schedule => {\\n560→                let evs = self.schedule_events();\\n                let mut v = Vec::new();\\n                for (i, e) in evs.iter().enumerate().take(4) {\\n                    let done = if self.today_played.iter().any(|p| p == e.key()) { \\\" · done\\\" } else { \\\"\\\" };\\n                    v.push((100 + i as u16, format!(\\\"{}{done}\\\", e.title())));\\n                }\\n                if self.day_clear() {\\n                    v.push((ACT_END_DAY, \\\"End the day\\\".into()));\\n                }\\n                v.push((ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into()));\\n570→                v\\n            }\\n            Flow::Result => vec![\\n                (ACT_RESULT_BACK, \\\"Back to the island\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_RETRY, \\\"Retry\\\".into()),\\n            ],\\n            Flow::Together => vec![\\n                (ACT_G2, \\\"2 guests\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_G3, \\\"3 guests\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_G4, \\\"4 guests\\\".into()),\\n580→                (ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into()),\\n            ],\\n            Flow::Settings => self.settings_items(),\\n            Flow::Dev => self.dev_items(),\\n            Flow::Pause => vec![(ACT_RESUME, \\\"Resume\\\".into()), (ACT_SETTINGS, \\\"Settings\\\".into())],\\n            Flow::About | Flow::HowTo | Flow::Wardrobe | Flow::Calendar => vec![(ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into())],\\n            Flow::Attract if self.touch_only => vec![(ACT_SETTINGS, \\\"Settings\\\".into())],\\n            Flow::Podium => vec![(ACT_BACK, \\\"Back to the title\\\".into())],\\n            _ => Vec::new(),\\n        }\\n590→    }\\n\\n    fn settings_items(&self) -> Vec<(u16, String)> {\\n        let m = self.settings.music;\\n        match self.page {\\n            0 => vec![\\n                (610, format!(\\\"Music {:.0}%\\\", m * 100.0)),\\n                (611, format!(\\\"Effects {:.0}%\\\", self.settings.sfx * 100.0)),\\n                (612, format!(\\\"Voices {:.0}%\\\", self.settings.voice * 100.0)),\\n                (ACT_XBOX, if self.settings.xbox { \\\"Glyphs: Xbox\\\" } else { \\\"Glyphs: PlayStation\\\" }.into()),\\n600→                (613, format!(\\\"Lean {:.0}%\\\", self.settings.sensitivity * 100.0)),\\n                (ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into()),\\n            ],\\n            _ => vec![\\n                (614, format!(\\\"Wobble assist {:.0}%\\\", self.settings.wobble_assist * 100.0)),\\n                (615, \\\"Rhythm offset\\\".into()),\\n                (616, format!(\\\"Text {:.1}\\\", self.settings.text_speed)),\\n                (ACT_FULLSCREEN, if self.settings.fullscreen { \\\"Fullscreen on\\\" } else { \\\"Fullscreen off\\\" }.into()),\\n                (ACT_RESET_SAVE, if self.reset_arm { \\\"Confirm erase\\\" } else { \\\"Erase save\\\" }.into()),\\n                (ACT_BACK, \\\"Back\\\".into()),\\n610→            ],\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn dev_items(&self) -> Vec<(u16, String)> {\\n        match self.page {\\n            0 => vec![\\n                (ACT_RESUME, \\\"Resume\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_DEV_RESET, \\\"Reset feel\\\".into()),\\n                (43, \\\"Wardrobe\\\".into()),\\n620→                (44, \\\"Calendar\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_SETTINGS, \\\"Settings\\\".into()),\\n                (ACT_ABOUT, \\\"About\\\".into()),\\n            ],\\n            _ => {\\n                let mut rules = self.rules.clone();\\n                let infos = params::list(&mut rules);\\n                let start = (self.page - 1) * 4;\\n                let mut v: Vec<(u16, String)> = infos\\n                    .iter()\\n630→                    .enumerate()\\n                    .skip(start)\\n                    .take(4)\\n                    .map(|(i, info)| {\\n                        let label = match &info.value {\\n                            ParamValue::Float(f) => format!(\\\"{} {f:.2}\\\", info.path),\\n                            ParamValue::Int(n) => format!(\\\"{} {n}\\\", info.path),\\n                            _ => info.path.clone(),\\n                        };\\n                        (300 + i as u16, label)\",\"content_concise\":\"520→    fn schedule_events(&self) -> Vec<EventId> {\\n        if self.free_play {\\n            EventId::ALL.into_iter().filter(|e| !matches!(e, EventId::Check | EventId::BigStand)).collect()\\n        } else if self.day >= 5 {\\n            vec![EventId::BigStand]\\n        } else {\\n            EventId::for_day(self.day).to_vec()\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n530→    fn screen_items(&self) -> Vec<(u16, String)> {\\