e(),\\n                        };\\n                        (300 + i as u16, label)\\n\",\"total_lines\":1852}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"5f82b8f3-d572-48d1-a527-0da1e76e0f5d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_268","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plan is set. I am ready to write code.\n\nI will write the core files in large chunks. The UI changes include a painter, fonts, and tests in `fit.rs`, plus updates to `lib.rs`, headless setup, `has_ui`, and `input.rs` for gamepad bindings. I am also checking button constants and confirming slider behavior.\n\nI am now planning the remaining files: app.rs, weblink.rs, main.rs, audio, effects, build, status tick, settings boot, index.html, and tests. I also noticed a headless font timing issue: set_fonts only takes effect on the next pass, so text might panic on the first pass before the last pass tessellates it.\n\nI will install fonts once before the headless loop and warm up the UI. Calling set_fonts inside game_lines every pass would reset the font timer and leave the last pass without fonts. Default fonts prevent panics, but custom families will crash.\n\nI will use Nunito as the proportional font and Fredoka by name. The install_fonts function will always register fonts, relying on a warmup run_ui to let egui process them before the loop begins.\n\nThe painter will enforce a 1080p baseline for text sizing. Titles scale to 64 points at full resolution and shrink proportionally at lower resolutions. Body text scales to 34 points at 1080p and scales down accordingly.\n\nI am writing unit tests for the fit helper. One test will verify that title text is at least 64 points at 1920x1080. I am also drafting a prompt test to check that each device type shows the correct button label.\n\nThe prompt test will render each device type at 1920x1080 and assert that the HUD reading contains the expected button label. The painter draws both the glyph and footer text. I am now updating `game_lines`.\n\nI am wiring the fit painter into `game_lines` and adding a guard so boot, stats, guide, card, hint, feel, course HUD, and the F1 panel are skipped when `fit_ui` is active. I will clone `curr.hud.fit` before the closure to check it cheaply. The input frame construction is the next tricky piece.\n\nI am adding a `fit_frame` method to `Input` that returns lean, device, any input, UI state, and movement direction for the fit loop. I will also store total mouse movement per frame in a new `moved` field and add a `consume_motion` helper. For the fit sample logic, I will track lean ramp state with `lean_ramp` and `lean_from`, then compute stick and key directions from raw pad and keyboard inputs.\n\nI am resolving the sign convention for keyboard lean. Screen space Y points down, so I will flip the cursor offset to make up positive, matching gilrs stick conventions.\n\nI am finalizing the fit input logic. The lean ramp will decay to zero when keys are released. The `any` flag will be true for pressed buttons, stick movement over 0.3, mouse motion over 6 pixels, or left clicks. The last active device will be tracked by comparing stick length, key direction, and mouse movement.\n\nI am finalizing the fit input rules. The `any` flag will be true for pressed buttons, stick movement over 0.3, mouse motion over 6 pixels, or left clicks. A device 4 click will reset idle state only on `Click` events, not on wake. Mouse primary is mapped to `PRIMARY` rather than `CONFIRM`, so a click will not accidentally trigger confirmation.\n\nHover will be set every frame while the cursor is over an item and no button is held.\n\nI am also adding a `HubSample` struct in `weblink::sample()` that returns game state, completion status, today’s goal, about text, and a touch-only flag. When serial data changes, the host will export it and save it to localStorage.\n\nI will read localStorage on boot and import saved data, but I must avoid breaking tests because native builds lack that API. I am updating the audio command system and adding a BigSplash sound before the wildcard match arm. I will add tests for music gain ratios and verify that SFX IDs 1–32, songs 1–7, and syllables are distinct. For Patch formants, I will use two extra sine voices inside the syllable arm instead of adding new Patch fields.\n\nI am working out how to apply voice gain to syllable patches. The mixer currently only knows SFX gain, so I need a way to pass the voice gain into `play_event` for syllables while keeping music separate.\n\nI will add a `voice_gain` field to `AudioOut` and set it through `Cmd::Bus`. In `play_event`, syllables will be multiplied by this gain while music and other events keep the SFX gain. This avoids changing the mixer's existing SFX-only interface.\n\nMusic will stay silent by default so the explosion test still passes. Song 0 adds zero gain, and the peak is kept near 1 around 0.5 so 0.10 yields roughly 0.05 after tanh. The tests/run.sh script will be rewritten to run from the engine directory. PROGRESS.md will be updated as work proceeds.\n\nI will write a brief PROGRESS.md now and update it later. I am checking the buttons module for bit names and deferring checkbox flipping to the goal plan checklist. I have enough context to begin writing code. In app.rs, I will insert fit handling into the InputFrame block and gate start_pressed so it only triggers the menu when fit is not active.\n\nI noticed the fit flag is read from the previous frame's HUD, so the first fit frame may be missed. The Start menu toggle currently runs before `curr` is read, which means one frame could open the engine menu while fit is active. I will move that check to after the fit state is known, or store the previous HUD on `App` to avoid the lag.\n\nI will move the Start menu toggle to after `curr` is loaded, so it only fires when fit mode is known. A `fit_mode` flag will be updated from `hud.fit` to prevent one frame of lag. Escape handling is next.\n\nI am adding fit-mode guards to the remaining input handlers. Keyboard events are blocked while `fit` is active, except for F11 and F12. Right-click drag, mouse wheel, and rewind logic are all gated behind `!self.input.fit`. Touch events will always route to egui during fit mode.\n\nTouch-end events will store the click position and route to egui. On WASM, a `coarse_only` flag will be set by checking media queries for `(pointer: coarse)` while ensuring no fine pointer exists.\n\nA `real_device` flag will track keyboard or pad activity to clear the coarse-only assumption when input arrives. After the UI, the simulation status JSON will include a tick field and be published as a string for the hub.\n\nI will expose the UI array as `window.__gameUi` by parsing the JSON into a real JavaScript array, and set `window.__gameStatus` to the raw status string. I need to verify whether tests access `.tick` directly on that string or expect it parsed first.\n\nI will keep the hub IIFE unchanged and set `__gameStatus` to a raw JSON string. This avoids a conflict with the plan's exact-block requirement, though tests may need to parse the string themselves.\n\nI will set `window.__gameStatus` to a raw JSON string so the hub script's `JSON.parse` still works. Browser tests will verify the tick field by parsing that string themselves. I considered exposing a parsed object as well, but that would require extra documentation.\n\nI am exploring a JavaScript String object for `__gameStatus`. JSON.parse coerces it to the raw string, so the hub script still works. I can also attach `.tick` directly to the object. I need to check if js-sys exposes the String constructor.\n\nI will create a JavaScript String object from the JSON string and attach `.tick` to it via `Reflect.set`. The hub script's `JSON.parse` still works because a String object coerces to its raw content. I am checking whether a String object is truthy.\n\nI will add a label field to each UI item. The about page will be expanded with fuller feedback, keeping the UI to four pages rather than a scrolling wall; page two gets more content and page one gains a source line. The exit interview and chat sections will receive the full feedback text.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a2958a29-4d40-4947-ad75-932da947624d-86","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"struct HudFrame","glob":"**/pav_core/src/frame.rs","-A":35}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5671,"output_tokens":4660,"cache_read_input_tokens":141952,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"5fdd1888-bd8f-4777-8c94-4673523f563d"}
