32,115,116,114,117,99,116,32,67,111,117,114,115,101,72,117,100,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/feel.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":9,\"content\":\"pub struct FeelReport {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/course.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":62,\"content\":\"pub struct CourseHud {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"799688b1-4cce-4698-8dfc-a96b2e6c1427"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_271","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The UI test will live in `pav_ui` and call `fit::draw`.\n\nThe test will use `pav_core::Sim::new(\"fit\", seed)` to generate a real HUD frame. It will then pass that frame to `Headless::frame` for rendering.\n\nThe title screen will display \"Wobble Minutes\" and \"New Stay\". The footer will show \"Cross\" because the default device is 0. A fresh simulation frame already contains the correct HUD state, so no extra input is needed.\n\nThe test must live in `pav_ui` because `Headless` is defined there and `pav_core` does not depend on it. `Sim::new` and `frame` are public, so the test can build a fit simulation directly.\n\nHeadless rendering will warm up fonts before drawing. The camera yaw will be synced from the HUD frame at the end of `sync_camera`. `Sim::frame()` is cheap enough to call for this purpose.\n\nThe camera yaw sync will read `game.fit_ui` directly instead of calling `frame()`. This avoids duplicating render work. The app camera rig yaw will be set from the HUD state.\n\nThe camera yaw will only be overwritten during a lap. If the HUD yaw is None, the existing value is preserved.\n\nThe core UI test will use Slider events instead of mouse dragging. This keeps the test self-contained within the simulation.\n\nA `tick` field will be added to the status struct. The parameter name in the constructor will change to match.\n\nMusic events will be handled directly in both `play_event` functions. This prevents them from falling through to `sounds_for` and ensures the active song is set correctly.\n\n`render_events` will route through `play_event`, so the active song is set correctly for tests. `Mixer` will expose `set_song` and `set_gains` for test access. Each song will use a distinct BPM and root frequency to keep them non-silent and distinguishable.\n\nSong 7 is the final song index. Higher indices wrap to 1. Each song uses a distinct envelope and root frequency. SFX patches use five waveforms: sine, square, triangle, saw, and noise. The frequency scales with the effect ID.\n\nSFX patches now include glide, decay, and cutoff parameters that vary by effect ID. The syllable function defines base frequencies for five speakers and scales them by pitch.\n\nSyllable synthesis uses three sine and sawtooth patches with speaker-specific formants. The test will render two different speakers and assert their audio samples differ. BigSplash noise bursts scale volume with size.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3fc24b2d-a9ab-46b6-888f-f570da179aa9-89","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn shipped_text|Source:|wii","glob":"**/tests/fit.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":431,"output_tokens":2079,"cache_read_input_tokens":152960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"9a0d4e31-8b2c-447d-98fe-27b4e4b2ac8e"}
