{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_276","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking whether the App struct has a place to add fields.\n\nDeciding between adding fields to the App struct or storing fit state on Input to avoid struct changes. Audio bus values can be read from status JSON each frame. The save serial will be compared against a stored value.\n\nAdding fields to the App struct and updating its literal. The new fields will be inserted just before the fatal field. A `FitSample` struct and a `fit_axes` method in input.rs will handle fit input.\n\nThe `fit_sample` method will take UI items and a click flag. Device codes are assigned based on input history: coarse non-real devices get 4, gamepads get 1, mouse or lean input gets 3, and touch gets 2. Real device detection is set by key presses and pad activity, while touch does not trigger it.\n\nTouch moves will not count as input when the device is coarse non-real. Touch clicks still trigger UI events.\n\nThe `any` flag will be computed before clearing button taps, since `buttons()` consumes them.\n\nThe app will clone the fit state and set `input.fit` at the start of the fit input block.\n\nThe fit binding override must run before `buttons()` so the fit controls take effect. It will be inserted immediately after the game_mode block and before the button handling. Room rebinds happen only on room changes, so this per-frame override will not conflict with them.\n\nThe fit binding override will be placed immediately before `buttons()` is called. After button processing, the lean vector will be reshaped and the input lock contents replaced when fit is active. The primary mouse button must also be cleared so it does not trigger bomb throws. The InputFrame sent to the simulation still carries game pre() buttons, while the player character input is handled separately.\n\nThe InputFrame sent to FitGame::pre will carry lean, buttons, device, ui, any, hub, and move_dir. FitGame does not need the PRIMARY button from mouse clicks, since held() always sets it for left-clicked buttons. The fit bindings already provide CONFIRM and other required inputs.\n\nMouse clicks will correctly exit attract mode because the left button sets PRIMARY, which makes woke() true. The fit device code remains 3 rather than 4.\n\nFor island movement, move_dir should be set from the rig relative_move of the key axis, matching existing WASD walking behavior. The app currently lacks easy access to the flow state needed to apply this.\n\nThe hub field will be read from the status JSON each frame in wasm, while native builds keep it at zero. The song_pos field is optional and can remain empty for tests.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4f4bbedd-93a7-436f-93a6-157d84940cba-95","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn exec\\(","glob":"**/pav_app/src/simhost.rs","-A":12}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1187,"output_tokens":1499,"cache_read_input_tokens":157952,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"9250d6af-069a-4376-b090-3ab2ee8a3842"}
