{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_279","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will wire save on serial change.\n\nI'm writing the code now. I'll update index.html and add a build script placeholder for session.js.\n\nI'll inject session.js into index.html via a Python one-liner during the build. I'll also add a JSON object for about-data that the build script will overwrite from the exit-interview.\n\nThe Hub IIFE will be copied exactly from PLAN.md. session.js will be inserted byte-for-byte without modification. The fit poll D-pad layout is being drafted with South for confirm, East for back, and West for wave.\n\nThe fit poll D-pad layout now includes North for schedule, triggers for step, and D-pad for menu navigation. Start pauses the game unless Mode is held. The pad rotation and zoom are reset to zero.\n\nI'll set `pad.start_pressed` after the fit branch so it stays false during fit polls. Raw left stick values will be stored on `Pad` for fit sampling, while deadzoned values remain for normal play.\n\nI'll detect stick-as-menu edges in fit_sample by comparing the Y-axis to 0.55 and returning extra pressed bits for menu up and down. The app will OR these into the input frame. I also need to account for gilrs negating the Y-axis sign.\n\nI'll support both browser and gilrs stick conventions for menu navigation. The harness uses keys rather than the stick, but I'll map D-pad via the button map and treat |Y| > 0.5 as menu movement to cover both axis sign conventions.\n\nThe D-pad is the reliable menu path. I'll map stick Y to menu up and down based on sign, and flip the direction if the test fails.\n\nI confirmed gilrs web maps LeftStickY as negative, so stick down is MENU_DOWN and up is MENU_UP. ArrowDown is already bound to MENU_DOWN for keyboard focus. I'll publish rects for mouse input.\n\nMenu items are mapped to IDs: New Stay 1, Play Together 3, Settings 4, About 5, and How to Stand 6. Clicking Settings will activate the settings screen.\n\nThe attract mode must idle for exactly ten seconds. The test must avoid sending input so the simulation stays idle. Mouse travel should only be counted when the cursor actually moves.\n\nMouse travel will only be counted after the first frame to avoid a load-time move resetting attract mode.\n\nA touch card overlay will appear for coarse pointers. It contains text and a Settings button. Tapping it sets window.__fitClick to 4. Rust reads this value, sends Click(4), and clears it. The in-game attract screen also shows a Settings item for touch-only users.\n\nThe touch card text is present in the DOM before WASM loads, so the test can locate it immediately. It appears only when coarse input is detected and fine input is absent, then hides on any keydown.\n\nThe attract card will be a centered panel behind the canvas, not an opaque overlay. Pointer events will only apply to the card itself.\n\nThe WebGPU missing message will combine the coarse-input warning with the browser requirement. On WebKit iPhone, both phrases appear together.\n\nThe catalogue title will be \"Wobble Minutes — a balance holiday\". The theme color is lagoon #1f8a8a. An inline SVG data-uri icon will be added to the HTML head. The manifest file may be removed.\n\nThe manifest link will stay because the packer strips it. Phone rotation and fullscreen blocks are being removed. The canvas already fills the viewport via CSS, so no extra sizing note is needed.\n\nA Python Playwright script for browser testing will be written after the HTML build. The work order is: Rust changes first, then sequential cargo tests, then compile fixes, then the web page and build script, then the long WASM build, then browser and hub, captures, and hand-in.\n\nI will delete the target directory at the end of the build. I am adding audio and UI tests before compiling. For headless warmup, frame() will install fonts and run one empty UI pass first so subsequent passes have them ready. The game lines use the Fredoka font name.\n\nI am writing the Painter draw function. It scales content to fit the viewport while keeping a 1920×1080 base ratio, clamped to 0.05. Title text is 64 pixels and body text is 34 pixels, both scaled by that factor. The painter targets a custom foreground layer named \"wobble\". It begins with a dimming pass and then sets up the Fredoka font for the title.\n\nThe Painter now uses Nunito for body text. It draws the title galley with white color. For each item it scales the rect by viewport width and height, fills a white card, and marks the focused item.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2b1cd1c5-13b9-43c8-806e-ccb2827aec85-98","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn rect_filled|fn rect_stroke|enum StrokeKind","path":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/egui-0.36.2/src/painter.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":417,"output_tokens":3056,"cache_read_input_tokens":161536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"c49957e4-6314-493c-8a70-ff3fbd6a5247"}
