04,111,119,95,103,117,105,100,101,32,38,38,32,115,101,108,102,46,115,116,97,114,116,101,100,46,101,108,97,112,115,101,100,40,41,46,97,115,95,115,101,99,115,95,102,51,50,40,41,32,60,32,50,53,46,48,32,38,38,32,33,99,97,114,100,95,118,105,115,105,98,108,101,59,10,49,52,50,48,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,105,102,32,103,117,105,100,101,95,118,105,115,105,98,108,101,32,38,38,32,33,109,101,110,117,95,111,112,101,110,32,38,38,32,33,116,111,117,99,104,95,117,105,32,123,10,49,52,51,57,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,105,102,32,99,97,114,100,95,118,105,115,105,98,108,101,32,38,38,32,33,109,101,110,117,95,111,112,101,110,32,38,38,32,104,117,100,46,99,97,114,100,40,38,99,116,120,44,32,100,101,118,105,99,101,41,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":6,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":347,\"content\":\"        } else if self.hud.card_visible() {\"},{\"line_number\":1337,\"content\":\"        let card_visible = !studio_active && self.hud.card_visible();\"},{\"line_number\":1338,\"content\":\"        let guide_visible =\"},{\"line_number\":1339,\"content\":\"            !studio_active && self.app_settings.show_guide && self.started.elapsed().as_secs_f32() < 25.0 && !card_visible;\"},{\"line_number\":1420,\"content\":\"            if guide_visible && !menu_open && !touch_ui {\"},{\"line_number\":1439,\"content\":\"            if card_visible && !menu_open && hud.card(&ctx, device) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"3566db2d-52f3-49c5-8773-1718e72b1dfc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_282","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will set guide_visible and card_visible to false when the fit is complete.\n\nI'll implement fit.rs, music changes, and patches next. I also need to add weblink as a module in main.rs. A circular dependency issue came up: settings.rs cannot call weblink.rs since they are sibling modules.\n\nThe circular dependency is resolved by calling `crate::weblink::boot_scene()` from settings. I am now writing the `weblink.rs` module with WASM bindings for `Reflect.get`, `Reflect.set`, and `JSON.parse`.\n\nI added `JSON.stringify` to the `weblink.rs` WASM bindings. I also defined a `DomString` type for JavaScript strings and showed how to convert it to `JsValue` via `JsCast`.\n\nI will copy known top-level fields like `tick`, `phase`, `music`, `demo`, and `touch_card` directly onto the parsed JSON string object. This allows direct dot access without needing `Object.keys`. Nested objects such as `hub` still require parsing.\n\nI will copy `hub` onto the parsed string object as well, since it is an object. I also need to set `__gameUi` from the UI JSON array. Next I will read the boot scene.\n\nI wrote `boot_override()` to read `__gameBoot` from the window object. It extracts the scene string, seed number, and today number. I am checking how `web_sys::window()` converts to `JsValue`.\n\nI will use `win.as_ref()` to convert the window into a `JsValue` for the Reflect calls. I also wrote `take_fit_click()` to read and clear the `__fitClick` value from the window object.\n\nI defined a `HubLink` struct with a `code` field to represent hub states: 0 for none, 1 for wait, and 2 for go. The `hub_code()` function will read the `__hub` property from the window object and return the corresponding code. I also added `storage_get` and `storage_set` wrappers around `window.local_storage()`. The coarse input logic can live in either the weblink or platform module.\n\nI will place the coarse input logic in `weblink::coarse_only()`.\n\nI am adding `set_song` and `set_gains` to `AudioOut`. The mixer callback needs both music gain and voice gain. I will add `Cmd::MusicGain`, `Cmd::VoiceGain`, and `Cmd::Song`.\n\nI cannot easily mutate `voice_gain` inside `play_event` because it takes `&self`. There is no atomic `f32` type, and `AudioOut` may not be `Sync`. I need a different approach.\n\nI will store `voice_gain` in a `std::sync::Mutex<f32>` on `AudioOut`. `play_event` and `set_gains` will lock it to read or update the value. Music gain will be sent through `Cmd::MusicGain` so the mixer callback applies it directly. The app will also apply gains from the status.\n\nThe app will parse the JSON status each frame and call `set_gains` with the music and voice values. Default values are 0.10 for music and 0.80 for voice. The mixer's default music gain of 1.0 would blast until the first status arrives, so the initial audio gain should be set to 0.10.\n\nI will reorder the app loop so `set_gains` runs before the play event loop. This ensures the mixer gain is applied before any song events fire, keeping the channel ordered correctly. I am also considering setting the mixer's default music gain to 0.10.\n\nThe mixer will keep its default music gain at 1.0 so existing unit tests remain valid. The app will explicitly set the gain to 0.10 before any song events fire.\n\nI will add `song`, `song_t`, `phase`, and `music_gain` fields to `Mixer::new`. The render loop will add the music sample to both left and right channels before the tanh stage. Song output will be silenced when `song == 0`.\n\nEverything is ready to be written.\n\nThe About page constant will include the feedback sentences so they appear before the HTML override. The Source line stays on the nintendo line.\n\nThe status method will add `tick` from `sim.state.tick`.\n\nA headless UI test in `pav_ui` will avoid GPU requirements by using a warmup pass with fonts. It may panic on font loading, but that is acceptable.\n\n`egui::FontFamily::Name` expects an `Arc<str>`, so `\"Fredoka\".into()` must be wrapped.\n\n`\"Fredoka\".into()` works for `Arc<str>` in `FontFamily::Name`. I will verify that `content_rect` matches `screen_rect` during headless runs. Painter text opacity defaults to 1. Empty labels must not panic. The `game_lines` early-return must be adjusted so the fit draw still executes.\n\nI will change the order of operations. `session.rs` needs only a one-line change. I will read the camera yaw from the fit UI at the end of `sync_camera` and apply it to the camera parameters. The `play` trait object is `GameBox`, so `fit_ui` is available there. I will also update the App rig yaw after `rig.update`.\n\nThe rig yaw will be updated after the fit flag is known. This prevents pad rotation from overriding the camera during the fit sequence.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-926fc4aa-1d15-43a8-b102-a8193e8ad109-101","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":990,"limit":55}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3066,"output_tokens":3058,"cache_read_input_tokens":165376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"2b1229c6-bfc4-40c5-87d9-b1ab2e102fad"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-926fc4aa-1d15-43a8-b102-a8193e8ad109-101","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"990→        host.pump();\\n        #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n        if let Some(b) = &self.bridge {\\n            // Agent tools run on the simulation thread and can change the camera, view and look.\\n            if let Some(l) = b.poll(host, &mut self.rig, &mut self.view, self.look_ui.look()) {\\n                self.look_ui.set_look(l);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let ui_wants_keys = self.egui_ctx.egui_wants_keyboard_input();\\n        let game_input = !self.menu_open && !ui_wants_keys;\\n1000→        let rewinding = game_input && self.studio_mode == StudioMode::World && self.input.rewind_held();\\n        host.set_control(|c| c.rewinding = rewinding);\\n\\n        let (prev, curr, curr_at, tick_wall) = host.frames();\\n        let studio_mode = curr.studio_mode();\\n        let studio_active = curr.studio_active();\\n        self.studio_navigation |= studio_active;\\n        let snap_camera = studio_mode != self.studio_mode\\n            || prev.studio_mode() != studio_mode\\n            || prev.live_edit_ticket != curr.live_edit_ticket;\\n1010→        let game_input = game_input && !studio_active;\\n        if studio_mode != self.studio_mode {\\n            let keep_object_redo = studio_mode == StudioMode::World && self.asset_ui.open && self.asset_ui.creation_removed();\\n            let keep_creature_redo =\\n                studio_mode == StudioMode::World && self.creature_ui.open && self.creature_ui.creation_removed();\\n            self.builder = ViewBuilder::new();\\n            if let Some(gfx) = &mut self.gfx {\\n                gfx.renderer.clear_particles();\\n            }\\n            self.studio_mode = studio_mode;\\n1020→            self.animation_ui.open = studio_mode == StudioMode::Animation;\\n            self.asset_ui.open = studio_mode == StudioMode::Prop || keep_object_redo;\\n            self.creature_ui.open = studio_mode == StudioMode::Creature || keep_creature_redo;\\n        }\\n        if !studio_active {\\n            let room_before = self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| (r.id, std::sync::Arc::as_ptr(&r.def)));\\n            let quarters = curr.room.as_ref().map(|r| r.quarters).unwrap_or(0);\\n            self.director.update(&curr.hud, quarters, &mut self.rig);\\n            let room_id_before = self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| r.id);\\n            self.hud.update(&curr.room, &mut self.rig);\\n1030→            // Rooms and pads can change view settings (night lighting, bloom, filters).\\n            let key = (curr.room.as_ref().map(|r| r.id), curr.hud.view_serial);\\n            if key != self.view_key {\\n                self.view_key = key;\\n                if let Some(b) = self.view_base.take() {\\n                    self.view = b;\\n                }\\n                let q = curr.room.as_ref().map(|r| r.quarters).unwrap_or(0);\\n                let room = curr.room.as_ref().map(|r| pav_view::build::room_view_map(&r.def.view, q)).unwrap_or_default();\\n                let pads = pav_view::build::room_view_map(&curr.hud.view, q);\\n1040→                if !room.is_empty() || !pads.is_empty() {\\n                    self.view_base = Some(self.view.clone());\\n                    for u in self.view.apply(&room).into_iter().chain(self.view.apply(&pads)) {\\n                        log::warn!(\\\"unknown view setting '{u}'\\\");\\n                    }\",\"content_concise\":\"990→        host.pump();\\n        #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n        if let Some(b) = &self.bridge {\\n            // Agent tools run on the simulation thread and can change the camera, view and look.\\n            if let Some(l) = b.poll(host, &mut self.rig, &mut self.view, self.look_ui.look()) {\\n                self.look_ui.set_look(l);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let ui_wants_keys = self.egui_ctx.egui_wants_keyboard_input();\\n        let game_input = !self.menu_open && !ui_wants_keys;\\n1000→        let rewinding = game_input && self.studio_mode == StudioMode::World && self.input.rewind_held();\\n        host.set_control(|c| c.rewinding = rewinding);\\n\\n        let (prev, curr, curr_at, tick_wall) = host.frames();\\n        let studio_mode = curr.studio_mode();\\n        let studio_active = curr.studio_active();\\n        self.studio_navigation |= studio_active;\\n        let snap_camera = studio_mode != self.studio_mode\\n            || prev.studio_mode() != studio_mode\\n            || prev.live_edit_ticket != curr.live_edit_ticket;\\n1010→        let game_input = game_input && !studio_active;\\n        if studio_mode != self.studio_mode {\\n            let keep_object_redo = studio_mode == StudioMode::World && self.asset_ui.open && self.asset_ui.creation_removed();\\n            let keep_creature_redo =\\n                studio_mode == StudioMode::World && self.creature_ui.open && self.creature_ui.creation_removed();\\n            self.builder = ViewBuilder::new();\\n            if let Some(gfx) = &mut self.gfx {\\n                gfx.renderer.clear_particles();\\n            }\\n            self.studio_mode = studio_mode;\\n1020→            self.animation_ui.open = studio_mode == StudioMode::Animation;\\n            self.asset_ui.open = studio_mode == StudioMode::Prop || keep_object_redo;\\n            self.creature_ui.open = studio_mode == StudioMode::Creature || keep_creature_redo;\\n        }\\n        if !studio_active {\\n            let room_before = self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| (r.id, std::sync::Arc::as_ptr(&r.def)));\\n            let quarters = curr.room.as_ref().map(|r| r.quarters).unwrap_or(0);\\n            self.director.update(&curr.hud, quarters, &mut self.rig);\\n            let room_id_before = self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| r.id);\\n            self.hud.update(&curr.room, &mut self.rig);\\n1030→            // Rooms and pads can change view settings (night lighting, bloom, filters).\\n            let key = (curr.room.as_ref().map(|r| r.id), curr.hud.view_serial);\\n            if key != self.view_key {\\n                self.view_key = key;\\n                if let Some(b) = self.view_base.take() {\\n                    self.view = b;\\n                }\\n                let q = curr.room.as_ref().map(|r| r.quarters).unwrap_or(0);\\n                let room = curr.room.as_ref().map(|r| pav_view::build::room_view_map(&r.def.view, q)).unwrap_or_default();\\n                let pads = pav_view::build::room_view_map(&curr.hud.view, q);\\n1040→                if !room.is_empty() || !pads.is_empty() {\\n                    self.view_base = Some(self.view.clone());\\n                    for u in self.view.apply(&room).into_iter().chain(self.view.apply(&pads)) {\\n                        log::warn!(\\\"unknown view setting '{u}'\\\");\\n                    }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs\",\"offset\":990,\"limit\":55,\"raw_output\":\"        host.pump();\\n        #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n        if let Some(b) = &self.bridge {\\n            // Agent tools run on the simulation thread and can change the camera, view and look.\\n            if let Some(l) = b.poll(host, &mut self.rig, &mut self.view, self.look_ui.look()) {\\n                self.look_ui.set_look(l);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let ui_wants_keys = self.egui_ctx.egui_wants_keyboard_input();\\n        let game_input = !self.menu_open && !ui_wants_keys;\\n        let rewinding = game_input && self.studio_mode == StudioMode::World && self.input.rewind_held();\\n        host.set_control(|c| c.rewinding = rewinding);\\n\\n        let (prev, curr, curr_at, tick_wall) = host.frames();\\n        let studio_mode = curr.studio_mode();\\n        let studio_active = curr.studio_active();\\n        self.studio_navigation |= studio_active;\\n        let snap_camera = studio_mode != self.studio_mode\\n            || prev.studio_mode() != studio_mode\\n            || prev.live_edit_ticket != curr.live_edit_ticket;\\n        let game_input = game_input && !studio_active;\\n        if studio_mode != self.studio_mode {\\n            let keep_object_redo = studio_mode == StudioMode::World && self.asset_ui.open && self.asset_ui.creation_removed();\\n            let keep_creature_redo =\\n                studio_mode == StudioMode::World && self.creature_ui.open && self.creature_ui.creation_removed();\\n            self.builder = ViewBuilder::new();\\n            if let Some(gfx) = &mut self.gfx {\\n                gfx.renderer.clear_particles();\\n            }\\n            self.studio_mode = studio_mode;\\n            self.animation_ui.open = studio_mode == StudioMode::Animation;\\n            self.asset_ui.open = studio_mode == StudioMode::Prop || keep_object_redo;\\n            self.creature_ui.open = studio_mode == StudioMode::Creature || keep_creature_redo;\\n        }\\n        if !studio_active {\\n            let room_before = self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| (r.id, std::sync::Arc::as_ptr(&r.def)));\\n            let quarters = curr.room.as_ref().map(|r| r.quarters).unwrap_or(0);\\n            self.director.update(&curr.hud, quarters, &mut self.rig);\\n            let room_id_before = self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| r.id);\\n            self.hud.update(&curr.room, &mut self.rig);\\n            // Rooms and pads can change view settings (night lighting, bloom, filters).\\n            let key = (curr.room.as_ref().map(|r| r.id), curr.hud.view_serial);\\n            if key != self.view_key {\\n                self.view_key = key;\\n                if let Some(b) = self.view_base.take() {\\n                    self.view = b;\\n                }\\n                let q = curr.room.as_ref().map(|r| r.quarters).unwrap_or(0);\\n                let room = curr.room.as_ref().map(|r| pav_view::build::room_view_map(&r.def.view, q)).unwrap_or_default();\\n                let pads = pav_view::build::room_view_map(&curr.hud.view, q);\\n                if !room.is_empty() || !pads.is_empty() {\\n                    self.view_base = Some(self.view.clone());\\n                    for u in self.view.apply(&room).into_iter().chain(self.view.apply(&pads)) {\\n                        log::warn!(\\\"unknown view setting '{u}'\\\");\\n                    }\\n\",\"total_lines\":2266}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"feaa49d8-f05b-4276-85d7-d1ca22b9a987"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_283","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"host.frames() is at 1003, after the pad rotate at 986.\n\nI'll move the pad rotate lines to after frames() so they respect the fit state. I'll set a `self.in_fit` flag immediately after frames() and gate the rotate block by it.\n\nI'll gate the start menu and pad rotate/zoom with `!self.input.fit`. The fit state will be set at the end of the input section so the first frame defaults to false.\n\nOne frame of engine menu risk on the first frame is acceptable. The menu will also close automatically when fit activates. Map toggle will be gated by fit as well.\n\nI'm adding `raw_left` to the Pad struct and placing the fit binding after game(). I verified all required button names exist. Escape will trigger both PAUSE and BACK, with PAUSE checked first in FitGame.\n\nArrow keys will be mapped to both the axis and menu buttons so they trigger MENU_ actions. Q, E, F, and Tab map to STEP_L, STEP_R, WAVE, and SCHEDULE. L1 corresponds to LeftTrigger. Unbound digit keys are safely skipped during fit mode. Backspace is handled separately for rewind.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f2734f71-a6f3-4e5a-99a1-6fefefc6c989-102","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub fn new\\(","glob":"**/pav_core/src/sim.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f2734f71-a6f3-4e5a-99a1-6fefefc6c989-103","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub fn step\\(","glob":"**/pav_core/src/sim.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4103,"output_tokens":916,"cache_read_input_tokens":168320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"c2bb9313-760e-4b96-a579-ff0d0654bcdf"}
