o-1949cf8c6b5b557f/epaint-0.36.2/src/corner_radius.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":34,\"content\":\"impl From<u8> for CornerRadius {\"},{\"line_number\":41,\"content\":\"impl From<f32> for CornerRadius {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/epaint-0.36.2/src/corner_radius_f32.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":53,\"content\":\"impl From<f32> for CornerRadiusF32 {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"1693b7b7-7ec9-4d98-9355-3341797c4c9e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_287","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will write everything now. I will also add a circle for the puck using the painter.\n\nI will write fit.rs and update app.rs. I will fix the game_mode bindings overwrite by overriding them before buttons() each frame.\n\nI will also prevent the room rebind from interfering by placing the override right before buttons(). I am replacing the shared input block in fit.rs to handle fit sampling.\n\nI am populating the shared input struct with fit sampling results. I clear the primary button when a UI element is active so clicks register as UI events.\n\nI am also clearing the confirm button from the shared input when a UI element is active. I am adding extra menu bits from the stick to fit sampling. I am handling device 4 and touch detection so coarse input stays as device 4 even if phantom mouse events appear. A tap on a Playwright phone counts as touch, so the card remains visible until Settings is tapped.\n\nI will only mark a device as seen when it is a key or gamepad. Mouse events will not trigger this flag, so Playwright mouse moves cannot accidentally drop the card. On desktop, mouse input remains device 3 because coarse mode is disabled.\n\nThe test detects the card via DOM visibility and the touch_card status flag. The card remains visible from the start on coarse input because the simulator sets touch_only for device 4.\n\nTapping the Settings button sends Click(4) and transitions the flow to the settings phase. Canvas hit testing also works for that item. The test may tap coordinates of the Settings text in the DOM rather than the canvas item.\n\nThe Settings button will use the exact label \"Settings\" so Playwright can tap it directly. On a phone, attract mode starts because there are no keys and the device stays as device 4. A touch click on the Settings item during attract correctly opens settings. The DOM card is centered rather than full-screen, so attract content remains visible around it. I am considering whether to hide the DOM card when settings opens.\n\nThe DOM card will be hidden via JavaScript when the Settings button is tapped. A keyboard keydown listener will also hide it on phones, since Rust marks the device as seen and drops the card. The in-game lines already include the required phrase for canvas capture. The `__gameUi` status will be published every frame even before items are ready, and the tick string will change each frame so the test can observe progression.\n\nI will publish the weblink status after the egui pass, using the current frame's fit item rects. Canvas coordinates will be scaled by the physical window size to match the cursor space and avoid DPR mismatches.\n\nI will keep the current coordinate logic and only adjust it if the test fails. The published item rects are in window pixels, but Playwright converts CSS pixels to physical pixels for mouse events, so hit testing in physical pixels aligns with the test clicks.\n\nI will publish the UI rectangles in CSS pixels rather than physical pixels. On WASM I will divide the physical window size by the scale factor to get CSS dimensions, while native already uses physical pixels. This ensures the coordinates match what Playwright computes from getBoundingClientRect.\n\nI will hit-test in physical pixels. The published CSS rectangles are normalized against CSS size, but the cursor event arrives in physical pixels. Comparing normalized physical coordinates to the physical cursor position keeps the hit test consistent.\n\nI will read the long-running skill before launching any cargo build. I will patch fit.rs and other files, then compile. I will also update the todo list as I go. The about text will include an honest note that the browser and hub are tested on this machine with Playwright.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1d5e4d9e-8efa-47a1-a186-1bced268b004-107","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"about_page","glob":"**/games/fit/mod.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":408,"output_tokens":2331,"cache_read_input_tokens":174976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"ca4a8416-99fd-4b70-bb25-2818c54b10a1"}
