{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_314","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The camera yaw is set to act.t * 0.35, which grows without bound. This value is assigned directly to yaw in degrees, causing an unbounded rotation.\n\nThe session assigns yaw as f64, so the app should do the same. The 90-second morning lap yields only about 31.5 degrees of rotation, which is acceptable. I also noticed that rig.params.yaw is mixed with f32 math elsewhere in the code.\n\nThe yaw value will be cast to f64 and applied after the director update and any pad rotation, before rendering.\n\nThe yaw will be set right before `self.rig.update(focus, dt)` so the rig uses it this frame. Absolute assignment prevents pad rotation from accumulating.\n\nThe localStorage key is `wobble-minutes-save-v1`. On boot, if fit is active and the save hasn't loaded yet, the host will import the stored text into the FitGame and set today.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9bbbc5bf-8792-4fc3-b72f-8eee8e1e452e-39","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs","offset":120,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9bbbc5bf-8792-4fc3-b72f-8eee8e1e452e-40","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn move_axis|pub fn relative_move","glob":"**/{input.rs,camera.rs,rig.rs}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9bbbc5bf-8792-4fc3-b72f-8eee8e1e452e-41","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":1,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1742,"output_tokens":865,"cache_read_input_tokens":77056,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"1b3f2617-d38e-4d8a-a902-a2b34e540330"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9bbbc5bf-8792-4fc3-b72f-8eee8e1e452e-39","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"120→\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nimpl SimHost {\\n    pub fn start(mut sim: Sim) -> Self {\\n        let shared = shared_for(&mut sim);\\n        let (tx, rx) = std::sync::mpsc::channel();\\n        let sh = shared.clone();\\n        let thread = std::thread::Builder::new()\\n            .name(\\\"simulation\\\".into())\\n            .spawn(move || {\\n130→                let sh2 = sh.clone();\\n                let r = std::panic::catch_unwind(std::panic::AssertUnwindSafe(move || run(sim, rx, sh2)));\\n                if let Err(e) = r {\\n                    let msg = e\\n                        .downcast_ref::<&str>()\\n                        .map(|s| s.to_string())\\n                        .or_else(|| e.downcast_ref::<String>().cloned())\\n                        .unwrap_or_else(|| \\\"unknown panic\\\".into());\\n                    *sh.crashed.lock().unwrap() = Some(msg);\\n                }\\n140→            })\\n            .expect(\\\"spawn simulation thread\\\");\\n        Self { tx, shared, thread: Some(thread) }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs `f` on the simulation thread (fire and forget).\\n    pub fn exec(&self, f: impl FnOnce(&mut Sim) + Send + 'static) {\\n        let _ = self.tx.send(Cmd::Run(Box::new(f)));\\n    }\\n\\n150→    /// Runs `f` on the simulation thread and waits for its result.\\n    pub fn query<R: Send + 'static>(&self, f: impl FnOnce(&mut Sim) -> R + Send + 'static) -> Option<R> {\\n        let (rtx, rrx) = std::sync::mpsc::channel();\\n        self.exec(move |sim| {\\n            let _ = rtx.send(f(sim));\\n        });\\n        rrx.recv_timeout(Duration::from_secs(5)).ok()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Advances the simulation (the thread does this by itself natively).\\n160→    pub fn pump(&self) {}\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\nimpl SimHost {\\n    pub fn start(mut sim: Sim) -> Self {\\n        let shared = shared_for(&mut sim);\\n        Self { sim: std::cell::RefCell::new(sim), clock: std::cell::RefCell::new(Clock::new()), shared }\\n    }\\n\\n170→    pub fn exec(&self, f: impl FnOnce(&mut Sim) + 'static) {\\n        let mut sim = self.sim.borrow_mut();\\n        f(&mut sim);\\n        let dt = sim.dt();\\n        publish(&mut sim, &self.shared, dt, Instant::now());\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn query<R: 'static>(&self, f: impl FnOnce(&mut Sim) -> R + 'static) -> Option<R> {\\n        let mut sim = self.sim.borrow_mut();\\n        let r = f(&mut sim);\\n180→        let dt = sim.dt();\\n        publish(&mut sim, &self.shared, dt, Instant::now());\\n        Some(r)\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs the ticks that are due (called once per frame).\\n    pub fn pump(&self) {\\n        self.clock.borrow_mut().advance(&mut self.sim.borrow_mut(), &self.shared);\\n    }\\n}\\n190→\\nimpl SimHost {\\n    pub fn frames(&self) -> (Arc<RenderFrame>, Arc<RenderFrame>, Instant, f32) {\\n        let f = self.shared.frames.lock().unwrap();\\n        (f.prev.clone(), f.curr.clone(), f.curr_at, f.tick_wall)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn control(&self) -> TimeControl {\\n        *self.shared.control.lock().unwrap()\\n    }\",\"content_concise\":\"120→\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nimpl SimHost {\\n    pub fn start(mut sim: Sim) -> Self {\\n        let shared = shared_for(&mut sim);\\n        let (tx, rx) = std::sync::mpsc::channel();\\n        let sh = shared.clone();\\n        let thread = std::thread::Builder::new()\\n            .name(\\\"simulation\\\".into())\\n            .spawn(move || {\\n130→                let sh2 = sh.clone();\\n                let r = std::panic::catch_unwind(std::panic::AssertUnwindSafe(move || run(sim, rx, sh2)));\\n                if let Err(e) = r {\\n                    let msg = e\\n                        .downcast_ref::<&str>()\\n                        .map