{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_322","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Applying all patches now.\n\nFound a borrow conflict: `set_menu` needs `&mut self`, but `host` is already borrowed as an immutable reference. I'll fix this before wiring the app.\n\nThe host borrow lasts the entire frame, so set_menu cannot be called afterward. I need to close the menu before that borrow begins, but fit depends on frames() which requires host.\n\nI'll close the menu directly by setting `self.menu_open = false`, calling `host.set_control` to unpause, and clearing input. I need to verify that Rust allows mutably borrowing other fields while `host` is partially borrowed.\n\nConfirmed that Rust allows separate borrows of `self.input` and `self.menu_open` while `host` is partially borrowed. The menu close logic will directly set `menu_open = false`, restore the host paused state, and clear input without calling `set_menu`. Also noted that the fit flag should be checked before polling.\n\nThe fit flag will be set mid-frame so the current frame uses fit layout, and it persists on `self.input.fit` for the next poll. Fit bindings are applied after room rebind but before button polling, ensuring the next frame keeps fit bindings if the room does not change.\n\nFit bindings will be applied every frame when `fit_on` is true, immediately before button polling. The existing `dt` variable is already in scope for the input section. I'll use fully qualified imports for `buttons::PRIMARY` to match the current code style.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-259f25c6-4cf9-417e-9a00-77e5eec113fc-57","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"attract|woke\\(|device != 4|touch_only|fn woke","glob":"**/games/fit/mod.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":987,"output_tokens":1007,"cache_read_input_tokens":97664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"864bea18-75eb-4258-96f0-b35ca8ea8eea"}
