{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a59961e4-d136-4aa7-9742-5fd6800fd6ea-63","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"240→    studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Clock {\\n    fn new() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            next: Instant::now(),\\n            window_start: Instant::now(),\\n            window_ticks: 0,\\n            busy: Duration::ZERO,\\n250→            rewound: false,\\n            studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode::World,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs whatever is due now; returns how long until the next tick.\\n    fn advance(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared) -> Duration {\\n        let previewing = sim.studio_active();\\n        let mode = sim.studio_mode();\\n        if self.studio_mode != mode {\\n260→            self.studio_mode = mode;\\n            self.next = Instant::now();\\n        }\\n        let ctl = *sh.control.lock().unwrap();\\n        // The animation stage has its own play, pause and speed controls. The world's time\\n        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n270→                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().take() };\\n            let t = Instant::now();\\n280→            sim.step(&input);\\n            *busy += t.elapsed();\\n            if let Some(s) = stamp {\\n                *sh.latency_probe.lock().unwrap() = Some((s, Instant::now(), sim.state.tick));\\n            }\\n            *window_ticks += 1;\\n            publish(sim, sh, tick_wall, at);\\n        };\\n\\n        let now = Instant::now();\",\"content_concise\":\"240→    studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Clock {\\n    fn new() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            next: Instant::now(),\\n            window_start: Instant::now(),\\n            window_ticks: 0,\\n            busy: Duration::ZERO,\\n250→            rewound: false,\\n            studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode::World,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs whatever is due now; returns how long until the next tick.\\n    fn advance(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared) -> Duration {\\n        let previewing = sim.studio_active();\\n        let mode = sim.studio_mode();\\n        if self.studio_mode != mode {\\n260→            self.studio_mode = mode;\\n            self.next = Instant::now();\\n        }\\n        let ctl = *sh.control.lock().unwrap();\\n        // The animation stage has its own play, pause and speed controls. The world's time\\n        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n270→                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().take() };\\n            let t = Instant::now();\\n280→            sim.step(&input);\\n            *busy += t.elapsed();\\n            if let Some(s) = stamp {\\n                *sh.latency_probe.lock().unwrap() = Some((s, Instant::now(), sim.state.tick));\\n            }\\n            *window_ticks += 1;\\n            publish(sim, sh, tick_wall, at);\\n        };\\n\\n        let now = Instant::now();\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs\",\"offset\":240,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"    studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Clock {\\n    fn new() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            next: Instant::now(),\\n            window_start: Instant::now(),\\n            window_ticks: 0,\\n            busy: Duration::ZERO,\\n            rewound: false,\\n            studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode::World,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs whatever is due now; returns how long until the next tick.\\n    fn advance(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared) -> Duration {\\n        let previewing = sim.studio_active();\\n        let mode = sim.studio_mode();\\n        if self.studio_mode != mode {\\n            self.studio_mode = mode;\\n            self.next = Instant::now();\\n        }\\n        let ctl = *sh.control.lock().unwrap();\\n        // The animation stage has its own play, pause and speed controls. The world's time\\n        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().take() };\\n            let t = Instant::now();\\n            sim.step(&input);\\n            *busy += t.elapsed();\\n            if let Some(s) = stamp {\\n                *sh.latency_probe.lock().unwrap() = Some((s, Instant::now(), sim.state.tick));\\n            }\\n            *window_ticks += 1;\\n            publish(sim, sh, tick_wall, at);\\n        };\\n\\n        let now = Instant::now();\\n\",\"total_lines\":427}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"880294c1-04ad-4dbc-964d-b34a8cd0a04e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_326","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The frame was copied, including lean, ui, any, device, and hub.\n\nPresses are cleared after copying so the next frame starts fresh. UI state is assigned every tick to prevent clicks from sticking. Any, lean, device, hub, move_dir, and held are also updated each frame. Cmd is left untouched because simhost handles it separately.\n\nAim is set to None each fit frame to suppress the aim marker. The marker code uses a local `aim` variable computed before the lock, so leaving it as Some would still draw a ground marker during fit.\n\nThe aim marker condition will include `!fit_on`. `fit_on` is defined just before the input section so it is available for the marker, audio, and UI. When fit is active, input bindings switch to fit mode.\n\nClosing the menu restores the paused state and clears input. Camera yaw is computed before rig.update. The fit_on boolean can be captured by the UI closure because it is Copy.\n\nPanel UI, boot panel, and on-screen controls like touch.draw will be hidden during fit. Stats, guide, card, hint, feel, course HUD, pad note, and the final publish step are also gated by `!fit_on`. The scale factor for publishing must be handled because gfx is mutably borrowed.\n\nThe fit HUD items are serialized to JSON with coordinates scaled from window pixels to CSS pixels using the window scale factor.\n\nThe fit HUD JSON is published and persisted. `stay_persist` cannot be called as a method because it would re-borrow `self.host` while the host reference is already held; the persistence logic must be inlined instead.\n\nThe persistence logic is inlined directly. A `persist_stay` method would borrow `self` mutably and the host reference simultaneously, which is impossible. Instead, the code checks `fit_save_loaded`, loads the saved fit state from storage, and executes it through the host.\n\nPartial borrows of different struct fields are allowed in Rust. Borrowing `self.host` and `self.fit_save_loaded` together is valid because they do not overlap. This pattern is already used elsewhere in the function. The fit save logic should also run on native, since tests do not use the window.\n\nNative storage_get returns None, so the fit save logic is gated to wasm to avoid a hitch. Publish remains unconditional because it is a cheap no-op on native. The audio block will be modified before play_event. Fonts are initialized after the app is built in new(). Coarse input is set based on touch_screen or weblink::coarse_only(), and touch_screen also sets last_device to Touch and hides the boot panel.\n\nhandle_key returns early for Escape and digit keys during fit, so they do not trigger menus or input. F11 and F12 remain available for studio modes. Mouse wheel events are gated by `!self.input.fit`. The cursor uses note_pointer in the fit path.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-553406ef-2355-490d-8e1d-f9e5f78d25a6-64","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn pad_menus","glob":"**/pav_app/src/app.rs","-A":35}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":730,"output_tokens":1962,"cache_read_input_tokens":104064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"e1f5f3a1-3244-40d4-aa5d-aaf822cb014a"}
