{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_344","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Proceeding to write all the patches.\n\nPlanning to batch the remaining patches. Need to fix session yaw and weblink date_now. Also drafting a free function in app.rs for browser save persistence that avoids taking &mut self.\n\nConfirmed the compiler allows borrowing host and a different field mutably in one call. Will implement apply_browser_save as a private module function.\n\nWriting the `apply_browser_save` function body. It parses the JSON status string to extract the save serial, marks the save as loaded, and retrieves the existing saved data from web storage.\n\nInside the `apply_browser_save` function, it retrieves today's date from boot parts or falls back to the epoch day. It then executes a host closure to access the FitGame state, imports any saved text if present, and resets the game flow to Title.\n\nThe function now updates the game's today field. If the save serial changed, it exports the current FitGame state and writes it to web storage. On wasm, host.query republishes the save once per serial change. The epoch day fallback uses the date when boot today is unavailable.\n\nThe save import will run only on the first frame. The publish_stay function is being drafted to read HUD status and compute CSS dimensions from the window scale factor.\n\nThe publish_stay function now maps each HUD item to a JSON object with scaled CSS coordinates. It serializes the list and publishes it via weblink. This will be called when fit_on is active.\n\nConfirmed that fit_on implies hud.fit is present and status is truthy. The status string is always non-empty because it is JSON. Gfx::size and window are public. UI patches will be applied as multiple small replacements rather than one large block.\n\nTen UI sections need wrapping: panel actions, boot panel, stats, guide, touch draw, card visibility, pad note, course HUD, feel UI, and hint bar. The `fit_on` boolean is a local Copy value defined before the UI closure, so it can be captured by copy without moving.\n\nInside the UI closure, `show_boot` will be forced to false whenever `fit_on` is true. Guide visibility checks will also include `&& !fit_on`. The F1 panel will remain visually closed during fit mode.\n\nThe panel and show_boot flags will be forced to closed before the UI closure is entered, since the closure already mutably borrows the panel.\n\nThe feel panel will also be forced closed before its mutable borrow. Touch draw, editor UI, and the look window will all be gated behind `!fit_on` so they do not appear during fit mode.\n\nThe teleport menu will be hidden during fit mode. Studio windows are already closed by default and do not need changes. The aim marker, pad rotate, and touch stick will also be hidden to keep the fit view clean.\n\nF2 is already gated, so teleport stays closed without extra draw logic. The guide panel is visible for 25 seconds and must be hidden. show_boot, show_stats, and the hint bar are always on by default and must be hidden. The room card, feel UI, course HUD, and aim marker will also be suppressed during fit mode.\n\nshow_stats will be suppressed during fit without changing the setting, so it reappears afterward. The code will be written as several search_replace calls. A wasm_bindgen DomString constructor is being added to safely wrap String values for the weblink module.\n\nThe `js_sys` crate is not a direct dependency of pav_app, so the `extends = js_sys::Object` attribute is invalid. The `String` type name also conflicts with Rust's built-in `String`, so the constructor must use `js_name` or `js_class` to target the JavaScript String constructor.\n\nThe `js_name = String` attribute on the `DomString` type will let the constructor invoke the JavaScript `String` constructor directly, avoiding the need for a `js_sys` dependency.\n\nLeaving the existing `js_class = \"String\"` constructor attribute in place and deferring a fix until compilation fails. Native builds will not catch wasm_bindgen errors because the bind module is gated behind `#[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]`, so a later `cargo check --target wasm32` run is needed to verify the fix.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The window still uses the engine’s own keys and chrome. I’ll connect the stay’s bindings, lean, and status publishing, then compile."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6b159f52-cba2-4ec9-b375-f04491d8d7ee-87","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_tools/src/session.rs","old_string":"            if let Some(yaw) = play.fit_ui(&self.sim).and_then(|ui| ui.camera_yaw) {\n                self.camera.params.yaw = yaw as f64;\n            }","new_string":"            if let Some(yaw) = play.fit_ui(&self.sim).and_then(|ui| ui.camera_yaw) {\n                self.camera.params.yaw = yaw;\n            }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6b159f52-cba2-4ec9-b375-f04491d8d7ee-88","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/weblink.rs","old_string":"        #[wasm_bindgen(js_namespace = JSON, js_name = parse, catch)]\n        pub fn parse(text: &str) -> Result<JsValue, JsValue>;\n\n        type DomString;\n        #[wasm_bindgen(constructor, js_class = \"String\")]\n        fn new(s: &str) -> DomString;\n    }","new_string":"        #[wasm_bindgen(js_namespace = JSON, js_name = parse, catch)]\n        pub fn parse(text: &str) -> Result<JsValue, JsValue>;\n        #[wasm_bindgen(js_namespace = Date, js_name = now)]\n        pub fn date_now() -> f64;\n\n        #[wasm_bindgen(js_name = String)]\n        type DomString;\n        #[wasm_bindgen(constructor)]\n        fn new(s: &st