{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_367","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A unit test failed: the gust should tip within 2 seconds.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ce7a3d2d-2cea-439f-a2dc-d25d77abad7b-136","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/core.rs","offset":120,"limit":160}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1182,"output_tokens":270,"cache_read_input_tokens":164608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"6427088a-7245-46c2-bdc2-f6e52165e4c7"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ce7a3d2d-2cea-439f-a2dc-d25d77abad7b-136","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"120→    pub t: f32,\\n    pub amp: f32,\\n    pub phase: [f32; 4],\\n    pub kick_in: f32,\\n    pub gust: Vec2,\\n    pub kicks: bool,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for BalanceCore {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n130→        Self {\\n            cob: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            vel: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            tip_t: 0.0,\\n            tipped: false,\\n            t: 0.0,\\n            amp: 0.12,\\n            phase: [0.4, 1.7, 2.2, 0.9],\\n            kick_in: 1.4,\\n            gust: Vec2::ZERO,\\n140→            kicks: true,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl BalanceCore {\\n    pub fn wobble(&self) -> Vec2 {\\n        let ax = |t: f32, a: f32, b: f32| {\\n            self.amp * (0.7 * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 1.3 * t + a).sin() + 0.3 * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 2.9 * t + b).sin())\\n        };\\n150→        Vec2::new(ax(self.t, self.phase[0], self.phase[1]), ax(self.t, self.phase[2], self.phase[3]))\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Advance one tick. `lean` is already shaped, in the disc.\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, rng: &mut crate::rng::Rng) {\\n        self.tipped = false;\\n        let target = lean.clamp_length_max(1.0) * rules.reach + self.wobble();\\n        let acc = (target - self.cob) * rules.stiffness - self.vel * rules.damping + self.gust;\\n        self.vel += acc * dt;\\n        if self.kicks {\\n160→            self.kick_in -= dt;\\n            if self.kick_in <= 0.0 {\\n                let ang = rng.range(0.0, std::f32::consts::TAU);\\n                self.vel += Vec2::new(ang.cos(), ang.sin()) * 0.1;\\n                self.kick_in = rng.range(1.0, 2.0);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.cob += self.vel * dt;\\n        self.t += dt;\\n        if self.cob.length() > 1.0 {\\n170→            self.tip_t += dt;\\n            if self.tip_t >= rules.tip_time {\\n                self.tipped = true;\\n                self.tip_t = 0.0;\\n                self.cob = self.cob.normalize_or_zero() * 0.72;\\n                self.vel = Vec2::ZERO;\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            self.tip_t = 0.0;\\n        }\\n180→    }\\n\\n    /// Step without the seeded wander, for the feel tests.\\n    pub fn step_clean(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules) {\\n        let mut rng = crate::rng::Rng::new(1);\\n        let kicks = self.kicks;\\n        self.kicks = false;\\n        let amp = self.amp;\\n        self.amp = 0.0;\\n        self.step(lean, dt, rules, &mut rng);\\n190→        self.amp = amp;\\n        self.kicks = kicks;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Balance Age. Better skill, more days and more stars all come out younger.\\npub fn balance_age(skill: f32, days_completed: u32, total_stars: u32) -> u8 {\\n    let skill = skill.clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    let age = 24.0 + 56.0 * (1.0 - skill).powf(1.1) - 2.0 * days_completed as f32 - (total_stars as f32 / 3.0).min(8.0);\\n    age.round().clamp(18.0, 99.0) as u8\\n200→}\\n\\npub fn stars_from_score(score: f32) -> u8 {\\n    if score >= 850.0 {\\n        3\\n    } else if score >= 650.0 {\\n        2\\n    } else if score >= 400.0 {\\n        1\\n    } else {\\n210→        0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn stars_from_plank(secs: f32) -> u8 {\\n    if secs >= 55.0 {\\n        3\\n    } else if secs >= 40.0 {\\n        2\\n    } else if secs >= 25.0 {\\n220→        1\\n    } else {\\n        0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n230→    #[test]\\n    fn full_lean_settles_inside_the_disc() {\\n        let rules = Rules::default();\\n        let mut b = BalanceCore::default();\\n        b.kicks = false;\\n        b.amp = 0.0;\\n        let lean = Vec2::new(1.0, 0.0);\\n        let mut peak = 0.0_f32;\\n        for _ in 0..180 {\\n            b.step_clean(lean, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n240→            peak = peak.max(b.cob.length());\\n        }\\n        assert!(peak < 1.0, \\\"peak {peak}\\\");\\n        assert!(b.cob.x > 0.85, \\\"settled at {}\\\", b.cob.x);\\n        assert!(!b.tipped);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn a_hard_gust_tips_and_a_release_returns() {\\n        let rules = Rules::default();\\n250→        let mut b = BalanceCore::default();\\n        b.kicks = false;\\n        b.amp = 0.0;\\n        b.gust = Vec2::new(30.0, 0.0);\\n        let mut tipped = false;\\n        for _ in 0..120 {\\n            b.step_clean(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n            tipped |= b.tipped;\\n        }\\n        assert!(tipped, \\\"gust should tip within 2s\\\");\\n260→        b.gust = Vec2::ZERO;\\n        for _ in 0..180 {\\n            b.step_clean(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n        }\\n        assert!(b.cob.length() < 0.2, \\\"returned to {}\\\", b.cob);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn age_moves_the_right_way_and_stays_in_range() {\\n        let young = balance_age(1.0, 4, 30);\\n270→        let older = balance_age(0.0, 0, 0);\\n        assert!(young < older);\\n        assert!((18..=99).contains(&young));\\n        assert!((18..=99).contains(&older));\\n        assert_eq!(balance_age(1.0, 0, 0), 24);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(399.0), 0);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(400.0), 1);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(650.0), 2);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(850.0), 3);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(24.0), 0);\",\"content_concise\":\"120→    pub t: f32,\\n    pub amp: f32,\\n    pub phase: [f32; 4],\\n    pub kick_in: f32,\\n    pub gust: Vec2,\\n    pub kicks: bool,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for BalanceCore {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n130→        Self {\\n            cob: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            vel: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            tip_t: 0.0,\\n            tipped: false,\\n            t: 0.0,\\n            amp: 0.12,\\n            phase: [0.4, 1.7, 2.2, 0.9],\\n            kick_in: 1.4,\\n            gust: Vec2::ZERO,\\n140→            kicks: true,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl BalanceCore {\\n    pub fn wobble(&self) -> Vec2 {\\n        let ax = |t: f32, a: f32, b: f32| {\\n            self.amp * (0.7 * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 1.3 * t + a).sin() + 0.3 * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 2.9 * t + b).sin())\\n        };\\n150→        Vec2::new(ax(self.t, self.phase[0], self.phase[1]), ax(self.t, self.phase[2], self.phase[3]))\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Advance one tick. `lean` is already shaped, in the disc.\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, rng: &mut crate::rng::Rng) {\\n        self.tipped = false;\\n        let target = lean.clamp_length_max(1.0) * rules.reach + self.wobble();\\n        let acc = (target - self.cob) * rules.stiffness - self.vel * rules.damping + self.gust;\\n        self.vel += acc * dt;\\n        if self.kicks {\\n160→            self.kick_in -= dt;\\n            if self.kick_in <= 0.0 {\\n                let ang = rng.range(0.0, std::f32::consts::TAU);\\n                self.vel += Vec2::new(ang.cos(), ang.sin()) * 0.1;\\n                self.kick_in = rng.range(1.0, 2.0);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.cob += self.vel * dt;\\n        self.t += dt;\\n        if self.cob.length() > 1.0 {\\n170→            self.tip_t += dt;\\n            if self.tip_t >= rules.tip_time {\\n                self.tipped = true;\\n                self.tip_t = 0.0;\\n                self.cob = self.cob.normalize_or_zero() * 0.72;\\n                self.vel = Vec2::ZERO;\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            self.tip_t = 0.0;\\n        }\\n180→    }\\n\\n    /// Step without the seeded wander, for the feel tests.\\n    pub fn step_clean(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules) {\\n        let mut rng = crate::rng::Rng::new(1);\\n        let kicks = self.kicks;\\n        self.kicks = false;\\n        let amp = self.amp;\\n        self.amp = 0.0;\\n        self.step(lean, dt, rules, &mut rng);\\n190→        self.amp = amp;\\n        self.kicks = kicks;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Balance Age. Better skill, more days and more stars all come out younger.\\npub fn balance_age(skill: f32, days_completed: u32, total_stars: u32) -> u8 {\\n    let skill = skill.clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    let age = 24.0 + 56.0 * (1.0 - skill).powf(1.1) - 2.0 * days_completed as f32 - (total_stars as f32 / 3.0).min(8.0);\\n    age.round().clamp(18.0, 99.0) as u8\\n200→}\\n\\npub fn stars_from_score(score: f32) -> u8 {\\n    if score >= 850.0 {\\n        3\\n    } else if score >= 650.0 {\\n        2\\n    } else if score >= 400.0 {\\n        1\\n    } else {\\n210→        0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn stars_from_plank(secs: f32) -> u8 {\\n    if secs >= 55.0 {\\n        3\\n    } else if secs >= 40.0 {\\n        2\\n    } else if secs >= 25.0 {\\n220→        1\\n    } else {\\n        0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n230→    #[test]\\n    fn full_lean_settles_inside_the_disc() {\\n        let rules = Rules::default();\\n        let mut b = BalanceCore::default();\\n        b.kicks = false;\\n        b.amp = 0.0;\\n        let lean = Vec2::new(1.0, 0.0);\\n        let mut peak = 0.0_f32;\\n        for _ in 0..180 {\\n            b.step_clean(lean, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n240→            peak = peak.max(b.cob.length());\\n        }\\n        assert!(peak < 1.0, \\\"peak {peak}\\\");\\n        assert!(b.cob.x > 0.85, \\\"settled at {}\\\", b.cob.x);\\n        assert!(!b.tipped);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn a_hard_gust_tips_and_a_release_returns() {\\n        let rules = Rules::default();\\n250→        let mut b = BalanceCore::default();\\n        b.kicks = false;\\n        b.amp = 0.0;\\n        b.gust = Vec2::new(30.0, 0.0);\\n        let mut tipped = false;\\n        for _ in 0..120 {\\n            b.step_clean(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n            tipped |= b.tipped;\\n        }\\n        assert!(tipped, \\\"gust should tip within 2s\\\");\\n260→        b.gust = Vec2::ZERO;\\n        for _ in 0..180 {\\n            b.step_clean(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n        }\\n        assert!(b.cob.length() < 0.2, \\\"returned to {}\\\", b.cob);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn age_moves_the_right_way_and_stays_in_range() {\\n        let young = balance_age(1.0, 4, 30);\\n270→        let older = balance_age(0.0, 0, 0);\\n        assert!(young < older);\\n        assert!((18..=99).contains(&young));\\n        assert!((18..=99).contains(&older));\\n        assert_eq!(balance_age(1.0, 0, 0), 24);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(399.0), 0);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(400.0), 1);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(650.0), 2);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(850.0), 3);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(24.0), 0);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/core.rs\",\"offset\":120,\"limit\":160,\"raw_output\":\"    pub t: f32,\\n    pub amp: f32,\\n    pub phase: [f32; 4],\\n    pub kick_in: f32,\\n    pub gust: Vec2,\\n    pub kicks: bool,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for BalanceCore {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            cob: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            vel: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            tip_t: 0.0,\\n            tipped: false,\\n            t: 0.0,\\n            amp: 0.12,\\n            phase: [0.4, 1.7, 2.2, 0.9],\\n            kick_in: 1.4,\\n            gust: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            kicks: true,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl BalanceCore {\\n    pub fn wobble(&self) -> Vec2 {\\n        let ax = |t: f32, a: f32, b: f32| {\\n            self.amp * (0.7 * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 1.3 * t + a).sin() + 0.3 * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 2.9 * t + b).sin())\\n        };\\n        Vec2::new(ax(self.t, self.phase[0], self.phase[1]), ax(self.t, self.phase[2], self.phase[3]))\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Advance one tick. `lean` is already shaped, in the disc.\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, rng: &mut crate::rng::Rng) {\\n        self.tipped = false;\\n        let target = lean.clamp_length_max(1.0) * rules.reach + self.wobble();\\n        let acc = (target - self.cob) * rules.stiffness - self.vel * rules.damping + self.gust;\\n        self.vel += acc * dt;\\n        if self.kicks {\\n            self.kick_in -= dt;\\n            if self.kick_in <= 0.0 {\\n                let ang = rng.range(0.0, std::f32::consts::TAU);\\n                self.vel += Vec2::new(ang.cos(), ang.sin()) * 0.1;\\n                self.kick_in = rng.range(1.0, 2.0);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.cob += self.vel * dt;\\n        self.t += dt;\\n        if self.cob.length() > 1.0 {\\n            self.tip_t += dt;\\n            if self.tip_t >= rules.tip_time {\\n                self.tipped = true;\\n                self.tip_t = 0.0;\\n                self.cob = self.cob.normalize_or_zero() * 0.72;\\n                self.vel = Vec2::ZERO;\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            self.tip_t = 0.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Step without the seeded wander, for the feel tests.\\n    pub fn step_clean(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32, rules: &Rules) {\\n        let mut rng = crate::rng::Rng::new(1);\\n        let kicks = self.kicks;\\n        self.kicks = false;\\n        let amp = self.amp;\\n        self.amp = 0.0;\\n        self.step(lean, dt, rules, &mut rng);\\n        self.amp = amp;\\n        self.kicks = kicks;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Balance Age. Better skill, more days and more stars all come out younger.\\npub fn balance_age(skill: f32, days_completed: u32, total_stars: u32) -> u8 {\\n    let skill = skill.clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    let age = 24.0 + 56.0 * (1.0 - skill).powf(1.1) - 2.0 * days_completed as f32 - (total_stars as f32 / 3.0).min(8.0);\\n    age.round().clamp(18.0, 99.0) as u8\\n}\\n\\npub fn stars_from_score(score: f32) -> u8 {\\n    if score >= 850.0 {\\n        3\\n    } else if score >= 650.0 {\\n        2\\n    } else if score >= 400.0 {\\n        1\\n    } else {\\n        0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn stars_from_plank(secs: f32) -> u8 {\\n    if secs >= 55.0 {\\n        3\\n    } else if secs >= 40.0 {\\n        2\\n    } else if secs >= 25.0 {\\n        1\\n    } else {\\n        0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn full_lean_settles_inside_the_disc() {\\n        let rules = Rules::default();\\n        let mut b = BalanceCore::default();\\n        b.kicks = false;\\n        b.amp = 0.0;\\n        let lean = Vec2::new(1.0, 0.0);\\n        let mut peak = 0.0_f32;\\n        for _ in 0..180 {\\n            b.step_clean(lean, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n            peak = peak.max(b.cob.length());\\n        }\\n        assert!(peak < 1.0, \\\"peak {peak}\\\");\\n        assert!(b.cob.x > 0.85, \\\"settled at {}\\\", b.cob.x);\\n        assert!(!b.tipped);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn a_hard_gust_tips_and_a_release_returns() {\\n        let rules = Rules::default();\\n        let mut b = BalanceCore::default();\\n        b.kicks = false;\\n        b.amp = 0.0;\\n        b.gust = Vec2::new(30.0, 0.0);\\n        let mut tipped = false;\\n        for _ in 0..120 {\\n            b.step_clean(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n            tipped |= b.tipped;\\n        }\\n        assert!(tipped, \\\"gust should tip within 2s\\\");\\n        b.gust = Vec2::ZERO;\\n        for _ in 0..180 {\\n            b.step_clean(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0, &rules);\\n        }\\n        assert!(b.cob.length() < 0.2, \\\"returned to {}\\\", b.cob);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn age_moves_the_right_way_and_stays_in_range() {\\n        let young = balance_age(1.0, 4, 30);\\n        let older = balance_age(0.0, 0, 0);\\n        assert!(young < older);\\n        assert!((18..=99).contains(&young));\\n        assert!((18..=99).contains(&older));\\n        assert_eq!(balance_age(1.0, 0, 0), 24);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(399.0), 0);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(400.0), 1);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(650.0), 2);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_score(850.0), 3);\\n        assert_eq!(stars_from_plank(24.0), 0);\\n\",\"total_lines\":284}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"54250258-5efe-4f90-bc53-a9a44f3ea0b1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_368","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Gust is added directly to acceleration as a separate term.\n\nWith stiffness 40 and a 30-unit gust, equilibrium settles at 0.75 inside the disc. The spring cancels the gust entirely, so the disc never tips. The test expects tipping, suggesting the gust magnitude may be too small or the spring should not fully counteract it.\n\nThe BOT controller cancels the gust by leaning. The test was written in a previous session and never executed. It expects a 30-unit gust to tip the disc within two seconds, but the physics formula prevents this. The next step is to increase the test gust magnitude so it exceeds the spring's restoring force.\n\nA 50-unit gust would tip the disc, but the test calls for a \"hard\" gust of 30. Changing the value to match physics may weaken the contract. The real issue might be that the gust is applied as a constant acceleration that the spring balances exactly, rather than a velocity kick.\n\nThe test author likely intended the gust to be added to the target offset rather than as raw acceleration. That would make equilibrium position equal to the gust magnitude, so a 30-unit gust would tip the disc instantly. Adding it to velocity each frame would cause an unbounded explosion.\n\nThe bot's cancel capacity is 36.8, so a 30-unit gust is fully cancellable. The test uses zero lean, meaning the player never cancels it. This confirms the physics model is sound and the test expectation is wrong.\n\nThe test will be updated to a 50-unit gust. That exceeds the spring's maximum restoring force of 40, so the disc tips past the rim and passes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4d8bc45b-ecd3-4afa-8887-c8cdf853b053-137","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"gust","glob":"**/PLAN.md","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4d8bc45b-ecd3-4afa-8887-c8cdf853b053-138","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"gust","glob":"**/games/fit/**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2029,"output_tokens":1089,"cache_read_input_tokens":165760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"f85e8f32-c662-406c-8d5e-3fd263879af3"}
