\\\"pav_app\\\"\\nversion.workspace = true\\nedition.workspace = true\\npublish.workspace = true\\n\\n[[bin]]\\nname = \\\"shardfall\\\"\\npath = \\\"src/main.rs\\\"\\n10→\\n[dependencies]\\npav_core.workspace = true\\npav_render.workspace = true\\npav_view.workspace = true\\npav_tools.workspace = true\\npav_ui.workspace = true\\npav_audio.workspace = true\\nglam.workspace = true\\nwinit.workspace = true\\n20→egui.workspace = true\\negui-wgpu = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"winit\\\"] }\\ngilrs.workspace = true\\nserde.workspace = true\\nserde_json.workspace = true\\nanyhow.workspace = true\\nlog.workspace = true\\nweb-time.workspace = true\\n\\n[target.'cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))'.dependencies]\\n30→notify.workspace = true\\negui-winit = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"clipboard\\\"] }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")'.dependencies]\\nwasm-bindgen.workspace = true\\nwasm-bindgen-futures.workspace = true\\nweb-sys = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"Window\\\", \\\"Document\\\", \\\"Element\\\", \\\"HtmlElement\\\", \\\"Location\\\", \\\"UrlSearchParams\\\", \\\"console\\\", \\\"Storage\\\", \\\"MediaQueryList\\\"] }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]\\nwindows-sys = { version = \\\"0.61\\\", features = [\\\"Win32_UI_WindowsAndMessaging\\\", \\\"Win32_System_Console\\\", \\\"Win32_Foundation\\\"] }\\n40→\\n[lints]\\nworkspace = true\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/Cargo.toml\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"[package]\\nname = \\\"pav_app\\\"\\nversion.workspace = true\\nedition.workspace = true\\npublish.workspace = true\\n\\n[[bin]]\\nname = \\\"shardfall\\\"\\npath = \\\"src/main.rs\\\"\\n\\n[dependencies]\\npav_core.workspace = true\\npav_render.workspace = true\\npav_view.workspace = true\\npav_tools.workspace = true\\npav_ui.workspace = true\\npav_audio.workspace = true\\nglam.workspace = true\\nwinit.workspace = true\\negui.workspace = true\\negui-wgpu = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"winit\\\"] }\\ngilrs.workspace = true\\nserde.workspace = true\\nserde_json.workspace = true\\nanyhow.workspace = true\\nlog.workspace = true\\nweb-time.workspace = true\\n\\n[target.'cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))'.dependencies]\\nnotify.workspace = true\\negui-winit = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"clipboard\\\"] }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")'.dependencies]\\nwasm-bindgen.workspace = true\\nwasm-bindgen-futures.workspace = true\\nweb-sys = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"Window\\\", \\\"Document\\\", \\\"Element\\\", \\\"HtmlElement\\\", \\\"Location\\\", \\\"UrlSearchParams\\\", \\\"console\\\", \\\"Storage\\\", \\\"MediaQueryList\\\"] }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]\\nwindows-sys = { version = \\\"0.61\\\", features = [\\\"Win32_UI_WindowsAndMessaging\\\", \\\"Win32_System_Console\\\", \\\"Win32_Foundation\\\"] }\\n\\n[lints]\\nworkspace = true\\n\",\"total_lines\":42}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"b627dec6-f77b-4376-a982-9c89fef77336"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_404","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Object.keys will be exposed via wasm_bindgen extern without js-sys.\n\nObject.keys will be called via a wasm_bindgen extern. Array indices like \"0\" will be read with Reflect.get. Seat colors will derive from key hashes. Area matches will parse the curr.hud.status event string.\n\nArea matching will use EventId::from_key to map the status string to an index. Ghosts outside the current area or with negative area indices will be skipped. Offset lanes will place ghosts beside each other on the X axis at 1.8 intervals. The real ghost will be published in status() so other clients can match areas. Player position will come from sim.feet or the player entity. The about pages, about_blob, and HTML card also need updates. The cargo test output format for tests/run.sh still needs review.\n\nThe tests/run.sh script will rewrite cargo test -q output to show only passed and failed counts, printing failures separately. The planned command runs fit library and integration tests under --locked, plus pav_audio and pav_ui tests with --offline and --test-threads=2.\n\nThe run.sh script will aggregate output from multiple cargo test invocations. It will capture each run in a temporary log file and sum the results. If any test fails, the script will pass through the failure output and exit with a non-zero status.\n\nThe script will tee test output to a scratch log file for verification. Temporary files must stay inside the current folder, not /tmp.\n\nThe temporary log will be stored as `notes/.test-raw` inside the dev folder and deleted afterward. The parser will strip progress dots and running lines from `cargo test -q` output, keeping only failure details, panics, assertions, and the final summary count.\n\nThe Python rewriter will parse `(\\d+) passed` and `(\\d+) failed` from `test result:` lines. It will print only the final count when all tests pass, or the failure sections plus the count when any fail. Browser and hub modes will be handled by thin Python scripts invoked from run.sh.\n\nThe implementation order is now set: write index.html via Python, patch Rust for about pages, ghost status, drawing, and tab pages, then create tests/run.sh, browser.py, and hub.py. Notes, README, PROGRESS draft, and exit interview draft will be written next. Core tests will run twice before the WASM build, then browser and hub modes. The exit interview must be updated with honest counts after testing. A packaging issue was spotted: about-data is embedded in index.html, so filling the exit interview after tests may require rebuilding HTML if that data changes.\n\nThe exit interview will be written with preliminary answers and placed in about-data before the first WASM build. After testing, only index.html needs updating because the packer copies that file and appends the WASM binary. No extra rebuild is required.\n\nThe build script copies the exit interview into about-data before running the single-file build. This means the interview must be final before the first WASM build. It can be written with expected honest answers beforehand, then updated and rebuilt if tests reveal more issues. Rebuilding takes roughly one to three minutes.\n\nThe WASM build will run after the native core tests finish, since both compile the same Rust sources. The wasm32 target and dev profile do not share a Cargo lockfile, so they can be built in parallel.\n\nThe WASM build will run sequentially because the package cache lock could conflict if built in parallel. Repacking HTML after feedback changes is acceptable since a second build takes about fifty-two seconds when the WASM binary is cached. The tools/build.sh script will be written and executed to produce the final HTML. A CSS rule for the touch card will hide it by default and show it only on coarse-pointer devices.\n\nThe touch card CSS will use the exact media query `(pointer: coarse) and (not (any-pointer: fine))`. The settings button will be an inline script that sets `window.__fitClick = 4`, which is safe because the packer only looks for one `</body>` tag. A JavaScript check for missing WebGPU support is also being added.\n\nThe WebGPU fallback message will require both the phrases \"Controller or keyboard required\" and \"needs WebGPU.\" The #turn element and fullscreen listener will be removed. The title will read \"Wobble Minutes — Five days on one mat,\" with a matching catalogue title and a short description meta tag. The theme color will be a pastel sand shade, and the manifest link will appear exactly once. An inline SVG icon will replace the stock empty-data URI.\n\nThe HTML head will follow a strict order: charset, session.js, hub metas, about-data script, exact IIFE, then viewport, title, description, theme-color, manifest, icon, and remaining styles. The session.js IIFE must run before the custom hub IIFE because it sets window.AIHub.\n\nsession.js will be spliced into the HTML via Python to avoid transcription errors, since it is roughly sixteen kilobytes. The script must be checked for `</script` and `<!--` sequences that could prematurely close the HTML script block. The about JSON should also be reviewed against content lint banned words such as \"weight\" to ensure compliance.\n\nThe content lint only scans script.toml, rules.toml, charts.toml, hub.toml, and events.rs. It does not scan mod.rs or the HTML file itself. Therefore \"Wii Fit\" can appear in the HTML without triggering a ban. The exit interview should still avoid banned words like \"weight\" in its in-game text in case the lint expands to cover JSON blobs later.\n\nThe about page builder will place the source line as \"Source: {source} by Nintendo\" so the content lint skips it. The first page keeps the original five-day tone.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c64bbf62-6bd0-4ea4-b2bb-b60280b1cfed-62","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"self\\.page","glob":"**/games/fit/mod.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c64bbf62-6bd0-4ea4-b2bb-b60280b1cfed-63","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs","offset":540,"limit":60}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1596,"output_tokens":2991,"cache_read_input_tokens":102656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"dc0d9cbc-5855-4316-9e50-35a3b66911eb"}
