{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_406","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"EventId::from_key is public. EventId can be cast to i32 because it is a fieldless enum.\n\nWriting all files now. Checking session.js for script tags and comments before embedding it exactly. Will read the long-running skill before cargo builds.\n\nThe IIFE will be copied exactly from PLAN. exit-interview.json will be written first with honest feedback, then embedded in the initial index.html. build.sh will replace the script contents later. Drafting honest testing feedback now.\n\nSix issues were identified in the simulation and shell. They include a gust test mismatch, a dropped egui texture delta, a private intent module, fonts bound too late, a ghost field typed as boolean, and About pages that failed to advance. One critical issue was also noted.\n\nThe font atlas panic is the only critical issue, since it stops the browser frame loop. The gust test mismatch was a test bug, not a game bug.\n\nThe bot playthrough on three seeds and per-event star checks were the most helpful. A blank 1080p WebGPU screenshot is the least helpful due to readback limits.\n\nEngine highlights include one sim tick, headless tests, egui as a pure view, and the puppet.\n\nGust is acceleration, not a force that tips by itself. The egui 0.36 TexturesDelta drop and the wasm String constructor are also stuck issues. Pause still increments ticks.\n\nThe balance game, flow, events, and synth are built. The hardest part was fitting a new game into the app frame loop without engine chrome and keys, plus the wasm/JS bridge without js-sys.\n\nChanges include frozen() early return, InputFrame fields, HudFrame.fit, audio mixer song beds, weblink, fit bindings, hide chrome, BigSplash/Wake, puppet tilt, capture has_ui, and headless font warmup.\n\nThe prompt was specific enough to build a whole game, but filenames versus behaviour as the contract were confusing. The song map and listed names also conflicted. The hardest part was the full roster plus browser and hub checks on a 20GB machine.\n\nThe plan should note which sections are guidance when engine APIs differ. It should also explicitly state the gust-on-a-full-lean test in the physics formula.\n\nA documented way to publish string objects to JavaScript is needed, or dropped texture deltas must not panic.\n\nThe title was chosen by RNG from fifty riffs. No new web search was performed this session.\n\nThe aiHub entry for Wobble Minutes is now complete with name, tagline, description, type, genre, source, series, player count, and controls.\n\nThe aiHub entry now includes tags, usage note, date, plan reference, genre, perspective, and technical details. The engine stack is Shardfall/Pavilion on commit 49ef2ba with wasm-bindgen 0.2.129. Art is engine cel style with high-key pastel beach props. Animation uses the engine puppet plus tilt about the feet.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-57174e89-330b-4f05-972f-25f33740e3e2-67","name":"list_dir","input":{"target_directory":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-57174e89-330b-4f05-972f-25f33740e3e2-68","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"</script|<script|<!--","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/hub/session.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1807,"output_tokens":1355,"cache_read_input_tokens":108288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"23e51a82-e33d-4bbc-ac98-5044d40a6f88"}
