{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_419","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"PuppetFrame is located in the frame module.\n\nPuppetFrame::new takes Shape and Color. Ghosts will be drawn as spheres with radius 0.0. Their positions are calculated from feet coordinates plus a Y offset of 0.9 to align the figure's base.\n\nAll patches will be applied and files written. The dev items page will remain unchanged to avoid breaking tests. exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, README, decisions, tests, tools, and index.html will be created via Python. The HTML generator will be a one-shot command or kept logic in tools/build.sh. The about-data script will be designed for easy JSON replacement.\n\nThe about-data script will use `type=\"application/json\"` and compact JSON to avoid escaping issues. The Python script will embed the interview data using `json.dumps`. Player counts in meta will be written as \"1-4\" with a hyphen rather than an en-dash, which the harness regex already handles. I also need to verify that \"ghost\" is accepted by modeOf.\n\nThe browser test script will use Playwright to launch Chromium with WebGPU flags against a local file URL. It targets a 320x180 viewport and verifies game status, tick advancement, pad stubs, keyboard input, mouse hover and clicks on UI rectangles, prompt changes, and Xbox settings.\n\nBrowser tests will wait roughly ten seconds for the attract phase to end before checking that input exits it. Music verification requires patching AudioBufferSourceNode and confirming non-silent buffers after a user gesture unlocks the audio context, since attract mode is silent. The test plan includes iPhone 13 and iPad device emulation via Playwright.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-edcf30a5-2dc2-4cc3-ac9e-ab569973400d-86","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"capture","glob":"**/pav_tools/src/main.rs","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-edcf30a5-2dc2-4cc3-ac9e-ab569973400d-87","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn capture|capture","glob":"**/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":576,"output_tokens":972,"cache_read_input_tokens":132224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"ad5fa84d-c5a1-497b-8c36-c08ff638068e"}
