{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_427","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Testing will be done via `sim.play().unwrap()`.\n\nAbout menu flow is verified. Clicking About triggers ACT_ABOUT without device 4. TAB_R activates the menu. fit_ui runs after both steps. Idle increments and 600 ticks trigger attract mode. Title clicks work correctly.\n\nAbout menu pages are planned. Page 0 shows a Source line with feedback names and usage. Page 1 shows \"Five days\". Page 2 shows Testing Feedback. Page 3 shows Engine Feedback. Page 4 shows Prompt Feedback. Page 5 shows Fonts. The test will verify page 0 has Source and that two TAB_R presses reach the Testing Feedback heading.\n\nAll three feedback headings will be placed on page 0 of the fallback text. This lets the first About screen satisfy acceptance criteria without requiring a tab press. The detailed answers remain on later pages.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bbe0972-1877-4872-87fe-0b0f19fd4d2d-95","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn kind_now","glob":"**/games/fit/mod.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1133,"output_tokens":1257,"cache_read_input_tokens":140800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"5b8bfbef-edbe-46f9-ae50-7c782a774563"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1bbe0972-1877-4872-87fe-0b0f19fd4d2d-95","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,103,97,109,101,115,47,102,105,116,47,109,111,100,46,114,115,10,54,56,50,58,32,32,32,32,102,110,32,107,105,110,100,95,110,111,119,40,38,115,101,108,102,41,32,45,62,32,79,112,116,105,111,110,60,69,118,101,110,116,73,100,62,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":682,\"content\":\"    fn kind_now(&self) -> Option<EventId> {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"6e487ffd-818a-406f-a355-581d951c8b4d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_428","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"EventId works as an i32 for fieldless enums in Rust.\n\nConfirmed entity access via sim.state.entities.get. Drafting ghost_json to serialize player position and facing from the simulation state.\n\nRealized calling `sim.player()` and `sim.feet()` in the same statement would cause a double borrow of `sim`. Will split the code to avoid this conflict.\n\nSplit the ghost_json logic into two sequential statements to avoid double borrowing sim. Vec3 is already imported. Will add a test next. The hub_ghosts function belongs in weblink.rs because bind functions are public.\n\nDefined a `HubGhost` struct to hold ghost data. `hub_ghosts()` will use `#[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]` to return real ghosts on WASM and an empty vector elsewhere. The `read_hub_ghosts` helper is also gated behind that same cfg.\n\nImplementing `read_hub_ghosts` to fetch the `__hub` object from the global window, read its `ghosts` property, and extract the keys array length via `bind::object_keys`.\n\nIterating over the first eight ghost keys. Extracting area, position, and facing from each ghost object using js_f32 and js_vec3.\n\nFinished the `read_hub_ghosts` loop by extracting the `lean` vector and deriving the seat from the ghost key. Noted that `bind::get` requires a `&JsValue` for its key argument, so `&key.as_str().into()` needs an explicit temporary binding. Started drafting the `js_f32` helper.\n\nCompleted the `js_f32` and `js_vec3` helpers. They extract numeric values from `JsValue` objects, with `js_vec3` supporting both indexed and named keys. Both are gated behind `#[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]`. The `object_keys` binding will use `js_name` in the extern block. `boot_about` needs similar WASM-only wrappers.\n\nPatching `apply_browser_save` to capture the about string in a closure. The closure moves both `about` and `saved` into the `host.exec` block. If the game is not fit, `get_mut` returns None and the code exits before touching about.\n\nThe HTML generator will be a separate file in tools so build.sh can refresh about-data without regenerating the entire page. build.sh will use Python to replace only the JSON content of the about-data script. The manifest link will remain. The icon will be an inline SVG data URI, kept as a single line.\n\nSet the page title to \"Wobble Minutes — Five days, one mat\". The description describes Tippy Cay as a pastel resort staffed by talking gym gear. Set the theme color to #f4e7d4. Added a touch-card HTML block for controller or keyboard requirements with a settings button. Started drafting CSS.\n\nThe touch card will use `display: none` by default and reveal itself via a media query for coarse pointers. The `hidden` attribute is avoided because it would override the media query. The settings button will be styled large for touch. The loader script is a module, while the card script can be classic or placed inside the module.\n\nThe touch-card logic will live in a classic script inside the body so it runs even if the module fails. It adds a click listener to the settings button, removes the card on keydown, and polls for gamepads.\n\nThe touch-card script polls gamepads every 250 ms and removes the card when any button is pressed. The page will use a single closing `</body>` tag. The no-webgpu module will replace message children with both sentences. Loading text will appear in `document.title`. Phone fullscreen is removed. The mutation observer stays. CSS will include `touch-action: none` so the game fills the viewport. Canvas styling remains unchanged. The `#msg` element stays for loading and no-webgpu states.\n\nThe no-webgpu path must keep both sentences in the message element. The touch card may also appear on phones without WebGPU, which is acceptable. Desktop Chromium hides the card because it reports a fine pointer. Playwright phone profiles emulate coarse pointers, so the media query will match.\n\nA JavaScript class will be added to the HTML element when `matchMedia` detects a coarse pointer without a fine one. The CSS will use this class as a fallback to show the touch card, since some Playwright versions report media queries inconsistently.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bc22af97-7eb3-4b5e-9ffe-f414f20606c7-96","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"URLSearchParams|playMs|scenario","glob":"**/hub/harness.html","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1529,"output_tokens":3088,"cache_read_input_tokens":141824,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"d07001ab-139a-42a1-b395-326f26534690"}
