,\\n        \\\"back\\\" if pad => \\\"Circle\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"back\\\" if device == 3 => \\\"Right click\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"back\\\" => \\\"Esc\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"schedule\\\" if pad && xbox => \\\"Y\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"schedule\\\" if pad => \\\"Triangle\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"schedule\\\" => \\\"Tab\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"wave\\\" if pad && xbox => \\\"X\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"wave\\\" if pad => \\\"Square\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"wave\\\" => \\\"F\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"pause\\\" if pad && xbox => \\\"Menu\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"pause\\\" if pad => \\\"Options\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"pause\\\" => \\\"Esc\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"step_l\\\" if pad && xbox => \\\"LB\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"step_l\\\" if pad => \\\"L1\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"step_l\\\" if device == 3 => \\\"Left click\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"step_l\\\" => \\\"Q\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"step_r\\\" if pad && xbox => \\\"RB\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"step_r\\\" if pad => \\\"R1\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"step_r\\\" if device == 3 => \\\"Right click\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"step_r\\\" => \\\"E\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"brace\\\" if pad && xbox => \\\"LT+RT\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"brace\\\" if pad => \\\"L2+R2\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"brace\\\" => \\\"Q+E\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"lean\\\" if pad => \\\"Left stick\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"lean\\\" if device == 3 || device == 4 => \\\"Mouse\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"lean\\\" => \\\"WASD\\\".into(),\\n        other => other.into(),\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Up to six stacked cards, centred.\\npub fn stack_rects(n: usize) -> Vec<[f32; 4]> {\\n    let n = n.min(6);\\n    let h = 0.09;\\n\",\"total_lines\":90}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"ad20d4b9-5e75-420d-bc7f-b7baeab4f736"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_449","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Adding prompt and menu_focus to the status.\n\nExisting tests will remain unaffected. The browser test can read the new fields. For Xbox, the test will navigate to Settings and toggle the Xbox option. The status JSON already includes an xbox flag that becomes true after the click. This proves the setting was applied.\n\nThe prompt starts as Cross. It switches to Space for keyboard and Click for mouse. The test will toggle the Xbox setting in Settings, then press a pad button to verify the prompt becomes A. Last device input wins. The sequence begins with a brief pad press, then a south press.\n\nThe test will stay on the title screen for all steps. It uses pad, keyboard, and mouse to advance menu focus and change the prompt glyph. Then it clicks Settings to enter that phase.\n\nSettings is not a pregame menu, so attract mode cannot start from there. The test will return to the title screen after toggling the Xbox setting, wait about ten seconds for attract idle, then press a key to resume title.\n\nThe full test will run twice to satisfy the 320×180 requirement. Music verification patches the audio node to accumulate RMS and checks that the buffer is non-silent after the gesture exits attract mode. The native test covers the exact volume ratio.\n\nThe browser test will record the music buffer's peak amplitude. It will assert that the buffer is non-silent and that status.music equals 0.10. A single page cannot compare two gains, so the exact ratio check remains in the native test.\n\nThe browser test will verify that status.music is 0.10 and that a started audio buffer has RMS greater than zero.\n\nFor the 320×180 check, the test will read the canvas width and height from both the drawing buffer and the CSS client dimensions.\n\nThe canvas width and height will be checked against the viewport, allowing a one-pixel tolerance. For the phone test, Playwright devices such as iPhone 13 or iPad Pro 11 will be used. Chromium must have WebGPU enabled via flags. The card text must remain visible, and the test will assert that the required controller or keyboard message appears.\n\nAttract mode lasts 600 ticks. On a phone viewport the simulation may run slower than 60 fps, so the idle wait must be longer than ten seconds. The iPhone SE is 320 by 568 pixels, which is still taller than 180, and at roughly 30 fps that duration equals about twenty seconds.\n\nThe test will wait up to forty seconds for attract mode to begin. Tapping the Settings button in the touch card will use its bounding box center. WebGPU flags are unnecessary on WebKit iPhone. The controller message must contain both required phrases.\n\nThe browser test will launch WebKit headlessly on the iPhone 13 device profile. It will skip canvas readiness checks.\n\nTwo engine captures will be run with `pav_tools` at 1920 by 1080 resolution. One capture covers forty ticks of the fit scene. The other covers four hundred ticks of the fit, event, or pose scene. Each capture runs twice and the outputs are compared.\n\nThe engine directory must be the working directory for `pav capture` so level files resolve correctly. Headless WebGPU is expected to work on this machine. A blank check will use ImageMagick's standard deviation metric, and two captures of the same scene should have similar mean colors. The PNG outputs will be read directly after capture.\n\nThe browser sound check is optional if the unit test passes. The status JSON will include `menu_focus` and `prompt`. I will write the files now. I also need to verify that clicking Settings from the title screen works with mouse input via `__gameUi` coordinates.\n\nThe hit test uses physical pixels, so a CSS coordinate click aligns with the published `__gameUi` rectangle when the device pixel ratio is one. Hovering a rectangle centers the cursor and triggers mouse input once travel exceeds six pixels. I will now write the page and scripts.\n\nThe HTML generator will remain `tools/write_index.py` and run from `build.sh`. The script will generate the page from `session.js` and the exit interview. `build.sh` will then compile the single-file fit scene with the title, description, theme color, and output path.\n\nThe catalogue title already appears in index.html, so build.sh passes it explicitly as a safeguard. The em dash in the title is safe for HTML escaping and packer replacement. Player count meta will read \"1-4\", which the harness regex accepts.\n\nThe player count meta will use an en dash, not a hyphen. A byte-compare helper will be added to hub.py. The hub serve directory will be copied to scratch/hub-serve/ so the repository stays clean; the game HTML is large. Four iframes loading 11 MB of WASM may need a timeout of two or three minutes. The harness itself has a twenty-second ready timeout, but the test will wait for data-complete instead.\n\nFour concurrent WASM compilations might exceed the timeout. Font panics could prevent `__gameStatus` from appearing, though fonts are already fixed; a constructor failure would show a console error. The packer rejects inline JavaScript snippets, so the `DomString` import workaround is unavailable.\n\nThe extern constructor is the correct approach. If it fails, a plain string will be published alongside a parallel object so JSON.parse still works for the IIFE. The browser test reads window.__gameStatus.tick directly, so a plain string would leave that property undefined.\n\nThe IIFE cannot be changed, so the status must be a String object. The current `DomString` constructor approach will be tried first; if the WASM build fails, an alternative will be found.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-06037886-c8a4-4cc2-a0bf-fdd02896c9a4-133","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs","old_string":"            \"touch_card\": self.touch_only,","new_string":"            \"touch_card\": self.touch_only,\n            \"menu_focus\": self.focus,\n            \"prompt\": fit_ui::prompt(\"confirm\", self.device, self.settings.xbox),"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":793,"output_tokens":3075,"cache_read_input_tokens":170624,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"2897f4ea-b3ad-4dc1-b5f8-aa76853a21f7"}
