\"xbox\\\"] {\",\"new_line\":225,\"context_before\":\"        let Some(win) = web_sys::window() else { return };\\n        let obj = bind::string_obj(status);\\n        if let Ok(parsed) = bind::parse(status) {\\n\",\"context_after\":\"                if let Ok(v) = bind::get(&parsed, &(*key).into()) {\\n                    let _ = bind::set(&obj, &(*key).into(), &v);\\n                }\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"364c3e03-0480-4a91-b53b-90e6a4d45948"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_451","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing exit-interview.json and a Python script to build index.html and tests.\n\nWriting the remaining files: README, decisions, PROGRESS, run.sh, browser.py, hub.py, and build.sh. The Python script will be placed in the dev tools folder. The test runner will handle core Rust tests, browser checks, hub checks, and an all-in-one mode.\n\nCore tests will print exactly `N passed, 0 failed`. The all mode will output one combined line. The cargo parser will read the quiet test output.\n\nThe cargo parser will use a Python script to extract pass and fail counts from test output. It will match the \"test result\" line with regex and suppress noise like dots and \"running\" lines.\n\nThe cargo parser will also catch compiler errors when `cargo test` fails. If the exit code is non-zero, it prints the full output so compile failures are visible.\n\nThe test runner will use `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8` and run with `--offline --locked --test-threads=2`. Core tests will be filtered to the `games::fit` module to avoid running 98 unrelated library tests. The Python summarizer will receive output via a heredoc, with an extra `--keep-errors` flag when cargo itself fails.\n\npav_ui and pav_audio tests will run together. I verified they do not require a device. I am writing the files in parallel now. The IIFE boot script must match PLAN.md lines 401-431 exactly, including special spaces.\n\nThe boot script initializes the hub state and scene. It reads the AI hub seed from the URL query string. It connects to the hub as a ghost player with seats 1 and 4. It checks for WebGPU support. It reports a zero status before the first hub update arrives.\n\nThe boot script polls `window.__gameStatus` every 50 milliseconds until it is ready. It reports the initial score and stats once, then sends periodic progress updates while the hub session is active.\n\nThe boot script will be embedded as a raw string in the Python build script. The exit interview JSON will be escaped so that `<` characters become `\\u003c`, preventing them from closing the script tag.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-58654dc1-d64c-4cb7-aaeb-3631f191af5f-135","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/STAGE.md","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":619,"output_tokens":1697,"cache_read_input_tokens":174464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"a425141a-8e8b-40a2-bd0c-751c81366f87"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-58654dc1-d64c-4cb7-aaeb-3631f191af5f-135","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/STAGE.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"3f700f6e-04c9-4536-b658-fef6766f5734"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_452","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"PROGRESS.md must be present and current.\n\nWriting files in batches. browser.py will manage one browser at a time and close contexts to save memory. PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE must be exported directly in the script because non-interactive shells may not source ~/.bashrc. Headless Playwright should not need xvfb, but xvfb-run is a fallback if Chromium fails.\n\nPad button presses will be held for roughly 200 ms before release so the game registers a single edge event. This ensures MENU_DOWN moves focus by exactly one step.\n\nKeyboard presses will use keydown, wait 100 ms, then keyup to avoid flakiness. Mouse moves will be followed by a wait. After returning to the title screen, input will be paused for 11 seconds so the attract mode can run uninterrupted.\n\nThe script will poll for attract mode or demo state for up to 14 seconds. Returning to the title from settings requires clicking the \"Back\" item in __gameUi. The boot sequence will press South, wait, release, and verify menu focus is 1. It will then press ArrowDown, wait, and verify focus is 2. A mouse move by 20 pixels in an empty area of the top screen will follow.\n\nThe boot sequence will hover over \"Settings\" to update menu focus. It will then enter settings, toggle the Glyphs or Xbox option, and return to the title screen. After waiting up to 15 seconds for attract mode, it will press Space to exit attract and verify the demo flag clears. It will also confirm music status is 0.10 and audio buffers are non-silent after the space press. A canvas size check runs at startup, and the errors array must remain empty.\n\nWebGPU warnings will be recorded but ignored unless they indicate a real failure. The full boot check will run twice to satisfy the requirement of booting twice. Phone, tablet, and iPhone WebKit contexts will each use a fresh browser instance with their respective device settings.\n\nThe browser script will invoke the Pav capture binary via cargo. Two captures per boot will be compared with RMSE to confirm agreement. A launch-error.log will be written if capture fails to start. Blank output is treated as a failure rather than a fallback.\n\nhub.py will copy the harness, bridge, round, session.js, and HTML into scratch/serve. It will start a Python HTTP server on port 0 bound to 127.0.0.1 and parse the assigned port from stderr using a background thread. A non-blank check will run before declaring success.\n\nThe HTTP server will be launched via subprocess.Popen with stderr redirected to stdout, and the assigned port will be parsed from the startup message. Playwright will then open one browser per scenario, navigate to the harness URL, wait for data-complete, and verify __hubCheck.pass.\n\nFour scenarios are planned: two players with auto mode, three players with auto mode plus latency, jitter, and loss, four players with the same network parameters, and two players with host-leave.\n\nThe host-leave scenario will use two players without extra latency. A solo test will open the game page directly, press Enter and Space, verify AIHub.active and AIHub.seeded are false, confirm no page errors, and check that ticks advance. The first script tag in the HTML starting with /*! aihub-session will be compared byte-for-byte against hub/session.js.\n\nThe embedded session.js script will be extracted from the HTML by locating the `/*! aihub-session` header and the following `</script>` tag. It will then be compared against the disk file, with whitespace differences allowed.\n\nThe embedded session.js script will be wrapped in `<script>` tags with no extra whitespace, so the bytes between the tags must match the file exactly.\n\nThe session.js script will be wrapped in `<script>` tags with no extra whitespace so the bytes between the tags match the file exactly. run.sh will be made executable via chmod. PROGRESS.md will be updated at the end to reflect current status and next steps. The test Click path is safe because confirm and click do not conflict.\n\nThe first step runs after the title screen is fully built, so Click(5) will match correctly. TAB_R and CONFIRM bit flags do not conflict. tools/build.sh and write_index.py are also needed. JSON quotes in the exit interview require careful handling.\n\nnotes/feedback.md will be created to track running test counts. PLAN.md will receive a ## Deviations section for any deviations found, plus checkboxes in the goal plan at the end once verified. The FitGame implementation correctly splits player and feet borrows.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The sim now publishes a real ghost sample and turns the About pages. Next I’ll put the hub page and the test command in place."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d445f73c-6955-4a68-aaea-9db0922b9b99-136","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json","content":"{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 22:21:32\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Third person\",\n    \"tech\": \"Shardfall engine (Pavilion: Rust, wgpu, egui 0.36.2), commit 49ef2ba, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's cel look, high-key pastel, beach and wellness props. Library props only for generic dressing.\",\n    \"animation\": \"Engine puppet, tilted about the feet by the balance dot. Motion clips are the engine library.\",\n    \"audio\": \"Music, effects and voices are synthesized in code. No audio files. Seven music beds, default music gain 0.10. At least 30 effects. Animalese voices.\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players. The round is the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup).\",\n    \"testing\": \"Headless sim tests, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU at 320×180, phone and tablet profiles, WebKit iPhone fallback, and the AI Hub harness.\",\n    \"research\": \"The build followed PLAN.md and the engine source. The title was drawn with a real RNG from 50 riffs. No separate web search in this session.\",\n    \"environment\": \"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\",\n    \"model\": \"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\",\n    \"usage\": \"added on import\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"Six defects showed up in testing: a gust check that did not match the acceleration model, an egui texture delta dropped on the floor, a private intent module, fonts bound in the same pass that drew them, a hub ghost field that was a boolean, and About pages that did not turn.\",\n    \"One was critical. The font and texture-delta panic stops the browser frame loop, so the page sits there with a status that never ticks.\",\n    \"The most helpful test was the bot playthrough: three seeds from New Stay to the credits, plus each event on five seeds against an idle player.\",\n    \"The least helpful check is a 1920×1080 WebGPU screenshot. On this machine that bitmap can come back blank while the sim is fine. 320×180 is the timing check, and the engine's own capture is the picture.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"The sim is one tick you can drive with no GPU, and the picture is a pure view of that tick. That split is what made the whole stay testable.\",\n    \"Yes. A gust is an acceleration, so gust 30 with no lean settles inside the disc and does not tip. egui 0.36 panics if a TexturesDelta is dropped. Pause still increments the tick; the world time is what freezes.\",\n    \"The balance model, the day loop, and every event. The engine does not have a centre-of-pressure verb.\",\n    \"The app frame. The demo's keys, menus and chrome run in the same function as the game, and a fit frame has to turn all of that off without breaking the engine's other scenes.\",\n    \"frozen() returns early inside the tick. InputFrame gained lean, device, ui and hub. The HUD carries the fit UI and a status string. The mixer plays song beds. The page bridge publishes status. Captures composite the fit UI. Puppets tilt about the feet. Splash and a silent wake were added for the lagoon.\",\n    \"A supported way to publish one JSON value that is both a string (for JSON.parse) and an object (for .tick), without hand-rolling a String constructor.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The plan is specific about the feel, the roster and the hub snippet, and it says behaviour is the contract when a filename does not match the engine.\",\n    \"Song numbers in the plan and the beds the sim actually requests do not use the same index. The hub snippet sends whatever status.hub.ghost is, so a boolean there is sent as a boolean.\",\n    \"Shipping the full roster, the 10-foot shell and the hub harness on a 20 GB machine where one extra browser gets killed.\",\n    \"Say, next to the gust sentence, that a full lean alone must not tip and a gust on top of that lean must. State that plan filenames are guidance in the same paragraph as the file tree.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Wobble Minutes\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Five days, one mat\",\n    \"description\": \"A third-person balance comedy at Tippy Cay. Lean through a week of sports mini-games, then stand still when it matters.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"series\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Lean with the stick, WASD or the mouse. Confirm with Cross, Space or click.\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"third-person\", \"sports\", \"comedy\", \"low-poly\", \"versus\"]\n  }\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d445f73c-6955-4a68-aaea-9db0922b9b99-137","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/tools/write_index.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Write engine/web/index.html with session.js pasted byte for byte and about-data filled.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport pathlib\n\nDEV = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nWORK = DEV.parent\nSESSION = (DEV / \"hub\" / \"session.js\").read_bytes()\nINTERVIEW = json.loads((WORK / \"exit-interview.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\nABOUT = json.dumps(INTERVIEW, ensure_ascii=False).replace(\"<\", \"\\\\u003c\")\n\nIIFE = r\"\"\"(() => {\n  const boot = window.__gameBoot = { scene: null, seed: null, today: Math.floor(Date.now() / 86400000),\n                                     about: document.getElementById('about-data')?.textContent ?? '' };\n  if (!window.AIHub || !AIHub.active) return;\n  const hub = window.__hub = { go: false, ended: false, players: [], me: 0, ghosts: {} };\n  boot.scene = 'fit/medley';\n  boot.seed = Number((/[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(location.search) || [])[1] || 1);\n  AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\n    if (!info) { location.replace(location.pathname); return; }   // no hub after all\n    if (!navigator.gpu) { AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU'); return; }\n    hub.me = info.me; hub.players = info.players;\n    // Before the first status arrives, report a zero: the hub must always hear a number.\n    const status = () => { try { return JSON.parse(window.__gameStatus || 'null')?.hub ?? null; } catch { return null; } };\n    const waitReady = () => (window.__gameStatus ? AIHub.ready() : setTimeout(waitReady, 50));\n    waitReady();\n    let reported = false;\n    const report = () => { if (reported) return; reported = true; const s = status(); AIHub.result({ score: s?.score ?? 0, stats: s?.stats ?? {} }); };\n    setInterval(() => {\n      if (AIHub.time() < 0 || hub.ended) return;\n      hub.go = true;\n      const s = status();\n      AIHub.progress({ score: s?.score ?? 0, label: s?.label ?? 'Warming up' });\n      if (!reported) AIHub.send(s?.ghost ?? { area: -1 }, { reliable: false });\n      if (s?.done) report();\n    }, 100);\n    AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => { hub.ghosts[from] = data; });\n    AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { delete hub.ghosts[id]; });\n    AIHub.on('time-up', report);\n    AIHub.on('end', () => { hub.ended = true; });\n  });\n})();\n\"\"\"\n\nPAGE = \"\"\"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>\"\"\" + SESSION.decode(\"utf-8\") + \"\"\"</script>\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Highest total across three balance events wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n<script id=\"about-data\" type=\"application/json\">\"\"\" + ABOUT + \"\"\"</script>\n<script>\n\"\"\" + IIFE + \"\"\"\n</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\">\n<title>Wobble Minutes — Five days, one mat</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Lean through a week of balance games at Tippy Cay, a pastel resort staffed by talking gym gear.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#f4e7d4\">\n<meta name=\"mobile-web-app-capable\" content=\"yes\">\n<meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\" content=\"yes\">\n<meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\" content=\"black-translucent\">\n<link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"manifest.webmanifest\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='14' fill='%23f4e7d4'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='4' fill='%233b2a4a'/%3E%3C/svg%3E\">\n<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #f4e7d4; overscroll-behavior: none;\n               touch-action: none; -webkit-user-select: none; user-select: none; -webkit-touch-callout: none;\n               -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; }\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100vw !important; height: 100vh !important; height: 100dvh !important;\n           outline: none; touch-action: none; }\n  #msg { position: fixed; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n         font: 18px system-ui, sans-serif; color: #3b2a4a; text-align: center; padding: 24px; pointer-events: none; }\n  #need { display: none; position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 6; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n          flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; background: rgba(244, 231, 212, 0.92); color: #3b2a4a;\n          font: 28px system-ui, sans-serif; text-align: center; padding: 24px; }\n  #need p { margin: 0; max-width: 18ch; }\n  #need-settings { font: 22px system-ui, sans-serif; padding: 14px 28px; border: 0; border-radius: 14px;\n                   background: #3b2a4a; color: #f4e7d4; }\n  @media (pointer: coarse) and (not (any-pointer: fine)) { #need { display: flex; } }\n  html.touch-only #need { display: flex; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"msg\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading Wobble Minutes…</div>\n<div id=\"need\"><p>Controller or keyboard required</p><button type=\"button\" id=\"need-settings\">Settings</button></div>\n<script>\n  const coarseOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches;\n  if (coarseOnly) document.documentElement.classList.add('touch-only');\n  const needBtn = document.getElementById('need-settings');\n  if (needBtn) needBtn.addEventListener('click', () => { window.__fitClick = 4; });\n  const dropNeed = () => { const n = document.getElementById('need'); if (n) n.remove(); };\n  addEventListener('keydown', dropNeed);\n  setInterval(() => {\n    const pads = navigator.getGamepads ? navigator.getGamepads() : [];\n    for (const p of pads) if (p && p.buttons && [...p.buttons].some((b) => b.pressed)) dropNeed();\n  }, 250);\n</script>\n<script type=\"module\">\n  const name = document.title;\n  const msg = document.getElementById('msg');\n  if (!navigator.gpu) {\n    msg.replaceChildren('Controller or keyboard required', document.createElement('br'),\n      `${name} needs WebGPU.`, document.createElement('br'),\n      'Use a recent Chrome, Edge or Safari (iOS 26 or later) with hardware acceleration enabled.');\n  } else {\n    new MutationObserver((_, obs) => {\n      const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\n      if (c) { c.setAttribute('aria-label', `${name} game`); msg.remove(); c.focus(); obs.disconnect(); }\n    }).observe(document.body, { childList: true });\n    try {\n      if (window.loadGame) await window.loadGame();\n      else await (await import('./shardfall.js')).default();\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(`${name} failed to load:`, error);\n      msg.textContent = `${name} could not load. Please reload the page. If it still fails, check that WebGPU and hardware acceleration are enabled.`;\n      document.body.append(msg);\n    }\n  }\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n\"\"\"\n\nout = DEV / \"engine\" / \"web\" / \"index.html\"\nout.write_text(PAGE, encoding=\"utf-8\")\ntext = out.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\nstart = text.index(\"/*! aihub-session\")\nend = text.index(\"</script>\", start)\npasted = text[start:end].encode(\"utf-8\")\nif pasted != SESSION:\n    raise SystemExit(f\"session.js paste mismatch: page {len(pasted)} file {len(SESSION)}\")\nprint(f\"wrote {out} ({out.stat().st_size} bytes), session.js matches\")\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1863,"output_tokens":5923,"cache_read_input_tokens":174976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"5278272c-b1cc-4272-abcc-e5cb5d582847"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d445f73c-6955-4a68-aaea-9db0922b9b99-136","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:21:32\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Shardfall engine (Pavilion: Rust, wgpu, egui 0.36.2), commit 49ef2ba, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's cel look, high-key pastel, beach and wellness props. Library props only for generic dressing.\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine puppet, tilted about the feet by the balance dot. Motion clips are the engine library.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Music, effects and voices are synthesized in code. No audio files. Seven music beds, default music gain 0.10. At least 30 effects. Animalese voices.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players. The round is the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup).\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU at 320×180, phone and tablet profiles, WebKit iPhone fallback, and the AI Hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The build followed PLAN.md and the engine source. The title was drawn with a real RNG from 50 riffs. No separate web search in this session.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Six defects showed up in testing: a gust check that did not match the acceleration model, an egui texture delta dropped on the floor, a private intent module, fonts bound in the same pass that drew them, a hub ghost field that was a boolean, and About pages that did not turn.\\\",\\n    \\\"One was critical. The font and texture-delta panic stops the browser frame loop, so the page sits there with a status that never ticks.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the bot playthrough: three seeds from New Stay to the credits, plus each event on five seeds against an idle player.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful check is a 1920×1080 WebGPU screenshot. On this machine that bitmap can come back blank while the sim is fine. 320×180 is the timing check, and the engine's own capture is the picture.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The sim is one tick you can drive with no GPU, and the picture is a pure view of that tick. That split is what made the whole stay testable.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A gust is an acceleration, so gust 30 with no lean settles inside the disc and does not tip. egui 0.36 panics if a TexturesDelta is dropped. Pause still increments the tick; the world time is what freezes.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance model, the day loop, and every event. The engine does not have a centre-of-pressure verb.\\\",\\n    \\\"The app frame. The demo's keys, menus and chrome run in the same function as the game, and a fit frame has to turn all of that off without breaking the engine's other scenes.\\\",\\n    \\\"frozen() returns early inside the tick. InputFrame gained lean, device, ui and hub. The HUD carries the fit UI and a status string. The mixer plays song beds. The page bridge publishes status. Captures composite the fit UI. Puppets tilt about the feet. Splash and a silent wake were added for the lagoon.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to publish one JSON value that is both a string (for JSON.parse) and an object (for .tick), without hand-rolling a String constructor.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan is specific about the feel, the roster and the hub snippet, and it says behaviour is the contract when a filename does not match the engine.\\\",\\n    \\\"Song numbers in the plan and the beds the sim actually requests do not use the same index. The hub snippet sends whatever status.hub.ghost is, so a boolean there is sent as a boolean.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping the full roster, the 10-foot shell and the hub harness on a 20 GB machine where one extra browser gets killed.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say, next to the gust sentence, that a full lean alone must not tip and a gust on top of that lean must. State that plan filenames are guidance in the same paragraph as the file tree.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Wobble Minutes\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Five days, one mat\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A third-person balance comedy at Tippy Cay. Lean through a week of sports mini-games, then stand still when it matters.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean with the stick, WASD or the mouse. Confirm with Cross, Space or click.\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"sports\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"low-poly\\\", \\\"versus\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:21:32\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Shardfall engine (Pavilion: Rust, wgpu, egui 0.36.2), commit 49ef2ba, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's cel look, high-key pastel, beach and wellness props. Library props only for generic dressing.\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine puppet, tilted about the feet by the balance dot. Motion clips are the engine library.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Music, effects and voices are synthesized in code. No audio files. Seven music beds, default music gain 0.10. At least 30 effects. Animalese voices.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players. The round is the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup).\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU at 320×180, phone and tablet profiles, WebKit iPhone fallback, and the AI Hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The build followed PLAN.md and the engine source. The title was drawn with a real RNG from 50 riffs. No separate web search in this session.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Six defects showed up in testing: a gust check that did not match the acceleration model, an egui texture delta dropped on the floor, a private intent module, fonts bound in the same pass that drew them, a hub ghost field that was a boolean, and About pages that did not turn.\\\",\\n    \\\"One was critical. The font and texture-delta panic stops the browser frame loop, so the page sits there with a status that never ticks.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the bot playthrough: three seeds from New Stay to the credits, plus each event on five seeds against an idle player.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful check is a 1920×1080 WebGPU screenshot. On this machine that bitmap can come back blank while the sim is fine. 320×180 is the timing check, and the engine's own capture is the picture.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The sim is one tick you can drive with no GPU, and the picture is a pure view of that tick. That split is what made the whole stay testable.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A gust is an acceleration, so gust 30 with no lean settles inside the disc and does not tip. egui 0.36 panics if a TexturesDelta is dropped. Pause still increments the tick; the world time is what freezes.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance model, the day loop, and every event. The engine does not have a centre-of-pressure verb.\\\",\\n    \\\"The app frame. The demo's keys, menus and chrome run in the same function as the game, and a fit frame has to turn all of that off without breaking the engine's other scenes.\\\",\\n    \\\"frozen() returns early inside the tick. InputFrame gained lean, device, ui and hub. The HUD carries the fit UI and a status string. The mixer plays song beds. The page bridge publishes status. Captures composite the fit UI. Puppets tilt about the feet. Splash and a silent wake were added for the lagoon.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to publish one JSON value that is both a string (for JSON.parse) and an object (for .tick), without hand-rolling a String constructor.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan is specific about the feel, the roster and the hub snippet, and it says behaviour is the contract when a filename does not match the engine.\\\",\\n    \\\"Song numbers in the plan and the beds the sim actually requests do not use the same index. The hub snippet sends whatever status.hub.ghost is, so a boolean there is sent as a boolean.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping the full roster, the 10-foot shell and the hub harness on a 20 GB machine where one extra browser gets killed.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say, next to the gust sentence, that a full lean alone must not tip and a gust on top of that lean must. State that plan filenames are guidance in the same paragraph as the file tree.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Wobble Minutes\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Five days, one mat\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A third-person balance comedy at Tippy Cay. Lean through a week of sports mini-games, then stand still when it matters.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean with the stick, WASD or the mouse. Confirm with Cross, Space or click.\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"sports\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"low-poly\\\", \\\"versus\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d445f73c-6955-4a68-aaea-9db0922b9b99-137","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Write engine/web/index.html with session.js pasted byte for byte and about-data filled.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json\\nimport pathlib\\n\\nDEV = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nWORK = DEV.parent\\nSESSION = (DEV / \\\"hub\\\" / \\\"session.js\\\").read_bytes()\\nINTERVIEW = json.loads((WORK / \\\"exit-interview.json\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"))\\nABOUT = json.dumps(INTERVIEW, ensure_ascii=False).replace(\\\"<\\\", \\\"\\\\\\\\u003c\\\")\\n\\nIIFE = r\\\"\\\"\\\"(() => {\\n  const boot = window.__gameBoot = { scene: null, seed: null, today: Math.floor(Date.now() / 86400000),\\n                                     about: document.getElementById('about-data')?.textContent ?? '' };\\n  if (!window.AIHub || !AIHub.active) return;\\n  const hub = window.__hub = { go: false, ended: false, players: [], me: 0, ghosts: {} };\\n  boot.scene = 'fit/medley';\\n  boot.seed = Number((/[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(location.search) || [])[1] || 1);\\n  AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\\n    if (!info) { location.replace(location.pathname); return; }   // no hub after all\\n    if (!navigator.gpu) { AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU'); return; }\\n    hub.me = info.me; hub.players = info.players;\\n    // Before the first status arrives, report a zero: the hub must always hear a number.\\n    const status = () => { try { return JSON.parse(window.__gameStatus || 'null')?.hub ?? null; } catch { return null; } };\\n    const waitReady = () => (window.__gameStatus ? AIHub.ready() : setTimeout(waitReady, 50));\\n    waitReady();\\n    let reported = false;\\n    const report = () => { if (reported) return; reported = true; const s = status(); AIHub.result({ score: s?.score ?? 0, stats: s?.stats ?? {} }); };\\n    setInterval(() => {\\n      if (AIHub.time() < 0 || hub.ended) return;\\n      hub.go = true;\\n      const s = status();\\n      AIHub.progress({ score: s?.score ?? 0, label: s?.label ?? 'Warming up' });\\n      if (!reported) AIHub.send(s?.ghost ?? { area: -1 }, { reliable: false });\\n      if (s?.done) report();\\n    }, 100);\\n    AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => { hub.ghosts[from] = data; });\\n    AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { delete hub.ghosts[id]; });\\n    AIHub.on('time-up', report);\\n    AIHub.on('end', () => { hub.ended = true; });\\n  });\\n})();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nPAGE = \\\"\\\"\\\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>\\\"\\\"\\\" + SESSION.decode(\\\"utf-8\\\") + \\\"\\\"\\\"</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Highest total across three balance events wins\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n<script id=\\\"about-data\\\" type=\\\"application/json\\\">\\\"\\\"\\\" + ABOUT + \\\"\\\"\\\"</script>\\n<script>\\n\\\"\\\"\\\" + IIFE + \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\\\">\\n<title>Wobble Minutes — Five days, one mat</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"Lean through a week of balance games at Tippy Cay, a pastel resort staffed by talking gym gear.\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"theme-color\\\" content=\\\"#f4e7d4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"mobile-web-app-capable\\\" content=\\\"yes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\\\" content=\\\"yes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\\\" content=\\\"black-translucent\\\">\\n<link rel=\\\"manifest\\\" href=\\\"manifest.webmanifest\\\">\\n<link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='14' fill='%23f4e7d4'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='4' fill='%233b2a4a'/%3E%3C/svg%3E\\\">\\n<style>\\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #f4e7d4; overscroll-behavior: none;\\n               touch-action: none; -webkit-user-select: none; user-select: none; -webkit-touch-callout: none;\\n               -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; }\\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100vw !important; height: 100vh !important; height: 100dvh !important;\\n           outline: none; touch-action: none; }\\n  #msg { position: fixed; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\\n         font: 18px system-ui, sans-serif; color: #3b2a4a; text-align: center; padding: 24px; pointer-events: none; }\\n  #need { display: none; position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 6; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\\n          flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; background: rgba(244, 231, 212, 0.92); color: #3b2a4a;\\n          font: 28px system-ui, sans-serif; text-align: center; padding: 24px; }\\n  #need p { margin: 0; max-width: 18ch; }\\n  #need-settings { font: 22px system-ui, sans-serif; padding: 14px 28px; border: 0; border-radius: 14px;\\n                   background: #3b2a4a; color: #f4e7d4; }\\n  @media (pointer: coarse) and (not (any-pointer: fine)) { #need { display: flex; } }\\n  html.touch-only #need { display: flex; }\\n</style>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n<div id=\\\"msg\\\" role=\\\"status\\\" aria-live=\\\"polite\\\">Loading Wobble Minutes…</div>\\n<div id=\\\"need\\\"><p>Controller or keyboard required</p><button type=\\\"button\\\" id=\\\"need-settings\\\">Settings</button></div>\\n<script>\\n  const coarseOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches;\\n  if (coarseOnly) document.documentElement.classList.add('touch-only');\\n  const needBtn = document.getElementById('need-settings');\\n  if (needBtn) needBtn.addEventListener('click', () => { window.__fitClick = 4; });\\n  const dropNeed = () => { const n = document.getElementById('need'); if (n) n.remove(); };\\n  addEventListener('keydown', dropNeed);\\n  setInterval(() => {\\n    const pads = navigator.getGamepads ? navigator.getGamepads() : [];\\n    for (const p of pads) if (p && p.buttons && [...p.buttons].some((b) => b.pressed)) dropNeed();\\n  }, 250);\\n</script>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\n  const name = document.title;\\n  const msg = document.getElementById('msg');\\n  if (!navigator.gpu) {\\n    msg.replaceChildren('Controller or keyboard required', document.createElement('br'),\\n      `${name} needs WebGPU.`, document.createElement('br'),\\n      'Use a recent Chrome, Edge or Safari (iOS 26 or later) with hardware acceleration enabled.');\\n  } else {\\n    new MutationObserver((_, obs) => {\\n      const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\\n      if (c) { c.setAttribute('aria-label', `${name} game`); msg.remove(); c.focus(); obs.disconnect(); }\\n    }).observe(document.body, { childList: true });\\n    try {\\n      if (window.loadGame) await window.loadGame();\\n      else await (await import('./shardfall.js')).default();\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      console.error(`${name} failed to load:`, error);\\n      msg.textContent = `${name} could not load. Please reload the page. If it still fails, check that WebGPU and hardware acceleration are enabled.`;\\n      document.body.append(msg);\\n    }\\n  }\\n</script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nout = DEV / \\\"engine\\\" / \\\"web\\\" / \\\"index.html\\\"\\nout.write_text(PAGE, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\ntext = out.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\nstart = text.index(\\\"/*! aihub-session\\\")\\nend = text.index(\\\"</script>\\\", start)\\npasted = text[start:end].encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\nif pasted != SESSION:\\n    raise SystemExit(f\\\"session.js paste mismatch: page {len(pasted)} file {len(SESSION)}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"wrote {out} ({out.stat().st_size} bytes), session.js matches\\\")\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/tools/write_index.py has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/tools/write_index.py has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/tools/write_index.py\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\