1,44,10,49,56,56,54,58,102,110,32,106,111,105,110,95,102,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,40,118,58,32,79,112,116,105,111,110,60,38,115,101,114,100,101,95,106,115,111,110,58,58,86,97,108,117,101,62,41,32,45,62,32,83,116,114,105,110,103,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":9,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1829,\"content\":\"    fn about_text(&self) -> String {\"},{\"line_number\":1838,\"content\":\"        about_from_blob(&self.about_blob).unwrap_or_else(|| ABOUT_FALLBACK.iter().map(|s| (*s).to_string()).collect())\"},{\"line_number\":1858,\"content\":\"const ABOUT_FALLBACK: [&str; 4] = [\"},{\"line_number\":1859,\"content\":\"    \\\"Source: a balance-and-wellness resort, in the spirit of Wii Fit by Nintendo. Usage: added on import. Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback are on this screen. Fredoka and Nunito are SIL OFL. Motion clips are the engine library.\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":1861,\"content\":\"    \\\"Testing Feedback: three seeds reach the credits with every stamp; each event is scored on five seeds; attract, pause, sliders, save, medley and the podium run in the sim. Browser checks use Playwright. A blank 1080p WebGPU photo is a readback limit; 320 by 180 is the timing check. Engine Feedback: one balance model, pause returns inside the tick, and music is the same mixer. Fonts must be installed a pass before they are drawn. Prompt Feedback: the full roster ships. The plan's time-cut list was not used. Plan filenames were guidance.\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":1865,\"content\":\"fn about_from_blob(blob: &str) -> Option<Vec<String>> {\"},{\"line_number\":1877,\"content\":\"        format!(\\\"Source: a balance-and-wellness resort, in the spirit of {source} by Nintendo. Usage: {usage}. Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback are on this screen.\\\"),\"},{\"line_number\":1879,\"content\":\"        format!(\\\"Testing Feedback: {testing}\\\"),\"},{\"line_number\":1886,\"content\":\"fn join_feedback(v: Option<&serde_json::Value>) -> String {\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7313b7ee-708e-4322-8748-2ee40a65b8dd-15","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,101,120,105,116,45,105,110,116,101,114,118,105,101,119,46,106,115,111,110,10,49,57,58,32,32,34,116,101,115,116,105,110,103,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,34,58,32,91,10,51,51,58,32,32,34,112,114,111,109,112,116,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,34,58,32,91,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\"},{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"f655f802-1653-4684-a1a6-99bb5a6b0513"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_469","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The about_from_blob function constructs \"Testing Feedback\" from the JSON.\n\nThe JSON contains the required fields: sourceInformation, testingFeedback, engineFeedback, and promptFeedback. The static check passes because the page's about-data block includes these fields. The heading strings are generated by Rust at display time.\n\nThe JSON stores \"source\": \"Wii Fit\", and about_from_blob will prefix it with \"Source:\". Starting browser tests now; they will take a while.\n\nThe browser test will run in the background to avoid memory pressure from earlyoom. The script runs the browser first, then captures after closing, so memory should stay stable.\n\nChecking whether Playwright device profiles set the `pointer: coarse` media query. This determines if phone profiles see `#need`, since both CSS media queries and `html.touch-only` are required.\n\nPlaywright's `isMobile` flag enables mobile emulation, which sets `pointer: coarse` and `hover: none`. Both the CSS media query and the JavaScript `html.touch-only` class should reveal `#need`. The card may be hidden by default, but `wait_for_selector` will wait for it to become visible once the media query matches.\n\nWASM boot time is a concern for the phone profile test. The 45-second status poll may be too short if WebGPU SwiftShader runs slowly on a 390x844 viewport. The simulation might drop to 15fps, making 600 idle ticks take about 40 seconds. Combined with WASM load time, the total could exceed the timeout.\n\nThe 45-second poll is too short for a 390x844 iPhone. At that resolution the simulation likely runs at about 10fps, so 600 idle ticks would take roughly 60 seconds. The card becomes visible immediately via CSS, but WASM may not have started ticking yet.\n\nThe 45-second poll must cover both WASM boot and 600 simulation ticks. If the tick rate is too low, attract will not start in time. The test will proceed as written, but a failure could be mitigated by extending the timeout.\n\nThe iPhone 13 Playwright profile sets device_scale_factor to 3, which would create a drawing buffer of 1170x2532 pixels. That extreme resolution would make the test run extremely slowly. If the browser test fails, the timeout can be raised to 120 seconds as a test adjustment rather than a game change.\n\nThe 320×180 viewport is the only one that passes surface_ok. The touch profile omits buffer size checks, but rendering at 3× DPR on a 390×844 viewport produces roughly 50 times more pixels than the timing viewport. The plan explicitly limits the 10-second attract check to 320×180 because software WebGPU is too slow at larger resolutions.\n\nIf the 3× DPR iPhone test is too slow, I will set device_scale_factor to 1 while keeping the viewport, user agent, and touch flags. This preserves the phone layout and touch behavior without extreme rendering overhead. The criterion requires attract mode to start and stay running.\n\nThe test will run with the default device scale factor first. If the phone profile times out, I will override it to 1 and extend the wait. Running the full suite twice is expensive.\n\nI am checking whether the engine sizes its canvas to CSS pixels or device pixels. If it uses clientWidth, the iPhone viewport would still be roughly 5.7 times larger than the timing viewport, which could drop the tick rate to 10–20 fps and make the 45-second attract poll impossible.\n\nThe simulation and rendering share the same WASM main thread, so slow SwiftShader rendering can directly reduce the tick rate. The test script runs all checks in one pass, so a phone failure would require rerunning the entire suite. I will start the test now and accept the cost of a wasted first boot if the phone profile needs adjustment.\n\nI am checking for console errors that could break boot even if behavior is correct. The browser test will run in the background with a 10-minute timeout.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The packed page matches `session.js` and has one title, description, and theme color. Starting the browser checks."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-514f68d0-170a-4b7d-9458-149798715174-16","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"tests/run.sh browser","description":"Run Playwright and engine capture checks","block_until_ms":0}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1142,"output_tokens":2202,"cache_read_input_tokens":67456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"bdb6e24b-ae0c-4292-a2af-4ce319b4ec56"}
