{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_483","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The game booted in 8 seconds.\n\nThe game loads successfully. The canvas and GPU are present. The scene enters 'fit'. No page errors appear. The deadlock theory is wrong. The status variable stays undefined. Publish() never sets it. The cause is a silent failure or an empty value.\n\nA panic in publish() may be killing the frame loop after boot. The simulation log reached the canvas, but status might be published each frame and crash on the first attempt. I will wait longer for more logs and check if requestAnimationFrame is still running.\n\nI will inspect the publish call sites and the status JSON generation. A huge or malformed JSON payload could cause Reflect.set to fail. The DomString constructor might also panic and halt the frame loop. I need to examine the Rust code. The current diagnostic only waited eight seconds, so I will extend it to check for continued tick logs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-afdcd63e-4cc0-41b1-bcef-cc95cc308974-36","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"weblink::publish|publish\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates","glob":"*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1953,"output_tokens":547,"cache_read_input_tokens":92544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"4610bff5-ae4a-41c9-a417-1d221429ccb5"}
