{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_491","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found the target function `__wbg_new_a50799cd0eeba856` in a JavaScript file.\n\nThe generated constructor calls `new DomString(...)`, which is undefined. This throws a ReferenceError on every publish call and prevents status from being set. The function is not wrapped in `handleError`, so the error should have triggered a pageerror.\n\nThe ReferenceError might be swallowed by wasm-bindgen's call wrapper or caught as a WASM trap. The frame loop could also be catching it silently, which would explain why no console error appeared in eight seconds of logs.\n\nThe exception likely aborts the Rust frame function. The JS caller may catch it silently, or it may surface as a pageerror. The diagnostic listener was already active before navigation, so a missed error is unlikely.\n\nThe exception unwinds through WASM and out to JavaScript. The Rust wrapper does not catch import errors, so the ReferenceError should reach the event loop. I need to find the Rust start or request_animation_frame wrapper to see why Playwright's pageerror listener did not catch it.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b1f2a89f-5a58-4ee1-9d03-834456eb0024-45","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fit_on","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":805,"output_tokens":697,"cache_read_input_tokens":103552,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"32719ef9-0684-4735-a440-1328d11ec806"}
