{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_494","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The DomString bug is real regardless.\n\nThe exception might be swallowed by the engine's animation frame wrapper. I will re-run diagnostics with a longer wait, capture window errors via an init script, patch requestAnimationFrame to count frames, and check if __gameStatus is set later.\n\nI will also check whether the game loop is actually running by monitoring canvas pixel changes.\n\nThe init script runs before page scripts, so the patched requestAnimationFrame should wrap any wasm-bound animation frames. I will fix the DomString bug regardless of the diagnostic results. Using js-sys::JsString is forbidden.\n\njs-sys is already a dependency of wasm-bindgen. It does not generate snippets on its own. Snippets come from `#[wasm_bindgen(inline_js)]` or module imports. The previous author avoided js-sys to prevent the packer from seeing those snippets.\n\nI will fix the extern declaration to generate `new String(...)` instead of `new DomString(...)`. Adding js-sys as a new dependency is forbidden.\n\nThe `js_name = String` attribute on the type did not rename the constructor call. The generated code still emits `new DomString`. I need to find the correct wasm-bindgen syntax to force `new String`.\n\nI am testing `#[wasm_bindgen(js_namespace = window, js_name = String)]` and `#[wasm_bindgen(js_name = \"String\")]` to force the constructor call to emit `new String`. The generated function still uses `new DomString`, so the Rust type name is likely overriding the `js_name` attribute. I will check the wasm-bindgen 0.2.129 source to confirm how constructors handle naming.\n\nI found the fix. The `js_class` attribute on the constructor must be set to `\"String\"`. I will try `#[wasm_bindgen(constructor, js_class = \"String\")]` to force the generated code to emit `new String(...)`.\n\nI am now exploring a workaround that avoids renaming the constructor entirely. I could build the string object using Reflect or JSON.parse, but the requirement explicitly states that wasm must publish a JS String via DomString::new so both JSON.parse and .tick work. This means the constructor fix is unavoidable.\n\nA primitive string cannot hold `.tick` because primitives are boxed temporarily and property assignments do not persist. A String object is required so that `JSON.parse` coerces it to its underlying primitive value.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf3ad586-99ee-4e90-9fc1-87690a693756-49","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"js_class = \\\"String\\\"|js_name = String","path":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src","glob":"**/wasm-bindgen-*/**/*.rs","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf3ad586-99ee-4e90-9fc1-87690a693756-50","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":1500,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2342,"output_tokens":1710,"cache_read_input_tokens":106624,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"b8ec7b37-fa43-4531-a798-2ba32fee0207"}
