{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_519","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The clock uses `Instant::now()`, which may not advance on WASM between synchronous rAF calls.\n\nThe build compiled `web-time`, but `std::time::Instant` on wasm32 may still be a non-advancing stub. If so, the tick loop would stall after the first catch-up.\n\nRust 1.98 should provide a working `Instant` on wasm32, so the clock may not be the culprit. Other possibilities include `ctl.paused` blocking ticks, the pump exiting early, or status failing to refresh. The rAF count of 43737 is suspicious.\n\nThe 43,000 count reflects `request_redraw` calls inside the event loop's `about_to_wait`, not pending callbacks. If those calls were scheduled but never executed, the tick loop would remain stalled.\n\nIf `Instant` is frozen during the entire `wait_for_timeout`, each pump call sees the same timestamp. The tick loop then advances `next` to that frozen value and never triggers again. This would explain why 43,000 frame calls produced no ticks.\n\nBoot logs show `Instant` advancing normally during initialization. The 1-second idle period should allow ticks if the clock works. The stall likely stems from the event loop spinning synchronously without yielding.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-23934708-7eeb-4cc6-8fa7-a70888508e06-83","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\\.paused|set_control|TimeControl","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src","glob":"*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2973,"output_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":142976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"d2bfb1c6-d9b3-4548-8165-11b260920420"}
