{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_527","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading app.rs around lines 1720-1800 to inspect texture application and the frame end.\n\nAn error before apply causes a panic. I will add a JavaScript init script to capture console errors, unhandled rejections, and WASM exceptions.\n\nNo console errors or page errors appeared in the first 8 seconds, so a panic is unlikely. The loop probably just stops. The poll strategy may rely on requestAnimationFrame, which headless environments might not fire continuously.\n\nThe first test showed the event loop was spinning. requestAnimationFrame fired 43,737 times per second. The tick still did not advance. The loop is running but the frame is not advancing.\n\nThe tick remained stuck at 5. The rAF wrapper may have queued callbacks without actually running the game loop. I am checking whether fit_on, hud.status, or an early return in frame() are blocking status updates.\n\nThe 43,000 queued callbacks might fire in a single burst at the end of the frame. During that burst, the clock could freeze and prevent the tick from advancing.\n\nThe 43,000 frame calls occurred over one second of wall time. performance.now advances during a tight loop, so the clock should have ticked. The stuck tick is therefore not caused by a frozen clock.\n\nI found a likely culprit in the frame() function. When touch_screen is enabled, an early return before host.pump() throttles frames to 60fps. This could prevent the tick from advancing even though the event loop is spinning.\n\nThe Reflect.set test showed only 3 status updates in one second without the rAF wrapper. With the wrapper, requestAnimationFrame fires 43,000 times per second. The wrapper is causing the loop to spin, but it is not advancing the tick. I am now examining the wrapper code itself.\n\nThe wrapper code itself is not causing the 43,000 callbacks. If winit's poll strategy uses requestAnimationFrame, each frame should only schedule two callbacks, not forty-three thousand. The massive loop must be coming from somewhere else.\n\nThe 43,000 callbacks per second likely come from a tight loop using setTimeout(0) or queueMicrotask. Each iteration calls request_redraw and schedules another animation frame. The browser may batch those callbacks instead of running them immediately. A synchronous loop that fast would freeze the clock and prevent the tick from advancing.\n\nThe 43,000 callbacks per second likely come from a setTimeout(0) storm rather than requestAnimationFrame. In headless mode, setTimeout(0) may be clamped to zero and fire at extreme speed. The wrapper itself is probably not the source of the loop.\n\nThe 43,000 callbacks per second are a microtask loop, not setTimeout. The real browser loop stops after a few frames without the wrapper. I will instrument the init script to count requestAnimationFrame and setTimeout calls and log errors.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f6c778be-fe06-46f0-bc1d-faccdf8bdd5f-95","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - << 'PY'\nimport os\nos.environ.setdefault(\"PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE\", \"ubuntu24.04-x64\")\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nfrom pathlib import Path\nHTML = Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html\")\nFLAGS = [\"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\",\"--enable-features=Vulkan\",\"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\",\"--use-angle=swiftshader\"]\nINIT = r\"\"\"\nwindow.__c = {raf:0, rafCb:0, timeout:0};\nwindow.__errs = [];\naddEventListener('error', (e) => window.__errs.push('err '+(e.message||e.error)));\naddEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => window.__errs.push('rej '+e.reason));\nconst raf = window.requestAnimationFrame.bind(window);\nwindow.requestAnimationFrame = (cb) => { window.__c.raf++; return raf((t) => { window.__c.rafCb++; return cb(t); }); };\nconst st = window.setTimeout.bind(window);\nwindow.setTimeout = (cb, ms, ...a) => { window.__c.timeout++; return st(cb, ms, ...a); };\n\"\"\"\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True, args=FLAGS)\n    page = browser.new_context(viewport={\"width\":320,\"height\":180}, device_scale_factor=1).new_page()\n    page.add_init_script(INIT)\n    logs=[]\n    page.on(\"console\", lambda m: logs.append(f\"{m.type}:{m.text[:180]}\") if m.type in (\"error\",\"warning\") else None)\n    page.on(\"pageerror\", lambda e: logs.append(\"page:\"+str(e)[:300]))\n    page.goto(HTML.as_uri(), wait_until=\"domcontentloaded\", timeout=60000)\n    page.wait_for_function(\"() => window.__gameStatus\", timeout=30000)\n    page.wait_for_timeout(1000)\n    info = page.evaluate(\"\"\"() => ({\n      tick: window.__gameStatus.tick,\n      c: window.__c,\n      errs: window.__errs.slice(0,8),\n      phase: window.__gameStatus.phase,\n    })\"\"\")\n    print(info)\n    print(\"LOGS\", logs[:12])\n    browser.close()\nPY","description":"Count frames versus sim ticks and capture errors"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2139,"output_tokens":2404,"cache_read_input_tokens":157056,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"f9b6aee3-7b41-4f27-8e3c-94e7349a862f"}
