{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_530","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The poll mechanism uses scheduler.postTask when available.\n\nChrome's scheduler.postTask may be causing a tight loop. Each poll iteration calls about_to_wait and request_redraw, which schedules an animation frame. The postTask queue then floods with 61,000 tasks over one second. Only 49 rAF callbacks fire because the flood overwhelms the browser's scheduling.\n\nThe main thread is too busy to process the flood of postTask tasks. Only 49 animation frame callbacks fire, so only 49 frames render. The tick count remains at 5 because pump() advances time by roughly 20 ms per call.\n\nThe tick count should have climbed from 5 to roughly 60. The web_time::Instant on WASM uses performance.now(), which advanced in earlier tests, so the clock itself is likely not frozen. The real issue may be that frame() returns early due to touch_screen throttling, or that the 49 callbacks arrive in a burst and fail to advance time.\n\nThe tick count might be frozen because `ctl.paused` is true. In `frame()`, `host.pump()` runs before UI panel logic, so the panel could set the paused flag during that window. If the flag changes, it gets written back at the end of the function.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d0abffb5-c34d-46db-8ab8-43e8e9ce22e4-100","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"let ctl|ctl_before|paused","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2763,"output_tokens":751,"cache_read_input_tokens":163328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"bc213380-6e4d-4682-85f0-71b86d371263"}
