{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_532","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The simulation should tick independently from the status tick.\n\nStatus updates from sim.state.tick during the render frame. If the pump fails to tick, both values remain unchanged. I am investigating a possible web_time Instant bug on WASM. The Clock::advance logic advances the next timestamp by sim.dt() each tick.\n\nThe pump ticked eight times during initialization, then stopped. This means `now` is no longer advancing relative to `self.next`, so the pump is likely not being called. I am checking whether all 49 animation frame callbacks actually trigger a frame.\n\nThe 49 animation frame callbacks should produce 49 redraws and 49 pumps. The boot log showed Instant advancing during async GPU initialization, so the freeze occurs after that async phase.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2eb4aa65-e8e7-4186-8be9-81478aa6aaf0-102","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn now|performance|Date","path":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/web-time-1.1.0/src","glob":"*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1465,"output_tokens":637,"cache_read_input_tokens":167168,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"9f7d5f36-f46a-4086-8e51-c534480e466a"}
