ype\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→use std::cell::Cell;\\nuse std::rc::Rc;\\nuse wasm_bindgen::closure::Closure;\\nuse wasm_bindgen::JsCast;\\n\\npub struct AnimationFrameHandler {\\n    window: web_sys::Window,\\n    closure: Closure<dyn FnMut()>,\\n    handle: Rc<Cell<Option<i32>>>,\\n10→}\\n\\nimpl AnimationFrameHandler {\\n    pub fn new(window: web_sys::Window) -> Self {\\n        let handle = Rc::new(Cell::new(None));\\n        let closure = Closure::new({\\n            let handle = handle.clone();\\n            move || handle.set(None)\\n        });\\n\\n20→        Self { window, closure, handle }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_animation_frame<F>(&mut self, mut f: F)\\n    where\\n        F: 'static + FnMut(),\\n    {\\n        let handle = self.handle.clone();\\n        self.closure = Closure::new(move || {\\n            handle.set(None);\\n30→            f();\\n        })\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn request(&self) {\\n        if let Some(handle) = self.handle.take() {\\n            self.window.cancel_animation_frame(handle).expect(\\\"Failed to cancel animation frame\\\");\\n        }\\n\\n        let handle = self\\n40→            .window\\n            .request_animation_frame(self.closure.as_ref().unchecked_ref())\\n            .expect(\\\"Failed to request animation frame\\\");\\n\\n        self.handle.set(Some(handle));\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn cancel(&mut self) {\\n        if let Some(handle) = self.handle.take() {\\n            self.window.cancel_animation_frame(handle).expect(\\\"Failed to cancel animation frame\\\");\\n50→        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Drop for AnimationFrameHandler {\\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\\n        if let Some(handle) = self.handle.take() {\\n            self.window.cancel_animation_frame(handle).expect(\\\"Failed to cancel animation frame\\\");\\n        }\\n    }\\n60→}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→use std::cell::Cell;\\nuse std::rc::Rc;\\nuse wasm_bindgen::closure::Closure;\\nuse wasm_bindgen::JsCast;\\n\\npub struct AnimationFrameHandler {\\n    window: web_sys::Window,\\n    closure: Closure<dyn FnMut()>,\\n    handle: Rc<Cell<Option<i32>>>,\\n10→}\\n\\nimpl AnimationFrameHandler {\\n    pub fn new(window: web_sys::Window) -> Self {\\n        let handle = Rc::new(Cell::new(None));\\n        let closure = Closure::new({\\n            let handle = handle.clone();\\n            move || handle.set(None)\\n        });\\n\\n20→        Self { window, closure, handle }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_animation_frame<F>(&mut self, mut f: F)\\n    where\\n        F: 'static + FnMut(),\\n    {\\n        let handle = self.handle.clone();\\n        self.closure = Closure::new(move || {\\n            handle.set(None);\\n30→            f();\\n        })\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn request(&self) {\\n        if let Some(handle) = self.handle.take() {\\n            self.window.cancel_animation_frame(handle).expect(\\\"Failed to cancel animation frame\\\");\\n        }\\n\\n        let handle = self\\n40→            .window\\n            .request_animation_frame(self.closure.as_ref().unchecked_ref())\\n            .expect(\\\"Failed to request animation frame\\\");\\n\\n        self.handle.set(Some(handle));\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn cancel(&mut self) {\\n        if let Some(handle) = self.handle.take() {\\n            self.window.cancel_animation_frame(handle).expect(\\\"Failed to cancel animation frame\\\");\\n50→        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Drop for AnimationFrameHandler {\\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\\n        if let Some(handle) = self.handle.take() {\\n            self.window.cancel_animation_frame(handle).expect(\\\"Failed to cancel animation frame\\\");\\n        }\\n    }\\n60→}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/winit-0.30.13/src/platform_impl/web/web_sys/animation_frame.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"use std::cell::Cell;\\nuse std::rc::Rc;\\nuse wasm_bindgen::closure::Closure;\\nuse wasm_bindgen::JsCast;\\n\\npub struct AnimationFrameHandler {\\n    window: web_sys::Window,\\n    closure: Closure<dyn FnMut()>,\\n    handle: Rc<Cell<Option<i32>>>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl AnimationFrameHandler {\\n    pub fn new(window: web_sys::Window) -> Self {\\n        let handle = Rc::new(Cell::new(None));\\n        let closure = Closure::new({\\n            let handle = handle.clone();\\n            move || handle.set(None)\\n        });\\n\\n        Self { window, closure, handle }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_animation_frame<F>(&mut self, mut f: F)\\n    where\\n        F: 'static + FnMut(),\\n    {\\n        let handle = self.handle.clone();\\n        self.closure = Closure::new(move || {\\n            handle.set(None);\\n            f();\\n        })\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn request(&self) {\\n        if let Some(handle) = self.handle.take() {\\n            self.window.cancel_animation_frame(handle).expect(\\\"Failed to cancel animation frame\\\");\\n        }\\n\\n        let handle = self\\n            .window\\n            .request_animation_frame(self.closure.as_ref().unchecked_ref())\\n            .expect(\\\"Failed to request animation frame\\\");\\n\\n        self.handle.set(Some(handle));\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn cancel(&mut self) {\\n        if let Some(handle) = self.handle.take() {\\n            self.window.cancel_animation_frame(handle).expect(\\\"Failed to cancel animation frame\\\");\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Drop for AnimationFrameHandler {\\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\\n        if let Some(handle) = self.handle.take() {\\n            self.window.cancel_animation_frame(handle).expect(\\\"Failed to cancel animation frame\\\");\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":60}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"c00e1615-6ad4-471b-91af-8123c8a03c06"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_534","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`request()` cancels the previous animation frame and schedules a new one every time.\n\nPoll runs scheduler.postTask roughly 61,000 times per second. Each iteration calls request_redraw, which cancels and reschedules the animation frame before the browser can fire it. The main thread is starved, so the rAF callback almost never executes. Only 49 callbacks occurred when the thread briefly yielded.\n\nThe 49 callbacks are genuine winit handlers, not cancelled placeholders. Each one runs the redraw flag and should advance the simulation. The postTask flood prevents actual drawing from happening often, so Instant advances while frames are skipped.\n\nThe 49 callbacks might not be the game's winit handlers at all. egui or wgpu could be requesting animation frames instead. A swallowed panic inside frame() is unlikely because no window errors appeared.\n\nThe 49 callbacks likely fired during the initial boot burst before the postTask flood began. Once the flood started, every new animation frame was cancelled before it could run. The simulation tick therefore remained stuck at its boot value.\n\nThis is a known winit issue. On web, `ControlFlow::Poll` combined with `request_redraw` inside `about_to_wait` continuously cancels the pending animation frame before it can fire. The browser never gets a chance to run the game loop, so the simulation tick remains frozen after boot.\n\nReconsidering the prior theory. Chrome's default postTask priority is \"user-visible\", so the browser should still interleave animation frames between tasks if the thread has idle time. The flood may not be starving rAF after all.\n\nThe 61,000 postTasks per second run back-to-back with almost no gap. The 49 animation frame callbacks should have drawn, yet the simulation tick remains frozen.\n\nA Rust-side counter was considered to verify whether RedrawRequested actually calls frame(), but patching the glue or hooking from JavaScript is impractical.\n\nThe engine uses ControlFlow::Poll by design and presumably works in a normal Chrome window. The next step is to check whether scheduler support is enabled and consider a slower poll strategy.\n\nThe test environment is headless Playwright with SwiftShader. That mode likely runs postTask far more aggressively than a real window, starving the animation frame and freezing the simulation tick. A real browser might tolerate Poll, but this computer must pass the test regardless.\n\nThe proposed fix is to stop using ControlFlow::Poll on wasm. Instead, the loop should wait until the next tick or rely solely on request_redraw's animation frame without the poll storm.\n\nThe winit crate cancels the pending animation frame internally, so skipping redundant `request_redraw` calls is not possible. Switching the wasm run loop from Poll to Wait would let the browser handle timing naturally, but the redraw flag still needs an event to wake the loop and process it.\n\nThe rAF callback wakes the loop via request_redraw. A Wait-based loop would process one frame per animation frame without any poll storm.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-00101383-7eca-4043-8651-635c56960264-105","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"request_redraw","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src","glob":"*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-00101383-7eca-4043-8651-635c56960264-106","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/winit-0.30.13/src/platform_impl/web/event_loop/mod.rs","offset":90,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1658,"output_tokens":1578,"cache_read_input_tokens":169728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-b