{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6cd0efa2-c413-4a14-a299-cfa82efd61e2-108","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"400→                                });\\n                            }\\n                        }\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }),\\n        ));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Generate a strictly increasing ID\\n410→    // This is used to differentiate windows when handling events\\n    pub fn generate_id(&self) -> u32 {\\n        let mut id = self.0.id.borrow_mut();\\n        *id += 1;\\n\\n        *id\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn request_redraw(&self, id: WindowId) {\\n        self.0.redraw_pending.borrow_mut().insert(id);\\n420→        self.send_events::<EventWrapper>(iter::empty());\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn init(&self) {\\n        // NB: For consistency all platforms must emit a 'resumed' event even though web\\n        // applications don't themselves have a formal suspend/resume lifecycle.\\n        self.run_until_cleared([Event::NewEvents(StartCause::Init), Event::Resumed].into_iter());\\n    }\\n\\n    // Run the polling logic for the Poll ControlFlow, which involves clearing the queue\\n430→    pub fn poll(&self) {\\n        let start_cause = Event::NewEvents(StartCause::Poll);\\n        self.run_until_cleared(iter::once(start_cause));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Run the logic for waking from a WaitUntil, which involves clearing the queue\\n    // Generally there shouldn't be events built up when this is called\\n    pub fn resume_time_reached(&self, start: Instant, requested_resume: Instant) {\\n        let start_cause =\\n            Event::NewEvents(StartCause::ResumeTimeReached { start, requested_resume });\\n440→        self.run_until_cleared(iter::once(start_cause));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Add an event to the event loop runner, from the user or an event handler\\n    //\\n    // It will determine if the event should be immediately sent to the user or buffered for later\\n    pub(crate) fn send_event<E: Into<EventWrapper>>(&self, event: E) {\\n        self.send_events(iter::once(event));\\n    }\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"400→                                });\\n                            }\\n                        }\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }),\\n        ));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Generate a strictly increasing ID\\n410→    // This is used to differentiate windows when handling events\\n    pub fn generate_id(&self) -> u32 {\\n        let mut id = self.0.id.borrow_mut();\\n        *id += 1;\\n\\n        *id\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn request_redraw(&self, id: WindowId) {\\n        self.0.redraw_pending.borrow_mut().insert(id);\\n420→        self.send_events::<EventWrapper>(iter::empty());\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn init(&self) {\\n        // NB: For consistency all platforms must emit a 'resumed' event even though web\\n        // applications don't themselves have a formal suspend/resume lifecycle.\\n        self.run_until_cleared([Event::NewEvents(StartCause::Init), Event::Resumed].into_iter());\\n    }\\n\\n    // Run the polling logic for the Poll ControlFlow, which involves clearing the queue\\n430→    pub fn poll(&self) {\\n        let start_cause = Event::NewEvents(StartCause::Poll);\\n        self.run_until_cleared(iter::once(start_cause));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Run the logic for waking from a WaitUntil, which involves clearing the queue\\n    // Generally there shouldn't be events built up when this is called\\n    pub fn resume_time_reached(&self, start: Instant, requested_resume: Instant) {\\n        let start_cause =\\n            Event::NewEvents(StartCause::ResumeTimeReached { start, requested_resume });\\n440→        self.run_until_cleared(iter::once(start_cause));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Add an event to the event loop runner, from the user or an event handler\\n    //\\n    // It will determine if the event should be immediately sent to the user or buffered for later\\n    pub(crate) fn send_event<E: Into<EventWrapper>>(&self, event: E) {\\n        self.send_events(iter::once(event));\\n    }\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/winit-0.30.13/src/platform_impl/web/event_loop/runner.rs\",\"offset\":400,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"                                });\\n                            }\\n                        }\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }),\\n        ));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Generate a strictly increasing ID\\n    // This is used to differentiate windows when handling events\\n    pub fn generate_id(&self) -> u32 {\\n        let mut id = self.0.id.borrow_mut();\\n        *id += 1;\\n\\n        *id\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn request_redraw(&self, id: WindowId) {\\n        self.0.redraw_pending.borrow_mut().insert(id);\\n        self.send_events::<EventWrapper>(iter::empty());\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn init(&self) {\\n        // NB: For consistency all platforms must emit a 'resumed' event even though web\\n        // applications don't themselves have a formal suspend/resume lifecycle.\\n        self.run_until_cleared([Event::NewEvents(StartCause::Init), Event::Resumed].into_iter());\\n    }\\n\\n    // Run the polling logic for the Poll ControlFlow, which involves clearing the queue\\n    pub fn poll(&self) {\\n        let start_cause = Event::NewEvents(StartCause::Poll);\\n        self.run_until_cleared(iter::once(start_cause));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Run the logic for waking from a WaitUntil, which involves clearing the queue\\n    // Generally there shouldn't be events built up when this is called\\n    pub fn resume_time_reached(&self, start: Instant, requested_resume: Instant) {\\n        let start_cause =\\n            Event::NewEvents(StartCause::ResumeTimeReached { start, requested_resume });\\n        self.run_until_cleared(iter::once(start_cause));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Add an event to the event loop runner, from the user or an event handler\\n    //\\n    // It will determine if the event should be immediately sent to the user or buffered for later\\n    pub(crate) fn send_event<E: Into<EventWrapper>>(&self, event: E) {\\n        self.send_events(iter::once(event));\\n    }\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":808}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6cd0efa2-c413-4a14-a299-cfa82efd61e2-109","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"115→    pub fn set_title(&self, title: &str) {\\n        self.canvas.borrow().set_attribute(\\\"alt\\\", title)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn set_transparent(&self, _transparent: bool) {}\\n120→\\n    pub fn set_blur(&self, _blur: bool) {}\\n\\n    pub fn set_visible(&self, _visible: bool) {\\n        // Intentionally a no-op\\n    }\\n\\n    #[inline]\\n    pub fn is_visible(&self) -> Option<bool> {\\n        None\\n130→    }\\n\\n    pub fn request_redraw(&self) {\\n        self.canvas.borrow().request_animation_frame();\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn pre_present_notify(&self) {}\\n\\n    pub fn outer_position(&self) -> Result<PhysicalPosition<i32>, NotSupportedError> {\\n        Ok(self.canvas.borrow().position().to_physical(self.scale_factor()))\\n140→    }\\n\\n    pub fn inner_position(&self) -> Result<PhysicalPosition<i32>, NotSupportedError> {\\n        // Note: the canvas element has no window decorations, so this is equal to `outer_position`.\\n        self.outer_position()\",\"content_concise\":\"115→    pub fn set_title(&self, title: &str) {\\n        self.canvas.borrow().set_attribute(\\\"alt\\\", title)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn set_transparent(&self, _transparent: bool) {}\\n120→\\n    pub fn set_blur(&self, _blur: bool) {}\\n\\n    pub fn set_visible(&self, _visible: bool) {\\n        // Intentionally a no-op\\n    }\\n\\n    #[inline]\\n    pub fn is_visible(&self) -> Option<bool> {\\n        None\\n130→    }\\n\\n    pub fn request_redraw(&self) {\\n        self.canvas.borrow().request_animation_frame();\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn pre_present_notify(&self) {}\\n\\n    pub fn outer_position(&self) -> Result<PhysicalPosition<i32>, NotSupportedError> {\\n        Ok(self.canvas.borrow().position().to_physical(self.scale_factor()))\\n140→    }\\n\\n    pub fn inner_position(&self) -> Result<PhysicalPosition<i32>, NotSupportedError> {\\n        // Note: the canvas element has no window decorations, so this is equal to `outer_position`.\\n        self.outer_position()\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/winit-0.30.13/src/platform_impl/web/window.rs\",\"offset\":115,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"    pub fn set_title(&self, title: &str) {\\n        self.canvas.borrow().set_attribute(\\\"alt\\\", title)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn set_transparent(&self, _transparent: bool) {}\\n\\n    pub fn set_blur(&self, _blur: bool) {}\\n\\n    pub fn set_visible(&self, _visible: bool) {\\n        // Intentionally a no-op\\n    }\\n\\n    #[inline]\\n    pub fn is_visible(&self) -> Option<bool> {\\n        None\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn request_redraw(&self) {\\n        self.canvas.borrow().request_animation_frame();\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn pre_present_notify(&self) {}\\n\\n    pub fn outer_position(&self) -> Result<PhysicalPosition<i32>, NotSupportedError> {\\n        Ok(self.canvas.borrow().position().to_physical(self.scale_factor()))\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn inner_position(&self) -> Result<PhysicalPosition<i32>, NotSupportedError> {\\n        // Note: the canvas element has no window decorations, so this is equal to `outer_position`.\\n        self.outer_position()\\n\",\"total_lines\":477}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"4af3859a-1060-4ee4-9089-984db695bf38"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_537","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"window.request_redraw() only schedules a requestAnimationFrame. It does not call runner.request_redraw.\n\nThe rAF callback calls runner.request_redraw. That queues the redraw and immediately processes send_events. The queue drains to emit RedrawRequested then AboutToWait. AboutToWait schedules the next rAF. apply_control_flow for Wait does not schedule another immediate poll.\n\nThe bug is that Poll control flow schedules a postTask that calls poll(). That triggers about_to_wait again and cancels the pending rAF before it fires. The fix is to use Wait on wasm so the render loop stays on requestAnimationFrame. Native should keep Poll because its simulation thread runs separately. I also need to check whether Resumed events trigger about_to_wait during the first frame.\n\nDuring the first frame, `init` calls `run_until_cleared`, which ends with `AboutToWait`. If `gfx` is still `None` at that point, no redraw is requested. The question is who wakes the loop once `finish_init` completes and the graphics context becomes ready.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-27f25e6f-7955-44f7-9ec5-465f4eed6733-110","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pending_gfx","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src","glob":"*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":915,"output_tokens":610,"cache_read_input_tokens":173824,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"19c12c65-28d3-4b35-88f2-b80a999a7f45"}
