{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_539","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Async graphics completion is detected by polling pending_gfx.\n\nPoll is necessary to detect async completion, but it cancels the previous animation frame on every request. The fix is to keep Poll while skipping redundant redraws on wasm.\n\nA `redraw_queued` flag would let `about_to_wait` request a redraw only when one is not already pending. The flag would be cleared in `RedrawRequested`. This approach seems flawed.\n\nThe `redraw_queued` flag actually works. Because `about_to_wait` runs after `RedrawRequested`, the flag is cleared before the next poll. The next poll sees no pending redraw and skips `request_redraw`. The animation frame stays pending and fires normally.\n\nThe animation frame callback processes the redraw synchronously and schedules the next frame. The poll postTask runs after this, but the `redraw_queued` flag prevents it from canceling that pending frame.\n\nThe `redraw_queued` flag must be added as a `bool` field on `App`. The poll loop still fires 61,000 postTasks per second. That CPU burn can cause timing failures and out-of-memory errors. The poll rate needs to be throttled.\n\nSwitching from Poll to Wait once graphics are ready would stop the poll storm entirely. The loop would then run only on animation frames. This keeps CPU usage low and avoids the 61,000 postTask per second burn.\n\nThe implementation sets `ControlFlow::Wait` inside `about_to_wait` once graphics finish initializing. The concern is whether `apply_control_flow` will see this change in the same iteration, since it reads the control flow cell after `about_to_wait` returns.\n\nConfirmed: `apply_control_flow` reads the updated control flow after `about_to_wait` returns, so switching to `Wait` works correctly. The poll storm lasts only until graphics finish initializing, roughly 0.8 seconds, after which the loop settles into a steady animation frame cycle.\n\nThe `redraw_queued` deduplication is unnecessary once the loop switches to `Wait`. The animation frame handler processes the redraw and calls `about_to_wait` exactly once per frame, so no extra poll occurs between frames. `request_redraw` is invoked only after the previous callback has finished, meaning the handler never cancels a pending frame.\n\nThe animation frame callback clears its handle before invoking the user function, so it never cancels a pending frame. This confirms that switching to Wait after graphics initialization is sufficient, and the `redraw_queued` flag is unnecessary. The native path of `about_to_wait` will remain on Poll.\n\nThe native `about_to_wait` path will request a redraw without changing control flow. The switch to `Wait` will only happen after `finish_init` succeeds, since failure already triggers `fail()`. A device code issue was also noted: an unset pad device defaulted to keyboard input, producing a Space prompt instead of the expected Cross.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8631096a-c7a8-4db6-8f6d-98ded6e8eeb0-112","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"device:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8631096a-c7a8-4db6-8f6d-98ded6e8eeb0-113","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn fit_sample|last_device|device =","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/input.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1189,"output_tokens":1920,"cache_read_input_tokens":175488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"c21fd94e-0c6c-4de7-87f6-27e499d44fc9"}
