{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_541","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The default last_device is KeyboardMouse, so the prompt shows Space before any input.\n\nThe boot prompt should show Cross, not Space. The default last_device is wrong: it defaults to KeyboardMouse, so the prompt shows pad glyphs at boot and sends device 2. It should be Gamepad instead.\n\nThe input layer should not claim keyboard until a key is actually seen. Defaulting last_device to Gamepad is correct because the design specifies pad glyphs by default, and the device will switch only when real input arrives. Need to verify that poll_gamepad does not immediately override this.\n\nseen_real stays false when no activity occurs, so attract idle still counts. The mouse cursor starts at 0,0, but note_pointer only fires on CursorMoved events, not every frame. Without a cursor event, the cursor remains at 0,0 and does not hover over any menu item.\n\nThe browser likely does not send an initial pointer move, so the prompt was Space rather than Click. The keyboard default also prevents attract idle from starting because it never sets `any`. I will implement the fix and rebuild to verify the loop ticks after the Wait fix. I also need to confirm the prompt function shows Cross for device 0 and 1. The test stubs the DOM gamepad API with `__setPad`, but the actual code uses gilrs instead.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ed991400-3f1c-4c03-a336-d7f0034580ce-115","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"getGamepads|navigator","path":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/gilrs-core-0.6.8","glob":"*.rs","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ed991400-3f1c-4c03-a336-d7f0034580ce-116","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn prompt","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/f