input.coarse = touch_screen || crate::weblink::coarse_only();\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/input.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":321,\"content\":\"    /// A key or a pad has been used. A coarse pointer stays touch-only until then.\"},{\"line_number\":322,\"content\":\"    pub seen_real: bool,\"},{\"line_number\":323,\"content\":\"    /// `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` and no fine pointer.\"},{\"line_number\":324,\"content\":\"    pub coarse: bool,\"},{\"line_number\":460,\"content\":\"            seen_real: false,\"},{\"line_number\":461,\"content\":\"            coarse: false,\"},{\"line_number\":499,\"content\":\"            self.seen_real = true;\"},{\"line_number\":503,\"content\":\"            self.seen_real = true;\"},{\"line_number\":505,\"content\":\"        if self.mouse_travel > 6.0 && !self.coarse {\"},{\"line_number\":540,\"content\":\"        let device = if self.coarse && !self.seen_real {\"},{\"line_number\":551,\"content\":\"        let any = !self.coarse && (self.pad.any_activity || travel > 6.0 || stick.length() > 0.3 || lean.length() > 0.3);\"},{\"line_number\":557,\"content\":\"        self.seen_real = true;\"},{\"line_number\":724,\"content\":\"            self.seen_real = true;\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/platform.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":47,\"content\":\"    web_sys::window().and_then(|w| w.match_media(\\\"(pointer: coarse)\\\").ok().flatten()).is_some_and(|m| m.matches())\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"ae39adf2-7a0f-4b8a-bd47-3a0a65ff25ef"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_582","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Captures look good. They show real game scenes rather than blank frames.\n\nTitle and pose text are correct. The footer repeats the title label but this is not a test failure. I will fix browser.py next with helpers for pad polling and hover-clicking labels. Fresh browsers will be used for touch tests to avoid OOM. The second boot failed so I will hold the D-pad and poll.\n\nThe init script runs before page scripts, so the pad stub should not race. I will fire a gamepadconnected event when setting the pad and keep the button held during polling. Focus may shift between release and sample, but a 200ms pause should prevent that.\n\nThe extra MENU flag from stick drift only triggers on frame edges, not continuously. Zero axes produce no extra input. D-pad and stick inputs can coexist safely.\n\nThe second boot failed because the gamepad was not yet connected when the button was pressed. The gilrs scan happened too late to catch the edge. This explains why boot one worked but boot two did not.\n\nBoot one likely succeeded because the pad was already connected before the button press. The boot checks wait for status and a 400ms tick, which should allow gilrs to scan getGamepads before any input is sent on both boots. The stub should be visible to the WASM module because it looks up the JavaScript function each event.\n\nChromium headless may ignore navigator.getGamepads overrides because the native property is non-configurable. The override likely works only when the property is writable. Boot one succeeded, so the override sometimes sticks. The game does not overwrite it. Two-frame definition is unlikely.\n\nThe test will wait for the pad stub to report connected before pressing button 13. It will poll status every 100 milliseconds for up to two seconds to catch a menu focus change, then release. Dispatching a gamepadconnected event is also included as a safeguard.\n\nKeyboard fallback was rejected to preserve the gamepad assertion. The pad stub returns a valid JS array and sets the pressed property correctly, so no stub-side fix is needed yet.\n\nThe `next_event` loop may block during the connect frame and drop the button edge. The pad is detected on the first scan, but `is_pressed` only reads state after the button is actually pressed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4e65edcd-3655-425e-9000-cd8b185d18d2-49","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"poll_gamepad","glob":"**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3868,"output_tokens":1290,"cache_read_input_tokens":85632,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"a10f65b1-dde6-41c6-8694-4993e61c27a2"}
