{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f9f752b5-0d06-4aa3-82e1-97103d070488-52","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Window events -> egui input. Natively this is egui-winit; in the browser (where egui-winit\\n//! does not build) a small adapter covers what the panels use: pointer, wheel, keys and text.\\n\\nuse winit::event::WindowEvent;\\nuse winit::window::Window;\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\npub struct UiInput(egui_winit::State);\\n\\n10→#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nimpl UiInput {\\n    pub fn new(ctx: &egui::Context, window: &Window, max_texture: usize) -> Self {\\n        Self(egui_winit::State::new(\\n            ctx.clone(),\\n            egui::ViewportId::ROOT,\\n            window,\\n            Some(window.scale_factor() as f32),\\n            None,\\n            Some(max_texture),\\n20→        ))\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Feeds an event to egui; true when egui used it (the game should ignore it).\\n    pub fn on_window_event(&mut self, window: &Window, event: &WindowEvent) -> bool {\\n        self.0.on_window_event(window, event).consumed\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn take(&mut self, window: &Window) -> egui::RawInput {\\n        self.0.take_egui_input(window)\\n30→    }\\n\\n    pub fn platform_output(&mut self, window: &Window, out: egui::PlatformOutput) {\\n        self.0.handle_platform_output(window, out);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\npub struct UiInput {\\n    ctx: egui::Context,\\n40→    raw: egui::RawInput,\\n    pointer: egui::Pos2,\\n    modifiers: egui::Modifiers,\\n    start: web_time::Instant,\\n    max_texture: usize,\\n    cursor: egui::CursorIcon,\\n    /// The finger that is egui's pointer (the first one down).\\n    touch_pointer: Option<u64>,\\n}\\n\\n50→#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\nimpl UiInput {\\n    pub fn new(ctx: &egui::Context, _window: &Window, max_texture: usize) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            ctx: ctx.clone(),\\n            raw: egui::RawInput::default(),\\n            pointer: egui::Pos2::ZERO,\\n            modifiers: egui::Modifiers::default(),\\n            start: web_time::Instant::now(),\\n            max_texture,\\n60→            cursor: egui::CursorIcon::Default,\\n            touch_pointer: None,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn ppp(&self, window: &Window) -> f32 {\\n        self.ctx.zoom_factor() * window.scale_factor() as f32\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_window_event(&mut self, window: &Window, event: &WindowEvent) -> bool {\\n70→        use egui::Event;\\n        use winit::event::{MouseButton, MouseScrollDelta};\\n        let ppp = self.ppp(window);\\n        let over_ui = |c: &egui::Context| c.egui_wants_pointer_input() || c.is_pointer_over_egui();\\n        let ev = &mut self.raw.events;\\n        match event {\\n            WindowEvent::CursorMoved { position, .. } => {\\n                self.pointer = egui::pos2(position.x as f32 / ppp, position.y as f32 / ppp);\\n                ev.push(Event::PointerMoved(self.pointer));\\n                over_ui(&self.ctx)\\n80→            }\\n            WindowEvent::CursorLeft { .. } => {\\n                ev.push(Event::PointerGone);\\n                false\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::MouseInput { state, button, .. } => {\\n                let button = match button {\\n                    MouseButton::Left => egui::PointerButton::Primary,\\n                    MouseButton::Right => egui::PointerButton::Secondary,\\n                    MouseButton::Middle => egui::PointerButton::Middle,\\n90→                    MouseButton::Back => egui::PointerButton::Extra1,\\n                    MouseButton::Forward => egui::PointerButton::Extra2,\\n                    MouseButton::Other(_) => return false,\\n                };\\n                ev.push(Event::PointerButton {\\n                    pos: self.pointer,\\n                    button,\\n                    pressed: state.is_pressed(),\\n                    modifiers: self.modifiers,\\n                });\\n100→                over_ui(&self.ctx)\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::MouseWheel { delta, .. } => {\\n                let (unit, delta) = match delta {\\n                    MouseScrollDelta::LineDelta(x, y) => (egui::MouseWheelUnit::Line, egui::vec2(*x, *y)),\\n                    MouseScrollDelta::PixelDelta(p) => (egui::MouseWheelUnit::Point, egui::vec2(p.x as f32, p.y as f32) / ppp),\\n                };\\n                ev.push(Event::MouseWheel { unit, delta, phase: egui::TouchPhase::Move, modifiers: self.modifiers });\\n                over_ui(&self.ctx)\\n            }\\n110→            WindowEvent::ModifiersChanged(m) => {\\n                let s = m.state();\\n                self.modifiers = egui::Modifiers {\\n                    alt: s.alt_key(),\\n                    ctrl: s.control_key(),\\n                    shift: s.shift_key(),\\n                    mac_cmd: false,\\n                    command: s.control_key(),\\n                };\\n                false\\n120→            }\\n            WindowEvent::KeyboardInput { event, .. } => {\\n                use winit::keyboard::Key as K;\\n                let pressed = event.state.is_pressed();\\n                let key = match &event.logical_key {\\n                    K::Named(n) => egui::Key::from_name(&format!(\\\"{n:?}\\\")),\\n                    K::Character(c) => egui::Key::from_name(c.as_str()),\\n                    _ => None,\\n                };\\n                if let Some(key) = key {\\n130→                    ev.push(Event::Key { key, physical_key: None, pressed, repeat: event.repeat, modifiers: self.modifiers });\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Window events -> egui input. Natively this is egui-winit; in the browser (where egui-winit\\n//! does not build) a small adapter covers what the panels use: pointer, wheel, keys and text.\\n\\nuse winit::event::WindowEvent;\\nuse winit::window::Window;\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\npub struct UiInput(egui_winit::State);\\n\\n10→#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nimpl UiInput {\\n    pub fn new(ctx: &egui::Context, window: &Window, max_texture: usize) -> Self {\\n        Self(egui_winit::State::new(\\n            ctx.clone(),\\n            egui::ViewportId::ROOT,\\n            window,\\n            Some(window.scale_factor() as f32),\\n            None,\\n            Some(max_texture),\\n20→        ))\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Feeds an event to egui; true when egui used it (the game should ignore it).\\n    pub fn on_window_event(&mut self, window: &Window, event: &WindowEvent) -> bool {\\n        self.0.on_window_event(window, event).consumed\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn take(&mut self, window: &Window) -> egui::RawInput {\\n        self.0.take_egui_input(window)\\n30→    }\\n\\n    pub fn platform_output(&mut self, window: &Window, out: egui::PlatformOutput) {\\n        self.0.handle_platform_output(window, out);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\npub struct UiInput {\\n    ctx: egui::Context,\\n40→    raw: egui::RawInput,\\n    pointer: egui::Pos2,\\n    modifiers: egui::Modifiers,\\n    start: web_time::Instant,\\n    max_texture: usize,\\n    cursor: egui::CursorIcon,\\n    /// The finger that is egui's pointer (the first one down).\\n    touch_pointer: Option<u64>,\\n}\\n\\n50→#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\nimpl UiInput {\\n    pub fn new(ctx: &egui::Context, _window: &Window, max_texture: usize) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            ctx: ctx.clone(),\\n            raw: egui::RawInput::default(),\\n            pointer: egui::Pos2::ZERO,\\n            modifiers: egui::Modifiers::default(),\\n            start: web_time::Instant::now(),\\n            max_texture,\\n60→            cursor: egui::CursorIcon::Default,\\n            touch_pointer: None,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn ppp(&self, window: &Window) -> f32 {\\n        self.ctx.zoom_factor() * window.scale_factor() as f32\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_window_event(&mut self, window: &Window, event: &WindowEvent) -> bool {\\n70→        use egui::Event;\\n        use winit::event::{MouseButton, MouseScrollDelta};\\n        let ppp = self.ppp(window);\\n        let over_ui = |c: &egui::Context| c.egui_wants_pointer_input() || c.is_pointer_over_egui();\\n        let ev = &mut self.raw.events;\\n        match event {\\n            WindowEvent::CursorMoved { position, .. } => {\\n                self.pointer = egui::pos2(position.x as f32 / ppp, position.y as f32 / ppp);\\n                ev.push(Event::PointerMoved(self.pointer));\\n                over_ui(&self.ctx)\\n80→            }\\n            WindowEvent::CursorLeft { .. } => {\\n                ev.push(Event::PointerGone);\\n                false\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::MouseInput { state, button, .. } => {\\n                let button = match button {\\n                    MouseButton::Left => egui::PointerButton::Primary,\\n                    MouseButton::Right => egui::PointerButton::Secondary,\\n                    MouseButton::Middle => egui::PointerButton::Middle,\\n90→                    MouseButton::Back => egui::PointerButton::Extra1,\\n                    MouseButton::Forward => egui::PointerButton::Extra2,\\n                    MouseButton::Other(_) => return false,\\n                };\\n                ev.push(Event::PointerButton {\\n                    pos: self.pointer,\\n                    button,\\n                    pressed: state.is_pressed(),\\n                    modifiers: self.modifiers,\\n                });\\n100→                over_ui(&self.ctx)\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::MouseWheel { delta, .. } => {\\n                let (unit, delta) = match delta {\\n                    MouseScrollDelta::LineDelta(x, y) => (egui::MouseWheelUnit::Line, egui::vec2(*x, *y)),\\n                    MouseScrollDelta::PixelDelta(p) => (egui::MouseWheelUnit::Point, egui::vec2(p.x as f32, p.y as f32) / ppp),\\n                };\\n                ev.push(Event::MouseWheel { unit, delta, phase: egui::TouchPhase::Move, modifiers: self.modifiers });\\n                over_ui(&self.ctx)\\n            }\\n110→            WindowEvent::ModifiersChanged(m) => {\\n                let s = m.state();\\n                self.modifiers = egui::Modifiers {\\n                    alt: s.alt_key(),\\n                    ctrl: s.control_key(),\\n                    shift: s.shift_key(),\\n                    mac_cmd: false,\\n                    command: s.control_key(),\\n                };\\n                false\\n120→            }\\n            WindowEvent::KeyboardInput { event, .. } => {\\n                use winit::keyboard::Key as K;\\n                let pressed = event.state.is_pressed();\\n                let key = match &event.logical_key {\\n                    K::Named(n) => egui::Key::from_name(&format!(\\\"{n:?}\\\")),\\n                    K::Character(c) => egui::Key::from_name(c.as_str()),\\n                    _ => None,\\n                };\\n                if let Some(key) = key {\\n130→                    ev.push(Event::Key { key, physical_key: None, pressed, repeat: event.repeat, modifiers: self.modifiers });\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/uiinput.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":130,\"raw_output\":\"//! Window events -> egui input. Natively this is egui-winit; in the browser (where egui-winit\\n//! does not build) a small adapter covers what the panels use: pointer, wheel, keys and text.\\n\\nuse winit::event::WindowEvent;\\nuse winit::window::Window;\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\npub struct UiInput(egui_winit::State);\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nimpl UiInput {\\n    pub fn new(ctx: &egui::Context, window: &Window, max_texture: usize) -> Self {\\n        Self(egui_winit::State::new(\\n            ctx.clone(),\\n            egui::ViewportId::ROOT,\\n            window,\\n            Some(window.scale_factor() as f32),\\n            None,\\n            Some(max_texture),\\n        ))\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Feeds an event to egui; true when egui used it (the game should ignore it).\\n    pub fn on_window_event(&mut self, window: &Window, event: &WindowEvent) -> bool {\\n        self.0.on_window_event(window, event).consumed\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn take(&mut self, window: &Window) -> egui::RawInput {\\n        self.0.take_egui_input(window)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn platform_output(&mut self, window: &Window, out: egui::PlatformOutput) {\\n        self.0.handle_platform_output(window, out);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\npub struct UiInput {\\n    ctx: egui::Context,\\n    raw: egui::RawInput,\\n    pointer: egui::Pos2,\\n    modifiers: egui::Modifiers,\\n    start: web_time::Instant,\\n    max_texture: usize,\\n    cursor: egui::CursorIcon,\\n    /// The finger that is egui's pointer (the first one down).\\n    touch_pointer: Option<u64>,\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\nimpl UiInput {\\n    pub fn new(ctx: &egui::Context, _window: &Window, max_texture: usize) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            ctx: ctx.clone(),\\n            raw: egui::RawInput::default(),\\n            pointer: egui::Pos2::ZERO,\\n            modifiers: egui::Modifiers::default(),\\n            start: web_time::Instant::now(),\\n            max_texture,\\n            cursor: egui::CursorIcon::Default,\\n            touch_pointer: None,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn ppp(&self, window: &Window) -> f32 {\\n        self.ctx.zoom_factor() * window.scale_factor() as f32\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_window_event(&mut self, window: &Window, event: &WindowEvent) -> bool {\\n        use egui::Event;\\n        use winit::event::{MouseButton, MouseScrollDelta};\\n        let ppp = self.ppp(window);\\n        let over_ui = |c: &egui::Context| c.egui_wants_pointer_input() || c.is_pointer_over_egui();\\n        let ev = &mut self.raw.events;\\n        match event {\\n            WindowEvent::CursorMoved { position, .. } => {\\n                self.pointer = egui::pos2(position.x as f32 / ppp, position.y as f32 / ppp);\\n                ev.push(Event::PointerMoved(self.pointer));\\n                over_ui(&self.ctx)\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::CursorLeft { .. } => {\\n                ev.push(Event::PointerGone);\\n                false\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::MouseInput { state, button, .. } => {\\n                let button = match button {\\n                    MouseButton::Left => egui::PointerButton::Primary,\\n                    MouseButton::Right => egui::PointerButton::Secondary,\\n                    MouseButton::Middle => egui::PointerButton::Middle,\\n                    MouseButton::Back => egui::PointerButton::Extra1,\\n                    MouseButton::Forward => egui::PointerButton::Extra2,\\n                    MouseButton::Other(_) => return false,\\n                };\\n                ev.push(Event::PointerButton {\\n                    pos: self.pointer,\\n                    button,\\n                    pressed: state.is_pressed(),\\n                    modifiers: self.modifiers,\\n                });\\n                over_ui(&self.ctx)\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::MouseWheel { delta, .. } => {\\n                let (unit, delta) = match delta {\\n                    MouseScrollDelta::LineDelta(x, y) => (egui::MouseWheelUnit::Line, egui::vec2(*x, *y)),\\n                    MouseScrollDelta::PixelDelta(p) => (egui::MouseWheelUnit::Point, egui::vec2(p.x as f32, p.y as f32) / ppp),\\n                };\\n                ev.push(Event::MouseWheel { unit, delta, phase: egui::TouchPhase::Move, modifiers: self.modifiers });\\n                over_ui(&self.ctx)\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::ModifiersChanged(m) => {\\n                let s = m.state();\\n                self.modifiers = egui::Modifiers {\\n                    alt: s.alt_key(),\\n                    ctrl: s.control_key(),\\n                    shift: s.shift_key(),\\n                    mac_cmd: false,\\n                    command: s.control_key(),\\n                };\\n                false\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::KeyboardInput { event, .. } => {\\n                use winit::keyboard::Key as K;\\n                let pressed = event.state.is_pressed();\\n                let key = match &event.logical_key {\\n                    K::Named(n) => egui::Key::from_name(&format!(\\\"{n:?}\\\")),\\n                    K::Character(c) => egui::Key::from_name(c.as_str()),\\n                    _ => None,\\n                };\\n                if let Some(key) = key {\\n                    ev.push(Event::Key { key, physical_key: None, pressed, repeat: event.repeat, modifiers: self.modifiers });\\n\",\"total_lines\":229}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"8907d1ca-4e8d-4671-a0e0-31be9d7f312f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_586","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found the bug in the Rust code. It involves an `over_ui` closure using `egui::Context`.\n\n`is_pointer_over_egui()` might return true for any egui area, not just interactive widgets. This would cause `MouseInput` events to be wrongly consumed. Checking the egui 0.36 docs to confirm.\n\nThe settings click worked, so clicks are not always consumed. This suggests `is_pointer_over_egui` might only trigger over actual widget areas. A coordinate bug was also spotted: pointer positions are divided by `ppp` twice.\n\nThe pointer coordinate bug is harmless when ppp equals 1. The real issue may be that `is_pointer_over_egui` reads the previous frame's egui output. A widget from the last frame could still register at the click point and consume the event. I will inspect the egui source code to verify this behavior.\n\nThe wasm adapter wrongly consumes pointer events when the cursor is over any egui area, even if the fit game needs them. During fit mode, all panels are forced closed, so no egui panels should be interactive. The fix is to ignore egui pointer input while fit is active.\n\nThe simplest fix is to set `consumed = false` in `app.rs` when `self.input.fit` is true, right after the egui event handler runs. This lets the fit game receive clicks that egui would otherwise swallow.\n\nThe fix is safe because the fit UI is painter-only and not egui widgets. Dev mode uses the game's own Flow::Dev, so it remains unaffected. The glyph click failure may be caused by a stray egui widget overlapping the glyph row but not the settings row, such as an invisible full-width area or a game_lines popup.\n\nThe settings screen opening contradicts the theory that every click is swallowed by egui. If a central panel covered the entire screen, clicks would never reach the game. The settings button must sit outside any egui area, or the click was not consumed after all.\n\nThe settings click worked because consumption was false at that position. The glyph row consumed the click instead, so the overlap is position-dependent. A small persistent egui widget likely sits in the lower screen area and overlaps the glyph row but not the title settings button.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f1cbd5b1-7841-4800-bc72-22b0b6b2a2ea-53","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\\.hud\\(\\)|lines:","glob":"**/pav_core/src/sim.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f1cbd5b1-7841-4800-bc72-22b0b6b2a2ea-54","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn is_pointer_over_egui|fn egui_wants_pointer_input","path":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src","glob":"**/egui-0.36*/src/context.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1604,"output_tokens":1294,"cache_read_input_tokens":97152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"1240dfa9-32e6-4e0d-8cd6-149ff0c01f2a"}
