{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_594","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug in the retry logic causes `check()` to count failures before retrying. If the first attempt returns False without throwing, the failure is already recorded and the retry is skipped.\n\nException-based crashes are handled correctly by the retry logic. Browser cleanup is also correct in both success and exception paths. There is a risk of double counting if old iPhone or iPad checks remain.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3f43df39-e82d-4820-9971-ae1aa311beed-69","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/tests/browser.py","old_string":"            context.close()\n        try:\n            check(touch_profile(browser, p, \"iPhone 13\"))\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"iphone: {e}\")\n            failed += 1\n        try:\n            check(touch_profile(browser, p, \"iPad (gen 7)\"))\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"ipad: {e}\")\n            failed += 1\n        browser.close()","new_string":"            context.close()\n        browser.close()"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3f43df39-e82d-4820-9971-ae1aa311beed-70","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"disable-backgrounding-occluded-windows","glob":"**/tests/hub.py"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":690,"output_tokens":725,"cache_read_input_tokens":115200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"e3c3e0d0-7281-4d83-b3ec-7bc503e5afb5"}
