{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_608","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The attract idle counter has a bug. Boot checks generate input that resets idle to zero.\n\nThe attract wait requires 600 ticks of no input. Mouse moves and clicks reset the idle counter, but they stop after returning to the title screen. The test's spacebar press to exit attract may be too short under slow frames, so polling is needed. Status evaluations during the attract wait do not count as game input.\n\nMouse movement alone does not wake the game. The pregame active check requires a click, lean, or slider input to count as waking. After a click, mouse travel resets each frame.\n\nThe cursor resting on the Back button after clicking may produce a mouse lean above 0.3 every frame. This would reset the idle counter indefinitely and prevent attract from ever starting. The prior test never verified attract after a click that leaves the cursor on a row, since it failed before reaching attract. The first boot in the original failing run also never reached attract.\n\nDesktop attract was never proven in the prior run. Phone attract passed because touch taps on a DOM button avoid the off-center cursor issue. The question remains whether resting the mouse away from center should count as a continuous lean input.\n\nAttract should not start while the player is leaning. The test must move the mouse back to center before waiting for attract, since a single move creates one frame of travel and then idle can accumulate. After releasing keyboard input, the lean ramp decays; switching to mouse uses lean_from directly without the ramp.\n\nThe test will move the mouse to the viewport center before waiting for attract, ensuring lean stays below 0.3. The wait will poll for up to four seconds. Attract lasts ninety ticks at five hundred milliseconds each, totaling forty-five seconds.\n\nThe suite will run with a ten-minute timeout to handle slow loads. The probe file will be deleted after the suite passes. Hovering over settings requires a mouse move, which sets the prompt to Click.\n\nThe mouse prompt check runs before click_label, so the subsequent move is harmless. The two-second keyboard and mouse waits should provide enough frames even under slow catch-up. Pressing Space to exit attract may be missed if no frame samples it, so holding Space or retrying the press in a loop until the phase changes is safer.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-99d9226d-5c86-4a0e-b307-9896e93b2915-88","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/tests/browser.py","offset":210,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1475,"output_tokens":1420,"cache_read_input_tokens":130304,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"8b6cbdcf-0053-4ca1-8885-fec13df800b4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-99d9226d-5c86-4a0e-b307-9896e93b2915-88","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"210→        return fail(f\\\"back did not return to title: {None if not s else s.get('phase')}\\\")\\n    attracted = False\\n    for _ in range(50):\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(500)\\n        s = status(page)\\n        if s.get(\\\"phase\\\") == \\\"attract\\\" or s.get(\\\"demo\\\") is True:\\n            attracted = True\\n            break\\n    if not attracted:\\n        return fail(f\\\"attract did not start: {status(page)}\\\")\\n220→    page.keyboard.press(\\\"Space\\\")\\n    page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n    s = status(page)\\n    if s.get(\\\"phase\\\") == \\\"attract\\\" or s.get(\\\"demo\\\") is True:\\n        return fail(f\\\"input did not leave attract: {s.get('phase')} demo {s.get('demo')}\\\")\\n    page.wait_for_timeout(600)\\n    heard = page.evaluate(\\\"() => (window.__fitAudio || []).some((n) => n > 0.0001)\\\")\\n    if not heard:\\n        return fail(\\\"no audible buffer after the gesture\\\")\\n    if errors:\\n230→        return fail(\\\"page errors: \\\" + \\\" | \\\".join(errors[:8]))\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef open_page(browser, viewport):\\n    context = browser.new_context(viewport=viewport, device_scale_factor=1)\\n    page = context.new_page()\\n    errors = []\\n    page.add_init_script(PAD + AUDIO)\\n    page.on(\\\"pageerror\\\", lambda e: errors.append(str(e)))\\n240→    page.on(\\\"console\\\", lambda msg: errors.append(msg.text) if msg.type == \\\"error\\\" else None)\\n    page.goto(HTML.as_uri())\\n    return context, page, errors\\n\\n\\ndef touch_profile(browser, playwright, device_name, viewport=None):\\n    device = dict(playwright.devices[device_name])\\n    # Software WebGPU cannot keep sim time at a phone's device pixel ratio.\\n    device[\\\"device_scale_factor\\\"] = 1\\n    if viewport:\",\"content_concise\":\