{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8cf06369-fd8a-49da-9b4d-6b8d7f8bd374-98","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→(node:182035) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\nxbox toggle False focus 3 label 'Glyphs: PlayStation'\\ntick did not advance 9 -> 9\\n4 passed, 2 failed\\nEXIT:1\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→(node:182035) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\nxbox toggle False focus 3 label 'Glyphs: PlayStation'\\ntick did not advance 9 -> 9\\n4 passed, 2 failed\\nEXIT:1\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/tmp/grok-goal-b3947fd4d9d9/implementer/tests-browser.log\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"(node:182035) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\nxbox toggle False focus 3 label 'Glyphs: PlayStation'\\ntick did not advance 9 -> 9\\n4 passed, 2 failed\\nEXIT:1\\n\",\"total_lines\":6}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"aae6dc5b-80e6-4a36-92ec-351f942a5436"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_617","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The first boot reached the Xbox toggle.\n\nHovering the glyph row works, but clicking it fails to toggle Xbox. The second boot stalled completely; the tick never advanced past 9 despite waiting four seconds. This suggests a GPU or browser context leak from the first boot is blocking the second run.\n\nThe Xbox bug is confirmed. The click lands on the glyph row but never toggles the Xbox state. The UI event likely fails to apply, applies twice, or activates the focused item through a path that skips the toggle.\n\nThe label remains 'Glyphs: PlayStation', confirming the Xbox state never flipped. The click function moves to center, waits for the glyph label, then clicks. The failure likely stems from a swallowed tap, a missing activation path, or a position mismatch between hover and click sampling. The `over_ui` flag is now set based on whether the cursor fits inside the window and egui wants pointer input.\n\nThe fix is confirmed in the HTML, since boot 1 reached the Xbox toggle. The new theory is a double-toggle: the click sets Xbox to true, but something else immediately sets it back to false. A CONFIRM event on the focused item in the same frame is suspected. The pre() function order is being examined.\n\nThe pre() function order confirms the double-toggle theory. Click toggles Xbox to true, but CONFIRM on the same frame toggles it back to false. This perfectly matches the observed label and focus state. The remaining question is why CONFIRM fires on the click frame. The mouse left button maps to PRIMARY, so the fit bindings may be incorrectly mapping left click to confirm. Another possibility is a sticky gamepad button state.\n\nThe gamepad stub only presses button 13, so the South button is not stuck. The fit menu uses CONFIRM exclusively, and the PRIMARY and CONFIRM constants are distinct bit flags. This rules out both a sticky gamepad state and a direct alias between PRIMARY and CONFIRM.\n\nA keyboard binding that synthesizes Enter from a mouse click is ruled out. The focus being 3 while the Xbox state stays false could also mean the click never fired at all, rather than toggling twice. The next step is to determine whether the click event actually reaches the game or if both the click and CONFIRM are firing in the same frame.\n\nThe tap recording path is being traced. Because the fit menu sets consumed to false, the mouse button press should register and insert a left_tap event. This suggests the click itself is being captured by the input system.\n\nThe frame() function clears mouse taps before buttons() samples them. The tap is consumed and removed, so buttons() never sees it. PRIMARY might still be held if the left button remains down, or it could be sampled as pressed if the click spans the frame boundary.\n\nThe frame-level input trace shows a single left click should produce exactly one click event. The tap is consumed during sampling, and the button remains held for the next frame. This rules out a double-toggle caused by the same click firing twice.\n\nThe hit-test theory is ruled out. Hover successfully focuses the glyph row using the same cursor coordinates, so the click should land inside the rectangle. The failure is not caused by a pixel mismatch or missed hit test.\n\nThe cursor should already be at the target before the click, so a stale-frame miss is unlikely. The next step is to verify that the published click ID matches ACT_XBOX (40) inside activate_settings.\n\nThe click event reaches activate_settings with the correct ACT_XBOX id. Focus index 3 maps to that same id, so the activation path is sound.\n\nThe click event reaches activate_settings with the correct ACT_XBOX id. The settings phase is not being reset by apply_slider or any other mechanism.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d731235b-ad67-4594-a1d6-3d581ca161b4-99","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"take_mouse_tap|\\.buttons\\(\\)|fn frame\\(","glob":"**/pav_app/src/app.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d731235b-ad67-4594-a1d6-3d581ca161b4-100","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn fit\\(","glob":"**/pav_app/src/input.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":279,"output_tokens":2172,"cache_read_input_tokens":142336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"4fd5129e-b56d-46a1-b81f-0cc03a0e5f55"}
