{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_620","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Settings is not a pregame flow for idle.\n\nI'll probe the settings toggle without rebuilding. I'll test whether a direct DOM click on ACT_XBOX triggers the setting, or if the WASM build is broken.\n\nI'll set `window.__fitClick = 40` after opening settings to test the direct toggle path. I'll also log focus and a custom counter during a mouse click to isolate the bug.\n\nI'll record the xbox state before and after setting `__fitClick = 40` to isolate whether the mouse click itself is failing. If the direct toggle works, I'll fix the mouse path rather than switching the test to bypass it. The settings click itself is confirmed working.\n\nThe glyph click fails even though it uses the same function. Focus resets to zero when settings opens, then moves to glyph and hover sets focus to three. The settings rows might be sliders that apply values on click rather than activate toggles. ACT_XBOX is 40, which sits outside the slider range, so activate_settings should match it.\n\nI ruled out tap consumption by the settings click. Each click is a new press, so the glyph click should register independently.\n\nI need to verify the WASM build actually contains the source change. The HTML timestamp and test output confirm the page is fresh.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2c6fad79-56be-48e5-966f-b3e7f74fa4f5-105","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":2268,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2c6fad79-56be-48e5-966f-b3e7f74fa4f5-106","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":1195,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1644,"output_tokens":875,"cache_read_input_tokens":147200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"bb13fec3-f8cf-43d2-8a94-b12e9db64666"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2c6fad79-56be-48e5-966f-b3e7f74fa4f5-105","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2268→\\n    fn window_event(&mut self, el: &ActiveEventLoop, _id: WindowId, event: WindowEvent) {\\n2270→        if let WindowEvent::Touch(t) = &event {\\n            self.on_touch(t, &event);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let mut consumed = match (&mut self.egui_state, &self.gfx) {\\n            (Some(st), Some(g)) => st.on_window_event(&g.window, &event),\\n            _ => false,\\n        };\\n        // Stay rows are sim hit-targets drawn with a painter. egui still reports the\\n        // pointer as \\\"over UI\\\" when that layer's rect overlaps a row, and the tap is lost.\\n2280→        if self.input.fit {\\n            consumed = false;\\n        }\\n        match event {\\n            WindowEvent::CloseRequested => {\\n                if let Some(host) = &self.host {\\n                    host.exec(|sim| crate::save::save_from(sim));\\n                }\\n                self.look_ui.save_if_dirty(true);\\n                el.exit()\\n2290→            }\\n            WindowEvent::Focused(false) => {\\n                self.input.clear();\\n                self.touch.clear();\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::Resized(sz) => {\\n                if let Some(g) = &mut self.gfx {\\n                    g.resize(sz.width, sz.height);\",\"content_concise\":\"2268→\\n    fn window_event(&mut self, el: &ActiveEventLoop, _id: WindowId, event: WindowEvent) {\\n2270→        if let WindowEvent::Touch(t) = &event {\\n            self.on_touch(t, &event);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let mut consumed = match (&mut self.egui_state, &self.gfx) {\\n            (Some(st), Some(g)) => st.on_window_event(&g.window, &event),\\n            _ => false,\\n        };\\n        // Stay rows are sim hit-targets drawn with a painter. egui still reports the\\n        // pointer as \\\"over UI\\\" when that layer's rect overlaps a row, and the tap is lost.\\n2280→        if self.input.fit {\\n            consumed = false;\\n        }\\n        match event {\\n            WindowEvent::CloseRequested => {\\n                if let Some(host) = &self.host {\\n                    host.exec(|sim| crate::save::save_from(sim));\\n                }\\n                self.look_ui.save_if_dirty(true);\\n                el.exit()\\n2290→            }\\n            WindowEvent::Focused(false) => {\\n                self.input.clear();\\n                self.touch.clear();\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::Resized(sz) => {\\n                if let Some(g) = &mut self.gfx {\\n                    g.resize(sz.width, sz.height);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs\",\"offset\":2268,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"\\n    fn window_event(&mut self, el: &ActiveEventLoop, _id: WindowId, event: WindowEvent) {\\n        if let WindowEvent::Touch(t) = &event {\\n            self.on_touch(t, &event);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let mut consumed = match (&mut self.egui_state, &self.gfx) {\\n            (Some(st), Some(g)) => st.on_window_event(&g.window, &event),\\n            _ => false,\\n        };\\n        // Stay rows are sim hit-targets drawn with a painter. egui still reports the\\n        // pointer as \\\"over UI\\\" when that layer's rect overlaps a row, and the tap is lost.\\n        if self.input.fit {\\n            consumed = false;\\n        }\\n        match event {\\n            WindowEvent::CloseRequested => {\\n                if let Some(host) = &self.host {\\n                    host.exec(|sim| crate::save::save_from(sim));\\n                }\\n                self.look_ui.save_if_dirty(true);\\n                el.exit()\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::Focused(false) => {\\n                self.input.clear();\\n                self.touch.clear();\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::Resized(sz) => {\\n                if let Some(g) = &mut self.gfx {\\n                    g.resize(sz.width, sz.height);\\n\",\"total_lines\":2548}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2c6fad79-56be-48e5-966f-b3e7f74fa4f5-106","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1195→                self.menu_open = false;\\n                self.input.clear();\\n            }\\n            host.set_control(|c| c.rewinding = false);\\n        }\\n1200→        let (w, h) = self.gfx.as_ref().unwrap().size();\\n        let size = Vec2::new(w as f32, h as f32);\\n        // Same as above: a painted stay row is not an egui control, so the tap stands.\\n        let over_ui = !fit_on && self.egui_ctx.egui_wants_pointer_input();\\n        let left_tap = self.input.take_mouse_tap(MouseButton::Left) && !over_ui;\\n        if over_ui {\\n            self.input.mouse_taps.clear();\\n        }\\n        let (mut held, mut pressed) = self.input.buttons();\\n        // Touch: the stick, the buttons and auto-attack.\\n1210→        let touch_game = curr.game.as_deref().filter(|_| game_input && !fit_on).map(|g| (g, feet, facing));\\n        let rig = &self.rig;\\n        let intent = self.touch.intent(touch_game, |v| rig.relative_move(v), self.prefs.auto_attack);\\n        if game_input && !fit_on {\\n            held |= intent.held;\\n            pressed |= intent.pressed;\\n        }\\n        if pressed & pav_core::input::buttons::INTERACT != 0 {\\n            if let Some(g) = &curr.game {\\n                if let Some(c) = self.game_ui.interact(g) {\\n1220→                    host.shared.command(c);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if pressed != 0 && self.input.last_device == Device::Gamepad {\\n            // Gamepad presses are timed from when they were polled (gilrs queues them).\\n            self.latency.press();\\n        }\\n        let room_id = self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| r.id);\\n        let left = self.input.mouse.contains(&MouseButton::Left) && !over_ui;\\n1230→        if left_tap && !self.editor.on && game_input && !fit_on {\\n            pressed |= pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\\n        if !fit_on && !studio_active && self.editor.update(host, &self.rig, self.input.cursor, size, left, left_tap, room_id) {\\n            held &= !pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n            pressed &= !pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\\n        let aim = match self.input.last_device {\\n            Device::KeyboardMouse => self.rig.ground_point(self.input.cursor, size, feet.y),\\n            Device::Gamepad => {\\n1240→                let r = self.input.pad.right;\\n                if r.length() > 0.2 {\\n                    let d = self.rig.relative_move(r);\\n                    Some(feet + Vec3::new(d.x, 0.0, d.y) * self.sim_config.bombs.throw_range * r.length().min(1.0))\\n                } else {\\n                    Some(feet + Vec3::new(facing.sin(), 0.0, facing.cos()) * 4.0)\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Device::Touch => intent.aim.or(Some(feet + Vec3::new(facing.sin(), 0.0, facing.cos()) * 4.0)),\\n        };\\n1250→        {\\n            let mut i = host.shared.input.lock().unwrap();\\n            if fit_on {\\n                let items: Vec<(u16, [f32; 4])> = curr\\n                    .hud\\n                    .fit\\n                    .as_ref()\\n                    .map(|u| u.items.iter().map(|it| (it.id, it.rect)).collect())\\n                    .unwrap_or_default();\\n                let dom = crate::weblink::take_fit_click();\\n1260→                let sample = self.input.fit_sample(dt, size, &items, left_tap || dom.is_some());\\n                let mut ui_ev = sample.ui;\\n                if let Some(id) = dom {\\n                    ui_ev = Some(pav_core::input::UiEvent::Click(id));\\n                }\\n                if ui_ev.is_some() {\\n                    held &= !pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n                    pressed &= !pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n                }\\n                pressed |= sample.extra;\\n1270→                i.move_dir = self.rig.relative_move(self.input.move_axis());\\n                i.held = held;\\n                i.pressed |= pressed;\\n                i.aim = None;\\n                i.lean = sample.lean;\",\"content_concise\":\"1195→                self.menu_open = false;\\n                self.input.clear();\\n            }\\n            host.set_control(|c| c.rewinding = false);\\n        }\\n1200→        let (w, h) = self.gfx.as_ref().unwrap().size();\\n        let size = Vec2::new(w as f32, h as f32);\\n        // Same as above: a painted stay row is not an egui control, so the tap stands.\\n        let over_ui = !fit_on && self.egui_ctx.egui_wants_pointer_input();\\n        let left_tap = self.input.take_mouse_tap(MouseButton::Left) && !over_ui;\\n        if over_ui {\\n            self.input.mouse_taps.clear();\\n        }\\n        let (mut held, mut pressed) = self.input.buttons();\\n        // Touch: the stick, the buttons and auto-attack.\\n1210→        let touch_game = curr.game.as_deref().filter(|_| game_input && !fit_on).map(|g| (g, feet, facing));\\n        let rig = &self.rig;\\n        let intent = self.touch.intent(touch_game, |v| rig.relative_move(v), self.prefs.auto_attack);\\n        if game_input && !fit_on {\\n            held |= intent.held;\\n            pressed |= intent.pressed;\\n        }\\n        if pressed & pav_core::input::buttons::INTERACT != 0 {\\n            if let Some(g) = &curr.game {\\n                if let Some(c) = self.game_ui.interact(g) {\\n1220→                    host.shared.command(c);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if pressed != 0 && self.input.last_device == Device::Gamepad {\\n