{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_629","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Even setting `__fitClick = 40` fails to toggle the Xbox.\n\nThe simulation is running. Settings clicks work, but the fit click does not. The fit click handler likely reads the value once and clears it to zero, so it toggles only once and stays off.\n\nMouse clicks work, but __fitClick does not. The fit click handler reads the value correctly and returns 40. The bug likely lies in app.rs where the returned DOM ID is processed.\n\nThe DOM click ID is correctly set to 40.0 and should pass the f64 conversion. The value is visible after a long delay, so the failure likely lies in how the Rust handler consumes it.\n\nThe `bind::get` function might not return numbers correctly. The `ACT_XBOX` constant matches the item ID 40, so a mismatch is unlikely. The settings toggle uses `&mut self`, so the state should update and publish properly.\n\nThe input UI is not clearing. fit_sample also generates a click. Both paths produce Click(40). The DOM value clears after one read. The next frame should be Hover. The toggle should stay true.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8a58624d-26b6-413e-99b6-cd4d9db144bd-116","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\\.xbox","glob":"**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":880,"output_tokens":927,"cache_read_input_tokens":157824,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"47739172-c1b1-4096-a2d9-847d905700d0"}
