1,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,100,111,99,115,47,65,83,83,69,84,95,83,89,83,84,69,77,95,80,76,65,78,46,109,100,10,49,53,49,55,58,99,104,101,99,107,108,105,115,116,59,32,114,111,119,115,32,114,117,110,32,105,110,32,111,114,100,101,114,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,112,108,97,110,39,115,32,115,101,99,116,105,111,110,115,32,115,112,101,99,105,102,121,32,101,97,99,104,32,119,111,114,107,32,105,116,101,109,46,32,84,104,101,32,194,167,51,32,100,101,99,105,115,105,111,110,115,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":26,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"    \\\"Six defects showed up in testing: a gust check that did not match the acceleration model, an egui texture delta dropped on the floor, a private intent module, fonts bound in the same pass that drew them, a hub ghost field that was a boolean, and About pages that did not turn.\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\"    \\\"Yes. A gust is an acceleration, so gust 30 with no lean settles inside the disc and does not tip. egui 0.36 panics if a TexturesDelta is dropped. Pause still increments the tick; the world time is what freezes.\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"    \\\"Say, next to the gust sentence, that a full lean alone must not tip and a gust on top of that lean must. State that plan filenames are guidance in the same paragraph as the file tree.\\\"\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":10,\"content\":\"- **Gaps:** if something is not covered, decide, write one line in `notes/decisions.md`, and carry on.\"},{\"line_number\":100,\"content\":\"acc    = (target - cob) * stiffness - vel * damping + gust + nudge\"},{\"line_number\":108,\"content\":\"**Feel targets** (these numbers give them, by numeric simulation at 60 ticks/s): full stick reaches 90% in about 0.4 s with about 5% overshoot, like a body. Release settles in about 0.45 s. Left alone, the dot wanders at a mean radius of 0.05, at most 0.08. A held full lean does not tip by itself; a gust on top of it does.\"},{\"line_number\":159,\"content\":\"2. A pose under rising gusts, 20 s.\"},{\"line_number\":329,\"content\":\"**SFX (at least 30):** UI move, confirm, back, stamp thunk, clam gulp, Age slot ticks, step, Pip squeak on landing, wood creak, small and big splash, gull squawk, crowd murmur, clap, gong, rep bell, ring whoosh, shell roll (noise by speed), shell plop, glass plop, confetti pop, gust, wave crash, sea-wash ambience, Eyes Closed tone.\"},{\"line_number\":367,\"content\":\"- **Tuning:** live sliders, generated from `impl Tunable for Rules` with `params::list` and `params::set`, grouped by core and by event, with **Reset to Defaults** per group and for all. Must include: stiffness, damping, wobble, tip time, stick curve, key rates, each event's main difficulty number, rhythm windows, spin band, gust strength, bounce gain, Big Stand gusts.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/notes/feedback.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1,\"content\":\"- Gust check expected a lean-free shove to tip. The model treats gust as acceleration, so it settles inside the disc. The check now holds a full lean first. Not a game bug.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/AGENTS.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":12,\"content\":\"need. The journal and past decisions are in `docs/HISTORY.md`, newest first: search it, don't\"},{\"line_number\":250,\"content\":\"  the decisions); then update `docs/PROGRESS.md`, which stays one page of current state.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/README.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":26,\"content\":\"  history and decisions: [`docs/HISTORY.md`](docs/HISTORY.md). Principles:\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/docs/ESCALATIONS.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":52,\"content\":\"  prompt to finish the project\\\". Their decisions in the same session: completion first; costs in\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/docs/DESIGN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":173,\"content\":\"- **Progress log:** `docs/PROGRESS.md` is one page of current state (where things stand, what's next, open issues), so any agent can resume; `docs/HISTORY.md` is the full journal of what was built and the decisions made.\"},{\"line_number\":175,\"content\":\"- **Decisions:** ask the user only about decisions that are genuinely theirs. Otherwise decide, record the decision (in this document if it changes the design, otherwise in `docs/HISTORY.md`), and continue. Escalations follow the doctrine and are logged in `docs/ESCALATIONS.md`.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/docs/PROGRESS.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":58,\"content\":\"changed, how it works, the decisions), then update the sections above. Keep this page under 60\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/docs/COOP_PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":645,\"content\":\"3. **Effort: extra (xhigh).** The design decisions are made here; what remains is a long,\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":69,\"content\":\"triggers. Choices that touch decisions the user already made (plan D5, local licence tiers, the\"},{\"line_number\":544,\"content\":\"history. The user's decisions of 2026-10-15 recorded here are binding.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/docs/HISTORY.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"The full journal, newest first: what was built, how it works, and the decisions made along the\"},{\"line_number\":1039,\"content\":\"- **Open:** nine decisions for the user, each with a default (§14).\"},{\"line_number\":1214,\"content\":\"- **Smaller fixes and decisions.** A view in which the source and the translation both draw\"},{\"line_number\":2945,\"content\":\"- **Wind** (`view.wind`, `wind_angle`, `wind_gusts`, `grass_push`): vertex animation in the scene\"},{\"line_number\":2948,\"content\":\"  the player's feet within 0.9 m, and sinks as it bends); gusts roll along the wind as a slow\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/docs/ASSET_SYSTEM_PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1517,\"content\":\"checklist; rows run in order and the plan's sections specify each work item. The §3 decisions\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"6aa4198f-a744-4397-b3cc-5bf18de80156"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_652","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The goal plan lacks a Deviations section.\n\nAdding a ## Deviations section to goal/plan.md. The first bullet notes that the song index follows desired_song.\n\nFive more deviations are being considered: first-six menus, gust test wording, wasm constructor js_class, starved rAF polling, and headless timer flags. These will be verified against notes/decisions.md before adding bullets. Checkboxes will not be flipped until the hub step is done and the target is deleted.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-edb5a063-6594-4c80-b632-1c0abd895f9a-147","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/notes/decisions.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-edb5a063-6594-4c80-b632-1c0abd895f9a-148","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2743,"output_tokens":587,"cache_read_input_tokens":184064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"4909f1ef-9e4c-4d8b-8d11-b58d5fbba41f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-edb5a063-6594-4c80-b632-1c0abd895f9a-147","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→- Last input device wins. Touch does not leave attract and does not count as a real controller.\\n- Hub ghosts are drawn in the view from `window.__hub.ghosts`. The sim only publishes its own sample, so a session stays deterministic.\\n- Long tests set `history_seconds` to 0. A normal boot keeps 8 seconds of rewind.\\n- About text comes from `#about-data` when the page sets it. Native runs keep a readable fallback with the same headings.\\n- The name, look and outfit menus show the first six entries. The rest stay in `script.toml`.\\n- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6. That is the sim's song map.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→- Last input device wins. Touch does not leave attract and does not count as a real controller.\\n- Hub ghosts are drawn in the view from `window.__hub.ghosts`. The sim only publishes its own sample, so a session stays deterministic.\\n- Long tests set `history_seconds` to 0. A normal boot keeps 8 seconds of rewind.\\n- About text comes from `#about-data` when the page sets it. Native runs keep a readable fallback with the same headings.\\n- The name, look and outfit menus show the first six entries. The rest stay in `script.toml`.\\n- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6. That is the sim's song map.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/notes/decisions.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"- Last input device wins. Touch does not leave attract and does not count as a real controller.\\n- Hub ghosts are drawn in the view from `window.__hub.ghosts`. The sim only publishes its own sample, so a session stays deterministic.\\n- Long tests set `history_seconds` to 0. A normal boot keeps 8 seconds of rewind.\\n- About text comes from `#about-data` when the page sets it. Native runs keep a readable fallback with the same headings.\\n- The name, look and outfit menus show the first six entries. The rest stay in `script.toml`.\\n- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6. That is the sim's song map.\\n\",\"total_lines\":6}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-edb5a063-6594-4c80-b632-1c0abd895f9a-148","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:21:32\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Shardfall engine (Pavilion: Rust, wgpu, egui 0.36.2), commit 49ef2ba, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's cel look, high-key pastel, beach and wellness props. Library props only for generic dressing.\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine puppet, tilted about the feet by the balance dot. Motion clips are the engine library.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Music, effects and voices are synthesized in code. No audio files. Seven music beds, default music gain 0.10. At least 30 effects. Animalese voices.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players. The round is the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup).\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU at 320×180, phone and tablet profiles, WebKit iPhone fallback, and the AI Hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The build followed PLAN.md and the engine source. The title was drawn with a real RNG from 50 riffs. No separate web search in this session.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Six defects showed up in testing: a gust check that did not match the acceleration model, an egui texture delta dropped on the floor, a private intent module, fonts bound in the same pass that drew them, a hub ghost field that was a boolean, and About pages that did not turn.\\\",\\n    \\\"One was critical. The font and texture-delta panic stops the browser frame loop, so the page sits there with a status that never ticks.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the bot playthrough: three seeds from New Stay to the credits, plus each event on five seeds against an idle player.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful check is a 1920×1080 WebGPU screenshot. On this machine that bitmap can come back blank while the sim is fine. 320×180 is the timing check, and the engine's own capture is the picture.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The sim is one tick you can drive with no GPU, and the picture is a pure view of that tick. That split is what made the whole stay testable.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A gust is an acceleration, so gust 30 with no lean settles inside the disc and does not tip. egui 0.36 panics if a TexturesDelta is dropped. Pause still increments the tick; the world time is what freezes.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance model, the day loop, and every event. The engine does not have a centre-of-pressure verb.\\\",\\n    \\\"The app frame. The demo's keys, menus and chrome run in the same function as the game, and a fit frame has to turn all of that off without breaking the engine's other scenes.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"frozen() returns early inside the tick. InputFrame gained lean, device, ui and hub. The HUD carries the fit UI and a status string. The mixer plays song beds. The page bridge publishes status. Captures composite the fit UI. Puppets tilt about the feet. Splash and a silent wake were added for the lagoon.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to publish one JSON value that is both a string (for JSON.parse) and an object (for .tick), without hand-rolling a String constructor.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan is specific about the feel, the roster and the hub snippet, and it says behaviour is the contract when a filename does not match the engine.\\\",\\n    \\\"Song numbers in the plan and the beds the sim actually requests do not use the same index. The hub snippet sends whatever status.hub.ghost is, so a boolean there is sent as a boolean.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping the full roster, the 10-foot shell and the hub harness on a 20 GB machine where one extra browser gets killed.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say, next to the gust sentence, that a full lean alone must not tip and a gust on top of that lean must. State that plan filenames are guidance in the same paragraph as the file tree.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Wobble Minutes\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Five days, one mat\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A third-person balance comedy at Tippy Cay. Lean through a week of sports mini-games, then stand still when it matters.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean with the stick, WASD or the mouse. Confirm with Cross, Space or click.\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"sports\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"low-poly\\\", \\\"versus\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:21:32\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Shardfall engine (Pavilion: Rust, wgpu, egui 0.36.2), commit 49ef2ba, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's cel look, high-key pastel, beach and wellness props. Library props only for generic dressing.\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine puppet, tilted about the feet by the balance dot. Motion clips are the engine library.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Music, effects and voices are synthesized in code. No audio files. Seven music beds, default music gain 0.10. At least 30 effects. Animalese voices.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players. The round is the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup).\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU at 320×180, phone and tablet profiles, WebKit iPhone fallback, and the AI Hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The build followed PLAN.md and the engine source. The title was drawn with a real RNG from 50 riffs. No separate web search in this session.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Six defects showed up in testing: a gust check that did not match the acceleration model, an egui texture delta dropped on the floor, a private intent module, fonts bound in the same pass that drew them, a hub ghost field that was a boolean, and About pages that did not turn.\\\",\\n    \\\"One was critical. The font and texture-delta panic stops the browser frame loop, so the page sits there with a status that never ticks.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the bot playthrough: three seeds from New Stay to the credits, plus each event on five seeds against an idle player.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful check is a 1920×1080 WebGPU screenshot. On this machine that bitmap can come back blank while the sim is fine. 320×180 is the timing check, and the engine's own capture is the picture.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The sim is one tick you can drive with no GPU, and the picture is a pure view of that tick. That split is what made the whole stay testable.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A gust is an acceleration, so gust 30 with no lean settles inside the disc and does not tip. egui 0.36 panics if a TexturesDelta is dropped. Pause still increments the tick; the world time is what freezes.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance model, the day loop, and every event. The engine does not have a centre-of-pressure verb.\\\",\\n    \\\"The app frame. The demo's keys, menus and chrome run in the same function as the game, and a fit frame has to turn all of that off without breaking the engine's other scenes.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"frozen() returns early inside the tick. InputFrame gained lean, device, ui and hub. The HUD carries the fit UI and a status string. The mixer plays song beds. The page bridge publishes status. Captures composite the fit UI. Puppets tilt about the feet. Splash and a silent wake were added for the lagoon.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to publish one JSON value that is both a string (for JSON.parse) and an object (for .tick), without hand-rolling a String constructor.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan is specific about the feel, the roster and the hub snippet, and it says behaviour is the contract when a filename does not match the engine.\\\",\\n    \\\"Song numbers in the plan and the beds the sim actually requests do not use the same index. The hub snippet sends whatever status.hub.ghost is, so a boolean there is sent as a boolean.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping the full roster, the 10-foot shell and the hub harness on a 20 GB machine where one extra browser gets killed.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say, next to the gust sentence, that a full lean alone must not tip and a gust on top of that lean must. State that plan filenames are guidance in the same paragraph as the file tree.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Wobble Minutes\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Five days, one mat\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A third-person balance comedy at Tippy Cay. Lean through a week of sports mini-games, then stand still when it matters.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean with the stick, WASD or the mouse. Confirm with Cross, Space or click.\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"sports\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"low-poly\\\", \\\"versus\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:21:32\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Shardfall engine (Pavilion: Rust, wgpu, egui 0.36.2), commit 49ef2ba, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's cel look, high-key pastel, beach and wellness props. Library props only for generic dressing.\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine puppet, tilted about the feet by the balance dot. Motion clips are the engine library.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Music, effects and voices are synthesized in code. No audio files. Seven music beds, default music gain 0.10. At least 30 effects. Animalese voices.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players. The round is the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup).\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, Playwright Chromium with software W