mber\":323,\"content\":\"    sentReady = true;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"10363550-f106-48f0-a787-e9001a6dc43c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_670","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand the timeline first.\n\nThe harness waits 20 seconds for all copies to be ready before starting the round. If AIHub.ready() is called immediately after connect, the round begins while games are still compiling and initializing WebGPU. The fourth game may boot too late, causing progress and ghost checks to fail.\n\nThree-player runs with network degradation passed, but the fourth copy failed only on ready. This points to a load issue: four heavy wasm and WebGPU iframes may not finish GPU initialization within the 20-second window. Calling ready() immediately would let all copies report ready before GPU boot, starting the round too early.\n\nI need to read the harness round-start logic and the game's progress sending. The key is calling ready within 20 seconds of page load while ensuring the game keeps running and sending progress during the play window. I am now weighing possible solutions.\n\nThree options are on the table. Ready immediately after the WebGPU check, but slow copies may not finish booting before the play window ends. Speed up boot to fit four iframes within 20 seconds, though software WebGPU shader compilation is inherently slow. Or ready early and rely on fast progress sending, but the harness controls the play window and verifier timeouts. I need to find the official harness.\n\nThe verifier likely uses the original harness from the plan rather than a modified local copy. Extending the 20-second timeout in hub/harness.html would not help if the official harness is running. The session.js comment confirms the intended contract: ready once the page loads, not after GPU initialization. This validates calling AIHub.ready() immediately as the correct fix.\n\nI need to verify that progress is still sent after the round starts. The game hub code should handle a late start correctly if hub.go is already true. The harness waits for the playing phase or a record before checking progress.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f50bc712-f936-41ae-a9a9-b6fd2dd3675f-5","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/tools/write_index.py","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f50bc712-f936-41ae-a9a9-b6fd2dd3675f-6","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/hub/harness.html","offset":60,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f50bc712-f936-41ae-a9a9-b6fd2dd3675f-7","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/hub/harness.html","offset":400,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f50bc712-f936-41ae-a9a9-b6fd2dd3675f-8","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/hub/session.js","offset":300,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2453,"output_tokens":1211,"cache_read_input_tokens":32000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"9d584ed0-337a-4b2d-8890-a3ba409d3766"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f50bc712-f936-41ae-a9a9-b6fd2dd3675f-5","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Write engine/web/index.html with session.js pasted byte for byte and about-data filled.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json\\nimport pathlib\\n\\nDEV = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nWORK = DEV.parent\\nSESSION = (DEV / \\\"hub\\\" / \\\"session.js\\\").read_bytes()\\n10→INTERVIEW = json.loads((WORK / \\\"exit-interview.json\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"))\\nABOUT = json.dumps(INTERVIEW, ensure_ascii=False).replace(\\\"<\\\", \\\"\\\\\\\\u003c\\\")\\n\\nIIFE = r\\\"\\\"\\\"(() => {\\n  const boot = window.__gameBoot = { scene: null, seed: null, today: Math.floor(Date.now() / 86400000),\\n                                     about: document.getElementById('about-data')?.textContent ?? '' };\\n  if (!window.AIHub || !AIHub.active) return;\\n  const hub = window.__hub = { go: false, ended: false, players: [], me: 0, ghosts: {} };\\n  boot.scene = 'fit/medley';\\n  boot.seed = Number((/[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(location.search) || [])[1] || 1);\\n20→  AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\\n    if (!info) { location.replace(location.pathname); return; }   // no hub after all\\n    if (!navigator.gpu) { AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU'); return; }\\n    hub.me = info.me; hub.players = info.players;\\n    // Before the first status arrives, report a zero: the hub must always hear a number.\\n    const status = () => { try { return JSON.parse(window.__gameStatus || 'null')?.hub ?? null; } catch { return null; } };\\n    const waitReady = () => (window.__gameStatus ? AIHub.ready() : setTimeout(waitReady, 50));\\n    waitReady();\\n    let reported = false;\\n    const report = () => { if (reported) return; reported = true; const s = status(); AIHub.result({ score: s?.score ?? 0, stats: s?.stats ?? {} }); };\\n30→    setInterval(() => {\\n      if (AIHub.time() < 0 || hub.ended) return;\\n      hub.go = true;\\n      const s = status();\\n      AIHub.progress({ score: s?.score ?? 0, label: s?.label ?? 'Warming up' });\\n      if (!reported) AIHub.send(s?.ghost ?? { area: -1 }, { reliable: false });\\n      if (s?.done) report();\\n    }, 100);\\n    AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => { hub.ghosts[from] = data; });\\n    AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { delete hub.ghosts[id]; });\\n40→    AIHub.on('time-up', report);\\n    AIHub.on('end', () => { hub.ended = true; });\\n  });\\n})();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nPAGE = \\\"\\\"\\\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n50→<script>\\\"\\\"\\\" + SESSION.decode(\\\"utf-8\\\") + \\\"\\\"\\\"</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Highest total across three balance events wins\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n<script id=\\\"about-data\\\" type=\\\"application/json\\\">\\\"\\\"\\\" + ABOUT + \\\"\\\"\\\"</script>\\n<script>\\n60→\\\"\\\"\\\" + IIFE + \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\\\">\\n<title>Wobble Minutes — Five days, one mat</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"Lean through a week of balance games at Tippy Cay, a pastel resort staffed by talking gym gear.\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"theme-color\\\" content=\\\"#f4e7d4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"mobile-web-app-capable\\\" content=\\\"yes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\\\" content=\\\"yes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\\\" content=\\\"black-translucent\\\">\\n<link rel=\\\"manifest\\\" href=\\\"manifest.webmanifest\\\">\\n70→<link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='14' fill='%23f4e7d4'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='4' fill='%233b2a4a'/%3E%3C/svg%3E\\\">\\n<style>\\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #f4e7d4; overscroll-behavior: none;\\n               touch-action: none; -webkit-user-select: none; user-select: none; -webkit-touch-callout: none;\\n               -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; }\\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100vw !important; height: 100vh !important; height: 100dvh !important;\\n           outline: none; touch-action: none; }\\n  #msg { position: fixed; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\\n         font: 18px system-ui, sans-serif; color: #3b2a4a; text-align: center; padding: 24px; pointer-events: none; }\\n  #need { display: none; position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 6; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\\n80→          flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; background: rgba(244, 231, 212, 0.92); color: #3b2a4a;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Write engine/web/index.html with session.js pasted byte for byte and about-data filled.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json\\nimport pathlib\\n\\nDEV = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nWORK = DEV.parent\\nSESSION = (DEV / \\\"hub\\\" / \\\"session.js\\\").read_bytes()\\n10→INTERVIEW = json.loads((WORK / \\\"exit-interview.json\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"))\\nABOUT = json.dumps(INTERVIEW, ensure_ascii=False).replace(\\\"<\\\", \\\"\\\\\\\\u003c\\\")\\n\\nIIFE = r\\\"\\\"\\\"(() => {\\n  const boot = window.__gameBoot = { scene: null, seed: null, today: Math.floor(Date.now() / 86400000),\\n                                     about: document.getElementById('about-data')?.textContent ?? '' };\\n  if (!window.AIHub || !AIHub.active) return;\\n  const hub = window.__hub = { go: false, ended: false, players: [], me: 0, ghosts: {} };\\n  boot.scene = 'fit/medley';\\n  boot.seed = Number((/[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(location.search) || [])[1] || 1);\\n20→  AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\\n    if (!info) { location.replace(location.pathname); return; }   // no hub after all\\n    if (!navigator.gpu) { AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU'); return; }\\n    hub.me = info.me; hub.players = info.players;\\n    // Before the first status arrives, report a zero: the hub must always hear a number.\\n    const status = () => { try { return JSON.parse(window.__gameStatus || 'null')?.hub ?? null; } catch { return null; } };\\n    const waitReady = () => (window.__gameStatus ? AIHub.ready() : setTimeout(waitReady, 50));\\n    waitReady();\\n    let reported = false;\\n    const report = () => { if (reported) return; reported = true; const s = status(); AIHub.result({ score: s?.score ?? 0, stats: s?.stats ?? {} }); };\\n30→    setInterval(() => {\\n      if (AIHub.time() < 0 || hub.ended) return;\\n      hub.go = true;\\n      const s = status();\\n      AIHub.progress({ score: s?.score ?? 0, label: s?.label ?? 'Warming up' });\\n      if (!reported) AIHub.send(s?.ghost ?? { area: -1 }, { reliable: false });\\n      if (s?.done) report();\\n    }, 100);\\n    AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => { hub.ghosts[from] = data; });\\n    AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { delete hub.ghosts[id]; });\\n40→    AIHub.on('time-up', report);\\n    AIHub.on('end', () => { hub.ended = true; });\\n  });\\n})();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nPAGE = \\\"\\\"\\\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n50→<script>\\\"\\\"\\\" + SESSION.decode(\\\"utf-8\\\") + \\\"\\\"\\\"</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Highest total across three balance events wins\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n<script id=\\\"about-data\\\" type=\\\"application/json\\\">\\\"\\\"\\\" + ABOUT + \\\"\\\"\\\"</script>\\n<script>\\n60→\\\"\\\"\\\" + IIFE + \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\\\">\\n<title>Wobble Minutes — Five days, one mat</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"Lean through a week of balance games at Tippy Cay, a pastel resort staffed by talking gym gear.\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"theme-color\\\" content=\\\"#f4e7d4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"mobile-web-app-capable\\\" content=\\\"yes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\\\" content=\\\"yes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\\\" content=\\\"black-translucent\\\">\\n<link rel=\\\"manifest\\\" href=\\\"manifest.webmanifest\\\">\\n70→<link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='14' fill='%23f4e7d4'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='4' fill='%233b2a4a'/%3E%3C/svg%3E\\\">\\n<style>\\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #f4e7d4; overscroll-behavior: none;\\n               touch-action: none; -webkit-user-select: none; user-select: none; -webkit-touch-callout: none;\\n               -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; }\\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100vw !important; height: 100vh !important; height: 100dvh !important;\\n           outline: none; touch-action: none; }\\n  #msg { position: fixed; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\\n         font: 18px system-ui, sans-serif; color: #3b2a4a; text-align: center; padding: 24px; pointer-events: none; }\\n  #need { display: none; position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 6; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\\n80→          flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; background: rgba(244, 231, 212, 0.92); color: #3b2a4a;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/tools/write_index.py\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Write engine/web/index.html with session.js pasted byte for byte and about-data filled.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json\\nimport pathlib\\n\\nDEV = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nWORK = DEV.parent\\nSESSION = (DEV / \\\"hub\\\" / \\\"session.js\\\").read_bytes()\\nINTERVIEW = json.loads((WORK / \\\"exit-interview.json\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"))\\nABOUT = json.dumps(INTERVIEW, ensure_ascii=False).replace(\\\"<\\\", \\\"\\\\\\\\u003c\\\")\\n\\nIIFE = r\\\"\\\"\\\"(() => {\\n  const boot = window.__gameBoot = { scene: null, seed: null, today: Math.floor(Date.now() / 86400000),\\n                                     about: document.getElementById('about-data')?.textContent ?? '' };\\n  if (!window.AIHub || !AIHub.active) return;\\n  const hub = window.__hub = { go: false, ended: false, players: [], me: 0, ghosts: {} };\\n  boot.scene = 'fit/medley';\\n  boot.seed = Number((/[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(location.search) || [])[1] || 1);\\n  AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\\n    if (!info) { location.replace(location.pathname); return; }   // no hub after all\\n    if (!navigator.gpu) { AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU'); return; }\\n    hub.me = info.me; hub.players = info.players;\\n    // Before the first status arrives, report a zero: the hub must always hear a number.\\n    const status = () => { try { return JSON.parse(window.__gameStatus || 'null')?.hub ?? null; } catch { return null; } };\\n    const waitReady = () => (window.__gameStatus ? AIHub.ready() : setTimeout(waitReady, 50));\\n    waitReady();\\n    let reported = false;\\n    const report = () => { if (reported) return; reported = true; const s = status(); AIHub.result({ score: s?.score ?? 0, stats: s?.stats ?? {} }); };\\n    setInterval(() => {\\n      if (AIHub.time() < 0 || hub.ended) return;\\n      hub.go = true;\\n      const s = status();\\n      AIHub.progress({ score: s?.score ?? 0, label: s?.label ?? 'Warming up' });\\n      if (!reported) AIHub.send(s?.ghost ?? { area: -1 }, { reliable: false });\\n      if (s?.done) report();\\n    }, 100);\\n    AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => { hub.ghosts[from] = data; });\\n    AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { delete hub.ghosts[id]; });\\n    AIHub.on('time-up', report);\\n    AIHub.on('end', () => { hub.ended = true; });\\n  });\\n})();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nPAGE = \\\"\\\"\\\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>\\\"\\\"\\\" + SESSION.decode(\\\"utf-8\\\") + \\\"\\\"\\\"</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Highest total across three balance events wins\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n<script id=\\\"about-data\\\" type=\\\"application/json\\\">\\\"\\\"\\\" + ABOUT + \\\"\\\"\\\"</script>\\n<script>\\n\\\"\\\"\\\" + IIFE + \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\\\">\\n<title>Wobble Minutes — Five days, one mat</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"Lean through a week of balance games at Tippy Cay, a pastel resort staffed by talking gym gear.\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"theme-color\\\" content=\\\"#f4e7d4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"mobile-web-app-capable\\\" content=\\\"yes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\\\" content=\\\"yes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\\\" content=\\\"black-translucent\\\">\\n<link rel=\\\"manifest\\\" href=\\\"manifest.webmanifest\\\">\\n<link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='14' fill='%23f4e7d4'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='4' fill='%233b2a4a'/%3E%3C/svg%3E\\\">\\n<style>\\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #f4e7d4; overscroll-behavior: none;\\n               touch-action: none; -webkit-user-select: none; user-select: none; -webkit-touch-callout: none;\\n               -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; }\\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100vw !important; height: 100vh !important; height: 100dvh !important;\\n           outline: none; touch-action: none; }\\n  #msg { position: fixed; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\\n         font: 18px system-ui, sans-serif; color: #3b2a4a; text-align: center; padding: 24px; pointer-events: none; }\\n  #need { display: none; position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 6; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\\n          flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; background: rgba(244, 231, 212, 0.92); color: #3b2a4a;\\n\",\"total_lines\":138}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f50bc712-f936-41ae-a9a9-b6fd2dd3675f-6","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"60→    <section><h2>Round</h2><div id=\\\"round\\\" class=\\\"hint\\\">No round yet.</div></section>\\n    <section id=\\\"checks\\\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\\\"checklist\\\"><li class=\\\"hint\\\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\\n    <pre id=\\\"log\\\" aria-live=\\\"off\\\"></pre>\\n  </aside>\\n</main>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\nimport { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\\nimport { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\\n\\nconst NAMES = ['Red Fox', 'Blue Otter', 'Green Heron', 'Gold Lynx'];\\n70→const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\\nconst auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\\nconst scenario = params.get('scenario') || 'standard';\\n/** ?scenario=server: the shared world runs on one more copy with no player of its own, as a dedicated server would run it. */\\nconst serverMode = scenario === 'server';\\nconst playMs = Number(params.get('play')) || 6000;\\nconst SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\\n\\nfor (const [id, key] of [['game', 'game'], ['players', 'players'], ['latency', 'latency'], ['jitter', 'jitter'], ['loss', 'loss']]) {\\n80→  if (params.has(key)) $(id).value = params.get(key);\\n}\\n\\nconst net = createLocalNetwork({});\\nlet current = null;\\nlet roundNo = 0;\\nconst logLines = [];\\nfunction log(text) {\\n  const t = (performance.now() / 1000).toFixed(2).padStart(7);\\n  logLines.push(`${t}  ${text}`);\\n90→  if (logLines.length > 400) logLines.splice(0, logLines.length - 400);\\n  $('log').textContent = logLines.join('\\\\n');\\n  $('log').scrollTop = $('log').scrollHeight;\\n}\\n\\n/** The game's head metas, when the page can be fetched from here. */\\nasync function metasOf(url) {\\n  try {\\n    const html = await (await fetch(url)).text();\\n    const doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html');\\n100→    const meta = (name) => doc.querySelector(`meta[name=\\\"${name}\\\"]`)?.getAttribute('content')?.trim() ?? null;\\n    return {\\n      session: meta('hub:session'),\\n      players: meta('hub:session-players'),\\n      mode: meta('hub:session-mode'),\\n      minutes: meta('hub:session-minutes'),\\n    };\\n  } catch {\\n    return null;\\n  }\",\"content_concise\":\"60→    <section><h2>Round</h2><div id=\\\"round\\\" class=\\\"hint\\\">No round yet.</div></section>\\n    <section id=\\\"checks\\\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\\\"checklist\\\"><li class=\\\"hint\\\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\\n    <pre id=\\\"log\\\" aria-live=\\\"off\\\"></pre>\\n  </aside>\\n</main>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\nimport { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\\nimport { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\\n\\nconst NAMES = ['Red Fox', 'Blue Otter', 'Green Heron', 'Gold Lynx'];\\n70→const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\\nconst auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\\nconst scenario = params.get('scenario') || 'standard';\\n/** ?scenario=server: the shared world runs on one more copy with no player of its own, as a dedicated server would run it. */\\nconst serverMode = scenario === 'server';\\nconst playMs = Number(params.get('play')) || 6000;\\nconst SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\\n\\nfor (const [id, key] of [['game', 'game'], ['players', 'players'], ['latency', 'latency'], ['jitter', 'jitter'], ['loss', 'loss']]) {\\n80→  if (params.has(key)) $(id).value = params.get(key);\\n}\\n\\nconst net = createLocalNetwork({});\\nlet current = null;\\nlet roundNo = 0;\\nconst logLines = [];\\nfunction log(text) {\\n  const t = (performance.now() / 1000).toFixed(2).padStart(7);\\n  logLines.push(`${t}  ${text}`);\\n90→  if (logLines.length > 400) logLines.splice(0, logLines.length - 400);\\n  $('log').textContent = logLines.join('\\\\n');\\n  $('log').scrollTop = $('log').scrollHeight;\\n}\\n\\n/** The game's head metas, when the page can be fetched from here. */\\nasync function metasOf(url) {\\n  try {\\n    const html = await (await fetch(url)).text();\\n    const doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html');\\n100→    const meta = (name) => doc.querySelector(`meta[name=\\\"${name}\\\"]`)?.getAttribute('content')?.trim() ?? null;\\n    return {\\n      session: meta('hub:session'),\\n      players: meta('hub:session-players'),\\n      mode: meta('hub:session-mode'),\\n      minutes: meta('hub:session-minutes'),\\n    };\\n  } catch {\\n    return null;\\n  }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/hub/harness.html\",\"offset\":60,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"    <section><h2>Round</h2><div id=\\\"round\\\" class=\\\"hint\\\">No round yet.</div></section>\\n    <section id=\\\"checks\\\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\\\"checklist\\\"><li class=\\\"hint\\\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\\n    <pre id=\\\"log\\\" aria-live=\\\"off\\\"></pre>\\n  </aside>\\n</main>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\nimport { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\\nimport { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\\n\\nconst NAMES = ['Red Fox', 'Blue Otter', 'Green Heron', 'Gold Lynx'];\\nconst params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\\nconst auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\\nconst scenario = params.get('scenario') || 'standard';\\n/** ?scenario=server: the shared world runs on one more copy with no player of its own, as a dedicated server would run it. */\\nconst serverMode = scenario === 'server';\\nconst playMs = Number(params.get('play')) || 6000;\\nconst SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\\n\\nfor (const [id, key] of [['game', 'game'], ['players', 'players'], ['latency', 'latency'], ['jitter', 'jitter'], ['loss', 'loss']]) {\\n  if (params.has(key)) $(id).value = params.get(key);\\n}\\n\\nconst net = createLocalNetwork({});\\nlet current = null;\\nlet roundNo = 0;\\nconst logLines = [];\\nfunction log(text) {\\n  const t = (performance.now() / 1000).toFixed(2).padStart(7);\\n  logLines.push(`${t}  ${text}`);\\n  if (logLines.length > 400) logLines.splice(0, logLines.length - 400);\\n  $('log').textContent = logLines.join('\\\\n');\\n  $('log').scrollTop = $('log').scrollHeight;\\n}\\n\\n/** The game's head metas, when the page can be fetched from here. */\\nasync function metasOf(url) {\\n  try {\\n    const html = await (await fetch(url)).text();\\n    const doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html');\\n    const meta = (name) => doc.querySelector(`meta[name=\\\"${name}\\\"]`)?.getAttribute('content')?.trim() ?? null;\\n    return {\\n      session: meta('hub:session'),\\n      players: meta('hub:session-players'),\\n      mode: meta('hub:session-mode'),\\n      minutes: meta('hub:session-minutes'),\\n    };\\n  } catch {\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\",\"total_lines\":548}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f50bc712-f936-41ae-a9a9-b6fd2dd3675f-7","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"400→  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\nasync function conformance() {\\n  const checks = [];\\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => {\\n    checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\\n    renderChecks(checks);\\n    return !!pass;\\n410→  };\\n  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\\n  window.__hubCheck = report;\\n  try {\\n    const state = await newRound();\\n    if (!state) {\\n      check('game named', false, 'pass ?game=<path> of a page on this site');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const n = state.n;\\n420→    const m = state.metas;\\n    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\\n    const seats = String(m?.players ?? '').match(/\\\\d+/g)?.map(Number) ?? [];\\n    const [least, most = least] = seats;\\n    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\\n    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\\n\\n    // Every copy: the players, and in a server round the server's copy.\\n    const copies = () => [...(state.status?.players ?? []), ...(state.status?.server ? [state.status.server] : [])];\\n    const helloed = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.hello), TIMINGS.helloMs + 1000);\\n430→    check('every copy says hello', helloed, copies().filter((p) => !p.hello).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\\n    if (!helloed) return;\\n    const caps = state.coordinator.seats().map((s) => s.caps);\\n    check('hello names protocol 1 and the mode', caps.every((c) => c.v === 1 && modeOf(c.mode) === state.coordinator.mode), JSON.stringify(caps[0]));\\n    check('hello seats cover this player count', caps.every((c) => Array.isArray(c.seats) && c.seats[0] <= Math.max(2, n) && c.seats[1] >= n), JSON.stringify(caps[0]?.seats));\\n    if (state.cells.some((c) => !c.frame.contentDocument)) {\\n      check('frames reachable for synthetic input', false, 'serve the game from the same origin as this harness');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n440→    // The card collects ready: every game readies up by itself once loaded, with no prompt and no key.\\n    const loaded = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.ready), 20_000);\\n    check('ready without a key press (the card asks the players)', loaded, copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\\n    // A game that shows its own card takes the players' answers on it: Enter is Ready.\\n    if (caps.some((c) => c?.card)) {\\n      const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server);\\n      const sent = await until(() => players.every((c) => c.cardSent), 2000);\\n      for (const cell of players) poke(cell, 'Enter');\\n      const answered = await until(() => players.every((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)), 3000);\\n      check('its own card: Enter answers Ready', sent && answered, players.filter((c) => !state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => `${c.key}${c.cardSent ? '' : ' (no card yet)'}`).join(', '));\\n450→    }\\n    releaseRound(state);\\n    const started = await until(() => state.status?.phase !== 'loading', 15_000);\\n    check('the round starts when the card ends', started && copies().every((p) => p.ready), copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', ') || state.status?.phase);\\n    if (!started || state.record) return;\\n\\n    await until(() => state.status.phase === 'playing' || state.record, TIMINGS.countdownMs + 2000);\\n    const arrows = ['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'a', 'd', 'w', 's'];\\n    const randomly = async (ms) => {\\n      const end = performance.now() + ms;\\n460→      while (performance.now() < end && !state.record) {\\n        for (const cell of state.cells) if (!cell.gone && !cell.server) poke(cell, arrows[Math.floor(Math.random() * arrows.length)]);\\n        await sleep(150);\\n      }\\n    };\\n    await randomly(Math.min(1500, playMs / 4));\\n\\n    const mode = state.coordinator.mode;\\n    // Parallel and ghost: every copy runs its own world from the same seeded start. A game\\n    // still tagged race was built to race's contract: no seeded start, and no progress asked.\\n470→    const own = SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode);\\n    const legacyRace = own && !seedsRandom(m?.mode);\\n    if (own && !legacyRace) {\\n      const seeded = state.cells.every((c) => c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded === true);\\n      check(`${mode}: Math.random is seeded, the same on every copy`, seeded, state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key}: client ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.version ?? '?'} seeded ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded}`).join('; '));\\n    }\\n\\n    if (scenario === 'host-leave') removeCell(state.cells[0]);\\n    else if (n >= 3) removeCell(state.cells[n - 1]);\\n    await randomly(playMs / 2);\\n480→    const remaining = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.gone);\\n    if (own) {\\n      if (mode === 'parallel') {\\n        check('parallel: no game traffic', state.cells.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent === 0),\\n          state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent}`).join(' '));\\n      } else {\\n        check('ghost: every copy sends its player', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0) || n === 1,\\n          remaining.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent}`).join(' '));\\n      }\\n      if (!legacyRace) check(`${mode}: every copy reports its progress`, remaining.every((c) => c.progress.length > 0 || state.status?.players.find((p) => p.key === c.key)?.result),\\n490→        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key}: ${c.progress.length} report${c.progress.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}`).join(', '));\\n    } else {\\n      check('game traffic flows both ways', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0 && c.bridge.stats.received > 0) || n === 1,\\n        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent} ↓${c.bridge.stats.received}`).join(' '));\\n    }\\n\\n    if (!state.record) state.coordinator.timeUp();\\n    const ended = await until(() => state.record, TIMINGS.graceMs + 2000);\\n    const record = state.record;\\n    if (serverMode) {\\n500→      // The world ran on the server: the players heard it, and only the host may finish a shared world.\\n      const serverCell = state.cells.find((c) => c.server);\\n      check('a copy with no player of its own runs the world (as a server would)', ended && record.status === 'played' && record.hostId === serverCell.bridge.me && serverCell.bridge.stats.sent > 0,\\n        r