eflect::set(&win, &JsValue::from_str(\\\"__gameStatus\\\"), &JsValue::from_str(&status)).ok();\"},{\"line_number\":545,\"content\":\"- `egui::Context::set_fonts` takes effect next pass; using a font family in the same pass panics \\\"not bound to any fonts\\\". Install fonts before the first `run_ui`, in `App::new` and in `Headless::frame`, which makes a new context per frame. In the browser that panic stopped the frame loop with nothing on the page to say so: `__gameStatus` simply stopped changing (verified). Log console errors and assert that the tick advances in every browser test.\"},{\"line_number\":574,\"content\":\"**`browser` (Playwright, one browser, 320x180, `file://`):** boots with no errors; `__gameStatus` appears; the pad stub moves focus and confirms; keyboard does the same; mouse hover moves focus and click activates, using rects the UI publishes in `window.__gameUi`; prompts switch with the device; Settings has the Xbox option; attract starts after 10 s and any input exits it; music reaches about 10% by the sound patch. Touch: Chromium with a phone and a tablet profile (it has WebGPU) must show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", run attract, and respond to a Settings tap by `page.touchscreen.tap`. WebKit with an iPhone profile, which has no WebGPU here, must show the fallback message from section 11.\"},{\"line_number\":587,\"content\":\"2. **Seams.** Hide the chrome, fit input layout, `lean`, fonts, `fit_ui` with a Title and a Pause, Flow state machine, `weblink`, `__gameStatus`, save, a one-event Medley stub, hub JS. Get the harness and the browser smoke green now, before content exists.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-02343bb3-c2b5-4944-8eaf-8df421a6c11d-16","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,1