9,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/scripts/build-web.sh\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":8,\"content\":\"#        cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version <the wasm-bindgen version in Cargo.lock>\"},{\"line_number\":32,\"content\":\"cargo build --locked --profile dist --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p pav_app\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"f41b8ec9-3f7b-4750-9e27-006c24dfbc2f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_679","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Splash is on info. AIHub will also be used.\n\nSplash is set globally before resolve as a safeguard. The HTML change won't force a full Rust recompile, so the build should be fast if the target is warm. I'll check for any running cargo processes first. I also need to review Deviations and confirm whether to add them to the goal plan.\n\nThe plan is at goal/plan.md. Deviations must be real divergences only, and the ## Deviations section does not exist yet. The prior \"confirm before editing\" note was internal to the previous agent, not a user instruction. The goal forbids follow-up questions.\n\nThe goal plan's implementation approach says to record spec gaps in dev notes. The ## Deviations section does not exist yet. I will wait until a real divergence appears before adding it.\n\nI'll read STAGE.md, TASK.md, and notes/decisions.md to locate the deviations section. I'll also check PROGRESS.md format. I'll apply the IIFE fix and start the build now. While it compiles, I'll prepare PROGRESS and deviations notes. I won't mark checkboxes until the hub is green and the target is deleted last. I'll check if a deviations notes file already exists.\n\nI'll check for running cargo processes with `ps` before starting the build. I won't kill them.\n\nThe IIFE fix will be minimal. It sets hub.me and hub.players from info, calls AIHub.ready() when info.splash is true, and ensures the hub receives a zero status before the first real update.\n\nThe IIFE fix is a real divergence from the exact block. It polls `window.__gameStatus` every 50 ms and calls `AIHub.ready()` once the value is present. If the GPU never reports status, this loop runs forever, matching the original behavior.\n\nThe 50 ms poll is wasteful but acceptable. I will check build-web.sh for offline flags and review the lockfile before editing. I will update todos and draft PROGRESS.md from current files while the build runs.\n\nI will check notes/decisions.md for deviation style and TASK.md for hand-in requirements. I will read PROGRESS.md and TASK.md in parallel with the edit. The hub retry's server and Chromium browser should already be dead. The 4-player hub test is heavy, so I will run the full hub suite after the build.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-faf8fd1f-3e9d-44c9-91dd-230b40b4e08e-30","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/hub/harness.html","offset":510,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-faf8fd1f-3e9d-44c9-91dd-230b40b4e08e-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/PROGRESS.md","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-faf8fd1f-3e9d-44c9-91dd-230b40b4e08e-32","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"cargo","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/scripts/build-web.sh"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1667,"output_tokens":1349,"cache_read_input_tokens":59008,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"7f9379b7-6f62-46be-bf1f-acbb0661c1b6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-faf8fd1f-3e9d-44c9-91dd-230b40b4e08e-30","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"510→    await sleep(300);\\n    check('every remaining copy is told the round ended', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.ended), remaining.filter((c) => !c.bridge.ended).map((c) => c.key).join(', '));\\n    const issues = [...(state.status?.issues ?? []), ...state.cells.flatMap((c) => c.bridge.issues)];\\n    check('no protocol problems', issues.length === 0, issues.map((i) => `${i.key}: ${i.problem}`).join('; '));\\n    const violations = state.cells.flatMap((c) => {\\n      let extra = [];\\n      try {\\n        extra = c.frame.contentWindow?.__hubViolations ?? [];\\n      } catch {}\\n      return [...c.violations, ...extra].map((v) => `${c.key}: ${v}`);\\n520→    });\\n    check('no errors, dialogs, popups or sockets', violations.length === 0, violations.slice(0, 6).join('; '));\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    check('harness ran', false, String(error?.stack || error));\\n  } finally {\\n    report.pass = checks.length > 0 && checks.every((c) => c.pass);\\n    report.done = true;\\n    document.body.dataset.complete = 'true';\\n    log(`conformance: ${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}`);\\n  }\\n530→}\\n\\nfunction renderChecks(checks) {\\n  $('checklist').replaceChildren(\\n    ...checks.map((c) => {\\n      const li = document.createElement('li');\\n      li.className = c.pass ? 'ok' : 'bad';\\n      li.textContent = c.name + (c.detail && !c.pass ? ` — ${c.detail}` : '');\\n      li.title = c.detail;\\n      return li;\\n540→    }),\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nif (auto) conformance();\\nelse if ($('game').value) newRound();\\n</script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"510→    await sleep(300);\\n    check('every remaining copy is told the round ended', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.ended), remaining.filter((c) => !c.bridge.ended).map((c) => c.key).join(', '));\\n    const issues = [...(state.status?.issues ?? []), ...state.cells.flatMap((c) => c.bridge.issues)];\\n    check('no protocol problems', issues.length === 0, issues.map((i) => `${i.key}: ${i.problem}`).join('; '));\\n    const violations = state.cells.flatMap((c) => {\\n      let extra = [];\\n      try {\\n        extra = c.frame.contentWindow?.__hubViolations ?? [];\\n      } catch {}\\n      return [...c.violations, ...extra].map((v) => `${c.key}: ${v}`);\\n520→    });\\n    check('no errors, dialogs, popups or sockets', violations.length === 0, violations.slice(0, 6).join('; '));\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    check('harness ran', false, String(error?.stack || error));\\n  } finally {\\n    report.pass = checks.length > 0 && checks.every((c) => c.pass);\\n    report.done = true;\\n    document.body.dataset.complete = 'true';\\n    log(`conformance: ${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}`);\\n  }\\n530→}\\n\\nfunction renderChecks(checks) {\\n  $('checklist').replaceChildren(\\n    ...checks.map((c) => {\\n      const li = document.createElement('li');\\n      li.className = c.pass ? 'ok' : 'bad';\\n      li.textContent = c.name + (c.detail && !c.pass ? ` — ${c.detail}` : '');\\n      li.title = c.detail;\\n      return li;\\n540→    }),\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nif (auto) conformance();\\nelse if ($('game').value) newRound();\\n</script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/hub/harness.html\",\"offset\":510,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"    await sleep(300);\\n    check('every remaining copy is told the round ended', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.ended), remaining.filter((c) => !c.bridge.ended).map((c) => c.key).join(', '));\\n    const issues = [...(state.status?.issues ?? []), ...state.cells.flatMap((c) => c.bridge.issues)];\\n    check('no protocol problems', issues.length === 0, issues.map((i) => `${i.key}: ${i.problem}`).join('; '));\\n   