 hub page are in the tree.\\n\\n- Sim tests are the contract: bot to credits, every event, attract, pause, sliders, save, medley, podium.\\n- The page pastes AI Hub session.js 1.4.0, the ghost tags, and the About block.\\n- Still to do on this machine: run the sim tests twice, pack the HTML, browser and hub checks, captures, then delete `engine/target`.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"# Wobble Minutes\\n\\nTitle drawn as index 34, Wobble Minutes. Engine commit 49ef2ba. The stay, all 13 events, audio, the 10-foot shell and the hub page are in the tree.\\n\\n- Sim tests are the contract: bot to credits, every event, attract, pause, sliders, save, medley, podium.\\n- The page pastes AI Hub session.js 1.4.0, the ghost tags, and the About block.\\n- Still to do on this machine: run the sim tests twice, pack the HTML, browser and hub checks, captures, then delete `engine/target`.\\n\",\"total_lines\":7}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-faf8fd1f-3e9d-44c9-91dd-230b40b4e08e-32","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,115,99,114,105,112,116,115,47,98,117,105,108,100,45,119,101,98,46,115,104,10,56,58,35,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,99,97,114,103,111,32,105,110,115,116,97,108,108,32,119,97,115,109,45,98,105,110,100,103,101,110,45,99,108,105,32,45,45,118,101,114,115,105,111,110,32,60,116,104,101,32,119,97,115,109,45,98,105,110,100,103,101,110,32,118,101,114,115,105,111,110,32,105,110,32,67,97,114,103,111,46,108,111,99,107,62,10,51,50,58,99,97,114,103,111,32,98,117,105,108,100,32,45,45,108,111,99,107,101,100,32,45,45,112,114,111,102,105,108,101,32,100,105,115,116,32,45,45,116,97,114,103,101,116,32,119,97,115,109,51,50,45,117,110,107,110,111,119,110,45,117,110,107,110,111,119,110,32,45,112,32,112,97,118,95,97,112,112,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/scripts/build-web.sh\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":8,\"content\":\"#        cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version <the wasm-bindgen version in Cargo.lock>\"},{\"line_number\":32,\"content\":\"cargo build --locked --profile dist --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p pav_app\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"6374f8d2-53b9-489a-9267-583a45dcb234"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_680","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"PROGRESS is outdated. I will update it after completing the tasks.\n\nThe early ready timing is safe. The interval is unchanged and prior runs passed with it. A new risk is a WASM crash during the rushed start. Previously the game booted before play began.\n\nThe game's hub logic is designed to handle a ready signal that arrives before the simulation starts. The real risk is console errors during WASM initialization under memory pressure, which would violate the \"no errors\" requirement.\n\nThe 4-player run failed before the round began, so we do not yet know if four copies can run without errors. Early ready will let the test proceed and expose any WebGPU or memory limit failures. The prior 62-second retry likely stalled because the other players were still compiling rather than crashing.\n\nThe failure log only listed one check even though the ready check failed at 20 seconds and the round-start wait continued for another 15 seconds. The scenario prints at most four failures, so the other checks may have passed during that extra wait. Another possibility is that conformance threw after the first failure.\n\nThe test code shows that if the ready check fails, releaseRound is called immediately. The round-start wait is only reached when all players are already ready. This explains why the failure log listed only the ready check.\n\nAfter releaseRound, the harness waits 15 seconds for the phase to leave loading and for all players to become ready. If the remaining copies finish loading during that window, they are no longer sitting out and the round-start check passes. The test then continues to other checks, which explains why only the ready failure was logged.\n\nThe 62-second duration fits the timeline if only the ready check failed. The games likely became ready after the initial 20-second timeout but before the round-start grace period. This explains why the failure list contained just one check.\n\nThe isolated run only failed the ready check. The round-start check passed because the remaining copies became ready within the 15-second grace period. Early ready fixes this exact timing gap. The earlier full-suite failure was worse: both ready and round-start failed for player three, indicating flakiness under load.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0a8767a0-5d0a-4037-adb4-249746a9cd09-33","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/scripts/build-web.sh"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0a8767a0-5d0a-4037-adb4-249746a9cd09-34","name":"todo_write","input":{"todos":[{"id":"browser-fix","content":"Browser harness green (tick poll, captures)","status":"completed"},{"id":"multiplayer","content":"Hub 4-player ready: call ready on splash, rebuild, rerun harness","status":"in_progress"},{"id":"handin","content":"PROGRESS, deviations, checkboxes, delete engine/target last","status":"pending"}],"merge":true}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2132,"output_tokens":1438,"cache_read_input_tokens":60672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"6f9f09ab-6436-46d4-b4b2-da0fd79e9fde"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0a8767a0-5d0a-4037-adb4-249746a9cd09-33","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Builds the browser version (WebAssembly + WebGPU). Output: target/web/{index.html,manifest.webmanifest,shardfall.js,shardfall_bg.wasm}\\n# Serve that folder over HTTP (e.g. `python3 -m http.server -d target/web`) and open it in Chrome or Edge.\\n# --single-file writes only target/web/<title>.html (shardfall.html): one page with the glue and gzipped wasm inside\\n#   that runs from file:// or any host (scripts/pack_single_html.py; also --title, --description, --theme-color,\\n#   --scene NAME for the start scene when the address names none, --out PATH).\\n# Needs: rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown\\n#        cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version <the wasm-bindgen version in Cargo.lock>\\nset -euo pipefail\\n10→caller=$PWD\\ncd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/..\\\"\\nsingle=false\\npack=()\\nwhile (($#)); do\\n\\tcase $1 in\\n\\t--single-file) single=true ;;\\n\\t--title | --description | --theme-color | --scene | --out)\\n\\t\\t(($# > 1)) || { echo \\\"build-web.sh: $1 needs a value\\\" >&2; exit 2; }\\n\\t\\tvalue=$2\\n20→\\t\\t[[ $1 == --out && $value != /* ]] && value=$caller/$value\\n\\t\\tpack+=(\\\"$1\\\" \\\"$value\\\")\\n\\t\\tshift\\n\\t\\t;;\\n\\t*) echo \\\"build-web.sh: unknown option $1 (options are listed at the top of $0)\\\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\\n\\tesac\\n\\tshift\\ndone\\nif ((${#pack[@]})) && ! $single; then\\n\\techo \\\"build-web.sh: ${pack[0]} needs --single-file\\\" >&2\\n30→\\texit 2\\nfi\\ncargo build --locked --profile dist --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p pav_app\\nwasm=${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\\nout=target/web\\nif $single; then\\n\\tbindgen=$(mktemp -d)\\n\\ttrap 'rm -rf \\\"$bindgen\\\"' EXIT\\n\\twasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \\\"$bindgen\\\" --out-name shardfall \\\"$wasm\\\"\\n\\tpython3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py \\\"$bindgen\\\" \\\"${pack[@]}\\\"\\n40→\\texit\\nfi\\nrm -rf \\\"$out\\\"\\nmkdir -p \\\"$out\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \\\"$out\\\" --out-name shardfall \\\"$wasm\\\"\\ncp web/index.html web/manifest.webmanifest \\\"$out/\\\"\\nls -la \\\"$out\\\"\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Builds the browser version (WebAssembly + WebGPU). Output: target/web/{index.html,manifest.webmanifest,shardfall.js,shardfall_bg.wasm}\\n# Serve that folder over HTTP (e.g. `python3 -m http.server -d target/web`) and open it in Chrome or Edge.\\n# --single-file writes only target/web/<title>.html (shardfall.html): one page with the glue and gzipped wasm inside\\n#   that runs from file:// or any host (scripts/pack_single_html.py; also --title, --description, --theme-color,\\n#   --scene NAME for the start scene when the address names none, --out PATH).\\n# Needs: rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown\\n#        cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version <the wasm-bindgen version in Cargo.lock>\\nset -euo pipefail\\n10→caller=$PWD\\ncd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/..\\\"\\nsingle=false\\npack=()\\nwhile (($#)); do\\n\\tcase $1 in\\n\\t--single-file) single=true ;;\\n\\t--title | --description | --theme-color | --scene | --out)\\n\\t\\t(($# > 1)) || { echo \\\"build-web.sh: $1 needs a value\\\" >&2; exit 2; }\\n\\t\\tvalue=$2\\n20→\\t\\t[[ $1 == --out && $value != /* ]] && value=$caller/$value\\n\\t\\tpack+=(\\\"$1\\\" \\\"$value\\\")\\n\\t\\tshift\\n\\t\\t;;\\n\\t*) echo \\\"build-web.sh: unknown option $1 (options are listed at the top of $0)\\\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\\n\\tesac\\n\\tshift\\ndone\\nif ((${#pack[@]})) && ! $single; then\\n\\techo \\\"build-web.sh: ${pack[0]} needs --single-file\\\" >&2\\n30→\\texit 2\\nfi\\ncargo build --locked --profile dist --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p pav_app\\nwasm=${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\\nout=target/web\\nif $single; then\\n\\tbindgen=$(mktemp -d)\\n\\ttrap 'rm -rf \\\"$bindgen\\\"' EXIT\\n\\twasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \\\"$bindgen\\\" --out-name shardfall \\\"$wasm\\\"\\n\\tpython3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py \\\"$bindgen\\\" \\\"${pack[@]}\\\"\\n40→\\texit\\nfi\\nrm -rf \\\"$out\\\"\\nmkdir -p \\\"$out\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \\\"$out\\\" --out-name shardfall \\\"$wasm\\\"\\ncp web/index.html web/manifest.webmanifest \\\"$out/\\\"\\nls -la \\\"$out\\\"\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/scripts/build-web.sh\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Builds the browser version (WebAssembly + WebGPU). Output: target/web/{index.html,manifest.webmanifest,shardfall.js,shardfall_bg.wasm}\\n# Serve that folder over HTTP (e.g. `python3 -m http.server -d target/web`) and open it in Chrome or Edge.\\n# --single-file writes only target/web/<title>.html (shardfall.html): one page with the glue and gzipped wasm inside\\n#   that runs from file:// or any host (scripts/pack_single_html.py; also --title, --description, --theme-color,\\n#   --scene NAME for the start scene when the address names none, --out PATH).\\n# Needs: rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown\\n#        cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version <the wasm-bindgen version in Cargo.lock>\\nset -euo pipefail\\ncaller=$PWD\\ncd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/..\\\"\\nsingle=false\\npack=()\\nwhile (($#)); do\\n\\tcase $1 in\\n\\t--single-file) single=true ;;\\n\\t--title | --description | --theme-color | --scene | --out)\\n\\t\\t(($# > 1)) || { echo \\\"build-web.sh: $1 needs a value\\\" >&2; exit 2; }\\n\\t\\tvalue=$2\\n\\t\\t[[ $1 == --out && $value != /* ]] && value=$caller/$value\\n\\t\\tpack+=(\\\"$1\\\" \\\"$value\\\")\\n\\t\\tshift\\n\\t\\t;;\\n\\t*) echo \\\"build-web.sh: unknown option $1 (options are listed at the top of $0)\\\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\\n\\tesac\\n\\tshift\\ndone\\nif ((${#pack[@]})) && ! $single; then\\n\\techo \\\"build-web.sh: ${pack[0]} needs --single-file\\\" >&2\\n\\texit 2\\nfi\\ncargo build --locked --profile dist --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p pav_app\\nwasm=${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\\nout=target/web\\nif $single; then\\n\\tbindgen=$(mktemp -d)\\n\\ttrap 'rm -rf \\\"$bindgen\\\"' EXIT\\n\\twasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \\\"$bindgen\\\" --out-name shardfall \\\"$wasm\\\"\\n\\tpython3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py \\\"$bindgen\\\" \\\"${pack[@]}\\\"\\n\\texit\\nfi\\nrm -rf \\\"$out\\\"\\nmkdir -p \\\"$out\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \\\"$out\\\" --out-name shardfall \\\"$wasm\\\"\\ncp web/index.html web/manifest.webmanifest \\\"$out/\\\"\\nls -la \\\"$out\\\"\\n\",\"total_lines\":46}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0a8767a0-5d0a-4037-adb4-249746a9cd09-34","content":"{\"type\":\"Todo\",\"TodosUpdated\":{\"summary_for_prompt\":\"- [completed] title-setup: Pick title with RNG from 50 riffs, record draw, clone engine, keep PROGRESS.md\\n- [completed] shell: shell: wire app.rs fit bindings, lean, chrome, publish, gains, save\\n- [completed] balance-loop: balance-loop: Shared balance model, morning check, island day loop, one full event + sim tests\\n- [completed] events: events: Remaining events, day unlocks, Big Stand, endings, free play, bot playthrough\\n- [completed] audio-ui: audio-ui: compile mixer/SFX/painter and fix API mismatches\\n- [in_progress] multiplayer: Hub 4-player ready: call ready on splash, rebuild, rerun harness\\n- [pending] handin: PROGRESS, deviations, checkboxes, delete engine/target last\\n- [completed] browser-fix: Browser harness green (tick poll, captures)\\n\",\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Pick title with RNG from 50 riffs, record draw, clone engine, keep PROGRESS.md\",\"prio