\"Golden\\\"]\"},{\"line_number\":235,\"content\":\"text = \\\"Four hammocks, four names, one very calm ledger.\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":950,\"content\":\"text = \\\"I named the glasses. You do not need the names. They need you.\\\"\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"6e19e1ba-3a22-4411-ba3a-91d2ae1876e5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_731","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a solid refute. I checked the settings row menu handler. It only handles focus up/down, tab page, back, and confirm. Left and right do not adjust values in pre().\n\nConfirm on the music row hits a dead branch in activate_settings. The test `music_defaults_quiet_and_a_dev_slider_resets` injects Slider events that the real input path never produces. The implementer should wire left/right or drag to emit Slider, or adjust values on confirm, and test through CONFIRM or MENU_LEFT instead of raw UiEvents.\n\nI will also flag free play, long stillness prompt, age adjustment, name cap, missing poses and props, and eyes-closed. Wardrobe and calendar are Back-only stubs that violate the no-stubs rule. Art lacks new props, pose clips, and multiple rooms.\n\nI will split the slider issue into a bug and a gap. The unreachable sliders are a bug. The missing jump, cheats, and time scale are a gap. I will also flag the name menu as a gap. This adversarial review targets only untestable or demonstrably broken features. Criteria 2 and 4 have holes.\n\nHub ghost area comparison is sound. EventId discriminants match the ghost area values.\n\nDirect run after_result returns early when hub_mode or Direct is active. It does not alter flow.\n\nRetry and Back on a direct event result keep the player on Result. This is acceptable for direct scene tests. The player cannot leave the result except by retrying.\n\nThe deviations document shortcuts rather than weakening the acceptance criteria. It does not excuse unmet criteria.\n\nFree play is a confirmed bug. When free_play is true, day_clear returns false and End Day disappears. The schedule then shows only the first four events, so the player can repeat those exercises forever. The plan requires free play to open every event.\n\nThe schedule shows only four events on day five before credits, then four again after free play. Story day four also contains exactly four events.\n\nThe missing pose and props finding cites capture and hub.toml. A search for anim/fit.json found none.\n\nProps are absent from lib/core. The anim directory holds style catalogs and motion data but no fit.json. I will now write the files. The tests-core.log summary is sufficient for verification.\n\nThe outfit list contains eight entries but the menu only displays six. The Golden outfit is hidden from selection even though its flip-flops set a golden flag.\n\nThe eyes-closed check runs during phase two in tick_check. The puck is always set in fit_ui when the flow is Check, and no sound effect plays.\n\nThe long stillness banner appears whenever phase reaches four or higher at events.rs line 1198.\n\nThe age adjustment path never subtracts score or calls balance_age again. The time_scale field is initialized but unused. Slider logic only handles Hover and Click events, and the real input path never emits UiEvent::Slider.\n\nI will present seven findings. The JSON and markdown files will be written carefully with valid escaping. I will include the full writeup in both fields and omit the system prompt. The terminal output must read exactly \"Refuted\". I am also considering a quick Rust spot-check for one logic bug.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The sim tests pass, but several required controls never reach the player. I’ll record those as defects against the shipped code."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a3bedd1-49a4-43a1-8c90-b0186890fa03-80","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/tmp/grok-goal-b3947fd4d9d9/goal-verdict-b3947fd4d9d9-1-0.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": true,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"kind\": \"bug\", \"location\": \"Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:536\", \"detail\": \"Live sliders are unreachable: fit_sample only emits Hover/Click, nothing constructs UiEvent::Slider, and confirming a Music/SFX/dev row is a no-op. Wire pad left/right or a drag through the real input path and assert that path; the sim test injects Slider(300) which a player can never send.\"},\n    {\"kind\": \"gap\", \"location\": \"Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs:618\", \"detail\": \"Dev Mode (opened by pause) has no jump, no cheats, and no time-scale control. time_scale is only initialized to 1.0 and never changed. Criterion 4 requires all three plus the sliders.\"},\n    {\"kind\": \"bug\", \"location\": \"Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs:567\", \"detail\": \"Free-play Schedule does .take(4) and ignores page, and the island has no event mats, so after credits only Breath, Pose, Squat, and Plank can be started. Step Party through Cannonball Cup are unreachable.\"},\n    {\"kind\": \"bug\", \"location\": \"Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs:1198\", \"detail\": \"Big Stand phase 5 forfeits on any press after 15s but never shows the fake Press-to-skip prompt; the event HUD keeps the score and song bed 3 never goes silent. Criterion 2 requires that prompt.\"},\n    {\"kind\": \"bug\", \"location\": \"Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs:757\", \"detail\": \"Big Stand ending uses the morning age only. PLAN.md final age (morning minus score/100, cap 10) is never applied, so a 41–50 morning age cannot check out by rowboat after a good finale.\"},\n    {\"kind\": \"bug\", \"location\": \"Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs:666\", \"detail\": \"Morning-check eyes-closed phase only averages cob distance. It never plays a pitch tone or hides the puck, so it is a second stillness test. Criterion 2 names the eyes-closed tone.\"},\n    {\"kind\": \"gap\", \"location\": \"Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs:560\", \"detail\": \"Name and outfit menus .take(6) and ignore page, so 34 of the 40 script names and the Swim/Golden outfits cannot be selected. TAB changes page but screen_items does not.\"},\n    {\"kind\": \"gap\", \"location\": \"Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/hub.toml:20\", \"detail\": \"No beach/wellness props and no hand-keyed poses. One sand/grass room is every set; apply_body only tilts the idle puppet; anim/fit.json does not exist. Pose Parade capture is a standing figure, not a pose. Wardrobe and Calendar flows are Back-only stubs.\"}\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": \"fit.rs bot/hub/browser logs pass, but input.rs:536 never emits Slider, schedule take(4) at mod.rs:567, and capture-pose-1.png is one bare room.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"See goal-classifier-b3947fd4d9d9-1-skeptic-0.md. Sim, browser, and hub logs are green, and the title capture is readable, but criterion 2 and 4 behaviors are missing or unwired: sliders, dev jump/cheats/time scale, free-play roster, Long Stillness prompt, finale age, eyes-closed tone, name list, props/poses.\"\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a3bedd1-49a4-43a1-8c90-b0186890fa03-81","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/tmp/grok-goal-b3947fd4d9d9/goal-classifier-b3947fd4d9d9-1-skeptic-0.md","content":"# Skeptic verdict: Refuted\n\nSim, browser, and hub logs in the implementer scratch dir do show `27 passed, 0 failed` twice, `6 passed, 0 failed` for the browser, and `6 passed, 0 failed` for the hub. The title capture is a readable Wobble Minutes menu. Those passes do not cover the holes below. The plan diff did not delete acceptance criteria; the recorded deviations do not satisfy them.\n\n## Unwired sliders (criterion 4)\n\n`FitInput::fit_sample` (`engine/crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:536`) only builds `UiEvent::Hover` or `UiEvent::Click`. A repo-wide search finds `UiEvent::Slider` constructed only in `tests/fit.rs`, which injects `Slider(300, 1.0)` straight into `sim.step`. `activate_settings` (`mod.rs:994`) ignores the Music, Effects, Voices, Lean, Wobble, Rhythm, and Text rows (`610`–`616`). Confirm on those rows is `_ => {}`. A player cannot change a live tunable or a settings gain. Reset Feel (`ACT_DEV_RESET`) is a real confirm. The slider test must drive the same buttons or pointer the app actually emits, after that path exists.\n\n## Dev Mode is a slider list, not the required tools\n\nPause sets `flow = Dev` (`mod.rs:1453`). `dev_items` (`mod.rs:618`) is Resume, Reset feel, Wardrobe, Calendar, Settings, About, then parameter labels. There is no jump (day, event, finale phase, attract, medley), no cheats, and no time-scale row. `time_scale` is set to `1.0` at init and never assigned again. Criterion 4 requires jump, cheats, and time scale.\n\n## Free play does not open the roster (criterion 2)\n\n`schedule_events` in free play returns every event except the check and Big Stand (`mod.rs:525`). `screen_items` for Schedule then `.take(4)` (`mod.rs:567`) and does not read `page`. The only room (`hub.toml`) has a player marker and no mats. After credits the schedule can start Breath Bloom, Pose Parade, Tempo Squats, and Plank Standoff only. Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap, Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, and Cannonball Cup are stuck off the menu. `fit/event/<name>` still boots them for tests; that is not the stay.\n\n## Long Stillness has no fake skip (criterion 2)\n\n`tick_big` phase 4 (`events.rs:1198`) sets `forfeit` if `pressed != 0` after 15s and then halves that phase. Nothing puts “Press Cross to skip” (or any skip line) on the HUD. `banner` for `Flow::Event` always shows the score (`mod.rs:1759`). `desired_song` keeps Big Stand on bed 3 (`mod.rs:1235`) and never fades to silence. The temptation prompt the criterion names is absent.\n\n## Finale does not move Balance Age\n\n`finish_play` for Big Stand (`mod.rs:757`) banks the event and picks `rowboat` iff `self.age <= 40`. It never subtracts `final_score / 100` (cap 10) from the morning age. A morning age of 41–50 that the finale should have brought to 40 or under still gets the Extended Stay.\n\n## Eyes-closed check is a second stillness test\n\n`tick_check` phase 2 (`events.rs:666`) only accumulates `cob` length for 6 seconds. No syllable or `Sfx` tracks the offset. `fit_ui` keeps the puck up for the whole check (`mod.rs:1693`). Criterion 2’s eyes-closed tone is not there, so the micro-test is identical to stand-still with the dot visible.\n\n## Name and outfit lists are capped at six\n\n`script.toml` has 40 names and 8 outfits. `Flow::Name` and `Flow::Outfit` both `.take(6)` (`mod.rs:560`, `mod.rs:562`). `page` increments on TAB for every menu, but those screens ignore it. Swim and Golden, and 34 names, cannot be chosen. `script_name_count >= 40` only counts the file.\n\n## One room, no new poses, stub wardrobe and calendar (criterion 4)\n\n`hub.toml` is a single sand/grass deck with a pool. `assets/props/lib/core/` has no palm, mat, kettlebell, raft, or other new beach/wellness props. There is no `engine/anim/fit.json`, and `apply_body` only writes `tilt_side` / `tilt_fwd`. Pose Parade’s capture (`capture-pose-1.png`) is the idle puppet standing in that room with a small puck, not a hand-keyed pose. `Flow::Wardrobe` and `Flow::Calendar` menu items are only Back (`mod.rs:589`), so those pause entries are stubs.\n\nHand-in files that do match the brief: `PROGRESS.md`, parseable `exit-interview.json` with `usage` `added on import` and `aiHub.players` `1–4`, title `Wobble Minutes` on the page and in `aiHub.name`, and the packed HTML beside the dev folder. Those do not clear the play holes above.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1965,"output_tokens":4160,"cache_read_input_tokens":145792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"ec35773f-fe9d-49b0-baa2-49927ae34c92"}
