{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_741","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading the HUD, desired song, body application, and slider test files.\n\nChecking puppet clip playback and hub.toml for props. Drafting a practical plan to close every skeptic item with tests. Slider controls will use pad left/right in settings or dev menus, and mouse drag will emit Slider events.\n\nTests will use MENU_LEFT and MENU_RIGHT instead of injecting Slider events. Slider values will be tracked from settings and nudged by 0.1, with dev parameters converted to 0-1 using ParamKind bounds. The Pause screen must open Dev Mode directly rather than through a separate menu, and it needs to include Resume, Schedule, Calendar, Wardrobe, Settings, How to Play, About, Dev Mode, and Quit to Title.\n\nThe existing Dev Mode page lacks jump, cheats, and time-scale controls. I will expand it into a tabbed layout with Jump, Cheats, Time, Tuning, and Resume pages. The current TAB key already switches between these pages.\n\nA `dev_tab` index will switch between Jump, Cheats, Time, and Tuning pages. The Jump tab will list events starting at 200+i plus Attract, Medley, Finale phases, and Day N. The Cheats tab will include toggles for No tips, Autoplay, Give minutes, Unlock all, and All stars.\n\nThe Cheats tab will also include Skip dialogue, Win event now, and Lose event now. The Time tab will offer 0.25x, 1x, 2x, and 4x speed, plus Pause time and a single-step advance. I need to verify that frozen() and island or event logic actually use dts so the time scale change takes effect. Tests will confirm pausing into Dev Mode, selecting 4x speed, jumping to an event, and checking that give minutes increases day_minutes. I also noticed the free-play schedule currently uses `.take(4)`, which ignores pagination.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-325a1e3d-3534-4fa6-9ac3-79746c15ef4a-103","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file"