{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-580b76c1-6315-4201-bef5-2d5d4bc4e33f-139","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"532→fn bot_big(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    match act.phase {\\n        0 => {\\n            let up = act.guide + 0.02 > act.lungs;\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), if up { buttons::CONFIRM } else { 0 })\\n        }\\n        1 => (pd(bal, rules, ring_center(act.sub)), 0),\\n        2 => bot_step(act),\\n540→        3 => (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), buttons::STEP_L | buttons::STEP_R),\\n        _ => (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), 0),\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn ring_center(t: f32) -> Vec2 {\\n    let a = 0.35;\\n    Vec2::new(a * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 0.12 * t).sin(), a * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 0.09 * t + 1.3).sin())\\n}\\n\\n550→fn squat_guide(t: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let c = (t / 3.2).fract();\\n    if c < 2.0 / 3.2 {\\n        c / (2.0 / 3.2)\\n    } else {\\n        1.0 - (c - 2.0 / 3.2) / (1.2 / 3.2)\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn breath_guide(t: f32) -> f32 {\\n560→    let c = (t / 8.0).fract();\\n    if c < 0.5 { c * 2.0 } else { 1.0 - (c - 0.5) * 2.0 }\\n}\\n\\npub fn tick(act: &mut Activity, bal: &mut BalanceCore, sim: &mut Sim, lean: Vec2, held: u32, pressed: u32, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    if act.done {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let amp = rules.wobble * act.amp_scale * if act.kind == EventId::Plank { 1.0 + act.t / 30.0 } else { 1.0 };\\n    bal.amp = amp;\\n570→    bal.gust = if act.kind == EventId::BigStand && act.phase == 1 {\\n        Vec2::new(rules.big_gust * (act.sub / 20.0) * (act.sub * 1.7).sin(), 0.0)\",\"content_concise\":\"532→fn bot_big(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    match act.phase {\\n        0 => {\\n            let up = act.guide + 0.02 > act.lungs;\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), if up { buttons::CONFIRM } else { 0 })\\n        }\\n        1 => (pd(bal, rules, ring_center(act.sub)), 0),\\n        2 => bot_step(act),\\n540→        3 => (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), buttons::STEP_L | buttons::STEP_R),\\n        _ => (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), 0),\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn ring_center(t: f32) -> Vec2 {\\n    let a = 0.35;\\n    Vec2::new(a * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 0.12 * t).sin(), a * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 0.09 * t + 1.3).sin())\\n}\\n\\n550→fn squat_guide(t: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let c = (t / 3.2).fract();\\n    if c < 2.0 / 3.2 {\\n        c / (2.0 / 3.2)\\n    } else {\\n        1.0 - (c - 2.0 / 3.2) / (1.2 / 3.2)\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn breath_guide(t: f32) -> f32 {\\n560→    let c = (t / 8.0).fract();\\n    if c < 0.5 { c * 2.0 } else { 1.0 - (c - 0.5) * 2.0 }\\n}\\n\\npub fn tick(act: &mut Activity, bal: &mut BalanceCore, sim: &mut Sim, lean: Vec2, held: u32, pressed: u32, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    if act.done {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let amp = rules.wobble * act.amp_scale * if act.kind == EventId::Plank { 1.0 + act.t / 30.0 } else { 1.0 };\\n    bal.amp = amp;\\n570→    bal.gust = if act.kind == EventId::BigStand && act.phase == 1 {\\n        Vec2::new(rules.big_gust * (act.sub / 20.0) * (act.sub * 1.7).sin(), 0.0)\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs\",\"offset\":532,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"fn bot_big(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    match act.phase {\\n        0 => {\\n            let up = act.guide + 0.02 > act.lungs;\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), if up { buttons::CONFIRM } else { 0 })\\n        }\\n        1 => (pd(bal, rules, ring_center(act.sub)), 0),\\n        2 => bot_step(act),\\n        3 => (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), buttons::STEP_L | buttons::STEP_R),\\n        _ => (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), 0),\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn ring_center(t: f32) -> Vec2 {\\n    let a = 0.35;\\n    Vec2::new(a * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 0.12 * t).sin(), a * (std::f32::consts::TAU * 0.09 * t + 1.3).sin())\\n}\\n\\nfn squat_guide(t: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let c = (t / 3.2).fract();\\n    if c < 2.0 / 3.2 {\\n        c / (2.0 / 3.2)\\n    } else {\\n        1.0 - (c - 2.0 / 3.2) / (1.2 / 3.2)\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn breath_guide(t: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let c = (t / 8.0).fract();\\n    if c < 0.5 { c * 2.0 } else { 1.0 - (c - 0.5) * 2.0 }\\n}\\n\\npub fn tick(act: &mut Activity, bal: &mut BalanceCore, sim: &mut Sim, lean: Vec2, held: u32, pressed: u32, dt: f32, rules: &Rules, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    if act.done {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let amp = rules.wobble * act.amp_scale * if act.kind == EventId::Plank { 1.0 + act.t / 30.0 } else { 1.0 };\\n    bal.amp = amp;\\n    bal.gust = if act.kind == EventId::BigStand && act.phase == 1 {\\n        Vec2::new(rules.big_gust * (act.sub / 20.0) * (act.sub * 1.7).sin(), 0.0)\\n\",\"total_lines\":1255}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-580b76c1-6315-4201-bef5-2d5d4bc4e33f-140","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! 10-foot painter for Wobble Minutes. The sim owns the layout; this only draws it.\\n\\nuse std::sync::Arc;\\n\\nuse egui::{Color32, CornerRadius, FontFamily, FontId, Pos2, Rect, Stroke, StrokeKind, Vec2};\\n\\nuse pav_core::fit_ui::FitUi;\\n\\nconst FREDOKA: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\\\"../fonts/Fredoka_600SemiBold.ttf\\\");\\n10→const NUNITO: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\\\"../fonts/Nunito_700Bold.ttf\\\");\\n\\n/// Title and body sizes at this window. At 1920×1080 they are 64 and 34.\\npub fn type_px(width: f32, height: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let scale = (width / 1920.0).min(height / 1080.0).max(0.0);\\n    (64.0 * scale, 34.0 * scale)\\n}\\n\\npub fn install_fonts(ctx: &egui::Context) {\\n    let mut fonts = egui::FontDefinitions::default();\\n20→    fonts.font_data.insert(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into(), Arc::new(egui::FontData::from_static(FREDOKA)));\\n    fonts.font_data.insert(\\\"Nunito\\\".into(), Arc::new(egui::FontData::from_static(NUNITO)));\\n    fonts.families.insert(FontFamily::Name(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into()), vec![\\\"Fredoka\\\".into(), \\\"Nunito\\\".into()]);\\n    fonts.families.insert(FontFamily::Name(\\\"Nunito\\\".into()), vec![\\\"Nunito\\\".into()]);\\n    if let Some(prop) = fonts.families.get_mut(&FontFamily::Proportional) {\\n        prop.insert(0, \\\"Nunito\\\".into());\\n    }\\n    ctx.set_fonts(fonts);\\n}\\n\\n30→fn text(painter: &egui::Painter, pos: Pos2, text: &str, size: f32, family: FontFamily, color: Color32) {\\n    if text.is_empty() || size < 1.0 {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let galley = painter.layout_no_wrap(text.to_string(), FontId::new(size, family), color);\\n    painter.galley(pos, galley, color);\\n}\\n\\n/// Draws the stay UI in pixels. `scale` is `min(w/1920, h/1080)`.\\npub fn draw(ctx: &egui::Context, ui: &FitUi) {\\n40→    let screen = ctx.content_rect();\\n    if screen.width() < 2.0 || screen.height() < 2.0 {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let (title_px, body_px) = type_px(screen.width(), screen.height());\\n    let scale = title_px / 64.0;\\n    let painter = ctx.layer_painter(egui::LayerId::new(egui::Order::Foreground, egui::Id::new(\\\"wobble_minutes\\\")));\\n    let ink = Color32::from_rgb(28, 48, 56);\\n    let teal = Color32::from_rgb(14, 122, 132);\\n    let fred = FontFamily::Name(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into());\\n50→    let nun = FontFamily::Name(\\\"Nunito\\\".into());\\n\\n    if ui.demo {\\n        let ribbon = Rect::from_min_size(screen.right_top() + Vec2::new(-220.0 * scale, 18.0 * scale), Vec2::new(200.0 * scale, 64.0 * scale));\\n        painter.rect_filled(ribbon, CornerRadius::from(18.0 * scale), Color32::from_rgb(214, 92, 58));\\n        text(&painter, ribbon.left_top() + Vec2::new(28.0 * scale, 8.0 * scale), \\\"DEMO\\\", title_px * 0.6, fred.clone(), Color32::WHITE);\\n    }\\n\\n    text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.center().x - title_px * ui.title.chars().count() as f32 * 0.28, 36.0 * scale), &ui.title, title_px, fred.clone(), Color32::WHITE);\\n\\n60→    if !ui.big.is_empty() {\\n        text(\\n            &painter,\\n            Pos2::new(screen.center().x - title_px * ui.big.chars().count() as f32 * 0.4, screen.height() * 0.16),\\n            &ui.big,\\n            title_px * 1.4,\\n            fred.clone(),\\n            Color32::from_rgb(255, 214, 120),\\n        );\\n    }\\n70→\\n    let mut y = 120.0 * scale;\\n    for line in ui.lines.iter().take(2) {\\n        text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.width() * 0.18, y), line, body_px, nun.clone(), Color32::from_rgb(230, 244, 242));\\n        y += body_px * 1.25;\\n    }\\n\\n    for it in &ui.items {\\n        let r = Rect::from_min_size(\\n            Pos2::new(screen.left() + it.rect[0] * screen.width(), screen.top() + it.rect[1] * screen.height()),\\n80→            Vec2::new(it.rect[2] * screen.width(), it.rect[3] * screen.height()),\\n        );\\n        painter.rect_filled(r, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Color32::WHITE);\\n        if it.id == ui.focus {\\n            painter.rect_stroke(r, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Stroke::new((8.0 * scale).max(2.0), teal), StrokeKind::Outside);\\n        }\\n        text(&painter, r.left_center() + Vec2::new(28.0 * scale, -body_px * 0.55), &it.label, body_px, nun.clone(), ink);\\n    }\\n\\n    if let Some([x, y, ring, _]) = ui.puck {\\n90→        let c = Pos2::new(screen.center().x, screen.height() * 0.72);\\n        let rad = (screen.height() * 0.16 * ring).max(8.0);\\n        painter.circle_stroke(c, rad, Stroke::new((4.0 * scale).max(1.5), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 255, 255, 180)));\\n        let dot = c + Vec2::new(x, -y) * rad;\\n        painter.circle_filled(dot, (14.0 * scale).max(3.0), Color32::from_rgb(255, 120, 96));\\n    }\\n\\n    if ui.touch_card {\\n        let card = Rect::from_center_size(screen.center(), Vec2::new(screen.width() * 0.7, body_px * 4.0));\\n        painter.rect_filled(card, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 255, 255, 235));\\n100→        text(&painter, card.left_top() + Vec2::new(24.0 * scale, 16.0 * scale), \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", body_px, nun.clone(), ink);\\n    }\\n\\n    let prompt = if ui.footer.is_empty() { ui.glyph.clone() } else { format!(\\\"{}   {}\\\", ui.glyph, ui.footer) };\\n    text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.width() * 0.28, screen.height() - body_px * 1.6), &prompt, body_px, nun, Color32::WHITE);\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n110→    use pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim};\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn type_holds_the_ten_foot_floor() {\\n        let (title, body) = type_px(1920.0, 1080.0);\\n        assert!(title >= 64.0 && body >= 34.0, \\\"{title} {body}\\\");\\n        let (small_t, _) = type_px(320.0, 180.0);\\n        assert!(small_t < 64.0 && small_t > 8.0, \\\"{small_t}\\\");\\n    }\\n\\n120→    #[test]\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! 10-foot painter for Wobble Minutes. The sim owns the layout; this only draws it.\\n\\nuse std::sync::Arc;\\n\\nuse egui::{Color32, CornerRadius, FontFamily, FontId, Pos2, Rect, Stroke, StrokeKind, Vec2};\\n\\nuse pav_core::fit_ui::FitUi;\\n\\nconst FREDOKA: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\\\"../fonts/Fredoka_600SemiBold.ttf\\\");\\n10→const NUNITO: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\\\"../fonts/Nunito_700Bold.ttf\\\");\\n\\n/// Title and body sizes at this window. At 1920×1080 they are 64 and 34.\\npub fn type_px(width: f32, height: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let scale = (width / 1920.0).min(height / 1080.0).max(0.0);\\n    (64.0 * scale, 34.0 * scale)\\n}\\n\\npub fn install_fonts(ctx: &egui::Context) {\\n    let mut fonts = egui::FontDefinitions::default();\\n20→    fonts.font_data.insert(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into(), Arc::new(egui::FontData::from_static(FREDOKA)));\\n    fonts.font_data.insert(\\\"Nunito\\\".into(), Arc::new(egui::FontData::from_static(NUNITO)));\\n    fonts.families.insert(FontFamily::Name(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into()), vec![\\\"Fredoka\\\".into(), \\\"Nunito\\\".into()]);\\n    fonts.families.insert(FontFamily::Name(\\\"Nunito\\\".into()), vec![\\\"Nunito\\\".into()]);\\n    if let Some(prop) = fonts.families.get_mut(&FontFamily::Proportional) {\\n        prop.insert(0, \\\"Nunito\\\".into());\\n    }\\n    ctx.set_fonts(fonts);\\n}\\n\\n30→fn text(painter: &egui::Painter, pos: Pos2, text: &str, size: f32, family: FontFamily, color: Color32) {\\n    if text.is_empty() || size < 1.0 {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let galley = painter.layout_no_wrap(text.to_string(), FontId::new(size, family), color);\\n    painter.galley(pos, galley, color);\\n}\\n\\n/// Draws the stay UI in pixels. `scale` is `min(w/1920, h/1080)`.\\npub fn draw(ctx: &egui::Context, ui: &FitUi) {\\n40→    let screen = ctx.content_rect();\\n    if screen.width() < 2.0 || screen.height() < 2.0 {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let (title_px, body_px) = type_px(screen.width(), screen.height());\\n    let scale = title_px / 64.0;\\n    let painter = ctx.layer_painter(egui::LayerId::new(egui::Order::Foreground, egui::Id::new(\\\"wobble_minutes\\\")));\\n    let ink = Color32::from_rgb(28, 48, 56);\\n    let teal = Color32::from_rgb(14, 122, 132);\\n    let fred = FontFamily::Name(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into());\\n50→    let nun = FontFamily::Name(\\\"Nunito\\\".into());\\n\\n    if ui.demo {\\n        let ribbon = Rect::from_min_size(screen.right_top() + Vec2::new(-220.0 * scale, 18.0 * scale), Vec2::new(200.0 * scale, 64.0 * scale));\\n        painter.rect_filled(ribbon, CornerRadius::from(18.0 * scale), Color32::from_rgb(214, 92, 58));\\n        text(&painter, ribbon.left_top() + Vec2::new(28.0 * scale, 8.0 * scale), \\\"DEMO\\\", title_px * 0.6, fred.clone(), Color32::WHITE);\\n    }\\n\\n    text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.center().x - title_px * ui.title.chars().count() as f32 * 0.28, 36.0 * scale), &ui.title, title_px, fred.clone(), Color32::WHITE);\\n\\n60→    if !ui.big.is_empty() {\\n        text(\\n            &painter,\\n            Pos2::new(screen.center().x - title_px * ui.big.chars().count() as f32 * 0.4, screen.height() * 0.16),\\n            &ui.big,\\n            title_px * 1.4,\\n            fred.clone(),\\n            Color32::from_rgb(255, 214, 120),\\n        );\\n    }\\n70→\\n    let mut y = 120.0 * scale;\\n    for line in ui.lines.iter().take(2) {\\n        text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.width() * 0.18, y), line, body_px, nun.clone(), Color32::from_rgb(230, 244, 242));\\n        y += body_px * 1.25;\\n    }\\n\\n    for it in &ui.items {\\n        let r = Rect::from_min_size(\\n            Pos2::new(screen.left() + it.rect[0] * screen.width(), screen.top() + it.rect[1] * screen.height()),\\n80→            Vec2::new(it.rect[2] * screen.width(), it.rect[3] * screen.height()),\\n        );\\n        painter.rect_filled(r, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Color32::WHITE);\\n        if it.id == ui.focus {\\n            painter.rect_stroke(r, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Stroke::new((8.0 * scale).max(2.0), teal), StrokeKind::Outside);\\n        }\\n        text(&painter, r.left_center() + Vec2::new(28.0 * scale, -body_px * 0.55), &it.label, body_px, nun.clone(), ink);\\n    }\\n\\n    if let Some([x, y, ring, _]) = ui.puck {\\n90→        let c = Pos2::new(screen.center().x, screen.height() * 0.72);\\n        let rad = (screen.height() * 0.16 * ring).max(8.0);\\n        painter.circle_stroke(c, rad, Stroke::new((4.0 * scale).max(1.5), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 255, 255, 180)));\\n        let dot = c + Vec2::new(x, -y) * rad;\\n        painter.circle_filled(dot, (14.0 * scale).max(3.0), Color32::from_rgb(255, 120, 96));\\n    }\\n\\n    if ui.touch_card {\\n        let card = Rect::from_center_size(screen.center(), Vec2::new(screen.width() * 0.7, body_px * 4.0));\\n        painter.rect_filled(card, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 255, 255, 235));\\n100→        text(&painter, card.left_top() + Vec2::new(24.0 * scale, 16.0 * scale), \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", body_px, nun.clone(), ink);\\n    }\\n\\n    let prompt = if ui.footer.is_empty() { ui.glyph.clone() } else { format!(\\\"{}   {}\\\", ui.glyph, ui.footer) };\\n    text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.width() * 0.28, screen.height() - body_px * 1.6), &prompt, body_px, nun, Color32::WHITE);\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n110→    use pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim};\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn type_holds_the_ten_foot_floor() {\\n        let (title, body) = type_px(1920.0, 1080.0);\\n        assert!(title >= 64.0 && body >= 34.0, \\\"{title} {body}\\\");\\n        let (small_t, _) = type_px(320.0, 180.0);\\n        assert!(small_t < 64.0 && small_t > 8.0, \\\"{small_t}\\\");\\n    }\\n\\n120→    #[test]\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/fit.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"//! 10-foot painter for Wobble Minutes. The sim owns the layout; this only draws it.\\n\\nuse std::sync::Arc;\\n\\nuse egui::{Color32, CornerRadius, FontFamily, FontId, Pos2, Rect, Stroke, StrokeKind, Vec2};\\n\\nuse pav_core::fit_ui::FitUi;\\n\\nconst FREDOKA: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\\\"../fonts/Fredoka_600SemiBold.ttf\\\");\\nconst NUNITO: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\\\"../fonts/Nunito_700Bold.ttf\\\");\\n\\n/// Title and body sizes at this window. At 1920×1080 they are 64 and 34.\\npub fn type_px(width: f32, height: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let scale = (width / 1920.0).min(height / 1080.0).max(0.0);\\n    (64.0 * scale, 34.0 * scale)\\n}\\n\\npub fn install_fonts(ctx: &egui::Context) {\\n    let mut fonts = egui::FontDefinitions::default();\\n    fonts.font_data.insert(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into(), Arc::new(egui::FontData::from_static(FREDOKA)));\\n    fonts.font_data.insert(\\\"Nunito\\\".into(), Arc::new(egui::FontData::from_static(NUNITO)));\\n    fonts.families.insert(FontFamily::Name(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into()), vec![\\\"Fredoka\\\".into(), \\\"Nunito\\\".into()]);\\n    fonts.families.insert(FontFamily::Name(\\\"Nunito\\\".into()), vec![\\\"Nunito\\\".into()]);\\n    if let Some(prop) = fonts.families.get_mut(&FontFamily::Proportional) {\\n        prop.insert(0, \\\"Nunito\\\".into());\\n    }\\n    ctx.set_fonts(fonts);\\n}\\n\\nfn text(painter: &egui::Painter, pos: Pos2, text: &str, size: f32, family: FontFamily, color: Color32) {\\n    if text.is_empty() || size < 1.0 {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let galley = painter.layout_no_wrap(text.to_string(), FontId::new(size, family), color);\\n    painter.galley(pos, galley, color);\\n}\\n\\n/// Draws the stay UI in pixels. `scale` is `min(w/1920, h/1080)`.\\npub fn draw(ctx: &egui::Context, ui: &FitUi) {\\n    let screen = ctx.content_rect();\\n    if screen.width() < 2.0 || screen.height() < 2.0 {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let (title_px, body_px) = type_px(screen.width(), screen.height());\\n    let scale = title_px / 64.0;\\n    let painter = ctx.layer_painter(egui::LayerId::new(egui::Order::Foreground, egui::Id::new(\\\"wobble_minutes\\\")));\\n    let ink = Color32::from_rgb(28, 48, 56);\\n    let teal = Color32::from_rgb(14, 122, 132);\\n    let fred = FontFamily::Name(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into());\\n    let nun = FontFamily::Name(\\\"Nunito\\\".into());\\n\\n    if ui.demo {\\n        let ribbon = Rect::from_min_size(screen.right_top() + Vec2::new(-220.0 * scale, 18.0 * scale), Vec2::new(200.0 * scale, 64.0 * scale));\\n        painter.rect_filled(ribbon, CornerRadius::from(18.0 * scale), Color32::from_rgb(214, 92, 58));\\n        text(&painter, ribbon.left_top() + Vec2::new(28.0 * scale, 8.0 * scale), \\\"DEMO\\\", title_px * 0.6, fred.clone(), Color32::WHITE);\\n    }\\n\\n    text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.center().x - title_px * ui.title.chars().count() as f32 * 0.28, 36.0 * scale), &ui.title, title_px, fred.clone(), Color32::WHITE);\\n\\n    if !ui.big.is_empty() {\\n        text(\\n            &painter,\\n            Pos2::new(screen.center().x - title_px * ui.big.chars().count() as f32 * 0.4, screen.height() * 0.16),\\n            &ui.big,\\n            title_px * 1.4,\\n            fred.clone(),\\n            Color32::from_rgb(255, 214, 120),\\n        );\\n    }\\n\\n    let mut y = 120.0 * scale;\\n    for line in ui.lines.iter().take(2) {\\n        text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.width() * 0.18, y), line, body_px, nun.clone(), Color32::from_rgb(230, 244, 242));\\n        y += body_px * 1.25;\\n    }\\n\\n    for it in &ui.items {\\n        let r = Rect::from_min_size(\\n            Pos2::new(screen.left() + it.rect[0] * screen.width(), screen.top() + it.rect[1] * screen.height()),\\n            Vec2::new(it.rect[2] * screen.width(), it.rect[3] * screen.height()),\\n        );\\n        painter.rect_filled(r, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Color32::WHITE);\\n        if it.id == ui.focus {\\n            painter.rect_stroke(r, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Stroke::new((8.0 * scale).max(2.0), teal), StrokeKind::Outside);\\n        }\\n        text(&painter, r.left_center() + Vec2::new(28.0 * scale, -body_px * 0.55), &it.label, body_px, nun.clone(), ink);\\n    }\\n\\n    if let Some([x, y, ring, _]) = ui.puck {\\n        let c = Pos2::new(screen.center().x, screen.height() * 0.72);\\n        let rad = (screen.height() * 0.16 * ring).max(8.0);\\n        painter.circle_stroke(c, rad, Stroke::new((4.0 * scale).max(1.5), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 255, 255, 180)));\\n        let dot = c + Vec2::new(x, -y) * rad;\\n        painter.circle_filled(dot, (14.0 * scale).max(3.0), Color32::from_rgb(255, 120, 96));\\n    }\\n\\n    if ui.touch_card {\\n        let card = Rect::from_center_size(screen.center(), Vec2::new(screen.width() * 0.7, body_px * 4.0));\\n        painter.rect_filled(card, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 255, 255, 235));\\n        text(&painter, card.left_top() + Vec2::new(24.0 * scale, 16.0 * scale), \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", body_px, nun.clone(), ink);\\n    }\\n\\n    let prompt = if ui.footer.is_empty() { ui.glyph.clone() } else { format!(\\\"{}   {}\\\", ui.glyph, ui.footer) };\\n    text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.width() * 0.28, screen.height() - body_px * 1.6), &prompt, body_px, nun, Color32::WHITE);\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n    use pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim};\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn type_holds_the_ten_foot_floor() {\\n        let (title, body) = type_px(1920.0, 1080.0);\\n        assert!(title >= 64.0 && body >= 34.0, \\\"{title} {body}\\\");\\n        let (small_t, _) = type_px(320.0, 180.0);\\n        assert!(small_t < 64.0 && small_t > 8.0, \\\"{small_t}\\\");\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n\",\"total_lines\":140}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"e0af61ac-d224-42f2-a7eb-6536ed529fe9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_754","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will implement a focused set of changes.\n\nReviewing tick() and slider ID 300 for the tuning page. Designing a three-tab dev menu: Hub, Jump, and Cheats.\n\nAdding Time and Tuning tabs to the dev menu. The first screen will be a control panel with direct actions, using TAB to navigate deeper pages. This keeps the menu pad-navigable without hunting.\n\nThe test plan is now concrete. It will pause into dev mode, adjust time scale with MENU_DOWN and MENU_RIGHT, trigger the Step Party jump event, verify minutes increase via \"Give minutes,\" and use tuning sliders. The Jump tab will list five events on page zero, with a \"More jumps\" option to advance pages.\n\nThe dev menu will use a `dev_tab` state machine. Page zero holds four top-level buttons: Jump, Cheats, Time, and Tuning. TAB_L returns to the menu. TAB_R pages within the active tab. The test will pause into dev mode and select Jump to enter the jump tab.\n\nThe jump tab will page through events, with the first five on page zero. The test will pause into dev mode, select Jump, confirm the first event to verify it enters the card phase with the breath event.\n\nCheats will be tested by toggling \"No tips\" and confirming \"Give minutes\" increases day_minutes. Time scale will be set to 4x and verified. Tuning sliders will be adjusted with MENU_RIGHT, starting from the stiffness parameter.\n\nThe existing music test will be updated to use MENU_RIGHT for slider adjustments instead of Slider(300). Reset feel will remain on the dev menu as a confirmable item, preserving the original Click(60) path. The revised test flow pauses into dev mode, navigates to Tuning, adjusts stiffness with MENU_RIGHT, and then returns to Reset feel.\n\nA shared `nudge_focused_slider` helper will handle MENU_LEFT and MENU_RIGHT for any focused slider, including settings music rows (IDs 610–616) and dev tuning parameters (IDs 300+). The implementation will check the focused item ID and verify it is a slider before adjusting its value.\n\nThe slider nudge helper will adjust the focused slider by 0.1 and clamp the result between 0 and 1. Mouse drag input will also be wired into fit_sample so a real player can scrub sliders with a mouse, though the simulation test will still assert pad left/right behavior.\n\nI will add a unit test in pav_app/src/input.rs to verify that fit_sample emits Slider events when the mouse is held over a slider rectangle. This covers the drag path the skeptic cited.\n\nThe fit_sample drag logic will check for held Left mouse state to emit Slider events during scrubbing. Pad left and right navigation will be tested in fit.rs. A page_slice helper is being added for name and outfit paging.\n\nThe page_slice helper wraps pages modulo the total count. Name and outfit IDs will stay 400+absolute index so activation works. Leaving the name screen resets the page to zero. TAB will wrap within each screen's bounds instead of growing unbounded.\n\nThe schedule screen will show four events per page, with the end-day option replacing one event slot to keep the visible count at six or fewer.\n\nIsland mats will be placed in a ring around the spawn point. Confirming near an empty mat starts the matching event if free play is active or the event is scheduled for today. The hub.toml file will also receive objects to give the room visible props. This makes island confirmation startable from the island itself, which is the intended free-play behavior.\n\nThe calendar screen will show five day rows with stamps or empty indicators, plus a Back button. It is read-only except for Back, matching the Back-only stub requirement.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-624aab91-4ad8-4f56-8882-b17f9f6da160-141","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"struct PuppetDef|helm|pub gloves","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/puppet.rs","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-624aab91-4ad8-4f56-8882-b17f9f6da160-142","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn look|GearLook|shirt","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2865,"output_tokens":2725,"cache_read_input_tokens":174464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"6d8ae5b0-5b0c-4c8e-9167-01c3955ce58f"}
