{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_770","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that schedule_events already returns all events in free play.\n\nEvents need pagination. The pause menu will remain as Dev Mode to preserve the existing test that expects phase \"dev\". Wardrobe and calendar will be added inside Dev. A fuller pause screen is planned but cannot replace Dev Mode.\n\nDev Mode will be implemented with a tabbed layout. Opening it from pause resets the tab and page to zero. The menu will contain six items: Jump, Cheats, Time, Tuning, Reset feel, and Resume. Wardrobe and calendar are being placed as real content screens rather than menu stubs.\n\nWardrobe and Calendar will be placed on the first page of the Dev menu, replacing Cheats and Time. Reset feel remains on the Tuning page. Resume is kept as a direct action item.\n\nThe Dev menu will use two pages. Page zero holds Jump, Cheats, Time, Tuning, Wardrobe, and Resume. Page one holds Calendar, Reset feel, Settings, About, and Back.\n\nJump items will be paged five per screen with IDs starting at 220. Cheats will contain eight toggles and actions, also paginated five per screen. Time will hold six speed controls and pause options.\n\nThe Time sub-tab will use six items: 0.25x, 1x, 2x, 4x, Pause clock, and Single step. A BACK button inside a sub-tab will return to the main Dev menu instead of exiting Dev Mode.\n\nSingle step in the Time menu will set time_scale to zero and queue a single world tick for execution when Dev Mode resumes. This is awkward because the world normally freezes while Dev is active.\n\nSingle step will pause the clock, then execute one world tick and return to paused. Because Dev Mode freezes the activity loop, this tick must be injected directly into post().\n\nSingle step will be triggered from pre() when activating the action, passing the simulation object. It will temporarily tick activity for one frame and advance world time by 1/60.\n\nFor the No tips cheat, a `no_tips` flag will be added to the cheat state. The activity tick will check this flag and skip incrementing the tip counter.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-00b482bd-01ba-4c36-98b2-cbf047f8077b-165","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"gag","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":684,"output_tokens":1654,"cache_read_input_tokens":196096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"177fa380-c0c4-48a3-bcb2-e7068c702e9e"}
