"line_number\":307,\"content\":\"            gag: false,\"},{\"line_number\":774,\"content\":\"            act.gag = true;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"eb28ab68-5ffd-4617-8b16-374d67d56595"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_771","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Do not reuse \"gag\" in the squat context.\n\nAdding a `quiet_tips` flag to Activity to suppress tip messages. Autoplay will use the existing bot injection path for event flows.\n\nThe quiet_tips flag will be applied in the same place as the demo bot injection.\n\nCheats will add 5 minutes, unlock all content and stamps, grant 9 stars, and skip dialogue by setting line_i to 999.\n\nWin now sets score to 1000 and stars to 3. Lose now sets both to zero.\n\nThe jump cheat starts a card activity with flow set to Direct. This avoids story banking issues during the test. After result returns early without island changes.\n\nAttract jump enters attract mode.\n\nMedley jump sets run to Medley, starts paddle, and keeps hub_mode false so pause still works.\n\nDay jump directly sets the current day number.\n\nThe jump page lists four events per page plus Attract, Medley, Day 5, and Big Stand phase 5. Finale phase selection is deferred.\n\nPhase jump targets Big Stand with act.phase set to 4 and act.sub to 0.\n\nThe skip prompt test will use the real menu path. It boots the fit, pauses, jumps to Stillness, resumes, and confirms. The phase is overwritten to 4 after start_activity sets it to 0. After fifteen seconds the footer shows \"Press Cross to skip\". The song is zero and the big score is hidden. Confirming forfeits.\n\nJumps will set flow directly to Event or Check. The card activity is skipped so the test lands immediately in the event.\n\nThe status UI will include act_phase and a footer cue text. The skip prompt test needs 900 steps at 60Hz. During Big Stand phase four the song is zero and updates on the next pre(). The eyes-closed test boots into an event or check flow and runs the bot until the UI shows \"Eyes closed\" or the phase reaches two.\n\nBot targets will finish in about eight seconds, capped at two thousand ticks. The bot then waits for the puck to vanish, a tone to play, and the screen to dim.\n\nStatus fields will include act_phase, tone, song, time_scale, and pose. Pose will expose the active clip name or id; the test boots a pose activity and asserts the clip is non-zero after a few frames.\n\nName paging will verify that Gray appears on the second page while the first page shows Avery through Finley. Outfit paging will confirm that page two contains Swim and Golden among the eight outfits.\n\nThe schedule test will enable free_play via the game state.\n\nUnlocking all content does not change the flow, so the test must still reach the island schedule. The full new stay is too long. A shorter path that skips the title boot is being considered.\n\nAn \"Island\" jump option will be added to the menu so the test can reach the island directly after unlocking all content. The schedule test will then open the schedule, tab until Cannonball appears in the event list, confirm it, and assert the screen items.\n\nA helper function will navigate the menu by pressing down until the focused item label contains a target substring, with a cap to prevent infinite loops. The focus state is tracked by matching the UI item ID against the current focus index.\n\nThe dev menu page zero lists Jump, Cheats, Time, Tuning, Wardrobe, and Resume. The jump menu splits the thirteen events into four pages of four items each. Page three holds Big Stand, Stillness, Attract, and Medley. Page four holds Day 5, Island, and the remaining finale entries.\n\nWardrobe items will be ordered as Sun cap, Towel turban, Crown, Halo, Sweatbands, Floaties, Belt, then the paged outfits. Selecting one applies gear to sim.config.puppet and uses IDs 260 and above.\n\nThe calendar screen shows each day as \"Day n · open\" or \"Day n · stamped\", depending on whether the day is completed. A dim field will be added to FitUi so the painter can fill the screen with black when ui.dim exceeds 0.01.\n\nThe Input struct is private, so a real drag test in input.rs would need gilrs initialization. A lighter unit test will verify the slider logic directly.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-421551ef-84cf-41e8-b09f-a79cfbc87abd-166","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/input.rs","offset":400,"limit":55}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-421551ef-84cf-41e8-b09f-a79cfbc87abd-167","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"struct FitSample|fn new\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/input.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1869,"output_tokens":2610,"cache_read_input_tokens":196736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"e49c2fdf-406a-4973-91be-dc54364bfa07"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-421551ef-84cf-41e8-b09f-a79cfbc87abd-166","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"400→                    \\\"left\\\" => st.left = vec(v)?,\\n                    \\\"right\\\" => st.right = vec(v)?,\\n                    \\\"hold\\\" => st.hold = v.split(',').map(button).collect::<Result<_, _>>()?,\\n                    \\\"tap\\\" => st.tap = v.split(',').map(button).collect::<Result<_, _>>()?,\\n                    o => return Err(format!(\\\"line {}: unknown '{o}'\\\", n + 1)),\\n                }\\n            }\\n            steps.push(st);\\n        }\\n        Ok(PadScript { steps, at: 0, frame: 0 })\\n410→    }\\n\\n    /// This frame's step (and whether it's the step's first frame); None when done.\\n    fn next(&mut self) -> Option<(PadStep, bool)> {\\n        let st = self.steps.get(self.at)?.clone();\\n        let first = self.frame == 0;\\n        self.frame += 1;\\n        if self.frame >= st.frames.max(1) {\\n            self.at += 1;\\n            self.frame = 0;\\n420→        }\\n        Some((st, first))\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn deadzone(v: Vec2, dz: f32) -> Vec2 {\\n    let l = v.length();\\n    if l < dz { Vec2::ZERO } else { v / l * ((l - dz) / (1.0 - dz)).min(1.0) }\\n}\\n\\n430→impl Input {\\n    pub fn new() -> Self {\\n        let gilrs = match gilrs::Gilrs::new() {\\n            Ok(g) => {\\n                for (_, gp) in g.gamepads() {\\n                    log::info!(\\\"gamepad: {} ({:?})\\\", gp.name(), gp.power_info());\\n                }\\n                Some(g)\\n            }\\n            Err(e) => {\\n440→                log::warn!(\\\"gamepads unavailable: {e}\\\");\\n                None\\n            }\\n        };\\n        Self {\\n            keys: HashSet::new(),\\n            mouse: HashSet::new(),\\n            cursor: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            mouse_active: false,\\n            gilrs,\\n450→            pad_script: None,\\n            pad: Pad::default(),\\n            // Pad glyphs until a key, a mouse move, or a stick is actually used.\\n            last_device: Device::Gamepad,\\n            prev_held: 0,\",\"content_concise\":\"400→                    \\\"left\\\" => st.left = vec(v)?,\\n                    \\\"right\\\" => st.right = vec(v)?,\\n                    \\\"hold\\\" => st.hold = v.split(',').map(button).collect::<Result<_, _>>()?,\\n                    \\\"tap\\\" => st.tap = v.split(',').map(button).collect::<Result<_, _>>()?,\\n                    o => return Err(format!(\\\"line {}: unknown '{o}'\\\", n + 1)),\\n                }\\n            }\\n            steps.push(st);\\n        }\\n        Ok(PadScript { steps, at: 0, frame: 0 })\\n410→    }\\n\\n    /// This frame's step (and whether it's the step's first frame); None when done.\\n    fn next(&mut self) -> Option<(PadStep, bool)> {\\n        let st = self.steps.get(self.at)?.clone();\\n        let first = self.frame == 0;\\n        self.frame += 1;\\n        if self.frame >= st.frames.max(1) {\\n            self.at += 1;\\n            self.frame = 0;\\n420→        }\\n        Some((st, first))\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn deadzone(v: Vec2, dz: f32) -> Vec2 {\\n    let l = v.length();\\n    if l < dz { Vec2::ZERO } else { v / l * ((l - dz) / (1.0 - dz)).min(1.0) }\\n}\\n\\n430→impl Input {\\n    pub fn new() -> Self {\\n        let gilrs = match gilrs::Gilrs::new() {\\n            Ok(g) => {\\n                for (_, gp) in g.gamepads() {\\n                    log::info!(\\\"gamepad: {} ({:?})\\\", gp.name(), gp.power_info());\\n                }\\n                Some(g)\\n            }\\n            Err(e) => {\\n440→                log::warn!(\\\"gamepads unavailable: {e}\\\");\\n                None\\n            }\\n        };\\n        Self {\\n            keys: HashSet::new(),\\n            mouse: HashSet::new(),\\n            cursor: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            mouse_active: false,\\n            gilrs,\\n450→            pad_script: None,\\n            pad: Pad::default(),\\n            // Pad glyphs until a key, a mouse move, or a stick is actually used.\\n            last_device: Device::Gamepad,\\n            prev_held: 0,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/input.rs\",\"offset\":400,\"limit\":55,\"raw_output\":\"                    \\\"left\\\" => st.left = vec(v)?,\\n                    \\\"right\\\" => st.right = vec(v)?,\\n                    \\\"hold\\\" => st.hold = v.split(',').map(button).collect::<Result<_, _>>()?,\\n                    \\\"tap\\\" => st.tap = v.split(',').map(button).collect::<Result<_, _>>()?,\\n                    o => return Err(format!(\\\"line {}: unknown '{o}'\\\", n + 1)),\\n                }\\n            }\\n            steps.push(st);\\n        }\\n        Ok(PadScript { steps, at: 0, frame: 0 })\\n    }\\n\\n    /// This frame's step (and whether it's the step's first frame); None when done.\\n    fn next(&mut self) -> Option<(PadStep, bool)> {\\n        let st = self.steps.get(self.at)?.clone();\\n        let first = self.frame == 0;\\n        self.frame += 1;\\n        if self.frame >= st.frames.max(1) {\\n            self.at += 1;\\n            self.frame = 0;\\n        }\\n        Some((st, first))\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn deadzone(v: Vec2, dz: f32) -> Vec2 {\\n    let l = v.length();\\n    if l < dz { Vec2::ZERO } else { v / l * ((l - dz) / (1.0 - dz)).min(1.0) }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Input {\\n    pub fn new() -> Self {\\n        let gilrs = match gilrs::Gilrs::new() {\\n            Ok(g) => {\\n                for (_, gp) in g.gamepads() {\\n                    log::info!(\\\"gamepad: {} ({:?})\\\", gp.name(), gp.power_info());\\n                }\\n                Some(g)\\n            }\\n            Err(e) => {\\n                log::warn!(\\\"gamepads unavailable: {e}\\\");\