{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_787","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Stiffness is the first float in visit(), so id 300 corresponds to stiffness.\n\nStiffness nudge math checks out: +0.1 yields 47.5, a 7.5-point jump. Reset feel is on the root menu page, reached by TAB then MENU_DOWN once. Started rewriting the test function.\n\nThe test steps through the dev menu to reach the Tuning page, selects stiffness via MENU_RIGHT, confirms it moved by more than one point, and returns to the root menu.\n\nThe test now returns to the root menu, selects Reset feel, and confirms stiffness reverts to its original value.\n\nA settings music slider test using MENU_RIGHT is planned to cover the pad path. A separate unit test for mouse drag emitting Slider in pav_app is also being considered.\n\nA settings music test will open Settings from the title screen, focus Music, and press MENU_RIGHT to raise volume from 0.10 to 0.20.\n\nSettings is index 2 on the title screen. The music slider test will be separate from the stiffness test. A mouse drag unit test for pav_app is being drafted.\n\nThe mouse drag test now asserts the slider value is 0.5 when the cursor is centered on a row. Need to check for existing pav_app input tests and the MouseButton import. Also considering whether a tap on a non-slider should emit Slider or Hover.\n\nThe design should emit Slider only while the left mouse button is held. A tap or click on a non-slider row must still produce a Click event so menus remain usable. Hover should stay for focus when the button is not pressed.\n\nThe panel requires the pad path, so mouse drag is optional. Emitting Slider whenever the left button is held would turn every tap into a drag and break menu clicks. The correct logic is to emit Slider only while dragging a slider row, emit Click on a fresh tap, and keep Hover for focus when nothing is pressed.\n\nThe mouse input logic now emits Slider only while the left button is held and the cursor is inside a slider row, and emits Click on a fresh tap. A test can hold Left without a tap flag to verify Slider output. The pad path routes through pre() instead of fit_sample. Settings page wrapping is unbounded.\n\nSettings page 2 currently mirrors page 1, so that existing behavior will be preserved. Name and outfit screens will use modulo to wrap pages. TAB_L uses saturating_sub to avoid negative values. Entering the Name, Look, or Outfit screens resets the page counter to zero. The Schedule paging logic is now being drafted.\n\nSchedule paging now caps each page at four events. The page counter wraps modulo the total page count, so pressing TAB still increments it even when the display does not change.\n\nEnd day appears when the schedule is clear, giving a maximum of six items per page. Island event mats will be stored as world coordinates after player spawn. The room layout is being mapped to determine cell size and origin.\n\nThe player is at row 6, column 7. Rather than guessing cell size and origin, the code will record the player's feet position in build() and place island event mats at fixed offsets from that point.\n\nIsland CONFIRM within 1.2 meters of a mat starts that event if free play is active or the event is scheduled for today. The island will use a `mats` vector storing each event ID with its world coordinates, computed from the player spawn position. Visual props will be placed around the player marker at fixed layout coordinates: rowboat, bench, lamp post, market stall, round table, chair, mat boxes, clam sphere, and calendar board.\n\nProps will use body = \"none\" so they do not fall or block the player during tests. This avoids physics collision that would slow down movement tests in a small room. The panel still needs beach and wellness props to be visible.\n\nThe island props are now defined with exact coordinates and colors. The wobble mat is a box at [5, 0.05, 8] with body none. The clam sphere sits at [4.2, 0.2, 9.2]. The calendar board is a box at [13, 1.1, 6]. These assets are confirmed to exist in the library hall so they will not break room parsing.\n\nThe island mat positions will be placed in a ring around the player at radius 2.4, using the 11 playable event kinds. If asset loading fails during boot, the code will fall back to primitive shapes instead.\n\nThe island CONFIRM handler checks `mat_here` using the player's feet position, then starts the event and switches to the Card flow if allowed. The SCHEDULE action remains available on the island without conflicting with flop collection.\n\nThe island event mats will be placed at a radius of 3.6 meters to avoid overlapping the 1.2-meter flop collection spots. The room is roughly 14 meters inside the walls, so this distance keeps them safely within bounds.\n\nVisual island mats will be placed in hub.toml as decorative objects. Logical mat positions will be computed in build() from the player spawn point. The panel requires both visual and logical mats, though exact coordinate alignment is not critical.\n\nThe schedule menu test is the required island test. Teleporting the player to verify mat placement would violate the no-cheating rule, so walking with input.move_dir is the proper path. The drive_player function already maps last_move to move_dir during Island flow.\n\nThe island test will read FitGame.mats through get_mut to find the nearest mat, then walk toward it and confirm. This avoids hard-coding coordinates while still following the shipped code path.\n\nTests cannot set `free_play` directly; they must use the cheat menu. The island test will read the `mats` vector from `FitGame` via `sim.state.play.get()`, so that field needs to be public since the test lives in an external crate.\n\nThe `mats` field will be a public vector of event indices and xz coordinates. The island test will expose these positions through the status JSON so the test can read them directly, then walk toward the nearest mat and confirm to start the event. At roughly 4 m/s, the 3.6 meter radius is about one second, or sixty ticks.\n\nChecking whether move_dir is world or camera-relative before writing the island walk test. If that mapping is too messy, the test will simply step the simulation with move_dir and confirm the distance to the mat decreases.\n\nThe island test will be written now and debugged later if it proves flaky. A mat will not be placed under the player to avoid accidental auto-starts. The tick_check signature is being updated to accept events. Phase 2 breathing will pitch its sfx based on balance length, but emitting one event per tick may be too frequent.\n\nThe breathing sfx will be emitted every tick rather than throttled, since the test requires the tone to shift with lean offsets. The activity pitch will be stored on the activity and copied into status. In fit_ui, the eyes-closed check now reads phase 2 directly from the active activity.\n\nThe eyes-closed banner will show \"Eyes closed. Follow the tone.\" and dim the screen to 0.92 while Puck vanishes. The score remains visible during this phase. The status JSON will expose the current tone pitch.\n\nThe status JSON will expose the tone pitch, activity phase, song, time scale, and player clip. The test will boot into the check event and step until phase 2, then assert that Puck is absent from status. The test needs to access FitUi through the Game trait.\n\nThe test will step the simulation with a lean input for thirty ticks after reaching phase two, then assert that the tone pitch changes. It also checks that the UI lines contain \"eyes\" and that the screen dim is above 0.5.\n\nThe `fit_ui` method is confirmed to exist on the `Game` trait and return `Option<FitUi>`, so external tests can call it through the simulation object without extra imports. Adding a `dim` field to `FitUi` requires updating only the constructor, though any JSON deserialization of that struct must also be checked to avoid breaking.\n\nA `#[serde(default)]` attribute will be added to the new `dim` field on `FitUi` so that old JSON deserialization does not break. The painter will draw a full-screen near-black rectangle with alpha scaled from the dim value, using a dark blue color.\n\nThe dim overlay will be drawn first in the UI layer so the title and text remain visible on top. The Big Stand phase 4 UI is being drafted next.\n\nThe Big Stand phase 4 UI is being drafted. The desired song switches to zero when the activity phase reaches four, which pre-pushes a Music event to stop playback. A banner will display a skip prompt once the activity has been active for fifteen seconds.\n\nThe Big Stand skip prompt will use the `prompt` helper to render the correct glyph for the default pad device, producing a line like \"Press Cross to skip\". This text will appear in both the banner footer and a separate UI line.\n\nThe skip prompt text will appear in both the banner footer and a UI line. The test will assert that the line contains \"Press\" and \"skip\". During Big Stand phase 4, the title will be cleared so the banner falls back to the default \"Wobble Minutes\" constant.\n\nThe Big Stand phase 4 banner will be completely empty before the fifteen-second mark, then show only the skip prompt line. The title will also be cleared during this phase so the HUD contains nothing but the puck and the prompt.\n\nA `quiet` flag in `fit_ui` will suppress the default title during long stillness. The footer stays empty before fifteen seconds and shows the skip prompt after that. Any input forfeits the Inner Peace bonus once the timer starts. The Big Stand event is now being finalized.\n\nThe Big Stand finale will compute age as the morning score divided by one hundred, floored and clamped to ten, then subtracted from the current age with a floor of eighteen. The ending string becomes \"rowboat\" when the result is forty or below, otherwise \"extended\". The test will set the morning age to forty-five before playing the finale, expecting the rowboat ending.\n\nThe direct-run path skips the Big Stand age formula entirely. Only Story mode applies it. The test must therefore use a Story run to verify the rowboat ending.\n\nThe test will set the morning age to forty-five on the FitGame, then use the dev menu to start Big Stand in Story mode. This bypasses the long real-play path and avoids assigning the ending directly.\n\nThe test may instead run the real morning check. With skill zero the formula yields age eighty, and with skill one it yields twenty-four.\n\nTo reach an age of forty-five, the morning score must be roughly five hundred ninety. The existing bot typically scores well on checks, so it should easily clear that threshold. The test will set the morning age to forty-five and play a strong finale to prove the rowboat ending.\n\nThe test will assert the age formula against the actual finale score rather than a fixed score. If the bot scores below five hundred, the age cut is zero and the ending stays extended. The bot should be improved so a morning age of forty-five can reach rowboat.\n\nThe Big Stand finale lasts 142 seconds, or about 8520 ticks. At four timescale it drops to roughly 2130 ticks. A score of at least five hundred is needed for the age cut to reach five and trigger the rowboat ending.\n\nHard-coding the morning age is rejected as a test violation. The plan is to boot a story run, set time to four timescale, and jump directly to the morning check to record the real age.\n\nDev-jumping directly to the morning check would preserve Story mode, but the flow would land in Reveal after the check. Advancing to Big Stand requires day five, so the test must set the day before the check finishes, which is awkward.\n\nThe test will use a dev jump to Day 5, then jump to the morning check. The check sets the real age, and the reveal flow advances into Big Stand. The test asserts the age formula against the actual score, and expects the rowboat ending only if the morning age is between forty-one and fifty and the finale score is at least five hundred.\n\nThe test will set the morning age to forty-five directly on the game struct as a stored check result, then play the finale. A controlled idle or lean during the check could instead yield a predictable skill score and a natural age in range.\n\nAn idle morning check yields a skill score of roughly 0.55, which maps to an age near 47. That age sits comfortably inside the required 41–50 range, so a strong finale can still trigger the rowboat ending without manually setting the morning age.\n\nThe idle morning check takes about thirty-four seconds. The test will boot the fit, set time to four timescale, jump to day five, and then start the check. This lands the flow on the Island so the reveal can advance into Big Stand.\n\nThe test will run the idle morning check first to record the actual age. If that age falls outside the required forty-one to fifty range, the strategy can be adjusted afterward rather than hard-coding a value. At four timescale, the check lasts about eight and a half seconds and Big Stand about thirty-five and a half seconds.\n\nThe four timescale persists through dev jumps and check events. After the morning check finishes, the flow becomes Reveal, which advances into Big Stand once the day is five and free play is off. The exact number of reveal lines must be confirmed so the test can advance through them correctly.\n\nThe reveal script line count is being checked. The test will press CONFIRM manually instead of using bot_until, which would otherwise trigger the Big Stand automatically.\n\nThe test will manually press CONFIRM through the reveal phase, then let the bot run until the ending or credits. It records the morning age before advancing, and after the finale asserts that the final age equals the morning age minus the score divided by one hundred and floored at ten, with a floor of eighteen.\n\nThe test must prove the rowboat ending is reachable. If the idle morning check yields an age outside forty-one to fifty, the assertion never fires and the gap remains unproven. A deterministic strategy is needed so the formula code path is actually exercised.\n\nThe test will fail with a clear message showing the recorded morning age and score so the strategy can be adjusted. If the finale score is below five hundred, the big stand bot will be improved. Cheats and \"Give minutes\" are ruled out as age sources. A focused unit test will play the finale directly while setting the morning age through an influencable check, and only assign the age if the panel summary explicitly permits it.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0efd7a37-5b02-4b3b-ad6d-7e65c8adefdd-56","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs","offset":396,"limit":110}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0efd7a37-5b02-4b3b-ad6d-7e65c8adefdd-57","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"tag = \\\"reveal\\\"","glob":"**/script.toml"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0efd7a37-5b02-4b3b-ad6d-7e65c8adefdd-58","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn game_post|fn play_pre","glob":"**/sim.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0efd7a37-5b02-4b3b-ad6d-7e65c8adefdd-59","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/notes/decisions.md","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5053,"output_tokens":9870,"cache_read_input_tokens":113024,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"93459518-9f3b-4157-9676-6ed5e25644de"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0efd7a37-5b02-4b3b-ad6d-7e65c8adefdd-56","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"396→pub fn bot(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    if act.lock > 0.0 {\\n        return (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), 0);\\n    }\\n400→    match act.kind {\\n        EventId::Check => bot_check(act, bal, rules),\\n        EventId::Breath => {\\n            let up = act.guide + 0.02 > act.lungs;\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), if up { buttons::CONFIRM } else { 0 })\\n        }\\n        EventId::Pose => {\\n            let c = ring_center(act.t);\\n            (pd(bal, rules, c), 0)\\n        }\\n410→        EventId::Squat => {\\n            let down = squat_guide(act.t) > act.depth;\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), if down { buttons::CONFIRM } else { 0 })\\n        }\\n        EventId::Plank => (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), buttons::STEP_L | buttons::STEP_R),\\n        EventId::Step => bot_step(act),\\n        EventId::Floatie => bot_floatie(act),\\n        EventId::Lap => bot_lap(act),\\n        EventId::Tide => bot_tide(act, bal, rules),\\n        EventId::Paddle => bot_paddle(act),\\n420→        EventId::Tray => (Vec2::new(tray_counter(act), 0.0), 0),\\n        EventId::Cannon => bot_cannon(act),\\n        EventId::BigStand => bot_big(act, bal, rules),\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_check(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    match act.phase {\\n        1 => {\\n            let targets = [-0.70, 0.55, 0.0];\\n430→            let x = targets.get(act.target_i as usize).copied().unwrap_or(0.0);\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::new(x, 0.0)), 0)\\n        }\\n        3 => {\\n            let beat = 0.6;\\n            let i = (act.sub / beat).floor();\\n            let at = i * beat;\\n            let side = if (i as i32) % 2 == 0 { buttons::STEP_L } else { buttons::STEP_R };\\n            let press = (act.sub - at).abs() <= 1.0 / 60.0 + 0.002 && i < 8.0 && i >= 0.0;\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), if press { side } else { 0 })\\n440→        }\\n        _ => (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), 0),\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_step(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let Some(n) = act.notes.get(act.note_i as usize) else { return (Vec2::ZERO, 0) };\\n    // A note can fall halfway between ticks. One frame is still inside the perfect window.\\n    if (act.t - n[0]).abs() > 1.0 / 60.0 + 0.002 {\\n        return (Vec2::ZERO, 0);\\n450→    }\\n    let lane = n[1] as u8;\\n    let b = if lane == 2 { buttons::STEP_L | buttons::STEP_R } else if lane == 0 { buttons::STEP_L } else { buttons::STEP_R };\\n    (Vec2::ZERO, b)\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_floatie(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let w = 7.5 * act.dir;\\n    let lean = Vec2::new((w * act.t).cos(), (w * act.t).sin()) * 0.75;\\n    let catches = [6.0, 13.0, 20.0, 27.0, 34.0, 41.0, 48.0];\\n460→    let mut b = 0;\\n    if let Some(t) = catches.get(act.catch_i as usize) {\\n        if (act.t - t).abs() < 0.02 {\\n            b = if act.catch_i % 2 == 0 { buttons::STEP_L } else { buttons::STEP_R };\\n        }\\n    }\\n    (lean, b)\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_lap(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n470→    let interval = 0.5;\\n    let i = (act.t / interval).floor();\\n    let at = i * interval;\\n    let press = (act.t - at).abs() < 0.02 && i >= 1.0;\\n    let side = if (i as i32) % 2 == 0 { buttons::STEP_L } else { buttons::STEP_R };\\n    let ribbon_x = ribbon_at(act.t);\\n    let lean_x = (ribbon_x - act.lateral).clamp(-1.0, 1.0);\\n    (Vec2::new(lean_x, 0.0), if press { side } else { 0 })\\n}\\n\\n480→fn ribbon_at(t: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let spots = [8.0_f32, 22.0, 40.0, 58.0, 75.0];\\n    let xs = [0.6, -0.7, 0.8, -0.5, 0.4];\\n    for (i, s) in spots.iter().enumerate() {\\n        if (t - s).abs() < 1.2 {\\n            return xs[i];\\n        }\\n    }\\n    0.0\\n}\\n490→\\nfn bot_tide(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let shell = act.shells.iter().find(|s| !s.pot);\\n    let pool = act.pools.first().copied().unwrap_or([0.0, 0.0]);\\n    let Some(s) = shell else { return (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), 0) };\\n    let to = Vec2::new(pool[0] - s.x, pool[1] - s.z);\\n    let want = to.normalize_or_zero() * 0.85;\\n    (want, 0)\\n}\\n\\n500→fn bot_paddle(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let gate_x = act.gates.get(act.gate_i as usize).map(|g| g[1]).unwrap_or(0.0);\\n    let steer = (gate_x - act.px).clamp(-1.0, 1.0);\\n    (Vec2::new(steer, 0.5), 0)\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"396→pub fn bot(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    if act.lock > 0.0 {\\n        return (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), 0);\\n    }\\n400→    match act.kind {\\n        EventId::Check => bot_check(act, bal, rules),\\n        EventId::Breath => {\\n            let up = act.guide + 0.02 > act.lungs;\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), if up { buttons::CONFIRM } else { 0 })\\n        }\\n        EventId::Pose => {\\n            let c = ring_center(act.t);\\n            (pd(bal, rules, c), 0)\\n        }\\n410→        EventId::Squat => {\\n            let down = squat_guide(act.t) > act.depth;\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), if down { buttons::CONFIRM } else { 0 })\\n        }\\n        EventId::Plank => (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), buttons::STEP_L | buttons::STEP_R),\\n        EventId::Step => bot_step(act),\\n        EventId::Floatie => bot_floatie(act),\\n        EventId::Lap => bot_lap(act),\\n        EventId::Tide => bot_tide(act, bal, rules),\\n        EventId::Paddle => bot_paddle(act),\\n420→        EventId::Tray => (Vec2::new(tray_counter(act), 0.0), 0),\\n        EventId::Cannon => bot_cannon(act),\\n        EventId::BigStand => bot_big(act, bal, rules),\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_check(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    match act.phase {\\n        1 => {\\n            let targets = [-0.70, 0.55, 0.0];\\n430→            let x = targets.get(act.target_i as usize).copied().unwrap_or(0.0);\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::new(x, 0.0)), 0)\\n        }\\n        3 => {\\n            let beat = 0.6;\\n            let i = (act.sub / beat).floor();\\n            let at = i * beat;\\n            let side = if (i as i32) % 2 == 0 { buttons::STEP_L } else { buttons::STEP_R };\\n            let press = (act.sub - at).abs() <= 1.0 / 60.0 + 0.002 && i < 8.0 && i >= 0.0;\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), if press { side } else { 0 })\\n440→        }\\n        _ => (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), 0),\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_step(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let Some(n) = act.notes.get(act.note_i as usize) else { return (Vec2::ZERO, 0) };\\n    // A note can fall halfway between ticks. One frame is still inside the perfect window.\\n    if (act.t - n[0]).abs() > 1.0 / 60.0 + 0.002 {\\n        return (Vec2::ZERO, 0);\\n450→    }\\n    let lane = n[1] as u8;\\n    let b = if lane == 2 { buttons::STEP_L | buttons::STEP_R } else if lane == 0 { buttons::STEP_L } else { buttons::STEP_R };\\n    (Vec2::ZERO, b)\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_floatie(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let w = 7.5 * act.dir;\\n    let lean = Vec2::new((w * act.t).cos(), (w * act.t).sin()) * 0.75;\\n    let catches = [6.0, 13.0, 20.0, 27.0, 34.0, 41.0, 48.0];\\n460→    let mut b = 0;\\n    if let Some(t) = catches.get(act.catch_i as usize) {\\n        if (act.t - t).abs() < 0.02 {\\n            b = if act.catch_i % 2 == 0 { buttons::STEP_L } else { buttons::STEP_R };\\n        }\\n    }\\n    (lean, b)\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_lap(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n470→    let interval = 0.5;\\n    let i = (act.t / interval).floor();\\n    let at = i * interval;\\n    let press = (act.t - at).abs() < 0.02 && i >= 1.0;\\n    let side = if (i as i32) % 2 == 0 { buttons::STEP_L } else { buttons::STEP_R };\\n    let ribbon_x = ribbon_at(act.t);\\n    let lean_x = (ribbon_x - act.lateral).clamp(-1.0, 1.0);\\n    (Vec2::new(lean_x, 0.0), if press { side } else { 0 })\\n}\\n\\n480→fn ribbon_at(t: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let spots = [8.0_f32, 22.0, 40.0, 58.0, 75.0];\\n    let xs = [0.6, -0.7, 0.8, -0.5, 0.4];\\n    for (i, s) in spots.iter().enumerate() {\\n        if (t - s).abs() < 1.2 {\\n            return xs[i];\\n        }\\n    }\\n    0.0\\n}\\n490→\\nfn bot_tide(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let shell = act.shells.iter().find(|s| !s.pot);\\n    let pool = act.pools.first().copied().unwrap_or([0.0, 0.0]);\\n    let Some(s) = shell else { return (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), 0) };\\n    let to = Vec2::new(pool[0] - s.x, pool[1] - s.z);\\n    let want = to.normalize_or_zero() * 0.85;\\n    (want, 0)\\n}\\n\\n500→fn bot_paddle(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let gate_x = act.gates.get(act.gate_i as usize).map(|g| g[1]).unwrap_or(0.0);\\n    let steer = (gate_x - act.px).clamp(-1.0, 1.0);\\n    (Vec2::new(steer, 0.5), 0)\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs\",\"offset\":396,\"limit\":110,\"raw_output\":\"pub fn bot(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    if act.lock > 0.0 {\\n        return (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), 0);\\n    }\\n    match act.kind {\\n        EventId::Check => bot_check(act, bal, rules),\\n        EventId::Breath => {\\n            let up = act.guide + 0.02 > act.lungs;\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), if up { buttons::CONFIRM } else { 0 })\\n        }\\n        EventId::Pose => {\\n            let c = ring_center(act.t);\\n            (pd(bal, rules, c), 0)\\n        }\\n        EventId::Squat => {\\n            let down = squat_guide(act.t) > act.depth;\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), if down { buttons::CONFIRM } else { 0 })\\n        }\\n        EventId::Plank => (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), buttons::STEP_L | buttons::STEP_R),\\n        EventId::Step => bot_step(act),\\n        EventId::Floatie => bot_floatie(act),\\n        EventId::Lap => bot_lap(act),\\n        EventId::Tide => bot_tide(act, bal, rules),\\n        EventId::Paddle => bot_paddle(act),\\n        EventId::Tray => (Vec2::new(tray_counter(act), 0.0), 0),\\n        EventId::Cannon => bot_cannon(act),\\n        EventId::BigStand => bot_big(act, bal, rules),\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_check(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    match act.phase {\\n        1 => {\\n            let targets = [-0.70, 0.55, 0.0];\\n            let x = targets.get(act.target_i as usize).copied().unwrap_or(0.0);\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::new(x, 0.0)), 0)\\n        }\\n        3 => {\\n            let beat = 0.6;\\n            let i = (act.sub / beat).floor();\\n            let at = i * beat;\\n            let side = if (i as i32) % 2 == 0 { buttons::STEP_L } else { buttons::STEP_R };\\n            let press = (act.sub - at).abs() <= 1.0 / 60.0 + 0.002 && i < 8.0 && i >= 0.0;\\n            (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), if press { side } else { 0 })\\n        }\\n        _ => (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), 0),\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_step(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let Some(n) = act.notes.get(act.note_i as usize) else { return (Vec2::ZERO, 0) };\\n    // A note can fall halfway between ticks. One frame is still inside the perfect window.\\n    if (act.t - n[0]).abs() > 1.0 / 60.0 + 0.002 {\\n        return (Vec2::ZERO, 0);\\n    }\\n    let lane = n[1] as u8;\\n    let b = if lane == 2 { buttons::STEP_L | buttons::STEP_R } else if lane == 0 { buttons::STEP_L } else { buttons::STEP_R };\\n    (Vec2::ZERO, b)\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_floatie(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let w = 7.5 * act.dir;\\n    let lean = Vec2::new((w * act.t).cos(), (w * act.t).sin()) * 0.75;\\n    let catches = [6.0, 13.0, 20.0, 27.0, 34.0, 41.0, 48.0];\\n    let mut b = 0;\\n    if let Some(t) = catches.get(act.catch_i as usize) {\\n        if (act.t - t).abs() < 0.02 {\\n            b = if act.catch_i % 2 == 0 { buttons::STEP_L } else { buttons::STEP_R };\\n        }\\n    }\\n    (lean, b)\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_lap(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let interval = 0.5;\\n    let i = (act.t / interval).floor();\\n    let at = i * interval;\\n    let press = (act.t - at).abs() < 0.02 && i >= 1.0;\\n    let side = if (i as i32) % 2 == 0 { buttons::STEP_L } else { buttons::STEP_R };\\n    let ribbon_x = ribbon_at(act.t);\\n    let lean_x = (ribbon_x - act.lateral).clamp(-1.0, 1.0);\\n    (Vec2::new(lean_x, 0.0), if press { side } else { 0 })\\n}\\n\\nfn ribbon_at(t: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let spots = [8.0_f32, 22.0, 40.0, 58.0, 75.0];\\n    let xs = [0.6, -0.7, 0.8, -0.5, 0.4];\\n    for (i, s) in spots.iter().enumerate() {\\n        if (t - s).abs() < 1.2 {\\n            return xs[i];\\n        }\\n    }\\n    0.0\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_tide(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let shell = act.shells.iter().find(|s| !s.pot);\\n    let pool = act.pools.first().copied().unwrap_or([0.0, 0.0]);\\n    let Some(s) = shell else { return (pd(bal, rules, Vec2::ZERO), 0) };\\n    let to = Vec2::new(pool[0] - s.x, pool[1] - s.z);\\n    let want = to.normalize_or_zero() * 0.85;\\n    (want, 0)\\n}\\n\\nfn bot_paddle(act: &Activity) -> (Vec2, u32) {\\n    let gate_x = act.gates.get(act.gate_i as usize).map(|g| g[1]).unwrap_or(0.0);\\n    let steer = (gate_x - act.px).clamp(-1.0, 1.0);\\n    (Vec2::new(steer, 0.5), 0)\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":1255}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0efd7a37-5b02-4b3b-ad6d-7e65c8adefdd-57","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,103,97,109,101,115,47,102,105,116,47,115,99,114,105,112,116,46,116,111,109,108,10,56,57,58,116,97,103,32,61,32,34,114,101,118,101,97,108,34,10,57,52,58,116,97,103,32,61,32,34,114,101,118,101,97,108,34,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/script.toml\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":89,\"content\":\"tag = \\\"reveal\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":94,\"content\":\"tag = \\\"reveal\\\"\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0efd7a37-5b02-4b3b-ad6d-7e65c8adefdd-58","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0efd7a37-5b02-4b3b-ad6d-7e65c8adefdd-59","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→- Last input device wins. Touch does not leave attract and does not count as a real controller.\\n- Hub ghosts are drawn in the view from `window.__hub.ghosts`. The sim only publishes its own sample, so a session stays deterministic.\\n- Long tests set `history_seconds` to 0. A normal boot keeps 8 seconds of rewind.\\n- About text comes from `#about-data` when the page sets it. Native runs keep a readable fallback with the same headings.\\n- The name, look and outfit menus show the first six entries. The rest stay in `script.toml`.\\n- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6. That is the sim's song map.\\n- On a splash round the page calls `AIHub.ready()` when connect resolves. Waiting for `__gameStatus` left the fourth software-WebGPU copy past the harness's 20s ready gate. A later `ready()` is a no-op.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→- Last input device wins. Touch does not leave attract and does not count as a real controller.\\n- Hub ghosts are drawn in the view from `window.__hub.ghosts`. The sim only publishes its own sample, so a session stays deterministic.\\n- Long tests set `history_seconds` to 0. A normal boot keeps 8 seconds of rewind.\\n- About text comes from `#about-data` when the page sets it. Native runs keep a readable fallback with the same headings.\\n- The name, look and outfit menus show the first six entries. The rest stay in `script.toml`.\\n- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6. That is the sim's song map.\\n- On a splash round the page calls `AIHub.ready()` when connect resolves. Waiting for `__gameStatus` left the fourth software-WebGPU copy past the harness's 20s ready gate. A later `ready()` is a no-op.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/notes/decisions.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"- Last input device wins. Touch does not leave attract and does not count as a real controller.\\n- Hub ghosts are drawn in the view from `window.__hub.ghosts`. The sim only publishes its own sample, so a session stays deterministic.\\n- Long tests set `history_seconds` to 0. A normal boot keeps 8 seconds of rewind.\\n- About text comes from `#about-data` when the page sets it. Native runs keep a readable fallback with the same headings.\\n- The name, look and outfit menus show the first six entries. The rest stay in `script.toml`.\\n- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6. That is the sim's song map.\\n- On a splash round the page calls `AIHub.ready()` when connect resolves. Waiting for `__gameStatus` left the fourth software-WebGPU copy past the harness's 20s ready gate. A later `ready()` is a no-op.\\n\",\"total_lines\":7}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"8a11b3c8-b589-4829-ab6a-90e8d22f8ed8"}
