{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-809a825e-1b54-4972-a28f-98a108931741-68","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"687→            for (btn, action) in layout {\\n                if is(*btn) {\\n                    held |= action;\\n690→                }\\n            }\\n            if self.fit {\\n                if st.lt2 {\\n                    held |= buttons::STEP_L;\\n                }\\n                if st.rt2 {\\n                    held |= buttons::STEP_R;\\n                }\\n                if is(Button::Start) && !is(Button::Mode) {\\n700→                    held |= buttons::PAUSE;\\n                }\\n            } else {\\n                if st.rt2 {\\n                    held |= if self.game { buttons::SKILL6 } else { buttons::USE };\\n                }\\n                if st.lt2 {\\n                    held |= buttons::FOCUS;\\n                }\\n            }\\n710→            pad.held = held;\\n            pad.rotate = if self.game || self.fit { 0.0 } else { (is(Button::RightTrigger) as i32 - is(Button::LeftTrigger) as i32) as f32 };\\n            // In the game the D-pad is potion / use / map / panels, not zoom.\\n            pad.zoom = if self.game || self.fit { 0.0 } else { (is(Button::DPadDown) as i32 - is(Button::DPadUp) as i32) as f32 };\\n            pad.a_held = is(Button::South);\\n            pad.x_held = is(Button::West);\\n            pad.y_held = is(Button::North);\\n            pad.back_held = is(Button::Select);\\n            if pad.left.length() > 0.3 || pad.right.length() > 0.3 || held != 0 {\\n                pad.any_activity = true;\\n720→            }\\n        }\\n        if pad.any_activity {\\n            self.last_device = Device::Gamepad;\\n            self.seen_real = true;\\n        }\\n        self.pad = pad;\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Screen-space movement (x right, y up) from keys and stick, length <= 1.\\n730→    pub fn move_axis(&self) -> Vec2 {\\n        let k = |codes: &[KeyCode]| codes.iter().any(|c| self.keys.contains(c)) as i32 as f32;\\n        let b = &self.bindings;\\n        let kb = Vec2::new(k(&b.right) - k(&b.left), k(&b.up) - k(&b.down));\\n        let v = if kb != Vec2::ZERO { kb.normalize() } else { self.pad.left };\\n        v.clamp_length_max(1.0)\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Held game buttons from all devices.\\n    pub fn held(&self) -> u32 {\\n740→        let mut b = self.pad.held;\\n        for (bit, codes) in &self.bindings.buttons {\\n            if codes.iter().any(|c| self.keys.contains(c)) {\\n                b |= bit;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.mouse.contains(&MouseButton::Left) {\\n            b |= buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\\n        if self.game && self.mouse.contains(&MouseButton::Right) {\\n750→            b |= buttons::SECONDARY;\\n        }\\n        b\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Returns (held, newly pressed since the last call).\\n    pub fn buttons(&mut self) -> (u32, u32) {\\n        let held = self.held();\\n        let mut pressed = held & !self.prev_held;\\n        for (bit, codes) in &self.bindings.buttons {\\n760→            if codes.iter().any(|c| self.key_taps.contains(c)) {\\n                pressed |= bit;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.mouse_taps.contains(&MouseButton::Left) {\\n            pressed |= buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\",\"content_concise\":\"687→            for (btn, action) in layout {\\n                if is(*btn) {\\n                    held |= action;\\n690→                }\\n            }\\n            if self.fit {\\n                if st.lt2 {\\n                    held |= buttons::STEP_L;\\n                }\\n                if st.rt2 {\\n                    held |= buttons::STEP_R;\\n                }\\n                if is(Button::Start) && !is(Button::Mode) {\\n700→                    held |= buttons::PAUSE;\\n                }\\n            } else {\\n                if st.rt2 {\\n                    held |= if self.game { buttons::SKILL6 } else { buttons::USE };\\n                }\\n                if st.lt2 {\\n                    held |= buttons::FOCUS;\\n                }\\n            }\\n710→            pad.held = held;\\n            pad.rotate = if self.game || self.fit { 0.0 } else { (is(Button::RightTrigger) as i32 - is(Button::LeftTrigger) as i32) as f32 };\\n            // In the game the D-pad is potion / use / map / panels, not zoom.\\n            pad.zoom = if self.game || self.fit { 0.0 } else { (is(Button::DPadDown) as i32 - is(Button::DPadUp) as i32) as f32 };\\n            pad.a_held = is(Button::South);\\n            pad.x_held = is(Button::West);\\n            pad.y_held = is(Button::North);\\n            pad.back_held = is(Button::Select);\\n            if pad.left.length() > 0.3 || pad.right.length() > 0.3 || held != 0 {\\n                pad.any_activity = true;\\n720→            }\\n        }\\n        if pad.any_activity {\\n            self.last_device = Device::Gamepad;\\n            self.seen_real = true;\\n        }\\n        self.pad = pad;\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Screen-space movement (x right, y up) from keys and stick, length <= 1.\\n730→    pub fn move_axis(&self) -> Vec2 {\\n        let k = |codes: &[KeyCode]| codes.iter().any(|c| self.keys.contains(c)) as i32 as f32;\\n        let b = &self.bindings;\\n        let kb = Vec2::new(k(&b.right) - k(&b.left), k(&b.up) - k(&b.down));\\n        let v = if kb != Vec2::ZERO { kb.normalize() } else { self.pad.left };\\n        v.clamp_length_max(1.0)\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Held game buttons from all devices.\\n    pub fn held(&self) -> u32 {\\n740→        let mut b = self.pad.held;\\n        for (bit, codes) in &self.bindings.buttons {\\n            if codes.iter().any(|c| self.keys.contains(c)) {\\n                b |= bit;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.mouse.contains(&MouseButton::Left) {\\n            b |= buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\\n        if self.game && self.mouse.contains(&MouseButton::Right) {\\n750→            b |= buttons::SECONDARY;\\n        }\\n        b\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Returns (held, newly pressed since the last call).\\n    pub fn buttons(&mut self) -> (u32, u32) {\\n        let held = self.held();\\n        let mut pressed = held & !self.prev_held;\\n        for (bit, codes) in &self.bindings.buttons {\\n760→            if codes.iter().any(|c| self.key_taps.contains(c)) {\\n                pressed |= bit;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.mouse_taps.contains(&MouseButton::Left) {\\n            pressed |= buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/input.rs\",\"offset\":687,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"            for (btn, action) in layout {\\n                if is(*btn) {\\n                    held |= action;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if self.fit {\\n                if st.lt2 {\\n                    held |= buttons::STEP_L;\\n                }\\n                if st.rt2 {\\n                    held |= buttons::STEP_R;\\n                }\\n                if is(Button::Start) && !is(Button::Mode) {\\n                    held |= buttons::PAUSE;\\n                }\\n            } else {\\n                if st.rt2 {\\n                    held |= if self.game { buttons::SKILL6 } else { buttons::USE };\\n                }\\n                if st.lt2 {\\n                    held |= buttons::FOCUS;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            pad.held = held;\\n            pad.rotate = if self.game || self.fit { 0.0 } else { (is(Button::RightTrigger) as i32 - is(Button::LeftTrigger) as i32) as f32 };\\n            // In the game the D-pad is potion / use / map / panels, not zoom.\\n            pad.zoom = if self.game || self.fit { 0.0 } else { (is(Button::DPadDown) as i32 - is(Button::DPadUp) as i32) as f32 };\\n            pad.a_held = is(Button::South);\\n            pad.x_held = is(Button::West);\\n            pad.y_held = is(Button::North);\\n            pad.back_held = is(Button::Select);\\n            if pad.left.length() > 0.3 || pad.right.length() > 0.3 || held != 0 {\\n                pad.any_activity = true;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if pad.any_activity {\\n            self.last_device = Device::Gamepad;\\n            self.seen_real = true;\\n        }\\n        self.pad = pad;\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Screen-space movement (x right, y up) from keys and stick, length <= 1.\\n    pub fn move_axis(&self) -> Vec2 {\\n        let k = |codes: &[KeyCode]| codes.iter().any(|c| self.keys.contains(c)) as i32 as f32;\\n        let b = &self.bindings;\\n        let kb = Vec2::new(k(&b.right) - k(&b.left), k(&b.up) - k(&b.down));\\n        let v = if kb != Vec2::ZERO { kb.normalize() } else { self.pad.left };\\n        v.clamp_length_max(1.0)\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Held game buttons from all devices.\\n    pub fn held(&self) -> u32 {\\n        let mut b = self.pad.held;\\n        for (bit, codes) in &self.bindings.buttons {\\n            if codes.iter().any(|c| self.keys.contains(c)) {\\n                b |= bit;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.mouse.contains(&MouseButton::Left) {\\n            b |= buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\\n        if self.game && self.mouse.contains(&MouseButton::Right) {\\n            b |= buttons::SECONDARY;\\n        }\\n        b\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Returns (held, newly pressed since the last call).\\n    pub fn buttons(&mut self) -> (u32, u32) {\\n        let held = self.held();\\n        let mut pressed = held & !self.prev_held;\\n        for (bit, codes) in &self.bindings.buttons {\\n            if codes.iter().any(|c| self.key_taps.contains(c)) {\\n                pressed |= bit;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.mouse_taps.contains(&MouseButton::Left) {\\n            pressed |= buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\\n\",\"total_lines\":803}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"a8dd9c07-7605-49eb-b839-dbdd3b0a6907"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_793","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"L1 and R1 are STEP. L2 and R2 are STEP when fit.\n\nShoulders are steps, not tabs. The keyboard ] key acts as TAB_R. Tests press the bit directly, so the pad map will stay unchanged unless paging is impossible. STEP_L and STEP_R will page paged menus on the pad when no event is active. During events they remain for gameplay.\n\nSTEP will be aliased to TAB in menu_flow only. This won't conflict with existing tests or gameplay.\n\nPaging is required for the dev menu's jump list. The pad paging wiring will be implemented. A skip_dialogue flag will let confirm skip entire conversations immediately. The win this event logic is being drafted.\n\nWinning an event awards 1000 points and three stars. Losing awards zero points and zero stars. Autoplay mode will replace player input with bot-generated lean and button states during events or checks.\n\nAutoplay will run after the input lean is assigned in pre(). The no_tips cheat adds a boolean field to activities and suppresses tip increments while clearing any active lock. Give minutes adds five minutes, unlock all enables free play, and all stars adds nine total stars. A dev_tab field with serde default is also being added.\n\nNew cheat fields are being added to the activity struct: no_tips, auto, skip_lines, and step_once. A mats vector and morning_age field are also being considered. The FitGame struct lacks a serde default on its derive, so adding new fields without defaults would break deserialization of old save data.\n\nEach new field will carry #[serde(default)] to preserve compatibility with old save data. The no_tips field must also be initialized in the activity struct literal inside start().\n\nThe time menu will offer five options: 0.25x, 1x, 2x, 4x, pause clock, and single step. Confirming a speed sets time_scale while keeping the menu open. Single step pauses the clock and triggers one tick via step_once.\n\nThe jump menu will list every event title with IDs starting at 220, plus two extra entries for Pose gusts and Step window.\n\nThe jump menu now includes Brace, Long stillness, Attract, Medley, and Island. Day entries occupy IDs 247 through 251. The menu will page four items at a time with a Back option.\n\nThe jump menu's page_slice helper now appends a Back entry to each page. The jump_to handler routes event IDs 220 through 239 to their corresponding EventId, switching the run mode from Demo to Story when needed.\n\nThe jump_to handler now starts the selected activity and sets the flow to Event or Check. It resets focus to zero. The handler also begins BigStand activities for Pose gusts through Step window.\n\nPose gusts through Step window map to phases 1 through 4. Their activity sub is reset to zero and done is false. The flow becomes Event.\n\nAttract jumps directly into the attract sequence.\n\nMedley mode starts with hub_mode disabled. It resets the medley index and launches the Paddle event.\n\nIsland jumps set flow to Island and switch run from Demo to Story. Day jumps set the day index, clear today_played, reset day_minutes, and also switch run from Demo to Story.\n\nThe prompt test will jump to Long stillness, then step until the activity sub reaches 15 seconds. The test must not set the phase directly because the jump menu controls it. The developer is now figuring out how to navigate the jump menu in tests.\n\nThe jump menu will be navigated by known positions rather than labels. The developer mapped the full six-page list: Check, Breath, Pose, Squat; Plank, Step, Floatie, Lap; Tide, Paddle, Tray, Cannon; BigStand, Pose gusts, Step window, Brace; Long stillness, Attract, Medley, Island; Day 1 through Day 4; and Day 5. Long stillness is page four, index zero.\n\nThe jump menu will be reached by pressing TAB_R four times from the dev root, then confirming. The free-play schedule lists twelve events; the developer mapped the Cannonball entry on page two. The cheats menu has eight items and must be split into two pages. The time menu also has seven entries, so it will be paginated to fit within six rows.\n\nThe time menu will be split into two pages. Page zero holds the four speed options plus Pause and Back. Page one holds Single step and Back.\n\nThe tuning menu will list parameters in groups of four with a Back option, plus a reachable Reset feel entry.\n\nReset feel will appear on every tuning page so the menu stays within six rows. The tuning_items helper paginates parameters in groups of four and assigns IDs starting at 300.\n\nThe slider test can confirm Reset feel without leaving the tuning menu. Focus remains on stiffness after MENU_RIGHT, so the test must move down four times to reach Reset feel. Alternatively it can return to root page one where Reset feel also lives.\n\nReset feel will be placed on both the root page and every tuning page. A new \"Reset page\" option is being considered to restore only the four visible parameters on the current tuning group.\n\nReset feel will restore all rules. It will appear on every tuning page and the dev root page. The developer rejected a per-group reset idea.\n\nThe developer settled on a per-group reset for tuning. Each page will include a \"Reset these\" option that restores only the four visible sliders, while the root page keeps a separate \"Reset feel\" entry to restore all rules. This satisfies both \"per group and all\". A `reset_tuning_page` helper is being drafted to apply default values to the current page's parameters.\n\nThe `reset_tuning_page` helper is now complete. It restores default values for the four visible sliders on the current tuning page. The reset-page action ID is 61, distinct from the all-rules reset at 60.\n\nThe wardrobe menu will list seven gear items and eight outfits, totaling sixteen entries. Six items per page would be needed to fit them.\n\nThe wardrobe menu will hold seven gear items and reuse the existing outfit IDs from 520 onward. It will be paginated to fit five gear entries plus a Back option on each page.\n\nThe wardrobe menu will be paginated five items per page, with a Back option. A `wear` helper is being drafted to apply gear and outfit selections by ID, setting the corresponding fields on `sim.config.puppet.gear`.\n\nThe `wear` helper is now complete. It maps each gear ID to its corresponding puppet field and color, and outfit IDs 520 through 529 set the active outfit index. After a selection it returns to the previous flow and resets focus to zero. HelmKind still needs to be imported. A test will open the wardrobe from the dev menu, confirm Sun cap, and assert the helm is Cap.\n\nThe calendar menu will show five days. Each day is marked stamped if the player has completed it or collected its stamp, and open otherwise.\n\nThe calendar menu will list five days with IDs 270 through 274, each labeled \"Day X · open\" or \"Day X · stamped\". A Back option completes the six-row layout. Tests will verify that a day item contains the text \"Day\".\n\nA generic `paged` helper is being drafted to paginate name lists into fixed-size pages.\n\nThe `paged` helper is now complete. It wraps the page index and maps each entry to a unique ID starting from `id0`.\n\nName lists will span seven pages, outfit lists two, and look lists one. Entering any of these menus resets the current page to zero.\n\nEyes-closed lines must dim the banner, hide the score, and apply puck and tone effects. The Big Stand song switches to track 0 once the phase reaches four, and it updates every tick during events rather than only in menus.\n\nA `long_stillness` helper will keep the puck visible during stillness. The `apply_body` function is being drafted to set the character's tilt angles from the balance center of mass and select a pose clip.\n\nThe `apply_body` function now sets the character's animation clip, resets its timer and flags, and locks the weight and speed to one. The `pose_clip` helper returns a pose animation only when the current flow is Event, Check, Attract, Countdown, or Card; otherwise it returns zero. For Pose events, it selects \"FIT/Tree\" for index 0, \"FIT/Warrior\" for index 1, and \"FIT/Fold\" for any other index.\n\nThe `pose_clip` helper now maps Squat to \"FIT/Squat\", Plank to \"FIT/Plank\", Breath to \"FIT/Bloom\", Lap to \"MESH2MOTION/Jog\", and Big Stand to \"FIT/Bloom\" at phase zero, \"FIT/Plank\" at phase three, and a phase-one pose at phase one. It returns zero for any unrecognized event. The developer also noted that `apply_body` does not run while the simulation is frozen.\n\n`apply_body` runs in `post` after the character tick, so it sets the pose clip before the next frame. If the default idle clip is empty, the character tick will not overwrite it. The first event frame therefore shows a non-zero clip immediately. Pose parade capture will step the simulation and render.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1cb89b4d-0891-45d0-a01d-b1119f786086-69","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/anim/mesh2motion.json","limit":5}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1cb89b4d-0891-45d0-a01d-b1119f786086-70","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"idle_clip","glob":"**/puppet.rs","head_limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1cb89b4d-0891-45d0-a01d-b1119f786086-71","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs","offset":380,"limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1cb89b4d-0891-45d0-a01d-b1119f786086-72","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub puppet","glob":"**/sim.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1158,"output_tokens":6103,"cache_read_input_tokens":135680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"7f8e3d72-f7ca-4513-853b-c4923c8de001"}
