:fit_ui(self, sim)\\n    }\\n    fn tint(&self, id: EntityId) -> Option<([f32; 3], f32)> {\\n        Game::tint(self, id)\\n    }\\n    fn as_any(&self) -> &dyn Any {\\n        self\\n    }\\n280→    fn as_any_mut(&mut self) -> &mut dyn Any {\\n        self\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Sim {\\n    /// The running game from [`GAMES`], if this scene is one.\\n    pub fn play(&self) -> Option<&GameBox> {\\n        self.state.play.as_ref()\\n    }\\n290→\\n    /// The running game's outcome (`Playing` when there is none).\\n    pub fn outcome(&self) -> Outcome {\\n        self.play().map(|g| g.outcome()).unwrap_or_default()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The running game's bot input (none without a game).\\n    pub fn bot_input(&self) -> InputFrame {\\n        self.play().map(|g| g.bot(self)).unwrap_or_default()\\n    }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/mod.rs\",\"offset\":270,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"    }\\n    fn fit_ui(&self, sim: &Sim) -> Option<crate::fit_ui::FitUi> {\\n        Game::fit_ui(self, sim)\\n    }\\n    fn tint(&self, id: EntityId) -> Option<([f32; 3], f32)> {\\n        Game::tint(self, id)\\n    }\\n    fn as_any(&self) -> &dyn Any {\\n        self\\n    }\\n    fn as_any_mut(&mut self) -> &mut dyn Any {\\n        self\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Sim {\\n    /// The running game from [`GAMES`], if this scene is one.\\n    pub fn play(&self) -> Option<&GameBox> {\\n        self.state.play.as_ref()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The running game's outcome (`Playing` when there is none).\\n    pub fn outcome(&self) -> Outcome {\\n        self.play().map(|g| g.outcome()).unwrap_or_default()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The running game's bot input (none without a game).\\n    pub fn bot_input(&self) -> InputFrame {\\n        self.play().map(|g| g.bot(self)).unwrap_or_default()\\n    }\\n\",\"total_lines\":331}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"dae49a17-a1b2-4206-acb5-ecc0cf9d67a8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_799","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking whether EntityMap implements the iter method.\n\nConfirmed Sim state is public. FitGame fresh() must explicitly set every field. New fields will be appended to structs with serde default and added to fresh(). The tick_check signature also needs updating.\n\nChecking for a second Activity literal. Menu page wrapping works correctly with modulo arithmetic. Entering a sub-tab resets the page to zero. The go_back handler clears the dev tab, page, and focus when exiting a dev sub-tab. Opening wardrobe from dev sets return_flow to Dev.\n\nWardrobe back navigation preserves the dev flow without resetting the dev tab. The activate handler for id 43 will be replaced with a broader match. Settings sliders will respond to menu left and right buttons.\n\nSlider nudging will adjust the focused item's normalized value by 0.1 in either direction, clamped between 0 and 1. This action is independent of confirmation and does not shift focus. A single-step mode will be inserted at the end of pre before drive_player.\n\nThe single-step logic advances world time by one frame. It ticks the currently running activity and finishes play if that activity completes. The flow returns to the state it was paused from.\n\nThe single-step logic is being simplified. A saved flow variable will replace the messy nested checks. The step will advance world time by one frame and tick the paused activity directly, keeping the Dev flow intact unless that activity finishes.\n\nThe single-step logic now applies the body after each tick. If the activity finishes, the flow returns to the paused state and play ends. Otherwise it restores the saved flow. The activity tick does not check flow itself. Setting the flow to the paused state before calling finish_play works correctly because that method transitions to Result. If the activity does not finish, the Dev flow remains active with time_scale unchanged.\n\nAutoplay must run after last_lean is set from input so it overrides. The attract flow already sets last_lean from the bot, and autoplay will overwrite it with the same value.\n\nThe cheat no-tips flag will be copied into the activity's no_tips field right after Activity::start.\n\nIsland mats will be stored as a vector of string keys and f32 coordinates in FitGame, with serde default.\n\nIsland mats will be arranged in a circle around the player at radius 3.4, with each mat type placed evenly spaced in a full rotation. In the Island flow, pressing Confirm will attempt to collect a mat via a new try_mat method.\n\ntry_mat checks the player's feet position against each island mat. It selects the nearest mat within 1.2 units and converts its key into an EventId.\n\ntry_mat now checks if the mat kind is allowed before starting the activity. It switches to the Card flow and resets its timer.\n\nhub.toml will gain small objects with body set to none to keep physics cheap. The room parser must tolerate unknown fields. Asset names for the objects are rowboat, park_bench, lamp_post, market_stall, round_table, and chair.\n\nThe hub.toml objects will be placed inside the walkable area using layout coordinates where x is column and z is row. Specific positions are chosen for the rowboat, bench, lamp, and stall to avoid the player cell.\n\nThe round table and chair are placed in the hub. A wobble mat, a lagoon mat, and a clam are added as decorative non-physics objects.\n\nA calendar board object is added to hub.toml. The first boot test will catch any asset loading failures. A compact fit.json file is being hand-keyed with pose data for standing and a tree pose.\n\nPose data for standing, tree, warrior, fold, and squat is being hand-keyed into fit.json.\n\nPose data for squat, plank, and bloom is being added to fit.json. Each pose will be stored as two keys so it becomes a clip with duration 2.0 and looping enabled.\n\nA small breathe motion will be added to the second pose key so the clip feels alive. The fit.json clip names are Tree, Warrior, Fold, Squat, Plank, and Bloom. A dim field will be added to FitUi with serde default. The painter dim will be placed right after painter creation so it covers the 3D view while UI text stays visible. Status fields including song will be added to the JSON.\n\nThe status JSON will include activity phase, subphase, time scale, outfit, and a clip ID read from the player entity. The tone value is taken from the Check activity's guide when it reaches phase two.\n\nA `long_still` helper will detect sustained stillness. The fit UI title becomes empty when still, otherwise it shows the normal title. Banner lines and footer will adapt to the still state. The desired song switches to BigStand after activity phase four. Play finish age is handled as designed. Name entry resets the page index.\n\nThe dev_items and screen_items sections will be rewritten. Cheat flags will be synced to the active activity at the start of each tick so mid-event changes take effect immediately.\n\nThe skip-dialogue logic for talk flows will loop through `talk_advance` while the flow remains in an intro or wake state, jumping to the final line each time. This bypasses intermediate lines and ends the conversation immediately.\n\nSetting line_i to the final index triggers the end path in talk_advance with a single call. A win or lose event during Dev flow correctly transitions to Result. World time will advance using scaled delta time so the pause clock resumes properly.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9eb28df3-252e-4cd6-badc-4f18837d1282-84","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"#\\[cfg\\(test\\)\\]","glob":"**/pav_app/src/input.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9eb28df3-252e-4cd6-badc-4f18837d1282-85","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs","offset":1893,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3251,"output_tokens":4447,"cache_read_input_tokens":145664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"a0072e7b-6b9b-422e-a99b-c24be49e434d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9eb28df3-252e-4cd6-badc-4f18837d1282-84","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,97,112,112,47,115,114,99,47,105,110,112,117,116,46,114,115,10,55,56,55,58,35,91,99,102,103,40,116,101,115,116,41,93,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/input.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":787,\"content\":\"#[cfg(test)]\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9eb28df3-252e-4cd6-badc-4f18837d1282-85","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1893→#[cfg(test)]\\nmod save_tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn save_round_trips_the_stay() {\\n        let mut g = FitGame::fresh();\\n1900→        g.day = 3;\\n        g.age = 22;\\n        g.stamps = 2;\\n        g.name = \\\"Kai\\\".into();\\n        g.settings.music = 0.25;\\n        let blob = g.export_save();\\n        g.day = 1;\\n        g.age = 80;\\n        g.settings.music = 0.10;\\n        assert!(g.import_save(&blob));\\n1910→        assert_eq!(g.day, 3);\\n        assert_eq!(g.age, 22);\\n        assert_eq!(g.stamps, 2);\\n        assert_eq!(g.name, \\\"Kai\\\");\\n        assert!((g.settings.music - 0.25).abs() < 1e-5);\\n        assert!(!g.import_save(\\\"{\\\"));\\n        assert!(!g.import_save(\\\"{\\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\":9,\\\\\\\"slots\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"settings\\\\\\\":{},\\\\\\\"last_day\\\\\\\":0}\\\"));\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n1920→    fn script_has_the_cast() {\\n        assert!(script_speaker_count(\\\"Pip\\\") >= 80, \\\"pip {}\\\", script_speaker_count(\\\"Pip\\\"));\\n        for s in [\\\"Posey\\\", \\\"Kettle\\\", \\\"Bounce\\\", \\\"Gull\\\"] {\\n            assert!(script_speaker_count(s) >= 25, \\\"{s} {}\\\", script_speaker_count(s));\\n        }\\n        assert!(script_title_count() >= 30);\\n        assert!(script_name_count() >= 40);\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1893→#[cfg(test)]\\nmod save_tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn save_round_trips_the_stay() {\\n        let mut g = FitGame::fresh();\\n1900→        g.day = 3;\\n        g.age = 22;\\n        g.stamps = 2;\\n        g.name = \\\"Kai\\\".into();\\n        g.settings.music = 0.25;\\n        let blob = g.export_save();\\n        g.day = 1;\\n        g.age = 80;\\n        g.settings.music = 0.10;\\n        assert!(g.import_save(&blob));\\n1910→        assert_eq!(g.day, 3);\\n        assert_eq!(g.age, 22);\\n        assert_eq!(g.stamps, 2);\\n        assert_eq!(g.name, \\\"Kai\\\");\\n        assert!((g.settings.music - 0.25).abs() < 1e-5);\\n        assert!(!g.import_save(\\\"{\\\"));\\n        assert!(!g.import_save(\\\"{\\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\":9,\\\\\\\"slots\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"settings\\\\\\\":{},\\\\\\\"last_day\\\\\\\":0}\\\"));\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n1920→    fn script_has_the_cast() {\\n        assert!(script_speaker_count(\\\"Pip\\\") >= 80, \\\"pip {}\\\", script_speaker_count(\\\"Pip\\\"));\\n        for s in [\\\"Posey\\\", \\\"Kettle\\\", \\\"Bounce\\\", \\\"Gull\\\"] {\\n            assert!(script_speaker_count(s) >= 25, \\\"{s} {}\\\", script_speaker_count(s));\\n        }\\n        assert!(script_title_count() >= 30);\\n        assert!(script_name_count() >= 40);\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs\",\"offset\":1893,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"#[cfg(test)]\\nmod save_tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn save_round_trips_the_stay() {\\n        let mut g = FitGame::fresh();\\n        g.day = 3;\\n        g.age = 22;\\n        g.stamps = 2;\\n        g.name = \\\"Kai\\\".into();\\n        g.settings.music = 0.25;\\n        let blob = g.export_save();\\n        g.day = 1;\\n        g.age = 80;\\n        g.settings.music = 0.10;\\n        assert!(g.import_save(&blob));\\n        assert_eq!(g.day, 3);\\n        assert_eq!(g.age, 22);\\n        assert_eq!(g.stamps, 2);\\n        assert_eq!(g.name, \\\"Kai\\\");\\n        assert!((g.settings.music - 0.25).abs() < 1e-5);\\n        assert!(!g.import_save(\\\"{\\\"));\\n        assert!(!g.import_save(\\\"{\\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\":9,\\\\\\\"slots\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"settings\\\\\\\":{},\\\\\\\"last_day\\\\\\\":0}\\\"));\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn script_has_the_cast() {\\n        assert!(script_speaker_count(\\\"Pip\\\") >= 80, \\\"pip {}\\\", script_speaker_count(\\\"Pip\\\"));\\n        for s in [\\\"Posey\\\", \\\"Kettle\\\", \\\"Bounce\\\", \\\"Gull\\\"] {\\n            assert!(script_speaker_count(s) >= 25, \\\"{s} {}\\\", script_speaker_count(s));\\n        }\\n        assert!(script_title_count() >= 30);\\n        assert!(script_name_count() >= 40);\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":1928}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"56ba4731-3eba-4632-a235-d7dd1ef9d945"}
