{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ff8edd82-e50d-48d6-93f7-346f7b89a197-86","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"770→        self.key_taps.clear();\\n        self.mouse_taps.clear();\\n        self.prev_held = held;\\n        // A tap shorter than a frame still counts as held for that frame.\\n        (held | pressed, pressed)\\n    }\\n\\n    /// True if `b` was pressed since the last call (consumes the tap).\\n    pub fn take_mouse_tap(&mut self, b: MouseButton) -> bool {\\n        self.mouse_taps.remove(&b)\\n780→    }\\n\\n    pub fn rewind_held(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.keys.contains(&KeyCode::Backspace) || self.pad.back_held\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod pad_script_tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n790→\\n    #[test]\\n    fn pad_scripts_parse_and_play() {\\n        let mut p = PadScript::parse(\\\"# open the bag\\\\n2\\\\n1 tap=DPadDown\\\\n3 left=0.5,-1 hold=A,Y\\\\n\\\").unwrap();\\n        assert_eq!(p.steps.len(), 3);\\n        let frames: Vec<(PadStep, bool)> = std::iter::from_fn(|| p.next()).collect();\\n        assert_eq!(frames.len(), 6);\\n        assert!(frames[2].1 && frames[2].0.tap == vec![gilrs::Button::DPadDown]);\\n        assert_eq!(frames[3].0.hold, vec![gilrs::Button::South, gilrs::Button::North]);\\n        assert_eq!(frames[5].0.left, Vec2::new(0.5, -1.0));\\n800→        assert!(PadScript::parse(\\\"x tap=A\\\").is_err());\\n        assert!(PadScript::parse(\\\"1 tap=Q\\\").is_err());\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"770→        self.key_taps.clear();\\n        self.mouse_taps.clear();\\n        self.prev_held = held;\\n        // A tap shorter than a frame still counts as held for that frame.\\n        (held | pressed, pressed)\\n    }\\n\\n    /// True if `b` was pressed since the last call (consumes the tap).\\n    pub fn take_mouse_tap(&mut self, b: MouseButton) -> bool {\\n        self.mouse_taps.remove(&b)\\n780→    }\\n\\n    pub fn rewind_held(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.keys.contains(&KeyCode::Backspace) || self.pad.back_held\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod pad_script_tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n790→\\n    #[test]\\n    fn pad_scripts_parse_and_play() {\\n        let mut p = PadScript::parse(\\\"# open the bag\\\\n2\\\\n1 tap=DPadDown\\\\n3 left=0.5,-1 hold=A,Y\\\\n\\\").unwrap();\\n        assert_eq!(p.steps.len(), 3);\\n        let frames: Vec<(PadStep, bool)> = std::iter::from_fn(|| p.next()).collect();\\n        assert_eq!(frames.len(), 6);\\n        assert!(frames[2].1 && frames[2].0.tap == vec![gilrs::Button::DPadDown]);\\n        assert_eq!(frames[3].0.hold, vec![gilrs::Button::South, gilrs::Button::North]);\\n        assert_eq!(frames[5].0.left, Vec2::new(0.5, -1.0));\\n800→        assert!(PadScript::parse(\\\"x tap=A\\\").is_err());\\n        assert!(PadScript::parse(\\\"1 tap=Q\\\").is_err());\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/input.rs\",\"offset\":770,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"        self.key_taps.clear();\\n        self.mouse_taps.clear();\\n        self.prev_held = held;\\n        // A tap shorter than a frame still counts as held for that frame.\\n        (held | pressed, pressed)\\n    }\\n\\n    /// True if `b` was pressed since the last call (consumes the tap).\\n    pub fn take_mouse_tap(&mut self, b: MouseButton) -> bool {\\n        self.mouse_taps.remove(&b)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn rewind_held(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.keys.contains(&KeyCode::Backspace) || self.pad.back_held\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod pad_script_tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn pad_scripts_parse_and_play() {\\n        let mut p = PadScript::parse(\\\"# open the bag\\\\n2\\\\n1 tap=DPadDown\\\\n3 left=0.5,-1 hold=A,Y\\\\n\\\").unwrap();\\n        assert_eq!(p.steps.len(), 3);\\n        let frames: Vec<(PadStep, bool)> = std::iter::from_fn(|| p.next()).collect();\\n        assert_eq!(frames.len(), 6);\\n        assert!(frames[2].1 && frames[2].0.tap == vec![gilrs::Button::DPadDown]);\\n        assert_eq!(frames[3].0.hold, vec![gilrs::Button::South, gilrs::Button::North]);\\n        assert_eq!(frames[5].0.left, Vec2::new(0.5, -1.0));\\n        assert!(PadScript::parse(\\\"x tap=A\\\").is_err());\\n        assert!(PadScript::parse(\\\"1 tap=Q\\\").is_err());\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":803}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"2bd483e0-d614-4f0a-aaa2-544bf3627333"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_801","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Input::new() may be slow or fail gracefully.\n\nConfirmed UiEvent path and Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied. FitUi needs dim 0.0 or the eyes value. Checking menu_flow includes Dev for slider nudges. Will not update checkboxes until tests pass.\n\nDev and Settings are not excluded from menu_flow. Nudge logic will live inside the menu_flow branch. TAB and nudge will use separate if conditions to avoid conflicts. STEP_R as a page alias will not double-fire with MENU since tests only send TAB_R. Arrow keys remain lean and menu bindings. The implementation order is fit.json, hub.toml objects, then FitUi dim and painter.\n\nThe implementation plan now includes events.rs, mod.rs, input.rs, tests, decisions.md, and goal plan deviations. Mod.rs will be updated via multiple search_replace operations. In the Dev flow, confirming Jump (id 200) sets dev_tab to 1, page to 0, and focus to 0 without leaving the dev flow. IDs 200 through 203 map to Jump, Cheats, Time, and Tuning. Root page 0 items exclude Back.\n\nPage 1 Back leaves the dev flow because dev_tab resets to zero. The PAUSE input resets dev_tab to zero when entering Pause or Dev. Cheats list labels are \"No tips\", \"Autoplay\", \"Give minutes\", \"Unlock all\", \"All stars\", \"Skip dialogue\", \"Win this event\", and \"Lose this event\". Time labels are \"0.25x\", \"1x\", \"2x\", \"4x\", and \"Pause clock\".\n\n\"Single step\" is added to the Time list. The go_to search logic uses exact string matching rather than substring containment. This prevents \"1x\" from matching \"0.25x\", \"Day 1\" from matching \"Day 5\", and \"Reset page\" from matching \"Reset feel\". \"Sun cap\" is unique.\n\n\"Cannonball\" matches \"Cannonball Cup\". \"Gray\", \"Golden\", \"Tuning\", \"Cheats\", \"Jump\", \"Wardrobe\", and \"Calendar\" are unique. \"Island\" is also unique.\n\nThe go_to logic tabs through pages when the target item is missing, resets focus to zero, and loops up to thirty times. Jump has seven pages, schedule has three, and names have seven.\n\nThe go_to loop panics after 24 attempts to prevent infinite loops. Back items are found correctly across pages. Settings page wrapping is harmless because page two mirrors page one. Name and Outfit menus omit Back items; tests navigate them with TAB and confirm directly.\n\nName confirmation IDs are 400 plus the absolute index, so page boundaries align correctly. Outfit ID 527 maps to Golden on page one. The status module only needs to expose the existing outfit field; no save slot change is required. Character clips persist because idle_clip defaults to empty and the locomotion block is skipped. The renderer should display clip poses when clip_w is greater than zero.\n\nI will defer pose parade capture details until reverify. The immediate priority is compiling the code and passing tests. I am skipping the optional ghost clip update to minimize risk.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c7d784f6-b1e3-4d37-a2b5-c4b538587860-87","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Press Cross|Long Stillness|Dev Mode|eyes closed|Balance Age|wardrobe|calendar|slider","glob":"**/PLAN.md","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":578,"output_tokens":1587,"cache_read_input_tokens":153856,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"6719d767-3a7d-4a6f-94af-9634725cdf98"}
