{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_808","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will now write all the code.\n\nPlanning the mod.rs edits in sequence: imports, struct fields, item replacements, helper functions, activity logic, and status fields.\n\nThe plan now covers FitUi dim, banner and footer, body clips, and build mats. I will add a `paged_rows` helper and update events.rs, input.rs, tests, fit.json, hub.toml, and decisions.md. Starting with constants after ACT_G4.\n\nAdding the `ACT_DEV_RESET_GROUP` constant and struct fields. Writing the `page_labels` helper and new match arms for name, look, outfit, and schedule.\n\nThe `page_labels` helper is now complete. It paginates a list into fixed-size pages and returns the current slice with widget IDs. The schedule match arm is also being written to display paginated events.\n\nThe schedule match arm now marks completed events and adds an end-day button. The full dev_items replacement is next, with reset and norm logic carefully handled. slider_norm will return Option<f32>. Parameter IDs are absolute indices from the full list, not page-relative.\n\nConfirmed that slider IDs use absolute indices from the full list. Slider labels already display their current values. Started writing a `core_path` helper to detect core tuning groups for reset logic.\n\nThe `core_path` helper now matches core tuning fields and `.stiffness` paths. The `reset_rules` function is being written to compare default and current rules, then paginate the parameters into pages of three.\n\nThe `reset_rules` function now implements the three reset modes. \"all\" resets every parameter. \"group\" resets only the core parameters on the current page. \"page\" resets only the parameters currently visible on screen.\n\nThe `reset_rules` function now applies default values to matched parameters. The first three pages contain the eight core tuning fields, so group reset mode targets those core parameters when the page starts with one.\n\nGroup reset mode will target the parameter type of the first item on the current page. A mixed page starting with a core field resets all core parameters while leaving event fields untouched.\n\nI decided against splitting tuning pages into separate core and event sections. \"Reset group\" will reset only the parameters currently visible on screen, while \"Reset feel\" resets all parameters.\n\nThe `reset_rules` function is being simplified to a single `all` boolean. When false, it skips parameters outside the current page bounds.\n\nThe Dev banner will now display the active tab name, such as \"Jump\", \"Cheats\", \"Time\", or \"Tuning\". The `reset_rules` function is now fully implemented. Ready to write the code.\n\nAdding a `skip_prompt` helper to avoid duplicating the skip instruction string. A `long_still` check is being added to detect extended BigStand phases during events, checks, countdowns, cards, and attract flows. The card phase is confirmed to be zero before the event begins.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-afc936f1-7bf3-4c47-8597-bc635225928c-99","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub mod clips|pub use clips","glob":"**/pav_core/src/lib.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2840,"output_tokens":4918,"cache_read_input_tokens":175232,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"bcf5e94a-5ad5-4b2c-b65e-f99a68b6c1a7"}
