{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_809","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will carefully compose the major edits to mod.rs.\n\nParamValue derives Clone, so cloning default values is safe. I will write fit.json and append objects to hub.toml. I will update decisions.md and avoid banned words in the new text to pass the shipped_text_stays_in_bounds test.\n\nThe \"Press Cross to skip\" text is in mod.rs, not events.rs. I will avoid banned words like \"weight\", \"wii\", and \"nintendo\" in comments. Adding dim text will not break the painter HUD test. During long stillness, the score banner will return empty.\n\nThe fit_ui title will fall back to the default banner title only when the banner is empty and stillness is not active. The skip line belongs in the main lines list, not just the footer, and will be inserted at the front of the list in fit_ui. Puck logic also needs updating.\n\nThe skip line will be appended to the lines list only when the list has fewer than two entries. The test will verify the big banner is empty and the puck is present. The song must be unlocked and on track 3 before stillness so it can drop to silence.\n\nThe desired song returns 0 whenever audio is not yet unlocked. The test must therefore unlock audio before attempting stillness, since the default device is 0 and press() sets pressed without changing the device.\n\nThe test sequence is now fully defined. Pause unlocks audio and opens the dev menu. Jump to Big Stand, step once to confirm song 3, pause again, then jump to Long stillness. The song should drop to 0 before verifying the UI shows the skip prompt, a visible puck, and an empty big banner.\n\nThe test sequence now includes setting the time scale to 4x before jumping. The Big Stand event is the 13th item and will appear on page index 12 when paging by four.\n\nBig Stand is the first item on page three. Specials like Pose gusts, Step window, and Brace follow it. Long stillness is the first item on page four. The seek logic will tab through labels to find the target. After jumping to Big Stand the flow becomes Event, so pausing again resets the dev menu and its tab index.\n\nThe song will switch to track 3 immediately upon jumping to Big Stand. The status song field is self.song, so silence maps cleanly to 0. World time and the attract demo both use a 1x scale, preserving existing behavior. A single-step test is optional.\n\nA fast single-step test will pause during the breath event, select Time and Single step, then verify world_time advances by roughly one tick. Idle steps in the dev menu afterward will not advance time.\n\nThe single-step test asserts world_time advances by exactly one tick and time_scale remains frozen at 1.0. The post method increments world_time for Direct runs, confirming the step logic.\n\nThe single-step test is confirmed: the pre method adds one tick, and the frozen Dev flow prevents post from advancing time further. I will also add tests for cheat unlock, calendar, wardrobe, pose, props, eyes, big stand, age, and schedule. The name test does not require the dev menu.\n\nThe age test will be included despite its length. A timing issue was spotted: with a 4x time scale, the bot is evaluated once per frame using the current act.t, but post advances physics by roughly 0.066 seconds per frame. Notes that fall between those frames will be missed because the bot's perfect window is only about 0.019 seconds.\n\nThe age test will run at 1x time scale. At 4x the bot samples once per frame while physics advances roughly four frames, so it misses notes and scores poorly. The alternative of making the bot time-scale aware is impossible because it cannot see future delta times.\n\nA substepping fix is being considered for the 4x timing issue. The activity tick would split large delta times into 1/60-second intervals so rhythm bots can sample presses continuously across each frame instead of only at the start.\n\nSubstepping the activity tick into 1/60-second intervals would let rhythm bots sample presses continuously across each frame. However, a single press bit held for multiple substeps might register as multiple hits, or double-count, so tick_step needs to be checked before implementing this fix.\n\nSubstepping would not help at 4x. The bot evaluates once per frame using act.t, so it returns zero if the note is not close to that exact moment. A held press across multiple substeps might register as a double hit or extra hit, and the bot cannot see future delta times.\n\nSubstepping the activity tick into 1/60-second intervals would still miss notes, because the bot is only consulted once per frame. The age test will run at 1x time scale with 8520 steps. A similar existing test already passes.\n\nThe age test will run at 1x time scale with a 20000-tick cap. The full finale will be played from phase 0 rather than jumping directly to the end. The eyes test needs about 1400 ticks. The stillness prompt test can jump straight to phase 4 and wait 15 seconds, which is roughly 900 ticks at 1x.\n\nThe stillness prompt test will run at 4x time scale. The prompt and forfeit logic depend on activity time, not frame count, so 4x is valid here. This reduces the test to about 225 ticks. The age test will remain at 1x.\n\nThe age test will explicitly set time_scale to 1x before booting. Age will be set to 45 immediately after boot, before jumping to Big Stand, so the check does not overwrite it.\n\nThe age test must boot in Story mode and jump to Big Stand, because a Direct boot would skip the age formula. The finish_play logic uses the run type and event kind rather than paused_from, so jumping from the title screen is valid.\n\nThe age test will use bot_until to wait for the finale to end, since the activity bot controls input during Events. The flow becomes Ending after credits, and finish_play applies the age formula before that state is reached.\n\nThe bot will not forfeit during stillness because it returns no buttons in phase 4, so the inner peace bonus applies. The age test cap of 20,000 ticks is safely above the 8,520-step finale. The score flow is confirmed: finish_play copies act.score into self.score before applying the age cut. Ready to write the code and update the todo.\n\nThe large mod.rs insertion will be done in several search_replace calls. Schedule page indices were verified: day 4 has six entries before clearing and five afterward, while free play page two holds three entries ending at index ten. Name selection logic was also checked: tabbing advances the page modulo the total, the first name on page one is Gray, and outfit selection resets the page to zero.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The eight gaps are in the live menu, event, and pose paths. I’ll change those next, then drive them with the same inputs a player can send."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-30556f8b-bd72-45df-828a-211d3362458f-100","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/anim/fit.json","new_string":"{\n  \"set\": \"FIT\",\n  \"title\": \"Tippy Cay poses\",\n  \"format\": 1,\n  \"credit\": \"Original key poses for Wobble Minutes. Not a capture.\",\n  \"fps\": 30,\n  \"clips\": {\n    \"Tree\": {\"clip\": \"Tree\", \"dur\": 2.0, \"loop\": true, \"desc\": \"One knee lifted, both arms overhead\", \"keys\": [\n      {\"t\": 0, \"hips\": [0, 0, 100], \"body\": [0, 0, 6], \"chest\": [0, -6, 0], \"head\": [0, 8, 0],\n        \"armL\": [0, 18, 100, 14, 0], \"armR\": [0, 18, 100, 14, 0],\n        \"legL\": [-4, 4, -100, 6, 0], \"legR\": [55, 22, -10, 95, 8],\n        \"footL\": [0, 0, 0], \"footR\": [20, 8, 0]},\n      {\"t\": 2.0, \"hips\": [0, 0, 100], \"body\": [0, 0, 4], \"chest\": [0, -4, 0], \"head\": [0, 6, 0],\n        \"armL\": [0, 16, 98, 16, 0], \"armR\": [0, 16, 98, 16, 0],\n        \"legL\": [-4, 4, -