ss: f32,\"},{\"line_number\":46,\"content\":\"            stiffness: 40.0,\"},{\"line_number\":81,\"content\":\"        v.float(\\\"stiffness\\\", &mut self.stiffness, 5.0, 80.0, \\\"How fast the dot chases your lean\\\");\"},{\"line_number\":157,\"content\":\"        let acc = (target - self.cob) * rules.stiffness - self.vel * rules.damping + self.gust;\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":2093,\"content\":\"            \\\"stiffness\\\": self.rules.stiffness,\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"a2addf4a-2eea-4992-98f6-60e7d807a4ba"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_826","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The room is 16 by 12 cells. Its origin is [-8, 0, -6].\n\nPlayer P is at column 7, row 6. Column 0 maps to x = -8 and column 15 to x = 7.\n\nThe room interior spans roughly 14 meters. Mats will be placed in a ring at radius 3.6, avoiding the five flops positioned at relative offsets (2.2, 0.4), (-2.0, 1.2), (1.2, 2.4), (-1.4, -1.6), and (3.0, -0.8).\n\nThe 1.2 trigger radius means mat and flop centers must be more than 2.4 apart. The farthest flop is at distance 3.10, so the ring radius of 3.6 leaves only a narrow safe band. Mats will be placed at carefully chosen angles to avoid all five flops.\n\nRadius 2.0 is too close to the flops. A 3.6-meter ring with 50-degree angular separation between mats yields a chord distance of about 2.87 meters, safely clearing the 2.4-meter trigger threshold.\n\nThe forbidden angular zones around the five flops nearly cover the entire circle, leaving only a tiny gap. Eleven mats cannot fit in that space. The ring radius will be increased to 5.5 meters.\n\nA 5.5-meter radius risks hitting the room walls on the short axis. The interior is roughly 14 by 10 meters, so a radius near 5 meters is the practical limit. A simpler robust approach is to place mats at fixed offsets that are more than 2.5 meters from every flop.\n\nA line of mats at z = -4.2 is safe from the south flops. The north line at z = +4.2 is too close to flop C, so it must be raised to z = 4.9 or offset horizontally.\n\nA single row of eleven mats would be too crowded. Eleven mats spaced one meter apart would overlap their 1.2-meter triggers, and the room interior is only about fourteen meters wide.\n\nThe layout is being split into two arcs instead. The south arc will have six mats at z = -4.0 with horizontal spacing of 1.8 meters. The north arc will have five mats at z = 4.2 with the same spacing.\n\nThe north arc still needs adjustment. A mat at (1.8, 4.2) is only 1.9 meters from flop C, which is too close.\n\nThe north arc is abandoned because flop C remains too close. All eleven mats will be placed on the south side instead. The south row will sit at z = -4.2, with horizontal spacing of 1.8 meters.\n\nA single south row of eleven mats would span sixteen meters, so the layout is being split into two rows. The first row will sit at z = -3.6 with six mats spaced horizontally by 1.8 meters. The second row will sit at z = -4.8 with five mats spaced by the same amount. The coordinate system is being verified to confirm whether south corresponds to positive or negative z.\n\nSouth corresponds to negative z, and north to positive z. The interior spans about 5.5 meters toward the south wall and 4.5 meters toward the north wall. Mat positions will be offset from the player by +3.8 and -3.5 along z, keeping clear of flops C and D. Exact coordinates will be computed later if a test fails.\n\nThe south row is fixed at z = -4.2 with six mats at x = -4.2, -2.5, -0.8, 0.9, 2.6, and 4.3. These clear the farthest flop D by about 2.7 meters. A mat at x = 4.6 on the east side would still be too close to flops E and A.\n\nEleven mat offsets are being finalized. The south row holds six items at z = -4.2. The east side gets lap at (4.6, 1.8) and tide at (4.6, 3.2). The west side gets paddle at (-4.4, 2.8). These positions clear the nearest flops by roughly 2.7 meters.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-df042858-ed3a-4a48-aa74-67849a4df267-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"rowboat|park_bench|lamp_post|market_stall|round_table","glob":"**/*.{toml,json,rs}","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-df042858-ed3a-4a48-aa74-67849a4df267-34","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/hub.toml","offset":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-df042858-ed3a-4a48-aa74-67849a4df267-35","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub struct FitGame","glob":"**/games/fit/mod.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-df042858-ed3a-4a48-aa74-67849a4df267-36","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/core.rs","offset":180,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5025,"output_tokens":3830,"cache_read_input_tokens":76544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"3bc8e018-13c1-457d-a840-63635bc3656f"}
