,117,108,101,115,58,32,38,82,117,108,101,115,41,32,45,62,32,40,86,101,99,50,44,32,117,51,50,41,32,123,10,54,48,48,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,69,118,101,110,116,73,100,58,58,67,104,101,99,107,32,61,62,32,116,105,99,107,95,99,104,101,99,107,40,97,99,116,44,32,98,97,108,44,32,112,114,101,115,115,101,100,44,32,100,116,44,32,101,118,101,110,116,115,41,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":9,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":31,\"content\":\"        EventId::Check,\"},{\"line_number\":48,\"content\":\"            EventId::Check => \\\"check\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":70,\"content\":\"            EventId::Check => \\\"Morning Wobble Check\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":88,\"content\":\"            EventId::Check => \\\"Stand, lean, close your eyes, and step on the beat.\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":106,\"content\":\"            EventId::Check | EventId::BigStand => \\\"Pip\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":228,\"content\":\"            EventId::Check => 8.0 + 15.0 + 6.0 + 8.0 * 0.6,\"},{\"line_number\":405,\"content\":\"        EventId::Check => bot_check(act, bal, rules),\"},{\"line_number\":430,\"content\":\"fn bot_check(act: &Activity, bal: &BalanceCore, rules: &Rules) -> (Vec2, u32) {\"},{\"line_number\":600,\"content\":\"        EventId::Check => tick_check(act, bal, pressed, dt, events),\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"f5d886e5-97fc-41af-a1a4-d7a27894e6c6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_830","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Phase 2 lasts 6 seconds, or 360 ticks.\n\nA 30-tick hard lean in phase 2 should move the cob and change pitch. The eyes-closed UI requires flow == Check, which this path satisfies. The puck is shown for this event unless eyes are closed.\n\nThe puck is visible in phase 0 and 1 but hidden in phase 2. The test only checks phase 2.\n\nDim field must be included in the FitUi literal to compile.\n\nDuring long stillness, the title should remain empty so the banner does not fall back to TITLE. The speaker override only triggers when the title equals TITLE, which it does not during long stillness.\n\nAn empty title string causes the painter to skip text rendering. This makes the HUD vanish except for the puck. The big field is also empty.\n\nLines must be empty before the 15-second skip prompt. The footer should remain a lean prompt until that point, since it contains \"Left stick\" or \"WASD\" rather than \"Press\" or \"skip\".\n\nThe footer becomes the skip line after 15 seconds.\n\nPressing CONFIRM, PAUSE, or MENU on device 0 changes the device to 2 (keyboard). This is required for the stillness test: jump The Big Stand first to unlock audio, then jump Long stillness.\n\nPressing CONFIRM, PAUSE, or MENU on device 0 unlocks audio because the device becomes 2 and the skip prompt still contains \"Press\" and \"skip\". Pressing MENU_RIGHT or TAB keeps device 0, so the prompt says \"Press Cross to skip\" instead. To reach The Big Stand, pause opens the dev menu, jump is selected, and The Big Stand is chosen.\n\nThe 4x time scale is set before jumping to The Big Stand. At 4x speed, 15 seconds of real time equals 225 simulation ticks. The test sequence is: pause, set 4x, jump to The Big Stand and assert song==3, pause again, jump to Long stillness and assert song==0, then step until act_sub reaches 225.\n\nThe test will step without pressing buttons after the 15-second mark. The fit_ui struct must expose a song field for reading. A seek helper will handle jump navigation.\n\nHelper functions are being drafted to read the UI state. `items` collects all menu items with their IDs and labels. `focus_label` returns the label of the currently focused item. `label_hit` matches labels against search strings, with special handling for time-scale labels ending in \"x\" to avoid partial matches.\n\nThe `seek` helper iterates up to 48 times, checking the focused item and scanning all labels for a match. It returns true once the target is found.\n\nThe `seek` helper now steps the simulation with MENU_DOWN or MENU_UP to move focus toward a target label, falling back to TAB_R if the label is not found. A `pick` helper asserts the target exists and then presses CONFIRM. TAB_R is avoided on the About page because it switches the about page instead of the menu. On the Settings page, Music is focus 0.\n\nThe test sequence now covers the Settings and Tuning pages. It seeks to Settings, confirms, then moves focus to Music and nudges the volume up from 0.10 to 0.20. It then opens Tuning, selects stiffness as the first parameter, asserts it changes by more than one unit, picks Reset feel, confirms, and verifies stiffness returns to its original value.\n\nStiffness is normalized to 0.467, so a +0.1 nudge yields 47.5, which is more than one unit above the base value of 40. Reset feel is not a slider, so MENU_RIGHT on it does nothing and focus stays put. The Settings Music slider also ignores MENU_RIGHT, leaving focus on Music until Back is selected.\n\nSeeking Back will use MENU_DOWN to reach the back button. MENU_RIGHT during settings is harmless because the menu is frozen and focus does not move. The device stays at 0 unless a prior press already switched it to 2. Slider events must not be injected directly into the UI. Pausing from the Tuning page keeps the flow in Dev.\n\nThe name test sequence is being drafted. It starts from the title screen, selects New Stay, then enters the name phase and confirms \"Hammock\" or an empty slot to set the name to Gray. After confirming the first look, it moves to the outfit phase, navigates to page 1 with TAB_R, and selects Swim to verify the outfit value is 7.\n\nThe status struct needs an outfit field.\n\nA schedule test sequence is being drafted. It pauses to open the dev menu, unlocks all events via Cheats, jumps to Island, presses SCHEDULE, and selects Cannonball. Free play excludes Check and BigStand, so the event list contains only Breath, Pose, Squat, and Plank.\n\nThe schedule page layout is now clear. The event list spans three pages: 0–3 on page 0, 4–7 on page 1, and 8–10 on page 2. Cannonball is index 10 with id 110, so the seek helper will tab to the third page and menu down to it. After confirming, the flow becomes Card and the status event key reflects kind_now. The Back button after unlocking all events sits on the same cheat page, reachable with one MENU_DOWN. The eyes test is next.\n\nThe eyes test boots the check phase and waits for phase 2. It asserts the puck is hidden, dim is above 0.5, and lines contain \"eyes\". A hard lean is applied for 30 ticks, and the tone must change by more than 0.05.\n\nThe tone is set in the same tick that bot_until enters phase 2, so leaning immediately afterward is correct. The test file needs a Vec2 import for InputFrame.lean; I will use glam::Vec2 if pav_core re-exports it.\n\nThe stillness test boots the fit phase and opens the dev menu. It sets the time scale to 4x, jumps to The Big Stand, pauses again, then jumps to Long stillness. After 15 seconds of idle stepping, it asserts the skip prompt is present, the big field is empty, and the puck remains visible.\n\nThe stillness test must assert the title is an empty string, not a fallback like \"Wobble Minutes\" or \"The Big Stand\". The big field must also be empty.\n\nAn age test is being drafted. It boots the fit phase, manually sets the game age to 45, then jumps to The Big Stand via the dev menu while keeping the time scale at 1x. It waits for the phase to reach ending with a 20-second cap.\n\nThe age formula subtracts the score divided by 100, floored and capped at 10, from 45, then clamped to a minimum of 18. A score of 500 or higher yields a cut of 5, leaving age at 40 and triggering the rowboat ending. Scores below 500 still satisfy the formula but do not reach that threshold. The test will not assign the ending directly and will keep the time scale at 1x.\n\nThe bot will play the event automatically via sim.bot_input(), so cheat_auto is unnecessary. A Pose test is being drafted to boot the pose event, wait for the phase to reach Event, and read the clip status after 30 ticks.\n\nThe Pose test will verify the clip is FIT/Tree. At 30 ticks the pose timer is still below its threshold, so the clip remains unchanged.\n\nThe wardrobe test boots the fit phase, opens the dev menu, and selects Wardrobe to equip the Sun cap. HelmKind must be public for the test to read the puppet gear directly.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bc507a6-a375-4c88-b6ff-d8e77f67ba50-45","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub entities|fn iter","glob":"**/entity.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bc507a6-a375-4c88-b6ff-d8e77f67ba50-46","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub mod clips|pub mod puppet|pub use puppet","glob":"**/pav_core/src/lib.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bc507a6-a375-4c88-b6ff-d8e77f67ba50-47","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"enum HelmKind|pub struct Gear|pub helm","glob":"**/puppet.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2440,"output_tokens":4071,"cache_read_input_tokens":94976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"db2b8f7f-2f0b-4985-97ff-c1eee4528919"}
