":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"c3c98379-a794-45b2-91b8-ae1231d5caad"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_831","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `entities.iter()` method yields references to each entity.\n\nConfirmed the puppet gear helm path. A single-step optional test will verify world_time increments by roughly 1/60 during dev phases, while paused steps leave it unchanged.\n\nSingle-step will be implemented since the UI field and menu already exist. It runs at the end of the pre phase after copying last_lean, then resets the flag and ticks activity for one frame.\n\nThe single-step logic increments world_time by 1/60 and applies body updates. Because the flow remains Dev, pose_clip returns zero and the puppet does not animate during the step. This is acceptable for a clock-only test.\n\nSingle-step does not double-count world_time because post only increments time during Event flow. The clock remains paused at 0x until the user resumes. Started implementing a page_labels helper for menu pagination.\n\nCompleted the `page_labels` and `page_rows` pagination helpers. `page_rows` appends a Back button to each page. Confirmed that `script().names` is a `Vec<String>` and can be passed directly into `page_labels`.\n\nLook skins and outfits are also Vec<String>. The wardrobe menu passes a combined list into page_rows. The schedule page fits all six items on one screen, including the Back button.\n\nThe name page omits a back button because the BACK action returns to the previous menu. The 40 names split into six full pages and one final page of four entries. Outfit page zero holds six items and page one holds two. Look skins fit exactly on one page, with TAB_R wrapping via modulo.\n\nPlanning to update `pre()` with careful search-replace edits. The fit UI will show dim, eyes, and stillness indicators. The banner logic for Event and Check flows now handles long stillness, closed eyes, and normal titles. The eyes line is pushed into the banner extra field, which appends it when fewer than two lines exist.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b266d77d-d7f5-40d1-b4fa-b976a81f2618-48","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs","offset":500,"limit":60}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b266d77d-d7f5-40d1-b4fa-b976a81f2618-49","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub gear|pub struct PuppetDef|pub puppet:","glob":"**/sim.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b266d77d-d7f5-40d1-b4fa-b976a81f2618-50","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"struct SimConfig|pub puppet","glob":"**/sim.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4562,"output_tokens":3233,"cache_read_input_tokens":97408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"c2056033-83e4-4ddd-a908-f310028a9227"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b266d77d-d7f5-40d1-b4fa-b976a81f2618-48","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"500→                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Creature => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.creature_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::World => {}\\n510→        }\\n        if self.history.enabled && self.config.history_seconds > 0.0 {\\n            self.history.window = (self.config.history_seconds * self.config.tick_rate.hz() as f32) as u64;\\n            self.history.record(&self.state, input);\\n        }\\n        if self.recording.ticks() < MAX_RECORDING_TICKS {\\n            self.recording.push(input);\\n        }\\n        self.step_inner(input);\\n    }\\n520→\\n    fn step_inner(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        // Hit-stop slows the whole world for a moment.\\n        let raw_dt = self.dt();\\n        let dt = raw_dt * self.game_time_scale();\\n        self.state.physics.params.dt = dt as Real;\\n        self.state.physics.gravity = Vector::new(0.0, -self.config.gravity as Real, 0.0);\\n\\n        // Behaviours set this tick's velocities of moving objects; characters then move\\n        // (rapier's controller carries them with kinematic platforms) and the physics step\\n530→        // advances everything together.\\n        self.run_behaviors(dt);\\n\\n        // Getting in and out of vehicles.\\n        self.vehicle_interact(input);\\n\\n        // The game decides what the hero and its monsters do this tick.\\n        let mut events = Vec::new();\\n        let mut game_inputs = self.game_pre(input, dt, &mut events);\\n        game_inputs.extend(self.play_pre(input, dt, &mut events));\\n540→        // A frozen game (pause, menus) still ran `pre`. Skip the world so time and bodies stay put.\\n        if self.state.play.as_ref().is_some_and(|g| g.frozen()) {\\n            if let Some(p) = self.player() {\\n                self.state.focus = p.pos;\\n            }\\n            self.state.tick += 1;\\n            if !self.replaying {\\n                self.events.extend(events);\\n            }\\n            return;\\n550→        }\\n\\n        // Characters.\\n        let ids: Vec<EntityId> = self.state.entities.iter().filter(|e| e.character.is_some()).map(|e| e.id).collect();\\n        let mut actions = Vec::new();\\n        let idle = InputFrame::default();\\n        let player_feet = self.player().and_then(|p| Some(p.pos - Vec3::Y * p.character.as_ref()?.height() * 0.5));\\n        let all_feet: Vec<Vec3> =\\n            self.state.entities.iter().filter_map(|e| Some(e.pos - Vec3::Y * e.character.as_ref()?.height() * 0.5)).collect();\\n        let mut fallen = Vec::new();\",\"content_concise\":\"500→                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Creature => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.creature_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::World => {}\\n510→        }\\n        if self.history.enabled && self.config.history_seconds > 0.0 {\\n            self.history.window = (self.config.history_seconds * self.config.tick_rate.hz() as f32) as u64;\\n            self.history.record(&self.state, input);\\n        }\\n        if self.recording.ticks() < MAX_RECORDING_TICKS {\\n            self.recording.push(input);\\n        }\\n        self.step_inner(input);\\n    }\\n520→\\n    fn step_inner(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        // Hit-stop slows the whole world for a moment.\\n        let raw_dt = self.dt();\\n        let dt = raw_dt * self.game_time_scale();\\n        self.state.physics