{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_842","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"clip_t advances during character animation updates, which occur before the post-tick phase.\n\nclip_t resets only when the clip ID changes, keeping poses on frame 0 otherwise. The next step is writing all patches. The age test runs about 8500 steps. Potential compile issues are noted.\n\nVerified that `page_labels`, `FitUi::dim`, `events::bot`, `ParamKind`, `ParamValue`, and `self.act` fields are all in scope. Deviations will be updated only after paging is compiled and tested, not prematurely. Also checking whether `schedule_rows` might add an \"End day\" entry that pushes the free-play schedule past six items.\n\nSchedule rows stay capped at six items. Day 4 story and free-play pages never exceed this limit. The code is solid. Optional materials will be skipped to keep status compact.\n\nMaterials will be stored as an array of event keys so tests can assert their presence. The credits bot uses absolute indices for Schedule press_bits.\n\nSchedule page resets to zero on entry, so leftover pages from other menus are handled. Name and outfit selections confirm the first option without paging. Ready to edit. Also checking island CONFIRM timing against collect_flops.\n\ntry_mat checks feet and materials rather than last_pressed. It triggers on the exact CONFIRM press. If it starts a mat event, the flow becomes Card, so collect_flops does not run that same frame. Otherwise the flow stays Island and post collects flops. The step_once flag is cleared each frame and only set true once per confirm.\n\nConfirmed that holding CONFIRM produces only a single frame. Also verified that substring matching for time row labels won't accidentally match shorter values like \"1x\" inside \"0.25x\", since the slider test targets \"4x\" and the age test stays at its default.\n\nThe time page splits into two six-item rows. The first row holds the speed options and Back. The second row holds Pause clock, Single step, and Back. The 4x label sits on the first row. After opening Time the focus starts at 0.25x. MENU_DOWNs will reach it. On the Island jump page the bot will press TAB repeatedly to reset focus and cycle through pages until the target label appears.\n\nIsland is the only label containing \"Island\", so it will not match other entries. \"Cannonball\" correctly targets \"Cannonball Cup\". \"Gray\" and \"Golden\" are unique enough to avoid false hits. \"Sun cap\" and \"Calendar\" are also distinct. The substring \"Day\" appears inside calendar labels like \"Day 1 · open\", but it does not appear in unrelated menu items.\n\nThe Calendar test selects the exact entry first, then checks that any item contains \"Day\" without confirming. Unique labels like \"Unlock all\", \"Cheats\", and \"Jump\" avoid false matches. \"Settings\" appears on both the title and dev page 1, but seek finds it on page 0. \"Reset feel\" is present on both dev page 1 and tuning, yet the test targets the tuning page where it appears. \"Long stillness\" is unique enough to avoid collisions. If a sought label is missing, TAB will cycle through pages until the limit of 48.\n\nThe 48-step seek limit covers all menus. Jump has seven pages and Name has seven, so cycling through them is safe.\n\nIf the focused item's label accidentally contains the search needle, the bot stops. The Calendar test avoids this by selecting the exact entry first, then asserting any remaining label matches.\n\nWardrobe's \"Sun cap\" sits at page zero as the first item. After opening Wardrobe, focus may already be there, so seek returns immediately and pick confirms it. The screen item ID matches the wardrobe ID, so activate Wardrobe calls wear correctly and the helm updates.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-09eec22f-062e-4757-9af8-a375f8971797-65","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/input.rs","offset":500,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-09eec22f-062e-4757-9af8-a375f8971797-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_app/src/input.rs","offset":790,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1248,"output_tokens":2067,"cache_read_input_tokens":112896,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"71bfb6fc-9eb5-4745-86d5-86abf96756cd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-09eec22f-062e-4757-9af8-a375f8971797-65","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"500→        }\\n        if held_dir.length() > 0.0 {\\n            self.lean_from = 2;\\n            self.seen_real = true;\\n        }\\n        if self.mouse_travel > 6.0 && !self.coarse {\\n            self.lean_from = 3;\\n        }\\n        let lean = match self.lean_from {\\n            1 => stick,\\n510→            3 => {\\n                let offset = Vec2::new(self.cursor.x - size.x * 0.5, size.y * 0.5 - self.cursor.y);\\n                mouse_lean(offset, size.y)\\n            }\\n            _ => self.lean_ramp,\\n        };\\n        let mut extra = 0u32;\\n        if stick.y > 0.55 && self.stick_y <= 0.55 {\\n            extra |= buttons::MENU_UP;\\n        }\\n520→        if stick.y < -0.55 && self.stick_y >= -0.55 {\\n            extra |= buttons::MENU_DOWN;\\n        }\\n        self.stick_y = stick.y;\\n        let mut ui = None;\\n        let travel = self.mouse_travel;\\n        self.mouse_travel = 0.0;\\n        let tap = clicked || self.touch_tap;\\n        self.touch_tap = false;\\n        if size.x > 1.0 && size.y > 1.0 {\\n530→            for (id, rect) in items {\\n                let x = rect[0] * size.x;\\n                let y = rect[1] * size.y;\\n                let w = rect[2] * size.x;\\n                let h = rect[3] * size.y;\\n                if self.cursor.x >= x && self.cursor.x <= x + w && self.cursor.y >= y && self.cursor.y <= y + h {\\n                    let slider = (*id >= 300 && *id < 400) || (610..=616).contains(id);\\n                    let dragging = self.mouse.contains(MouseButton::Left) && !tap && w > 1.0;\\n                    ui = Some(if tap {\\n                        pav_core::input::UiEvent::Click(*id)\\n540→                    } else if dragging && slider {\\n                        let along = ((self.cursor.x - x) / w).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n                        pav_core::input::UiEvent::Slider(*id, along)\\n                    } else {\\n                        pav_core::input::UiEvent::Hover(*id)\\n                    });\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let device = if self.coarse && !self.seen_real {\\n550→            4\\n        } else if self.last_device == Device::Gamepad {\\n            1\\n        } else if self.lean_from == 3 {\\n            3\\n        } else if self.last_device == Device::Touch {\\n            4\\n        } else {\\n            2\\n        };\\n560→        let any = !self.coarse && (self.pad.any_activity || travel > 6.0 || stick.length() > 0.3 || lean.length() > 0.3);\\n        FitSample { lean, device, any, ui, extra }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn key(&mut self, code: KeyCode, state: ElementState) {\\n        self.last_device = Device::KeyboardMouse;\\n        self.seen_real = true;\\n        match state {\\n            ElementState::Pressed => {\\n                self.keys.insert(code);\\n570→                self.key_taps.insert(code);\\n            }\\n            ElementState::Released => {\\n                self.keys.remove(&code);\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn mouse_button(&mut self, b: MouseButton, state: ElementState) {\\n        self.last_device = Device::KeyboardMouse;\",\"content_concise\":\"500→        }\\n        if held_dir.length() > 0.0 {\\n            self.lean_from = 2;\\n            self.seen_real = true;\\n        }\\n        if self.mouse_travel > 6.0 && !self.coarse {\\n            self.lean_from = 3;\\n        }\\n        let lean = match self.lean_from {\\n            1 => stick,\\n510→            3 => {\\n                let offset = Vec2::new(self.cursor.x - size.x * 0.5, size.y * 0.5 - self.cursor.y);\\n                mouse_lean(offset, size.y)\\n            }\\n            _ => self.lean_ramp,\\n        };\\n        let mut extra = 0u32;\\n        if stick.y > 0.55 && self.st