{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_846","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Default rules match the rules.toml configuration.\n\nReady to write the code in several search_replace calls. The `events` module's `bot` is already public. I'll carefully replace the `pre()` function and update `fit_ui` with new lines, skip logic, and title/puck/dim settings.\n\nDrafting the `fit_ui` replacement. The new code adds eyes and stillness handling alongside the existing banner and touch-only logic.\n\nThe `fit_ui` title field will be hidden when the game is in a long still state. A new `dim` field will be added to the struct. The puck expression and the eyes and skip lines are also being updated.\n\nThe banner will return empty strings for title, big text, and extra when the game is in a long still state. The footer will also be updated.\n\nThe score banner will remain visible during the eyes state to avoid breaking existing tests. The footer is being rewritten to return a schedule prompt for the Island flow.\n\nThe footer now returns a skip line for Event or Check flows when the game is in a long still state and the current action has at least fifteen substeps. Otherwise it returns a lean prompt, and other flows return confirm.\n\nNext up are apply_body replacement, building materials, status fields, page helpers, pre changes, post world_time, and tests.\n\nThe fit_ui lines will include an \"Eyes closed\" prompt when the eyes are shut, and a skip line during long stillness. The puck is hidden while the eyes are closed.\n\nThe puck will be hidden during the eyes state and shown only for Event, Check, Attract, Countdown, and Card flows. The dim field will be 0.92 while the eyes are closed and 0.0 otherwise.\n\nMaterial placement will use the previously calculated offsets. A stronger test would walk onto a mat and confirm the real CONFIRM path triggers an event, rather than merely checking that the schedule vector exists.\n\nTeleporting the player onto a mat to test the CONFIRM path would skip the real walk. The schedule test already covers menu-started events. The mat path should be tested by actually walking there.\n\nWalking to a mat will take roughly eighty-four ticks at character speed. The test will read the mat positions from the game status, move the player toward the first one using real left-stick input, press CONFIRM, and expect a card. This avoids hard-coding coordinates while still exercising the real walk-and-confirm path.\n\nA `walk_to` helper is being drafted to move the player toward a target mat. It reads the player's feet position each tick, steers with normalized direction vectors, and stops once the distance drops below 0.9 meters. This prevents overshooting while keeping the test on the real walk path.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4a00b9c0-f692-4a45-b093-eeb66f469132-71","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"move_dir","glob":"**/*.rs","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":688,"output_tokens":1795,"cache_read_input_tokens":119936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"fc1b79a4-4782-44c9-a67e-c483e9844f71"}
