es-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/arpg/bot.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":127,\"content\":\"                f.move_dir = Vec2::new(a.x, a.z);\"},{\"line_number\":173,\"content\":\"                    f.move_dir = Vec2::new(n.x, n.z);\"},{\"line_number\":183,\"content\":\"            f.move_dir = Vec2::new(away.x, away.z);\"},{\"line_number\":196,\"content\":\"                f.move_dir = Vec2::new(n.x, n.z) * 0.5;\"},{\"line_number\":223,\"content\":\"                    f.move_dir = Vec2::new(n.x, n.z);\"},{\"line_number\":228,\"content\":\"                f.move_dir = Vec2::new(n.x, n.z);\"},{\"line_number\":285,\"content\":\"        f.move_dir = Vec2::new(n.x, n.z);\"},{\"line_number\":340,\"content\":\"        f.move_dir = Vec2::new(dir.x, dir.z);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"dc25bfec-8447-4267-b482-1859ea7e3f1f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_848","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Noted that move_dir.x represents world x.\n\nWorld y maps to world z. Mats will be placed on sand to avoid water and walls. The one-frame movement delay is acceptable for a walk loop.\n\nConfirmed movement updates and character driving happen in the same frame. Frozen menus won't block movement since the island isn't frozen. Now adding the walk test.\n\nCalculated that the south mat lands on sand row 2 and the north mat near the interior wall row 10. The player's exact z-position will be verified during the walk test.\n\nThe player's starting column falls inside the water's horizontal range. Walking south would cross the water pit, so the south mat must be placed on the opposite side of the lagoon.\n\nThe player sits below the water pit, so moving south into open sand is safe. Mats will be placed at positive z offsets and east or west of the water, not across it.\n\nMat positions are being set at z offsets from +1.5 to +3.2 and x offsets from -3 to +3, all on sand south of the player. Flop C sits at z+2.4, so the mat zone must extend past that point to avoid overlap.\n\nThe mat zone must extend to z=3.8 or higher to clear flop C at z=2.4, which leaves only a narrow horizontal band. The interior sand ends near z=4.5, so the south mat offset is capped around 3.6 meters.\n\nA west-side mat placement at x=-4.5 and z=0.0 clears flops B and D while avoiding the water pit entirely.\n\nEleven mat points are being placed at x=-4.5 with z offsets from -3.6 to +3.2 in steps of 0.68. The column lies on sand, and the next step is to verify distances to flops.\n\nAll flops are safely cleared by the west-side mat line. The 0.68-meter spacing is narrow but acceptable because try_mat picks the closest trigger. The walk path will stay inside columns 3–7 and rows 2–6.\n\nThe walk path from the player to the west mat line passes through column 3, which is sand and safely outside the water pit. The diagonal route does not clip the water boundary.\n\nThe west-side mat line risks clipping the water boundary at z=-1.5, so the walk target will be a positive-z mat instead. The first mat in the list at (-4.5, 1.2) is chosen as the safe destination.\n\nThe test will select a mat that is both south of the player and west of them, keeping the path on sand. A 10-second walk covers the roughly 4.6-meter distance easily. Props have no collision bodies, so they will not block movement. Everything is ready to implement now.\n\nA single-step pause test during the breath event will verify that time-scale control advances the world clock. The stillness test already implicitly checks 4x speed because it expects 15 sub-steps in under 400 ticks. If the 4x multiplier were broken, the test would still pass at normal speed.\n\nThe 400-frame cap is confirmed to require 4x speed, since 15 sub-steps at normal speed need 900 frames. The code scales activity delta time by the time scale multiplier. After jumping to big stand, the flow becomes Event phase 0 with song 3, and audio unlocks because the jump uses CONFIRM.\n\nThe test sequence will jump to Big Stand and assert song 3 immediately, before pausing. The pause causes the song to drop to 1 while the menu is active. Then jumping to long stillness asserts song 0 on that step. No assertion is needed for song 3 persisting through the menu.\n\nConfirmed the jump to \"The Big Stand\" is unique and correctly sets flow to Event. The long stillness jump maps to phase 4 via ID 243, and seek will locate it properly.\n\nThe menu navigation flow is confirmed: selecting 4x, pressing Back, and then Jump works correctly because Back returns to the main menu. The implementation will add helpers after press() and append new tests before the hub_ghost test. The existing music test will be replaced.\n\nThe FitGame age field is public, so the test can set it directly via get_mut. This stores the morning result that the formula consumes without skipping the finale. The formula computes age as 24 plus 56 times (1 minus skill) raised to the 1.1 power.\n\nAge 45 requires a skill near 0.59, so the test will inject that stored age directly via get_mut rather than attempting an exact in-game landing. The summary explicitly forbids setting ending or score. Entity fields and clips::find are confirmed accessible.\n\nThe HelmKind path is `pav_core::puppet::HelmKind::Cap`. Tests will import `pav_core::glam::Vec2`.\n\n`seek` only works in menus because `screen_items` is empty during events. The title screen and the Look screen after name entry are safe.\n\nAfter confirming the player name, focus resets to 0, so a second CONFIRM on the Look screen is safe without seeking first.\n\nFor outfit selection, the test will use explicit TAB_R and MENU_DOWN presses rather than `pick`, ensuring the exact sequence is followed.\n\nThe outfit selection will use `pick(\"Golden\")` to test paging. The name entry will use explicit TAB_R and CONFIRM presses instead of `pick`, strictly following the spec and avoiding accidental seeking.\n\nThe outfit selection test will use explicit TAB_R, MENU_DOWN, and CONFIRM presses rather than `pick` to verify the exact menu path. If TAB wraps incorrectly and the page stays at 0, MENU_DOWN would select Rash Guard (index 1) instead of Golden (index 7), which would cause a failure. The schedule test will still use `pick` since it exercises real menu paging. The eyes test does not involve menus. The status struct also needs to expose `act_phase` as a number.\n\nStatus JSON fields will use `as_u64()` for `act_phase`, `song`, and `clip`, `as_f64()` for `act_sub` and `tone`, and the `json!` macro is already imported. The credits test remains valid because world time advances by the scaled delta, which equals the raw delta at 1x speed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d0168e61-7e7e-4156-8b76-d51b100953e8-73","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn script\\(","glob":"**/games/fit/mod.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2299,"output_tokens":4693,"cache_read_input_tokens":124160,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"37187bfa-8410-41cd-84ad-3dea146a4951"}
