01,100,32,51,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,99,114,101,100,105,116,115,32,117,115,101,32,98,101,100,32,54,44,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,116,104,101,32,115,105,109,39,115,32,115,111,110,103,32,109,97,112,32,114,97,116,104,101,114,32,116,104,97,110,32,116,104,101,32,112,108,97,110,39,115,32,98,101,100,32,110,117,109,98,101,114,115,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":5,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d%2Fwork/01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":9,\"content\":\"3. **Every event is a finished mini-game.** Shipped and directly startable: Morning Wobble Check, Breath Bloom, Pose Parade, Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff, Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap, Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup, and the five-phase Big Stand, with the twists named in PLAN.md §5 (breath guide, drifting pose ring and gull, squat tempo, plank flop, 96 BPM two-lane chart, hula-style spin and ring catches, lap with step-rate zone, shell-tilt boards, paddle gates, tray of smoothies, cannonball judges, Long Stillness). Each event has a card, countdown, result (score, stars, deadpan title, minutes, personal best, Retry or Back), a bot that earns at least 2 stars on 5 seeds, and an idle-input result under 1 star. Score events use 0–1000 with stars at 400, 650, and 850; Plank uses the time gates in PLAN.md (25 / 40 / 55 s). Time-cut permission in PLAN.md §17 does not apply: this computer can run the full roster.\"},{\"line_number\":28,\"content\":\"- Dev folder of that basename: clone of `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall` (PLAN.md was checked against commit `49ef2ba`), game content and tests, notes, and a small README for adding an event, a set, or a song.\"},{\"line_number\":45,\"content\":\"## Deviations\"},{\"line_number\":47,\"content\":\"- Name, look, and outfit menus show the first six entries. The rest stay in `script.toml`.\"},{\"line_number\":48,\"content\":\"- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6, matching the sim's song map rather than the plan's bed numbers.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-35b5d265-eea6-49b2-a88d-40cb210394be-106","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→- Last input device wins. Touch does not leave attract and does not count as a real controller.\\n- Hub ghosts are drawn in the view from `window.__hub.ghosts`. The sim only publishes its own sample, so a session stays deterministic.\\n- Long tests set `history_seconds` to 0. A normal boot keeps 8 seconds of rewind.\\n- About text comes from `#about-data` when the page sets it. Native runs keep a readable fallback with the same headings.\\n- Name, look, and outfit menus page six at a time. The ids stay absolute, so a later page can still pick Gray, Swim, and Golden.\\n- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6. That is the sim's song map. Long Stillness is song 0, which stops the bed.\\n- On a splash round the page calls `AIHub.ready()` when connect resolves. Waiting for `__gameStatus` left the fourth software-WebGPU copy past the harness's 20s ready gate. A later `ready()` is a no-op.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→- Last input device wins. Touch does not leave attract and does not count as a real controller.\\n- Hub ghosts are drawn in the view from `window.__hub.ghosts`. The sim only publishes its own sample, so a session stays deterministic.\\n- Long tests set `history_seconds` to 0. A normal boot keeps 8 seconds of rewind.\\n- About text comes from `#about-data` when the page sets it. Native runs keep a readable fallback with the same headings.\\n- Name, look, and outfit menus page six at a time. The ids stay absolute, so a later page can still pick Gray, Swim, and Golden.\\n- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6. That is the sim's song map. Long Stillness is song 0, which stops the bed.\\n- On a splash round the page calls `AIHub.ready()` when connect resolves. Waiting for `__gameStatus` left the fourth software-WebGPU copy past the harness's 20s ready gate. A later `ready()` is a no-op.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/notes/decisions.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"- Last input device wins. Touch does not leave attract and does not count as a real controller.\\n- Hub ghosts are drawn in the view from `window.__hub.ghosts`. The sim only publishes its own sample, so a session stays deterministic.\\n- Long tests set `history_seconds` to 0. A normal boot keeps 8 seconds of rewind.\\n- About text comes from `#about-data` when the page sets it. Native runs keep a readable fallback with the same headings.\\n- Name, look, and outfit menus page six at a time. The ids stay absolute, so a later page can still pick Gray, Swim, and Golden.\\n- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6. That is the sim's song map. Long Stillness is song 0, which stops the bed.\\n- On a splash round the page calls `AIHub.ready()` when connect resolves. Waiting for `__gameStatus` left the fourth software-WebGPU copy past the harness's 20s ready gate. A later `ready()` is a no-op.\\n\",\"total_lines\":7}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"564656d4-7750-4135-b8e0-7ab4cc693f25"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_864","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The first-six cut is no longer true once the code pages are included. The goal plan deviation needs updating.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d1606c8c-561a-4d69-abaa-c10cd2162d14-107","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d%2Fwork/01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce/goal/plan.md","offset":30,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1161,"output_tokens":210,"cache_read_input_tokens":163840,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"4cbcdca6-9a2b-4075-8c3e-454dd9786ad8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d1606c8c-561a-4d69-abaa-c10cd2162d14-107","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"30→- Fredoka and Nunito (SIL OFL) embedded for UI text; engine puppet, egui, and synthesized audio extended as PLAN.md §§8–14 describe. Behavior is the contract; file names in PLAN.md are guidance.\\n- Playwright 1.63 (system Python, not `python3 -I`), Cargo, and `wasm-bindgen` 0.2.129. Chromium only for WebGPU play; Firefox and WebKit are fallback-message checks.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md for design numbers, writing, and the hub snippet; do not invent a second balance model or a second synth. Keep the whole flow (menus, dialogue, pause, settings, dev toggles, events) in the simulation so tests drive it with no GPU. Keep UI a pure view of that state. Keep tunable numbers and all dialogue in data files the tests load. Build a single HTML only after the sim tests pass. Disable the engine’s demo keys and on-screen chrome while this game is active so captures show the game, not the engine shell. Record any spec gap in one line in the dev notes and continue.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Pick the title with a real RNG from 50 riffs, record the draw, create the dev folder, clone the engine, and keep `PROGRESS.md` current.\\n- [x] Register the game, hide engine chrome, add lean input and the title/pause shell, save, and the hub page tags so a boot smoke test passes.\\n- [x] Implement the shared balance model, the morning check, the island day loop, and one full event; lock them with sim tests.\\n40→- [x] Implement the remaining events, day unlocks, Big Stand, both endings, free play, and the bot playthrough.\\n- [x] Add synthesized music, effects, and gibberish voices (music default 0.10), attract mode, settings, dev sliders with reset, and the touch-only card.\\n- [x] Add wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, Play Together, and the hub ghost medley; run the hub harness.\\n- [x] Write the full script and About text, fill `exit-interview.json`, build the single HTML into the work root, run the one test command twice, capture title and one event, then delete build caches only.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Splash rounds call `AIHub.ready()` when `connect` resolves. Waiting for `__gameStatus` left the fourth software-WebGPU copy past the harness's 20s ready gate. A later `ready()` is a no-op.\\n- Name, look, and outfit menus show the first six entries. The rest stay in `script.toml`.\\n- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6, matching the sim's song map rather than the plan's bed numbers.\\n\\n50→## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §17 allows cutting Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, and Plank Standoff if time runs short. The objective requires everything this computer can run, so a cut roster fails criterion 3.\\n- TASK.md warns that a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank even when the frame is live. A blank browser bitmap is not success and not an automatic environment waiver: the engine’s own capture must show a filled frame (step 2). Only a launcher that will not start is the fallback.\\n- Browser timing at 1920×1080 is too slow here (software WebGPU). The 10-second attract check is valid only around 320×180; a slow 1080p browser clock is not a game bug. Judge the 10-foot layout from the 1080p engine capture.\\n- Firefox and WebKit have no WebGPU here, so they cannot play the game. There is no physical pad, touch screen, listener, second human, or TV.\\n- A fresh clone may not be commit `49ef2ba`. If a “verified” engine note is wrong on the cloned revision, adapt and record the commit and the change; do not pretend the old note still held.\\n- Other agents share this machine. Use one browser, bind an OS-picked localhost port, and stop only PIDs this run started. `earlyoom` killing the browser is memory pressure, not a game bug.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"30→- Fredoka and Nunito (SIL OFL) embedded for UI text; engine puppet, egui, and synthesized audio extended as PLAN.md §§8–14 describe. Behavior is the contract; file names in PLAN.md are guidance.\\n- Playwright 1.63 (system Python, not `python3 -I`), Cargo, and `wasm-bindgen` 0.2.129. Chromium only for WebGPU play; Firefox and WebKit are fallback-message checks.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md for design numbers, writing, and the hub snippet; do not invent a second balance model or a second synth. Keep the whole flow (menus, dialogue, pause, settings, dev toggles, events) in the simulation so tests drive it with no GPU. Keep UI a pure view of that state. Keep tunable numbers and all dialogue in data files the tests load. Build a single HTML only after the sim tests pass. Disable the engine’s demo keys and on-screen chrome while this game is active so captures show the game, not the engine shell. Record any spec gap in one line in the dev notes and continue.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Pick the title with a real RNG from 50 riffs, record the draw, create the dev folder, clone the engine, and keep `PROGRESS.md` current.\\n- [x] Register the game, hide engine chrome, add lean input and the title/pause shell, save, and the hub page tags so a boot smoke test passes.\\n- [x] Implement the shared balance model, the morning check, the island day loop, and one full event; lock them with sim tests.\\n40→- [x] Implement the remaining events, day unlocks, Big Stand, both endings, free play, and the bot playthrough.\\n- [x] Add synthesized music, effects, and gibberish voices (music default 0.10), attract mode, settings, dev sliders with reset, and the touch-only card.\\n- [x] Add wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, Play Together, and the hub ghost medley; run the hub harness.\\n- [x] Write the full script and About text, fill `exit-interview.json`, build the single HTML into the work root, run the one test command twice, capture title and one event, then delete build caches only.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Splash rounds call `AIHub.ready()` when `connect` resolves. Waiting for `__gameStatus` left the fourth software-WebGPU copy past the harness's 20s ready gate. A later `ready()` is a no-op.\\n- Name, look, and outfit menus show the first six entries. The rest stay in `script.toml`.\\n- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6, matching the sim's song map rather than the plan's bed numbers.\\n\\n50→## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §17 allows cutting Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, and Plank Standoff if time runs short. The objective requires everything this computer can run, so a cut roster fails criterion 3.\\n- TASK.md warns that a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank even when the frame is live. A blank browser bitmap is not success and not an automatic environment waiver: the engine’s own capture must show a filled frame (step 2). Only a launcher that will not start is the fallback.\\n- Browser timing at 1920×1080 is too slow here (software WebGPU). The 10-second attract check is valid only around 320×180; a slow 1080p browser clock is not a game bug. Judge the 10-foot layout from the 1080p engine capture.\\n- Firefox and WebKit have no WebGPU here, so they cannot play the game. There is no physical pad, touch screen, listener, second human, or TV.\\n- A fresh clone may not be commit `49ef2ba`. If a “verified” engine note is wrong on the cloned revision, adapt and record the commit and the change; do not pretend the old note still held.\\n- Other agents share this machine. Use one browser, bind an OS-picked localhost port, and stop only PIDs this run started. `earlyoom` killing the browser is memory pressure, not a game bug.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d%2Fwork/01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":30,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"- Fredoka and Nunito (SIL OFL) embedded for UI text; engine puppet, egui, and synthesized audio extended as PLAN.md §§8–14 describe. Behavior is the contract; file names in PLAN.md are guidance.\\n- Playwright 1.63 (system Python, not `python3 -I`), Cargo, and `wasm-bindgen` 0.2.129. Chromium only for WebGPU play; Firefox and WebKit are fallback-message checks.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md for design numbers, writing, and the hub snippet; do not invent a second balance model or a second synth. Keep the whole flow (menus, dialogue, pause, settings, dev toggles, events) in the simulation so tests drive it with no GPU. Keep UI a pure view of that state. Keep tunable numbers and all dialogue in data files the tests load. Build a single HTML only after the sim tests pass. Disable the engine’s demo keys and on-screen chrome while this game is active so captures show the game, not the engine shell. Record any spec gap in one line in the dev notes and continue.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Pick the title with a real RNG from 50 riffs, record the draw, create the dev folder, clone the engine, and keep `PROGRESS.md` current.\\n- [x] Register the game, hide engine chrome, add lean input and the title/pause shell, save, and the hub page tags so a boot smoke test passes.\\n- [x] Implement the shared balance model, the morning check, the island day loop, and one full event; lock them with sim tests.\\n- [x] Implement the remaining events, day unlocks, Big Stand, both endings, free play, and the bot playthrough.\\n- [x] Add synthesized music, effects, and gibberish voices (music default 0.10), attract mode, settings, dev sliders with reset, and the touch-only card.\\n- [x] Add wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, Play Together, and the hub ghost medley; run the hub harness.\\n- [x] Write the full script and About text, fill `exit-interview.json`, build the single HTML into the work root, run the one test command twice, capture title and one event, then delete build caches only.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Splash rounds call `AIHub.ready()` when `connect` resolves. Waiting for `__gameStatus` left the fourth software-WebGPU copy past the harness's 20s ready gate. A later `ready()` is a no-op.\\n- Name, look, and outfit menus show the first six entries. The rest stay in `script.toml`.\\n- Big Stand uses music bed 3 and the credits use bed 6, matching the sim's song map rather than the plan's bed numbers.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §17 allows cutting Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, and Plank Standoff if time runs short. The objective requires everything this computer can run, so a cut roster fails criterion 3.\\n- TASK.md warns that a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank even when the frame is live. A blank browser bitmap is not success and not an automatic environment waiver: the engine’s own capture must show a filled frame (step 2). Only a launcher that will not start is the fallback.\\n- Browser timing at 1920×1080 is too slow here (software WebGPU). The 10-second attract check is valid only around 320×180; a slow 1080p browser clock is not a game bug. Judge the 10-foot layout from the 1080p engine capture.\\n- Firefox and WebKit have no WebGPU here, so they cannot play the game. There is no physical pad, touch screen, listener, second human, or TV.\\n- A fresh clone may not be commit `49ef2ba`. If a “verified” engine note is wrong on the cloned revision, adapt and record the commit and the change; do not pretend the old note still held.\\n- Other agents share this machine. Use one browser, bind an OS-picked localhost port, and stop only PIDs this run started. `earlyoom` killing the browser is memory pressure, not a game bug.\\n\",\"total_lines\":56}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"2c805616-5536-4c17-ad6a-c36ca3b07f23"}
