4,97,116,32,98,108,111,99,107,44,32,105,110,99,108,117,100,105,110,103,32,116,104,101,32,102,111,110,116,115,39,32,97,110,100,32,109,111,116,105,111,110,32,108,105,98,114,97,114,105,101,115,39,32,99,114,101,100,105,116,115,32,40,96,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,115,116,111,114,101,47,67,82,69,68,73,84,83,46,109,100,96,44,32,101,97,99,104,32,99,108,105,112,32,115,101,116,39,115,32,96,99,114,101,100,105,116,96,41,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":7,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":335,\"content\":\"**Route: egui in `pav_ui`, painter-drawn, no default windows.** This was verified at 1920x1080: rounded fonts, soft-shadow cards and painted glyphs look right and appear in headless `pav capture`. Keep all UI state in the sim (section 14), so tests can drive it.\"},{\"line_number\":435,\"content\":\"**Ghost drawing.** Append extra `RenderObject`s to clones of `prev` and `curr` before `builder.build` in `App::frame`, with a high id per seat and `PuppetFrame { state, feet_offset, def: Some(look), rig: None, tint: Some((seat_rgb, 0.55)) }`; copy how `Sim::frame` builds a character's object. The sim never sees hub ghosts, so it stays deterministic. Local ghosts (Yesterday You, Play Together) come from the sim's own save data and are appended in `Sim::frame`, through the same helper, so captures show them. Names are egui text projected above the head; never insert hub names as HTML. Ghost JSON: area (event index), position, facing, lean, clip id, clip time, score. Only draw a ghost whose area matches yours. 10 messages/s stays under the 20/s limit.\"},{\"line_number\":526,\"content\":\"- `pav capture ... width=1920 height=1080`: about 0.5 s. `pav play bot=true seeds=5`: under 1 s.\"},{\"line_number\":578,\"content\":\"**Second player:** the harness's copies, the only multi-player check possible on one computer. **TV:** judge 1920x1080 `pav capture`s.\"},{\"line_number\":580,\"content\":\"**Screenshots** only for what scripts cannot check: `pav capture` for composition, `filmstrip` and `animsheet` for motion, one 1080p sheet per set at the end. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"},{\"line_number\":588,\"content\":\"3. **First slice.** Balance Core, Puck, tilt, `studio` set, Pose Parade, event card and result, bot, one result screen in full art. Play it by bot and capture it. Tune until a ring streak feels good.\"},{\"line_number\":603,\"content\":\"2. Run `tools/build.sh`: copy the exit interview into `about-data` in the page, run the single-file build with your title, description and theme colour, and write the HTML where your brief says. The About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback from that block, including the fonts' and motion libraries' credits (`engine/store/CREDITS.md`, each clip set's `credit`).\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"04201777-4ffe-4cb5-900c-51652b74e17e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_878","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Targeted tests passed. Now running the full fit suite twice, plus audio/ui and pav_app slider tests.\n\nThe verification plan requires a command that prints only failures and a final pass count, run twice. The tests/run.sh script failed with exit 127 from the work root. I will use the cargo test commands for pav_core fit, pav_audio, pav_ui, and pav_app instead.\n\nThe fit test file contains ten original tests plus additional library tests. The prior 27-pass count likely included those extras. I am reviewing the rest of fit.rs to confirm the total.\n\nThe fit binary contains 18 tests total. The prior 27-pass count likely included audio and UI tests as well. I will run the fit suite twice, then audio and UI, then the pav_app slider test, all into tests-core.log with clear headers.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The new menu, slider, and finale tests passed. Next I’ll run the full sim suite twice, then recapture and repack."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5727efae-03c0-4730-a6c0-b0a2e4556e91-123","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"LOG=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/tmp/grok-goal-b3947fd4d9d9/implementer/tests-core.log\nENG=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine\"\ncd \"$ENG\" || exit 1\n{\n  echo \"=== fit run 1 $(date -Is) ===\"\n  CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 cargo test -q --offline --locked -p pav_core --test fit -- --test-threads=4\n  echo EXIT1:$?\n  echo \"=== fit run 2 $(date -Is) ===\"\n  CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 cargo test -q --offline --locked -p pav_core --test fit -- --test-threads=4\n  echo EXIT2:$?\n  echo \"=== pav_audio pav_ui $(date -Is) ===\"\n  CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 cargo test -q --offline --locked -p pav_audio -p pav_ui -- --test-threads=4\n  echo EXIT_AUDIO:$?\n  echo \"=== pav_app slider $(date -Is) ===\"\n  CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 cargo test -q --offline --locked -p pav_app --lib a_held_pointer -- --test-threads=4\n  echo EXIT_APP:$?\n} > \"$LOG\" 2>&1\necho SHELL:$? >> \"$LOG\"","description":"Run fit suite twice plus audio, UI, slider","block_until_ms":0}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5727efae-03c0-4730-a6c0-b0a2e4556e91-124","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pav capture|filmstrip|animsheet","glob":"**/*.{md,sh,py}","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3710,"output_tokens":1179,"cache_read_input_tokens":180736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"d8fdfa37-1bdd-467f-bedd-5fd782284031"}
