,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":6,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":92,\"content\":\"Xbox glyphs (Settings option) swap A B X Y, LB RB LT RT, Menu. Ignore Options while Create is held: that pair belongs to the AI Hub. Disable the engine's own keys (F1 to F10, digits, H, Backspace rewind, right-drag tilt) outside dev mode. Keep F11 for fullscreen.\"},{\"line_number\":354,\"content\":\"| Pause | Resume, Schedule, Calendar, Wardrobe, Settings, How to Play, About, Dev Mode, Quit to Title |\"},{\"line_number\":363,\"content\":\"**Dev Mode** (from Pause, not shown in hub sessions). Big rows, pad-navigable, in tabs:\"},{\"line_number\":383,\"content\":\"In a session there is no title, menu or attract. The game opens straight into the round. Pause shows only Resume and Settings; the world keeps running, because the hub's clock does. Quit, restart and dev mode do not exist there.\"},{\"line_number\":574,\"content\":\"**`browser` (Playwright, one browser, 320x180, `file://`):** boots with no errors; `__gameStatus` appears; the pad stub moves focus and confirms; keyboard does the same; mouse hover moves focus and click activates, using rects the UI publishes in `window.__gameUi`; prompts switch with the device; Settings has the Xbox option; attract starts after 10 s and any input exits it; music reaches about 10% by the sound patch. Touch: Chromium with a phone and a tablet profile (it has WebGPU) must show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", run attract, and respond to a Settings tap by `page.touchscreen.tap`. WebKit with an iPhone profile, which has no WebGPU here, must show the fallback message from section 11.\"},{\"line_number\":593,\"content\":\"8. **Shell.** Attract, Settings, Dev Mode, touch-only card, How to Play, About.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"ed3ef9ea-3d60-497f-b499-665a09be1c7b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_903","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The exit-interview animation field describes an engine puppet tilted about the feet by a balance dot.\n\nThe animation description is now slightly wrong because hand-keyed FIT clips were added. The About screen and exit interview must stay accurate. The three feedback arrays should only be updated if the answers themselves change.\n\nThe About screen incorrectly claims motion clips are the engine library. This is a factual error but not one of the eight gaps. The testing feedback still lists six defects. Eight more gaps were found after rejection. Updating the testing feedback to include the skeptic findings would be more honest.\n\nThe animation description should mention the hand-keyed FIT poses. The testing feedback should list all fourteen defects. The engine feedback may need to include slider drags and pose clips.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-995149ac-8b94-43a5-8c4f-9e066bc07b8b-20","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/PLAN.md","offset":350,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-995149ac-8b94-43a5-8c4f-9e066bc07b8b-21","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ABOUT_FALLBACK|about-data|animation","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132","glob":"*.{rs,py,html,json}","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2625,"output_tokens":659,"cache_read_input_tokens":68736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"3835e952-9e73-47cb-b1d5-0774147a5f76"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-995149ac-8b94-43a5-8c4f-9e066bc07b8b-20","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"350→| Event HUD | Puck, score, timer, one prompt row |\\n| Result | Score, stars, title, minutes, best, Retry or Back |\\n| Check report | Giant rolling number, sparkline, Pip's comment |\\n| Calendar | Five big days and stamps |\\n| Pause | Resume, Schedule, Calendar, Wardrobe, Settings, How to Play, About, Dev Mode, Quit to Title |\\n| Settings | Music (default 10%), SFX, Voices, Glyphs, Lean Sensitivity, Wobble Assist, Rhythm Offset, Text Speed, Fullscreen, Reset Save (with confirm) |\\n| About | Pages for each block your brief requires (section 18) |\\n| Play Together | Choose 2 to 4 guests, pass-the-pad interstitial, podium |\\n\\n**Mouse in the world:** on the island `InputFrame.aim` already holds the cursor's ground point. The nearest interactable within 1.2 m of it gets a highlight ring; clicking walks there with `NavGrid::path`, then interacts. Clicking open ground walks there.\\n360→\\n**Touch-only devices:** detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')`, no `(any-pointer: fine)`, and no gamepad or key seen yet. Show a centred card \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a Settings button (tap works; Settings is usable by tap). No touch controls: skip Shardfall's `touch.draw` for this game, and route touches directly to egui in `on_touch`, because the engine's touch layer otherwise treats a finger as a stick. Attract mode runs behind the card. Remove the phone-rotation hint and fullscreen-on-tap from `web/index.html`. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the card and start normally. A touch device without WebGPU cannot run the game at all, so the page's own fallback message there says both things: \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and that the game needs WebGPU.\\n\\n**Dev Mode** (from Pause, not shown in hub sessions). Big rows, pad-navigable, in tabs:\\n- **Jump:** any day, any event, any finale phase, attract, medley.\\n- **Cheats:** no tips, autoplay with the bot, give minutes, unlock all, all stars, skip dialogue, win or lose this event now.\\n- **Time:** scale 0.25x to 4x, pause, single step (`TimeControl`).\\n- **Tuning:** live sliders, generated from `impl Tunable for Rules` with `params::list` and `params::set`, grouped by core and by event, with **Reset to Defaults** per group and for all. Must include: stiffness, damping, wobble, tip time, stick curve, key rates, each event's main difficulty number, rhythm windows, spin band, gust strength, bounce gain, Big Stand gusts.\\n- **View:** input viewer, dot trace, engine stats overlay, free camera, ghost lanes.\\n- **Save:** reset this guest.\\n370→\\n## 12. Attract mode\\n\\nAfter 10 seconds without input on the title or pre-game menus (600 ticks), loop: island sweep 8 s, then about 15 s each of Cannonball Cup, Paddle Slalom, Step Party, Pose Parade, Tide Table, Floatie Spin, Tray Trek, Plank Standoff, Morning Lap, Big Stand, then the title card 5 s. The bot plays with `demo = true`: no tips, no failures, nothing saved. A \\\"DEMO\\\" ribbon and \\\"Press any button\\\" show on screen. Any input exits to the title: any key, button, stick beyond 0.3, mouse click or mouse move over 6 px (`InputFrame.any`). Touch-only devices keep it running.\\n\\nUse the same event code with the bot replacing input in `pre`. No separate replay system.\\n\\n## 13. Multiplayer\\n\\n**AI Hub session: mode `ghost`, 1 to 4 players.** Follow `lib/hub/README.md` in `michaelcrosato/ai-hub`. `ghost` is the choice because seeing friends wobble on the next mat is the fun of it, and it is barely more work than `parallel`; `shared-world` would need a host-run world this game does not need. Download `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` to `hub/`; these URLs work without auth (verified).\\n380→\\n**The round, the Inter-Resort Medley:** Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup, one after another, about 2 minutes, then final score = sum of the three event scores (0 to 3000), reported as `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })`. The same seed on every copy gives the same course. On a copy, other players appear as seat-coloured figures with their names in the same event: in another lane or on a neighbouring raft or board. They affect nothing. Use the hub's own card: do not pass `card: true`.\\n\\nIn a session there is no title, menu or attract. The game opens straight into the round. Pause shows only Resume and Settings; the world keeps running, because the hub's clock does. Quit, restart and dev mode do not exist there.\\n\\n**Order in the `<head>` of `web/index.html`:** `<meta charset>`, the client, the tags, the `about-data` block (section 14), then the JS below.\\n```html\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* session.js pasted byte for byte */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n390→<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Highest total across three balance events wins\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n```\\n\\n**Hub logic lives in about 30 lines of plain JS in the page; Rust only reads and writes window fields.** This exact block passed the harness on a real engine build at 2 players, at 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, and with `scenario=host-leave`, in 14 to 19 s each, and the page ran clean outside a session (verified):\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"350→| Event HUD | Puck, score, timer, one prompt row |\\n| Result | Score, stars, title, minutes, best, Retry or Back |\\n| Check report | Giant rolling number, sparkline, Pip's comment |\\n| Calendar | Five big days and stamps |\\n| Pause | Resume, Schedule, Calendar, Wardrobe, Settings, How to Play, About, Dev Mode, Quit to Title |\\n| Settings | Music (default 10%), SFX, Voices, Glyphs, Lean Sensitivity, Wobble Assist, Rhythm Offset, Text Speed, Fullscreen, Reset Save (with confirm) |\\n| About | Pages for each block your brief requires (section 18) |\\n| Play Together | Choose 2 to 4 guests, pass-the-pad interstitial, podium |\\n\\n**Mouse in the world:** on the island `InputFrame.aim` already holds the cursor's ground point. The nearest interactable within 1.2 m of it gets a highlight ring; clicking walks there with `NavGrid::path`, then interacts. Clicking open ground walks there.\\n360→\\n**Touch-only devices:** detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')`, no `(any-pointer: fine)`, and no gamepad or key seen yet. Show a centred card \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a Settings button (tap works; Settings is usable by tap). No touch controls: skip Shardfall's `touch.draw` for this game, and route touches directly to egui in `on_touch`, because the engine's touch layer otherwise treats a finger as a stick. Attract mode runs behind the card. Remove the phone-rotation hint and fullscreen-on-tap from `web/index.html`. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the card and start normally. A touch device without WebGPU cannot run the game at all, so the page's own fallback message there says both things: \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and that the game needs WebGPU.\\n\\n**Dev Mode** (from Pause, not shown in hub sessions). Big rows, pad-navigable, in tabs:\\n- **Jump:** any day, any event, any finale phase, attract, medley.\\n- **Cheats:** no tips, autoplay with the bot, give minutes, unlock all, all stars, skip dialogue, win or lose this event now.\\n- **Time:** scale 0.25x to 4x, pause, single step (`TimeControl`).\\n- **Tuning:** live sliders, generated from `impl Tunable for Rules` with `params::list` and `params::set`, grouped by core and by event, with **Reset to Defaults** per group and for all. Must include: stiffness, damping, wobble, tip time, stick curve, key rates, each event's main difficulty number, rhythm windows, spin band, gust strength, bounce gain, Big Stand gusts.\\n- **View:** input viewer, dot trace, engine stats overlay, free camera, ghost lanes.\\n- **Save:** reset this guest.\\n370→\\n## 12. Attract mode\\n\\nAfter 10 seconds without input on the title or pre-game menus (600 ticks), loop: island sweep 8 s, then about 15 s each of Cannonball Cup, Paddle Slalom, Step Party, Pose Parade, Tide Table, Floatie Spin, Tray Trek, Plank Standoff, Morning Lap, Big Stand, then the title card 5 s. The bot plays with `demo = true`: no tips, no failures, nothing saved. A \\\"DEMO\\\" ribbon and \\\"Press any button\\\" show on screen. Any input exits to the title: any key, button, stick beyond 0.3, mouse click or mouse move over 6 px (`InputFrame.any`). Touch-only devices keep it running.\\n\\nUse the same event code with the bot replacing input in `pre`. No separate replay system.\\n\\n## 13. Multiplayer\\n\\n**AI Hub session: mode `ghost`, 1 to 4 players.** Follow `lib/hub/README.md` in `michaelcrosato/ai-hub`. `ghost` is the choice because seeing friends wobble on the next mat is the fun of it, and it is barely more work than `parallel`; `shared-world` would need a host-run world this game does not need. Download `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` to `hub/`; these URLs work without auth (verified).\\n380→\\n**The round, the Inter-Resort Medley:** Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup, one after another, about 2 minutes, then final score = sum of the three event scores (0 to 3000), reported as `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })`. The same seed on every copy gives the same course. On a copy, other players appear as seat-coloured figures with their names in the same event: in another lane or on a neighbouring raft or board. They affect nothing. Use the hub's own card: do not pass `card: true`.\\n\\nIn a session there is no title, menu or attract. The game opens straight into the round. Pause shows only Resume and Settings; the world keeps running, because the hub's clock does. Quit, restart and dev mode do not exist there.\\n\\n**Order in the `<head>` of `web/index.html`:** `<meta charset>`, the client, the tags, the `about-data` block (section 14), then the JS below.\\n```html\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* session.js pasted byte for byte */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n390→<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Highest total across three balance events wins\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n```\\n\\n**Hub logic lives in about 30 lines of plain JS in the page; Rust only reads and writes window fields.** This exact block passed the harness on a real engine build at 2 players, at 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, and with `scenario=host-leave`, in 14 to 19 s each, and the page ran clean outside a session (verified):\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":350,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"| Event HUD | Puck, score, timer, one prompt row |\\n| Result | Score, stars, title, minutes, best, Retry or Back |\\n| Check report | Giant rolling number, sparkline, Pip's comment |\\n| Calendar | Five big days and stamps |\\n| Pause | Resume, Schedule, Calendar, Wardrobe, Settings, How to Play, About, Dev Mode, Quit to Title |\\n| Settings | Music (default 10%), SFX, Voices, Glyphs, Lean Sensitivity, Wobble Assist, Rhythm Offset, Text Speed, Fullscreen, Reset Save (with confirm) |\\n| About | Pages for each block your brief requires (section 18) |\\n| Play Together | Choose 2 to 4 guests, pass-the-pad interstitial, podium |\\n\\n**Mouse in the world:** on the island `InputFrame.aim` already holds the cursor's ground point. The nearest interactable within 1.2 m of it gets a highlight ring; clicking walks there with `NavGrid::path`, then interacts. Clicking open ground walks there.\\n\\n**Touch-only devices:** detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')`, no `(any-pointer: fine)`, and no gamepad or key seen yet. Show a centred card \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a Settings button (tap works; Settings is usable by tap). No touch controls: skip Shardfall's `touch.draw` for this game, and route touches directly to egui in `on_touch`, because the engine's touch layer otherwise treats a finger as a stick. Attract mode runs behind the card. Remove the phone-rotation hint and fullscreen-on-tap from `web/index.html`. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the card and start normally. A touch device without WebGPU cannot run the game at all, so the page's own fallback message there says both things: \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and that the game needs WebGPU.\\n\\n**Dev Mode** (from Pause, not shown in hub sessions). Big rows, pad-navigable, in tabs:\\n- **Jump:** any day, any event, any finale phase, attract, medley.\\n- **Cheats:** no tips, autoplay with the bot, give minutes, unlock all, all stars, skip dialogue, win or lose this event now.\\n- **Time:** scale 0.25x to 4x, pause, single step (`TimeControl`).\\n- **Tuning:** live sliders, generated from `impl Tunable for Rules` with `params::list` and `params::set`, grouped by core and by event, with **Reset to Defaults** per group and for all. Must include: stiffness, damping, wobble, tip time, stick curve, key rates, each event's main difficulty number, rhythm windows, spin band, gust strength, bounce gain, Big Stand gusts.\\n- **View:** input viewer, dot trace, engine stats overlay, free camera, ghost lanes.\\n- **Save:** reset this guest.\\n\\n## 12. Attract mode\\n\\nAfter 10 seconds without input on the title or pre-game menus (600 ticks), loop: island sweep 8 s, then about 15 s each of Cannonball Cup, Paddle Slalom, Step Party, Pose Parade, Tide Table, Floatie Spin, Tray Trek, Plank Standoff, Morning Lap, Big Stand, then the title card 5 s. The bot plays with `demo = true`: no tips, no failures, nothing saved. A \\\"DEMO\\\" ribbon and \\\"Press any button\\\" show on screen. Any input exits to the title: any key, button, stick beyond 0.3, mouse click or mouse move over 6 px (`InputFrame.any`). Touch-only devices keep it running.\\n\\nUse the same event code with the bot replacing input in `pre`. No separate replay system.\\n\\n## 13. Multiplayer\\n\\n**AI Hub session: mode `ghost`, 1 to 4 players.** Follow `lib/hub/README.md` in `michaelcrosato/ai-hub`. `ghost` is the choice because seeing friends wobble on the next mat is the fun of it, and it is barely more work than `parallel`; `shared-world` would need a host-run world this game does not need. Download `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` to `hub/`; these URLs work without auth (verified).\\n\\n**The round, the Inter-Resort Medley:** Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup, one after another, about 2 minutes, then final score = sum of the three event scores (0 to 3000), reported as `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })`. The same seed on every copy gives the same course. On a copy, other players appear as seat-coloured figures with their names in the same event: in another lane or on a neighbouring raft or board. They affect nothing. Use the hub's own card: do not pass `card: true`.\\n\\nIn a session there is no title, menu or attract. The game opens straight into the round. Pause shows only Resume and Settings; the world keeps running, because the hub's clock does. Quit, restart and dev mode do not exist there.\\n\\n**Order in the `<head>` of `web/index.html`:** `<meta charset>`, the client, the tags, the `about-data` block (section 14), then the JS below.\\n```html\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* session.js pasted byte for byte */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Highest total across three balance events wins\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n```\\n\\n**Hub logic lives in about 30 lines of plain JS in the page; Rust only reads and writes window fields.** This exact block passed the harness on a real engine build at 2 players, at 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, and with `scenario=host-leave`, in 14 to 19 s each, and the page ran clean outside a session (verified):\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":632}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-995149ac-8b94-43a5-8c4f-9e066bc07b8b-21","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,97,116,32,108,101,97,115,116,32,51,48,32,109,97,116,99,