{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_983","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking whether build.rs embeds anim/fit.json.\n\nConfirmed anim/fit.json is embedded at build time. Now checking hub.toml beach props, whether apply_body runs on the normal tick path, and if the renderer reads the clip set by apply_body.\n\nVerifying whether the character tick advances clip_t and applies keys. Will inspect PNG captures. Flagged a potential bug: one-shot sfx every frame during eyes-closed could stack 60 overlapping voices and overload the mixer.\n\nThe 60Hz sfx loop may produce a pitch tone, but the test only checks status.tone, not whether an Sfx event was emitted. This suggests the test theater.\n\nThe test checks that status.tone changes with lean. This proves tick_check phase 2 runs and act.guide tracks cob. The Sfx push is unconditional in that same function when phase is 2. If the test reaches phase 2 through the real update loop, the Sfx event is emitted.\n\nConfirmed the prior gap is fixed: the real tick path sets both the guide status and the Sfx event in the same branch. The skip prompt logic is sound; it appends only when the line list has fewer than two entries, and tests cover both the prompt and footer.\n\nConfirmed the real input path reaches phase 4 through the dev menu. The prior gap about never applying the ending is fixed; finish_play now unconditionally sets the ending from adjusted age, and the test only asserts the formula equality.\n\nConfirmed the age formula subtracts score/100 from morning age, capped at 10. The prior gap is fixed.\n\nNext: inspect free play schedule rows and screen items and material population. Also verify name page labels and that TAB switches pages.\n\nConfirmed page_labels uses the page variable and the test shows Gray. Slider input is wired through fit_sample, pad D-pad, and drag gestures; tests cover MENU_RIGHT.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-