{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_995","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Locomotion will not overwrite the FIT clip. The `ours` flag is false for non-idle, non-walk, non-run clips. STOP is not included in the flags.\n\napply_body resets clip_flags only when the clip changes. Pose sticks and capture confirms this. Character update runs before post in the same tick. The character sees the previous frame's clip. Post then applies the new clip. Render uses post state. Capture shows the pose.\n\nBrowser and hub log timestamps must be checked against the code changes. If the browser log predates the pack containing the fixes, the shipped HTML may not have been re-launched. Pack 2 was created at 03:17 after the 19-test runs, so file mtimes are needed to verify this. The full browser and hub logs need review. Tests-core must confirm that the 19 tests passed twice and that the new tests were actually executed in that run.\n\nThe Big Stand jump correctly overwrites flow to Event after start_activity sets it to card. Song 0 is assigned during the same pre() tick that sets phase 4, so the test asserting song 0 immediately passes. The music mixer also silences song 0.\n\nThe forfeit logic is sound. The test steps with an empty input frame, so the bot's step buttons cannot trigger a forfeit during the idle wait. A real player might accidentally forfeit by wiggling the stick past the menu edge, but that is an anti-ratchet edge case rather than a gating bug.\n\nThe eyes-closed tone is verified through the status tone check. The Sfx id 31 is valid because sfx_patch uses ids generically, so it counts toward the 30-effect requirement. The name page bug is harmless: page_labels omits a page indicator, but the test reached Gray at index 6 and all tests passed.\n\nOutfit 7 Golden is correctly mapped: page 1 index 0 is outfit 6, and MENU_DOWN advances to index 1 which is outfit 7. The test asserting outfit == 7 passed.\n\nThe schedule id bug is resolved. schedule_rows enumerates the full list and skips entries, so ids are 100 plus the original index. activate retrieves events with evs.get(id-100), which works correctly across pages. The seek logic wraps page indices using modulo pages, and the test tries up to 48 times. Free play events total 11, fitting across three pages.\n\nCannonball is correctly found in the schedule. After the credits, free_play becomes true at both the Ending and Credits advances, so schedule_events returns all events except Check and BigStand. Mats work properly once free play begins.\n\nOn day 5, the schedule contains only BigStand, which is absent from the mats list. try_mat requires either free_play or a matching schedule entry, so island mats cannot start events until free play begins. This behavior is correct for the finale day.\n\nThe mats are all at the west edge and might sit outside the room. The test reached the floatie mat, so they are walkable. Props have body none and appear in capture. I will now scan PLAN.md criteria and events for a real defect that still fails a criterion.\n\nThe anti-ratchet standard now applies only to demonstrable defects in shipped behavior or unmet gating criteria.\n\nI will verify the test log contains the new tests, check browser log freshness against file mtimes, and confirm the HTML was rebuilt after fixes.\n\nLikely bugs remain: balance age, song, dev time affecting pause, and slider confirm still being a no-op. The latter is acceptable if left/right works.\n\nA new concern is that frozen() returns true outside Island, Event, Check, and Attract states. In dev mode this freezes the simulation, so the main tick might skip post entirely.\n\nTests confirm the pause menu works while frozen, so frozen() does not skip pre and post entirely. world_time still stops during pause. At time_scale 0 during an event, post uses scaled dt and the event clock halts. The pause clock cheat remains functional. step_once ticks activity once at 1/60 even when time_scale is 0, and post also ticks if flow is Event with scaled 0.\n\nstep_once finishes the activity inside pre, so post's zero-tick call cannot double-count or re-trigger the event. The next step is to inspect the tail of tests-core.log and its timestamps.\n\nThe browser test for the packed HTML needs inspection. The music test presses MENU_RIGHT from the Settings page, which starts at focus 0 on the Music row; if it passed, the slider was correctly targeted. The dev tuning test assumes the first parameter is stiffness, so it will fail unless that assumption holds.\n\nThe dev tuning test passed, so the first slider is stiffness. Reset feel correctly maps to the default rules via ACT_DEV_RESET. The name page index calculation is sound. Look skin selection does not validate against the skins list length.\n\nThe prior gap requiring beach and wellness props is now satisfied. Library beach props, primitive mats, clams, and a calendar appear in the capture. The plan allows library dressing, so custom GLB models are not required.\n\nThe browser log may predate the packed HTML. If tests ran before the build, the launch evidence does not cover the current deliverable. This is a concrete gap: the audit requires launching the shipped binary, and stale logs leave that proof missing.\n\nThe browser test only covers boot, tick, input, attract, and viewports. It does not prove the packed HTML was launched after pack 2. The launch gate is a standing verification item under the whole contract, not merely a prior gap. If the implementer cannot produce fresh launch evidence, the objective remains refuted.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f9c77da9-fa6f-49c7-8d1b-1a5b73245efd-60","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"stat -c '%y %n' \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/tmp/grok-goal-b3947fd4d9d9/implementer/\"* \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/wo