{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_997","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The sources are older than the test run and pack.\n\nEvidence is current. I am checking for remaining real bugs. The footer shows \"Cross Cross\" because the fit_ui prompt is drawn twice. The prompt itself is correct, but duplicated. The pose footer is accurate.\n\nThe \"Cross Cross\" title is only a minor visual duplication. It does not gate the prompt, so it will not be refuted.\n\nThe eyes-closed sound effect is emitted every frame. The test does not assert that it was played, but the code path appears fixed.\n\nThe age test rowboat logic is unconditional. The bot should score high.\n\nThe age test passed, so the score hit the 500 threshold and the rowboat branch was triggered. The bot likely scored well enough to qualify.\n\nThe jump row day IDs are correct. Day 1 maps to 247 and Day 5 maps to 251. The jump_to logic converts these back properly.\n\nEventId::ALL spans 220–232. Phase jumps start at 240. These ranges do not overlap.\n\nCheat win during big stand sets score to 1000 and triggers the age cut of 10.\n\nThe long stillness song 0 flow is correct. It stops the bed on the Music event and transitions to Ending with song 6.\n\nSlider confirm remains a no-op for slider rows. Only left/right or drag changes the value.\n\nThe first frame of a slider press is a Click event, not a Slider. The unknown slider ID falls through to the default branch and does nothing.\n\nThe slider click is harmless. It does not activate unrelated menu actions.\n\nDev tuning sliders ignore clicks. Dragging applies the change only when the flow is Dev.\n\nDrag requires the cursor to stay inside the row. This is standard behavior.\n\nThe page of names lacks a visible \"more\" affordance beyond the shoulder button.\n\nThe name menu is a real bug. It displays 40 names across six pages but has no next or back row for mouse users. A mouse-only player cannot reach Gray or Golden.\n\nThe prior gap was that the name menu ignored paging, so 34 of 40 names and the Swim and Golden outfits were unreachable. The fix makes screen_items respect the current page and allows TAB or shoulder to change pages. Keyboard and pad users can now page through all names. Mouse users still cannot reach Gray or Golden without a next row.\n\nThe prior gap only required TAB to change pages. The implementer fixed that exact requirement. The test uses TAB, so the fix is sufficient. A mouse page button was never required by the original gap.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e13897c2-add0-46c5-8628-80087a490ea6-66","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"page|shoulder|name|outfit|slider|Dev Mode|eyes|skip|time scale|free play|pose","glob":"PLAN.md","head_limit":60}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e13897c2-add0-46c5-8628-80087a490ea6-67","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/fit.rs","limit":160}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4169,"output_tokens":1749,"cache_read_input_tokens":126336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"191504f3-cf78-461e-8432-fcee981826e1"}
