8,100,32,119,105,116,104,32,121,111,117,114,32,116,105,116,108,101,44,32,100,101,115,99,114,105,112,116,105,111,110,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,109,101,32,99,111,108,111,117,114,44,32,97,110,100,32,119,114,105,116,101,32,116,104,101,32,72,84,77,76,32,119,104,101,114,101,32,121,111,117,114,32,98,114,105,101,102,32,115,97,121,115,46,32,84,104,101,32,65,98,111,117,116,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,32,115,104,111,119,115,32,83,111,117,114,99,101,32,73,110,102,111,114,109,97,116,105,111,110,44,32,84,101,115,116,105,110,103,32,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,44,32,69,110,103,105,110,101,32,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,32,97,110,100,32,80,114,111,109,112,116,32,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,32,102,114,111,109,32,116,104,97,116,32,98,108,111,99,107,44,32,105,110,99,108,117,100,105,110,103,32,116,104,101,32,102,111,110,116,115,39,32,97,110,100,32,109,111,116,105,111,110,32,108,105,98,114,97,114,105,101,115,39,32,99,114,101,100,105,116,115,32,40,96,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,115,116,111,114,101,47,67,82,69,68,73,84,83,46,109,100,96,44,32,101,97,99,104,32,99,108,105,112,32,115,101,116,39,115,32,96,99,114,101,100,105,116,96,41,46,10,54,48,52,58,51,46,32,82,117,110,32,96,116,101,115,116,115,47,114,117,110,46,115,104,32,97,108,108,96,32,111,110,32,116,104,101,32,102,105,110,97,108,32,112,97,103,101,46,32,79,112,101,110,32,105,116,32,111,110,99,101,32,102,114,111,109,32,96,102,105,108,101,58,47,47,96,32,97,116,32,49,57,50,48,120,49,48,56,48,32,97,110,100,32,108,111,111,107,32,97,116,32,111,110,101,32,102,114,97,109,101,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":60,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"- **Your brief** means the brief in your own working folder. It wins on the title method, file and folder names, dates, the deliverables and the feedback questions. This plan names none of them.\"},{\"line_number\":9,\"content\":\"- **Numbers** are starting values. Tune them with the dev sliders and the bot. The structure is decided; change it only if it fails in play.\"},{\"line_number\":12,\"content\":\"- **Title:** pick it first, the way your brief says. Keep it in one constant. This plan calls it \\\"the game\\\". The resort's name, Tippy Cay, belongs to the world and does not depend on the title.\"},{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"## 1. The game in one page\"},{\"line_number\":42,\"content\":\"- Inside the game, use no Nintendo names (Wii, Mii, Balance Board and so on). The only exceptions are the Source line on the About screen and whatever your title's riff requires.\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"- No white rectangular board with dot eyes. No pale human trainer in a tank top and ponytail. No Mii-style avatars or face editors. No island or plaza from the source series.\"},{\"line_number\":45,\"content\":\"- Events have their own names and twists, as specified below.\"},{\"line_number\":52,\"content\":\"**New Stay:** choose one of 4 guest slots, pick a name from a list of about 40 funny preset names (no on-screen keyboard), pick a look (6 skin tones, 8 outfits). Then a short intro with Pip at reception, skippable.\"},{\"line_number\":66,\"content\":\"| 5 | The Big Stand, after the morning check | none | Finale, ending, free play |\"},{\"line_number\":121,\"content\":\"**Common frame:** event card (name, one-sentence goal, glyph prompts, one coach line), 3-2-1, play, result (score 0 to 1000, stars at 400, 650 and 850, a deadpan Title, minutes banked, personal best, difference from Yesterday You; Retry or Back).\"},{\"line_number\":123,\"content\":\"**Every event has:** a section of tunable numbers in `rules.toml`, a bot that earns at least 2 stars, an idle-input outcome below 1 star, a ghost lane, and an attract segment. Scenes `fit/event/<name>` start an event directly, for tools and tests.\"},{\"line_number\":129,\"content\":\"**Pose Parade** (3 poses, 20 s each). Six hand-keyed poses with deadpan names: the Patient Heron, the Apologetic Lunge, the Tired Lighthouse, the Folded Deck Chair, the Reluctant Bridge, Seated Disappointment. Day 1 uses the first three. Posey holds the pose beside you. A target ring (radius 0.30 shrinking to 0.18) drifts on a slow Lissajous path (amplitude 0.35, 0.12 Hz). Inside the ring a streak multiplier climbs x1 to x4, one step per 2 s; leaving resets it. At 12 s of pose 2 a gull lands on your head and wobble is x1.6 for 5 s (\\\"There is a bird on you. Accept the bird\\\"). A tip breaks the pose for 1.5 s. Score: time in ring weighted by multiplier. Bot: PD toward the ring centre.\"},{\"line_number\":135,\"content\":\"**Plank Standoff** (up to 60 s). Hold Brace and keep the dot in a ring shrinking from 0.40 to 0.20. Releasing, or leaving the ring for more than 1 s, collapses you in a comic flop. Fatigue ramps wobble; at 30 s add tremble; at 45 s Kettle laughs at his own joke and the nudge shakes the screen. Score: seconds survived / 60. Stars at 25, 40 and 55 s. Kettle, who has no arms, plank-talks you through it. Base the pose on one frame of `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`. Bot: survives at least 45 s.\"},{\"line_number\":147,\"content\":\"**Tide Table** (3 boards, 60 s total). You stand on a floating square raft and your lean tilts it. Roll hermit crabs in shells into tide pools. Board 1: 3 shells. Board 2: 5 shells and a moving pool. Board 3: 7 shells, bumpers and a rising tide. Fast shells skip over pools. Write the shell physics as simple 2D code (`a = tilt * g - friction * v`, wall bounce 0.5), not rapier: it is more tunable and bot-friendly. Score: shells potted plus time left. Camera: high 3/4 (tilt 62). Bot: PD steering of the nearest shell toward the nearest pool.\"},{\"line_number\":159,\"content\":\"2. A pose under rising gusts, 20 s.\"},{\"line_number\":162,\"content\":\"5. **The Long Stillness:** 30 s of nothing. Music fades to silence, the HUD vanishes except the Puck. At 15 s a fake prompt offers \\\"Press Cross to skip\\\". Pressing anything forfeits the Inner Peace bonus. Then Pip, quietly: \\\"...Oh. You're still here. Good.\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":184,\"content\":\"- **Calendar:** five big days, a stamp per completed day, then real days in free play. No tables.\"},{\"line_number\":189,\"content\":\"- **Absence comments:** the page passes today's date to the game at boot, and the save stores the last day played. \\\"You were away for 2 days. I did not count them. There were 2.\\\" Passing the date in as data keeps the rule that the sim never reads the clock.\"},{\"line_number\":190,\"content\":\"- **Saves:** versioned JSON in `localStorage`: guest slots (name, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings. Save on every change of day and every result.\"},{\"line_number\":198,\"content\":\"| **Pip** | Sky-blue round wobble cushion, two dot eyes (`blob` plan, scale 0.7, squash 2.0, plus a small valve) | Front desk and scorekeeper. Relentlessly pleasant. Keeps records of everything. Never technically insults you. Squeaky rubber voice |\"},{\"line_number\":199,\"content\":\"| **Posey** | Faceless wooden artist's mannequin (biped with eyes the colour of its skin; verified look in section 8) | Stillness. Serene, short, oddly poetic. Soft wood-block voice. It has no eyes and never blinks; \\\"This has not been discussed\\\" |\"},{\"line_number\":260,\"content\":\"name = \\\"far_sea\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":270,\"content\":\"**New props.** Hand-write format-2 JSON (`engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`) into `engine/assets/props/lib/core/<name>.json`; that folder is embedded in every build, including the browser. Use them as `asset = \\\"LIB/core/<name>\\\"`. A rebuild of `pav` is needed before `room_check` can see a new file (verified). A leaning palm (cone trunk, 6 radial ellipsoid fronds) and a kettlebell (sphere and torus) looked good on the first try. Check each with `asset_preview name=x views=true figure=true`.\"},{\"line_number\":279,\"content\":\"- **Posey:** `look = { skin = \\\"#d8b184\\\", shirt = \\\"#d8b184\\\", pants = \\\"#c79f6e\\\", shoes = \\\"#c79f6e\\\", eyes = \\\"#d8b184\\\", scale = 1.05, leg_length = 0.98 }`.\"},{\"line_number\":289,\"content\":\"**Hand-keyed clips (verified feasible).** Write readable key poses into `engine/anim/fit.json`. Test without rebuilding: in `pav repl` run `anim_reload`, then `animsheet clip=FIT/Tree frames=1 size=300 out=out/tree.png`. The build embeds every `anim/*.json`. A tree pose, a warrior lunge and a squat were recognisable at the first attempt:\"},{\"line_number\":296,\"content\":\"\\\"Warrior\\\":{\\\"clip\\\":\\\"Warrior\\\",\\\"dur\\\":2.0,\\\"loop\\\":true,\\\"tags\\\":[\\\"pose\\\"],\\\"desc\\\":\\\"Deep lunge, arms out.\\\",\\\"keys\\\":[\"},{\"line_number\":339,\"content\":\"**Rules:** at 1080p, body text at least 34 px and titles at least 64 px. Scale everything by `min(w/1920, h/1080)`, so it also works in small hub frames. Cards are white with radius 36. Focus is a thick teal outline, scale 1.05 and a soft bounce, with a sound on every move. At most 6 items visible. No tables, no dense stats, at most 4 numbers on a screen, and the About screen is pages, not a scrolling wall. Everything works by pad alone. Keyboard and mouse use the same screens. Hover moves focus, and click activates.\"},{\"line_number\":347,\"content\":\"| Dialogue | Bottom card, speaker name, 2 lines, advance glyph |\"},{\"line_number\":354,\"content\":\"| Pause | Resume, Schedule, Calendar, Wardrobe, Settings, How to Play, About, Dev Mode, Quit to Title |\"},{\"line_number\":361,\"content\":\"**Touch-only devices:** detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')`, no `(any-pointer: fine)`, and no gamepad or key seen yet. Show a centred card \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a Settings button (tap works; Settings is usable by tap). No touch controls: skip Shardfall's `touch.draw` for this game, and route touches directly to egui in `on_touch`, because the engine's touch layer otherwise treats a finger as a stick. Attract mode runs behind the card. Remove the phone-rotation hint and fullscreen-on-tap from `web/index.html`. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the card and start normally. A touch device without WebGPU cannot run the game at all, so the page's own fallback message there says both things: \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and that the game needs WebGPU.\"},{\"line_number\":363,\"content\":\"**Dev Mode** (from Pause, not shown in hub sessions). Big rows, pad-navigable, in tabs:\"},{\"line_number\":365,\"content\":\"- **Cheats:** no tips, autoplay with the bot, give minutes, unlock all, all stars, skip dialogue, win or lose this event now.\"},{\"line_number\":367,\"content\":\"- **Tuning:** live sliders, generated from `impl Tunable for Rules` with `params::list` and `params::set`, grouped by core and by event, with **Reset to Defaults** per group and for all. Must include: stiffness, damping, wobble, tip time, stick curve, key rates, each event's main difficulty number, rhythm windows, spin band, gust strength, bounce gain, Big Stand gusts.\"},{\"line_number\":381,\"content\":\"**The round, the Inter-Resort Medley:** Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup, one after another, about 2 minutes, then final score = sum of the three event scores (0 to 3000), reported as `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })`. The same seed on every copy gives the same course. On a copy, other players appear as seat-coloured figures with their names in the same event: in another lane or on a neighbouring raft or board. They affect nothing. Use the hub's own card: do not pass `card: true`.\"},{\"line_number\":389,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":390,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":391,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":392,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":393,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Highest total across three balance events wins\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":394,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":395,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":398,\"content\":\"**Hub logic lives in about 30 lines of plain JS in the page; Rust only reads and writes window fields.** This exact block passed the harness on a real engine build at 2 players, at 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, and with `scenario=host-leave`, in 14 to 19 s each, and the page ran clean outside a session (verified):\"},{\"line_number\":409,\"content\":\"    if (!info) { location.replace(location.pathname); return; }   // no hub after all\"},{\"line_number\":435,\"content\":\"**Ghost drawing.** Append extra `RenderObject`s to clones of `prev` and `curr` before `builder.build` in `App::frame`, with a high id per seat and `PuppetFrame { state, feet_offset, def: Some(look), rig: None, tint: Some((seat_rgb, 0.55)) }`; copy how `Sim::frame` builds a character's object. The sim never sees hub ghosts, so it stays deterministic. Local ghosts (Yesterday You, Play Together) come from the sim's own save data and are appended in `Sim::frame`, through the same helper, so captures show them. Names are egui text projected above the head; never insert hub names as HTML. Ghost JSON: area (event index), position, facing, lean, clip id, clip time, score. Only draw a ghost whose area matches yours. 10 messages/s stays under the 20/s limit.\"},{\"line_number\":437,\"content\":\"**The game on its own.** `AIHub.active` is false and nothing above runs. `Math.random` stays the browser's own. The hub's solo check opens the page, presses Enter and Space, and looks for errors and a drawn screen. Multiplayer exists here too, on one device:\"},{\"line_number\":466,\"content\":\"Register it as `entry::<fit::FitGame>(..., fit::build)`, `KEY = \\\"fit\\\"`. Scene names: `fit`, `fit/medley`, `fit/event/<name>`. Read data with `games::level_text(\\\"fit/rules\\\", include_str!(\\\"rules.toml\\\"))`: running from `engine/`, it reads the disk file, so text, numbers and set layouts change with no rebuild. Do not put sets in `engine/rooms/`: that folder feeds the pavilion demo.\"},{\"line_number\":492,\"content\":\"| `pav_core/src/games/mod.rs`, `sim.rs` | `Game::frozen()` with a default of false (add it to the trait and its `DynGame` and `GameBox` wrappers); when true, `step_inner` skips everything after `play_pre` except tick++ and events | Pause freezes the world while menus still run |\"},{\"line_number\":518,\"content\":\"**About text stays in plain text in the page.** Put it in `<script id=\\\"about-data\\\" type=\\\"application/json\\\">` in the `<head>`, not in the wasm. The agent that imports the game edits the Usage line later, and it cannot edit text inside a gzipped wasm. Rust reads it from `__gameBoot.about`.\"},{\"line_number\":525,\"content\":\"- `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene fit --title \\\"...\\\" --out <path>`: 2m24 first time, 52 s after. Output about 11.4 MB. The wasm target and `wasm-bindgen 0.2.129` are ready. `--out` takes your brief's file name.\"},{\"line_number\":531,\"content\":\"- Chromium flags that work: `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`. The set with `--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader` also works. Only Chromium has WebGPU here: Firefox and WebKit show the page's no-WebGPU message.\"},{\"line_number\":545,\"content\":\"- `egui::Context::set_fonts` takes effect next pass; using a font family in the same pass panics \\\"not bound to any fonts\\\". Install fonts before the first `run_ui`, in `App::new` and in `Headless::frame`, which makes a new context per frame. In the browser that panic stopped the frame loop with nothing on the page to say so: `__gameStatus` simply stopped changing (verified). Log console errors and assert that the tick advances in every browser test.\"},{\"line_number\":567,\"content\":\"- Pause freezes the world. Settings: music defaults to 0.10. Dev sliders change values and reset. Dev jump lands where it says.\"},{\"line_number\":574,\"content\":\"**`browser` (Playwright, one browser, 320x180, `file://`):** boots with no errors; `__gameStatus` appears; the pad stub moves focus and confirms; keyboard does the same; mouse hover moves focus and click activates, using rects the UI publishes in `window.__gameUi`; prompts switch with the device; Settings has the Xbox option; attract starts after 10 s and any input exits it; music reaches about 10% by the sound patch. Touch: Chromium with a phone and a tablet profile (it has WebGPU) must show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", run attract, and respond to a Settings tap by `page.touchscreen.tap`. WebKit with an iPhone profile, which has no WebGPU here, must show the fallback message from section 11.\"},{\"line_number\":576,\"content\":\"**`hub`:** copy the page and `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` into one served folder, open `harness.html?game=<page>&players=N&auto=1`, wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === \\\"true\\\"`, and require `window.__hubCheck.pass`. Run 2 players; 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and `scenario=host-leave`. Then a solo check like the hub's: open outside a session, press Enter and Space, expect no errors, `AIHub.active` false, and `Math.random` not seeded. Also byte-compare the pasted client with `hub/session.js`.\"},{\"line_number\":586,\"content\":\"1. **Setup.** Pick the title. `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall engine` (it is public). Copy the starter to `games/fit/`, register it, build `pav` and the web page, first `tests/run.sh`.\"},{\"line_number\":593,\"content\":\"8. **Shell.** Attract, Settings, Dev Mode, touch-only card, How to Play, About.\"},{\"line_number\":595,\"content\":\"10. **Polish.** Write the script to full length, feel pass on every event using the sliders, extra set dressing, particles, transitions, stingers.\"},{\"line_number\":602,\"content\":\"1. Write the exit interview your brief names. Fill every field honestly; `usage` is exactly \\\"added on import\\\". Suggested `aiHub` values: type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source `Wii Fit`, series `Wii Fit`, players `1–4`, tags from `3d`, `third-person`, `comedy`, `sports`, `versus`, `low-poly`. Check that it parses.\"},{\"line_number\":603,\"content\":\"2. Run `tools/build.sh`: copy the exit interview into `about-data` in the page, run the single-file build with your title, description and theme colour, and write the HTML where your brief says. The About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback from that block, including the fonts' and motion libraries' credits (`engine/store/CREDITS.md`, each clip set's `credit`).\"},{\"line_number\":604,\"content\":\"3. Run `tests/run.sh all` on the final page. Open it once from `file://` at 1920x1080 and look at one frame.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e13897c2-add0-46c5-8628-80087a490ea6-67","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! 10-foot painter for Wobble Minutes. The sim owns the layout; this only draws it.\\n\\nuse std::sync::Arc;\\n\\nuse egui::{Color32, CornerRadius, FontFamily, FontId, Pos2, Rect, Stroke, StrokeKind, Vec2};\\n\\nuse pav_core::fit_ui::FitUi;\\n\\nconst FREDOKA: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\\\"../fonts/Fredoka_600SemiBold.ttf\\\");\\n10→const NUNITO: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\\\"../fonts/Nunito_700Bold.ttf\\\");\\n\\n/// Title and body sizes at this window. At 1920×1080 they are 64 and 34.\\npub fn type_px(width: f32, height: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let scale = (width / 1920.0).min(height / 1080.0).max(0.0);\\n    (64.0 * scale, 34.0 * scale)\\n}\\n\\npub fn install_fonts(ctx: &egui::Context) {\\n    let mut fonts = egui::FontDefinitions::default();\\n20→    fonts.font_data.insert(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into(), Arc::new(egui::FontData::from_static(FREDOKA)));\\n    fonts.font_data.insert(\\\"Nunito\\\".into(), Arc::new(egui::FontData::from_static(NUNITO)));\\n    fonts.families.insert(FontFamily::Name(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into()), vec![\\\"Fredoka\\\".into(), \\\"Nunito\\\".into()]);\\n    fonts.families.insert(FontFamily::Name(\\\"Nunito\\\".into()), vec![\\\"Nunito\\\".into()]);\\n    if let Some(prop) = fonts.families.get_mut(&FontFamily::Proportional) {\\n        prop.insert(0, \\\"Nunito\\\".into());\\n    }\\n    ctx.set_fonts(fonts);\\n}\\n\\n30→fn text(painter: &egui::Painter, pos: Pos2, text: &str, size: f32, family: FontFamily, color: Color32) {\\n    if text.is_empty() || size < 1.0 {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let galley = painter.layout_no_wrap(text.to_string(), FontId::new(size, family), color);\\n    painter.galley(pos, galley, color);\\n}\\n\\n/// Draws the stay UI in pixels. `scale` is `min(w/1920, h/1080)`.\\npub fn draw(ctx: &egui::Context, ui: &FitUi) {\\n40→    let screen = ctx.content_rect();\\n    if screen.width() < 2.0 || screen.height() < 2.0 {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let (title_px, body_px) = type_px(screen.width(), screen.height());\\n    let scale = title_px / 64.0;\\n    let painter = ctx.layer_painter(egui::LayerId::new(egui::Order::Foreground, egui::Id::new(\\\"wobble_minutes\\\")));\\n    if ui.dim > 0.01 {\\n        let a = (ui.dim.clamp(0.0, 1.0) * 255.0) as u8;\\n        painter.rect_filled(screen, CornerRadius::ZERO, Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(4, 6, 10, a));\\n50→    }\\n    let ink = Color32::from_rgb(28, 48, 56);\\n    let teal = Color32::from_rgb(14, 122, 132);\\n    let fred = FontFamily::Name(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into());\\n    let nun = FontFamily::Name(\\\"Nunito\\\".into());\\n\\n    if ui.demo {\\n        let ribbon = Rect::from_min_size(screen.right_top() + Vec2::new(-220.0 * scale, 18.0 * scale), Vec2::new(200.0 * scale, 64.0 * scale));\\n        painter.rect_filled(ribbon, CornerRadius::from(18.0 * scale), Color32::from_rgb(214, 92, 58));\\n        text(&painter, ribbon.left_top() + Vec2::new(28.0 * scale, 8.0 * scale), \\\"DEMO\\\", title_px * 0.6, fred.clone(), Color32::WHITE);\\n60→    }\\n\\n    text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.center().x - title_px * ui.title.chars().count() as f32 * 0.28, 36.0 * scale), &ui.title, title_px, fred.clone(), Color32::WHITE);\\n\\n    if !ui.big.is_empty() {\\n        text(\\n            &painter,\\n            Pos2::new(screen.center().x - title_px * ui.big.chars().count() as f32 * 0.4, screen.height() * 0.16),\\n            &ui.big,\\n            title_px * 1.4,\\n70→            fred.clone(),\\n            Color32::from_rgb(255, 214, 120),\\n        );\\n    }\\n\\n    let mut y = 120.0 * scale;\\n    for line in ui.lines.iter().take(2) {\\n        text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.width() * 0.18, y), line, body_px, nun.clone(), Color32::from_rgb(230, 244, 242));\\n        y += body_px * 1.25;\\n    }\\n80→\\n    for it in &ui.items {\\n        let r = Rect::from_min_size(\\n            Pos2::new(screen.left() + it.rect[0] * screen.width(), screen.top() + it.rect[1] * screen.height()),\\n            Vec2::new(it.rect[2] * screen.width(), it.rect[3] * screen.height()),\\n        );\\n        painter.rect_filled(r, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Color32::WHITE);\\n        if it.id == ui.focus {\\n            painter.rect_stroke(r, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Stroke::new((8.0 * scale).max(2.0), teal), StrokeKind::Outside);\\n        }\\n90→        text(&painter, r.left_center() + Vec2::new(28.0 * scale, -body_px * 0.55), &it.label, body_px, nun.clone(), ink);\\n    }\\n\\n    if let Some([x, y, ring, _]) = ui.puck {\\n        let c = Pos2::new(screen.center().x, screen.height() * 0.72);\\n        let rad = (screen.height() * 0.16 * ring).max(8.0);\\n        painter.circle_stroke(c, rad, Stroke::new((4.0 * scale).max(1.5), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 255, 255, 180)));\\n        for p in &ui.trace {\\n            let d = c + Vec2::new(p[0], -p[1]) * rad;\\n            painter.circle_filled(d, (6.0 * scale).max(2.0), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 214, 120, 170));\\n100→        }\\n        let dot = c + Vec2::new(x, -y) * rad;\\n        painter.circle_filled(dot, (14.0 * scale).max(3.0), Color32::from_rgb(255, 120, 96));\\n    }\\n    if !ui.overlay.is_empty() {\\n        text(&painter, Pos2::new(28.0 * scale, 28.0 * scale), &ui.overlay, body_px * 0.7, nun.clone(), Color32::from_rgb(230, 244, 242));\\n    }\\n\\n    if ui.touch_card {\\n        let card = Rect::from_center_size(screen.center(), Vec2::new(screen.width() * 0.7, body_px * 4.0));\\n110→        painter.rect_filled(card, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 255, 255, 235));\\n        text(&painter, card.left_top() + Vec2::new(24.0 * scale, 16.0 * scale), \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", body_px, nun.clone(), ink);\\n    }\\n\\n    let prompt = if ui.footer.is_empty() { ui.glyph.clone() } else { format!(\\\"{}   {}\\\", ui.glyph, ui.footer) };\\n    text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.width() * 0.28, screen.height() - body_px * 1.6), &prompt, body_px, nun, Color32::WHITE);\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n120→    use super::*;\\n    use pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim};\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn type_holds_the_ten_foot_floor() {\\n        let (title, body) = type_px(1920.0, 1080.0);\\n        assert!(title >= 64.0 && body >= 34.0, \\\"{title} {body}\\\");\\n        let (small_t, _) = type_px(320.0, 180.0);\\n        assert!(small_t < 64.0 && small_t > 8.0, \\\"{small_t}\\\");\\n    }\\n130→\\n    #[test]\\n    fn title_prompts_follow_the_device() {\\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"fit\\\", 1).expect(\\\"fit\\\");\\n        let cases = [(1u8, false, \\\"Cross\\\"), (1, true, \\\"A\\\"), (2, false, \\\"Space\\\"), (3, false, \\\"Click\\\")];\\n        for (device, xbox, word) in cases {\\n            {\\n                let g = sim.state.play.as_mut().unwrap().get_mut::<pav_core::games::fit::FitGame>().unwrap();\\n                g.settings.xbox = xbox;\\n            }\\n140→            sim.step(&InputFrame { device, ..Default::default() });\\n            let frame = sim.frame();\\n            let mut head = crate::headless::Headless::default();\\n            let mut drawn = head.frame(None, &frame.hud, glam::Mat4::IDENTITY, 1920, 1080, Default::default());\\n            let blob = drawn.reading.hud.iter().map(|t| t.text.as_str()).collect::<Vec<_>>().join(\\\" | \\\");\\n            drawn.paint.textures.clear();\\n            assert!(blob.contains(\\\"Wobble Minutes\\\"), \\\"{blob}\\\");\\n            assert!(blob.contains(\\\"New Stay\\\"), \\\"{blob}\\\");\\n            assert!(blob.contains(word), \\\"device {device} xbox {xbox}: {blob}\\\");\\n        }\\n150→    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! 10-foot painter for Wobble Minutes. The sim owns the layout; this only draws it.\\n\\nuse std::sync::Arc;\\n\\nuse egui::{Color32, CornerRadius, FontFamily, FontId, Pos2, Rect, Stroke, StrokeKind, Vec2};\\n\\nuse pav_core::fit_ui::FitUi;\\n\\nconst FREDOKA: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\\\"../fonts/Fredoka_600SemiBold.ttf\\\");\\n10→const NUNITO: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\\\"../fonts/Nunito_700Bold.ttf\\\");\\n\\n/// Title and body sizes at this window. At 1920×1080 they are 64 and 34.\\npub fn type_px(width: f32, height: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let scale = (width / 1920.0).min(height / 1080.0).max(0.0);\\n    (64.0 * scale, 34.0 * scale)\\n}\\n\\npub fn install_fonts(ctx: &egui::Context) {\\n    let mut fonts = egui::FontDefinitions::default();\\n20→    fonts.font_data.insert(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into(), Arc::new(egui::FontData::from_static(FREDOKA)));\\n    fonts.font_data.insert(\\\"Nunito\\\".into(), Arc::new(egui::FontData::from_static(NUNITO)));\\n    fonts.families.insert(FontFamily::Name(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into()), vec![\\\"Fredoka\\\".into(), \\\"Nunito\\\".into()]);\\n    fonts.families.insert(FontFamily::Name(\\\"Nunito\\\".into()), vec![\\\"Nunito\\\".into()]);\\n    if let Some(prop) = fonts.families.get_mut(&FontFamily::Proportional) {\\n        prop.insert(0, \\\"Nunito\\\".into());\\n    }\\n    ctx.set_fonts(fonts);\\n}\\n\\n30→fn text(painter: &egui::Painter, pos: Pos2, text: &str, size: f32, family: FontFamily, color: Color32) {\\n    if text.is_empty() || size < 1.0 {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let galley = painter.layout_no_wrap(text.to_string(), FontId::new(size, family), color);\\n    painter.galley(pos, galley, color);\\n}\\n\\n/// Draws the stay UI in pixels. `scale` is `min(w/1920, h/1080)`.\\npub fn draw(ctx: &egui::Context, ui: &FitUi) {\\n40→    let screen = ctx.content_rect();\\n    if screen.width() < 2.0 || screen.height() < 2.0 {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let (title_px, body_px) = type_px(screen.width(), screen.height());\\n    let scale = title_px / 64.0;\\n    let painter = ctx.layer_painter(egui::LayerId::new(egui::Order::Foreground, egui::Id::new(\\\"wobble_minutes\\\")));\\n    if ui.dim > 0.01 {\\n        let a = (ui.dim.clamp(0.0, 1.0) * 255.0) as u8;\\n        painter.rect_filled(screen, CornerRadius::ZERO, Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(4, 6, 10, a));\\n50→    }\\n    let ink = Color32::from_rgb(28, 48, 56);\\n    let teal = Color32::from_rgb(14, 122, 132);\\n    let fred = FontFamily::Name(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into());\\n    let nun = FontFamily::Name(\\\"Nunito\\\".into());\\n\\n    if ui.demo {\\n        let ribbon = Rect::from_min_size(screen.right_top() + Vec2::new(-220.0 * scale, 18.0 * scale), Vec2::new(200.0 * scale, 64.0 * scale));\\n        painter.rect_filled(ribbon, CornerRadius::from(18.0 * scale), Color32::from_rgb(214, 92, 58));\\n        text(&painter, ribbon.left_top() + Vec2::new(28.0 * scale, 8.0 * scale), \\\"DEMO\\\", title_px * 0.6, fred.clone(), Color32::WHITE);\\n60→    }\\n\\n    text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.center().x - title_px * ui.title.chars().count() as f32 * 0.28, 36.0 * scale), &ui.title, title_px, fred.clone(), Color32::WHITE);\\n\\n    if !ui.big.is_empty() {\\n        text(\\n            &painter,\\n            Pos2::new(screen.center().x - title_px * ui.big.chars().count() as f32 * 0.4, screen.height() * 0.16),\\n            &ui.big,\\n            title_px * 1.4,\\n70→            fred.clone(),\\n            Color32::from_rgb(255, 214, 120),\\n        );\\n    }\\n\\n    let mut y = 120.0 * scale;\\n    for line in ui.lines.iter().take(2) {\\n        text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.width() * 0.18, y), line, body_px, nun.clone(), Color32::from_rgb(230, 244, 242));\\n        y += body_px * 1.25;\\n    }\\n80→\\n    for it in &ui.items {\\n        let r = Rect::from_min_size(\\n            Pos2::new(screen.left() + it.rect[0] * screen.width(), screen.top() + it.rect[1] * screen.height()),\\n            Vec2::new(it.rect[2] * screen.width(), it.rect[3] * screen.height()),\\n        );\\n        painter.rect_filled(r, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Color32::WHITE);\\n        if it.id == ui.focus {\\n            painter.rect_stroke(r, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Stroke::new((8.0 * scale).max(2.0), teal), StrokeKind::Outside);\\n        }\\n90→        text(&painter, r.left_center() + Vec2::new(28.0 * scale, -body_px * 0.55), &it.label, body_px, nun.clone(), ink);\\n    }\\n\\n    if let Some([x, y, ring, _]) = ui.puck {\\n        let c = Pos2::new(screen.center().x, screen.height() * 0.72);\\n        let rad = (screen.height() * 0.16 * ring).max(8.0);\\n        painter.circle_stroke(c, rad, Stroke::new((4.0 * scale).max(1.5), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 255, 255, 180)));\\n        for p in &ui.trace {\\n            let d = c + Vec2::new(p[0], -p[1]) * rad;\\n            painter.circle_filled(d, (6.0 * scale).max(2.0), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 214, 120, 170));\\n100→        }\\n        let dot = c + Vec2::new(x, -y) * rad;\\n        painter.circle_filled(dot, (14.0 * scale).max(3.0), Color32::from_rgb(255, 120, 96));\\n    }\\n    if !ui.overlay.is_empty() {\\n        text(&painter, Pos2::new(28.0 * scale, 28.0 * scale), &ui.overlay, body_px * 0.7, nun.clone(), Color32::from_rgb(230, 244, 242));\\n    }\\n\\n    if ui.touch_card {\\n        let card = Rect::from_center_size(screen.center(), Vec2::new(screen.width() * 0.7, body_px * 4.0));\\n110→        painter.rect_filled(card, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 255, 255, 235));\\n        text(&painter, card.left_top() + Vec2::new(24.0 * scale, 16.0 * scale), \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", body_px, nun.clone(), ink);\\n    }\\n\\n    let prompt = if ui.footer.is_empty() { ui.glyph.clone() } else { format!(\\\"{}   {}\\\", ui.glyph, ui.footer) };\\n    text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.width() * 0.28, screen.height() - body_px * 1.6), &prompt, body_px, nun, Color32::WHITE);\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n120→    use super::*;\\n    use pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim};\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn type_holds_the_ten_foot_floor() {\\n        let (title, body) = type_px(1920.0, 1080.0);\\n        assert!(title >= 64.0 && body >= 34.0, \\\"{title} {body}\\\");\\n        let (small_t, _) = type_px(320.0, 180.0);\\n        assert!(small_t < 64.0 && small_t > 8.0, \\\"{small_t}\\\");\\n    }\\n130→\\n    #[test]\\n    fn title_prompts_follow_the_device() {\\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"fit\\\", 1).expect(\\\"fit\\\");\\n        let cases = [(1u8, false, \\\"Cross\\\"), (1, true, \\\"A\\\"), (2, false, \\\"Space\\\"), (3, false, \\\"Click\\\")];\\n        for (device, xbox, word) in cases {\\n            {\\n                let g = sim.state.play.as_mut().unwrap().get_mut::<pav_core::games::fit::FitGame>().unwrap();\\n                g.settings.xbox = xbox;\\n            }\\n140→            sim.step(&InputFrame { device, ..Default::default() });\\n            let frame = sim.frame();\\n            let mut head = crate::headless::Headless::default();\\n            let mut drawn = head.frame(None, &frame.hud, glam::Mat4::IDENTITY, 1920, 1080, Default::default());\\n            let blob = drawn.reading.hud.iter().map(|t| t.text.as_str()).collect::<Vec<_>>().join(\\\" | \\\");\\n            drawn.paint.textures.clear();\\n            assert!(blob.contains(\\\"Wobble Minutes\\\"), \\\"{blob}\\\");\\n            assert!(blob.contains(\\\"New Stay\\\"), \\\"{blob}\\\");\\n            assert!(blob.contains(word), \\\"device {device} xbox {xbox}: {blob}\\\");\\n        }\\n150→    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/fit.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":160,\"raw_output\":\"//! 10-foot painter for Wobble Minutes. The sim owns the layout; this only draws it.\\n\\nuse std::sync::Arc;\\n\\nuse egui::{Color32, CornerRadius, FontFamily, FontId, Pos2, Rect, Stroke, StrokeKind, Vec2};\\n\\nuse pav_core::fit_ui::FitUi;\\n\\nconst FREDOKA: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\\\"../fonts/Fredoka_600SemiBold.ttf\\\");\\nconst NUNITO: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\\\"../fonts/Nunito_700Bold.ttf\\\");\\n\\n/// Title and body sizes at this window. At 1920×1080 they are 64 and 34.\\npub fn type_px(width: f32, height: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let scale = (width / 1920.0).min(height / 1080.0).max(0.0);\\n    (64.0 * scale, 34.0 * scale)\\n}\\n\\npub fn install_fonts(ctx: &egui::Context) {\\n    let mut fonts = egui::FontDefinitions::default();\\n    fonts.font_data.insert(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into(), Arc::new(egui::FontData::from_static(FREDOKA)));\\n    fonts.font_data.insert(\\\"Nunito\\\".into(), Arc::new(egui::FontData::from_static(NUNITO)));\\n    fonts.families.insert(FontFamily::Name(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into()), vec![\\\"Fredoka\\\".into(), \\\"Nunito\\\".into()]);\\n    fonts.families.insert(FontFamily::Name(\\\"Nunito\\\".into()), vec![\\\"Nunito\\\".into()]);\\n    if let Some(prop) = fonts.families.get_mut(&FontFamily::Proportional) {\\n        prop.insert(0, \\\"Nunito\\\".into());\\n    }\\n    ctx.set_fonts(fonts);\\n}\\n\\nfn text(painter: &egui::Painter, pos: Pos2, text: &str, size: f32, family: FontFamily, color: Color32) {\\n    if text.is_empty() || size < 1.0 {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let galley = painter.layout_no_wrap(text.to_string(), FontId::new(size, family), color);\\n    painter.galley(pos, galley, color);\\n}\\n\\n/// Draws the stay UI in pixels. `scale` is `min(w/1920, h/1080)`.\\npub fn draw(ctx: &egui::Context, ui: &FitUi) {\\n    let screen = ctx.content_rect();\\n    if screen.width() < 2.0 || screen.height() < 2.0 {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let (title_px, body_px) = type_px(screen.width(), screen.height());\\n    let scale = title_px / 64.0;\\n    let painter = ctx.layer_painter(egui::LayerId::new(egui::Order::Foreground, egui::Id::new(\\\"wobble_minutes\\\")));\\n    if ui.dim > 0.01 {\\n        let a = (ui.dim.clamp(0.0, 1.0) * 255.0) as u8;\\n        painter.rect_filled(screen, CornerRadius::ZERO, Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(4, 6, 10, a));\\n    }\\n    let ink = Color32::from_rgb(28, 48, 56);\\n    let teal = Color32::from_rgb(14, 122, 132);\\n    let fred = FontFamily::Name(\\\"Fredoka\\\".into());\\n    let nun = FontFamily::Name(\\\"Nunito\\\".into());\\n\\n    if ui.demo {\\n        let ribbon = Rect::from_min_size(screen.right_top() + Vec2::new(-220.0 * scale, 18.0 * scale), Vec2::new(200.0 * scale, 64.0 * scale));\\n        painter.rect_filled(ribbon, CornerRadius::from(18.0 * scale), Color32::from_rgb(214, 92, 58));\\n        text(&painter, ribbon.left_top() + Vec2::new(28.0 * scale, 8.0 * scale), \\\"DEMO\\\", title_px * 0.6, fred.clone(), Color32::WHITE);\\n    }\\n\\n    text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.center().x - title_px * ui.title.chars().count() as f32 * 0.28, 36.0 * scale), &ui.title, title_px, fred.clone(), Color32::WHITE);\\n\\n    if !ui.big.is_empty() {\\n        text(\\n            &painter,\\n            Pos2::new(screen.center().x - title_px * ui.big.chars().count() as f32 * 0.4, screen.height() * 0.16),\\n            &ui.big,\\n            title_px * 1.4,\\n            fred.clone(),\\n            Color32::from_rgb(255, 214, 120),\\n        );\\n    }\\n\\n    let mut y = 120.0 * scale;\\n    for line in ui.lines.iter().take(2) {\\n        text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.width() * 0.18, y), line, body_px, nun.clone(), Color32::from_rgb(230, 244, 242));\\n        y += body_px * 1.25;\\n    }\\n\\n    for it in &ui.items {\\n        let r = Rect::from_min_size(\\n            Pos2::new(screen.left() + it.rect[0] * screen.width(), screen.top() + it.rect[1] * screen.height()),\\n            Vec2::new(it.rect[2] * screen.width(), it.rect[3] * screen.height()),\\n        );\\n        painter.rect_filled(r, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Color32::WHITE);\\n        if it.id == ui.focus {\\n            painter.rect_stroke(r, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Stroke::new((8.0 * scale).max(2.0), teal), StrokeKind::Outside);\\n        }\\n        text(&painter, r.left_center() + Vec2::new(28.0 * scale, -body_px * 0.55), &it.label, body_px, nun.clone(), ink);\\n    }\\n\\n    if let Some([x, y, ring, _]) = ui.puck {\\n        let c = Pos2::new(screen.center().x, screen.height() * 0.72);\\n        let rad = (screen.height() * 0.16 * ring).max(8.0);\\n        painter.circle_stroke(c, rad, Stroke::new((4.0 * scale).max(1.5), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 255, 255, 180)));\\n        for p in &ui.trace {\\n            let d = c + Vec2::new(p[0], -p[1]) * rad;\\n            painter.circle_filled(d, (6.0 * scale).max(2.0), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 214, 120, 170));\\n        }\\n        let dot = c + Vec2::new(x, -y) * rad;\\n        painter.circle_filled(dot, (14.0 * scale).max(3.0), Color32::from_rgb(255, 120, 96));\\n    }\\n    if !ui.overlay.is_empty() {\\n        text(&painter, Pos2::new(28.0 * scale, 28.0 * scale), &ui.overlay, body_px * 0.7, nun.clone(), Color32::from_rgb(230, 244, 242));\\n    }\\n\\n    if ui.touch_card {\\n        let card = Rect::from_center_size(screen.center(), Vec2::new(screen.width() * 0.7, body_px * 4.0));\\n        painter.rect_filled(card, CornerRadius::from(36.0 * scale), Color32::from_rgba_unmultiplied(255, 255, 255, 235));\\n        text(&painter, card.left_top() + Vec2::new(24.0 * scale, 16.0 * scale), \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", body_px, nun.clone(), ink);\\n    }\\n\\n    let prompt = if ui.footer.is_empty() { ui.glyph.clone() } else { format!(\\\"{}   {}\\\", ui.glyph, ui.footer) };\\n    text(&painter, Pos2::new(screen.width() * 0.28, screen.height() - body_px * 1.6), &prompt, body_px, nun, Color32::WHITE);\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n    use pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim};\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn type_holds_the_ten_foot_floor() {\\n        let (title, body) = type_px(1920.0, 1080.0);\\n        assert!(title >= 64.0 && body >= 34.0, \\\"{title} {body}\\\");\\n        let (small_t, _) = type_px(320.0, 180.0);\\n        assert!(small_t < 64.0 && small_t > 8.0, \\\"{small_t}\\\");\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn title_prompts_follow_the_device() {\\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"fit\\\", 1).expect(\\\"fit\\\");\\n        let cases = [(1u8, false, \\\"Cross\\\"), (1, true, \\\"A\\\"), (2, false, \\\"Space\\\"), (3, false, \\\"Click\\\")];\\n        for (device, xbox, word) in cases {\\n            {\\n                let g = sim.state.play.as_mut().unwrap().get_mut::<pav_core::games::fit::FitGame>().unwrap();\\n                g.settings.xbox = xbox;\\n            }\\n            sim.step(&InputFrame { device, ..Default::default() });\\n            let frame = sim.frame();\\n            let mut head = crate::headless::Headless::default();\\n            let mut drawn = head.frame(None, &frame.hud, glam::Mat4::IDENTITY, 1920, 1080, Default::default());\\n            let blob = drawn.reading.hud.iter().map(|t| t.text.as_str()).collect::<Vec<_>>().join(\\\" | \\\");\\n            drawn.paint.textures.clear();\\n            assert!(blob.contains(\\\"Wobble Minutes\\\"), \\\"{blob}\\\");\\n            assert!(blob.contains(\\\"New Stay\\\"), \\\"{blob}\\\");\\n            assert!(blob.contains(word), \\\"device {device} xbox {xbox}: {blob}\\\");\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":151}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"992810b4-0937-41c2-88d6-0e16aafb7df2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_998","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking whether the plan requirements still hold or have become new defects.\n\nThe Pose Parade uses generic poses like Tree and Warrior instead of the six named ones from the plan. Day 1 only uses three poses, not the six specified.\n\nThe prior gap only required poses to exist, not their specific names. The six named poses are criterion 3 \"named twists\". If the UI uses generic names like Tree and Warrior instead of Patient Heron, this is a content gap that existed in round 1 but was never flagged.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule prevents new objections from being style preferences. Round 1 never required the six named poses, so that naming gap is a genuine defect.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule does not bar new objections when a prior round failed to flag an unmet gating criterion. The verifier must inspect the player-facing UI to confirm whether the poses display as generic names like Tree or as the six named poses from the plan.\n\nThe plan's example JSON already uses \"Tree\" and \"Warrior\" as clip names. This suggests the generic pose names may be intentional. The verifier should check whether the script text itself names the six required poses, or if the display names simply match the internal clip identifiers.\n\nThe script text at line 289 names the poses as \"a tree pose, a warrior lunge and a squat\". The JSON example also uses \"Warrior\", so the internal clip names match the plan's verified example. The six named poses are display labels rather than clip identifiers. I will grep the UI code to confirm whether those display names actually appear.\n\nThe Pause menu is missing its required rows. The plan specifies a hub-style pause menu with Resume, Schedule, Calendar, Wardrobe, Settings, How to Play, About, Dev Mode, and Quit to Title. The current code instead freezes the world and jumps directly to Dev Mode. This violates the derived acceptance criteria that require a pause menu containing Dev Mode.\n\nThe pause menu may actually be correct. The prior gap only required jump, cheats, and time scale. The harness criteria say pause opens Dev Mode directly, so Schedule and Quit to Title are not new requirements. The Dev Mode screen already includes Wardrobe, Calendar, Settings, About, How to Stand, and Resume.\n\nThe name selection screen has six items but no on-screen Back button. Mouse users have no way to return from that page.\n\nThe Long Stillness sequence stops song 0 instantly instead of fading to silence. The plan requires a fifteen-second fade and a fake prompt.\n\nThe Long Stillness HUD vanishes except the Puck. The skip prompt appears at fifteen seconds. The score banner clears.\n\nThe skip prompt reads \"Press Cross to skip\". This matches the plan and the test.\n\nInner Peace bonus forfeit halves the score. Otherwise it adds two hundred points.\n\nThe plan requires hand-writing format-2 JSON into engine/assets/props/lib/core/ for a leaning palm and a kettlebell.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ac1bb6ec-4c02-4d51-b951-80650b94e0bf-68","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^fn |#\\[ignore\\]|#\\[test\\]","glob":"**/pav_core/tests/fit.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ac1bb6ec-4c02-4d51-b951-80650b94e0bf-69","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"TODO|unimplemented!|todo!","glob":"**/games/fit/**/*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ac1bb6ec-4c02-4d51-b951-80650b94e0bf-70","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Patient Heron|pose_i|There is a bird","glob":"**/games/fit/**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8441,"output_tokens":3006,"cache_read_input_tokens":130432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"02267a64-cd8d-480a-b553-69f37c03051b"}
