{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1018","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nI will read PLAN.md to verify Dev Mode requirements.\n\nI also need to spot-check the implementations directly. I will check if time_scale is actually applied, whether big stand skip prompts and forfeits work, if eyes closed tone is correct, if poses and beach props are present, and if sliders wire through the simulation. I also need to confirm whether pick() searches all items or only the current page, since the schedule test selects \"Cannonball\" without paging.\n\nThe schedule test passed without paging, so pick() must be paging through items or Cannonball is on the first page.The tests-core.log shows 18 passed tests, but fit.rs contains more.\n\nSchedule item IDs are global indices (`100 + i`) drawn from the full list before skipping, not page-local. I am counting events to see if Cannonball appears on the first page.\n\nCounting the test names in fit.rs to reconcile the discrepancy.\n\nEleven schedule events remain after filtering out Check and Big Stand. Cannonball is the 11th item, so it falls on page two of a four-item page. The schedule test passed without paging, which confirms that pick() now pages through items across pages. This resolves the prior bug where .take(4) ignored pagination.\n\nfit.rs contains 19 tests, not 18. The final response claims 19 passed, which conflicts with the log showing 18. The targeted log was truncated after 11 tests. I will read the remaining logs and check the slider compilation failure.\n\nThe 18-pass log likely predates the current code. The implementer probably added the 19th test after the run was captured. I still need to verify whether the slider retry passed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a8d2e3c5-46b0-499c-8f4f-f685d9ed06d4-18","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn pick|fn confirm|MENU_RIGHT|Slider\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.bui