{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1022","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" name counts, check hub.toml properties, review anim fit.json, and re-examine the Back button mapping. I am now checking whether `pick(\"Back\")` could match a label from a previous screen if activation returns to the root dev menu. The activate_dev handler for tab 3 only calls set_time, so it does not change tabs.\n\nThe Back button was likely removed from the time tab after the test run, which would explain why the prior 18-pass log is stale. I will run just the long_stillness test to confirm whether this is a real defect.\n\nA single filtered test run is a cheap spot-check. The targeted log compiled 100 cratesChecking the age cut code around line 900 in two minutes, so one test should finish and the desired_song quickly. I will run just the long_stillness section. test to confirm whether the Back button bug is real.\n\nChecking if time_scale 0 freezes during the long stillness test. The test sets 4x speed, pauses to jump, then waits for act_sub >= 15. With 4x scaling, 15 seconds of simulation time equals roughly 3.75 real seconds.\n\nThe 4x speed test passed with 225 steps against a 400 guard.\n\nThe Back button is The pose parade test reachable through the now passes, confirming physical BACK input, anim/fit.json exists not just a screen label. The pre() handler calls and the Tree clip is go_back when BACK is registered. The age pressed, and that function formula at line 929 still needs review. resets the Dev tab to 0. This means the player can exit the time menu even without a visible Back row.\n\nNeed to verify whether apply_body actually sets the clip on the puppet or merely reports it in status.\n\nBeach props require checking hub.toml to determine if they are pre-existing\n\nThe Back button is reachable via the physical BACK input, yet the test expects a visible \"Back\" row. The 18-pass log likely predates the current source, or the test was not run against this code. I am now counting the exact `#[test]` lines in fit.rs to verify the discrepancy. engine props or newly added room entities.\n\nCaptured images should be reviewed for additional context.\n\nThe 18 versus 19 test discrepancy is notable: FINAL_RESPONSE claims 19 tests passed, but the captured 18-test run shows no evidence of a 19th test. This suggests the 19th test may be unrun or missing from the logs.\n\nThe captured log is stale relative to the current source, which now contains 19 tests. The verification plan requires running the command twice to confirm the full suite passes. Missing evidence that the current suite passes","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-043a1d02-ac91-4fe2-8d31-b0b9d7ded49a-25","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/tmp/grok-goal-b3947fd4d9d9/implementer/tests-targeted.log","offset":70,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-043a1d02-ac91-4fe2-8d31-b0b9d7ded49a-26","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"passed|failed|EXIT|error","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/tmp/grok-goal-b3947fd4d9d9/implementer","glob":"*.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-043a1d02-ac91-4fe2-8d31-b0b9d7ded49a-27","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn desired_song|fn menu_flow|names =|outfits","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-043a1d02-ac91-4fe2-8d31-b0b9d7ded49a-28","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"FIT/Tree|beach|umbrella|towel|mat","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine","glob":"**/*.{json,toml,rs}","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":168