{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1035","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" proving the formula was applied.\n\nThe test only asserts the rowboat ending when the score reaches 500. It never checksThe pose capture shows the score itself, so the bot could have  a raised-arm pose.scored below 100 and still passed without ever exercising the age formula.\n\nThe big stand lasts roughly 142 seconds. That is about 8,500 frames at 60fps. The 20,000-frame cap allows the bot to finish.\n\nChecking where FIT clips are defined. The mat spacing bug is confirmed: 0.8m vertical gaps between spots allow the 1.2m detection radius to trigger neighboring mats.\n\nA passing bot playthrough for the big stand should yield at least two stars. That threshold likely requires a score of 650 or higher, which would trigger the rowboat ending and exercise the age formula. The exact score from this specific test is still unknown.\n\nThe mat spacing is actually correct. The closest mat wins, so standing on a spot triggers the right one. The floatie and cannon are reachable. Wardrobe tests check the Sun cap helm and calendar days.\n\nThe jump-to-big-stand path correctly sets the run state to Story, so the age cut applies. The test passed without revealing the bot's score, which leaves the age formula unverified. I will not refute this criterion for missing edge cases.\n\nWardrobe and calendar are now fully implemented with gear, outfits, and day stamps. They remain reachable only through the dev menu or pause screen for now.\n\nA test should only be refuted if it is dishonest. This test could pass against a wrong implementation when the bot scores below 100. I will not modify code or write a new test to verify the score. I will inspect the bot function or\n\nThe prior gap covered existing output to  wardrobe and calendarestimate the score. as Back-only stubs with no props or poses. Those are now implemented. The acceptance criteria only require new beach props and exercise poses, which the capture shows. I will not raise the bar about island menu reachability since the prior gap is fixed.\n\nThe test prints no score on success. I will inspect the big stand bot and scoring logic to estimate the score. The jump-to-big-stand\n\nThe title capture  path correctly usesfooter shows \"Cross  the game's bot input.Cross\" twice. This may I may also run the  be a real prompt bugexisting test with --nocapture or minor polish issue. to reveal the actual Criterion 4 requires score. PlayStation glyphs to follow the last input, so duplicate Cross labels could still satisfy that rule.\n\nThe duplicate \"Cross Cross\" footer is not worth refuting. Some mat spots may sit inside walls or outside the room, but the floatie mat is reachable and","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-71201ce0-8130-4ad8-b02c-b3ebed635ad0-40","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Dev Mode|time scale|View|Save|slider|Long Stillness|eyes.closed|outfit|pose","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/PLAN.md","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-71201ce0-8130-4ad8-b02c-b3ebed635ad0-41","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/anim/fit.json","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-71201ce0-8130-4ad8-b02c-b3ebed635ad0-42","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs","offset":1860,"limit":60}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-71201ce0-8130-4ad8-b02c-b3ebed635ad0-43","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn bot\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/c