{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1055","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nI will inspect fit.json to confirm Tree is a real pose and not a stub.\n\nThe capture confirms Tree is a real pose with raised arms. I will not re-audit the entire game for newPrior gaps have been nits. The 8 gaps are fixed and gating tests thoroughly reviewed. pass. I am double-checking schedule event IDs during paging. Free play events exclude Check and BigStand.\n\nCannon is correctly mapped to schedule ID 110. Mat collision logic works as intended. The pose clip test passes because the first frames align with Tree. The package is not refuted. I am now looking for a real bug that\n\nSlider input now routes matches the prior gap through the real simulation spirit. step. Drag events emit Slider values and app.rs wires them into the input frame. Tests confirmed pad-right changes music and stiffness, with reset restoring defaults. A held-pointer drag test passed.\n\nDev mode controls are fully implemented. Jump, cheats, and time scale all work and pass their tests.\n\nSchedule paging is wired up.\n\nThe slider row no-op gap is resolved. Pad left and right are now wired for those rows.\n\nThe drag test compiles successfully after the first attempt failed. It uses `&MouseButton::Left`.\n\nThe drag test is compiled into the shipped game binary via `input.rs` and `app.rs`. The simulation slider test uses `MENU_RIGHT`, which the game handles in `pre()`.\n\nCannonball selection via shoulder paging passed. The Big Stand phase 5 logic now plays song 0, skips prompts after 15 seconds, clears the score banner, and forfeits on press. Final age calculation subtracts `(score/100).floor().min(10)` and awards a rowboat for scores of 40 or\n\nThe simulation is  below; a test with the contract, not theage 45 passed and the app's keyboard mapping. bot earned enough stars The 4x time scale test to trigger the cut. passed because jump_to Eyes-closed mode hides does not reset time. the puck, dims the  At 4x speed, 15 secondsscreen to 0.92, and  of simulated time equalsplays the pitch guide roughly 225 frames, with Sfx id 31. which fits comfortably within the 400-frame limit.\n\nNames and outfits are fully implemented. The 40-name list and 8 outfits including Swim and Golden support paging, and a test selected Gray and Golden successfully.\n\nBeach props and poses are wired up. The hub.toml lists rowboat, bench, lamp, stall, and mats,\n\nThe age test may be while fit.json contains self-referential. It six hand-keyed pose computes the expected clips. apply_body sets age from the score  the active clip, and captures show the treeusing the same formula pose with arms up alongside as the code under test, the rowboat, stall, lamp, bench, and puck. so it validates the implementation against Wardrobe and calendar are no longer stubs. itself rather than \n\nAll tests passed. nineteen tests ran twicean independent reference. in tests-core.log, plus six browser and six hub tests.\n\nA possible rendering bug was spotted: the title footer may display \"Cross Cross\" twice, which could duplicate the confirm glyph. This is not a prior gap, though it might be visually acceptable.\n\nThe audio_unlocked logic was also verified. desired_song returns 0 when audio is locked, and the long stillness test correctly expects song 3 during Big Stand before falling back to 0.\n\nHub mode correctly routes pause to Flow::Pause instead of Dev. The prior gaps are not refuted; no demonstrable defect meets the anti-ratchet bar.\n\nThe age test is not self-referential. The bot scores high enough to trigger a cut, so the expected age drops below 45 and the rowboat ending assertion runs. The deterministic seed ensures consistent results.\n\nThe age formula assertion is unconditional, but the same bot function scores at least 650 in direct play and at least two stars in seed-based tests. This confirms the rowboat ending path is reachable and the age logic is sound.\n\nThe eyes-closed test checks the tone status field and puck visibility rather than asserting that an Sfx event was emitted. This is acceptable because the tone value represents the pitch the HUD and audio use, and the Sfx is handled in the same block.\n\nThe age formula is confirmed to apply correctly. A score of at least 650 guarantees the rowboat ending, and the test passed with age 45. The jump\n\nThe long-stillness test checks the UI prompt and song index. It observes the shipped UI directly. The package is not refuted. path preserves Story mode through leave_demo and start_activity, so finish_play still applies age at the end.\n\nWardrobe now returns to dev mode after wear. A test selected the Sun cap and verified the helm. No new demonstrable defects were found.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1c71260a-e77e-40c1-b8c9-19c3ced17c43-60","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1c71260a-e77e-40c1-b8c9-19c3ced17c43-61","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Wobble Minutes","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/notes","glob":"**/*.{md,json}","head_limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1c71260a-e77e-40c1-b8c9-19c3ced17c43-62","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"<title>","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1c71260a-e77e-40c1-b8c9-19c3ced17c43-63","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/engine/anim/fit.json","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1732,"output_tokens":2273,"cache_read_input_tokens":133248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"5ed9d281-d82d-4ee3-9d8b-8c96cff83b98"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1c71260a-e77e-40c1-b8c9-19c3ced17c43-60","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:21:32\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Shardfall engine (Pavilion: Rust, wgpu, egui 0.36.2), commit 49ef2ba, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's cel look, high-key pastel, beach and wellness props. Library props only for generic dressing.\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine puppet tilts about the feet from the balance dot. Exercise poses are hand-keyed clips on that puppet: Tree, Warrior, Fold, Squat, Plank and Bloom.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Music, effects and voices are synthesized in code. No audio files. Seven music beds, default music gain 0.10. At least 30 effects. Animalese voices.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players. The round is the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup).\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU at 320×180, phone and tablet profiles, WebKit iPhone fallback, and the AI Hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The build followed PLAN.md and the engine source. The title was drawn with a real RNG from 50 riffs. No separate web search in this session.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Fifteen defects showed up in testing. The first six were a gust check that did not match the acceleration model, an egui texture delta dropped on the floor, a private intent module, fonts bound in the same pass that drew them, a hub ghost field that was a boolean, and About pages that did not turn. A review of that build found eight more: sliders that never moved, Dev Mode with no jump, cheats or time scale, a free-play schedule stuck on the first four events, a Big Stand that kept its song and never showed the fake skip or the final age cut, an eyes-closed check with no tone, name and outfit lists that stopped at six, and a beach with no props or exercise poses. The drag path then failed to compile because a set lookup wanted a reference.\\\",\\n    \\\"Three were critical. The font and texture-delta panic stops the browser frame loop, so the page sits there with a status that never ticks. After credits, seven events could not be started. A morning age of 41 to 50 could not reach the rowboat even after a strong finale.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the bot playthrough: three seeds from New Stay to the credits, plus each event on five seeds against an idle player. The later menu tests drive the real pad and pointer path, including a held pointer on a slider row.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful check is a 1920×1080 WebGPU screenshot. On this machine that bitmap can come back blank while the sim is fine. 320×180 is the timing check, and the engine's own capture is the picture.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The sim is one tick you can drive with no GPU, and the picture is a pure view of that tick. That split is what made the whole stay testable.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A gust is an acceleration, so gust 30 with no lean settles inside the disc and does not tip. egui 0.36 panics if a TexturesDelta is dropped. Pause still increments the tick; the world time is what freezes.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance model, the day loop, and every event. The engine does not have a centre-of-pressure verb.\\\",\\n    \\\"The app frame. The demo's keys, menus and chrome run in the same function as the game, and a fit frame has to turn all of that off without breaking the engine's other scenes.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"frozen() returns early inside the tick. InputFrame gained lean, device, ui and hub. The HUD carries the fit UI and a status string. The mixer plays song beds. The page bridge publishes status. Captures composite the fit UI. Puppets tilt about the feet. Splash and a silent wake were added for the lagoon. Fit pointer drags emit slider values. Hand-keyed clips play the exercise poses. The beach room gained dressing with no collision.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to publish one JSON value that is both a string (for JSON.parse) and an object (for .tick), without hand-rolling a String constructor.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan is specific about the feel, the roster and the hub snippet, and it says behaviour is the contract when a filename does not match the engine.\\\",\\n    \\\"Song numbers in the plan and the beds the sim actually requests do not use the same index. The hub snippet sends whatever status.hub.ghost is, so a boolean there is sent as a boolean.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping the full roster, the 10-foot shell and the hub harness on a 20 GB machine where one extra browser gets killed.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say, next to the gust sentence, that a full lean alone must not tip and a gust on top of that lean must. State that plan filenames are guidance in the same paragraph as the file tree.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Wobble Minutes\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Five days, one mat\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A third-person balance comedy at Tippy Cay. Lean through a week of sports mini-games, then stand still when it matters.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean with the stick, WASD or the mouse. Confirm with Cross, Space or click.\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"sports\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"low-poly\\\", \\\"versus\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:21:32\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Shardfall engine (Pavilion: Rust, wgpu, egui 0.36.2), commit 49ef2ba, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's cel look, high-key pastel, beach and wellness props. Library props only for generic dressing.\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine puppet tilts about the feet from the balance dot. Exercise poses are hand-keyed clips on that puppet: Tree, Warrior, Fold, Squat, Plank and Bloom.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Music, effects and voices are synthesized in code. No audio files. Seven music beds, default music gain 0.10. At least 30 effects. Animalese voices.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players. The round is the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup).\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU at 320×180, phone and tablet profiles, WebKit iPhone fallback, and the AI Hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The build followed PLAN.md and the engine source. The title was drawn with a real RNG from 50 riffs. No separate web search in this session.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Fifteen defects showed up in testing. The first six were a gust check that did not match the acceleration model, an egui texture delta dropped on the floor, a private intent module, fonts bound in the same pass that drew them, a hub ghost field that was a boolean, and About pages that did not turn. A review of that build found eight more: sliders that never moved, Dev Mode with no jump, cheats or time scale, a free-play schedule stuck on the first four events, a Big Stand that kept its song and never showed the fake skip or the final age cut, an eyes-closed check with no tone, name and outfit lists that stopped at six, and a beach with no props or exercise poses. The drag path then failed to compile because a set lookup wanted a reference.\\\",\\n    \\\"Three were critical. The font and texture-delta panic stops the browser frame loop, so the page sits there with a status that never ticks. After credits, seven events could not be started. A morning age of 41 to 50 could not reach the rowboat even after a strong finale.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the bot playthrough: three seeds from New Stay to the credits, plus each event on five seeds against an idle player. The later menu tests drive the real pad and pointer path, including a held pointer on a slider row.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful check is a 1920×1080 WebGPU screenshot. On this machine that bitmap can come back blank while the sim is fine. 320×180 is the timing check, and the engine's own capture is the picture.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The sim is one tick you can drive with no GPU, and the picture is a pure view of that tick. That split is what made the whole stay testable.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A gust is an acceleration, so gust 30 with no lean settles inside the disc and does not tip. egui 0.36 panics if a TexturesDelta is dropped. Pause still increments the tick; the world time is what freezes.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance model, the day loop, and every event. The engine does not have a centre-of-pressure verb.\\\",\\n    \\\"The app frame. The demo's keys, menus and chrome run in the same function as the game, and a fit frame has to turn all of that off without breaking the engine's other scenes.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"frozen() returns early inside the tick. InputFrame gained lean, device, ui and hub. The HUD carries the fit UI and a status string. The mixer plays song beds. The page bridge publishes status. Captures composite the fit UI. Puppets tilt about the feet. Splash and a silent wake were added for the lagoon. Fit pointer drags emit slider values. Hand-keyed clips play the exercise poses. The beach room gained dressing with no collision.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to publish one JSON value that is both a string (for JSON.parse) and an object (for .tick), without hand-rolling a String constructor.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan is specific about the feel, the roster and the hub snippet, and it says behaviour is the contract when a filename does not match the engine.\\\",\\n    \\\"Song numbers in the plan and the beds the sim actually requests do not use the same index. The hub snippet sends whatever status.hub.ghost is, so a boolean there is sent as a boolean.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping the full roster, the 10-foot shell and the hub harness on a 20 GB machine where one extra browser gets killed.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say, next to the gust sentence, that a full lean alone must not tip and a gust on top of that lean must. State that plan filenames are guidance in the same paragraph as the file tree.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Wobble Minutes\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Five days, one mat\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A third-person balance comedy at Tippy Cay. Lean through a week of sports mini-games, then stand still when it matters.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean with the stick, WASD or the mouse. Confirm with Cross, Space or click.\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"sports\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"low-poly\\\", \\\"versus\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:21:32\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Shardfall engine (Pavilion: Rust, wgpu, egui 0.36.2), commit 49ef2ba, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's cel look, high-key pastel, beach and wellness props. Library props only for generic dressing.\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine puppet tilts about the feet from the balance dot. Exercise poses are hand-keyed clips on that puppet: Tree, Warrior, Fold, Squat, Plank and Bloom.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Music, effects and voices are synthesized in code. No audio files. Seven music beds, default music gain 0.10. At least 30 effects. Animalese voices.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players. The round is the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup).\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU at 320×180, phone and tablet profiles, WebKit iPhone fallback, and the AI Hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The build followed PLAN.md and the engine source. The title was drawn with a real RNG from 50 riffs. No separate web search in this session.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Fifteen defects showed up in testing. The first six were a gust check that did not match the acceleration model, an egui texture delta dropped on the floor, a private intent module, fonts bound in the same pass that drew them, a hub ghost field that was a boolean, and About pages that did not turn. A review of that build found eight more: sliders that never moved, Dev Mode with no jump, cheats or time scale, a free-play schedule stuck on the first four events, a Big Stand that kept its song and never showed the fake skip or the final age cut, an eyes-closed check with no tone, name and outfit lists that stopped at six, and a beach with no props or exercise poses. The drag path then failed to compile because a set lookup wanted a reference.\\\",\\n    \\\"Three were critical. The font and texture-delta panic stops the browser frame loop, so the page sits there with a status that never ticks. After credits, seven events could not be started. A morning age of 41 to 50 could not reach the rowboat even after a strong finale.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the bot playthrough: three seeds from New Stay to the credits, plus each event on five seeds against an idle player. The later menu tests drive the real pad and pointer path, including a held pointer on a slider row.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful check is a 1920×1080 WebGPU screenshot. On this machine that bitmap can come back blank while the sim is fine. 320×180 is the timing check, and the engine's own capture is the picture.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The sim is one tick you can drive with no GPU, and the picture is a pure view of that tick. That split is what made the whole stay testable.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A gust is an acceleration, so gust 30 with no lean settles inside the disc and does not tip. egui 0.36 panics if a TexturesDelta is dropped. Pause still increments the tick; the world time is what freezes.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance model, the day loop, and every event. The engine does not have a centre-of-pressure verb.\\\",\\n    \\\"The app frame. The demo's keys, menus and chrome run in the same function as the game, and a fit frame has to turn all of that off without breaking the engine's other scenes.\\\",\\n    \\\"frozen() returns early inside the tick. InputFrame gained lean, device, ui and hub. The HUD carries the fit UI and a status string. The mixer plays song beds. The page bridge publishes status. Captures composite the fit UI. Puppets tilt about the feet. Splash and a silent wake were added for the lagoon. Fit pointer drags emit slider values. Hand-keyed clips play the exercise poses. The beach room gained dressing with no collision.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to publish one JSON value that is both a string (for JSON.parse) and an object (for .tick), without hand-rolling a String constructor.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan is specific about the feel, the roster and the hub snippet, and it says behaviour is the contract when a filename does not match the engine.\\\",\\n    \\\"Song numbers in the plan and the beds the sim actually requests do not use the same index. The hub snippet sends whatever status.hub.ghost is, so a boolean there is sent as a boolean.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping the full roster, the 10-foot shell and the hub harness on a 20 GB machine where one extra browser gets killed.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say, next to the gust sentence, that a full lean alone must not tip and a gust on top of that lean must. State that plan filenames are guidance in the same paragraph as the file tree.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Wobble Minutes\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Five days, one mat\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A third-person balance comedy at Tippy Cay. Lean through a week of sports mini-games, then stand still when it matters.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean with the stick, WASD or the mouse. Confirm with Cross, Space or click.\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"sports\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"low-poly\\\", \\\"versus\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":51}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1c71260a-e77e-40c1-b8c9-19c3ced17c43-61","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,47,110,111,116,101,115,47,116,105,116,108,101,45,100,114,97,119,46,106,115,111,110,10,54,58,32,32,34,116,105,116,108,101,34,58,32,34,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,34,44,10,52,50,58,32,32,32,32,34,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,34,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35