.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\\n\\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\\n\\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\nEffort: Spend effort however you see fit.\\n\\n## This computer\\nChecked 2026-11-04 20:05 (America/Vancouver) by node check-environment.mjs.\\n\\n- **Computer:** Worki9: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap. Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).\\n- **Space:** 850 GB free in the home folder. /tmp: 9.8 GB, in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.\\n- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\\n- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\\n  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\\n  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\\n  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\\n- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\\n- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\\n- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\\n- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\\n- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \\\"Target closed\\\", \\\"page crashed\\\" or \\\"browser has been closed\\\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\\n\\n### What this computer doesn't have\\n\\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\\n\\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\\n\\n### Sharing this computer\\n\\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\\n\\nScope\\n\\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\\n\\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\\n\\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\\n\\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\\n\\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\\n\\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\\n\\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\\n\\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\\n\\n## Done\\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:21:32\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"tech\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"animation\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"audio\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"online\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"testing\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"research\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"environment\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\nTesting Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"total_lines\":151}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d064fcd3-1bf6-4951-b108-422d07e2083d-4","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Game plan: a balance-and-wellness comedy inspired by Wii Fit\\n\\nYou will build this game from this plan alone. The director is not available for questions.\\n\\n## 0. How to read this plan\\n\\n- **Your brief** means the brief in your own working folder. It wins on the title method, file and folder names, dates, the deliverables and the feedback questions. This plan names none of them.\\n- **Paths** are relative to the dev folder your brief tells you to create. Clone the engine to `engine/` inside it.\\n- **Numbers** are starting values. Tune them with the dev sliders and the bot. The structure is decided; change it only if it fails in play.\\n10→- **Gaps:** if something is not covered, decide, write one line in `notes/decisions.md`, and carry on.\\n- **Verified** means it was run on this computer on 2026-11-04, against engine commit `49ef2ba` and AI Hub client 1.4.0. Section 15 lists those results.\\n- **Title:** pick it first, the way your brief says. Keep it in one constant. This plan calls it \\\"the game\\\". The resort's name, Tippy Cay, belongs to the world and does not depend on the title.\\n- **Reading cost:** you do not need to read the engine's source to start. Read `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` whole (about 3k tokens) and `engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/starter.rs`, then use this plan. Search `engine/docs/REFERENCE.md` and `engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` when you need a tool or a prop field.\\n\\n## 1. The game in one page\\n\\nYou have won a five-day stay at Tippy Cay, a small wellness resort staffed entirely by talking gym equipment. You do not remember entering. Each morning a relentlessly pleasant wobble cushion tests your balance and gives you a Balance Age. Each day you walk the island, try short stillness, strength, cardio and balance events, and bank minutes in a giant clam. Checkout requires a Balance Age of 40 or better. Day 5 ends in the Big Stand, a finale whose last test is to do nothing at all for thirty seconds while the game tries to make you press something.\\n\\n- **Genre:** sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame (daily ritual, unlocks, wardrobe). Catalogue genre: Sports.\\n20→- **Perspective:** third person throughout, with a camera chosen per activity: 3/4 follow on the island, a mirror-style front view for exercises on the spot, chase for the jog and the paddle, high 3/4 for the table, side view for the dives.\\n- **Length:** a first run takes 25 to 40 minutes. It shows every feature. Free play follows.\\n\\n| What makes Wii Fit distinctive | How this game turns it into play |\\n|---|---|\\n| A balance board: your centre of pressure is the only verb, and tiny movements matter | The Balance Core (section 4): one analog dot driven by lean. Every event is played through it |\\n| The body test and the verdict of a fitness age | The Morning Wobble Check and Balance Age. Never weight, BMI or body shape |\\n| Equipment that talks: cheerful, polite, quietly rude | Pip, a talking wobble cushion, plus a whole staff of talking gear |\\n| A calm, uncanny instructor | Posey, a faceless wooden artist's mannequin |\\n| Four disciplines: yoga, strength, aerobics, balance games | Four pavilions, each with its own coach and events |\\n30→| The daily ritual: calendar stamps, banked minutes that unlock more | Calendar stamps and the Minute Clam |\\n| Noticing how long you stayed away | Real-date absence comments from Pip |\\n| A family sharing one board and comparing progress | Hot-seat Medley, Yesterday You ghosts, AI Hub sessions |\\n| Clean, quiet, pastel, unintentionally funny | High-key pastel look, gentle lounge music, short deadpan text |\\n\\n**Pillars.** Check every decision against these.\\n1. **Small movements, big consequences.** Mastery means doing less. The best moments are held breaths.\\n2. **Deadpan encouragement.** Everything you do is commented on, kindly, and slightly too honestly.\\n3. **A daily ritual.** Check in, get a number, do your exercises, get a stamp.\\n4. **Calm surface, silly underneath.** The screen stays serene while a seagull stands on your head.\\n40→\\n**Originality rules.** This is an original game in the same genre, not a recreation.\\n- Inside the game, use no Nintendo names (Wii, Mii, Balance Board and so on). The only exceptions are the Source line on the About screen and whatever your title's riff requires.\\n- No white rectangular board with dot eyes. No pale human trainer in a tank top and ponytail. No Mii-style avatars or face editors. No island or plaza from the source series.\\n- No source music, jingles, menu layouts or screen compositions. Do not quote or paraphrase its lines. Write your own.\\n- Events have their own names and twists, as specified below.\\n- Respect bodies: no weight, BMI, body-shape jokes or diet talk anywhere. Pip judges your wobble, your habits and your absences.\\n\\n## 2. Structure of play\\n\\n50→**Boot:** title screen over a slow island sweep. Menu: New Stay or Continue, Play Together, Settings, About. After 10 seconds with no input on the title or any pre-game menu, attract mode starts (section 12).\\n\\n**New Stay:** choose one of 4 guest slots, pick a name from a list of about 40 funny preset names (no on-screen keyboard), pick a look (6 skin tones, 8 outfits). Then a short intro with Pip at reception, skippable.\\n\\n**A day:**\\n1. Wake on the cabana deck. Pip greets you, with an absence comment if real days have passed.\\n2. Morning Wobble Check (about 70 seconds), Balance Age reveal, Pip's comment.\\n3. Free time on the island: walk, talk to guests, find lost flip-flops, step on an event mat. The Schedule (Triangle or Tab) lists everything and fast-travels.\\n4. When the day's minute goal is met, Pip says so. Sleep at your cabana (or choose End Day in the Schedule). A big stamp lands on the Calendar. Next day.\\n\\n60→| Day | Opens | Minute goal | Story beat |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Stillness Studio: Breath Bloom, Pose Parade | 3 | Arrival. The checkout rule. \\\"Nobody has asked to leave yet\\\" |\\n| 2 | Iron Gazebo: Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff | 5 | Big Kettle. Wardrobe opens |\\n| 3 | Boardwalk: Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap | 7 | Yesterday You appears as a ghost. \\\"I am not comparing you\\\" |\\n| 4 | Lagoon: Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup | 9 | Guests start whispering about the Big Stand |\\n| 5 | The Big Stand, after the morning check | none | Finale, ending, free play |\\n\\n**Minutes:** the first clear of an event each day banks 1 + stars (0 to 3 stars, so 1 to 4 minutes); repeats bank 1. Resort minutes are openly not real minutes (\\\"Our minutes are longer. It is a wellness thing\\\").\\n\\n70→**Endings:** Balance Age 40 or better: you may check out, by rowboat (`LIB/core/rowboat`). Otherwise: the Extended Stay ending, gentle and funny. Both roll credits, then unlock Free Play: every event open, personal bests, star goals, and a calendar that keeps stamping real days.\\n\\n**Bot rule:** `Game::bot` must be able to play this entire flow, menus included, from New Stay to the credits. That is your scripted playthrough and the base of attract mode.\\n\\n## 3. Controls\\n\\nThe left stick is both walking and leaning. Prompts always show the glyph for the input used last.\\n\\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n80→| Walk on the island, lean in events | Left stick | W A S D (arrows also walk) | Island: click a place or thing to walk there. Events: cursor offset from screen centre is the lean |\\n| Fine lean | Stick itself | Hold Shift (half key rate) | Small cursor moves |\\n| Jog on the island | Hold R2 | Hold Shift | |\\n| Action: talk, begin, inhale, squat, bounce | Cross | Space | Left button |\\n| Left step / right step | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 | Q or Left / E or Right | Left button / right button |\\n| Brace (hold both) | L2+R2 or L1+R1 | Q+E | Both buttons |\\n| Wave at someone | Square | F | |\\n| Schedule | Triangle | Tab | |\\n| Island camera | Right stick | | Right-drag, wheel zooms |\\n| Pause | Options | Esc | |\\n90→| Menus | D-pad or left stick, Cross confirms, Circle backs, L1/R1 change tabs | Arrows or W A S D, Enter or Space, Esc backs, Q/E change tabs | Hover moves focus, click activates, right-click backs |\\n\\nXbox glyphs (Settings option) swap A B X Y, LB RB LT RT, Menu. Ignore Options while Create is held: that pair belongs to the AI Hub. Disable the engine's own keys (F1 to F10, digits, H, Backspace rewind, right-drag tilt) outside dev mode. Keep F11 for fullscreen.\\n\\n## 4. The Balance Core\\n\\nOne struct, `BalanceCore`, used by every event. Its state is `cob` (the dot, unit disc, x right, y up on screen) and `vel`.\\n\\n```\\ntarget = shaped lean input * reach + wobble(t)\\n100→acc    = (target - cob) * stiffness - vel * damping + gust + nudge\\nvel   += acc * dt\\ncob   += vel * dt\\ntip    = |cob| > 1 for tip_time seconds\\n```\\n\\nStart with `stiffness 40`, `damping 8.5`, `reach 0.92`, `tip_time 0.35`. `wobble` is `amp * (0.7 * sin(2*pi*1.3*t + a) + 0.3 * sin(2*pi*2.9*t + b))` per axis, phases from `sim.state.rng`, base `amp 0.12`, scaled per event and by fatigue, plus a velocity kick of 0.1 units/s in a random direction every 1 to 2 seconds. Use sim time, never the clock.\\n\\n**Feel targets** (these numbers give them, by numeric simulation at 60 ticks/s): full stick reaches 90% in about 0.4 s with about 5% overshoot, like a body. Release settles in about 0.45 s. Left alone, the dot wanders at a mean radius of 0.05, at most 0.08. A held full lean does not tip by itself; a gust on top of it does.\\n\\n110→**Input shaping** (in `pav_app`, passed as `InputFrame.lean`, screen space):\\n- **Stick:** deadzone 0.12, response curve `x^1.5` so small motions are fine.\\n- **Keyboard:** keys move the target at 1.6 units/s and it returns at 1.2 units/s when released. Tapping gives small nudges, so keys feel native, not bang-bang.\\n- **Mouse:** cursor offset from the screen centre divided by 0.38 of the window height, clamped to the disc. No pointer lock. The device moved last wins.\\n\\n**Body:** the figure tilts with the dot (`cob * 14` degrees about the feet, engine change in section 14). Beyond |cob| 0.75 an upper-body arm-flail clip fades in. A tip plays a stumble and, over water, a splash. Tips never end the game; they cost time or score.\\n\\n**HUD, the Puck:** a large circular gauge drawn in egui: a pale disc, a green target ring, a coral dot, and stars at the edge when streaking. It must read from 10 feet. It looks good at 340 px diameter at 1080p (verified). Put it top centre or bottom centre, whichever does not cover the figure in that event.\\n\\n## 5. Events\\n120→\\n**Common frame:** event card (name, one-sentence goal, glyph prompts, one coach line), 3-2-1, play, result (score 0 to 1000, stars at 400, 650 and 850, a deadpan Title, minutes banked, personal best, difference from Yesterday You; Retry or Back).\\n\\n**Every event has:** a section of tunable numbers in `rules.toml`, a bot that earns at least 2 stars, an idle-input outcome below 1 star, a ghost lane, and an attract segment. Scenes `fit/event/<name>` start an event directly, for tools and tests.\\n\\n### Stillness Studio (Posey). Set: `studio`, a round white deck on a calm dawn lagoon. Camera: mirror view (yaw 0, tilt 12, distance 8.5, fov 36; the figure faces +Z, toward the camera, and stick right is screen right).\\n\\n**Breath Bloom** (45 s). Hold Action to inhale, release to exhale, following a guide ring: 4 s in, 4 s out, 5 cycles, the last one longer. `lungs` rises while held and falls when not. Keep the dot inside a centre ring of radius 0.35. Tick score: `0.7 * (1 - clamp(|lungs - guide| / 0.35)) + 0.3 * inRing`. Each good cycle opens a lotus on the water with a rising pentatonic chime; a perfect run blooms the whole pond. Scrub the clip `FIT/Breath` by `lungs`. No fail state. Bot: holds while the guide rises.\\n\\n**Pose Parade** (3 poses, 20 s each). Six hand-keyed poses with deadpan names: the Patient Heron, the Apologetic Lunge, the Tired Lighthouse, the Folded Deck Chair, the Reluctant Bridge, Seated Disappointment. Day 1 uses the first three. Posey holds the pose beside you. A target ring (radius 0.30 shrinking to 0.18) drifts on a slow Lissajous path (amplitude 0.35, 0.12 Hz). Inside the ring a streak multiplier climbs x1 to x4, one step per 2 s; leaving resets it. At 12 s of pose 2 a gull lands on your head and wobble is x1.6 for 5 s (\\\"There is a bird on you. Accept the bird\\\"). A tip breaks the pose for 1.5 s. Score: time in ring weighted by multiplier. Bot: PD toward the ring centre.\\n130→\\n### Iron Gazebo (Big Kettle). Set: `gazebo`, a white iron gazebo at golden hour. Camera: 3/4 front.\\n\\n**Tempo Squats** (10 reps, about 50 s). Hold Action to go down (2 s to full depth), release to rise (1 s). A guide bar shows the tempo; a low bell marks the bottom. Keep the dot in a band |x| < 0.25; wobble grows 8% per rep. Rep score: `0.7 * timing + 0.3 * band`. Scrub `FIT/Squat` by depth. Gag: rep 10 is followed by \\\"Ten. Also eleven.\\\" Bot: follows the guide.\\n\\n**Plank Standoff** (up to 60 s). Hold Brace and keep the dot in a ring shrinking from 0.40 to 0.20. Releasing, or leaving the ring for more than 1 s, collapses you in a comic flop. Fatigue ramps wobble; at 30 s add tremble; at 45 s Kettle laughs at his own joke and the nudge shakes the screen. Score: seconds survived / 60. Stars at 25, 40 and 55 s. Kettle, who has no arms, plank-talks you through it. Base the pose on one frame of `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`. Bot: survives at least 45 s.\\n\\n### Boardwalk (Bounce). Set: `boardwalk`, a beach boardwalk at bright midday.\\n\\n**Step Party** (64 s, 96 BPM, song 4). A rhythm game: notes in two lanes fall to two footprints, left, right or both, on an aerobic step box. Perfect within 55 ms, Good within 120 ms. About 100 notes, data in `charts.toml`, starting with quarter notes and building to eighths and doubles. Bounce bounces on the beat and guests clap on downbeats. Timing uses the audio clock (section 10). Camera: mirror view, slightly high. Bot: presses exactly on each note.\\n140→\\n**Floatie Spin** (50 s). Circle the lean (stick, mouse, or rolling W-D-S-A) to spin inflatable rings around your hips. Spin speed is the smoothed angular velocity of the lean while |lean| > 0.4; the sweet band is 6 to 9 rad/s, and a `spin_band_scale` rule widens it for keyboard. \\\"Switch!\\\" flips the required direction every 15 s. Guests toss new rings from left or right: press that side's step within 0.25 s of arrival to catch it. Out of band, rings sink; on the floor they are lost. Maximum 7 rings. Score: rings times time in band. Rings are no-physics entities positioned in code. Bot: 7.5 rad/s circle, presses on arrivals.\\n\\n**Morning Lap** (about 90 s, one lap of the hub island). Alternate left and right steps to set your pace (1.6 to 2.4 steps/s is the zone). Too fast raises a stitch meter that makes you stumble; too slow and Bounce, the pacer rolling ahead, gets away. The path steers you; lean moves you up to 1.2 m sideways to dodge crabs, sunbathers and towels and to grab ribbons. Flip-flops can be found here too. Score: time in zone, plus ribbons, minus bumps. Camera: chase with per-tick yaw. Use `MESH2MOTION/Jog` scaled to speed. Bot: 2 steps/s, steers to ribbons.\\n\\n### Lagoon (Commodore Gull). Sets: `tide`, `channel`, `pier`, `tower`.\\n\\n**Tide Table** (3 boards, 60 s total). You stand on a floating square raft and your lean tilts it. Roll hermit crabs in shells into tide pools. Board 1: 3 shells. Board 2: 5 shells and a moving pool. Board 3: 7 shells, bumpers and a rising tide. Fast shells skip over pools. Write the shell physics as simple 2D code (`a = tilt * g - friction * v`, wall bounce 0.5), not rapier: it is more tunable and bot-friendly. Score: shells potted plus time left. Camera: high 3/4 (tilt 62). Bot: PD steering of the nearest shell toward the nearest pool.\\n\\n**Paddle Slalom** (about 45 s). Stand on a paddleboard on a long channel and pass buoy gates. Lean x steers. Lean forward speeds up and risks tipping, lean back brakes. Gusts, shown as ripple streaks, push the dot. A tip is a big splash and a 2 s remount. A missed gate adds 2 s. `score = clamp((1.6 * par - t) / (0.8 * par)) * 1000`. Standing on water uses the trick in section 15; a silent `Wake` event every few ticks draws the wake. Camera: chase (tilt 22, distance 10). Bot: steers to gate centres at forward lean 0.5.\\n150→\\n**Tray Trek** (about 50 s). Walk a long pier at a fixed pace, carrying a tray with a stack of 5 smoothies. Waves, plank gaps and swooping gulls jolt the tray. Your dot tilts it. Glasses slide with tilt and plop into the sea past the edge. Score: 200 per glass delivered, plus a no-spill bonus. Marjorie receives what is left and comments. Use `STYLE100/Balance_Walk` plus an upper-body `FIT/CarryTray` clip. Bot: counters the jolts it knows are coming.\\n\\n**Cannonball Cup** (3 dives, about 40 s). The board bounces with a 1.2 s period. Press Action at the bottom of 3 bounces to build power, the 4th press leaps. In the air, hold Action to tuck and lean to rotate. Enter tucked and high for the biggest splash. Three gull judges hold up cards: \\\"6.5\\\", \\\"7\\\", \\\"See me\\\". \\\"We are not here for form. We are here for splash.\\\" Score: height x tuck x timing. Camera: side view (yaw 90, tilt 6, distance 14). The splash must be huge: a new `BigSplash` event scales the water dents and particles. This is the attract mode's hero shot. Bot: presses on bottoms, tucks at the apex.\\n\\n### The Big Stand (finale, about 2.5 minutes). Set: `bay`, a tiny post in the bay at sunset, with the whole cast watching from rafts.\\n\\nFive phases, reusing event code with new numbers:\\n1. Breathing, 4 cycles.\\n2. A pose under rising gusts, 20 s.\\n160→3. Step Party for 16 bars with a marching band of guests, wobble on.\\n4. Brace while waves crash, 20 s.\\n5. **The Long Stillness:** 30 s of nothing. Music fades to silence, the HUD vanishes except the Puck. At 15 s a fake prompt offers \\\"Press Cross to skip\\\". Pressing anything forfeits the Inner Peace bonus. Then Pip, quietly: \\\"...Oh. You're still here. Good.\\\"\\n\\nA tip drops you in the sea to a groan from the crowd and puts you back; it costs score and cannot end the run. Final Balance Age = morning age minus `final_score / 100` (up to 10).\\n\\n### Morning Wobble Check. Set: `studio`. About 70 s, four micro-tests, Pip presiding.\\n\\n| Test | What you do | Metric (0 to 1) |\\n|---|---|---|\\n170→| Stand Still (\\\"This is the whole test\\\") | Hold the dot centred for 8 s; one small nudge at 5 s | Mean distance from centre |\\n| Lean Targets | A left/right bar: reach \\\"70% left\\\", then two more targets, within 6%, hold 1.5 s; 5 s limit each | Time taken |\\n| Eyes Closed | 6 s. The screen dims to almost black, the Puck vanishes. A tone's pitch tells your offset, and rumble if the pad has it | Mean distance |\\n| Step Test | 8 alternating steps to a 100 BPM metronome | Timing |\\n\\n```\\nskill = 0.30*still + 0.25*targets + 0.25*blind + 0.20*steps\\nage   = 24 + 56 * (1 - skill)^1.1 - 2*days_completed - min(total_stars/3, 8)\\n```\\nClamp to 18..99, round. A middling player (skill 0.5) starts at 50 and reaches about 34 by Day 5; a weak one (skill 0.2) starts at 68 and ends near 52, before the finale's bonus. The big number rolls like a slot machine. Pip's comment is chosen by the change since yesterday and by the worst metric. A sparkline of 5 big dots shows the week. Your figure's posture improves as the age falls (a small constant forward slump through the tilt field, shrinking each day): visible progress, no numbers needed.\\n180→\\n## 6. Meta systems\\n\\n- **Minute Clam:** a giant clam at reception that gulps banked minutes with a gibberish burp. Totals unlock wardrobe items.\\n- **Calendar:** five big days, a stamp per completed day, then real days in free play. No tables.\\n- **Titles:** after each event Pip awards a deadpan title by score: Human Soup, Acceptable Human, Certified Lean-To, Wobble Enthusiast, Seasoned Tilter, Stillness Intern, Professional Standing Person, Alarmingly Balanced. At least 30, in `script.toml`.\\n- **Wardrobe:** reuse the engine's `GearLook`, which needs no new drawing (verified): `helm = cap` (sun cap), `helm = hood` (towel turban), `crown`, `halo`; `gloves` (sweatbands), `belt`, `pauldrons` (reads as arm floaties, funny). Plus shirt, pants and shoe colours. Skip `cape`: it draws long sticks.\\n- **Lost flip-flops:** 5 hidden on the island, for Two-Towel Tom. Reward: Golden Flip-Flops (gold shoes) and a line. This is the exploration layer.\\n- **Yesterday You:** your best run of each event is recorded and replayed as a tinted figure in a neighbouring lane, from Day 3.\\n- **Absence comments:** the page passes today's date to the game at boot, and the save stores the last day played. \\\"You were away for 2 days. I did not count them. There were 2.\\\" Passing the date in as data keeps the rule that the sim never reads the clock.\\n190→- **Saves:** versioned JSON in `localStorage`: guest slots (name, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings. Save on every change of day and every result.\\n\\n## 7. World, cast and writing\\n\\n**Tippy Cay** is about 64 x 48 m: reception at the centre (Pip's desk, Calendar wall, Minute Clam), a ring path for jogging, four pavilions around it, a row of cabanas, a pier, a diving tower and a water channel in the distance. Palms, grass, sand terraces, sea on all sides, circling gulls.\\n\\n| Character | What it is | Voice and manner |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Pip** | Sky-blue round wobble cushion, two dot eyes (`blob` plan, scale 0.7, squash 2.0, plus a small valve) | Front desk and scorekeeper. Relentlessly pleasant. Keeps records of everything. Never technically insults you. Squeaky rubber voice |\\n| **Posey** | Faceless wooden artist's mannequin (biped with eyes the colour of its skin; verified look in section 8) | Stillness. Serene, short, oddly poetic. Soft wood-block voice. It has no eyes and never blinks; \\\"This has not been discussed\\\" |\\n200→| **Big Kettle** | Cast-iron kettlebell (dark `blob` plus a torus handle part; add a `Handle` attach kind) | Strength. Booming, gentle, deeply supportive. No arms or legs, cannot do any exercise |\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Game plan: a balance-and-wellness comedy inspired by Wii Fit\\n\\nYou will build this game from this plan alone. The director is not available for questions.\\n\\n## 0. How to read this plan\\n\\n- **Your brief** means the brief in your own working folder. It wins on the title method, file and folder names, dates, the deliverables and the feedback questions. This plan names none of them.\\n- **Paths** are relative to the dev folder your brief tells you to create. Clone the engine to `engine/` inside it.\\n- **Numbers** are starting values. Tune them with the dev sliders and the bot. The structure is decided; change it only if it fails in play.\\n10→- **Gaps:** if something is not covered, decide, write one line in `notes/decisions.md`, and carry on.\\n- **Verified** means it was run on this computer on 2026-11-04, against engine commit `49ef2ba` and AI Hub client 1.4.0. Section 15 lists those results.\\n- **Title:** pick it first, the way your brief says. Keep it in one constant. This plan calls it \\\"the game\\\". The resort's name, Tippy Cay, belongs to the world and does not depend on the title.\\n- **Reading cost:** you do not need to read the engine's source to start. Read `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` whole (about 3k tokens) and `engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/starter.rs`, then use this plan. Search `engine/docs/REFERENCE.md` and `engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` when you need a tool or a prop field.\\n\\n## 1. The game in one page\\n\\nYou have won a five-day stay at Tippy Cay, a small wellness resort staffed entirely by talking gym equipment. You do not remember entering. Each morning a relentlessly pleasant wobble cushion tests your balance and gives you a Balance Age. Each day you walk the island, try short stillness, strength, cardio and balance events, and bank minutes in a giant clam. Checkout requires a Balance Age of 40 or better. Day 5 ends in the Big Stand, a finale whose last test is to do nothing at all for thirty seconds while the game tries to make you press something.\\n\\n- **Genre:** sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame (daily ritual, unlocks, wardrobe). Catalogue genre: Sports.\\n20→- **Perspective:** third person throughout, with a camera chosen per activity: 3/4 follow on the island, a mirror-style front view for exercises on the spot, chase for the jog and the paddle, high 3/4 for the table, side view for the dives.\\n- **Length:** a first run takes 25 to 40 minutes. It shows every feature. Free play follows.\\n\\n| What makes Wii Fit distinctive | How this game turns it into play |\\n|---|---|\\n| A balance board: your centre of pressure is the only verb, and tiny movements matter | The Balance Core (section 4): one analog dot driven by lean. Every event is played through it |\\n| The body test and the verdict of a fitness age | The Morning Wobble Check and Balance Age. Never weight, BMI or body shape |\\n| Equipment that talks: cheerful, polite, quietly rude | Pip, a talking wobble cushion, plus a whole staff of talking gear |\\n| A calm, uncanny instructor | Posey, a faceless wooden artist's mannequin |\\n| Four disciplines: yoga, strength, aerobics, balance games | Four pavilions, each with its own coach and events |\\n30→| The daily ritual: calendar stamps, banked minutes that unlock more | Calendar stamps and the Minute Clam |\\n| Noticing how long you stayed away | Real-date absence comments from Pip |\\n| A family sharing one board and comparing progress | Hot-seat Medley, Yesterday You ghosts, AI Hub sessions |\\n| Clean, quiet, pastel, unintentionally funny | High-key pastel look, gentle lounge music, short deadpan text |\\n\\n**Pillars.** Check every decision against these.\\n1. **Small movements, big consequences.** Mastery means doing less. The best moments are held breaths.\\n2. **Deadpan encouragement.** Everything you do is commented on, kindly, and slightly too honestly.\\n3. **A daily ritual.** Check in, get a number, do your exercises, get a stamp.\\n4. **Calm surface, silly underneath.** The screen stays serene while a seagull stands on your head.\\n40→\\n**Originality rules.** This is an original game in the same genre, not a recreation.\\n- Inside the game, use no Nintendo names (Wii, Mii, Balance Board and so on). The only exceptions are the Source line on the About screen and whatever your title's riff requires.\\n- No white rectangular board with dot eyes. No pale human trainer in a tank top and ponytail. No Mii-style avatars or face editors. No island or plaza from the source series.\\n- No source music, jingles, menu layouts or screen compositions. Do not quote or paraphrase its lines. Write your own.\\n- Events have their own names and twists, as specified below.\\n- Respect bodies: no weight, BMI, body-shape jokes or diet talk anywhere. Pip judges your wobble, your habits and your absences.\\n\\n## 2. Structure of play\\n\\n50→**Boot:** title screen over a slow island sweep. Menu: New Stay or Continue, Play Together, Settings, About. After 10 seconds with no input on the title or any pre-game menu, attract mode starts (section 12).\\n\\n**New Stay:** choose one of 4 guest slots, pick a name from a list of about 40 funny preset names (no on-screen keyboard), pick a look (6 skin tones, 8 outfits). Then a short intro with Pip at reception, skippable.\\n\\n**A day:**\\n1. Wake on the cabana deck. Pip greets you, with an absence comment if real days have passed.\\n2. Morning Wobble Check (about 70 seconds), Balance Age reveal, Pip's comment.\\n3. Free time on the island: walk, talk to guests, find lost flip-flops, step on an event mat. The Schedule (Triangle or Tab) lists everything and fast-travels.\\n4. When the day's minute goal is met, Pip says so. Sleep at your cabana (or choose End Day in the Schedule). A big stamp lands on the Calendar. Next day.\\n\\n60→| Day | Opens | Minute goal | Story beat |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Stillness Studio: Breath Bloom, Pose Parade | 3 | Arrival. The checkout rule. \\\"Nobody has asked to leave yet\\\" |\\n| 2 | Iron Gazebo: Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff | 5 | Big Kettle. Wardrobe opens |\\n| 3 | Boardwalk: Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap | 7 | Yesterday You appears as a ghost. \\\"I am not comparing you\\\" |\\n| 4 | Lagoon: Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup | 9 | Guests start whispering about the Big Stand |\\n| 5 | The Big Stand, after the morning check | none | Finale, ending, free play |\\n\\n**Minutes:** the first clear of an event each day banks 1 + stars (0 to 3 stars, so 1 to 4 minutes); repeats bank 1. Resort minutes are openly not real minutes (\\\"Our minutes are longer. It is a wellness thing\\\").\\n\\n70→**Endings:** Balance Age 40 or better: you may check out, by rowboat (`LIB/core/rowboat`). Otherwise: the Extended Stay ending, gentle and funny. Both roll credits, then unlock Free Play: every event open, personal bests, star goals, and a calendar that keeps stamping real days.\\n\\n**Bot rule:** `Game::bot` must be able to play this entire flow, menus included, from New Stay to the credits. That is your scripted playthrough and the base of attract mode.\\n\\n## 3. Controls\\n\\nThe left stick is both walking and leaning. Prompts always show the glyph for the input used last.\\n\\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n80→| Walk on the island, lean in events | Left stick | W A S D (arrows also walk) | Island: click a place or thing to walk there. Events: cursor offset from screen centre is the lean |\\n| Fine lean | Stick itself | Hold Shift (half key rate) | Small cursor moves |\\n| Jog on the island | Hold R2 | Hold Shift | |\\n| Action: talk, begin, inhale, squat, bounce | Cross | Space | Left button |\\n| Left step / right step | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 | Q or Left / E or Right | Left button / right button |\\n| Brace (hold both) | L2+R2 or L1+R1 | Q+E | Both buttons |\\n| Wave at someone | Square | F | |\\n| Schedule | Triangle | Tab | |\\n| Island camera | Right stick | | Right-drag, wheel zooms |\\n| Pause | Options | Esc | |\\n90→| Menus | D-pad or left stick, Cross confirms, Circle backs, L1/R1 change tabs | Arrows or W A S D, Enter or Space, Esc backs, Q/E change tabs | Hover moves focus, click activates, right-click backs |\\n\\nXbox glyphs (Settings option) swap A B X Y, LB RB LT RT, Menu. Ignore Options while Create is held: that pair belongs to the AI Hub. Disable the engine's own keys (F1 to F10, digits, H, Backspace rewind, right-drag tilt) outside dev mode. Keep F11 for fullscreen.\\n\\n## 4. The Balance Core\\n\\nOne struct, `BalanceCore`, used by every event. Its state is `cob` (the dot, unit disc, x right, y up on screen) and `vel`.\\n\\n```\\ntarget = shaped lean input * reach + wobble(t)\\n100→acc    = (target - cob) * stiffness - vel * damping + gust + nudge\\nvel   += acc * dt\\ncob   += vel * dt\\ntip    = |cob| > 1 for tip_time seconds\\n```\\n\\nStart with `stiffness 40`, `damping 8.5`, `reach 0.92`, `tip_time 0.35`. `wobble` is `amp * (0.7 * sin(2*pi*1.3*t + a) + 0.3 * sin(2*pi*2.9*t + b))` per axis, phases from `sim.state.rng`, base `amp 0.12`, scaled per event and by fatigue, plus a velocity kick of 0.1 units/s in a random direction every 1 to 2 seconds. Use sim time, never the clock.\\n\\n**Feel targets** (these numbers give them, by numeric simulation at 60 ticks/s): full stick reaches 90% in about 0.4 s with about 5% overshoot, like a body. Release settles in about 0.45 s. Left alone, the dot wanders at a mean radius of 0.05, at most 0.08. A held full lean does not tip by itself; a gust on top of it does.\\n\\n110→**Input shaping** (in `pav_app`, passed as `InputFrame.lean`, screen space):\\n- **Stick:** deadzone 0.12, response curve `x^1.5` so small motions are fine.\\n- **Keyboard:** keys move the target at 1.6 units/s and it returns at 1.2 units/s when released. Tapping gives small nudges, so keys feel native, not bang-bang.\\n- **Mouse:** cursor offset from the screen centre divided by 0.38 of the window height, clamped to the disc. No pointer lock. The device moved last wins.\\n\\n**Body:** the figure tilts with the dot (`cob * 14` degrees about the feet, engine change in section 14). Beyond |cob| 0.75 an upper-body arm-flail clip fades in. A tip plays a stumble and, over water, a splash. Tips never end the game; they cost time or score.\\n\\n**HUD, the Puck:** a large circular gauge drawn in egui: a pale disc, a green target ring, a coral dot, and stars at the edge when streaking. It must read from 10 feet. It looks good at 340 px diameter at 1080p (verified). Put it top centre or bottom centre, whichever does not cover the figure in that event.\\n\\n## 5. Events\\n120→\\n**Common frame:** event card (name, one-sentence goal, glyph prompts, one coach line), 3-2-1, play, result (score 0 to 1000, stars at 400, 650 and 850, a deadpan Title, minutes banked, personal best, difference from Yesterday You; Retry or Back).\\n\\n**Every event has:** a section of tunable numbers in `rules.toml`, a bot that earns at least 2 stars, an idle-input outcome below 1 star, a ghost lane, and an attract segment. Scenes `fit/event/<name>` start an event directly, for tools and tests.\\n\\n### Stillness Studio (Posey). Set: `studio`, a round white deck on a calm dawn lagoon. Camera: mirror view (yaw 0, tilt 12, distance 8.5, fov 36; the figure faces +Z, toward the camera, and stick right is screen right).\\n\\n**Breath Bloom** (45 s). Hold Action to inhale, release to exhale, following a guide ring: 4 s in, 4 s out, 5 cycles, the last one longer. `lungs` rises while held and falls when not. Keep the dot inside a centre ring of radius 0.35. Tick score: `0.7 * (1 - clamp(|lungs - guide| / 0.35)) + 0.3 * inRing`. Each good cycle opens a lotus on the water with a rising pentatonic chime; a perfect run blooms the whole pond. Scrub the clip `FIT/Breath` by `lungs`. No fail state. Bot: holds while the guide rises.\\n\\n**Pose Parade** (3 poses, 20 s each). Six hand-keyed poses with deadpan names: the Patient Heron, the Apologetic Lunge, the Tired Lighthouse, the Folded Deck Chair, the Reluctant Bridge, Seated Disappointment. Day 1 uses the first three. Posey holds the pose beside you. A target ring (radius 0.30 shrinking to 0.18) drifts on a slow Lissajous path (amplitude 0.35, 0.12 Hz). Inside the ring a streak multiplier climbs x1 to x4, one step per 2 s; leaving resets it. At 12 s of pose 2 a gull lands on your head and wobble is x1.6 for 5 s (\\\"There is a bird on you. Accept the bird\\\"). A tip breaks the pose for 1.5 s. Score: time in ring weighted by multiplier. Bot: PD toward the ring centre.\\n130→\\n### Iron Gazebo (Big Kettle). Set: `gazebo`, a white iron gazebo at golden hour. Camera: 3/4 front.\\n\\n**Tempo Squats** (10 reps, about 50 s). Hold Action to go down (2 s to full depth), release to rise (1 s). A guide bar shows the tempo; a low bell marks the bottom. Keep the dot in a band |x| < 0.25; wobble grows 8% per rep. Rep score: `0.7 * timing + 0.3 * band`. Scrub `FIT/Squat` by depth. Gag: rep 10 is followed by \\\"Ten. Also eleven.\\\" Bot: follows the guide.\\n\\n**Plank Standoff** (up to 60 s). Hold Brace and keep the dot in a ring shrinking from 0.40 to 0.20. Releasing, or leaving the ring for more than 1 s, collapses you in a comic flop. Fatigue ramps wobble; at 30 s add tremble; at 45 s Kettle laughs at his own joke and the nudge shakes the screen. Score: seconds survived / 60. Stars at 25, 40 and 55 s. Kettle, who has no arms, plank-talks you through it. Base the pose on one frame of `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`. Bot: survives at least 45 s.\\n\\n### Boardwalk (Bounce). Set: `boardwalk`, a beach boardwalk at bright midday.\\n\\n**Step Party** (64 s, 96 BPM, song 4). A rhythm game: notes in two lanes fall to two footprints, left, right or both, on an aerobic step box. Perfect within 55 ms, Good within 120 ms. About 100 notes, data in `charts.toml`, starting with quarter notes and building to eighths and doubles. Bounce bounces on the beat and guests clap on downbeats. Timing uses the audio clock (section 10). Camera: mirror view, slightly high. Bot: presses exactly on each note.\\n140→\\n**Floatie Spin** (50 s). Circle the lean (stick, mouse, or rolling W-D-S-A) to spin inflatable rings around your hips. Spin speed is the smoothed angular velocity of the lean while |lean| > 0.4; the sweet band is 6 to 9 rad/s, and a `spin_band_scale` rule widens it for keyboard. \\\"Switch!\\\" flips the required direction every 15 s. Guests toss new rings from left or right: press that side's step within 0.25 s of arrival to catch it. Out of band, rings sink; on the floor they are lost. Maximum 7 rings. Score: rings times time in band. Rings are no-physics entities positioned in code. Bot: 7.5 rad/s circle, presses on arrivals.\\n\\n**Morning Lap** (about 90 s, one lap of the hub island). Alternate left and right steps to set your pace (1.6 to 2.4 steps/s is the zone). Too fast raises a stitch meter that makes you stumble; too slow and Bounce, the pacer rolling ahead, gets away. The path steers you; lean moves you up to 1.2 m sideways to dodge crabs, sunbathers and towels and to grab ribbons. Flip-flops can be found here too. Score: time in zone, plus ribbons, minus bumps. Camera: chase with per-tick yaw. Use `MESH2MOTION/Jog` scaled to speed. Bot: 2 steps/s, steers to ribbons.\\n\\n### Lagoon (Commodore Gull). Sets: `tide`, `channel`, `pier`, `tower`.\\n\\n**Tide Table** (3 boards, 60 s total). You stand on a floating square raft and your lean tilts it. Roll hermit crabs in shells into tide pools. Board 1: 3 shells. Board 2: 5 shells and a moving pool. Board 3: 7 shells, bumpers and a rising tide. Fast shells skip over pools. Write the shell physics as simple 2D code (`a = tilt * g - friction * v`, wall bounce 0.5), not rapier: it is more tunable and bot-friendly. Score: shells potted plus time left. Camera: high 3/4 (tilt 62). Bot: PD steering of the nearest shell toward the nearest pool.\\n\\n**Paddle Slalom** (about 45 s). Stand on a paddleboard on a long channel and pass buoy gates. Lean x steers. Lean forward speeds up and risks tipping, lean back brakes. Gusts, shown as ripple streaks, push the dot. A tip is a big splash and a 2 s remount. A missed gate adds 2 s. `score = clamp((1.6 * par - t) / (0.8 * par)) * 1000`. Standing on water uses the trick in section 15; a silent `Wake` event every few ticks draws the wake. Camera: chase (tilt 22, distance 10). Bot: steers to gate centres at forward lean 0.5.\\n150→\\n**Tray Trek** (about 50 s). Walk a long pier at a fixed pace, carrying a tray with a stack of 5 smoothies. Waves, plank gaps and swooping gulls jolt the tray. Your dot tilts it. Glasses slide with tilt and plop into the sea past the edge. Score: 200 per glass delivered, plus a no-spill bonus. Marjorie receives what is left and comments. Use `STYLE100/Balance_Walk` plus an upper-body `FIT/CarryTray` clip. Bot: counters the jolts it knows are coming.\\n\\n**Cannonball Cup** (3 dives, about 40 s). The board bounces with a 1.2 s period. Press Action at the bottom of 3 bounces to build power, the 4th press leaps. In the air, hold Action to tuck and lean to rotate. Enter tucked and high for the biggest splash. Three gull judges hold up cards: \\\"6.5\\\", \\\"7\\\", \\\"See me\\\". \\\"We are not here for form. We are here for splash.\\\" Score: height x tuck x timing. Camera: side view (yaw 90, tilt 6, distance 14). The splash must be huge: a new `BigSplash` event scales the water dents and particles. This is the attract mode's hero shot. Bot: presses on bottoms, tucks at the apex.\\n\\n### The Big Stand (finale, about 2.5 minutes). Set: `bay`, a tiny post in the bay at sunset, with the whole cast watching from rafts.\\n\\nFive phases, reusing event code with new numbers:\\n1. Breathing, 4 cycles.\\n2. A pose under rising gusts, 20 s.\\n160→3. Step Party for 16 bars with a marching band of guests, wobble on.\\n4. Brace while waves crash, 20 s.\\n5. **The Long Stillness:** 30 s of nothing. Music fades to silence, the HUD vanishes except the Puck. At 15 s a fake prompt offers \\\"Press Cross to skip\\\". Pressing anything forfeits the Inner Peace bonus. Then Pip, quietly: \\\"...Oh. You're still here. Good.\\\"\\n\\nA tip drops you in the sea to a groan from the crowd and puts you back; it costs score and cannot end the run. Final Balance Age = morning age minus `final_score / 100` (up to 10).\\n\\n### Morning Wobble Check. Set: `studio`. About 70 s, four micro-tests, Pip presiding.\\n\\n| Test | What you do | Metric (0 to 1) |\\n|---|---|---|\\n170→| Stand Still (\\\"This is the whole test\\\") | Hold the dot centred for 8 s; one small nudge at 5 s | Mean distance from centre |\\n| Lean Targets | A left/right bar: reach \\\"70% left\\\", then two more targets, within 6%, hold 1.5 s; 5 s limit each | Time taken |\\n| Eyes Closed | 6 s. The screen dims to almost black, the Puck vanishes. A tone's pitch tells your offset, and rumble if the pad has it | Mean distance |\\n| Step Test | 8 alternating steps to a 100 BPM metronome | Timing |\\n\\n```\\nskill = 0.30*still + 0.25*targets + 0.25*blind + 0.20*steps\\nage   = 24 + 56 * (1 - skill)^1.1 - 2*days_completed - min(total_stars/3, 8)\\n```\\nClamp to 18..99, round. A middling player (skill 0.5) starts at 50 and reaches about 34 by Day 5; a weak one (skill 0.2) starts at 68 and ends near 52, before the finale's bonus. The big number rolls like a slot machine. Pip's comment is chosen by the change since yesterday and by the worst metric. A sparkline of 5 big dots shows the week. Your figure's posture improves as the age falls (a small constant forward slump through the tilt field, shrinking each day): visible progress, no numbers needed.\\n180→\\n## 6. Meta systems\\n\\n- **Minute Clam:** a giant clam at reception that gulps banked minutes with a gibberish burp. Totals unlock wardrobe items.\\n- **Calendar:** five big days, a stamp per completed day, then real days in free play. No tables.\\n- **Titles:** after each event Pip awards a deadpan title by score: Human Soup, Acceptable Human, Certified Lean-To, Wobble Enthusiast, Seasoned Tilter, Stillness Intern, Professional Standing Person, Alarmingly Balanced. At least 30, in `script.toml`.\\n- **Wardrobe:** reuse the engine's `GearLook`, which needs no new drawing (verified): `helm = cap` (sun cap), `helm = hood` (towel turban), `crown`, `halo`; `gloves` (sweatbands), `belt`, `pauldrons` (reads as arm floaties, funny). Plus shirt, pants and shoe colours. Skip `cape`: it draws long sticks.\\n- **Lost flip-flops:** 5 hidden on the island, for Two-Towel Tom. Reward: Golden Flip-Flops (gold shoes) and a line. This is the exploration layer.\\n- **Yesterday You:** your best run of each event is recorded and replayed as a tinted figure in a neighbouring lane, from Day 3.\\n- **Absence comments:** the page passes today's date to the game at boot, and the save stores the last day played. \\\"You were away for 2 days. I did not count them. There were 2.\\\" Passing the date in as data keeps the rule that the sim never reads the clock.\\n190→- **Saves:** versioned JSON in `localStorage`: guest slots (name, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings. Save on every change of day and every result.\\n\\n## 7. World, cast and writing\\n\\n**Tippy Cay** is about 64 x 48 m: reception at the centre (Pip's desk, Calendar wall, Minute Clam), a ring path for jogging, four pavilions around it, a row of cabanas, a pier, a diving tower and a water channel in the distance. Palms, grass, sand terraces, sea on all sides, circling gulls.\\n\\n| Character | What it is | Voice and manner |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Pip** | Sky-blue round wobble cushion, two dot eyes (`blob` plan, scale 0.7, squash 2.0, plus a small valve) | Front desk and scorekeeper. Relentlessly pleasant. Keeps records of everything. Never technically insults you. Squeaky rubber voice |\\n| **Posey** | Faceless wooden artist's mannequin (biped with eyes the colour of its skin; verified look in section 8) | Stillness. Serene, short, oddly poetic. Soft wood-block voice. It has no eyes and never blinks; \\\"This has not been discussed\\\" |\\n200→| **Big Kettle** | Cast-iron kettlebell (dark `blob` plus a torus handle part; add a `Handle` attach kind) | Strength. Booming, gentle, deeply supportive. No arms or legs, cannot do any exercise |\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":200,\"raw_output\":\"# Game plan: a balance-and-wellness comedy inspired by Wii Fit\\n\\nYou will build this game from this plan alone. The director is not available for questions.\\n\\n## 0. How to read this plan\\n\\n- **Your brief** means the brief in your own working folder. It wins on the title method, file and folder names, dates, the deliverables and the feedback questions. This plan names none of them.\\n- **Paths** are relative to the dev folder your brief tells you to create. Clone the engine to `engine/` inside it.\\n- **Numbers** are starting values. Tune them with the dev sliders and the bot. The structure is decided; change it only if it fails in play.\\n- **Gaps:** if something is not covered, decide, write one line in `notes/decisions.md`, and carry on.\\n- **Verified** means it was run on this computer on 2026-11-04, against engine commit `49ef2ba` and AI Hub client 1.4.0. Section 15 lists those results.\\n- **Title:** pick it first, the way your brief says. Keep it in one constant. This plan calls it \\\"the game\\\". The resort's name, Tippy Cay, belongs to the world and does not depend on the title.\\n- **Reading cost:** you do not need to read the engine's source to start. Read `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` whole (about 3k tokens) and `engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/starter.rs`, then use this plan. Search `engine/docs/REFERENCE.md` and `engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` when you need a tool or a prop field.\\n\\n## 1. The game in one page\\n\\nYou have won a five-day stay at Tippy Cay, a small wellness resort staffed entirely by talking gym equipment. You do not remember entering. Each morning a relentlessly pleasant wobble cushion tests your balance and gives you a Balance Age. Each day you walk the island, try short stillness, strength, cardio and balance events, and bank minutes in a giant clam. Checkout requires a Balance Age of 40 or better. Day 5 ends in the Big Stand, a finale whose last test is to do nothing at all for thirty seconds while the game tries to make you press something.\\n\\n- **Genre:** sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame (daily ritual, unlocks, wardrobe). Catalogue genre: Sports.\\n- **Perspective:** third person throughout, with a camera chosen per activity: 3/4 follow on the island, a mirror-style front view for exercises on the spot, chase for the jog and the paddle, high 3/4 for the table, side view for the dives.\\n- **Length:** a first run takes 25 to 40 minutes. It shows every feature. Free play follows.\\n\\n| What makes Wii Fit distinctive | How this game turns it into play |\\n|---|---|\\n| A balance board: your centre of pressure is the only verb, and tiny movements matter | The Balance Core (section 4): one analog dot driven by lean. Every event is played through it |\\n| The body test and the verdict of a fitness age | The Morning Wobble Check and Balance Age. Never weight, BMI or body shape |\\n| Equipment that talks: cheerful, polite, quietly rude | Pip, a talking wobble cushion, plus a whole staff of talking gear |\\n| A calm, uncanny instructor | Posey, a faceless wooden artist's mannequin |\\n| Four disciplines: yoga, strength, aerobics, balance games | Four pavilions, each with its own coach and events |\\n| The daily ritual: calendar stamps, banked minutes that unlock more | Calendar stamps and the Minute Clam |\\n| Noticing how long you stayed away | Real-date absence comments from Pip |\\n| A family sharing one board and comparing progress | Hot-seat Medley, Yesterday You ghosts, AI Hub sessions |\\n| Clean, quiet, pastel, unintentionally funny | High-key pastel look, gentle lounge music, short deadpan text |\\n\\n**Pillars.** Check every decision against these.\\n1. **Small movements, big consequences.** Mastery means doing less. The best moments are held breaths.\\n2. **Deadpan encouragement.** Everything you do is commented on, kindly, and slightly too honestly.\\n3. **A daily ritual.** Check in, get a number, do your exercises, get a stamp.\\n4. **Calm surface, silly underneath.** The screen stays serene while a seagull stands on your head.\\n\\n**Originality rules.** This is an original game in the same genre, not a recreation.\\n- Inside the game, use no Nintendo names (Wii, Mii, Balance Board and so on). The only exceptions are the Source line on the About screen and whatever your title's riff requires.\\n- No white rectangular board with dot eyes. No pale human trainer in a tank top and ponytail. No Mii-style avatars or face editors. No island or plaza from the source series.\\n- No source music, jingles, menu layouts or screen compositions. Do not quote or paraphrase its lines. Write your own.\\n- Events have their own names and twists, as specified below.\\n- Respect bodies: no weight, BMI, body-shape jokes or diet talk anywhere. Pip judges your wobble, your habits and your absences.\\n\\n## 2. Structure of play\\n\\n**Boot:** title screen over a slow island sweep. Menu: New Stay or Continue, Play Together, Settings, About. After 10 seconds with no input on the title or any pre-game menu, attract mode starts (section 12).\\n\\n**New Stay:** choose one of 4 guest slots, pick a name from a list of about 40 funny preset names (no on-screen keyboard), pick a look (6 skin tones, 8 outfits). Then a short intro with Pip at reception, skippable.\\n\\n**A day:**\\n1. Wake on the cabana deck. Pip greets you, with an absence comment if real days have passed.\\n2. Morning Wobble Check (about 70 seconds), Balance Age reveal, Pip's comment.\\n3. Free time on the island: walk, talk to guests, find lost flip-flops, step on an event mat. The Schedule (Triangle or Tab) lists everything and fast-travels.\\n4. When the day's minute goal is met, Pip says so. Sleep at your cabana (or choose End Day in the Schedule). A big stamp lands on the Calendar. Next day.\\n\\n| Day | Opens | Minute goal | Story beat |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Stillness Studio: Breath Bloom, Pose Parade | 3 | Arrival. The checkout rule. \\\"Nobody has asked to leave yet\\\" |\\n| 2 | Iron Gazebo: Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff | 5 | Big Kettle. Wardrobe opens |\\n| 3 | Boardwalk: Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap | 7 | Yesterday You appears as a ghost. \\\"I am not comparing you\\\" |\\n| 4 | Lagoon: Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup | 9 | Guests start whispering about the Big Stand |\\n| 5 | The Big Stand, after the morning check | none | Finale, ending, free play |\\n\\n**Minutes:** the first clear of an event each day banks 1 + stars (0 to 3 stars, so 1 to 4 minutes); repeats bank 1. Resort minutes are openly not real minutes (\\\"Our minutes are longer. It is a wellness thing\\\").\\n\\n**Endings:** Balance Age 40 or better: you may check out, by rowboat (`LIB/core/rowboat`). Otherwise: the Extended Stay ending, gentle and funny. Both roll credits, then unlock Free Play: every event open, personal bests, star goals, and a calendar that keeps stamping real days.\\n\\n**Bot rule:** `Game::bot` must be able to play this entire flow, menus included, from New Stay to the credits. That is your scripted playthrough and the base of attract mode.\\n\\n## 3. Controls\\n\\nThe left stick is both walking and leaning. Prompts always show the glyph for the input used last.\\n\\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Walk on the island, lean in events | Left stick | W A S D (arrows also walk) | Island: click a place or thing to walk there. Events: cursor offset from screen centre is the lean |\\n| Fine lean | Stick itself | Hold Shift (half key rate) | Small cursor moves |\\n| Jog on the island | Hold R2 | Hold Shift | |\\n| Action: talk, begin, inhale, squat, bounce | Cross | Space | Left button |\\n| Left step / right step | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 | Q or Left / E or Right | Left button / right button |\\n| Brace (hold both) | L2+R2 or L1+R1 | Q+E | Both buttons |\\n| Wave at someone | Square | F | |\\n| Schedule | Triangle | Tab | |\\n| Island camera | Right stick | | Right-drag, wheel zooms |\\n| Pause | Options | Esc | |\\n| Menus | D-pad or left stick, Cross confirms, Circle backs, L1/R1 change tabs | Arrows or W A S D, Enter or Space, Esc backs, Q/E change tabs | Hover moves focus, click activates, right-click backs |\\n\\nXbox glyphs (Settings option) swap A B X Y, LB RB LT RT, Menu. Ignore Options while Create is held: that pair belongs to the AI Hub. Disable the engine's own keys (F1 to F10, digits, H, Backspace rewind, right-drag tilt) outside dev mode. Keep F11 for fullscreen.\\n\\n## 4. The Balance Core\\n\\nOne struct, `BalanceCore`, used by every event. Its state is `cob` (the dot, unit disc, x right, y up on screen) and `vel`.\\n\\n```\\ntarget = shaped lean input * reach + wobble(t)\\nacc    = (target - cob) * stiffness - vel * damping + gust + nudge\\nvel   += acc * dt\\ncob   += vel * dt\\ntip    = |cob| > 1 for tip_time seconds\\n```\\n\\nStart with `stiffness 40`, `damping 8.5`, `reach 0.92`, `tip_time 0.35`. `wobble` is `amp * (0.7 * sin(2*pi*1.3*t + a) + 0.3 * sin(2*pi*2.9*t + b))` per axis, phases from `sim.state.rng`, base `amp 0.12`, scaled per event and by fatigue, plus a velocity kick of 0.1 units/s in a random direction every 1 to 2 seconds. Use sim time, never the clock.\\n\\n**Feel targets** (these numbers give them, by numeric simulation at 60 ticks/s): full stick reaches 90% in about 0.4 s with about 5% overshoot, like a body. Release settles in about 0.45 s. Left alone, the dot wanders at a mean radius of 0.05, at most 0.08. A held full lean does not tip by itself; a gust on top of it does.\\n\\n**Input shaping** (in `pav_app`, passed as `InputFrame.lean`, screen space):\\n- **Stick:** deadzone 0.12, response curve `x^1.5` so small motions are fine.\\n- **Keyboard:** keys move the target at 1.6 units/s and it returns at 1.2 units/s when released. Tapping gives small nudges, so keys feel native, not bang-bang.\\n- **Mouse:** cursor offset from the screen centre divided by 0.38 of the window height, clamped to the disc. No pointer lock. The device moved last wins.\\n\\n**Body:** the figure tilts with the dot (`cob * 14` degrees about the feet, engine change in section 14). Beyond |cob| 0.75 an upper-body arm-flail clip fades in. A tip plays a stumble and, over water, a splash. Tips never end the game; they cost time or score.\\n\\n**HUD, the Puck:** a large circular gauge drawn in egui: a pale disc, a green target ring, a coral dot, and stars at the edge when streaking. It must read from 10 feet. It looks good at 340 px diameter at 1080p (verified). Put it top centre or bottom centre, whichever does not cover the figure in that event.\\n\\n## 5. Events\\n\\n**Common frame:** event card (name, one-sentence goal, glyph prompts, one coach line), 3-2-1, play, result (score 0 to 1000, stars at 400, 650 and 850, a deadpan Title, minutes banked, personal best, difference from Yesterday You; Retry or Back).\\n\\n**Every event has:** a section of tunable numbers in `rules.toml`, a bot that earns at least 2 stars, an idle-input outcome below 1 star, a ghost lane, and an attract segment. Scenes `fit/event/<name>` start an event directly, for tools and tests.\\n\\n### Stillness Studio (Posey). Set: `studio`, a round white deck on a calm dawn lagoon. Camera: mirror view (yaw 0, tilt 12, distance 8.5, fov 36; the figure faces +Z, toward the camera, and stick right is screen right).\\n\\n**Breath Bloom** (45 s). Hold Action to inhale, release to exhale, following a guide ring: 4 s in, 4 s out, 5 cycles, the last one longer. `lungs` rises while held and falls when not. Keep the dot inside a centre ring of radius 0.35. Tick score: `0.7 * (1 - clamp(|lungs - guide| / 0.35)) + 0.3 * inRing`. Each good cycle opens a lotus on the water with a rising pentatonic chime; a perfect run blooms the whole pond. Scrub the clip `FIT/Breath` by `lungs`. No fail state. Bot: holds while the guide rises.\\n\\n**Pose Parade** (3 poses, 20 s each). Six hand-keyed poses with deadpan names: the Patient Heron, the Apologetic Lunge, the Tired Lighthouse, the Folded Deck Chair, the Reluctant Bridge, Seated Disappointment. Day 1 uses the first three. Posey holds the pose beside you. A target ring (radius 0.30 shrinking to 0.18) drifts on a slow Lissajous path (amplitude 0.35, 0.12 Hz). Inside the ring a streak multiplier climbs x1 to x4, one step per 2 s; leaving resets it. At 12 s of pose 2 a gull lands on your head and wobble is x1.6 for 5 s (\\\"There is a bird on you. Accept the bird\\\"). A tip breaks the pose for 1.5 s. Score: time in ring weighted by multiplier. Bot: PD toward the ring centre.\\n\\n### Iron Gazebo (Big Kettle). Set: `gazebo`, a white iron gazebo at golden hour. Camera: 3/4 front.\\n\\n**Tempo Squats** (10 reps, about 50 s). Hold Action to go down (2 s to full depth), release to rise (1 s). A guide bar shows the tempo; a low bell marks the bottom. Keep the dot in a band |x| < 0.25; wobble grows 8% per rep. Rep score: `0.7 * timing + 0.3 * band`. Scrub `FIT/Squat` by depth. Gag: rep 10 is followed by \\\"Ten. Also eleven.\\\" Bot: follows the guide.\\n\\n**Plank Standoff** (up to 60 s). Hold Brace and keep the dot in a ring shrinking from 0.40 to 0.20. Releasing, or leaving the ring for more than 1 s, collapses you in a comic flop. Fatigue ramps wobble; at 30 s add tremble; at 45 s Kettle laughs at his own joke and the nudge shakes the screen. Score: seconds survived / 60. Stars at 25, 40 and 55 s. Kettle, who has no arms, plank-talks you through it. Base the pose on one frame of `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`. Bot: survives at least 45 s.\\n\\n### Boardwalk (Bounce). Set: `boardwalk`, a beach boardwalk at bright midday.\\n\\n**Step Party** (64 s, 96 BPM, song 4). A rhythm game: notes in two lanes fall to two footprints, left, right or both, on an aerobic step box. Perfect within 55 ms, Good within 120 ms. About 100 notes, data in `charts.toml`, starting with quarter notes and building to eighths and doubles. Bounce bounces on the beat and guests clap on downbeats. Timing uses the audio clock (section 10). Camera: mirror view, slightly high. Bot: presses exactly on each note.\\n\\n**Floatie Spin** (50 s). Circle the lean (stick, mouse, or rolling W-D-S-A) to spin inflatable rings around your hips. Spin speed is the smoothed angular velocity of the lean while |lean| > 0.4; the sweet band is 6 to 9 rad/s, and a `spin_band_scale` rule widens it for keyboard. \\\"Switch!\\\" flips the required direction every 15 s. Guests toss new rings from left or right: press that side's step within 0.25 s of arrival to catch it. Out of band, rings sink; on the floor they are lost. Maximum 7 rings. Score: rings times time in band. Rings are no-physics entities positioned in code. Bot: 7.5 rad/s circle, presses on arrivals.\\n\\n**Morning Lap** (about 90 s, one lap of the hub island). Alternate left and right steps to set your pace (1.6 to 2.4 steps/s is the zone). Too fast raises a stitch meter that makes you stumble; too slow and Bounce, the pacer rolling ahead, gets away. The path steers you; lean moves you up to 1.2 m sideways to dodge crabs, sunbathers and towels and to grab ribbons. Flip-flops can be found here too. Score: time in zone, plus ribbons, minus bumps. Camera: chase with per-tick yaw. Use `MESH2MOTION/Jog` scaled to speed. Bot: 2 steps/s, steers to ribbons.\\n\\n### Lagoon (Commodore Gull). Sets: `tide`, `channel`, `pier`, `tower`.\\n\\n**Tide Table** (3 boards, 60 s total). You stand on a floating square raft and your lean tilts it. Roll hermit crabs in shells into tide pools. Board 1: 3 shells. Board 2: 5 shells and a moving pool. Board 3: 7 shells, bumpers and a rising tide. Fast shells skip over pools. Write the shell physics as simple 2D code (`a = tilt * g - friction * v`, wall bounce 0.5), not rapier: it is more tunable and bot-friendly. Score: shells potted plus time left. Camera: high 3/4 (tilt 62). Bot: PD steering of the nearest shell toward the nearest pool.\\n\\n**Paddle Slalom** (about 45 s). Stand on a paddleboard on a long channel and pass buoy gates. Lean x steers. Lean forward speeds up and risks tipping, lean back brakes. Gusts, shown as ripple streaks, push the dot. A tip is a big splash and a 2 s remount. A missed gate adds 2 s. `score = clamp((1.6 * par - t) / (0.8 * par)) * 1000`. Standing on water uses the trick in section 15; a silent `Wake` event every few ticks draws the wake. Camera: chase (tilt 22, distance 10). Bot: steers to gate centres at forward lean 0.5.\\n\\n**Tray Trek** (about 50 s). Walk a long pier at a fixed pace, carrying a tray with a stack of 5 smoothies. Waves, plank gaps and swooping gulls jolt the tray. Your dot tilts it. Glasses slide with tilt and plop into the sea past the edge. Score: 200 per glass delivered, plus a no-spill bonus. Marjorie receives what is left and comments. Use `STYLE100/Balance_Walk` plus an upper-body `FIT/CarryTray` clip. Bot: counters the jolts it knows are coming.\\n\\n**Cannonball Cup** (3 dives, about 40 s). The board bounces with a 1.2 s period. Press Action at the bottom of 3 bounces to build power, the 4th press leaps. In the air, hold Action to tuck and lean to rotate. Enter tucked and high for the biggest splash. Three gull judges hold up cards: \\\"6.5\\\", \\\"7\\\", \\\"See me\\\". \\\"We are not here for form. We are here for splash.\\\" Score: height x tuck x timing. Camera: side view (yaw 90, tilt 6, distance 14). The splash must be huge: a new `BigSplash` event scales the water dents and particles. This is the attract mode's hero shot. Bot: presses on bottoms, tucks at the apex.\\n\\n### The Big Stand (finale, about 2.5 minutes). Set: `bay`, a tiny post in the bay at sunset, with the whole cast watching from rafts.\\n\\nFive phases, reusing event code with new numbers:\\n1. Breathing, 4 cycles.\\n2. A pose under rising gusts, 20 s.\\n3. Step Party for 16 bars with a marching band of guests, wobble on.\\n4. Brace while waves crash, 20 s.\\n5. **The Long Stillness:** 30 s of nothing. Music fades to silence, the HUD vanishes except the Puck. At 15 s a fake prompt offers \\\"Press Cross to skip\\\". Pressing anything forfeits the Inner Peace bonus. Then Pip, quietly: \\\"...Oh. You're still here. Good.\\\"\\n\\nA tip drops you in the sea to a groan from the crowd and puts you back; it costs score and cannot end the run. Final Balance Age = morning age minus `final_score / 100` (up to 10).\\n\\n### Morning Wobble Check. Set: `studio`. About 70 s, four micro-tests, Pip presiding.\\n\\n| Test | What you do | Metric (0 to 1) |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Stand Still (\\\"This is the whole test\\\") | Hold the dot centred for 8 s; one small nudge at 5 s | Mean distance from centre |\\n| Lean Targets | A left/right bar: reach \\\"70% left\\\", then two more targets, within 6%, hold 1.5 s; 5 s limit each | Time taken |\\n| Eyes Closed | 6 s. The screen dims to almost black, the Puck vanishes. A tone's pitch tells your offset, and rumble if the pad has it | Mean distance |\\n| Step Test | 8 alternating steps to a 100 BPM metronome | Timing |\\n\\n```\\nskill = 0.30*still + 0.25*targets + 0.25*blind + 0.20*steps\\nage   = 24 + 56 * (1 - skill)^1.1 - 2*days_completed - min(total_stars/3, 8)\\n```\\nClamp to 18..99, round. A middling player (skill 0.5) starts at 50 and reaches about 34 by Day 5; a weak one (skill 0.2) starts at 68 and ends near 52, before the finale's bonus. The big number rolls like a slot machine. Pip's comment is chosen by the change since yesterday and by the worst metric. A sparkline of 5 big dots shows the week. Your figure's posture improves as the age falls (a small constant forward slump through the tilt field, shrinking each day): visible progress, no numbers needed.\\n\\n## 6. Meta systems\\n\\n- **Minute Clam:** a giant clam at reception that gulps banked minutes with a gibberish burp. Totals unlock wardrobe items.\\n- **Calendar:** five big days, a stamp per completed day, then real days in free play. No tables.\\n- **Titles:** after each event Pip awards a deadpan title by score: Human Soup, Acceptable Human, Certified Lean-To, Wobble Enthusiast, Seasoned Tilter, Stillness Intern, Professional Standing Person, Alarmingly Balanced. At least 30, in `script.toml`.\\n- **Wardrobe:** reuse the engine's `GearLook`, which needs no new drawing (verified): `helm = cap` (sun cap), `helm = hood` (towel turban), `crown`, `halo`; `gloves` (sweatbands), `belt`, `pauldrons` (reads as arm floaties, funny). Plus shirt, pants and shoe colours. Skip `cape`: it draws long sticks.\\n- **Lost flip-flops:** 5 hidden on the island, for Two-Towel Tom. Reward: Golden Flip-Flops (gold shoes) and a line. This is the exploration layer.\\n- **Yesterday You:** your best run of each event is recorded and replayed as a tinted figure in a neighbouring lane, from Day 3.\\n- **Absence comments:** the page passes today's date to the game at boot, and the save stores the last day played. \\\"You were away for 2 days. I did not count them. There were 2.\\\" Passing the date in as data keeps the rule that the sim never reads the clock.\\n- **Saves:** versioned JSON in `localStorage`: guest slots (name, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings. Save on every change of day and every result.\\n\\n## 7. World, cast and writing\\n\\n**Tippy Cay** is about 64 x 48 m: reception at the centre (Pip's desk, Calendar wall, Minute Clam), a ring path for jogging, four pavilions around it, a row of cabanas, a pier, a diving tower and a water channel in the distance. Palms, grass, sand terraces, sea on all sides, circling gulls.\\n\\n| Character | What it is | Voice and manner |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Pip** | Sky-blue round wobble cushion, two dot eyes (`blob` plan, scale 0.7, squash 2.0, plus a small valve) | Front desk and scorekeeper. Relentlessly pleasant. Keeps records of everything. Never technically insults you. Squeaky rubber voice |\\n| **Posey** | Faceless wooden artist's mannequin (biped with eyes the colour of its skin; verified look in section 8) | Stillness. Serene, short, oddly poetic. Soft wood-block voice. It has no eyes and never blinks; \\\"This has not been discussed\\\" |\\n| **Big Kettle** | Cast-iron kettlebell (dark `blob` plus a torus handle part; add a `Handle` attach kind) | Strength. Booming, gentle, deeply supportive. No arms or legs, cannot do any exercise |\\n\",\"total_lines\":632}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d064fcd3-1bf6-4951-b108-422d07e2083d-5","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Wobble Minutes\\n\\nFive days at Tippy Cay. One verb: lean. The stay, the menus and every event live in the sim (`engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/`). The window only draws that state and sends input back.\\n\\nRun the tests from this folder:\\n\\n```sh\\ntests/run.sh core\\n```\\n10→\\nPack the single page (writes the HTML into the work folder):\\n\\n```sh\\ntools/build.sh\\n```\\n\\n## Add an event\\n\\n1. Add a variant to `EventId` in `events.rs`, plus its key, title and blurb. `ALL` is the list the schedule, the lint and direct scene `fit/event/<key>` use.\\n20→2. Put its duration and the one number you tune in `rules.toml`. Reset copies that file.\\n3. Teach `Activity` to play it in `events.rs`, including the bot's lean. Stars are 400 / 650 / 850, except the plank, which uses its time gates.\\n4. Add a card line in `script.toml`. Mention it on the day that opens it, in the day table in `mod.rs`.\\n5. `tests/run.sh core` plays it with the bot on five seeds and with idle input.\\n\\n## Add a set\\n\\nThe island is one room, `hub.toml`, placed by `build()`. A new mat is another cluster of props in that file (or a second room whose origin sits 200 m away, the way `RoomDef` placement already works). Give the zone a water colour if it is a pool. Do not put the set in `engine/rooms/`: that folder feeds the pavilion demo. `pav capture scene=fit` shows the result.\\n\\n## Add a song\\n30→\\nBeds live in the mixer in `pav_audio`: a root frequency and a tempo per song id. `FitGame::desired_song` picks the id (0 is silence, used by the attract and before the first real input). Default music gain is 0.10. Add the bed, map the flow or the event to the new id, and keep the audio test green: every bed is non-silent, and 0.10 is a tenth of full scale.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Wobble Minutes\\n\\nFive days at Tippy Cay. One verb: lean. The stay, the menus and every event live in the sim (`engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/`). The window only draws that state and sends input back.\\n\\nRun the tests from this folder:\\n\\n```sh\\ntests/run.sh core\\n```\\n10→\\nPack the single page (writes the HTML into the work folder):\\n\\n```sh\\ntools/build.sh\\n```\\n\\n## Add an event\\n\\n1. Add a variant to `EventId` in `events.rs`, plus its key, title and blurb. `ALL` is the list the schedule, the lint and direct scene `fit/event/<key>` use.\\n20→2. Put its duration and the one number you tune in `rules.toml`. Reset copies that file.\\n3. Teach `Activity` to play it in `events.rs`, including the bot's lean. Stars are 400 / 650 / 850, except the plank, which uses its time gates.\\n4. Add a card line in `script.toml`. Mention it on the day that opens it, in the day table in `mod.rs`.\\n5. `tests/run.sh core` plays it with the bot on five seeds and with idle input.\\n\\n## Add a set\\n\\nThe island is one room, `hub.toml`, placed by `build()`. A new mat is another cluster of props in that file (or a second room whose origin sits 200 m away, the way `RoomDef` placement already works). Give the zone a water colour if it is a pool. Do not put the set in `engine/rooms/`: that folder feeds the pavilion demo. `pav capture scene=fit` shows the result.\\n\\n## Add a song\\n30→\\nBeds live in the mixer in `pav_audio`: a root frequency and a tempo per song id. `FitGame::desired_song` picks the id (0 is silence, used by the attract and before the first real input). Default music gain is 0.10. Add the bed, map the flow or the event to the new id, and keep the audio test green: every bed is non-silent, and 0.10 is a tenth of full scale.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/README.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":150,\"raw_output\":\"# Wobble Minutes\\n\\nFive days at Tippy Cay. One verb: lean. The stay, the menus and every event live in the sim (`engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/`). The window only draws that state and sends input back.\\n\\nRun the tests from this folder:\\n\\n```sh\\ntests/run.sh core\\n```\\n\\nPack the single page (writes the HTML into the work folder):\\n\\n```sh\\ntools/build.sh\\n```\\n\\n## Add an event\\n\\n1. Add a variant to `EventId` in `events.rs`, plus its key, title and blurb. `ALL` is the list the schedule, the lint and direct scene `fit/event/<key>` use.\\n2. Put its duration and the one number you tune in `rules.toml`. Reset copies that file.\\n3. Teach `Activity` to play it in `events.rs`, including the bot's lean. Stars are 400 / 650 / 850, except the plank, which uses its time gates.\\n4. Add a card line in `script.toml`. Mention it on the day that opens it, in the day table in `mod.rs`.\\n5. `tests/run.sh core` plays it with the bot on five seeds and with idle input.\\n\\n## Add a set\\n\\nThe island is one room, `hub.toml`, placed by `build()`. A new mat is another cluster of props in that file (or a second room whose origin sits 200 m away, the way `RoomDef` placement already works). Give the zone a water colour if it is a pool. Do not put the set in `engine/rooms/`: that folder feeds the pavilion demo. `pav capture scene=fit` shows the result.\\n\\n## Add a song\\n\\nBeds live in the mixer in `pav_audio`: a root frequency and a tempo per song id. `FitGame::desired_song` picks the id (0 is silence, used by the attract and before the first real input). Default music gain is 0.10. Add the bed, map the flow or the event to the new id, and keep the audio test green: every bed is non-silent, and 0.10 is a tenth of full scale.\\n\",\"total_lines\":31}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"1e9e45b9-01ba-4dd6-bde4-d6f474715baa"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1064","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to read more of PLAN.md to understand the game and how to run it.\n\nThe deliverable is a single playable HTML file. Open it in a browser to play.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fecbf228-95d2-412c-99e5-b2c40f463eb2-6","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fecbf228-95d2-412c-99e5-b2c40f463eb2-7","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/hub/README.md","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fecbf228-95d2-412c-99e5-b2c40f463eb2-8","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fecbf228-95d2-412c-99e5-b2c40f463eb2-9","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"open |file://|how to play|browser|index.html","glob":"README.md","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10138,"output_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":12160,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa27-ba86-7730-89c2-9178ff908bce","uuid":"600537f4-fd2e-4254-8e27-0ea4f52ed2a5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fecbf228-95d2-412c-99e5-b2c40f463eb2-6","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n10→  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n20→  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n30→    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n40→    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n50→      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\\n      },\\n      removeItem: function (k) {\\n        delete data[String(k)];\\n      },\\n60→      clear: function () {\\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\\n      },\\n      key: function (i) {\\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\\n      },\\n    };\\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\\n    return new Proxy(api, {\\n70→      get: function (t, k) {\\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\\n      },\\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\\n        return true;\\n      },\\n      has: function (t, k) {\\n80→        return k in data || k in t;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n10→  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n20→  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n30→    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n40→    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n50→      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\\n      },\\n      removeItem: function (k) {\\n        delete data[String(k)];\\n      },\\n60→      clear: function () {\\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\\n      },\\n      key: function (i) {\\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\\n      },\\n    };\\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\\n    return new Proxy(api, {\\n70→      get: function (t, k) {\\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\\n      },\\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\\n        return true;\\n      },\\n      has: function (t, k) {\\n80→        return k in data || k in t;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132.html\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\\n      },\\n      removeItem: function (k) {\\n        delete data[String(k)];\\n      },\\n      clear: function () {\\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\\n      },\\n      key: function (i) {\\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\\n      },\\n    };\\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\\n    return new Proxy(api, {\\n      get: function (t, k) {\\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\\n      },\\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\\n        return true;\\n      },\\n      has: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data || k in t;\\n\",\"total_lines\":3253}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fecbf228-95d2-412c-99e5-b2c40f463eb2-7","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\\n\\nAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\\nplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\\nround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\\nscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\\nround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\\n\\n**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\\n10→\\nThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\\ndescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\\n\\n- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\\n- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\\n\\nTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\\n\\n> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\\n20→> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\\n> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Modes\\n\\nA game declares one mode.\\n\\n| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\\n30→|---|---|---|\\n| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\\n| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\\n| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\\n\\n- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\\n  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\\n- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\\n  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\\n  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\\n40→- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\\n  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\\n  world the host sends them.\\n\\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\\n`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## A round\\n50→\\n1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\\n   to 30 seconds with the game's card: what the game is, how to win, the\\n   controls. The card is the hub's, from the game's tags, or the game's own\\n   (*The card*).\\n2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\\n4. The game reports how it goes.\\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\\n60→   over the game, then removes it.\\n\\n### Tags\\n\\nIn the game's `<head>`:\\n\\n```html\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"MIN-MAX\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"MODE\\\">\\n70→<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"GOAL\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"CONTROLS\\\">\\n```\\n\\n- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\\n  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\\n  is in that range.\\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\\n  controls, shown on the hub's card.\\n80→\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\\n\\nAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\\nplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\\nround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\\nscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\\nround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\\n\\n**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\\n10→\\nThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\\ndescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\\n\\n- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\\n- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\\n\\nTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\\n\\n> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\\n20→> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\\n> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Modes\\n\\nA game declares one mode.\\n\\n| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\\n30→|---|---|---|\\n| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\\n| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\\n| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\\n\\n- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\\n  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\\n- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\\n  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\\n  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\\n40→- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\\n  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\\n  world the host sends them.\\n\\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\\n`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## A round\\n50→\\n1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\\n   to 30 seconds with the game's card: what the game is, how to win, the\\n   controls. The card is the hub's, from the game's tags, or the game's own\\n   (*The card*).\\n2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\\n4. The game reports how it goes.\\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\\n60→   over the game, then removes it.\\n\\n### Tags\\n\\nIn the game's `<head>`:\\n\\n```html\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"MIN-MAX\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"MODE\\\">\\n70→<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"GOAL\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"CONTROLS\\\">\\n```\\n\\n- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\\n  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\\n  is in that range.\\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\\n  controls, shown on the hub's card.\\n80→\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/Wobble Minutes-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-222132/hub/README.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\\n\\nAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\\nplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\\nround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\\nscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\\nround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\\n\\n**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\\n\\nThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\\ndescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\\n\\n- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\\n- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\\n\\nTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\\n\\n> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\\n> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\\n> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Modes\\n\\nA game declares one mode.\\n\\n| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\\n| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\\n| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\\n\\n- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\\n  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\\n- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\\n  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\\n  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\\n- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\\n  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\\n  world the host sends them.\\n\\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\\n`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## A round\\n\\n1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\\n   to 30 seconds with the game's card: what the game is, how to win, the\\n   controls. The card is the hub's, from the game's tags, or the game's own\\n   (*The card*).\\n2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\\n4. The game reports how it goes.\\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\\n   over the game, then removes it.\\n\\n### Tags\\n\\nIn the game's `<head>`:\\n\\n```html\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"MIN-MAX\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"MODE\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"GOAL\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"CONTROLS\\\">\\n```\\n\\n- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\\n  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\\n  is in that range.\\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\\n  controls, shown on the hub's card.\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":410}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fecbf228-95d2-412c-99e5-b2c40f463eb2-8","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:21:32\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Shardfall engine (Pavilion: Rust, wgpu, egui 0.36.2), commit 49ef2ba, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's cel look, high-key pastel, beach and wellness props. Library props only for generic dressing.\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine puppet tilts about the feet from the balance dot. Exercise poses are hand-keyed clips on that puppet: Tree, Warrior, Fold, Squat, Plank and Bloom.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Music, effects and voices are synthesized in code. No audio files. Seven music beds, default music gain 0.10. At least 30 effects. Animalese voices.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players. The round is the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup).\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU at 320×180, phone and tablet profiles, WebKit iPhone fallback, and the AI Hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The build followed PLAN.md and the engine source. The title was drawn with a real RNG from 50 riffs. No separate web search in this session.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Fifteen defects showed up in testing. The first six were a gust check that did not match the acceleration model, an egui texture delta dropped on the floor, a private intent module, fonts bound in the same pass that drew them, a hub ghost field that was a boolean, and About pages that did not turn. A review of that build found eight more: sliders that never moved, Dev Mode with no jump, cheats or time scale, a free-play schedule stuck on the first four events, a Big Stand that kept its song and never showed the fake skip or the final age cut, an eyes-closed check with no tone, name and outfit lists that stopped at six, and a beach with no props or exercise poses. The drag path then failed to compile because a set lookup wanted a reference.\\\",\\n    \\\"Three were critical. The font and texture-delta panic stops the browser frame loop, so the page sits there with a status that never ticks. After credits, seven events could not be started. A morning age of 41 to 50 could not reach the rowboat even after a strong finale.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the bot playthrough: three seeds from New Stay to the credits, plus each event on five seeds against an idle player. The later menu tests drive the real pad and pointer path, including a held pointer on a slider row.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful check is a 1920×1080 WebGPU screenshot. On this machine that bitmap can come back blank while the sim is fine. 320×180 is the timing check, and the engine's own capture is the picture.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The sim is one tick you can drive with no GPU, and the picture is a pure view of that tick. That split is what made the whole stay testable.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A gust is an acceleration, so gust 30 with no lean settles inside the disc and does not tip. egui 0.36 panics if a TexturesDelta is dropped. Pause still increments the tick; the world time is what freezes.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance model, the day loop, and every event. The engine does not have a centre-of-pressure verb.\\\",\\n    \\\"The app frame. The demo's keys, menus and chrome run in the same function as the game, and a fit frame has to turn all of that off without breaking the engine's other scenes.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"frozen() returns early inside the tick. InputFrame gained lean, device, ui and hub. The HUD carries the fit UI and a status string. The mixer plays song beds. The page bridge publishes status. Captures composite the fit UI. Puppets tilt about the feet. Splash and a silent wake were added for the lagoon. Fit pointer drags emit slider values. Hand-keyed clips play the exercise poses. The beach room gained dressing with no collision.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to publish one JSON value that is both a string (for JSON.parse) and an object (for .tick), without hand-rolling a String constructor.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan is specific about the feel, the roster and the hub snippet, and it says behaviour is the contract when a filename does not match the engine.\\\",\\n    \\\"Song numbers in the plan and the beds the sim actually requests do not use the same index. The hub snippet sends whatever status.hub.ghost is, so a boolean there is sent as a boolean.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping the full roster, the 10-foot shell and the hub harness on a 20 GB machine where one extra browser gets killed.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say, next to the gust sentence, that a full lean alone must not tip and a gust on top of that lean must. State that plan filenames are guidance in the same paragraph as the file tree.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Wobble Minutes\\\",\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:21:32\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Shardfall engine (Pavilion: Rust, wgpu, egui 0.36.2), commit 49ef2ba, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's cel look, high-key pastel, beach and wellness props. Library props only for generic dressing.\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine puppet tilts about the feet from the balance dot. Exercise poses are hand-keyed clips on that puppet: Tree, Warrior, Fold, Squat, Plank and Bloom.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Music, effects and voices are synthesized in code. No audio files. Seven music beds, default music gain 0.10. At least 30 effects. Animalese voices.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players. The round is the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup).\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU at 320×180, phone and tablet profiles, WebKit iPhone fallback, and the AI Hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The build followed PLAN.md and the engine source. The title was drawn with a real RNG from 50 riffs. No separate web search in this session.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Fifteen defects showed up in testing. The first six were a gust check that did not match the acceleration model, an egui texture delta dropped on the floor, a private intent module, fonts bound in the same pass that drew them, a hub ghost field that was a boolean, and About pages that did not turn. A review of that build found eight more: sliders that never moved, Dev Mode with no jump, cheats or time scale, a free-play schedule stuck on the first four events, a Big Stand that kept its song and never showed the fake skip or the final age cut, an eyes-closed check with no tone, name and outfit lists that stopped at six, and a beach with no props or exercise poses. The drag path then failed to compile because a set lookup wanted a reference.\\\",\\n    \\\"Three were critical. The font and texture-delta panic stops the browser frame loop, so the page sits there with a status that never ticks. After credits, seven events could not be started. A morning age of 41 to 50 could not reach the rowboat even after a strong finale.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the bot playthrough: three seeds from New Stay to the credits, plus each event on five seeds against an idle player. The later menu tests drive the real pad and pointer path, including a held pointer on a slider row.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful check is a 1920×1080 WebGPU screenshot. On this machine that bitmap can come back blank while the sim is fine. 320×180 is the timing check, and the engine's own capture is the picture.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The sim is one tick you can drive with no GPU, and the picture is a pure view of that tick. That split is what made the whole stay testable.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A gust is an acceleration, so gust 30 with no lean settles inside the disc and does not tip. egui 0.36 panics if a TexturesDelta is dropped. Pause still increments the tick; the world time is what freezes.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance model, the day loop, and every event. The engine does not have a centre-of-pressure verb.\\\",\\n    \\\"The app frame. The demo's keys, menus and chrome run in the same function as the game, and a fit frame has to turn all of that off without breaking the engine's other scenes.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"frozen() returns early inside the tick. InputFrame gained lean, device, ui and hub. The HUD carries the fit UI and a status string. The mixer plays song beds. The page bridge publishes status. Captures composite the fit UI. Puppets tilt about the feet. Splash and a silent wake were added for the lagoon. Fit pointer drags emit slider values. Hand-keyed clips play the exercise poses. The beach room gained dressing with no collision.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to publish one JSON value that is both a string (for JSON.parse) and an object (for .tick), without hand-rolling a String constructor.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan is specific about the feel, the roster and the hub snippet, and it says behaviour is the contract when a filename does not match the engine.\\\",\\n    \\\"Song numbers in the plan and the beds the sim actually requests do not use the same index. The hub snippet sends whatever status.hub.ghost is, so a boolean there is sent as a boolean.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping the full roster, the 10-foot shell and the hub harness on a 20 GB machine where one extra browser gets killed.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say, next to the gust sentence, that a full lean alone must not tip and a gust on top of that lean must. State that plan filenames are guidance in the same paragraph as the file tree.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Wobble Minutes\\\",\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-222132__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:21:32\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Shardfall engine (Pavilion: Rust, wgpu, egui 0.36.2), commit 49ef2ba, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's cel look, high-key pastel, beach and wellness props. Library props only for generic dressing.\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine puppet tilts about the feet from the balance dot. Exercise poses are hand-keyed clips on that puppet: Tree, Warrior, Fold, Squat, Plank and Bloom.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Music, effects and voices are synthesized in code. No audio files. Seven music beds, default music gain 0.10. At least 30 effects. Animalese voices.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players. The round is the Inter-Resort Medley (Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup).\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU at 320×180, phone and tablet profiles, WebKit iPhone fallback, and the AI Hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The build followed PLAN.md and the engine source. The title was drawn with a real RNG from 50 riffs. No separate web search in this session.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Fifteen defects showed up in testing. The first six were a gust check that did not match the acceleration model, an egui texture delta dropped on the floor, a private intent module, fonts bound in the same pass that drew them, a hub ghost field that was a boolean, and About pages that did not turn. A review of that build found eight more: sliders that never moved, Dev Mode with no jump, cheats or time scale, a free-play schedule stuck on the first four events, a Big Stand that kept its song and never showed the fake skip or the final age cut, an eyes-closed check with no tone, name and outfit lists that stopped at six, and a beach with no props or exercise poses. The drag path then failed to compile because a set lookup wanted a reference.\\\",\\n    \\\"Three were critical. The font and texture-delta panic stops the browser frame loop, so the page sits there with a status that never ticks. After credits, seven events could not be started. A morning age of 41 to 50 could not reach the rowboat even after a strong finale.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the bot playthrough: three seeds from New Stay to the credits, plus each event on five seeds against an idle player. The later menu tests drive the real pad and pointer path, including a held pointer on a slider row.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful check is a 1920×1080 WebGPU screenshot. On this machine that bitmap can come back blank while the sim is fine. 320×180 is the timing check, and the engine's own capture is the picture.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The sim is one tick you can drive with no GPU, and the picture is a pure view of that tick. That split is what made the whole stay testable.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A gust is an acceleration, so gust 30 with no lean settles inside the disc and does not tip. egui 0.36 panics if a TexturesDelta is dropped. Pause still increments the tick; the world time is what freezes.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance model, the day loop, and every event. The engine does not have a centre-of-pressure verb.\\\",\\n    \\\"The app frame. The demo's keys, menus and chrome run in the same function as the game, and a fit frame has to turn all of that off without breaking the engine's other scenes.\\\",\\n    \\\"frozen() returns early inside the tick. InputFrame gained lean, device, ui and hub. The HUD carries the fit UI and a status string. The mixer plays song beds. The page bridge publishes status. Captures composite the fit UI. Puppets tilt about the feet. Splash and a silent wake were added for the lagoon. Fit pointer drags emit slider values. Hand-keyed clips play the exercise poses. The beach room gained dressing with no collision.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to publish one JSON value that is both a string (for JSON.parse) and an object (for .tick), without hand-rolling a String constructor.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan is specific about the feel, the roster and the hub snippet, and it says behaviour is the contract when a filename does not match the engine.\\\",\\n    \\\"Song numbers in the plan and the beds the sim actually requests do not use the same index. The hub snippet sends whatever status.hub.ghost is, so a boolean there is sent as a boolean.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping the full roster, the 10-foot shell and the hub harness on a 20 GB machine where one extra browser gets killed.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say, next to the gust sentence, that a full lean alone must not tip and a gust on top of that lean must. State that plan filenames are guidance in the same paragraph as the file tree.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Wobble Minutes\\\",\\n\",\"total_lines\":51}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fecbf228-95d2-412c-99e5-b2c40f463eb2-9","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,95,95,120,51,53,49,49,50,100,47,119,111,114,107,47,87,111,98,98,108,101,32,77,105,110,117,116,101,115,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,50,49,51,50,47,104,117,98,47,82,69,65,68,77,69,46,109,100,10,56,54,58,32,32,116,104,101,110,32,100,101,97,108,115,32,105,116,32,111,110,108,121,32,119,104,101,110,32,101,118,101,114,121,32,112,108,97,121,101,114,39,115,32,98,114,111,119,115,101,114,32,104,97,115,32,87,101,98,71,80,85,46,10,50,50,57,58,45,32,96,65,73,72,117,98,46,102,97,105,108,40,109,101,115,115,97,103,101,41,96,58,32,116,104,101,32,103,97,109,101,32,99,97,110,110,111,116,32,114,117,110,32,105,110,32,116,104,105,115,32,98,114,111,119,115,101,114,46,32,70,114,111,109,32,116,104,101,32,104,111,115,116,10,51,50,55,58,84,104,101,110,32,111,112,101,110,32,96,104,116,116,112,58,47,47,108,111,99,97,108,104,111,115,116,58,56,48,48,48,47,104,97,114,110,101,115,115,46,104,116,109,108,63,103,97,109,101,61,71,65,77,69,46,